{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_9","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to create the game workspace and understand the starter game and GAME-GUIDE.\n\nThe game name must be lowercase: trauma-compass. The work folder already contains PLAN.md, STAGE.md, and TASK.md, so the new game must be created in a subfolder to avoid overwrites.\n\nThe work root will later hold the HTML deliverable, exit-interview.json, and PROGRESS.md. The starter game files and GAME-GUIDE need review to inform the architecture. The simulation core will be pure TypeScript with minimal engine imports, using engine/sim-api.ts for RNG and events. Tests will import the sim directly.\n\nTests will live in labs/game and run via npm test. A pure simulation module would be easier to test than one tightly coupled to the engine. I am weighing whether to wrap the scene around a standalone sim or import engine utilities like defineScene directly.\n\nThe simulation will live in labs/game/sim/ as a pure, deterministic module with no DOM or Math.random. The scene will wrap it and feed hand intents. Tests will import the sim directly and may also exercise it through the scene. The plan forbids three.js and graphics imports on the sim side.\n\nESLint rules for labs/game must be checked to confirm permitted imports. Every source file under labs/ needs a @file comment and must stay under 400 lines. The starter game's settings, intents, and defineScene patterns need review. A compact but complete simulation design is now being drafted.\n\nThe simulation tick rate is fixed at 60 Hz. Normal field ticks advance by 100 each step, while Stillpoint mode advances by 25. Vitals drain proportionally to field time per step. The clock counts down in seconds of field time. Hands input will be processed per seat every tick.\n\nThe simulation will accept a structured hands object from the page and tests, while the net sequencer sends an array form. Counter inputs are monotonic press counts to tolerate lost packets. The available tools are scalpel, forceps, suture, drain, laser, syringe, gel, and scanner. Target kinds include pool, shard, wound, guide, mass, and nodule.\n\nAdditional target types include bleeder, abrasion, numb, flap, lull variants, solace, reverie, decoy, balm-node, balm-cell, mercy, mote, tendril, binder-point, and arterial. Every tool will have a defined effect or refusal against each target kind in a large data matrix. A simple bot strategy is being designed to solve cases using known geometry and case data.\n\nThe bot strategy selects the highest-priority target for the current tool and moves the cursor toward it, holding use when in range. Each tool has a distinct movement pattern: scalpel follows a guide polyline, suture zigzags across a wound, drain holds over a pool center, forceps grabs and pulls away, laser holds on a target, syringe charges to 0.85 before releasing on a patient or binder point, gel paints a spiral, and scanner holds near hidden targets. A perfect bot that follows guides within TEXTBOOK distance should win.\n\nThe bot must win the case, not merely mimic human cursor speed. Difficulty scales with vitals drain, clock length, parasite health and speed, and slip limits. Parasite health increases by 60% per extra surgeon, while targets grow by 25%. Two and four seat runs will be tested, so extra targets must remain clearable.\n\nI will read the starter scene, main entry point, HTML shell, GAME-GUIDE, test configuration, and ESLint rules before scaffolding. The new game will be placed in a subfolder of the work directory. I plan to run npm ci after copying the starter files.\n\nThe pure simulation module will be split into five files: types, balance, tools, ratings, hands, and actions. Each file must stay under 400 lines. GAME-GUIDE headings and starter files will be read in parallel with scaffolding.\n\nThe simulation module is being expanded to include vitals, gift mechanics, strain state machines, phase runners, operation steps, case data, story beats, bot policy, state hashing, lockstep sequencing, and an index entry point. Tests will cover the operation step, bot strategy, and content.\n\nTests for the sequencer and flow modules are being added. The page and engine integration is the hardest part. I will extend the starter labs/game directory rather than replace it. The engine scene will render an OR with a live mesh sheet. HTML UI overlays for title, HUD, and story screens will read from sim state exposed on window. The engine scene will run the simulation each tick via custom intents.\n\nThe page will boot the engine for 3D visuals and run the simulation in page code, syncing them. Tests will import the sim modules directly. The engine test suite covers labs/game/**/*.test.ts via vitest. Browser end-to-end tests load the single-file HTML deliverable. The scene needs OR props, a live sheet mesh driven by field state, and a camera above the field to avoid a blank screen. The simulation will run inside the scene's fixedUpdate, with state exposed through a getter for the page to read.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5251bc04-72ad-4993-a39c-2c27a44fcb70-14","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"BASE=\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731\"\nmkdir -p \"$BASE\"\nexport TMPDIR=/tmp/g.tUENBo\nexport CHROMIUM_PATH=$(ls -d ~/.cache/ms-playwright/chromium-*/chrome-linux64/chrome | head -1)\necho \"CHROMIUM=$CHROMIUM_PATH\"\nnode /tmp/src.WxqBqe/tools/game/new-game.mjs \"$BASE\" --name trauma-compass\necho \"NEWGAME_EXIT:$?\"\nls \"$BASE\" | head -30","description":"Scaffold trauma-compass game from engine"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5251bc04-72ad-4993-a39c-2c27a44fcb70-15","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/tmp/src.WxqBqe/labs/game/main.ts","limit":200}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5251bc04-72ad-4993-a39c-2c27a44fcb70-16","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/tmp/src.WxqBqe/labs/game/scenes/play.ts","limit":200}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5251bc04-72ad-4993-a39c-2c27a44fcb70-17","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/tmp/src.WxqBqe/labs/game/index.html"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8568,"output_tokens":2794,"cache_read_input_tokens":60544,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"c317b89c-f742-4e04-bd59-81298527d500"}
