/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/world/props/prop.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":27,\"content\":\" * `prop:crate` after a warning (`CORE_UNKNOWN_ID`).\"},{\"line_number\":34,\"content\":\" * getProp('prop:crate', reg).body.type; // 'dynamic': the engine's props come with the kind\"},{\"line_number\":71,\"content\":\"    description: 'Its name, unique in the prop: the ID pass names its batch `<prop>/<name>` (prop:crate/mesh).',\"},{\"line_number\":341,\"content\":\"    fallback: 'prop:crate',\"},{\"line_number\":360,\"content\":\"/** The prop `id` of `registry` (the shared one by default); a missing id gives `prop:crate`, with a warning. */\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/world/props/catalog.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":37,\"content\":\"  'prop:crate': {\"},{\"line_number\":88,\"content\":\"  'prop:pillar': {\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/world/props/place.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":22,\"content\":\" * propBody({ prop: 'prop:crate', at: [1, 0, 2], yaw: 0 })?.position; // [1, 0.375, 2]: the crate's centre\"},{\"line_number\":35,\"content\":\"  /** The prop, by id (`prop:crate`). */\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"32459b80-7285-49be-b4c0-f5f387e21145"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_23","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I have a solid plan and am ready to write the code.\n\nI'll create the simulation files in a batch. I'm designing the bot carefully to avoid debugging delays. I'll use seeded RNGs instead of Math.random for deterministic offsets. Case 1 phase 2 will trigger syringe when vitals drop below 50 and no targets exist. Case 3 flatline requires setting vitals to zero on phase entry so the bot paddles immediately.\n\nVitals will be set to zero at the end of a step so the next step begins code. The bot waits for the band to activate before paddling. I'm also checking whether case 1 allows code or fails immediately when vitals hit zero.\n\nI'll add a `codeAllowed` flag to each case. Code is permitted for cases 3, 5, 6, 7, 8, and gala; otherwise a flatline fails immediately. Attract mode cannot fail. The bot will use scalpel only on guides and fall back to textbook when mean distance is near zero.\n\nI'm designing the suture zigzag logic. A side-of-wound detector will use cross products to place alternating points left and right of the wound. The bot will space these points along the wound length.\n\nStitch placement will trigger when the bot crosses the wound side and stays within 0.6 units of the segment, spaced at least 0.36 units apart. Even spacing and quick stitching earn TEXTBOOK. Guide following requires holding use while aiming at each cut point until within 0.2 units.\n\nGuide paths will use roughly 18 points spaced every 0.4 meters along a curve, completing in about one second at 8 m/s. Forceps pulls will use 5 m/s to stay under the ROUGH speed threshold. Gel coverage will be judged by keeping the cursor inside the target's gel radius for the required number of ticks.\n\nGel coverage will be measured by a 3x3 grid of sample points. Each tick marks points within the gel radius of the cursor. A 90% hit rate counts as done. Small patches can be covered by sitting in the center. Larger areas may need lawnmower movement.\n\nScanner mechanics require holding the cursor in place for 0.2 seconds before revealing. The hidden mass phase will sequence as scan, laser nodules, loop-cut, then forceps. The loop guide will be hidden until the scan completes.\n\nThe hidden mass phase will sequence as scan, laser nodules, loop-cut, then forceps. The hidden mass, nodules, and loop guide will be placed close together so one scan reveals all three. A drama event will display \"IT MOVED.\" when the mass is removed in case 2 without pausing the simulation. I will also add a `runBot` export that returns the final operation.\n\nThe simulation will run for a maximum of 43,200 steps, or twelve minutes. If the bot does not finish in time, it returns a lost status with the reason \"bot timeout\".\n\nFor multi-seat cases, extra seats duplicate the first target pool with a twenty-five percent offset and scale parasite health accordingly.\n\nIntern and attending difficulty levels apply clock speed scales of 1.3 and 0.85 at creation, drain each step, and adjust parasite health and slip limits.\n\nThree test seeds will be run even though the simulation is largely deterministic.\n\nI'll add small seeded jitter to target positions so different seeds still produce valid wins. I'm also writing original refusal lines and a compact scene builder for the story, plus a full content scan of all game text including UI strings.\n\nI will scan the source code for banned words rather than relying on a separate test. The regex catches specific names and terms like \"derek stiles\" and \"hope hospital\". I will avoid using \"Adam\" and \"Bliss\" to prevent false positives. \"Second opinion\" is permitted.\n\nI will avoid placeholder, TODO, and lorem words in labs/game comments to prevent test failures. I will scan string literals or aggregated story and case data for banned terms. Engine feedback and testing logs will be written as issues arise. I am ready to begin coding.\n\nI'm registering game settings via `defineSettings` so the page can pass values like run mode, phase, seats, and difficulty into the scene module.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-91b05739-a73f-4ee0-a981-3ce172e797b1-57","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"when: 'scene'|when: 'live'|WHEN","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/core","glob":"*settings*","head_limit":20}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-91b05739-a73f-4ee0-a981-3ce172e797b1-58","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/best.ts","limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8196,"output_tokens":2570,"cache_read_input_tokens":127360,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"38ac9ebf-1b28-4adf-a949-51a7dd3b6a5d"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-91b05739-a73f-4ee0-a981-3ce172e797b1-57","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,55,51,49,95,95,120,53,57,99,49,100,51,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,78,111,32,109,97,116,99,104,101,115,32,102,111,117,110,100,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":1,\"match_count\":0,\"file_matches\":[]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-91b05739-a73f-4ee0-a981-3ce172e797b1-58","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The starter game's best round (PLAN.md WP 10.9): the fastest round won, kept across sessions in the engine's\\n * store (engine/app/store.ts) under the game's own prefix. `bestOf(store)` reads it (null before a first win) and\\n * `recordBest(store, seconds)` keeps a time that beats it, returning the best after. The page (labs/game/main.ts)\\n * records each won round's time and shows the best in the HUD; a replay's page opens the store in its `demo` mode, so\\n * a replay never sets a best.\\n *\\n * Game code, a page's: it imports only the engine's public API (engine/index.ts).\\n *\\n10→ * @example\\n * import { createStore } from '../../engine';\\n * const store = createStore({ mode: 'demo' }); // in memory: nothing kept past the page\\n * [recordBest(store, 14.2), recordBest(store, 16), recordBest(store, 9.5), bestOf(store)]; // [14.2, 14.2, 9.5, 9.5]\\n * @see labs/game/best.test.ts\\n */\\nimport type { Store } from '../../engine';\\n\\n/** The key the best round is kept under. */\\nexport const BEST_KEY = 'best';\\n20→\\n/** The fastest won round kept (s), or null: none yet, or a value that is no time. */\\nexport function bestOf(store: Store): number | null {\\n  const best = store.get<unknown>(BEST_KEY, null);\\n  return typeof best === 'number' && best > 0 ? best : null;\\n}\\n\\n/** Keeps `seconds` when it beats the best kept; returns the best after. */\\nexport function recordBest(store: Store, seconds: number): number {\\n  const best = bestOf(store);\\n30→  if (best !== null && best <= seconds) return best;\\n  store.set(BEST_KEY, seconds);\\n  return seconds;\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The starter game's best round (PLAN.md WP 10.9): the fastest round won, kept across sessions in the engine's\\n * store (engine/app/store.ts) under the game's own prefix. `bestOf(store)` reads it (null before a first win) and\\n * `recordBest(store, seconds)` keeps a time that beats it, returning the best after. The page (labs/game/main.ts)\\n * records each won round's time and shows the best in the HUD; a replay's page opens the store in its `demo` mode, so\\n * a replay never sets a best.\\n *\\n * Game code, a page's: it imports only the engine's public API (engine/index.ts).\\n *\\n10→ * @example\\n * import { createStore } from '../../engine';\\n * const store = createStore({ mode: 'demo' }); // in memory: nothing kept past the page\\n * [recordBest(store, 14.2), recordBest(store, 16), recordBest(store, 9.5), bestOf(store)]; // [14.2, 14.2, 9.5, 9.5]\\n * @see labs/game/best.test.ts\\n */\\nimport type { Store } from '../../engine';\\n\\n/** The key the best round is kept under. */\\nexport const BEST_KEY = 'best';\\n20→\\n/** The fastest won round kept (s), or null: none yet, or a value that is no time. */\\nexport function bestOf(store: Store): number | null {\\n  const best = store.get<unknown>(BEST_KEY, null);\\n  return typeof best === 'number' && best > 0 ? best : null;\\n}\\n\\n/** Keeps `seconds` when it beats the best kept; returns the best after. */\\nexport function recordBest(store: Store, seconds: number): number {\\n  const best = bestOf(store);\\n30→  if (best !== null && best <= seconds) return best;\\n  store.set(BEST_KEY, seconds);\\n  return seconds;\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/best.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file The starter game's best round (PLAN.md WP 10.9): the fastest round won, kept across sessions in the engine's\\n * store (engine/app/store.ts) under the game's own prefix. `bestOf(store)` reads it (null before a first win) and\\n * `recordBest(store, seconds)` keeps a time that beats it, returning the best after. The page (labs/game/main.ts)\\n * records each won round's time and shows the best in the HUD; a replay's page opens the store in its `demo` mode, so\\n * a replay never sets a best.\\n *\\n * Game code, a page's: it imports only the engine's public API (engine/index.ts).\\n *\\n * @example\\n * import { createStore } from '../../engine';\\n * const store = createStore({ mode: 'demo' }); // in memory: nothing kept past the page\\n * [recordBest(store, 14.2), recordBest(store, 16), recordBest(store, 9.5), bestOf(store)]; // [14.2, 14.2, 9.5, 9.5]\\n * @see labs/game/best.test.ts\\n */\\nimport type { Store } from '../../engine';\\n\\n/** The key the best round is kept under. */\\nexport const BEST_KEY = 'best';\\n\\n/** The fastest won round kept (s), or null: none yet, or a value that is no time. */\\nexport function bestOf(store: Store): number | null {\\n  const best = store.get<unknown>(BEST_KEY, null);\\n  return typeof best === 'number' && best > 0 ? best : null;\\n}\\n\\n/** Keeps `seconds` when it beats the best kept; returns the best after. */\\nexport function recordBest(store: Store, seconds: number): number {\\n  const best = bestOf(store);\\n  if (best !== null && best <= seconds) return best;\\n  store.set(BEST_KEY, seconds);\\n  return seconds;\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":33}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"92ba2c85-326e-4a34-a204-2c7b27a9dc64"}
