: \\\"A plate's height, its seam included.\\\",\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/input/devices/touch.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":162,\"content\":\"/** The closest element to `target` (itself included) that matches `selector`, or null. */\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/tests/baselines/perf/box-room.json\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":18,\"content\":\"  \\\"reason\\\": \\\"WP 5.5, measured with node x perf labs/box --scene room on the development platform (Chromium 141 on SwiftShader at 960 x 540, 20 cores at a load average of 35 to 42 from up to 6 lanes): 120 steps, then 60 frames drawn. The counts were the same in three runs and are the budgets, so with the 15% tolerance a room that draws 5 more calls, adds 3 textures or builds one pipeline after the warm-up fails, and its WP records the new counts with its reason. The means of the last 60 steps and frames were 0.013 to 0.14 ms a step (0.003 to 0.105 of them physics, no anim) and 2.1 to 3.1 ms of CPU a frame; their budgets leave about 7x and 4x over the loaded means, so only a real regression fails. Re-recorded by WP 7.4 (ADR-0008 amendment 7): createEngine now draws every frame through the post chain (engine/gfx/post/chain.ts), which makes its targets and builds every pass's pipelines in the warm-up, so a filter or look switch builds nothing; on the default look (look:clean) a frame is pl [... truncated (1031 chars total)]\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/gfx/textures/generators/runes.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":82,\"content\":\"  if (![4, 8, 16, 32].includes(spokes)) t