tending seed 1 lost 23ms score 14058 case:mercy lost stalled 5::0:6:14:0:1:0:0:0:0:0:0.0,15:0:1:0:0:0:0:0:0.0,16:0:0:0:0:0:0:0:0.0 phase 5/10 tick 1095 vitals 7 slips 0 left wound14,wound15,wound16\\ncoop 2 lost stalled 3::1:0:13:0:1:0:0:0:0:0:0.0 score 5632\\ncoop 4 lost stalled 3::1:0:16:0:1:0:0:0:0:0:0.0,17:0:1:0:0:0:0:0:0.0 score 6215\\ngala lost Edda Marlow is gone. case:gala-shift lost Edda Marlow is gone. phase 0/3 tick 3601 vitals 0/78 slips 0 left flap1,shard2,shard3,lull4,numb5,numb6,numb7,numb8,numb9,numb10,numb11,numb12,numb13\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"command\":\"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731 && ./node_modules/.bin/tsx /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/run-cases.ts\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Run bot on every story case\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3%2Fwork/01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151/terminal/call-331c3863-bcbe-4a8f-990d-8b5c572e2a01-44.log\",\"total_bytes\":6392}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"20efb319-1bff-42b4-b201-0bc3a2b17de3"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_59","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Several cases are now won: first-cut, quiet-lump, and it-moves.\n\ncrosstalk is stalled on the last wound. Only one stitch landed; the second stitch failed to register after 600 ticks. The bot likely oscillates without crossing far enough, or sutureSide gets stuck.\n\nThe spacing check should allow the second stitch. The bot may be targeting the wrong wound, or sutureSide logic may be stuck.\n\nThe sutureSide flip logic is now clear. If the second stitch fails to register, the bot oscillates forever at the same u coordinate because stitches never increments. The first stitch may have landed too close to 0.75, causing the spacing check to fail.\n\nThe diagonal travel from u=0.25 to u=0.75 may cross the wound near u=0.5. That would make the stitch spacing only 0.287, below the required 0.3825 threshold.\n\nThe spacing check should actually pass for the second stitch at u=0.75, since 0.575 exceeds the threshold. The stall may instead be caused by both points landing on the same side of the wound.\n\nThe nearest() function may be targeting the wrong wound. If another wound is closer when the bot reaches u=0.75, the stitch lands on that different wound instead of the intended one. The crosstalk case places its three wounds on separate sites, so nearest() only evaluates the current site.\n\nThe pool is drained first, so only one wound remains per site after phase 1. The bot should finish it.\n\nsegmentSide may return 0 when the bot is close to the line during approach. That would prevent a side change from registering, which is required for the cross condition to fire.\n\nsutureSide is stored on the seat, not the wound. When the bot switches sites, that side state persists. The next site's wound may therefore start with an incorrect side value, which could break the cross condition.\n\nThe bot may cross the new wound at a random u coordinate while traveling, registering an invalid stitch. That would place the first stitch too close to 0.75, so the second stitch fails the spacing check. Resetting sutureSide when the target changes should fix this.\n\nThe bot should not mutate the seat state directly. A sim-side fix is better: reset sutureSide when the target wound changes or the site changes. The cutting field is already used for guides, so it cannot be reused for this purpose.\n\nThe sim fix is confirmed. When the bot begins stitching a fresh wound, sutureSide will be reset to zero so the first contact correctly establishes the side without counting an invalid stitch.\n\nsutureSide is not hashed, so adding it to the Seat interface is safe. The reset will be applied inside `stitch()` when the target wound has zero stitches and the cursor is far from the line.\n\nThe reset logic is refined: it only clears sutureSide when the bot is far from the line and stitches are zero, so a close approach can still register a cross.\n\nIn struck-off and solace, four wounds remain stalled with tiny strokes. They likely stay below generation three because split() only accumulates movement when the cursor is inside radius plus 0.3.\n\nThe bot's 18-tick leg oscillation covers roughly 2.4 meters per cycle, more than enough to exceed the 1.5-meter generation threshold. The split motion should accumulate normally if the cursor stays inside the radius-plus-0.3 boundary. Multiple overlapping solace wounds are also being considered, since nearest() selects the closest target.\n\nThe bot's stroke is being split across four overlapping solace wounds because nearest() can switch targets while the cursor moves. The fix is to spawn child wounds farther apart, or to make the bot stick to one target until it is fully done.\n\nThe split spawn distance will be increased to 1.6 meters so child wounds do not overlap. At that spacing, a generation-1 radius of 0.9 and a generation-2 reach of 0.85 keep the children safely separated.\n\nThe 1.6-meter horizontal offset alone is insufficient. Generation-3 children from the two generation-2 parents would still overlap at the center. A z offset is needed to keep all spawned wounds fully separated.\n\nThe simplest robust fix for child wound placement is to spread them in a circle around the parent using the parent's target.id as an angle. Each child will be placed at x + 1.5·cos(id) and z + 1.5·sin(id), ensuring all spawned wounds stay fully separated.\n\nThe 2.6-meter separation between child wounds is well above the 1.2-meter combined reach of generation-2 radii, so they will not overlap. Generation-3 children will stay safely inside the ±8 field bounds.\n\nThe zero strokes on two solace wounds confirm the bot was stuck wiggling the first ones and never reached the others. Proper separation should let it finish each wound individually.\n\nLasers should be used for generation-three targets.\n\nThe zero burn confirms the stalled solace wounds are not generation three. A generation-three target would be laser-destroyed, not split. The four remaining wounds are therefore generation two or lower. The parent generation-one split should have produced only two generation-two children, so the extra two must be partially split generation-two parents that spawned before finishing.\n\nThe split logic only spawns children once when stroke crosses 1.5, so partial splits are impossible. Four alive solace wounds must therefore be generation three, yet burn is zero and stroke is tiny. A generation-three target should be laser-destroyed rather than split, which contradicts the observed behavior.\n\nThe zero burn confirms the bot is not laser-destroying generation-three targets. It is splitting them instead, so they must be generation two or lower. The split function should still fire for generation three, which suggests the laser connection itself is failing. For laser targeting, nearest() uses a radius-plus-0.25 limit.\n\nThe laser targeting radius is 0.6, well above the generation-three reach of 0.32, so a generation-three target should be destroyed rather than split. The zero burn confirms the bot is not laser-destroying generation-three targets. The four stalled solace wounds are therefore generation two or lower. Their tiny strokes confirm that split() is being called, yet the zero values prove the bot never reaches them because nearest() keeps switching targets while the cursor moves. This validates the overlapping-target theory.\n\nThe debug output shows four alive solace targets with IDs 4, 5, 6, and 7. The parent is already done, so those four must be generation three. This confirms the bot is splitting generation-three targets instead of laser-destroying them.\n\nThe four stalled solace wounds are generation two, not three. Their tiny strokes prove split() was called and they were never finished. They were spawned by parents that completed their own splits, not by the current generation-three targets.\n\nThe split function adds stroke before checking generation, so generation-three targets still accumulate movement. This contradicts the zero burn observed, so the bot must be calling split() instead of burn(). The next step is to log the generation values of the stalled solace wounds to resolve this contradiction.\n\nThe root cause is now clear. For generation-three solace targets, the code skips the early return and falls through to `rightTool`. Because scalpel is listed before laser in the tool map, `rightTool('solace')` returns scalpel. The tool check then fails to match any case, so the bot does nothing.\n\nThe bot sets the scalpel tool but never moves, so stroke stays zero. The 0.1 and 0.4 strokes on the alive wounds prove split() is still being called, meaning they are generation two or lower. The puzzle of how four alive wounds exist when only two should remain after one generation-one split is now being re-examined.\n\ntypescript\nif (target.stroke < 1.5 || target.gen >= 3) return true;\ntarget.done = true;\n\nThe reverie target never died because the laser damage never finished. The full 360-second time limit elapsed, and the score of 1620 reflects only guide actions. The signature likely truncated the reverie entry. Burn needs five seconds of laser to kill it.\n\nThe reverie target stayed hidden under a closed flap, so the bot could not scan it. The colleague opened the flap and set the target done, but the bot may have scanned too late or failed to connect the laser while surfaced. This prevented the five-second burn from accumulating.\n\nThe burn() function for reverie returns false immediately if the target is not surfaced. The surface logic only runs after that check, so the bot never surfaces the target before attempting laser damage.\n\nThe early return in burn() for unrevealed reverie targets must be removed so the later surfacing logic can run. The gala-night balm issue is that nodes are not dying and cells are spawning instead; the bot should bind nodes because they outrank cells, but it may be blocked by nearby cells.\n\nThe syringe tool sees the nearest object first. Balm cells spawn every four seconds in a grid around the node, so they often sit closer than the node itself. When the bot tries to bind the node, it sees a cell instead and refuses to bind because that pair is refuse. The fix is to raise the priority of balm cells when they are close to a node, forcing the bot to gel them before attempting to bind.\n\nThe bot stalled at tick 4201, seventy seconds in, with no node doses applied. Balm cells spawn every four seconds, so the node must be bound before the first cell appears. The stall prevented the bot from reaching the node in time.\n\nThe bot should reach the first node at site zero because it sorts by lowest ID when ranks are equal. The colleague does not bind nodes. The zero dose means the target is out of range, the syringe refused the pair, or the tool was never used. work() falls through to rightTool for balmNode and sets the tool to syringe.\n\nThe bot sets the tool to syringe for balmNode targets, but the rightTool function never handles syringe. It only returns drain, burn, or paint. Because no case matches, the bot never approaches or uses the syringe, so bind() is never called.\n\nThe fix for balmNode is to add it to the bind() tool check alongside binder and matron.\n\nMercy phase five stalled with one stitch on a wound. The same suture bug as crosstalk is present there. Vitals are low because code set them to 25 and wounds bled. Fixing suture should resolve mercy too, though slow stitch may still kill vitals.\n\nCoop first-cut phase three stalled during stitch. The signature shows phase 3, which is stitch. This is the same suture bug.\n\nMultiple seats worsen sutureSide chaos. The injected flag is 1, so the stable phase passed.\n\nIn gala shift the patient died at tick 3601 after sixty seconds. Lull and numbs drained vitals. The lull was still alive and the shard under the flap remained unlifted. The bot likely stalled trying to lift the flap or kill the lull. Flap lift uses pull(), which should work.\n\nThe lull might be blocking the flap lift. If the bot tries to pull the flap while the lull is nearest, forceps on the lull is refuse and the lift fails. The lull sits about 1.1 meters away, which exceeds the 0.85 nearest limit, so it should not block the flap unless the bot stands on the lull.\n\nThe bot likely never reaches the shard under the flap because it is too subtle. Numbs are optional and ignored, so they do not block progress. The lull should die in two seconds once laser damage begins, but if the bot stalls on the flap instead, vitals drain until death. I will add logging for gala shift after fixing the clear bugs. The suture fix belongs in act.ts stitch start, and solace child spread needs correction there as well.\n\nThe syringe fix will prioritize binder, matron, and balmNode targets over nearby refuse objects in nearest(). This prevents cells from blocking the node. If cells spawn too quickly, the bot must still gel them while binding the node.\n\nThe syringe fix will be implemented directly inside `syringe()` in `act.ts`. It will scan for a binder, matron, or balmNode target within reach and bind it immediately, bypassing any refuse objects that might otherwise block the node.\n\nThe co-op suture fix resets each seat's sutureSide, preventing multiple seats from fighting over the same wound. pick() splits targets across seats, so two seats on three wounds divide them cleanly and a fourth seat idles. The gel phase should work once stitch is fixed. In mercy, vitals stayed at eleven because the stuck stitch caused continuous bleeding during the stall.\n\nThe first three wounds stitched successfully, but the second rake phase stalled because leftover sutureSide state from the first set persisted. Resetting that state when stitches reach zero and the bot is far away should fix the second-phase failure.\n\nWounds are spaced more than one meter apart, so the distance reset will trigger between them. I will also add a `stitchId` field to each seat and reset `sutureSide` whenever the wound ID changes, even if the bot is already close.\n\nThe `stitchId` reset logic is now implemented: whenever the seat’s current wound ID differs from the target, it updates `stitchId` and resets `sutureSide`. This field is added to the `Seat` interface and `makeSeat`, and all seat construction uses that factory so nothing else needs changing.\n\nThe lull will be ranked above the flap so the bot kills it first. The lull bleeds vitals while the shard under the flap does not. This prevents the patient from dying before the shard can be reached.\n\nKilling the lull in three seconds should prevent numbs from accumulating, since they only spawn while the lull is alive. The reverie burn timer is also being checked: with a five-second burnNeed scaled to health, surface time is 2.2 seconds, and the step count works out to exactly 132 steps.\n\nReverie burn damage is sufficient: 132 steps yield 2.2 damage, and three cycles exceed the 5-point threshold. The bot rescans between submerge and surface, so hidden state is handled correctly. I will also check reverie under the flap.\n\nThe bot will lift the flap before scanning for decoys, since decoys are hidden and the flap is not. After lifting, scanning reveals any decoys in range. Solace generation three or higher will be handled as burn damage explicitly before rightTool.\n\nReverie laser heat is safe because the burn timer pauses between surface and submerge cycles. The solace target branch will explicitly return burn for generation three or higher, while lower generations still split. The coop gel stall was actually a stitch-phase failure, so the suture fix resolves it too. I also need to verify that a wound with length 1.15 stitches correctly after the sutureSide reset.\n\nCase 1 succeeded, so sequential wounds on a single site stitch correctly. Case 3 still fails with one stuck stitch. The difference is multiple sites: pick() returns the lowest wound id across all sites, so the bot may switch sites mid-wound and lose its sutureSide state.\n\nThe stuck stitch is on the same wound, not a site switch. Case 3 drains pools before stitching, but the pool and wound do not overlap, so it cannot be blocking the suture.\n\nThe stuck stitch is a spacing-oscillation bug. The bot lands the first cross at u=0.25, then oscillates without a valid second cross. Case 1 succeeds because its geometry allows the second cross to land, but case 3 fails on this specific layout. Jitter is unlikely to be the cause.\n\nThe stuck stitch likely occurs because the bot lands a cross at u=0.5 and then oscillates around that same point instead of advancing. The fix is to make the bot cross only at fixed perpendicular u positions, travel straight to side A, then side B, and only advance once both crosses register.\n\nThe stuck stitch is caused by a spacing failure. The first cross lands at a u value that is too close to the second target u, so every subsequent cross fails to register and the bot oscillates forever.\n\nThe stitch rewrite will keep the u coordinate fixed at 0.15 or 0.85 and move only in the perpendicular direction. The spacing check will remain unchanged.\n\nThe stitch rewrite clamps the u coordinate between 0.08 and 0.92 and offsets it per side by 0.4 meters. The bot will approach each target point directly without crossing in between, since travel between u values while use is true causes unwanted stitches.\n\nThe bot will only trigger the suture hand while it is very close to the target side point or while its along-track u is within 0.12 of the clamped u value. This prevents accidental stitches during travel between u positions. The `segmentU` helper must be imported from world.\n\nThe stitchId reset and the use flag will be implemented together as a double safeguard. The reverie phase will no longer return early.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-dc319d27-c889-40e3-83f8-21b16b7de163-45","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/types.ts","old_string":"  sutureSide: number;","new_string":"  sutureSide: number;\n  /** Wound the suture side belongs to, or -1. Not part of the hash. */\n  stitchId: number;"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-dc319d27-c889-40e3-83f8-21b16b7de163-46","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/world.ts","old_string":"    sutureSide: 0,","new_string":"    sutureSide: 0,\n    stitchId: -1,"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-dc319d27-c889-40e3-83f8-21b16b7de163-47","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/act.ts","old_string":"  if (target.lacquer || target.stitches >= target.need) return !target.lacquer && target.stitches >= target.need;\n  if (!use) return false;","new_string":"  if (target.lacquer || target.stitches >= target.need) return !target.lacquer && target.stitches >= target.need;\n  if (seat.stitchId !== target.id) {\n    seat.stitchId = target.id;\n    seat.sutureSide = 0;\n  }\n  if (!use) return false;"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-dc319d27-c889-40e3-83f8-21b16b7de163-48","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/act.ts","old_string":"  target.done = true;\n  const alive = op.targets.filter((item) => item.kind === 'solace' && !item.done).length;\n  if (alive < 12) {\n    const gen = target.gen + 1;\n    addTarget(op, { kind: 'solace', x: target.x - 0.35, z: target.z, gen, site: target.site, patient: target.patient }, target.phase);\n    if (alive + 1 < 12) {\n      addTarget(op, { kind: 'solace', x: target.x + 0.35, z: target.z, gen, site: target.site, patient: target.patient }, target.phase);\n    }\n  }","new_string":"  target.done = true;\n  const alive = op.targets.filter((item) => item.kind === 'solace' && !item.done).length;\n  if (alive < 12) {\n    const gen = target.gen + 1;\n    const angle = target.id * 1.7;\n    const spread = 1.45;\n    addTarget(op, { kind: 'solace', x: target.x + Math.cos(angle) * spread, z: target.z + Math.sin(angle) * spread, gen, site: target.site, patient: target.patient }, target.phase);\n    if (alive + 1 < 12) {\n      addTarget(op, { kind: 'solace', x: target.x + Math.cos(angle + 2.2) * spread, z: target.z + Math.sin(angle + 2.2) * spread, gen, site: target.site, patient: target.patient }, target.phase);\n    }\n  }"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-dc319d27-c889-40e3-83f8-21b16b7de163-49","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/act.ts","old_string":"  if (seat.laserCool > 0) return true;\n  if (target.kind === 'solace' && target.gen < 3) return false;\n  if (target.kind === 'reverie' && !target.surfaced) return false;","new_string":"  if (seat.laserCool > 0) return true;\n  if (target.kind === 'solace' && target.gen < 3) return false;"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-dc319d27-c889-40e3-83f8-21b16b7de163-50","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/act.ts","old_string":"function syringe(op: Op, seat: Seat, near: Target | null, use: boolean, edge: boolean): void {\n  if (near && (near.kind === 'binder' || near.kind === 'matron')) {\n    const applied = bind(op, seat, near, use);\n    if (!applied && edge) bark(op, seat, near, specialRefusal('syringe', near) || refusalLine('syringe', near.kind));\n    return;\n  }","new_string":"function syringe(op: Op, seat: Seat, near: Target | null, use: boolean, edge: boolean): void {\n  const bindable = bindTarget(op, seat) ?? (near && (near.kind === 'binder' || near.kind === 'matron' || near.kind === 'balmNode') ? near : null);\n  if (bindable) {\n    const applied = bind(op, seat, bindable, use);\n    if (!applied && edge) bark(op, seat, bindable, specialRefusal('syringe', bindable) || refusalLine('syringe', bindable.kind));\n    return;\n  }"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-dc319d27-c889-40e3-83f8-21b16b7de163-51","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/bot.ts","old_string":"import { idleHand } from './world';","new_string":"import { idleHand, segmentU } from './world';"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-dc319d27-c889-40e3-83f8-21b16b7de163-52","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/bot.ts","old_string":"function rank(target: Target): number {\n  if (target.kind === 'flap') return 0;\n  if (target.kind === 'matron' && target.vulnerable) return 1;\n  if (target.hidden) return 2;\n  if (target.kind === 'lull' || target.kind === 'bleeder' || target.kind === 'mote') return 3;\n  if (target.kind === 'pool') return 4;","new_string":"function rank(target: Target): number {\n  if (target.kind === 'lull' || target.kind === 'bleeder' || target.kind === 'mote') return 0;\n  if (target.kind === 'flap') return 1;\n  if (target.kind === 'matron' && target.vulnerable) return 1;\n  if (target.hidden) return 2;\n  if (target.kind === 'pool') return 4;"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-dc319d27-c889-40e3-83f8-21b16b7de163-53","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/bot.ts","old_string":"  if (target.kind === 'solace' && target.gen < 3) return split(op, seat, hand, target);\n  if (target.kind === 'guide') return cut(op, seat, hand, target);\n  if (target.kind === 'wound') return stitch(op, seat, hand, target);\n  if (target.kind === 'shard' || target.kind === 'mass' || target.kind === 'cocoon' || target.kind === 'tendril') return pull(op, seat, hand, target);\n  if (target.kind === 'flap') return pull(op, seat, hand, target);\n  if (target.kind === 'binder' || target.kind === 'matron') return bind(op, seat, hand, target);","new_string":"  if (target.kind === 'solace' && target.gen < 3) return split(op, seat, hand, target);\n  if (target.kind === 'solace') return burn(op, seat, hand, target);\n  if (target.kind === 'guide') return cut(op, seat, hand, target);\n  if (target.kind === 'wound') return stitch(op, seat, hand, target);\n  if (target.kind === 'shard' || target.kind === 'mass' || target.kind === 'cocoon' || target.kind === 'tendril') return pull(op, seat, hand, target);\n  if (target.kind === 'flap') return pull(op, seat, hand, target);\n  if (target.kind === 'binder' || target.kind === 'matron' || target.kind === 'balmNode') return bind(op, seat, hand, target);"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-dc319d27-c889-40e3-83f8-21b16b7de163-54","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/bot.ts","old_string":"function stitch(op: Op, seat: Seat, hand: Hand, target: Target): void {\n  const dx = target.x2 - target.x;\n  const dz = target.z2 - target.z;\n  const length = Math.max(0.5, Math.hypot(dx, dz));\n  const u = (target.stitches + 0.5) / Math.max(1, target.need);\n  const side = seat.sutureSide >= 0 ? -1 : 1;\n  const x = target.x + dx * u + (-dz / length) * 0.36 * side;\n  const z = target.z + dz * u + (dx / length) * 0.36 * side;\n  approach(hand, seat, x, z, op.balance.cursor);\n  hand.use = seat.sutureSide !== 0 || Math.hypot(seat.x - x, seat.z - z) < 0.2;\n  hand.tool = 2;\n}","new_string":"function stitch(op: Op, seat: Seat, hand: Hand, target: Target): void {\n  const dx = target.x2 - target.x;\n  const dz = target.z2 - target.z;\n  const length = Math.max(0.5, Math.hypot(dx, dz));\n  const u = Math.min(0.9, Math.max(0.1, (target.stitches + 0.5) / Math.max(1, target.need)));\n  const side = seat.sutureSide >= 0 ? -1 : 1;\n  const x = target.x + dx * u + (-dz / length) * 0.4 * side;\n  const z = target.z + dz * u + (dx / length) * 0.4 * side;\n  approach(hand, seat, x, z, op.balance.cursor);\n  const along = segmentU(seat.x, seat.z, target);\n  const atLine = Math.abs(along - u) < 0.14;\n  hand.use = atLine && (seat.sutureSide !== 0 || Math.hypot(seat.x - x, seat.z - z) < 0.18);\n  hand.tool = 2;\n}"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3524,"output_tokens":12897,"cache_read_input_tokens":138496,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"9ed37f50-c1b9-47c3-bb1f-17673c1f4549"}
