{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_62","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Almost everything is complete.\n\nMercy tendrils remain stalled. The forceps cannot grab them. The pull function is failing to activate.\n\nThe bot stalled at tick 1194 after the mercy-rites guide was cut. The forceps are not grabbing the tendrils. The nearest target may be wrong, or another nearby object may be interfering.\n\nThe bot is grabbing the wrong tendril. When approaching a target, the nearest object in the simulation may be a different tendril. The bot checks that it is holding the picked target ID, but the simulation holds the nearest one instead. This mismatch causes the pull to fail.\n\nThe held tendril is snapped to the seat position. It stays at that spot while the bot moves toward the picked target. The nearest-tendril check therefore keeps returning the wrong object.\n\nThe held tendril is being pulled as the bot moves toward the picked target. That would falsely register progress, but none of the tendrils are actually done. The pull distance never reaches 1.2.\n\nThe bot releases the held tendril while traveling toward the picked target. The forceps are not holding anything during that movement, so no pull can occur.\n\nThe bot releases the held tendril the moment it moves toward the picked target, so nothing ever pulls 1.2 meters. The fix is to prioritize pulling whatever the forceps are already holding, rather than switching to the nearest target.\n\nTendrils will be spaced 1.2 meters apart so the forceps cannot grab the wrong one initially.\n\nThe coop stitch stall remains in phase 3. One wound has only one stitch, suggesting a suture bug with multiple seats. Two seats should cover different wounds, yet the progress is stuck.\n\nThe stitch stall may be caused by both seats targeting the same wound. With four seats, the duplicate-wound formula yields two extra wounds, so five wounds should split evenly among four seats. The current state shows two wounds left, with one already at one stitch.\n\nThe stitch logic is being traced step by step. The side point sits 0.4 units off the line, so segmentU should equal u when the bot arrives. The side flag gets set, then flips on the next frame to trigger the cross. This suggests the stitch sequence itself is sound.\n\nThe stitchId reset logic is not the culprit. Each seat has its own stitchId and does not overwrite another seat's progress. The duplicate-position theory is also unlikely because the wound length is 1.15, which should accommodate two stitches at u 0.25 and 0.75. The coop stitch stall requires a closer look.\n\nA debug run will log which wound and stitch positions are active during coop mode. The `atLine` logic using clamped segmentU is sound. Independent suture sides across seats should not stall progress; if two seats land on the same wound at different u values, the stitch count would rise faster rather than slower.\n\nThe second stitch never registers. The bot's crossing step is not being detected. Overshooting the side point in one step was considered, but a side flip from -1 to +1 should still count as a stitch.\n\nOvershooting the side point and landing on the line should still trigger a stitch on the next step, so that theory is ruled out. The next step is to add temporary logging that prints each target's stitch count, stitchAt, seat positions, and sutureSide when the coop run stalls.\n\nThe Gala phase is stuck on the flap. The lull was killed and the cocoon left, yet the flap never lifts. The bot likely grabs the cocoon or a nearby shard instead of the flap, so the lift never triggers.\n\nThe Gala bot is at site 0, the flap is at (-0.3, 0.2), and the cocoon is at (-1.2, -0.5). The distance between them is about 1.1 units, so the nearest-tendril check should see the flap first. The path from the lull position to the flap passes near the cocoon, which may cause the forceps to grab it instead.\n\nThe forceps only activate when the bot is within 0.48 units of the flap, so the cocoon should not be grabbed during travel. The lift code advances only while the seat holds the correct target ID and pulls away; it stops at 0.8 distance. The stall may be caused by an early release or a hold mismatch. A debug script will trace the gala, mercy, and coop states.\n\nThe bot will now commit to whatever it is holding. If the forceps grab the wrong object, the bot will finish pulling that held item before picking the next target. This should fix the tendril, flap, and cocoon stalls.\n\nThe hold-commit fix will be inserted at the start of the work section, after the gift, code, and inject checks. Tendrils will be spaced 1.1 meters apart. The coop stitch stall is a separate issue from the hold logic, so it will be debugged with a quick script before making further edits.\n\nThe coop debug signature shows only one wound left, so the other four are already done. The remaining wound is stuck at a single stitch. The new `atLine` logic still fails to register the second cross on that last wound. The bot may never reach the side point where the line check triggers.\n\nThe stitch logic is being traced step by step. When the bot reaches the goal with sutureSide at zero, use becomes true and stitch() sets the side flag. The next frame the side flips, and the bot moves to the opposite side point. Because the approach is purely perpendicular, along stays constant and atLine remains true throughout that move. This means the cross should register, so the stall must come from somewhere else.\n\nThe `stitch()` function resets `sutureSide` whenever the current `stitchId` does not match the target ID. Because each seat has its own unique stitch ID, this reset should not occur between seats. The `use` flag is also being verified: it is only true when the bot is both near and actively using the forceps, so the stitch path should not fire while `use` is false.\n\nThe stitch logic is being traced step by step. When use becomes true at the side point, stitch runs, sets stitchId, and resets sutureSide to zero. The next frame the side flips and stitch counts. This should work correctly. The only remaining concern is that the first step might record a side of zero if the bot is too close to the line.\n\nThe coop stitch stall is not caused by two seats sharing a wound. When only one wound remains, the mine filter assigns it to seat 0 and leaves seat 1 idle. The remaining bug must be elsewhere.\n\nThe stuck coop wound may be a duplicate placed nearby. If the nearest-target check alternates between two overlapping wounds, stitchId resets every step and sutureSide is wiped out. That would prevent any stitch from ever registering.\n\nThe duplicate wound offset of 0.8 is within 0.85 of the original, so the nearest-target check alternates between them and resets stitchId every step. The fix is to space coop duplicates farther apart, only reset sutureSide when intentionally switching to a done wound, and have the bot stick to one wound ID until it is finished.\n\nThe bot will write its committed wound ID into `seat.memo` so the simulation cannot reset it. The flicker between two nearby wounds resets the side flag every step. The nearest-target check is too unstable to fix directly, so the commitment must live in the bot's own memo.\n\nWriting the committed wound ID into `seat.memo` is acceptable scratch space, not simulation state. The bot can set it between steps and read it on the next call, since `stepOp` does not consume that field.\n\nThe bot will read a `go:` prefix from `seat.memo` to lock onto a target. If that target is still open and un-done, it stays locked; otherwise the memo clears. The automatic `sutureSide` reset in `act.ts` is being removed because it causes the flicker bug. The side flag will only reset when stitches are zero and the side is stale.\n\nRemoving the automatic sutureSide reset entirely would leave stale side data from a previous wound, which could corrupt the first stitch on a new target. The bot cannot directly modify simulation state. The flicker bug is confirmed: when two nearby wounds both have stitches, switching between them resets the side flag and wipes out the cross count.\n\nThe side reset rule is being tightened: only reset `sutureSide` when entering a wound that has zero stitches. If the bot flickers between two wounds where one already has stitches, the side flag would stay stale and fail to re-establish itself on the target.\n\nCommitting to a target in the bot's memo does not stop the simulation from stitching the nearest wound instead. If two wounds overlap, the bot can aim at one while the suture lands on the other. Spacing coop duplicates by 2.2 meters fixes this overlap; the original wounds are only about 1.6 units apart.\n\nA +2.2 duplicate offset would still place the first duplicate near the second wound, leaving only 0.3 units of overlap. A larger shift is needed to keep duplicates safely apart.\n\nThe duplicate offset is being increased to +4 in x and +2 in z. The first duplicate lands at 2.2, 1.8, which is 0.7 units from the nearest original wound and 2.7 units away in z. This keeps the nearest-target distance safely above the 0.85 limit.\n\nThe duplicate offset formula is broken. Because the extra duplicates are appended after the ordinary ones, `Math.floor(n / ordinary.length)` is zero for every new target. Every duplicate therefore shifts by +3.5 in x and stacks on top of the first one instead of spreading across the field.\n\nThe duplicate offset formula is being corrected. The whole extra copy will shift by 4 meters in x, using `Math.floor(n / ordinary.length)` to assign each duplicate its own offset. This spreads the copies across the field instead of stacking them on top of the first one.\n\nA 4-meter x-shift is too small; the original and duplicate wound spans overlap by about 0.5 meters. Shifting only in z by 3 meters places the duplicate at z=2 to 4, safely beyond the 0.85 nearest-target limit.\n\nThe duplicate offset is being raised to z + 3.2 so the copied wounds sit safely beyond the nearest-target limit. Tendrils will be spaced one meter apart at positions -2, -1, 0, 1, and 2. The bot will also commit to holding tendril targets.\n\nThe cocoon and flap are 1.14 meters apart, so the nearest-target check should not pick the cocoon when the bot is at the flap. The stall may instead be caused by pull() failing to set use correctly when hold is -1, or by the bot selecting the cocoon first.\n\nThe `open()` check confirms the flap is pickable and should rank above the cocoon. The shard under the flap is blocked until the flap opens, so it cannot be selected first.\n\nThe lift math for the flap is sound: about fifteen steps should reach the required 0.8 threshold. The ox position is fixed on grab, so it cannot drift. A focused debug will run after the hold-commit and z-offset fixes to inspect seat.hold, flap.lift, and positions if gala still stalls. The mercy tendrils fix should also resolve their grab-release cycle.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2397884d-a0fe-4e89-a21f-3b3cf2930f12-57","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/world.ts","old_string":"    placeSpawn(op, { ...spawn, x: spawn.x + 0.8 * (1 + Math.floor(n / ordinary.length)), z: spawn.z + 0.4 }, index);","new_string":"    const copy = 1 + Math.floor(n / ordinary.length);\n    placeSpawn(op, { ...spawn, z: spawn.z + 3.2 * copy }, index);"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2397884d-a0fe-4e89-a21f-3b3cf2930f12-58","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/cases.ts","old_string":"        [-0.8, -0.4, 0, 0.4, 0.8].map((x) => ({ kind: 'tendril' as const, x, z: 0.25 })),","new_string":"        [-2, -1, 0, 1, 2].map((x) => ({ kind: 'tendril' as const, x, z: 0.2 })),"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2397884d-a0fe-4e89-a21f-3b3cf2930f12-59","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/bot.ts","old_string":"  if (phase?.until === 'injected' && !op.injected) return inject(op, seat, hand);\n  if (phase?.until === 'code') return hand;\n  const target = pick(op, seat);","new_string":"  if (phase?.until === 'injected' && !op.injected) return inject(op, seat, hand);\n  if (phase?.until === 'code') return hand;\n  if (seat.hold >= 0) {\n    const held = op.targets.find((item) => item.id === seat.hold && !item.done);\n    if (held) {\n      if (held.site !== seat.site) hand.site = held.site;\n      pull(op, seat, hand, held);\n      return hand;\n    }\n  }\n  const target = pick(op, seat);"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2397884d-a0fe-4e89-a21f-3b3cf2930f12-60","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/act.ts","old_string":"  if (seat.stitchId !== target.id) {\n    seat.stitchId = target.id;\n    seat.sutureSide = 0;\n  }","new_string":"  if (seat.stitchId !== target.id) {\n    seat.stitchId = target.id;\n    if (target.stitches === 0) seat.sutureSide = 0;\n  }"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1922,"output_tokens":7457,"cache_read_input_tokens":156288,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"3818d319-96c7-4936-b700-7f4f1241ded3"}
