{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_66","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"At tick 120, the bot is holding both the flap and the shard.\n\nThe seat moved to x=7 and hit the clamp. Lift stuck at 0.50 because it is computed from the original ox position captured when the shard was grabbed. Switching hold to the flap did not update that reference point.\n\nThe flap's holder was never released when the shard was grabbed. At tick 150 the seat holds the flap but lift remains stuck at 0.50.\n\nAt tick 180 the seat has moved to x=2.97, yet lift remains stuck at 0.50. The lift function does not update target.x to follow the seat; only grab() does. Since ox is set only at grab start and never moves with the seat, the pulled distance should have grown from 0.97 to 2.97 and lift should have hit 1. The fact that it did not suggests ox may somehow be tracking the seat after all.\n\nThe seat may not be targeting the flap. If nearest is the cocoon or nothing, lift() never runs. The seat holds the flap but does not lift it. use is true so the hold persists, yet lift stays frozen.\n\nThe seat is pulling away from the flap instead of toward it. The shard underneath becomes the nearest forceps target because the open flap makes it reachable. The seat switches hold to the shard, but the flap's holder stays at zero.\n\nThe grab function assigns a new holder without clearing the old one. The seat switches to the shard and stops lifting the flap, which stays open with no holder. When the seat later returns to the flap, its stale ox is far away and nearest is no longer the flap, so lift never updates again.\n\nThe lift display is stale because the lift function is not running while the nearest target is not the flap. Two fixes are needed: release the previous hold when grabbing a new target, and stop pulling a flap once lift reaches 0.8 instead of continuing indefinitely.\n\nThe bot's pull loop uses a shard-specific finish condition that does not apply to flaps. Because lift() never sets done for flaps, the seat keeps pulling indefinitely past the field edge. The fix is to drop and re-approach when lift fails to increase.\n\nThe bot should pull the flap only a short distance—about one meter from the original position—so nearest remains the flap and lift can update. The step size must be small enough to keep the seat within 0.85 of the target.\n\nThe nearest-target radius is 0.85 meters, but the forceps pull must travel 0.96 meters to reach lift 0.8. Moving one meter away from the original position therefore leaves the target out of range before lift can increase. This explains why lift froze around 0.5–0.6: the seat exited the 0.85 radius before the required distance was covered.\n\nThe chosen fix is to make lift() move the flap with the seat, just as grab() does. This keeps the nearest distance at zero and lets lift grow from the original ox as the seat moves.\n\nThe lift function now moves the target to the seat position and sets done once lift reaches 0.8. The claim helper releases any previous holder before assigning a new one, and both grab and lift will use it.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The flap stays put while the forceps walk off, so the lift freezes halfway. I’ll make a held flap follow the hand, and let go of the previous hold before grabbing something else."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b8d596d1-efda-4b9c-8738-de3a10286c2e-64","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/act.ts","old_string":"  if (target.holder >= 0 && target.holder !== seat.id) return false;\n  if (seat.hold !== target.id) {\n    if (hypot(seat.x, seat.z, target.x, target.z) > REACH) return false;\n    seat.hold = target.id;\n    target.holder = seat.id;\n    target.ox = seat.x;\n    target.oz = seat.z;\n    return true;\n  }","new_string":"  if (target.holder >= 0 && target.holder !== seat.id) return false;\n  if (seat.hold !== target.id) {\n    if (hypot(seat.x, seat.z, target.x, target.z) > REACH) return false;\n    claim(op, seat, target);\n    return true;\n  }"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b8d596d1-efda-4b9c-8738-de3a10286c2e-65","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/act.ts","old_string":"  if (seat.hold !== target.id) {\n    if (hypot(seat.x, seat.z, target.x, target.z) > REACH) return false;\n    seat.hold = target.id;\n    target.holder = seat.id;\n    target.ox = seat.x;\n    target.oz = seat.z;\n    return true;\n  }\n  const pulled = hypot(seat.x, seat.z, target.ox, target.oz);\n  target.lift = Math.min(1, pulled / op.balance.forceps);","new_string":"  if (seat.hold !== target.id) {\n    if (hypot(seat.x, seat.z, target.x, target.z) > REACH) return false;\n    claim(op, seat, target);\n    return true;\n  }\n  target.x = seat.x;\n  target.z = seat.z;\n  const pulled = hypot(seat.x, seat.z, target.ox, target.oz);\n  target.lift = Math.min(1, pulled / op.balance.forceps);"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b8d596d1-efda-4b9c-8738-de3a10286c2e-66","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/act.ts","old_string":"/** Let go of whatever the forceps hold. */\nfunction release(op: Op, seat: Seat): void {","new_string":"/** Take a target with the forceps, dropping anything this hand already held. */\nfunction claim(op: Op, seat: Seat, target: Target): void {\n  if (seat.hold >= 0 && seat.hold !== target.id) release(op, seat);\n  seat.hold = target.id;\n  target.holder = seat.id;\n  target.ox = seat.x;\n  target.oz = seat.z;\n}\n\n/** Let go of whatever the forceps hold. */\nfunction release(op: Op, seat: Seat): void {"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6647,"output_tokens":2987,"cache_read_input_tokens":169472,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"10ab915a-b237-4e2e-a814-6e571c1ecec8"}
