ext_before\":\"\\n  it('loses when slips pass the limit', () => {\\n    const op = createBare();\\n\",\"context_after\":\"  });\\n\\n  it('brings a patient back inside the green band and fails two misses', () => {\\n\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"87f280be-76cf-429b-9df3-627391a8b173"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_75","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The simulation is in good shape. Next up are the story, director, voice, sequencer, and frontend.\n\nThe remaining work is massive. I will finish the simulation first, then build the story system, sequencer, frontend, audio synthesis, and end-to-end tests.\n\nI will write the story and director modules next. The story data will contain 16 scenes with roughly 256 original lines. I am designing compact TypeScript interfaces for boxes, scenes, and the director's playStory function.\n\nThe director will walk story cases, run the bot, record postcards, and end at credits with free surgery unlocked. Voice synthesis will be deterministic using character hashes. The sequencer will simulate a host plus three clients with latency, jitter, five percent packet loss, a leaver, and matching hashes across 3600 ticks. I am also checking index.html size and engine options to prepare the page.\n\nI will run the failing test and read the engine page APIs in parallel. The hub boot order in PLAN 16 is critical for the page. This turn I will finish tests green and write the story, voice, director, sequencer, and their tests. Once those pass, the simulation, content, and bot gating items will be nearly complete.\n\nThe story file will be separate from cases.ts to keep it under 600 lines. Each scene will contain 14 boxes with earnest, short lines. Boxes will include drama flags for six to ten captioned moments like \"IT MOVED.\" The director and voice modules will live in director.ts and voice.ts.\n\nThe sequencer will live in sequencer.ts with tests in story.test.ts and sequencer.test.ts. playStory delegates to runBot so it stays fast. The sequencer will simulate network delay on hands before all peers step the same applied hands. It will use a NetHand type tracking tick, seat, hand, and reliability. A simpler design is to run four copies of the same operation.\n\nThe sequencer will use deterministic bot hands derived from a seeded formula. Each client generates identical hands because all copies share the same state. The host receives hands with latency and jitter, drops five percent of unreliable packets, and applies the last known hand or a false hand for a leaver. It then broadcasts the applied hands reliably to all clients. Everyone steps with the same hands, and the hashes are compared.\n\nThe host will generate all hands from its own state. Every peer will compute identical hands locally and send them to the host. The host applies the received hands and broadcasts the results back to all clients. This keeps every copy's state synchronized so hashes match across 3600 ticks.\n\nThe sequencer will use a sine-based seeded RNG instead of Math.random to stay deterministic. Network latency will be 3–8 ticks with ±2 jitter, and five percent of packets will be dropped. Client three will stop sending at tick 1800, so the host applies their last known hand with use false. All four copies will run the same operation—either gala or the first cut—so every hash matches after 3600 ticks.\n\nThe first-cut operation would finish in about three hundred ticks, so it is too short to test ongoing divergence. I will use a long scripted circling hand instead. The hands will move shards around in a sine wave pattern across all seats. This keeps the simulation running for all three thousand six hundred ticks. Hashes include positions, so any missed hand will cause divergence.\n\nThe sequencer will use a concrete scripted hand formula with sine and cosine positions, periodic tool changes, and intermittent presses. Tool indices must be sent as absolute values because applyHands only updates the tool when it differs. The client-server flow is now fully defined: each peer sends its local intent, the host applies delayed or lost packets using the last known hand, then broadcasts the assembled hands reliably for all peers to step.\n\nHashes will be compared at the exact tick each peer receives its host command, not wall time. Each peer buffers incoming hands and steps only when that tick arrives. The leaver's last known hand is broadcast to all peers as a substitute, so every copy applies the same sequence of 3600 commands.\n\nThe test will assert that the host command log contains exactly 3600 entries, all four peers reach the same hash at tick 3600, and a peer that applied a different hand would diverge. It will also verify the leaver’s use flag is false after they stop sending, and that some packets were dropped.\n\nI will also test the sequencer with clients stepping independently under delayed delivery. I am drafting the story file now, using a compact scene builder to keep the 224 lines manageable.\n\nThe slip test is already fixed. The director will expose a `playThrough` function that runs each story case through the bot and records the result in a `StorySave` object. It will throw if any case fails to win.\n\nThe `playThrough` function will collect postcards and mark cases cleared, then set credits, free surgery, and attending flags. Content tests will verify eight cases contain the rules, scenes span twelve to thirty-five boxes, postcards exist, voice synthesis is deterministic, and no banned words appear. I will write the story carefully but not linger on literary quality, and I will update the todos.\n\nScene IDs will run from before-1 to after-8, matching the case storyBefore and storyAfter strings. Each box will hold a speaker, text, and an optional drama flag. The voice hash will use a deterministic FNV-1a algorithm over character codes of both the character name and the line text.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The bot clears every required case. Four sim checks were failing because the practice field ended early; I’ll fix those and add the story, the director, and the lockstep sequencer."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-94cd5ce2-7530-45bf-acf7-adb7301710f6-91","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/story.ts","new_string":"/**\n * @file The campaign's scenes. Each one is a run of short boxes, twelve to thirty-five, said out loud over captions.\n * A drama box is a snapped close-up and a caption. Nothing here is quoted from another game.\n */\nexport interface Box {\n  who: string;\n  text: string;\n  /** A huge caption, when this beat is a drama cut. */\n  drama?: string;\n}\n\n/** One skippable scene. */\nexport interface Scene {\n  id: string;\n  where: string;\n  boxes: Box[];\n}\n\n/** `WHO: line` or `WHO: line :: CAPTION`. */\nfunction boxes(lines: readonly string[]): Box[] {\n  return lines.map((line) => {\n    const cut = line.indexOf(' :: ');\n    const body = cut === -1 ? line : line.slice(0, cut);\n    const speaker = body.indexOf(': ');\n    return {\n      who: body.slice(0, speaker),\n      text: body.slice(speaker + 2),\n      ...(cut === -1 ? {} : { drama: line.slice(cut + 4) }),\n    };\n  });\n}\n\n/** Every story scene, in the order the director plays them. */\nexport const SCENES: readonly Scene[] = [\n  {\n    id: 'before-1',\n    where: 'Harbor Light, night',\n    boxes: boxes([\n      'ODIE: Congratulations, Doctor. You are the only surgeon in the building.',\n      'WREN: The storm took the bridge. I can hear the glass in it.',\n      'ODIE: And the ad. Turn that down before it turns you.',\n      'VOSS: Pain is just a feeling you have not paid to remove yet.',\n      'WREN: Halcyon. Because you deserve to feel nothing. Who bought that line?',\n      'ODIE: Everyone with a wallet. Tomás Reyes is on table one. Deck hatch. Glass.',\n      'WREN: Is he awake?',\n      'ODIE: Awake enough to ask after a dog. The dog is in the corridor, against every rule I have.',\n      'WREN: Leave the dog. I will be quick.',\n      'ODIE: You will be careful. Quick is how people become stories.',\n      'WREN: Drain, forceps, suture. I have had the lecture.',\n      'ODIE: Then give it back to me with your hands. Vitals are seventy and rude about it.',\n      'WREN: Sorry. I say that to them even when they cannot hear.',\n      'ODIE: Good. Start with the water. The glass can wait its turn.',\n    ]),\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'after-1',\n    where: 'The corridor',\n    boxes: boxes([\n      'ODIE: He is breathing like a man who intends to keep the habit.',\n      'WREN: The dog is still here.',\n      'ODIE: I am looking at the chart. I see no dog. Charts are famous for this.',\n      'WREN: Tomás. Your dog stayed. I told him you were busy.',\n      'TOMAS: He waits out storms. He is better at it than I am.',\n      'ODIE: Visiting hours were cancelled by the weather. Do not quote me.',\n      'WREN: I nicked nothing I meant to leave. I think.',\n      'ODIE: In this hallway, \"I think\" is how you ask me to count again. I counted. He is fine.',\n      'WREN: The ad is still playing in the ward.',\n      'ODIE: Let it. Tired people buy quiet. We sell the other thing, which is work.',\n      'WREN: I should write the closure note.',\n      'ODIE: You should eat. The note can be brilliant on a full stomach.',\n      'TOMAS: Tell the dog he can come up. Just for a minute. I will pretend it was clinical.',\n      'WREN: One minute. Then I am a doctor again.',\n    ]),\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'before-2',\n    where: 'A quiet bay',\n    boxes: boxes([\n      'GWEN: If you drop a trumpet in a harbor it plays one note and then it is a trumpet for crabs.',\n      'WREN: Gwen Abara. It says cyst. It says you play.',\n      'GWEN: I play. The cyst is a rumour my scar started.',\n      'ODIE: Old graft, lip, two years ago. Halcyon. She showed me the brochure like it was a medal.',\n      'GWEN: It was a medal. I sang the week after. High C, rude and shiny.',\n      'WREN: And now it pulls?',\n      'GWEN: When the weather does. Or when I laugh. Today I did both, so here we are.',\n      'ODIE: Routine. Scanner if the lump is shy. Laser if it is not. You have done harder things before breakfast.',\n      'WREN: I had no breakfast.',\n      'ODIE: Then you have done harder things before coffee, which is the same tragedy.',\n      'GWEN: Do not take the note. Take the lump. I can find another note.',\n      'WREN: I will talk to you the whole time. You will not hear it. I do it anyway.',\n      'ODIE: Scalpel on the line. If you wander, I will say your name the way my mother did.',\n      'WREN: That is the most frightening instrument in the room.',\n    ]),\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'after-2',\n    where: 'The scrub room',\n    boxes: boxes([\n      'WREN: It moved. :: IT MOVED.',\n      'ODIE: I saw it. Do not perform that sentence for the corridor.',\n      'WREN: A cyst does not flinch when the forceps close.',\n      'ODIE: A cyst does not do anything. That is the appeal of cysts.',\n      'WREN: So what do I write?',\n      'ODIE: You write cyst. You sleep. You and I remember the other word and we do not spend it yet.',\n      'WREN: If I write cyst, I am lying.',\n      'ODIE: If you write monster, you are unemployed and she is a rumour. Give me one night.',\n      'WREN: She asked if she could play tomorrow.',\n      'ODIE: Tell her yes. Be right about that part.',\n      'WREN: The scar looked like a smile that had changed its mind.',\n      'ODIE: Poetic. Keep it out of the chart.',\n      'WREN: I want a second look. Not a committee. A person.',\n      'ODIE: Then find one who is not paid by the people who made the smile.',\n    ]),\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'before-3',\n    where: 'Emergency, overflow',\n    boxes: boxes([\n      'CHIEF: Breakwater Road is in my emergency room. Try not to add yourself to it.',\n      'WREN: How many?',\n      'CHIEF: One for you. Hal Minsky. Bus driver. Liver, lung, arm. The bus is not your patient, whatever the radio says.',\n      'ODIE: Three sites. They bleed while you are elsewhere. That is not a metaphor.',\n      'WREN: I have not run three sites.',\n      'CHIEF: In my operating room, \"I have not\" is a cause of death. You have now.',\n      'WREN: His route?',\n      'ODIE: Four. He said the number twice before the drugs took the rest.',\n      'CHIEF: If he dies, you will know which part you were not standing on. Go and stand on all of them.',\n      'WREN: And if the line goes flat?',\n      'ODIE: Then you are in a Code. Green band. Two tries. I will count so you do not have to be brave and numerate at once.',\n      'WREN: What if there is no time left for the arteries?',\n      'ODIE: Then we find time. Do not ask me how until you need it.',\n      'CHIEF: Finish, Doctor. Feeling is what the waiting room is for.',\n    ]),\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'after-3',\n    where: 'Outside theatre',\n    boxes: boxes([\n      'WREN: Something happened in there. The room got slow and my hands did not.',\n      'ODIE: You were fast. Do not make it weird.',\n      'WREN: I could hear the monitor like it was under water, and then I was ahead of it.',\n      'ODIE: Stillpoint. That is the word you are chewing. Spit it out or swallow it. Not both.',\n      'WREN: Is it a real word?',\n      'ODIE: It is today. Hal is alive. The arm will argue with him for a month and then do as it is told.',\n      'WREN: The Chief watched.',\n      'ODIE: The Chief watches the way a cliff watches. It is not a compliment and it is not an attack.',\n      'WREN: I want to tell him about the slowing.',\n      'ODIE: You want to be believed. Those are different errands. Run the second one later.',\n      'WREN: Route four. He will be angry about the timetable.',\n      'ODIE: Good. Angry people get on buses. Write the note. Eat the soup. Stop discovering powers in the corridor.',\n      'WREN: I am not discovering. I am reporting.',\n      'ODIE: Then report it to me, quietly, where it cannot get you suspended before pudding.',\n    ]),\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'before-4',\n    where: 'The gallery',\n    boxes: boxes([\n      'GWEN: It is moving. I would like to be wrong in public. :: THE SCAR MOVES.',\n      'WREN: You are not wrong. I am sorry. That is a bad sentence to be right about.',\n      'CHIEF: A surgeon does not feel. A surgeon finishes. Kindly do the second one where I can see it.',\n      'ODIE: He is in the gallery. He brought his moustache and his opinions, which are the same size.',\n      'WREN: Gwen. Your trumpet is in the nurses\\' station. Nobody will tune it.',\n      'GWEN: If I do not wake up, give it to someone who will play it badly. Badly is honest.',\n      'ODIE: Three of them, if the chart is telling the truth. They are quiet. Quiet is the nasty kind.',\n      'WREN: Laser. Then the little shell they leave. Then whatever is wearing them.',\n      'CHIEF: You saw a twitch, Doctor, at a bad hour. Do not build a theology out of a twitch.',\n      'WREN: I built a retractor out of one. Watch.',\n      'ODIE: Binder for the big one. She only opens her mouth to yawn. Be there when she does.',\n      'WREN: And if the Chief is right?',\n      'ODIE: Then you did a tidy operation and I will buy you a bun. I am not worried about the bun.',\n      'GWEN: Tell me when it is out. Use small words. I will be under, but I am superstitious about tenses.',\n    ]),\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'after-4',\n    where: 'The chief\\'s office',\n    boxes: boxes([\n      'CHIEF: The sample is gone. :: SAMPLE GONE.',\n      'WREN: I put it in the tray. I labelled it with her name, not mine.',\n      'CHIEF: Halcyon\\'s lawyers have the tray. They also have a story in which you were tired.',\n      'ODIE: He is suspending you. He is using his gentle voice, which is how you know.',\n      'CHIEF: You saw a twitch, Doctor, at hour nineteen of a shift. Get a second opinion. If you can find a fool to give one.',\n      'WREN: Gwen is alive.',\n      'CHIEF: Alive is not a diagnosis. It is a courtesy. Go home.',\n      'WREN: You have a scar under that collar.',\n      'CHIEF: And you have a career, briefly. Do not spend it on my neck.',\n      'ODIE: Outside. Now. Before you say the true thing at the wrong volume.',\n      'WREN: I need the name of the woman they struck off.',\n      'ODIE: Sabine Oyelaran. A ship, not a hospital. If you go, you are done being comfortable.',\n      'WREN: I was not good at comfortable.',\n      'ODIE: I noticed. Take a coat. The harbour does not care that you were right.',\n    ]),\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'before-5',\n    where: 'The hospital ship',\n    boxes: boxes([\n      'SABINE: Everyone agreed I was wrong. That is what consensus feels like from the inside.',\n      'WREN: Dr. Oyelaran. I brought a story and a bad coat.',\n      'SABINE: I am not a doctor on this deck. I am the person who still owns a lamp. Talk fast. The weather is working.',\n      'WREN: A graft flinched. Then it had children. The Chief called it a twitch and took my name off the door.',\n      'SABINE: Halcyon. They did the same to the trials. Smiled, filed, sailed.',\n      'ANA: I am not a trial. I am a stevedore and I am going over. :: ON THE DECK.',\n      'SABINE: Big Ana. Winch crew. Get her on the table before the ship rolls her off it.',\n      'WREN: I do not have privileges here.',\n      'SABINE: You have hands. I have a drug they did not put in your textbook. Second Pulse. It keeps the numbers from falling while you work.',\n      'WREN: And the roll?',\n      'SABINE: The roll is the sea, pretending to be a critic. Ignore the critic.',\n      'ODIE: I came because somebody has to count. Do not look surprised. I hate boats. I hate lawyers more.',\n      'WREN: There is a flap. Something warm is under it.',\n      'SABINE: Then we do not give it the laser until it is small enough to deserve one. Cut it in half. Then in half again.',\n    ]),\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'after-5',\n    where: 'The galley',\n    boxes: boxes([\n      'SABINE: I am not a doctor anymore, Dr. Tolliver. I am a second opinion.',\n      'WREN: Ana will shout at the winch by morning. That is her version of a thank-you.',\n      'ODIE: The samples match. Yours and the one Sabine kept in a coffee tin, which is not a protocol I will be writing up.',\n      'SABINE: Solace. That is what they called this one, because the brochure needed a spa.',\n      'WREN: It hugged the vessel like it was cold.',\n      'SABINE: It is cold. It wants heat. The laser is a kiss it has not earned until the third splitting.',\n      'ODIE: The Chief\\'s scar. You said collar. Sabine, tell her she is not the only one who noticed necks.',\n      'SABINE: Bram Achterberg signed the early sheets. I watched his hand. It did not shake. I think about that more than I sleep.',\n      'WREN: If he is carrying one, he will not come to us.',\n      'SABINE: Then we wait until his body files the complaint his mouth will not.',\n      'ODIE: That is a grim timetable. I prefer buses.',\n      'WREN: My hands shook. On the deck.',\n      'SABINE: Your hands are shaking. Then that is new. Use it. Shaking is a kind of attention.',\n      'WREN: I will. And I will not call you anything you did not ask for.',\n    ]),\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'before-6',\n    where: 'A boardroom, then a bay',\n    boxes: boxes([\n      'CHIEF: Not here. Not in front of them. :: THE COLLAR OPENS.',\n      'ODIE: He tore the collar himself. There is a scar under it and it is not old enough.',\n      'WREN: Dr. Achterberg. Look at me. You are the patient now. The title can sit in the hall.',\n      'CHIEF: I signed the trial. I would like to finish a sentence before your friend with the coat does.',\n      'SABINE: Your friend with the coat is already here. Two sites. Chest and abdomen. We can swap if your hands want a different sin.',\n      'WREN: There is something under the sheet. It moves when the monitor does.',\n      'ODIE: Reverie. Scanner first. The decoys pop. The real one keeps time with him, which is vain and useful.',\n      'CHIEF: If you find it, do not lecture me while you burn it. I am very fast at lectures. You would lose.',\n      'WREN: I am not here to win against you.',\n      'SABINE: Consult, if we both spend the gift. Two opinions, one extra stretch of time. Try not to enjoy the metaphor.',\n      'ODIE: Vitals sixty-five. He is embarrassed, which is not a vital, but it is doing a lot of work.',\n      'WREN: Sir. I am sorry. I am going to say that through the whole operation. It is a habit, not a verdict.',\n      'CHIEF: Accepted. Now finish. A surgeon finishes. I was right about that part and wrong about the rest.',\n      'SABINE: On your mark. I have the abdomen. Shout if the sheet breathes.',\n    ]),\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'after-6',\n    where: 'A side room',\n    boxes: boxes([\n      'CHIEF: I signed them all. :: I SIGNED THEM.',\n      'WREN: The files.',\n      'CHIEF: Top drawer. The key is the ugly one. I kept it on the ring so I would feel it every day and I still signed.',\n      'SABINE: Gala access. He really did mean to confess. I hate that it makes me gentler.',\n      'ODIE: Gentler is allowed. Soft is not. Read the files standing up.',\n      'CHIEF: Voss will be on a screen the size of a mistake. The donors paid for the wing. The wing is where they will fall, if the batches match.',\n      'WREN: Then we will be in the wing.',\n      'CHIEF: You are suspended.',\n      'ODIE: She is suspended in a building that is about to need her. I can live with the paperwork.',\n      'SABINE: Two of us. Swap when the site changes. Do not be noble about who holds the knife.',\n      'WREN: What do I call you now?',\n      'CHIEF: Bram, if I live. Doctor, if you need the distance. I have earned the distance.',\n      'ODIE: He will live. I have decided. My decisions have a good record today.',\n      'WREN: Then we go to the gala. I am not dressing up.',\n    ]),\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'before-7',\n    where: 'The new wing',\n    boxes: boxes([\n      'VOSS: Welcome to the part of the hospital that thanks you properly.',\n      'ODIE: Three tables. Three donors. One speech that will not stop for haemorrhage. :: THEY ARE FALLING.',\n      'WREN: Maris, Owen, Safiya. I read the place cards like a triage list, which is what they are now.',\n      'SABINE: Balm. It spreads like a varnish and then the thread will not hold. Gel the cells. Two doses in the node.',\n      'WREN: If one of them dies, the night is a loss. He will call it a fainting on the news.',\n      'ODIE: Then none of them die. I have reserved the right to be impossible.',\n      'VOSS: Pain is a rumour spread by people who have not met my product.',\n      'SABINE: His product is on their skin. Wren, Second Pulse when the bars start to race. I will take table C.',\n      'WREN: The colleague on the drains. Odie, if I look at the screen, say my name.',\n      'ODIE: Wren. See how good I am at it already.',\n      'WREN: Sorry, Maris. You cannot hear me. Your pledge is not the thing I am here to collect.',\n      'SABINE: Nodes first. Film fades. Then the blood, which has been patient and should not have had to be.',\n      'ODIE: Voss is still smiling. I want that on the record as a complaint.',\n      'WREN: Begin. Tables A, B, and C. Nobody leaves in the middle of a toast.',\n    ]),\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'after-7',\n    where: 'Under the screen',\n    boxes: boxes([\n      'ODIE: All three. Breathing. Annoyed. I will take annoyed.',\n      'MARIS: I am cancelling the pledge. Spend it on gloves.',\n      'OWEN: Did the chandelier do that on purpose?',\n      'SAFIYA: I was mid-sentence. I would like the second half to be different.',\n      'WREN: You will have it. Not tonight. Tonight you lie still and dislike us in comfort.',\n      'VOSS: And if you have ever felt too much, ask yourself who sold you that— :: HE FALLS.',\n      'SABINE: He fell on his own product. I want to be kinder than I am and I am not there yet.',\n      'ODIE: Get him on a trolley. The speech can finish without a face.',\n      'WREN: It is in him. The same quiet. I can see it from here and I hate that I can.',\n      'SABINE: Then the last table is his. You know what Odie will say before you ask.',\n      'ODIE: We could be slow, Doctor. Nobody would know.',\n      'WREN: I would.',\n      'SABINE: Good. Bring him. I am not dressing his conscience. I am keeping the engine running.',\n      'ODIE: I will count for him too. I resent it. I will do it anyway.',\n    ]),\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'before-8',\n    where: 'Theatre one',\n    boxes: boxes([\n      'VOSS: This is a misunderstanding. I sell the absence of nights like this.',\n      'WREN: You are on the table. The misunderstanding can wait in the hall.',\n      'ODIE: Mercy. That is the name on the batch in his chest. They really do not hear themselves.',\n      'SABINE: Three movements. Motes, then she stops the heart on purpose, then she tries to live in it. We answer all three.',\n      'WREN: Every tool. I want them where my hands already know the order.',\n      'ODIE: We could be slow. I said it. I will not say it again. You answered.',\n      'VOSS: If I die, the city loses a great deal of optimism.',\n      'WREN: If you die, the city loses a man. I am not operating on the optimism.',\n      'SABINE: Anesthesia first. Burn the motes. When she opens, the binder, three times, inside the gift if the last movement demands it.',\n      'ODIE: Codes when she asks for them. Land the green. Do not show off.',\n      'WREN: Lucan. I am sorry. I will keep saying it. It does not make you clean. It makes me accurate.',\n      'SABINE: I have the second pair of hands. Swap if you freeze. Freezing is information. Use it and move.',\n      'ODIE: Vitals one hundred. She has not started. The hymn is going to be unpleasant.',\n      'WREN: Then we play a louder one. Begin.',\n    ]),\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'after-8',\n    where: 'Dawn, the ward',\n    boxes: boxes([\n      'VOSS: You saved me. That is the one thing I could never have sold.',\n      'WREN: The cuffs were not my department. The heart was. Both seem to be holding.',\n      'ODIE: Tomás sent a card. Gwen sent a recording of your name, played badly on purpose. I am framing the intent, not the pitch.',\n      'SABINE: Hal waved at the building from the bus. Ana threatened a winch and then smiled, which I am told is rare and expensive.',\n      'CHIEF: The files are copied. I will say the sentence in a room with a stenographer. I am tired of rooms without one.',\n      'MARIS: The wing can keep its name. I am keeping my pulse. We are not even.',\n      'WREN: I thought there would be a last patient and then a locked door.',\n      'ODIE: There is a manifest. A crate. Already at sea. :: CASE FILE REMAINS OPEN.',\n      'SABINE: Then we are not finished. We are between pages. Doctors know that shape.',\n      'WREN: Free surgery. Anyone who comes. The board stays up.',\n      'ODIE: And you will eat before the next one. This is now a clinical order.',\n      'VOSS: I will testify. Do not thank me. Thank the part of the night that was not for sale.',\n      'WREN: I was never going to thank you. I am glad you are alive to be difficult.',\n      'ODIE: Credits, then. Names, then the door. The harbour is still there. So are we.',\n    ]),\n  },\n];\n\n/** The scene with this id. */\nexport function sceneById(id: string): Scene | undefined {\n  return SCENES.find((scene) => scene.id === id);\n}\n","old_string":""}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-94cd5ce2-7530-45bf-acf7-adb7301710f6-92","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/voice.ts","new_string":"/**\n * @file Gibberish voices. Each character of a line picks one of sixteen syllables. The pick is a pure function of\n * the speaker and the character, so the same line always barks the same way. No samples, no files.\n */\n\n/** Sixteen mouth-shapes. The page plays them. The index is the whole contract. */\nexport const SYLLABLES = ['ba', 'ke', 'mi', 'to', 'ra', 'lu', 'ne', 'shi', 'ko', 'va', 'di', 'fu', 'pe', 'zo', 'ha', 'ri'] as const;\n\n/** FNV-1a over a string, unsigned. */\nfunction fnv(text: string, seed = 2166136261): number {\n  let hash = seed >>> 0;\n  for (let i = 0; i < text.length; i++) {\n    hash ^= text.charCodeAt(i);\n    hash = Math.imul(hash, 16777619);\n  }\n  return hash >>> 0;\n}\n\n/** Syllable indexes for one line, speaker included so two people never share a mouth by accident. */\nexport function voiceOf(who: string, text: string): number[] {\n  const salt = fnv(who);\n  const out: number[] = [];\n  for (let i = 0; i < text.length; i++) out.push(fnv(text[i] + String(i), salt) % SYLLABLES.length);\n  return out;\n}\n\n/** The same line joined, for a quick equality check. */\nexport function voiceKey(who: string, text: string): string {\n  return voiceOf(who, text).join('.');\n}\n","old_string":""}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-94cd5ce2-7530-45bf-acf7-adb7301710f6-93","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/director.ts","new_string":"/**\n * @file The campaign with no browser. Title, eight scenes, eight operations, debrief, credits, then Free Surgery.\n * The bot plays each case from that case's own start. The save at the end is what the Board would have written.\n */\nimport { runBot } from './bot';\nimport { storyCases } from './cases';\nimport { rankFor } from './ratings';\nimport { SCENES, sceneById } from './story';\nimport type { Difficulty, Rank } from './types';\nimport { createFromCase } from './world';\n\n/** What a finished shift remembers. */\nexport interface Through {\n  scenes: string[];\n  /** Case id, then the rank the debrief would show. */\n  ranks: { id: string; rank: Rank; score: number }[];\n  postcards: string[];\n  credits: boolean;\n  free: boolean;\n  attending: boolean;\n}\n\n/** Walk the whole story on one difficulty. Throws if a case does not clear, because the credits are not a consolation. */\nexport function playThrough(difficulty: Difficulty = 'resident', seed = 1): Through {\n  const scenes: string[] = [];\n  const ranks: Through['ranks'] = [];\n  const postcards: string[] = [];\n  for (const def of storyCases()) {\n    const before = sceneById(def.storyBefore);\n    const after = sceneById(def.storyAfter);\n    if (!before || !after) throw new Error(`Missing scene for ${def.id}`);\n    scenes.push(before.id);\n    const op = createFromCase(def.id, { difficulty, seed });\n    runBot(op);\n    if (op.status !== 'won') throw new Error(`${def.id} ${op.fail}`);\n    const rank = rankFor(op.score, def.par, op.slips, difficulty);\n    ranks.push({ id: def.id, rank, score: op.score });\n    const letter = rank === '★' || rank === 'S' ? 'S' : rank;\n    postcards.push(def.patients[0].postcards[letter]);\n    scenes.push(after.id);\n  }\n  if (!SCENES.some((scene) => scene.boxes.some((box) => box.drama === 'CASE FILE REMAINS OPEN'))) {\n    throw new Error('The last beat is missing');\n  }\n  return { scenes, ranks, postcards, credits: true, free: true, attending: true };\n}\n","old_string":""}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-94cd5ce2-7530-45bf-acf7-adb7301710f6-94","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/sequencer.ts","new_string":"/**\n * @file Host lockstep without a socket. Four copies, delayed intents, loss on the way to the host, one leaver.\n * The host's applied hands are what every copy steps. After the run, the hashes for each applied tick agree.\n */\nimport { stepOp, lastHash } from './step';\nimport type { Hand, Op } from './types';\nimport { createBare, idleHand } from './world';\n\n/** A roll in 0..1 from the tick and the seat, with no Math.random. */\nfunction roll(tick: number, seat: number): number {\n  const x = Math.sin(tick * 12.9898 + seat * 78.233) * 43758.5453;\n  return x - Math.floor(x);\n}\n\n/** What one surgeon meant to do on one tick. Pure, so every copy would have sent the same intent. */\nexport function intentAt(tick: number, seat: number, hand: Hand): Hand {\n  const angle = tick / 18 + seat;\n  return {\n    ...hand,\n    x: Math.sin(angle) * (1.4 + seat * 0.15),\n    z: Math.cos(angle * 0.8) * 0.9,\n    tool: Math.floor(tick / 90 + seat) % 8,\n    use: tick % 37 < 8,\n    gift: false,\n    paddle: false,\n    drop: false,\n    site: -1,\n    swap: false,\n    hint: false,\n  };\n}\n\n/** One peer's view of the operation. */\ninterface Peer {\n  op: Op;\n  /** Last intent that actually reached the host, per seat. */\n  last: Hand[];\n  /** Hash after each applied tick. */\n  hashes: string[];\n}\n\n/** Run the lockstep. Returns the peers so a test can read the hashes. */\nexport function runLockstep(ticks = 3600, seats = 4): { peers: Peer[]; dropped: number; leftAt: number } {\n  const peers: Peer[] = [];\n  for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) {\n    const op = createBare({ seats, code: false });\n    addAnchor(op);\n    peers.push({ op, last: op.seats.map((seat) => idleHand(seat)), hashes: [] });\n  }\n  const host = peers[0];\n  let dropped = 0;\n  const leftAt = Math.floor(ticks / 2);\n  const delay = 4;\n  /** Intents in flight: tick they were sent, seat, hand, and whether the wire kept them. */\n  const wire: { arrive: number; seat: number; hand: Hand }[] = [];\n  for (let tick = 0; tick < ticks; tick++) {\n    for (let seat = 0; seat < seats; seat++) {\n      if (seat === seats - 1 && tick >= leftAt) continue;\n      const hand = intentAt(tick, seat, host.last[seat]);\n      const lost = roll(tick, seat) < 0.05;\n      if (lost) {\n        dropped += 1;\n        continue;\n      }\n      const jitter = Math.floor(roll(tick, seat + 3) * 3);\n      wire.push({ arrive: tick + delay + jitter, seat, hand });\n    }\n    const applied = host.last.map((hand) => ({ ...hand, use: false }));\n    for (let i = wire.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {\n      const packet = wire[i];\n      if (packet.arrive > tick) continue;\n      applied[packet.seat] = packet.hand;\n      host.last[packet.seat] = packet.hand;\n      wire.splice(i, 1);\n    }\n    for (const peer of peers) {\n      stepOp(peer.op, applied);\n      peer.hashes.push(lastHash(peer.op));\n    }\n  }\n  return { peers, dropped, leftAt };\n}\n\n/** A target that keeps the bare operation from ending the moment it starts. */\nfunction addAnchor(op: Op): void {\n  op.targets.push({\n    ...op.targets[0],\n    id: op.nextId,\n    kind: 'mass',\n    x: 6,\n    z: 4,\n    done: false,\n    hidden: true,\n    locked: true,\n    phase: 0,\n    optional: false,\n  });\n  op.nextId += 1;\n}\n","old_string":""}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":912,"output_tokens":11179,"cache_read_input_tokens":201984,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"bbdea1fb-21df-4630-a7b9-6d8bd5b9936b"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-94cd5ce2-7530-45bf-acf7-adb7301710f6-91","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"/**\\n * @file The campaign's scenes. Each one is a run of short boxes, twelve to thirty-five, said out loud over captions.\\n * A drama box is a snapped close-up and a caption. Nothing here is quoted from another game.\\n */\\nexport interface Box {\\n  who: string;\\n  text: string;\\n  /** A huge caption, when this beat is a drama cut. */\\n  drama?: string;\\n}\\n\\n/** One skippable scene. */\\nexport interface Scene {\\n  id: string;\\n  where: string;\\n  boxes: Box[];\\n}\\n\\n/** `WHO: line` or `WHO: line :: CAPTION`. */\\nfunction boxes(lines: readonly string[]): Box[] {\\n  return lines.map((line) => {\\n    const cut = line.indexOf(' :: ');\\n    const body = cut === -1 ? line : line.slice(0, cut);\\n    const speaker = body.indexOf(': ');\\n    return {\\n      who: body.slice(0, speaker),\\n      text: body.slice(speaker + 2),\\n      ...(cut === -1 ? {} : { drama: line.slice(cut + 4) }),\\n    };\\n  });\\n}\\n\\n/** Every story scene, in the order the director plays them. */\\nexport const SCENES: readonly Scene[] = [\\n  {\\n    id: 'before-1',\\n    where: 'Harbor Light, night',\\n    boxes: boxes([\\n      'ODIE: Congratulations, Doctor. You are the only surgeon in the building.',\\n      'WREN: The storm took the bridge. I can hear the glass in it.',\\n      'ODIE: And the ad. Turn that down before it turns you.',\\n      'VOSS: Pain is just a feeling you have not paid to remove yet.',\\n      'WREN: Halcyon. Because you deserve to feel nothing. Who bought that line?',\\n      'ODIE: Everyone with a wallet. Tomás Reyes is on table one. Deck hatch. Glass.',\\n      'WREN: Is he awake?',\\n      'ODIE: Awake enough to ask after a dog. The dog is in the corridor, against every rule I have.',\\n      'WREN: Leave the dog. I will be quick.',\\n      'ODIE: You will be careful. Quick is how people become stories.',\\n      'WREN: Drain, forceps, suture. I have had the lecture.',\\n      'ODIE: Then give it back to me with your hands. Vitals are seventy and rude about it.',\\n      'WREN: Sorry. I say that to them even when they cannot hear.',\\n      'ODIE: Good. Start with the water. The glass can wait its turn.',\\n    ]),\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'after-1',\\n    where: 'The corridor',\\n    boxes: boxes([\\n      'ODIE: He is breathing like a man who intends to keep the habit.',\\n      'WREN: The dog is still here.',\\n      'ODIE: I am looking at the chart. I see no dog. Charts are famous for this.',\\n      'WREN: Tomás. Your dog stayed. I told him you were busy.',\\n      'TOMAS: He waits out storms. He is better at it than I am.',\\n      'ODIE: Visiting hours were cancelled by the weather. Do not quote me.',\\n      'WREN: I nicked nothing I meant to leave. I think.',\\n      'ODIE: In this hallway, \\\"I think\\\" is how you ask me to count again. I counted. He is fine.',\\n      'WREN: The ad is still playing in the ward.',\\n      'ODIE: Let it. Tired people buy quiet. We sell the other thing, which is work.',\\n      'WREN: I should write the closure note.',\\n      'ODIE: You should eat. The note can be brilliant on a full stomach.',\\n      'TOMAS: Tell the dog he can come up. Just for a minute. I will pretend it was clinical.',\\n      'WREN: One minute. Then I am a doctor again.',\\n    ]),\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'before-2',\\n    where: 'A quiet bay',\\n    boxes: boxes([\\n      'GWEN: If you drop a trumpet in a harbor it plays one note and then it is a trumpet for crabs.',\\n      'WREN: Gwen Abara. It says cyst. It says you play.',\\n      'GWEN: I play. The cyst is a rumour my scar started.',\\n      'ODIE: Old graft, lip, two years ago. Halcyon. She showed me the brochure like it was a medal.',\\n      'GWEN: It was a medal. I sang the week after. High C, rude and shiny.',\\n      'WREN: And now it pulls?',\\n      'GWEN: When the weather does. Or when I laugh. Today I did both, so here we are.',\\n      'ODIE: Routine. Scanner if the lump is shy. Laser if it is not. You have done harder things before breakfast.',\\n      'WREN: I had no breakfast.',\\n      'ODIE: Then you have done harder things before coffee, which is the same tragedy.',\\n      'GWEN: Do not take the note. Take the lump. I can find another note.',\\n      'WREN: I will talk to you the whole time. You will not hear it. I do it anyway.',\\n      'ODIE: Scalpel on the line. If you wander, I will say your name the way my mother did.',\\n      'WREN: That is the most frightening instrument in the room.',\\n    ]),\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'after-2',\\n    where: 'The scrub room',\\n    boxes: boxes([\\n      'WREN: It moved. :: IT MOVED.',\\n      'ODIE: I saw it. Do not perform that sentence for the corridor.',\\n      'WREN: A cyst does not flinch when the forceps close.',\\n      'ODIE: A cyst does not do anything. That is the appeal of cysts.',\\n      'WREN: So what do I write?',\\n      'ODIE: You write cyst. You sleep. You and I remember the other word and we do not spend it yet.',\\n      'WREN: If I write cyst, I am lying.',\\n      'ODIE: If you write monster, you are unemployed and she is a rumour. Give me one night.',\\n      'WREN: She asked if she could play tomorrow.',\\n      'ODIE: Tell her yes. Be right about that part.',\\n      'WREN: The scar looked like a smile that had changed its mind.',\\n      'ODIE: Poetic. Keep it out of the chart.',\\n      'WREN: I want a second look. Not a committee. A person.',\\n      'ODIE: Then find one who is not paid by the people who made the smile.',\\n    ]),\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'before-3',\\n    where: 'Emergency, overflow',\\n    boxes: boxes([\\n      'CHIEF: Breakwater Road is in my emergency room. Try not to add yourself to it.',\\n      'WREN: How many?',\\n      'CHIEF: One for you. Hal Minsky. Bus driver. Liver, lung, arm. The bus is not your patient, whatever the radio says.',\\n      'ODIE: Three sites. They bleed while you are elsewhere. That is not a metaphor.',\\n      'WREN: I have not run three sites.',\\n      'CHIEF: In my operating room, \\\"I have not\\\" is a cause of death. You have now.',\\n      'WREN: His route?',\\n      'ODIE: Four. He said the number twice before the drugs took the rest.',\\n      'CHIEF: If he dies, you will know which part you were not standing on. Go and stand on all of them.',\\n      'WREN: And if the line goes flat?',\\n      'ODIE: Then you are in a Code. Green band. Two tries. I will count so you do not have to be brave and numerate at once.',\\n      'WREN: What if there is no time left for the arteries?',\\n      'ODIE: Then we find time. Do not ask me how until you need it.',\\n      'CHIEF: Finish, Doctor. Feeling is what the waiting room is for.',\\n    ]),\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'after-3',\\n    where: 'Outside theatre',\\n    boxes: boxes([\\n      'WREN: Something happened in there. The room got slow and my hands did not.',\\n      'ODIE: You were fast. Do not make it weird.',\\n      'WREN: I could hear the monitor like it was under water, and then I was ahead of it.',\\n      'ODIE: Stillpoint. That is the word you are chewing. Spit it out or swallow it. Not both.',\\n      'WREN: Is it a real word?',\\n      'ODIE: It is today. Hal is alive. The arm will argue with him for a month and then do as it is told.',\\n      'WREN: The Chief watched.',\\n      'ODIE: The Chief watches the way a cliff watches. It is not a compliment and it is not an attack.',\\n      'WREN: I want to tell him about the slowing.',\\n      'ODIE: You want to be believed. Those are different errands. Run the second one later.',\\n      'WREN: Route four. He will be angry about the timetable.',\\n      'ODIE: Good. Angry people get on buses. Write the note. Eat the soup. Stop discovering powers in the corridor.',\\n      'WREN: I am not discovering. I am reporting.',\\n      'ODIE: Then report it to me, quietly, where it cannot get you suspended before pudding.',\\n    ]),\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'before-4',\\n    where: 'The gallery',\\n    boxes: boxes([\\n      'GWEN: It is moving. I would like to be wrong in public. :: THE SCAR MOVES.',\\n      'WREN: You are not wrong. I am sorry. That is a bad sentence to be right about.',\\n      'CHIEF: A surgeon does not feel. A surgeon finishes. Kindly do the second one where I can see it.',\\n      'ODIE: He is in the gallery. He brought his moustache and his opinions, which are the same size.',\\n      'WREN: Gwen. Your trumpet is in the nurses\\\\' station. Nobody will tune it.',\\n      'GWEN: If I do not wake up, give it to someone who will play it badly. Badly is honest.',\\n      'ODIE: Three of them, if the chart is telling the truth. They are quiet. Quiet is the nasty kind.',\\n      'WREN: Laser. Then the little shell they leave. Then whatever is wearing them.',\\n      'CHIEF: You saw a twitch, Doctor, at a bad hour. Do not build a theology out of a twitch.',\\n      'WREN: I built a retractor out of one. Watch.',\\n      'ODIE: Binder for the big one. She only opens her mouth to yawn. Be there when she does.',\\n      'WREN: And if the Chief is right?',\\n      'ODIE: Then you did a tidy operation and I will buy you a bun. I am not worried about the bun.',\\n      'GWEN: Tell me when it is out. Use small words. I will be under, but I am superstitious about tenses.',\\n    ]),\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'after-4',\\n    where: 'The chief\\\\'s office',\\n    boxes: boxes([\\n      'CHIEF: The sample is gone. :: SAMPLE GONE.',\\n      'WREN: I put it in the tray. I labelled it with her name, not mine.',\\n      'CHIEF: Halcyon\\\\'s lawyers have the tray. They also have a story in which you were tired.',\\n      'ODIE: He is suspending you. He is using his gentle voice, which is how you know.',\\n      'CHIEF: You saw a twitch, Doctor, at hour nineteen of a shift. Get a second opinion. If you can find a fool to give one.',\\n      'WREN: Gwen is alive.',\\n      'CHIEF: Alive is not a diagnosis. It is a courtesy. Go home.',\\n      'WREN: You have a scar under that collar.',\\n      'CHIEF: And you have a career, briefly. Do not spend it on my neck.',\\n      'ODIE: Outside. Now. Before you say the true thing at the wrong volume.',\\n      'WREN: I need the name of the woman they struck off.',\\n      'ODIE: Sabine Oyelaran. A ship, not a hospital. If you go, you are done being comfortable.',\\n      'WREN: I was not good at comfortable.',\\n      'ODIE: I noticed. Take a coat. The harbour does not care that you were right.',\\n    ]),\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'before-5',\\n    where: 'The hospital ship',\\n    boxes: boxes([\\n      'SABINE: Everyone agreed I was wrong. That is what consensus feels like from the inside.',\\n      'WREN: Dr. Oyelaran. I brought a story and a bad coat.',\\n      'SABINE: I am not a doctor on this deck. I am the person who still owns a lamp. Talk fast. The weather is working.',\\n      'WREN: A graft flinched. Then it had children. The Chief called it a twitch and took my name off the door.',\\n      'SABINE: Halcyon. They did the same to the trials. Smiled, filed, sailed.',\\n      'ANA: I am not a trial. I am a stevedore and I am going over. :: ON THE DECK.',\\n      'SABINE: Big Ana. Winch crew. Get her on the table before the ship rolls her off it.',\\n      'WREN: I do not have privileges here.',\\n      'SABINE: You have hands. I have a drug they did not put in your textbook. Second Pulse. It keeps the numbers from falling while you work.',\\n      'WREN: And the roll?',\\n      'SABINE: The roll is the sea, pretending to be a critic. Ignore the critic.',\\n      'ODIE: I came because somebody has to count. Do not look surprised. I hate boats. I hate lawyers more.',\\n      'WREN: There is a flap. Something warm is under it.',\\n      'SABINE: Then we do not give it the laser until it is small enough to deserve one. Cut it in half. Then in half again.',\\n    ]),\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'after-5',\\n    where: 'The galley',\\n    boxes: boxes([\\n      'SABINE: I am not a doctor anymore, Dr. Tolliver. I am a second opinion.',\\n      'WREN: Ana will shout at the winch by morning. That is her version of a thank-you.',\\n      'ODIE: The samples match. Yours and the one Sabine kept in a coffee tin, which is not a protocol I will be writing up.',\\n      'SABINE: Solace. That is what they called this one, because the brochure needed a spa.',\\n      'WREN: It hugged the vessel like it was cold.',\\n      'SABINE: It is cold. It wants heat. The laser is a kiss it has not earned until the third splitting.',\\n      'ODIE: The Chief\\\\'s scar. You said collar. Sabine, tell her she is not the only one who noticed necks.',\\n      'SABINE: Bram Achterberg signed the early sheets. I watched his hand. It did not shake. I think about that more than I sleep.',\\n      'WREN: If he is carrying one, he will not come to us.',\\n      'SABINE: Then we wait until his body files the complaint his mouth will not.',\\n      'ODIE: That is a grim timetable. I prefer buses.',\\n      'WREN: My hands shook. On the deck.',\\n      'SABINE: Your hands are shaking. Then that is new. Use it. Shaking is a kind of attention.',\\n      'WREN: I will. And I will not call you anything you did not ask for.',\\n    ]),\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'before-6',\\n    where: 'A boardroom, then a bay',\\n    boxes: boxes([\\n      'CHIEF: Not here. Not in front of them. :: THE COLLAR OPENS.',\\n      'ODIE: He tore the collar himself. There is a scar under it and it is not old enough.',\\n      'WREN: Dr. Achterberg. Look at me. You are the patient now. The title can sit in the hall.',\\n      'CHIEF: I signed the trial. I would like to finish a sentence before your friend with the coat does.',\\n      'SABINE: Your friend with the coat is already here. Two sites. Chest and abdomen. We can swap if your hands want a different sin.',\\n      'WREN: There is something under the sheet. It moves when the monitor does.',\\n      'ODIE: Reverie. Scanner first. The decoys pop. The real one keeps time with him, which is vain and useful.',\\n      'CHIEF: If you find it, do not lecture me while you burn it. I am very fast at lectures. You would lose.',\\n      'WREN: I am not here to win against you.',\\n      'SABINE: Consult, if we both spend the gift. Two opinions, one extra stretch of time. Try not to enjoy the metaphor.',\\n      'ODIE: Vitals sixty-five. He is embarrassed, which is not a vital, but it is doing a lot of work.',\\n      'WREN: Sir. I am sorry. I am going to say that through the whole operation. It is a habit, not a verdict.',\\n      'CHIEF: Accepted. Now finish. A surgeon finishes. I was right about that part and wrong about the rest.',\\n      'SABINE: On your mark. I have the abdomen. Shout if the sheet breathes.',\\n    ]),\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'after-6',\\n    where: 'A side room',\\n    boxes: boxes([\\n      'CHIEF: I signed them all. :: I SIGNED THEM.',\\n      'WREN: The files.',\\n      'CHIEF: Top drawer. The key is the ugly one. I kept it on the ring so I would feel it every day and I still signed.',\\n      'SABINE: Gala access. He really did mean to confess. I hate that it makes me gentler.',\\n      'ODIE: Gentler is allowed. Soft is not. Read the files standing up.',\\n      'CHIEF: Voss will be on a screen the size of a mistake. The donors paid for the wing. The wing is where they will fall, if the batches match.',\\n      'WREN: Then we will be in the wing.',\\n      'CHIEF: You are suspended.',\\n      'ODIE: She is suspended in a building that is about to need her. I can live with the paperwork.',\\n      'SABINE: Two of us. Swap when the site changes. Do not be noble about who holds the knife.',\\n      'WREN: What do I call you now?',\\n      'CHIEF: Bram, if I live. Doctor, if you need the distance. I have earned the distance.',\\n      'ODIE: He will live. I have decided. My decisions have a good record today.',\\n      'WREN: Then we go to the gala. I am not dressing up.',\\n    ]),\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'before-7',\\n    where: 'The new wing',\\n    boxes: boxes([\\n      'VOSS: Welcome to the part of the hospital that thanks you properly.',\\n      'ODIE: Three tables. Three donors. One speech that will not stop for haemorrhage. :: THEY ARE FALLING.',\\n      'WREN: Maris, Owen, Safiya. I read the place cards like a triage list, which is what they are now.',\\n      'SABINE: Balm. It spreads like a varnish and then the thread will not hold. Gel the cells. Two doses in the node.',\\n      'WREN: If one of them dies, the night is a loss. He will call it a fainting on the news.',\\n      'ODIE: Then none of them die. I have reserved the right to be impossible.',\\n      'VOSS: Pain is a rumour spread by people who have not met my product.',\\n      'SABINE: His product is on their skin. Wren, Second Pulse when the bars start to race. I will take table C.',\\n      'WREN: The colleague on the drains. Odie, if I look at the screen, say my name.',\\n      'ODIE: Wren. See how good I am at it already.',\\n      'WREN: Sorry, Maris. You cannot hear me. Your pledge is not the thing I am here to collect.',\\n      'SABINE: Nodes first. Film fades. Then the blood, which has been patient and should not have had to be.',\\n      'ODIE: Voss is still smiling. I want that on the record as a complaint.',\\n      'WREN: Begin. Tables A, B, and C. Nobody leaves in the middle of a toast.',\\n    ]),\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'after-7',\\n    where: 'Under the screen',\\n    boxes: boxes([\\n      'ODIE: All three. Breathing. Annoyed. I will take annoyed.',\\n      'MARIS: I am cancelling the pledge. Spend it on gloves.',\\n      'OWEN: Did the chandelier do that on purpose?',\\n      'SAFIYA: I was mid-sentence. I would like the second half to be different.',\\n      'WREN: You will have it. Not tonight. Tonight you lie still and dislike us in comfort.',\\n      'VOSS: And if you have ever felt too much, ask yourself who sold you that— :: HE FALLS.',\\n      'SABINE: He fell on his own product. I want to be kinder than I am and I am not there yet.',\\n      'ODIE: Get him on a trolley. The speech can finish without a face.',\\n      'WREN: It is in him. The same quiet. I can see it from here and I hate that I can.',\\n      'SABINE: Then the last table is his. You know what Odie will say before you ask.',\\n      'ODIE: We could be slow, Doctor. Nobody would know.',\\n      'WREN: I would.',\\n      'SABINE: Good. Bring him. I am not dressing his conscience. I am keeping the engine running.',\\n      'ODIE: I will count for him too. I resent it. I will do it anyway.',\\n    ]),\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'before-8',\\n    where: 'Theatre one',\\n    boxes: boxes([\\n      'VOSS: This is a misunderstanding. I sell the absence of nights like this.',\\n      'WREN: You are on the table. The misunderstanding can wait in the hall.',\\n      'ODIE: Mercy. That is the name on the batch in his chest. They really do not hear themselves.',\\n      'SABINE: Three movements. Motes, then she stops the heart on purpose, then she tries to live in it. We answer all three.',\\n      'WREN: Every tool. I want them where my hands already know the order.',\\n      'ODIE: We could be slow. I said it. I will not say it again. You answered.',\\n      'VOSS: If I die, the city loses a great deal of optimism.',\\n      'WREN: If you die, the city loses a man. I am not operating on the optimism.',\\n      'SABINE: Anesthesia first. Burn the motes. When she opens, the binder, three times, inside the gift if the last movement demands it.',\\n      'ODIE: Codes when she asks for them. Land the green. Do not show off.',\\n      'WREN: Lucan. I am sorry. I will keep saying it. It does not make you clean. It makes me accurate.',\\n      'SABINE: I have the second pair of hands. Swap if you freeze. Freezing is information. Use it and move.',\\n      'ODIE: Vitals one hundred. She has not started. The hymn is going to be unpleasant.',\\n      'WREN: Then we play a louder one. Begin.',\\n    ]),\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'after-8',\\n    where: 'Dawn, the ward',\\n    boxes: boxes([\\n      'VOSS: You saved me. That is the one thing I could never have sold.',\\n      'WREN: The cuffs were not my department. The heart was. Both seem to be holding.',\\n      'ODIE: Tomás sent a card. Gwen sent a recording of your name, played badly on purpose. I am framing the intent, not the pitch.',\\n      'SABINE: Hal waved at the building from the bus. Ana threatened a winch and then smiled, which I am told is rare and expensive.',\\n      'CHIEF: The files are copied. I will say the sentence in a room with a stenographer. I am tired of rooms without one.',\\n      'MARIS: The wing can keep its name. I am keeping my pulse. We are not even.',\\n      'WREN: I thought there would be a last patient and then a locked door.',\\n      'ODIE: There is a manifest. A crate. Already at sea. :: CASE FILE REMAINS OPEN.',\\n      'SABINE: Then we are not finished. We are between pages. Doctors know that shape.',\\n      'WREN: Free surgery. Anyone who comes. The board stays up.',\\n      'ODIE: And you will eat before the next one. This is now a clinical order.',\\n      'VOSS: I will testify. Do not thank me. Thank the part of the night that was not for sale.',\\n      'WREN: I was never going to thank you. I am glad you are alive to be difficult.',\\n      'ODIE: Credits, then. Names, then the door. The harbour is still there. So are we.',\\n    ]),\\n  },\\n];\\n\\n/** The scene with this id. */\\nexport function sceneById(id: string): Scene | undefined {\\n  return SCENES.find((scene) => scene.id === id);\\n}\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/story.ts has been created successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/story.ts has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/story.ts\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"/**\\n * @file The campaign's scenes. Each one is a run of short boxes, twelve to thirty-five, said out loud over captions.\\n * A drama box is a snapped close-up and a caption. Nothing here is quoted from another game.\\n */\\nexport interface Box {\\n  who: string;\\n  text: string;\\n  /** A huge caption, when this beat is a drama cut. */\\n  drama?: string;\\n}\\n\\n/** One skippable scene. */\\nexport interface Scene {\\n  id: string;\\n  where: string;\\n  boxes: Box[];\\n}\\n\\n/** `WHO: line` or `WHO: line :: CAPTION`. */\\nfunction boxes(lines: readonly string[]): Box[] {\\n  return lines.map((line) => {\\n    const cut = line.indexOf(' :: ');\\n    const body = cut === -1 ? line : line.slice(0, cut);\\n    const speaker = body.indexOf(': ');\\n    return {\\n      who: body.slice(0, speaker),\\n      text: body.slice(speaker + 2),\\n      ...(cut === -1 ? {} : { drama: line.slice(cut + 4) }),\\n    };\\n  });\\n}\\n\\n/** Every story scene, in the order the director plays them. */\\nexport const SCENES: readonly Scene[] = [\\n  {\\n    id: 'before-1',\\n    where: 'Harbor Light, night',\\n    boxes: boxes([\\n      'ODIE: Congratulations, Doctor. You are the only surgeon in the building.',\\n      'WREN: The storm took the bridge. I can hear the glass in it.',\\n      'ODIE: And the ad. Turn that down before it turns you.',\\n      'VOSS: Pain is just a feeling you have not paid to remove yet.',\\n      'WREN: Halcyon. Because you deserve to feel nothing. Who bought that line?',\\n      'ODIE: Everyone with a wallet. Tomás Reyes is on table one. Deck hatch. Glass.',\\n      'WREN: Is he awake?',\\n      'ODIE: Awake enough to ask after a dog. The dog is in the corridor, against every rule I have.',\\n      'WREN: Leave the dog. I will be quick.',\\n      'ODIE: You will be careful. Quick is how people become stories.',\\n      'WREN: Drain, forceps, suture. I have had the lecture.',\\n      'ODIE: Then give it back to me with your hands. Vitals are seventy and rude about it.',\\n      'WREN: Sorry. I say that to them even when they cannot hear.',\\n      'ODIE: Good. Start with the water. The glass can wait its turn.',\\n    ]),\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'after-1',\\n    where: 'The corridor',\\n    boxes: boxes([\\n      'ODIE: He is breathing like a man who intends to keep the habit.',\\n      'WREN: The dog is still here.',\\n      'ODIE: I am looking at the chart. I see no dog. Charts are famous for this.',\\n      'WREN: Tomás. Your dog stayed. I told him you were busy.',\\n      'TOMAS: He waits out storms. He is better at it than I am.',\\n      'ODIE: Visiting hours were cancelled by the weather. Do not quote me.',\\n      'WREN: I nicked nothing I meant to leave. I think.',\\n      'ODIE: In this hallway, \\\"I think\\\" is how you ask me to count again. I counted. He is fine.',\\n      'WREN: The ad is still playing in the ward.',\\n      'ODIE: Let it. Tired people buy quiet. We sell the other thing, which is work.',\\n      'WREN: I should write the closure note.',\\n      'ODIE: You should eat. The note can be brilliant on a full stomach.',\\n      'TOMAS: Tell the dog he can come up. Just for a minute. I will pretend it was clinical.',\\n      'WREN: One minute. Then I am a doctor again.',\\n    ]),\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'before-2',\\n    where: 'A quiet bay',\\n    boxes: boxes([\\n      'GWEN: If you drop a trumpet in a harbor it plays one note and then it is a trumpet for crabs.',\\n      'WREN: Gwen Abara. It says cyst. It says you play.',\\n      'GWEN: I play. The cyst is a rumour my scar started.',\\n      'ODIE: Old graft, lip, two years ago. Halcyon. She showed me the brochure like it was a medal.',\\n      'GWEN: It was a medal. I sang the week after. High C, rude and shiny.',\\n      'WREN: And now it pulls?',\\n      'GWEN: When the weather does. Or when I laugh. Today I did both, so here we are.',\\n      'ODIE: Routine. Scanner if the lump is shy. Laser if it is not. You have done harder things before breakfast.',\\n      'WREN: I had no breakfast.',\\n      'ODIE: Then you have done harder things before coffee, which is the same tragedy.',\\n      'GWEN: Do not take the note. Take the lump. I can find another note.',\\n      'WREN: I will talk to you the whole time. You will not hear it. I do it anyway.',\\n      'ODIE: Scalpel on the line. If you wander, I will say your name the way my mother did.',\\n      'WREN: That is the most frightening instrument in the room.',\\n    ]),\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'after-2',\\n    where: 'The scrub room',\\n    boxes: boxes([\\n      'WREN: It moved. :: IT MOVED.',\\n      'ODIE: I saw it. Do not perform that sentence for the corridor.',\\n      'WREN: A cyst does not flinch when the forceps close.',\\n      'ODIE: A cyst does not do anything. That is the appeal of cysts.',\\n      'WREN: So what do I write?',\\n      'ODIE: You write cyst. You sleep. You and I remember the other word and we do not spend it yet.',\\n      'WREN: If I write cyst, I am lying.',\\n      'ODIE: If you write monster, you are unemployed and she is a rumour. Give me one night.',\\n      'WREN: She asked if she could play tomorrow.',\\n      'ODIE: Tell her yes. Be right about that part.',\\n      'WREN: The scar looked like a smile that had changed its mind.',\\n      'ODIE: Poetic. Keep it out of the chart.',\\n      'WREN: I want a second look. Not a committee. A person.',\\n      'ODIE: Then find one who is not paid by the people who made the smile.',\\n    ]),\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'before-3',\\n    where: 'Emergency, overflow',\\n    boxes: boxes([\\n      'CHIEF: Breakwater Road is in my emergency room. Try not to add yourself to it.',\\n      'WREN: How many?',\\n      'CHIEF: One for you. Hal Minsky. Bus driver. Liver, lung, arm. The bus is not your patient, whatever the radio says.',\\n      'ODIE: Three sites. They bleed while you are elsewhere. That is not a metaphor.',\\n      'WREN: I have not run three sites.',\\n      'CHIEF: In my operating room, \\\"I have not\\\" is a cause of death. You have now.',\\n      'WREN: His route?',\\n      'ODIE: Four. He said the number twice before the drugs took the rest.',\\n      'CHIEF: If he dies, you will know which part you were not standing on. Go and stand on all of them.',\\n      'WREN: And if the line goes flat?',\\n      'ODIE: Then you are in a Code. Green band. Two tries. I will count so you do not have to be brave and numerate at once.',\\n      'WREN: What if there is no time left for the arteries?',\\n      'ODIE: Then we find time. Do not ask me how until you need it.',\\n      'CHIEF: Finish, Doctor. Feeling is what the waiting room is for.',\\n    ]),\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'after-3',\\n    where: 'Outside theatre',\\n    boxes: boxes([\\n      'WREN: Something happened in there. The room got slow and my hands did not.',\\n      'ODIE: You were fast. Do not make it weird.',\\n      'WREN: I could hear the monitor like it was under water, and then I was ahead of it.',\\n      'ODIE: Stillpoint. That is the word you are chewing. Spit it out or swallow it. Not both.',\\n      'WREN: Is it a real word?',\\n      'ODIE: It is today. Hal is alive. The arm will argue with him for a month and then do as it is told.',\\n      'WREN: The Chief watched.',\\n      'ODIE: The Chief watches the way a cliff watches. It is not a compliment and it is not an attack.',\\n      'WREN: I want to tell him about the slowing.',\\n      'ODIE: You want to be believed. Those are different errands. Run the second one later.',\\n      'WREN: Route four. He will be angry about the timetable.',\\n      'ODIE: Good. Angry people get on buses. Write the note. Eat the soup. Stop discovering powers in the corridor.',\\n      'WREN: I am not discovering. I am reporting.',\\n      'ODIE: Then report it to me, quietly, where it cannot get you suspended before pudding.',\\n    ]),\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'before-4',\\n    where: 'The gallery',\\n    boxes: boxes([\\n      'GWEN: It is moving. I would like to be wrong in public. :: THE SCAR MOVES.',\\n      'WREN: You are not wrong. I am sorry. That is a bad sentence to be right about.',\\n      'CHIEF: A surgeon does not feel. A surgeon finishes. Kindly do the second one where I can see it.',\\n      'ODIE: He is in the gallery. He brought his moustache and his opinions, which are the same size.',\\n      'WREN: Gwen. Your trumpet is in the nurses\\\\' station. Nobody will tune it.',\\n      'GWEN: If I do not wake up, give it to someone who will play it badly. Badly is honest.',\\n      'ODIE: Three of them, if the chart is telling the truth. They are quiet. Quiet is the nasty kind.',\\n      'WREN: Laser. Then the little shell they leave. Then whatever is wearing them.',\\n      'CHIEF: You saw a twitch, Doctor, at a bad hour. Do not build a theology out of a twitch.',\\n      'WREN: I built a retractor out of one. Watch.',\\n      'ODIE: Binder for the big one. She only opens her mouth to yawn. Be there when she does.',\\n      'WREN: And if the Chief is right?',\\n      'ODIE: Then you did a tidy operation and I will buy you a bun. I am not worried about the bun.',\\n      'GWEN: Tell me when it is out. Use small words. I will be under, but I am superstitious about tenses.',\\n    ]),\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'after-4',\\n    where: 'The chief\\\\'s office',\\n    boxes: boxes([\\n      'CHIEF: The sample is gone. :: SAMPLE GONE.',\\n      'WREN: I put it in the tray. I labelled it with her name, not mine.',\\n      'CHIEF: Halcyon\\\\'s lawyers have the tray. They also have a story in which you were tired.',\\n      'ODIE: He is suspending you. He is using his gentle voice, which is how you know.',\\n      'CHIEF: You saw a twitch, Doctor, at hour nineteen of a shift. Get a second opinion. If you can find a fool to give one.',\\n      'WREN: Gwen is alive.',\\n      'CHIEF: Alive is not a diagnosis. It is a courtesy. Go home.',\\n      'WREN: You have a scar under that collar.',\\n      'CHIEF: And you have a career, briefly. Do not spend it on my neck.',\\n      'ODIE: Outside. Now. Before you say the true thing at the wrong volume.',\\n      'WREN: I need the name of the woman they struck off.',\\n      'ODIE: Sabine Oyelaran. A ship, not a hospital. If you go, you are done being comfortable.',\\n      'WREN: I was not good at comfortable.',\\n      'ODIE: I noticed. Take a coat. The harbour does not care that you were right.',\\n    ]),\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'before-5',\\n    where: 'The hospital ship',\\n    boxes: boxes([\\n      'SABINE: Everyone agreed I was wrong. That is what consensus feels like from the inside.',\\n      'WREN: Dr. Oyelaran. I brought a story and a bad coat.',\\n      'SABINE: I am not a doctor on this deck. I am the person who still owns a lamp. Talk fast. The weather is working.',\\n      'WREN: A graft flinched. Then it had children. The Chief called it a twitch and took my name off the door.',\\n      'SABINE: Halcyon. They did the same to the trials. Smiled, filed, sailed.',\\n      'ANA: I am not a trial. I am a stevedore and I am going over. :: ON THE DECK.',\\n      'SABINE: Big Ana. Winch crew. Get her on the table before the ship rolls her off it.',\\n      'WREN: I do not have privileges here.',\\n      'SABINE: You have hands. I have a drug they did not put in your textbook. Second Pulse. It keeps the numbers from falling while you work.',\\n      'WREN: And the roll?',\\n      'SABINE: The roll is the sea, pretending to be a critic. Ignore the critic.',\\n      'ODIE: I came because somebody has to count. Do not look surprised. I hate boats. I hate lawyers more.',\\n      'WREN: There is a flap. Something warm is under it.',\\n      'SABINE: Then we do not give it the laser until it is small enough to deserve one. Cut it in half. Then in half again.',\\n    ]),\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'after-5',\\n    where: 'The galley',\\n    boxes: boxes([\\n      'SABINE: I am not a doctor anymore, Dr. Tolliver. I am a second opinion.',\\n      'WREN: Ana will shout at the winch by morning. That is her version of a thank-you.',\\n      'ODIE: The samples match. Yours and the one Sabine kept in a coffee tin, which is not a protocol I will be writing up.',\\n      'SABINE: Solace. That is what they called this one, because the brochure needed a spa.',\\n      'WREN: It hugged the vessel like it was cold.',\\n      'SABINE: It is cold. It wants heat. The laser is a kiss it has not earned until the third splitting.',\\n      'ODIE: The Chief\\\\'s scar. You said collar. Sabine, tell her she is not the only one who noticed necks.',\\n      'SABINE: Bram Achterberg signed the early sheets. I watched his hand. It did not shake. I think about that more than I sleep.',\\n      'WREN: If he is carrying one, he will not come to us.',\\n      'SABINE: Then we wait until his body files the complaint his mouth will not.',\\n      'ODIE: That is a grim timetable. I prefer buses.',\\n      'WREN: My hands shook. On the deck.',\\n      'SABINE: Your hands are shaking. Then that is new. Use it. Shaking is a kind of attention.',\\n      'WREN: I will. And I will not call you anything you did not ask for.',\\n    ]),\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'before-6',\\n    where: 'A boardroom, then a bay',\\n    boxes: boxes([\\n      'CHIEF: Not here. Not in front of them. :: THE COLLAR OPENS.',\\n      'ODIE: He tore the collar himself. There is a scar under it and it is not old enough.',\\n      'WREN: Dr. Achterberg. Look at me. You are the patient now. The title can sit in the hall.',\\n      'CHIEF: I signed the trial. I would like to finish a sentence before your friend with the coat does.',\\n      'SABINE: Your friend with the coat is already here. Two sites. Chest and abdomen. We can swap if your hands want a different sin.',\\n      'WREN: There is something under the sheet. It moves when the monitor does.',\\n      'ODIE: Reverie. Scanner first. The decoys pop. The real one keeps time with him, which is vain and useful.',\\n      'CHIEF: If you find it, do not lecture me while you burn it. I am very fast at lectures. You would lose.',\\n      'WREN: I am not here to win against you.',\\n      'SABINE: Consult, if we both spend the gift. Two opinions, one extra stretch of time. Try not to enjoy the metaphor.',\\n      'ODIE: Vitals sixty-five. He is embarrassed, which is not a vital, but it is doing a lot of work.',\\n      'WREN: Sir. I am sorry. I am going to say that through the whole operation. It is a habit, not a verdict.',\\n      'CHIEF: Accepted. Now finish. A surgeon finishes. I was right about that part and wrong about the rest.',\\n      'SABINE: On your mark. I have the abdomen. Shout if the sheet breathes.',\\n    ]),\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'after-6',\\n    where: 'A side room',\\n    boxes: boxes([\\n      'CHIEF: I signed them all. :: I SIGNED THEM.',\\n      'WREN: The files.',\\n      'CHIEF: Top drawer. The key is the ugly one. I kept it on the ring so I would feel it every day and I still signed.',\\n      'SABINE: Gala access. He really did mean to confess. I hate that it makes me gentler.',\\n      'ODIE: Gentler is allowed. Soft is not. Read the files standing up.',\\n      'CHIEF: Voss will be on a screen the size of a mistake. The donors paid for the wing. The wing is where they will fall, if the batches match.',\\n      'WREN: Then we will be in the wing.',\\n      'CHIEF: You are suspended.',\\n      'ODIE: She is suspended in a building that is about to need her. I can live with the paperwork.',\\n      'SABINE: Two of us. Swap when the site changes. Do not be noble about who holds the knife.',\\n      'WREN: What do I call you now?',\\n      'CHIEF: Bram, if I live. Doctor, if you need the distance. I have earned the distance.',\\n      'ODIE: He will live. I have decided. My decisions have a good record today.',\\n      'WREN: Then we go to the gala. I am not dressing up.',\\n    ]),\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'before-7',\\n    where: 'The new wing',\\n    boxes: boxes([\\n      'VOSS: Welcome to the part of the hospital that thanks you properly.',\\n      'ODIE: Three tables. Three donors. One speech that will not stop for haemorrhage. :: THEY ARE FALLING.',\\n      'WREN: Maris, Owen, Safiya. I read the place cards like a triage list, which is what they are now.',\\n      'SABINE: Balm. It spreads like a varnish and then the thread will not hold. Gel the cells. Two doses in the node.',\\n      'WREN: If one of them dies, the night is a loss. He will call it a fainting on the news.',\\n      'ODIE: Then none of them die. I have reserved the right to be impossible.',\\n      'VOSS: Pain is a rumour spread by people who have not met my product.',\\n      'SABINE: His product is on their skin. Wren, Second Pulse when the bars start to race. I will take table C.',\\n      'WREN: The colleague on the drains. Odie, if I look at the screen, say my name.',\\n      'ODIE: Wren. See how good I am at it already.',\\n      'WREN: Sorry, Maris. You cannot hear me. Your pledge is not the thing I am here to collect.',\\n      'SABINE: Nodes first. Film fades. Then the blood, which has been patient and should not have had to be.',\\n      'ODIE: Voss is still smiling. I want that on the record as a complaint.',\\n      'WREN: Begin. Tables A, B, and C. Nobody leaves in the middle of a toast.',\\n    ]),\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'after-7',\\n    where: 'Under the screen',\\n    boxes: boxes([\\n      'ODIE: All three. Breathing. Annoyed. I will take annoyed.',\\n      'MARIS: I am cancelling the pledge. Spend it on gloves.',\\n      'OWEN: Did the chandelier do that on purpose?',\\n      'SAFIYA: I was mid-sentence. I would like the second half to be different.',\\n      'WREN: You will have it. Not tonight. Tonight you lie still and dislike us in comfort.',\\n      'VOSS: And if you have ever felt too much, ask yourself who sold you that— :: HE FALLS.',\\n      'SABINE: He fell on his own product. I want to be kinder than I am and I am not there yet.',\\n      'ODIE: Get him on a trolley. The speech can finish without a face.',\\n      'WREN: It is in him. The same quiet. I can see it from here and I hate that I can.',\\n      'SABINE: Then the last table is his. You know what Odie will say before you ask.',\\n      'ODIE: We could be slow, Doctor. Nobody would know.',\\n      'WREN: I would.',\\n      'SABINE: Good. Bring him. I am not dressing his conscience. I am keeping the engine running.',\\n      'ODIE: I will count for him too. I resent it. I will do it anyway.',\\n    ]),\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'before-8',\\n    where: 'Theatre one',\\n    boxes: boxes([\\n      'VOSS: This is a misunderstanding. I sell the absence of nights like this.',\\n      'WREN: You are on the table. The misunderstanding can wait in the hall.',\\n      'ODIE: Mercy. That is the name on the batch in his chest. They really do not hear themselves.',\\n      'SABINE: Three movements. Motes, then she stops the heart on purpose, then she tries to live in it. We answer all three.',\\n      'WREN: Every tool. I want them where my hands already know the order.',\\n      'ODIE: We could be slow. I said it. I will not say it again. You answered.',\\n      'VOSS: If I die, the city loses a great deal of optimism.',\\n      'WREN: If you die, the city loses a man. I am not operating on the optimism.',\\n      'SABINE: Anesthesia first. Burn the motes. When she opens, the binder, three times, inside the gift if the last movement demands it.',\\n      'ODIE: Codes when she asks for them. Land the green. Do not show off.',\\n      'WREN: Lucan. I am sorry. I will keep saying it. It does not make you clean. It makes me accurate.',\\n      'SABINE: I have the second pair of hands. Swap if you freeze. Freezing is information. Use it and move.',\\n      'ODIE: Vitals one hundred. She has not started. The hymn is going to be unpleasant.',\\n      'WREN: Then we play a louder one. Begin.',\\n    ]),\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'after-8',\\n    where: 'Dawn, the ward',\\n    boxes: boxes([\\n      'VOSS: You saved me. That is the one thing I could never have sold.',\\n      'WREN: The cuffs were not my department. The heart was. Both seem to be holding.',\\n      'ODIE: Tomás sent a card. Gwen sent a recording of your name, played badly on purpose. I am framing the intent, not the pitch.',\\n      'SABINE: Hal waved at the building from the bus. Ana threatened a winch and then smiled, which I am told is rare and expensive.',\\n      'CHIEF: The files are copied. I will say the sentence in a room with a stenographer. I am tired of rooms without one.',\\n      'MARIS: The wing can keep its name. I am keeping my pulse. We are not even.',\\n      'WREN: I thought there would be a last patient and then a locked door.',\\n      'ODIE: There is a manifest. A crate. Already at sea. :: CASE FILE REMAINS OPEN.',\\n      'SABINE: Then we are not finished. We are between pages. Doctors know that shape.',\\n      'WREN: Free surgery. Anyone who comes. The board stays up.',\\n      'ODIE: And you will eat before the next one. This is now a clinical order.',\\n      'VOSS: I will testify. Do not thank me. Thank the part of the night that was not for sale.',\\n      'WREN: I was never going to thank you. I am glad you are alive to be difficult.',\\n      'ODIE: Credits, then. Names, then the door. The harbour is still there. So are we.',\\n    ]),\\n  },\\n];\\n\\n/** The scene with this id. */\\nexport function sceneById(id: string): Scene | undefined {\\n  return SCENES.find((scene) => scene.id === id);\\n}\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-94cd5ce2-7530-45bf-acf7-adb7301710f6-92","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"/**\\n * @file Gibberish voices. Each character of a line picks one of sixteen syllables. The pick is a pure function of\\n * the speaker and the character, so the same line always barks the same way. No samples, no files.\\n */\\n\\n/** Sixteen mouth-shapes. The page plays them. The index is the whole contract. */\\nexport const SYLLABLES = ['ba', 'ke', 'mi', 'to', 'ra', 'lu', 'ne', 'shi', 'ko', 'va', 'di', 'fu', 'pe', 'zo', 'ha', 'ri'] as const;\\n\\n/** FNV-1a over a string, unsigned. */\\nfunction fnv(text: string, seed = 2166136261): number {\\n  let hash = seed >>> 0;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < text.length; i++) {\\n    hash ^= text.charCodeAt(i);\\n    hash = Math.imul(hash, 16777619);\\n  }\\n  return hash >>> 0;\\n}\\n\\n/** Syllable indexes for one line, speaker included so two people never share a mouth by accident. */\\nexport function voiceOf(who: string, text: string): number[] {\\n  const salt = fnv(who);\\n  const out: number[] = [];\\n  for (let i = 0; i < text.length; i++) out.push(fnv(text[i] + String(i), salt) % SYLLABLES.length);\\n  return out;\\n}\\n\\n/** The same line joined, for a quick equality check. */\\nexport function voiceKey(who: string, text: string): string {\\n  return voiceOf(who, text).join('.');\\n}\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/voice.ts has been created successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/voice.ts has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/voice.ts\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"/**\\n * @file Gibberish voices. Each character of a line picks one of sixteen syllables. The pick is a pure function of\\n * the speaker and the character, so the same line always barks the same way. No samples, no files.\\n */\\n\\n/** Sixteen mouth-shapes. The page plays them. The index is the whole contract. */\\nexport const SYLLABLES = ['ba', 'ke', 'mi', 'to', 'ra', 'lu', 'ne', 'shi', 'ko', 'va', 'di', 'fu', 'pe', 'zo', 'ha', 'ri'] as const;\\n\\n/** FNV-1a over a string, unsigned. */\\nfunction fnv(text: string, seed = 2166136261): number {\\n  let hash = seed >>> 0;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < text.length; i++) {\\n    hash ^= text.charCodeAt(i);\\n    hash = Math.imul(hash, 16777619);\\n  }\\n  return hash >>> 0;\\n}\\n\\n/** Syllable indexes for one line, speaker included so two people never share a mouth by accident. */\\nexport function voiceOf(who: string, text: string): number[] {\\n  const salt = fnv(who);\\n  const out: number[] = [];\\n  for (let i = 0; i < text.length; i++) out.push(fnv(text[i] + String(i), salt) % SYLLABLES.length);\\n  return out;\\n}\\n\\n/** The same line joined, for a quick equality check. */\\nexport function voiceKey(who: string, text: string): string {\\n  return voiceOf(who, text).join('.');\\n}\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-94cd5ce2-7530-45bf-acf7-adb7301710f6-93","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"/**\\n * @file The campaign with no browser. Title, eight scenes, eight operations, debrief, credits, then Free Surgery.\\n * The bot plays each case from that case's own start. The save at the end is what the Board would have written.\\n */\\nimport { runBot } from './bot';\\nimport { storyCases } from './cases';\\nimport { rankFor } from './ratings';\\nimport { SCENES, sceneById } from './story';\\nimport type { Difficulty, Rank } from './types';\\nimport { createFromCase } from './world';\\n\\n/** What a finished shift remembers. */\\nexport interface Through {\\n  scenes: string[];\\n  /** Case id, then the rank the debrief would show. */\\n  ranks: { id: string; rank: Rank; score: number }[];\\n  postcards: string[];\\n  credits: boolean;\\n  free: boolean;\\n  attending: boolean;\\n}\\n\\n/** Walk the whole story on one difficulty. Throws if a case does not clear, because the credits are not a consolation. */\\nexport function playThrough(difficulty: Difficulty = 'resident', seed = 1): Through {\\n  const scenes: string[] = [];\\n  const ranks: Through['ranks'] = [];\\n  const postcards: string[] = [];\\n  for (const def of storyCases()) {\\n    const before = sceneById(def.storyBefore);\\n    const after = sceneById(def.storyAfter);\\n    if (!before || !after) throw new Error(`Missing scene for ${def.id}`);\\n    scenes.push(before.id);\\n    const op = createFromCase(def.id, { difficulty, seed });\\n    runBot(op);\\n    if (op.status !== 'won') throw new Error(`${def.id} ${op.fail}`);\\n    const rank = rankFor(op.score, def.par, op.slips, difficulty);\\n    ranks.push({ id: def.id, rank, score: op.score });\\n    const letter = rank === '★' || rank === 'S' ? 'S' : rank;\\n    postcards.push(def.patients[0].postcards[letter]);\\n    scenes.push(after.id);\\n  }\\n  if (!SCENES.some((scene) => scene.boxes.some((box) => box.drama === 'CASE FILE REMAINS OPEN'))) {\\n    throw new Error('The last beat is missing');\\n  }\\n  return { scenes, ranks, postcards, credits: true, free: true, attending: true };\\n}\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/director.ts has been created successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/director.ts has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/director.ts\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"/**\\n * @file The campaign with no browser. Title, eight scenes, eight operations, debrief, credits, then Free Surgery.\\n * The bot plays each case from that case's own start. The save at the end is what the Board would have written.\\n */\\nimport { runBot } from './bot';\\nimport { storyCases } from './cases';\\nimport { rankFor } from './ratings';\\nimport { SCENES, sceneById } from './story';\\nimport type { Difficulty, Rank } from './types';\\nimport { createFromCase } from './world';\\n\\n/** What a finished shift remembers. */\\nexport interface Through {\\n  scenes: string[];\\n  /** Case id, then the rank the debrief would show. */\\n  ranks: { id: string; rank: Rank; score: number }[];\\n  postcards: string[];\\n  credits: boolean;\\n  free: boolean;\\n  attending: boolean;\\n}\\n\\n/** Walk the whole story on one difficulty. Throws if a case does not clear, because the credits are not a consolation. */\\nexport function playThrough(difficulty: Difficulty = 'resident', seed = 1): Through {\\n  const scenes: string[] = [];\\n  const ranks: Through['ranks'] = [];\\n  const postcards: string[] = [];\\n  for (const def of storyCases()) {\\n    const before = sceneById(def.storyBefore);\\n    const after = sceneById(def.storyAfter);\\n    if (!before || !after) throw new Error(`Missing scene for ${def.id}`);\\n    scenes.push(before.id);\\n    const op = createFromCase(def.id, { difficulty, seed });\\n    runBot(op);\\n    if (op.status !== 'won') throw new Error(`${def.id} ${op.fail}`);\\n    const rank = rankFor(op.score, def.par, op.slips, difficulty);\\n    ranks.push({ id: def.id, rank, score: op.score });\\n    const letter = rank === '★' || rank === 'S' ? 'S' : rank;\\n    postcards.push(def.patients[0].postcards[letter]);\\n    scenes.push(after.id);\\n  }\\n  if (!SCENES.some((scene) => scene.boxes.some((box) => box.drama === 'CASE FILE REMAINS OPEN'))) {\\n    throw new Error('The last beat is missing');\\n  }\\n  return { scenes, ranks, postcards, credits: true, free: true, attending: true };\\n}\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-94cd5ce2-7530-45bf-acf7-adb7301710f6-94","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"/**\\n * @file Host lockstep without a socket. Four copies, delayed intents, loss on the way to the host, one leaver.\\n * The host's applied hands are what every copy steps. After the run, the hashes for each applied tick agree.\\n */\\nimport { stepOp, lastHash } from './step';\\nimport type { Hand, Op } from './types';\\nimport { createBare, idleHand } from './world';\\n\\n/** A roll in 0..1 from the tick and the seat, with no Math.random. */\\nfunction roll(tick: number, seat: number): number {\\n  const x = Math.sin(tick * 12.9898 + seat * 78.233) * 43758.5453;\\n  return x - Math.floor(x);\\n}\\n\\n/** What one surgeon meant to do on one tick. Pure, so every copy would have sent the same intent. */\\nexport function intentAt(tick: number, seat: number, hand: Hand): Hand {\\n  const angle = tick / 18 + seat;\\n  return {\\n    ...hand,\\n    x: Math.sin(angle) * (1.4 + seat * 0.15),\\n    z: Math.cos(angle * 0.8) * 0.9,\\n    tool: Math.floor(tick / 90 + seat) % 8,\\n    use: tick % 37 < 8,\\n    gift: false,\\n    paddle: false,\\n    drop: false,\\n    site: -1,\\n    swap: false,\\n    hint: false,\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n/** One peer's view of the operation. */\\ninterface Peer {\\n  op: Op;\\n  /** Last intent that actually reached the host, per seat. */\\n  last: Hand[];\\n  /** Hash after each applied tick. */\\n  hashes: string[];\\n}\\n\\n/** Run the lockstep. Returns the peers so a test can read the hashes. */\\nexport function runLockstep(ticks = 3600, seats = 4): { peers: Peer[]; dropped: number; leftAt: number } {\\n  const peers: Peer[] = [];\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) {\\n    const op = createBare({ seats, code: false });\\n    addAnchor(op);\\n    peers.push({ op, last: op.seats.map((seat) => idleHand(seat)), hashes: [] });\\n  }\\n  const host = peers[0];\\n  let dropped = 0;\\n  const leftAt = Math.floor(ticks / 2);\\n  const delay = 4;\\n  /** Intents in flight: tick they were sent, seat, hand, and whether the wire kept them. */\\n  const wire: { arrive: number; seat: number; hand: Hand }[] = [];\\n  for (let tick = 0; tick < ticks; tick++) {\\n    for (let seat = 0; seat < seats; seat++) {\\n      if (seat === seats - 1 && tick >= leftAt) continue;\\n      const hand = intentAt(tick, seat, host.last[seat]);\\n      const lost = roll(tick, seat) < 0.05;\\n      if (lost) {\\n        dropped += 1;\\n        continue;\\n      }\\n      const jitter = Math.floor(roll(tick, seat + 3) * 3);\\n      wire.push({ arrive: tick + delay + jitter, seat, hand });\\n    }\\n    const applied = host.last.map((hand) => ({ ...hand, use: false }));\\n    for (let i = wire.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {\\n      const packet = wire[i];\\n      if (packet.arrive > tick) continue;\\n      applied[packet.seat] = packet.hand;\\n      host.last[packet.seat] = packet.hand;\\n      wire.splice(i, 1);\\n    }\\n    for (const peer of peers) {\\n      stepOp(peer.op, applied);\\n      peer.hashes.push(lastHash(peer.op));\\n    }\\n  }\\n  return { peers, dropped, leftAt };\\n}\\n\\n/** A target that keeps the bare operation from ending the moment it starts. */\\nfunction addAnchor(op: Op): void {\\n  op.targets.push({\\n    ...op.targets[0],\\n    id: op.nextId,\\n    kind: 'mass',\\n    x: 6,\\n    z: 4,\\n    done: false,\\n    hidden: true,\\n    locked: true,\\n    phase: 0,\\n    optional: false,\\n  });\\n  op.nextId += 1;\\n}\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/sequencer.ts has been created successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/sequencer.ts has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/sequencer.ts\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"/**\\n * @file Host lockstep without a socket. Four copies, delayed intents, loss on the way to the host, one leaver.\\n * The host's applied hands are what every copy steps. After the run, the hashes for each applied tick agree.\\n */\\nimport { stepOp, lastHash } from './step';\\nimport type { Hand, Op } from './types';\\nimport { createBare, idleHand } from './world';\\n\\n/** A roll in 0..1 from the tick and the seat, with no Math.random. */\\nfunction roll(tick: number, seat: number): number {\\n  const x = Math.sin(tick * 12.9898 + seat * 78.233) * 43758.5453;\\n  return x - Math.floor(x);\\n}\\n\\n/** What one surgeon meant to do on one tick. Pure, so every copy would have sent the same intent. */\\nexport function intentAt(tick: number, seat: number, hand: Hand): Hand {\\n  const angle = tick / 18 + seat;\\n  return {\\n    ...hand,\\n    x: Math.sin(angle) * (1.4 + seat * 0.15),\\n    z: Math.cos(angle * 0.8) * 0.9,\\n    tool: Math.floor(tick / 90 + seat) % 8,\\n    use: tick % 37 < 8,\\n    gift: false,\\n    paddle: false,\\n    drop: false,\\n    site: -1,\\n    swap: false,\\n    hint: false,\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n/** One peer's view of the operation. */\\ninterface Peer {\\n  op: Op;\\n  /** Last intent that actually reached the host, per seat. */\\n  last: Hand[];\\n  /** Hash after each applied tick. */\\n  hashes: string[];\\n}\\n\\n/** Run the lockstep. Returns the peers so a test can read the hashes. */\\nexport function runLockstep(ticks = 3600, seats = 4): { peers: Peer[]; dropped: number; leftAt: number } {\\n  const peers: Peer[] = [];\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) {\\n    const op = createBare({ seats, code: false });\\n    addAnchor(op);\\n    peers.push({ op, last: op.seats.map((seat) => idleHand(seat)), hashes: [] });\\n  }\\n  const host = peers[0];\\n  let dropped = 0;\\n  const leftAt = Math.floor(ticks / 2);\\n  const delay = 4;\\n  /** Intents in flight: tick they were sent, seat, hand, and whether the wire kept them. */\\n  const wire: { arrive: number; seat: number; hand: Hand }[] = [];\\n  for (let tick = 0; tick < ticks; tick++) {\\n    for (let seat = 0; seat < seats; seat++) {\\n      if (seat === seats - 1 && tick >= leftAt) continue;\\n      const hand = intentAt(tick, seat, host.last[seat]);\\n      const lost = roll(tick, seat) < 0.05;\\n      if (lost) {\\n        dropped += 1;\\n        continue;\\n      }\\n      const jitter = Math.floor(roll(tick, seat + 3) * 3);\\n      wire.push({ arrive: tick + delay + jitter, seat, hand });\\n    }\\n    const applied = host.last.map((hand) => ({ ...hand, use: false }));\\n    for (let i = wire.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {\\n      const packet = wire[i];\\n      if (packet.arrive > tick) continue;\\n      applied[packet.seat] = packet.hand;\\n      host.last[packet.seat] = packet.hand;\\n      wire.splice(i, 1);\\n    }\\n    for (const peer of peers) {\\n      stepOp(peer.op, applied);\\n      peer.hashes.push(lastHash(peer.op));\\n    }\\n  }\\n  return { peers, dropped, leftAt };\\n}\\n\\n/** A target that keeps the bare operation from ending the moment it starts. */\\nfunction addAnchor(op: Op): void {\\n  op.targets.push({\\n    ...op.targets[0],\\n    id: op.nextId,\\n    kind: 'mass',\\n    x: 6,\\n    z: 4,\\n    done: false,\\n    hidden: true,\\n    locked: true,\\n    phase: 0,\\n    optional: false,\\n  });\\n  op.nextId += 1;\\n}\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"f7da82d8-e706-4c48-b212-a0f2a7e439f6"}
