{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-e5a21458-9071-4ff4-99cb-2a389c93b173-25","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"110→/** A `sim/no-restricted-imports` block: every Node built-in by its bare name, then `patterns`. */\\nfunction imports(name: string, files: string[], patterns: object[]): Linter.Config {\\n  const paths = builtinModules\\n    .filter((module) => !module.startsWith('node:'))\\n    .map((module) => ({ name: module, message: NODE }));\\n  return {\\n    name,\\n    files,\\n    ignores: ['**/*.test.ts'],\\n    plugins: { sim: simPlugin },\\n120→    rules: { 'sim/no-restricted-imports': ['error', { paths, patterns }] },\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n/** The sim-side blocks: globals, properties and syntax over all sim-side files, then imports (core/math.ts last). */\\nexport function simSideBlocks(): Linter.Config[] {\\n  const banned = `/^(${Object.keys(GLOBALS).join('|')})$/`;\\n  const named = (node: string) => `:matches([${node}.name=${banned}], [${node}.value=${banned}])`;\\n  const viaHost = [\\n    `MemberExpression[object.name=${HOSTS}]${named('property')}`,\\n130→    `MemberExpression[object.name=${HOSTS}] > TemplateLiteral.property[expressions.length=0][quasis.0.value.cooked=${banned}]`,\\n    `:matches(VariableDeclarator[init.name=${HOSTS}], AssignmentExpression[right.name=${HOSTS}]) > ObjectPattern > Property${named('key')}`,\\n  ].join(', ');\\n  const swapped = `/^(${SIM_MATH_NAMES.join('|')})$/`;\\n  const mathFunction = `MemberExpression[object.name='Math']:matches([property.name=${swapped}], [property.value=${swapped}])`;\\n  const alias = [\\n    `:matches(VariableDeclarator[init.name='Math'], AssignmentExpression[right.name='Math']) > ObjectPattern`,\\n    `VariableDeclarator > ${mathFunction}.init`,\\n    `AssignmentExpression > ${mathFunction}.right`,\\n  ].join(', ');\\n140→  return [\\n    {\\n      name: 'sim: clocks, randomness, DOM, Web Audio',\\n      files: SIM_SIDE,\\n      ignores: ['**/*.test.ts'],\\n      plugins: { sim: simPlugin },\\n      rules: {\\n        'sim/no-restricted-globals': [\\n          'error',\\n          ...Object.entries(GLOBALS).map(([name, message]) => ({ name, message })),\\n150→        ],\\n        'sim/no-restricted-properties': ['error', { object: 'Math', property: 'random', message: RANDOM }],\\n        'sim/no-restricted-syntax': [\\n          'error',\\n          {\\n            selector: viaHost,\\n            message:\\n              \\\"a banned global reached through globalThis, self or global is still banned: sim-side code reads no clock, schedules nothing by wall time, touches no DOM or Web Audio, and draws randomness only from named streams, rng('<stream>') (PLAN.md §6.5)\\\",\\n          },\\n          { selector: 'ImportExpression', message: DYNAMIC },\\n160→          { selector: alias, message: ALIAS },\\n          {\\n            selector: \\\"BinaryExpression[operator='**'], AssignmentExpression[operator='**=']\\\",\\n            message:\\n              'write Math.pow in sim-side code: the sim swaps an fdlibm pow into Math while it steps, and ** escapes it (PLAN.md §6.5)',\\n          },\\n        ],\\n      },\\n    },\\n    imports('sim: three.js and Node built-ins', SIM_SIDE, [THREE_ENTRY, NODE_PREFIX]),\\n170→    imports('sim: Node built-ins in core/math.ts, which takes three.js', ['engine/core/math.ts'], [NODE_PREFIX]),\\n  ];\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"110→/** A `sim/no-restricted-imports` block: every Node built-in by its bare name, then `patterns`. */\\nfunction imports(name: string, files: string[], patterns: object[]): Linter.Config {\\n  const paths = builtinModules\\n    .filter((module) => !module.startsWith('node:'))\\n    .map((module) => ({ name: module, message: NODE }));\\n  return {\\n    name,\\n    files,\\n    ignores: ['**/*.test.ts'],\\n    plugins: { sim: simPlugin },\\n120→    rules: { 'sim/no-restricted-imports': ['error', { paths, patterns }] },\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n/** The sim-side blocks: globals, properties and syntax over all sim-side files, then imports (core/math.ts last). */\\nexport function simSideBlocks(): Linter.Config[] {\\n  const banned = `/^(${Object.keys(GLOBALS).join('|')})$/`;\\n  const named = (node: string) => `:matches([${node}.name=${banned}], [${node}.value=${banned}])`;\\n  const viaHost = [\\n    `MemberExpression[object.name=${HOSTS}]${named('property')}`,\\n130→    `MemberExpression[object.name=${HOSTS}] > TemplateLiteral.property[expressions.length=0][quasis.0.value.cooked=${banned}]`,\\n    `:matches(VariableDeclarator[init.name=${HOSTS}], AssignmentExpression[right.name=${HOSTS}]) > ObjectPattern > Property${named('key')}`,\\n  ].join(', ');\\n  const swapped = `/^(${SIM_MATH_NAMES.join('|')})$/`;\\n  const mathFunction = `MemberExpression[object.name='Math']:matches([property.name=${swapped}], [property.value=${swapped}])`;\\n  const alias = [\\n    `:matches(VariableDeclarator[init.name='Math'], AssignmentExpression[right.name='Math']) > ObjectPattern`,\\n    `VariableDeclarator > ${mathFunction}.init`,\\n    `AssignmentExpression > ${mathFunction}.right`,\\n  ].join(', ');\\n140→  return [\\n    {\\n      name: 'sim: clocks, randomness, DOM, Web Audio',\\n      files: SIM_SIDE,\\n      ignores: ['**/*.test.ts'],\\n      plugins: { sim: simPlugin },\\n      rules: {\\n        'sim/no-restricted-globals': [\\n          'error',\\n          ...Object.entries(GLOBALS).map(([name, message]) => ({ name, message })),\\n150→        ],\\n        'sim/no-restricted-properties': ['error', { object: 'Math', property: 'random', message: RANDOM }],\\n        'sim/no-restricted-syntax': [\\n          'error',\\n          {\\n            selector: viaHost,\\n            message:\\n              \\\"a banned global reached through globalThis, self or global is still banned: sim-side code reads no clock, schedules nothing by wall time, touches no DOM or Web Audio, and draws randomness only from named streams, rng('<stream>') (PLAN.md §6.5)\\\",\\n          },\\n          { selector: 'ImportExpression', message: DYNAMIC },\\n160→          { selector: alias, message: ALIAS },\\n          {\\n            selector: \\\"BinaryExpression[operator='**'], AssignmentExpression[operator='**=']\\\",\\n            message:\\n              'write Math.pow in sim-side code: the sim swaps an fdlibm pow into Math while it steps, and ** escapes it (PLAN.md §6.5)',\\n          },\\n        ],\\n      },\\n    },\\n    imports('sim: three.js and Node built-ins', SIM_SIDE, [THREE_ENTRY, NODE_PREFIX]),\\n170→    imports('sim: Node built-ins in core/math.ts, which takes three.js', ['engine/core/math.ts'], [NODE_PREFIX]),\\n  ];\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/tools/eslint/simSide.ts\",\"offset\":110,\"limit\":150,\"raw_output\":\"/** A `sim/no-restricted-imports` block: every Node built-in by its bare name, then `patterns`. */\\nfunction imports(name: string, files: string[], patterns: object[]): Linter.Config {\\n  const paths = builtinModules\\n    .filter((module) => !module.startsWith('node:'))\\n    .map((module) => ({ name: module, message: NODE }));\\n  return {\\n    name,\\n    files,\\n    ignores: ['**/*.test.ts'],\\n    plugins: { sim: simPlugin },\\n    rules: { 'sim/no-restricted-imports': ['error', { paths, patterns }] },\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n/** The sim-side blocks: globals, properties and syntax over all sim-side files, then imports (core/math.ts last). */\\nexport function simSideBlocks(): Linter.Config[] {\\n  const banned = `/^(${Object.keys(GLOBALS).join('|')})$/`;\\n  const named = (node: string) => `:matches([${node}.name=${banned}], [${node}.value=${banned}])`;\\n  const viaHost = [\\n    `MemberExpression[object.name=${HOSTS}]${named('property')}`,\\n    `MemberExpression[object.name=${HOSTS}] > TemplateLiteral.property[expressions.length=0][quasis.0.value.cooked=${banned}]`,\\n    `:matches(VariableDeclarator[init.name=${HOSTS}], AssignmentExpression[right.name=${HOSTS}]) > ObjectPattern > Property${named('key')}`,\\n  ].join(', ');\\n  const swapped = `/^(${SIM_MATH_NAMES.join('|')})$/`;\\n  const mathFunction = `MemberExpression[object.name='Math']:matches([property.name=${swapped}], [property.value=${swapped}])`;\\n  const alias = [\\n    `:matches(VariableDeclarator[init.name='Math'], AssignmentExpression[right.name='Math']) > ObjectPattern`,\\n    `VariableDeclarator > ${mathFunction}.init`,\\n    `AssignmentExpression > ${mathFunction}.right`,\\n  ].join(', ');\\n  return [\\n    {\\n      name: 'sim: clocks, randomness, DOM, Web Audio',\\n      files: SIM_SIDE,\\n      ignores: ['**/*.test.ts'],\\n      plugins: { sim: simPlugin },\\n      rules: {\\n        'sim/no-restricted-globals': [\\n          'error',\\n          ...Object.entries(GLOBALS).map(([name, message]) => ({ name, message })),\\n        ],\\n        'sim/no-restricted-properties': ['error', { object: 'Math', property: 'random', message: RANDOM }],\\n        'sim/no-restricted-syntax': [\\n          'error',\\n          {\\n            selector: viaHost,\\n            message:\\n              \\\"a banned global reached through globalThis, self or global is still banned: sim-side code reads no clock, schedules nothing by wall time, touches no DOM or Web Audio, and draws randomness only from named streams, rng('<stream>') (PLAN.md §6.5)\\\",\\n          },\\n          { selector: 'ImportExpression', message: DYNAMIC },\\n          { selector: alias, message: ALIAS },\\n          {\\n            selector: \\\"BinaryExpression[operator='**'], AssignmentExpression[operator='**=']\\\",\\n            message:\\n              'write Math.pow in sim-side code: the sim swaps an fdlibm pow into Math while it steps, and ** escapes it (PLAN.md §6.5)',\\n          },\\n        ],\\n      },\\n    },\\n    imports('sim: three.js and Node built-ins', SIM_SIDE, [THREE_ENTRY, NODE_PREFIX]),\\n    imports('sim: Node built-ins in core/math.ts, which takes three.js', ['engine/core/math.ts'], [NODE_PREFIX]),\\n  ];\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":172}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-e5a21458-9071-4ff4-99cb-2a389c93b173-26","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,55,51,49,95,95,120,53,57,99,49,100,51,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,78,111,32,109,97,116,99,104,101,115,32,102,111,117,110,100,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":1,\"match_count\":0,\"file_matches\":[]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-e5a21458-9071-4ff4-99cb-2a389c93b173-27","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,55,51,49,95,95,120,53,57,99,49,100,51,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,78,111,32,109,97,116,99,104,101,115,32,102,111,117,110,100,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":1,\"match_count\":0,\"file_matches\":[]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-e5a21458-9071-4ff4-99cb-2a389c93b173-28","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file Shared types for the operation sim (labs/game/op/): tools, target kinds, seats, and the operation itself.\\n * The sim is plain TypeScript. It reads hands, never the clock, the DOM, or Math.random. Pages and tests both\\n * drive `stepOp` (labs/game/op/step.ts) with the same hand records a pad would produce.\\n */\\n\\n/** The eight instruments, in radial order. */\\nexport const TOOLS = ['scalpel', 'forceps', 'suture', 'drain', 'laser', 'syringe', 'gel', 'scanner'] as const;\\n\\n10→/** One instrument id. */\\nexport type Tool = (typeof TOOLS)[number];\\n\\n/** Every target kind a tool can meet, including bare tissue (`body`). */\\nexport const KINDS = [\\n  'body',\\n  'pool',\\n  'shard',\\n  'wound',\\n  'guide',\\n20→  'mass',\\n  'nodule',\\n  'bleeder',\\n  'abrasion',\\n  'numb',\\n  'flap',\\n  'cocoon',\\n  'lull',\\n  'matron',\\n  'solace',\\n30→  'reverie',\\n  'decoy',\\n  'balmNode',\\n  'balmCell',\\n  'mercy',\\n  'mote',\\n  'tendril',\\n  'binder',\\n] as const;\\n\\n40→/** One target kind. */\\nexport type Kind = (typeof KINDS)[number];\\n\\n/** What a tool does to a kind, or `refuse` when it must not. */\\nexport type Effect =\\n  | 'cut'\\n  | 'slip'\\n  | 'split'\\n  | 'grab'\\n  | 'lift'\\n50→  | 'stitch'\\n  | 'drain'\\n  | 'burn'\\n  | 'inject'\\n  | 'bind'\\n  | 'paint'\\n  | 'reveal'\\n  | 'pop'\\n  | 'refuse';\\n\\n60→/** How hard the shift is. */\\nexport type Difficulty = 'intern' | 'resident' | 'attending';\\n\\n/** A finished action's grade. */\\nexport type Rating = 'TEXTBOOK' | 'CLEAN' | 'ROUGH' | 'SLIP';\\n\\n/** Letter rank, plus the attending secret. */\\nexport type Rank = 'C' | 'B' | 'A' | 'S' | '★';\\n\\n/** One thing on the field. Unused numbers stay 0 so every kind shares one shape. */\\n70→export interface Target {\\n  id: number;\\n  kind: Kind;\\n  phase: number;\\n  site: number;\\n  patient: number;\\n  x: number;\\n  z: number;\\n  x2: number;\\n  z2: number;\\n80→  done: boolean;\\n  tag: string;\\n  /** Flap id this hides under, or -1. */\\n  under: number;\\n  locked: boolean;\\n  hidden: boolean;\\n  /** Field ticks of reveal left. 0 means a permanent reveal. */\\n  reveal: number;\\n  volume: number;\\n  volumeMax: number;\\n90→  bleed: number;\\n  deep: boolean;\\n  bleeding: boolean;\\n  lacquer: boolean;\\n  stitches: number;\\n  need: number;\\n  /** Fractional positions of stitches along the wound, 0 to 1. */\\n  stitchAt: number[];\\n  /** Guide polyline as flat x,z pairs. */\\n  path: number[];\\n100→  cut: number;\\n  samples: number;\\n  distSum: number;\\n  loop: boolean;\\n  burn: number;\\n  burnNeed: number;\\n  hp: number;\\n  gen: number;\\n  radius: number;\\n  stroke: number;\\n110→  cover: number;\\n  coverNeed: number;\\n  lift: number;\\n  /** Field ticks the flap stays clipped. */\\n  clipped: number;\\n  vulnerable: boolean;\\n  dose: number;\\n  doseNeed: number;\\n  surfaced: boolean;\\n  exposures: number;\\n120→  laserDamage: number;\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file Shared types for the operation sim (labs/game/op/): tools, target kinds, seats, and the operation itself.\\n * The sim is plain TypeScript. It reads hands, never the clock, the DOM, or Math.random. Pages and tests both\\n * drive `stepOp` (labs/game/op/step.ts) with the same hand records a pad would produce.\\n */\\n\\n/** The eight instruments, in radial order. */\\nexport const TOOLS = ['scalpel', 'forceps', 'suture', 'drain', 'laser', 'syringe', 'gel', 'scanner'] as const;\\n\\n10→/** One instrument id. */\\nexport type Tool = (typeof TOOLS)[number];\\n\\n/** Every target kind a tool can meet, including bare tissue (`body`). */\\nexport const KINDS = [\\n  'body',\\n  'pool',\\n  'shard',\\n  'wound',\\n  'guide',\\n20→  'mass',\\n  'nodule',\\n  'bleeder',\\n  'abrasion',\\n  'numb',\\n  'flap',\\n  'cocoon',\\n  'lull',\\n  'matron',\\n  'solace',\\n30→  'reverie',\\n  'decoy',\\n  'balmNode',\\n  'balmCell',\\n  'mercy',\\n  'mote',\\n  'tendril',\\n  'binder',\\n] as const;\\n\\n40→/** One target kind. */\\nexport type Kind = (typeof KINDS)[number];\\n\\n/** What a tool does to a kind, or `refuse` when it must not. */\\nexport type Effect =\\n  | 'cut'\\n  | 'slip'\\n  | 'split'\\n  | 'grab'\\n  | 'lift'\\n50→  | 'stitch'\\n  | 'drain'\\n  | 'burn'\\n  | 'inject'\\n  | 'bind'\\n  | 'paint'\\n  | 'reveal'\\n  | 'pop'\\n  | 'refuse';\\n\\n60→/** How hard the shift is. */\\nexport type Difficulty = 'intern' | 'resident' | 'attending';\\n\\n/** A finished action's grade. */\\nexport type Rating = 'TEXTBOOK' | 'CLEAN' | 'ROUGH' | 'SLIP';\\n\\n/** Letter rank, plus the attending secret. */\\nexport type Rank = 'C' | 'B' | 'A' | 'S' | '★';\\n\\n/** One thing on the field. Unused numbers stay 0 so every kind shares one shape. */\\n70→export interface Target {\\n  id: number;\\n  kind: Kind;\\n  phase: number;\\n  site: number;\\n  patient: number;\\n  x: number;\\n  z: number;\\n  x2: number;\\n  z2: number;\\n80→  done: boolean;\\n  tag: string;\\n  /** Flap id this hides under, or -1. */\\n  under: number;\\n  locked: boolean;\\n  hidden: boolean;\\n  /** Field ticks of reveal left. 0 means a permanent reveal. */\\n  reveal: number;\\n  volume: number;\\n  volumeMax: number;\\n90→  bleed: number;\\n  deep: boolean;\\n  bleeding: boolean;\\n  lacquer: boolean;\\n  stitches: number;\\n  need: number;\\n  /** Fractional positions of stitches along the wound, 0 to 1. */\\n  stitchAt: number[];\\n  /** Guide polyline as flat x,z pairs. */\\n  path: number[];\\n100→  cut: number;\\n  samples: number;\\n  distSum: number;\\n  loop: boolean;\\n  burn: number;\\n  burnNeed: number;\\n  hp: number;\\n  gen: number;\\n  radius: number;\\n  stroke: number;\\n110→  cover: number;\\n  coverNeed: number;\\n  lift: number;\\n  /** Field ticks the flap stays clipped. */\\n  clipped: number;\\n  vulnerable: boolean;\\n  dose: number;\\n  doseNeed: number;\\n  surfaced: boolean;\\n  exposures: number;\\n120→  laserDamage: number;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/types.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":120,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file Shared types for the operation sim (labs/game/op/): tools, target kinds, seats, and the operation itself.\\n * The sim is plain TypeScript. It reads hands, never the clock, the DOM, or Math.random. Pages and tests both\\n * drive `stepOp` (labs/game/op/step.ts) with the same hand records a pad would produce.\\n */\\n\\n/** The eight instruments, in radial order. */\\nexport const TOOLS = ['scalpel', 'forceps', 'suture', 'drain', 'laser', 'syringe', 'gel', 'scanner'] as const;\\n\\n/** One instrument id. */\\nexport type Tool = (typeof TOOLS)[number];\\n\\n/** Every target kind a tool can meet, including bare tissue (`body`). */\\nexport const KINDS = [\\n  'body',\\n  'pool',\\n  'shard',\\n  'wound',\\n  'guide',\\n  'mass',\\n  'nodule',\\n  'bleeder',\\n  'abrasion',\\n  'numb',\\n  'flap',\\n  'cocoon',\\n  'lull',\\n  'matron',\\n  'solace',\\n  'reverie',\\n  'decoy',\\n  'balmNode',\\n  'balmCell',\\n  'mercy',\\n  'mote',\\n  'tendril',\\n  'binder',\\n] as const;\\n\\n/** One target kind. */\\nexport type Kind = (typeof KINDS)[number];\\n\\n/** What a tool does to a kind, or `refuse` when it must not. */\\nexport type Effect =\\n  | 'cut'\\n  | 'slip'\\n  | 'split'\\n  | 'grab'\\n  | 'lift'\\n  | 'stitch'\\n  | 'drain'\\n  | 'burn'\\n  | 'inject'\\n  | 'bind'\\n  | 'paint'\\n  | 'reveal'\\n  | 'pop'\\n  | 'refuse';\\n\\n/** How hard the shift is. */\\nexport type Difficulty = 'intern' | 'resident' | 'attending';\\n\\n/** A finished action's grade. */\\nexport type Rating = 'TEXTBOOK' | 'CLEAN' | 'ROUGH' | 'SLIP';\\n\\n/** Letter rank, plus the attending secret. */\\nexport type Rank = 'C' | 'B' | 'A' | 'S' | '★';\\n\\n/** One thing on the field. Unused numbers stay 0 so every kind shares one shape. */\\nexport interface Target {\\n  id: number;\\n  kind: Kind;\\n  phase: number;\\n  site: number;\\n  patient: number;\\n  x: number;\\n  z: number;\\n  x2: number;\\n  z2: number;\\n  done: boolean;\\n  tag: string;\\n  /** Flap id this hides under, or -1. */\\n  under: number;\\n  locked: boolean;\\n  hidden: boolean;\\n  /** Field ticks of reveal left. 0 means a permanent reveal. */\\n  reveal: number;\\n  volume: number;\\n  volumeMax: number;\\n  bleed: number;\\n  deep: boolean;\\n  bleeding: boolean;\\n  lacquer: boolean;\\n  stitches: number;\\n  need: number;\\n  /** Fractional positions of stitches along the wound, 0 to 1. */\\n  stitchAt: number[];\\n  /** Guide polyline as flat x,z pairs. */\\n  path: number[];\\n  cut: number;\\n  samples: number;\\n  distSum: number;\\n  loop: boolean;\\n  burn: number;\\n  burnNeed: number;\\n  hp: number;\\n  gen: number;\\n  radius: number;\\n  stroke: number;\\n  cover: number;\\n  coverNeed: number;\\n  lift: number;\\n  /** Field ticks the flap stays clipped. */\\n  clipped: number;\\n  vulnerable: boolean;\\n  dose: number;\\n  doseNeed: number;\\n  surfaced: boolean;\\n  exposures: number;\\n  laserDamage: number;\\n\",\"total_lines\":364}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"e22b08f4-83f6-4864-91c9-91f25fed0dfd"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_83","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Sim-side import restrictions for lab scenes only ban three.js and Node builtins. Local modules can still be imported.\n\nLinting is file-based, not transitive. Scenes can import op/ modules that use banned features like Date or DOM. The scene file itself must stay sim-side clean. Next I will look at custom intent registration and how axis works.\n\nI will examine labs/box for look and prop examples. The main scene will use settings for game state and balance sliders. An opview component will expose the Op to the HUD. Since components are plain data, the Op itself must live in a module-level variable that the scene writes and the page reads.\n\nA dedicated `opState.ts` module is the cleanest way to share the Op between scene and page. The scene steps it and the page reads it for rendering. Storing the Op on the world via a WeakMap is another option, but arbitrary fields may not be allowed.\n\nA module-level singleton in `bridge.ts` is the chosen approach. The scene will create and assign the Op to a module-level variable, and the page will read it via a getter. This avoids sim-side restrictions on world fields, though it assumes one engine per world.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7ab135f3-504b-47a2-879a-699429b34eac-29","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/types.ts","offset":120,"limit":250}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7ab135f3-504b-47a2-879a-699429b34eac-30","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"export function defineSettings|export function defineScene|export function defineComponent|CustomIntent|defineDevAction","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-