ber\":130,\"content\":\"      \\\"The look drawn instead while the camera is a perspective one (its variant: same style, sky, resolution and textures); '' keeps this.\\\",\"},{\"line_number\":132,\"content\":\"  resolution: {\"},{\"line_number\":137,\"content\":\"      \\\"The resolution mode it is drawn at while gfx.resolution is 'auto' (pixels, balanced or full); '' keeps the engine's pixels.\\\",\"},{\"line_number\":139,\"content\":\"  textures: {\"},{\"line_number\":144,\"content\":\"      \\\"How every material's textures are filtered: 'smooth' blends their texels, 'pixel' keeps them crisp; '' keeps each texture's own.\\\",\"},{\"line_number\":240,\"content\":\"    description: 'Low resolution on a curved tube with scanlines, glow and colour fringes.',\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"6a847414-042d-4fee-926a-78dd20e92417"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_92","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I will implement a substantial but coherent game.\n\nStarting file creation. The bridge scene will hold the live Op and expose bind, read, and clear functions. The main scene will manage game settings and a component chart.\n\nThe scene setup will create the Op and spawn the player and props. The step logic must skip stepping when no hands are present, or the clock would keep running on title screens. The director controls game.run, so the scene should only execute operations during active gameplay.\n\nThe director will manage six runs: title, story scenes, briefs, ops, debriefs, board, credits, and free surgery. Story and brief screens will not step the operation. Free Surgery mode will unlock after the story and select any cleared case. The page director in flow.ts is the UI state machine, separate from the bot walk director.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2cc98b5f-170c-4786-9ac5-c60606d087c1-64","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/input/devices/virtual.ts","limit":100}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2cc98b5f-170c-4786-9ac5-c60606d087c1-65","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"custom|axis","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/input/devices/virtual.ts"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2760,"output_tokens":725,"cache_read_input_tokens":98944,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"5b211b76-2aed-4fb0-9cdb-aa53e44565d8"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-2cc98b5f-170c-4786-9ac5-c60606d087c1-64","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The virtual device (PLAN.md WP 3.3, §8.3; doctrine: Agent-operable): input made by code instead of hands, the\\n * one `__engine.input` drives (engine/input/devices/inspector.ts). It works in actions and intents, not codes:\\n * `press('jump')` taps an action for the next step, `hold('sprint')` keeps one down, `axis('move', [0, 1])` pushes a\\n * virtual stick (`[right, forward]`, turned by the camera as keys are), and `axis('cam' | 'look' | 'aim' | 'game:…',\\n * value)` sets that intent outright; `null` lets go.\\n *\\n * `play(script, step)` runs a script one sim step at a time, each line `<steps> [move=x,y] [look=yaw,pitch] [cam=ψ]\\n * [aim=x,y,z] [hold=a,b] [tap=a] [game:key=n]`, `#` comments (engine/input/script.ts): a line holds its values for\\n10→ * its steps on top of what the device holds, and taps on its first step. A page's input (engine/input/input.ts)\\n * merges the device into every sample, so the same calls drive a running page.\\n *\\n * Invariants: taps last one step (the next sample or step played), holds and axes until changed. Values are checked\\n * when given (`INPUT_BAD_VIRTUAL`): names are non-empty strings, `move` and `look` two finite numbers, `aim` three,\\n * `cam` one, a custom key plain data. Intents come out unnormalized; the session normalizes them.\\n *\\n * @example\\n * const pad = createVirtualDevice();\\n * pad.axis('move', [0, 1]);\\n20→ * pad.press('jump');\\n * virtualIntents(pad.take(), Math.PI / 2); // { move: [1, 6.1e-17], b: [], p: ['jump'] }: forward is +X at ψ = π/2\\n * const steps: unknown[] = [];\\n * playScript(pad, '2 hold=sprint tap=dash\\\\n1', (intents) => steps.push(intents));\\n * steps.length; // 3: the second step holds sprint without the tap, the third holds nothing but the stick\\n * @see engine/input/devices/virtual.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { codeError, defineCodes } from '../../core/log';\\nimport { isPlainObject, show } from '../../core/schema';\\nimport { fromCamera, type IntentValue } from '../intents';\\n30→import { names, numbers, parseScript, type ValueReader } from '../script';\\n\\n/** The codes this module raises, with their fixes. */\\nexport const VIRTUAL_CODES = defineCodes('input', {\\n  INPUT_BAD_VIRTUAL: {\\n    template: '{what}: {problem}',\\n    fix: \\\"press(action) and hold(action) take an action's name; axis takes 'move' or 'look' [x, y], 'aim' [x, y, z], 'cam' (rad) or a 'game:key' with plain data, and null to let go\\\",\\n    doc: 'Raised by the virtual device (engine/input/devices/virtual.ts) and `__engine.input` for an empty action name, an unknown axis, or a value of the wrong shape.',\\n  },\\n});\\n40→\\n/** The axes the device can hold, and how many numbers each takes (0 for a custom key's plain data). */\\nconst AXES: Readonly<Record<string, number>> = { move: 2, look: 2, aim: 3, cam: 1 };\\n\\n/** A namespaced custom intent key. */\\nconst CUSTOM = /^[a-z][A-Za-z0-9]*:[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+$/;\\n\\n/** What the device holds for one step: actions held and tapped, and its axes by name. */\\nexport interface VirtualSample {\\n  held: string[];\\n50→  taps: string[];\\n  axes: Record<string, IntentValue>;\\n}\\n\\n/** The virtual device. */\\nexport interface VirtualDevice {\\n  /** Taps `action`: pressed in the next step, not held. */\\n  press(action: string): void;\\n  /** Holds `action` down (`down = false` lets go). */\\n  hold(action: string, down?: boolean): void;\\n60→  /** Sets an axis: `move` `[right, forward]`, `look`, `aim`, `cam` or a `game:key`; `null` lets go. */\\n  axis(name: string, value: unknown): void;\\n  /** What the device holds now, without using up its taps. */\\n  peek(): VirtualSample;\\n  /** What the device holds for the next step; its taps are used up. */\\n  take(): VirtualSample;\\n  /** Whether anything was pressed, held or moved since the last `take` (prompts follow the last device used). */\\n  readonly touched: boolean;\\n  /** Lets go of everything. */\\n  clear(): void;\\n70→}\\n\\n/** Throws `INPUT_BAD_VIRTUAL` unless `name` is an action's name. */\\nfunction checkAction(name: unknown, what: string): string {\\n  if (typeof name !== 'string' || !name) throw codeError('INPUT_BAD_VIRTUAL', { what, problem: `${show(name)} is no action name` }); // prettier-ignore\\n  return name;\\n}\\n\\n/** Makes a virtual device, holding nothing. */\\nexport function createVirtualDevice(): VirtualDevice {\\n80→  const held = new Set<string>();\\n  let taps = new Set<string>();\\n  const axes: Record<string, IntentValue> = {};\\n  let touched = false;\\n  const peek = (): VirtualSample => ({ held: [...held].sort(), taps: [...taps].sort(), axes: { ...axes } });\\n  return {\\n    press(action) {\\n      taps.add(checkAction(action, 'press'));\\n      touched = true;\\n    },\\n90→    hold(action, down = true) {\\n      if (down) held.add(checkAction(action, 'hold'));\\n      else held.delete(checkAction(action, 'hold'));\\n      touched = true;\\n    },\\n    axis(name, value) {\\n      const n = AXES[name];\\n      if (n === undefined && !CUSTOM.test(name)) {\\n        throw codeError('INPUT_BAD_VIRTUAL', { what: `axis(${show(name)})`, problem: 'no such axis' });\\n      }\\n100→      if (value === null || value === undefined) delete axes[name];\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The virtual device (PLAN.md WP 3.3, §8.3; doctrine: Agent-operable): input made by code instead of hands, the\\n * one `__engine.input` drives (engine/input/devices/inspector.ts). It works in actions and intents, not codes:\\n * `press('jump')` taps an action for the next step, `hold('sprint')` keeps one down, `axis('move', [0, 1])` pushes a\\n * virtual stick (`[right, forward]`, turned by the camera as keys are), and `axis('cam' | 'look' | 'aim' | 'game:…',\\n * value)` sets that intent outright; `null` lets go.\\n *\\n * `play(script, step)` runs a script one sim step at a time, each line `<steps> [move=x,y] [look=yaw,pitch] [cam=ψ]\\n * [aim=x,y,z] [hold=a,b] [tap=a] [game:key=n]`, `#` comments (engine/input/script.ts): a line holds its values for\\n10→ * its steps on top of what the device holds, and taps on its first step. A page's input (engine/input/input.ts)\\n * merges the device into every sample, so the same calls drive a running page.\\n *\\n * Invariants: taps last one step (the next sample or step played), holds and axes until changed. Values are checked\\n * when given (`INPUT_BAD_VIRTUAL`): names are non-empty strings, `move` and `look` two finite numbers, `aim` three,\\n * `cam` one, a custom key plain data. Intents come out unnormalized; the session normalizes them.\\n *\\n * @example\\n * const pad = createVirtualDevice();\\n * pad.axis('move', [0, 1]);\\n20→ * pad.press('jump');\\n * virtualIntents(pad.take(), Math.PI / 2); // { move: [1, 6.1e-17], b: [], p: ['jump'] }: forward is +X at ψ = π/2\\n * const steps: unknown[] = [];\\n * playScript(pad, '2 hold=sprint tap=dash\\\\n1', (intents) => steps.push(intents));\\n * steps.length; // 3: the second step holds sprint without the tap, the third holds nothing but the stick\\n * @see engine/input/devices/virtual.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { codeError, defineCodes } from '../../core/log';\\nimport { isPlainObject, show } from '../../core/schema';\\nimport { fromCamera, type IntentValue } from '../intents';\\n30→import { names, numbers, parseScript, type ValueReader } from '../script';\\n\\n/** The codes this module raises, with their fixes. */\\nexport const VIRTUAL_CODES = defineCodes('input', {\\n  INPUT_BAD_VIRTUAL: {\\n    template: '{what}: {problem}',\\n    fix: \\\"press(action) and hold(action) take an action's name; axis takes 'move' or 'look' [x, y], 'aim' [x, y, z], 'cam' (rad) or a 'game:key' with plain data, and null to let go\\\",\\n    doc: 'Raised by the virtual device (engine/input/devices/virtual.ts) and `__engine.input` for an empty action name, an unknown axis, or a value of the wrong shape.',\\n  },\\n});\\n40→\\n/** The axes the device can hold, and how many numbers each takes (0 for a custom key's plain data). */\\nconst AXES: Readonly<Record<string, number>> = { move: 2, look: 2, aim: 3, cam: 1 };\\n\\n/** A namespaced custom intent key. */\\nconst CUSTOM = /^[a-z][A-Za-z0-9]*:[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+$/;\\n\\n/** What the device holds for one step: actions held and tapped, and its axes by name. */\\nexport interface VirtualSample {\\n  held: string[];\\n50→  taps: string[];\\n  axes: Record<string, IntentValue>;\\n}\\n\\n/** The virtual device. */\\nexport interface VirtualDevice {\\n  /** Taps `action`: pressed in the next step, not held. */\\n  press(action: string): void;\\n  /** Holds `action` down (`down = false` lets go). */\\n  hold(action: string, down?: boolean): void;\\n60→  /** Sets an axis: `move` `[right, forward]`, `look`, `aim`, `cam` or a `game:key`; `null` lets go. */\\n  axis(name: string, value: unknown): void;\\n  /** What the device holds now, without using up its taps. */\\n  peek(): VirtualSample;\\n  /** What the device holds for the next step; its taps are used up. */\\n  take(): VirtualSample;\\n  /** Whether anything was pressed, held or moved since the last `take` (prompts follow the last device used). */\\n  readonly touched: boolean;\\n  /** Lets go of everything. */\\n  clear(): void;\\n70→}\\n\\n/** Throws `INPUT_BAD_VIRTUAL` unless `name` is an action's name. */\\nfunction checkAction(name: unknown, what: string): string {\\n  if (typeof name !== 'string' || !name) throw codeError('INPUT_BAD_VIRTUAL', { what, problem: `${show(name)} is no action name` }); // prettier-ignore\\n  return name;\\n}\\n\\n/** Makes a virtual device, holding nothing. */\\nexport function createVirtualDevice(): VirtualDevice {\\n80→  const held = new Set<string>();\\n  let taps = new Set<string>();\\n  const axes: Record<string, IntentValue> = {};\\n  let touched = false;\\n  const peek = (): VirtualSample => ({ held: [...held].sort(), taps: [...taps].sort(), axes: { ...axes } });\\n  return {\\n    press(action) {\\n      taps.add(checkAction(action, 'press'));\\n      touched = true;\\n    },\\n90→    hold(action, down = true) {\\n      if (down) held.add(checkAction(action, 'hold'));\\n      else held.delete(checkAction(action, 'hold'));\\n      touched = true;\\n    },\\n    axis(name, value) {\\n      const n = AXES[name];\\n      if (n === undefined && !CUSTOM.test(name)) {\\n        throw codeError('INPUT_BAD_VIRTUAL', { what: `axis(${show(name)})`, problem: 'no such axis' });\\n      }\\n100→      if (value === null || value === undefined) delete axes[name];\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/input/devices/virtual.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":100,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file The virtual device (PLAN.md WP 3.3, §8.3; doctrine: Agent-operable): input made by code instead of hands, the\\n * one `__engine.input` drives (engine/input/devices/inspector.ts). It works in actions and intents, not codes:\\n * `press('jump')` taps an action for the next step, `hold('sprint')` keeps one down, `axis('move', [0, 1])` pushes a\\n * virtual stick (`[right, forward]`, turned by the camera as keys are), and `axis('cam' | 'look' | 'aim' | 'game:…',\\n * value)` sets that intent outright; `null` lets go.\\n *\\n * `play(script, step)` runs a script one sim step at a time, each line `<steps> [move=x,y] [look=yaw,pitch] [cam=ψ]\\n * [aim=x,y,z] [hold=a,b] [tap=a] [game:key=n]`, `#` comments (engine/input/script.ts): a line holds its values for\\n * its steps on top of what the device holds, and taps on its first step. A page's input (engine/input/input.ts)\\n * merges the device into every sample, so the same calls drive a running page.\\n *\\n * Invariants: taps last one step (the next sample or step played), holds and axes until changed. Values are checked\\n * when given (`INPUT_BAD_VIRTUAL`): names are non-empty strings, `move` and `look` two finite numbers, `aim` three,\\n * `cam` one, a custom key plain data. Intents come out unnormalized; the session normalizes them.\\n *\\n * @example\\n * const pad = createVirtualDevice();\\n * pad.axis('move', [0, 1]);\\n * pad.press('jump');\\n * virtualIntents(pad.take(), Math.PI / 2); // { move: [1, 6.1e-17], b: [], p: ['jump'] }: forward is +X at ψ = π/2\\n * const steps: unknown[] = [];\\n * playScript(pad, '2 hold=sprint tap=dash\\\\n1', (intents) => steps.push(intents));\\n * steps.length; // 3: the second step holds sprint without the tap, the third holds nothing but the stick\\n * @see engine/input/devices/virtual.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { codeError, defineCodes } from '../../core/log';\\nimport { isPlainObject, show } from '../../core/schema';\\nimport { fromCamera, type IntentValue } from '../intents';\\nimport { names, numbers, parseScript, type ValueReader } from '../script';\\n\\n/** The codes this module raises, with their fixes. */\\nexport const VIRTUAL_CODES = defineCodes('input', {\\n  INPUT_BAD_VIRTUAL: {\\n    template: '{what}: {problem}',\\n    fix: \\\"press(action) and hold(action) take an action's name; axis takes 'move' or 'look' [x, y], 'aim' [x, y, z], 'cam' (rad) or a 'game:key' with plain data, and null to let go\\\",\\n    doc: 'Raised by the virtual device (engine/input/devices/virtual.ts) and `__engine.input` for an empty action name, an unknown axis, or a value of the wrong shape.',\\n  },\\n});\\n\\n/** The axes the device can hold, and how many numbers each takes (0 for a custom key's plain data). */\\nconst AXES: Readonly<Record<string, number>> = { move: 2, look: 2, aim: 3, cam: 1 };\\n\\n/** A namespaced custom intent key. */\\nconst CUSTOM = /^[a-z][A-Za-z0-9]*:[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+$/;\\n\\n/** What the device holds for one step: actions held and tapped, and its axes by name. */\\nexport interface VirtualSample {\\n  held: string[];\\n  taps: string[];\\n  axes: Record<string, IntentValue>;\\n}\\n\\n/** The virtual device. */\\nexport interface VirtualDevice {\\n  /** Taps `action`: pressed in the next step, not held. */\\n  press(action: string): void;\\n  /** Holds `action` down (`down = false` lets go). */\\n  hold(action: string, down?: boolean): void;\\n  /** Sets an axis: `move` `[right, forward]`, `look`, `aim`, `cam` or a `game:key`; `null` lets go. */\\n  axis(name: string, value: unknown): void;\\n  /** What the device holds now, without using up its taps. */\\n  peek(): VirtualSample;\\n  /** What the device holds for the next step; its taps are used up. */\\n  take(): VirtualSample;\\n  /** Whether anything was pressed, held or moved since the last `take` (prompts follow the last device used). */\\n  readonly touched: boolean;\\n  /** Lets go of everything. */\\n  clear(): void;\\n}\\n\\n/** Throws `INPUT_BAD_VIRTUAL` unless `name` is an action's name. */\\nfunction checkAction(name: unknown, what: string): string {\\n  if (typeof name !== 'string' || !name) throw codeError('INPUT_BAD_VIRTUAL', { what, problem: `${show(name)} is no action name` }); // prettier-ignore\\n  return name;\\n}\\n\\n/** Makes a virtual device, holding nothing. */\\nexport function createVirtualDevice(): VirtualDevice {\\n  const held = new Set<string>();\\n  let taps = new Set<string>();\\n  const axes: Record<string, IntentValue> = {};\\n  let touched = false;\\n  const peek = (): VirtualSample => ({ held: [...held].sort(), taps: [...taps].sort(), axes: { ...axes } });\\n  return {\\n    press(action) {\\n      taps.add(checkAction(action, 'press'));\\n      touched = true;\\n    },\\n    hold(action, down = true) {\\n      if (down) held.add(checkAction(action, 'hold'));\\n      else held.delete(checkAction(action, 'hold'));\\n      touched = true;\\n    },\\n    axis(name, value) {\\n      const n = AXES[name];\\n      if (n === undefined && !CUSTOM.test(name)) {\\n        throw codeError('INPUT_BAD_VIRTUAL', { what: `axis(${show(name)})`, problem: 'no such axis' });\\n      }\\n      if (value === null || value === undefined) delete axes[name];\\n\",\"total_lines\":179}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-2cc98b5f-170c-4786-9ac5-c60606d087c1-65","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,55,51,49,95,95,120,53,57,99,49,100,51,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,49,53,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,55,51,49,95,95,120,53,57,99,49,100,51,47,119,111,114,107,47,84,114,97,117,109,97,45,67,111,109,112,97,115,115,45,84,114,97,117,109,97,45,67,101,110,116,101,114,45,83,101,99,111,110,100,45,79,112,105,110,105,111,110,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,55,51,49,47,101,110,103,105,110,101,47,105,110,112,117,116,47,100,101,118,105,99,101,115,47,118,105,114,116,117,97,108,46,116,115,10,52,58,32,42,32,96,112,114,101,115,115,40,39,106,117,109,112,39,41,96,32,116,97,112,115,32,97,110,32,97,99,116,105,111,110,32,102,111,114,32,116,104,101,32,110,101,120,116,32,115,116,101,112,44,32,96,104,111,108,100,40,39,115,112,114,105,110,116,39,41,96,32,107,101,101,112,115,32,111,110,101,32,100,111,119,110,44,32,96,97,120,105,115,40,39,109,111,118,101,39,44,32,91,48,44,32,49,93,41,96,32,112,117,11