{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_95","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"index.html links to touch.css without the crossorigin attribute.\n\nThe stylesheet link must be removed so the one-file test passes. I will import touch.css from main.ts instead.\n\nImporting an engine CSS file might trigger a public-api rule. I will instead inline the needed styles in a game stylesheet and import it from main.ts.\n\nsession.js must be an inline script placed immediately after the charset meta tag. It cannot use a src attribute because externalRefs only checks src and href. The one-file build inserts the note after charset, then inlines the module script.\n\nThe inlineBuild comment is a comment, not a script. session.js remains the first script tag. The harness test should pass.\n\nThe harness test should verify the first script is session.js and its text matches the file. The WebGPU check script belongs immediately after session.js. I will now implement the game flow in app/flow.ts.\n\nThe game flow will use a screen manager to show one panel at a time. The store will hold progress data including cleared levels, ranks, postcards, attendance status, and settings. An attract mode will run for ten seconds on the title screen before cycling through bot hands. Any input returns the player to the title. During this mode saves are disabled so the store created at boot remains untouched.\n\nSave operations will be skipped during attract mode by returning early from save() when the game is attracting. The dev menu will contain tabs for Play, Balance, View, Author, and Data with sliders that call inspector.set. Audio will use defineSong for title, or, mercy, story, jingle, fanfare, and fail, plus defineSfx for tools, with music volume set to 0.1. Voice synthesis will generate syllables via OfflineAudioContext in audio/voicePlay.ts. The hub will download session.js into labs/game/net/session.js and paste it into index.html.\n\nA test will compare the downloaded session.js against the inline copy. The page-side lockstep wrapper will use pure sequencer logic, but its host tick differs from the node test version. Live sessions will route through AIHub.send, so I need to read the hub README for the exact send API. For now I will implement a client based on the plan's message shapes and typical AIHub methods like connect, ready, fail, answer, finish, send, on, time, active, and server. An end-to-end Playwright script will print JSON lines.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b30b896f-1bff-4688-a5c3-8ffad7e32057-72","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"defineProp\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/box","glob":"*.ts","head_limit":15}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b30b896f-1bff-4688-a5c3-8ffad7e32057-73","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/gfx/geometry/geometry.ts","limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b30b896f-1bff-4688-a5c3-8ffad7e32057-74","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/PLAN.md","offset":51,"limit":5}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3379,"output_tokens":1477,"cache_read_input_tokens":107520,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"0dc37485-72be-4f5b-a9ed-99d16b104aae"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-b30b896f-1bff-4688-a5c3-8ffad7e32057-72","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,55,51,49,95,95,120,53,57,99,49,100,51,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,78,111,32,109,97,116,99,104,101,115,32,102,111,117,110,100,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":1,\"match_count\":0,\"file_matches\":[]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-b30b896f-1bff-4688-a5c3-8ffad7e32057-73","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The geometry registry (PLAN.md WP 2.4, §6.6, I-29): the registry kind `geometry`, one entry per shape a prop,\\n * a level or a body names by id (§6.1: `world` names geometry by id, `gfx` builds it). An entry is a builder with its\\n * parameters as schema fields, each with a default, and a vertex budget: `defineGeometry('geometry:crate', {\\n * description, params, create: (params) => roundedBoxGeometry({ … }) })`. `buildGeometry(ref)` builds one, from an\\n * id or `{ geometry, params }`, as a three.js `BufferGeometry` the caller owns. The kit's shapes are built in\\n * (engine/gfx/geometry/builtins.ts): `geometry:box`, `roundedBox`, `limb`, `ramp`, `frustum`, `pillar`, `ring`.\\n *\\n * The `geo` QA family (tools/qa/geo.ts) builds every entry at its defaults and checks it (degenerate triangles,\\n10→ * normal consistency, bounds, the budget), so a game's geometry is checked as the engine's is.\\n *\\n * Invariants: an entry's parameter schema is checked when it is defined (each field valid and with a default); a\\n * builder is called with every parameter filled; `buildGeometry` never caches, so each call returns a new geometry;\\n * a missing id stands in as `geometry:box` after a warning (`CORE_UNKNOWN_ID`), as a missing material does.\\n *\\n * @example\\n * import { createRegistry } from '../../core/registry';\\n * const reg = createRegistry();\\n * buildGeometry({ geometry: 'geometry:box', params: { width: 2 } }, reg).getAttribute('position').count; // 24\\n20→ * reg.get('geometry', 'geometry:box').budget; // 24\\n * @see engine/gfx/geometry/geometry.test.ts\\n */\\nimport type { BufferGeometry } from 'three/webgpu';\\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Entry, type Registry } from '../../core/registry';\\nimport { checkField, isPlainObject, parse, type EntryOf, type Schema } from '../../core/schema';\\nimport { BUILT_IN_GEOMETRY } from './builtins';\\n\\n/** The fields of a `geometry` entry. */\\nexport const GEOMETRY_FIELDS = {\\n30→  description: { type: 'string', required: true, description: 'What it is, in plain sentences.' },\\n  params: {\\n    type: 'object',\\n    default: {},\\n    description:\\n      \\\"Its parameters as schema fields (engine/core/schema.ts: type, default, description, minimum…), each with a default: what a prop's geometry may set.\\\",\\n  },\\n  budget: {\\n    type: 'integer',\\n    default: 4096,\\n40→    minimum: 1,\\n    description: 'The most vertices it may have at its default parameters (the geo QA family checks it).',\\n  },\\n  create: {\\n    type: 'function',\\n    required: true,\\n    description:\\n      'The builder: (params) => BufferGeometry, standing on the ground, in metres, with normals and UVs in metres (engine/gfx/geometry/).',\\n  },\\n} as const satisfies Schema;\\n50→\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The geometry registry (PLAN.md WP 2.4, §6.6, I-29): the registry kind `geometry`, one entry per shape a prop,\\n * a level or a body names by id (§6.1: `world` names geometry by id, `gfx` builds it). An entry is a builder with its\\n * parameters as schema fields, each with a default, and a vertex budget: `defineGeometry('geometry:crate', {\\n * description, params, create: (params) => roundedBoxGeometry({ … }) })`. `buildGeometry(ref)` builds one, from an\\n * id or `{ geometry, params }`, as a three.js `BufferGeometry` the caller owns. The kit's shapes are built in\\n * (engine/gfx/geometry/builtins.ts): `geometry:box`, `roundedBox`, `limb`, `ramp`, `frustum`, `pillar`, `ring`.\\n *\\n * The `geo` QA family (tools/qa/geo.ts) builds every entry at its defaults and checks it (degenerate triangles,\\n10→ * normal consistency, bounds, the budget), so a game's geometry is checked as the engine's is.\\n *\\n * Invariants: an entry's parameter schema is checked when it is defined (each field valid and with a default); a\\n * builder is called with every parameter filled; `buildGeometry` never caches, so each call returns a new geometry;\\n * a missing id stands in as `geometry:box` after a warning (`CORE_UNKNOWN_ID`), as a missing material does.\\n *\\n * @example\\n * import { createRegistry } from '../../core/registry';\\n * const reg = createRegistry();\\n * buildGeometry({ geometry: 'geometry:box', params: { width: 2 } }, reg).getAttribute('position').count; // 24\\n20→ * reg.get('geometry', 'geometry:box').budget; // 24\\n * @see engine/gfx/geometry/geometry.test.ts\\n */\\nimport type { BufferGeometry } from 'three/webgpu';\\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Entry, type Registry } from '../../core/registry';\\nimport { checkField, isPlainObject, parse, type EntryOf, type Schema } from '../../core/schema';\\nimport { BUILT_IN_GEOMETRY } from './builtins';\\n\\n/** The fields of a `geometry` entry. */\\nexport const GEOMETRY_FIELDS = {\\n30→  description: { type: 'string', required: true, description: 'What it is, in plain sentences.' },\\n  params: {\\n    type: 'object',\\n    default: {},\\n    description:\\n      \\\"Its parameters as schema fields (engine/core/schema.ts: type, default, description, minimum…), each with a default: what a prop's geometry may set.\\\",\\n  },\\n  budget: {\\n    type: 'integer',\\n    default: 4096,\\n40→    minimum: 1,\\n    description: 'The most vertices it may have at its default parameters (the geo QA family checks it).',\\n  },\\n  create: {\\n    type: 'function',\\n    required: true,\\n    description:\\n      'The builder: (params) => BufferGeometry, standing on the ground, in metres, with normals and UVs in metres (engine/gfx/geometry/).',\\n  },\\n} as const satisfies Schema;\\n50→\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/gfx/geometry/geometry.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file The geometry registry (PLAN.md WP 2.4, §6.6, I-29): the registry kind `geometry`, one entry per shape a prop,\\n * a level or a body names by id (§6.1: `world` names geometry by id, `gfx` builds it). An entry is a builder with its\\n * parameters as schema fields, each with a default, and a vertex budget: `defineGeometry('geometry:crate', {\\n * description, params, create: (params) => roundedBoxGeometry({ … }) })`. `buildGeometry(ref)` builds one, from an\\n * id or `{ geometry, params }`, as a three.js `BufferGeometry` the caller owns. The kit's shapes are built in\\n * (engine/gfx/geometry/builtins.ts): `geometry:box`, `roundedBox`, `limb`, `ramp`, `frustum`, `pillar`, `ring`.\\n *\\n * The `geo` QA family (tools/qa/geo.ts) builds every entry at its defaults and checks it (degenerate triangles,\\n * normal consistency, bounds, the budget), so a game's geometry is checked as the engine's is.\\n *\\n * Invariants: an entry's parameter schema is checked when it is defined (each field valid and with a default); a\\n * builder is called with every parameter filled; `buildGeometry` never caches, so each call returns a new geometry;\\n * a missing id stands in as `geometry:box` after a warning (`CORE_UNKNOWN_ID`), as a missing material does.\\n *\\n * @example\\n * import { createRegistry } from '../../core/registry';\\n * const reg = createRegistry();\\n * buildGeometry({ geometry: 'geometry:box', params: { width: 2 } }, reg).getAttribute('position').count; // 24\\n * reg.get('geometry', 'geometry:box').budget; // 24\\n * @see engine/gfx/geometry/geometry.test.ts\\n */\\nimport type { BufferGeometry } from 'three/webgpu';\\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Entry, type Registry } from '../../core/registry';\\nimport { checkField, isPlainObject, parse, type EntryOf, type Schema } from '../../core/schema';\\nimport { BUILT_IN_GEOMETRY } from './builtins';\\n\\n/** The fields of a `geometry` entry. */\\nexport const GEOMETRY_FIELDS = {\\n  description: { type: 'string', required: true, description: 'What it is, in plain sentences.' },\\n  params: {\\n    type: 'object',\\n    default: {},\\n    description:\\n      \\\"Its parameters as schema fields (engine/core/schema.ts: type, default, description, minimum…), each with a default: what a prop's geometry may set.\\\",\\n  },\\n  budget: {\\n    type: 'integer',\\n    default: 4096,\\n    minimum: 1,\\n    description: 'The most vertices it may have at its default parameters (the geo QA family checks it).',\\n  },\\n  create: {\\n    type: 'function',\\n    required: true,\\n    description:\\n      'The builder: (params) => BufferGeometry, standing on the ground, in metres, with normals and UVs in metres (engine/gfx/geometry/).',\\n  },\\n} as const satisfies Schema;\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":135}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-b30b896f-1bff-4688-a5c3-8ffad7e32057-74","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"51→**Never use, in any form:** Derek Stiles, Angie Thompson, Naomi Kimishima, Nozomi Weaver, Hope Hospital, Caduceus, Delphi,\\nGUILT, Healing Touch, Kyriaki and the other Greek weekday strain names, Adam, Bliss, Z-Cells, the star gesture, or the\\nsource's art, music, UI, levels or sentences. The title may riff on the source's name as TASK.md asks; nothing else\\ndoes. \\\"Second opinion\\\" appears only as the ordinary phrase, in dialogue.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"51→**Never use, in any form:** Derek Stiles, Angie Thompson, Naomi Kimishima, Nozomi Weaver, Hope Hospital, Caduceus, Delphi,\\nGUILT, Healing Touch, Kyriaki and the other Greek weekday strain names, Adam, Bliss, Z-Cells, the star gesture, or the\\nsource's art, music, UI, levels or sentences. The title may riff on the source's name as TASK.md asks; nothing else\\ndoes. \\\"Second opinion\\\" appears only as the ordinary phrase, in dialogue.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":51,\"limit\":5,\"raw_output\":\"**Never use, in any form:** Derek Stiles, Angie Thompson, Naomi Kimishima, Nozomi Weaver, Hope Hospital, Caduceus, Delphi,\\nGUILT, Healing Touch, Kyriaki and the other Greek weekday strain names, Adam, Bliss, Z-Cells, the star gesture, or the\\nsource's art, music, UI, levels or sentences. The title may riff on the source's name as TASK.md asks; nothing else\\ndoes. \\\"Second opinion\\\" appears only as the ordinary phrase, in dialogue.\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":952}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"0f71cd7c-bb9e-4c28-a9df-987bb6ed154f"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_96","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-57a4a3a5-96f6-4215-8f2c-c73aa0a26a7e-75","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"defineProp\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs","glob":"*.ts","head_limit":15}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-57a4a3a5-96f6-4215-8f2c-c73aa0a26a7e-76","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/world/props/prop.ts","limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2438,"output_tokens":207,"cache_read_input_tokens":110848,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"6659fabe-e971-4b1b-987d-2ece10b3adc5"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-57a4a3a5-96f6-4215-8f2c-c73aa0a26a7e-75","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,55,51,49,95,95,120,53,57,99,49,100,51,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,78,111,32,109,97,116,99,104,101,115,32,102,111,117,110,100,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":1,\"match_count\":0,\"file_matches\":[]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-57a4a3a5-96f6-4215-8f2c-c73aa0a26a7e-76","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The prop registry (PLAN.md WP 4.5, §6.6): the registry kind `prop`, one entry per kind of thing that stands\\n * in a level, as data: the meshes it is drawn with (geometry and material by id, §6.1: `world` names them, `gfx`\\n * builds them, engine/gfx/props.ts), its body (a shape and a material for the physics world), an optional light\\n * spot, where a level places it, and its interaction hooks. The engine's props are the crate, the barrel, the\\n * brazier's fire and the pillar (engine/world/props/catalog.ts), the library's sconce, banner, chest, door, table,\\n * bench, statue, lantern and chair (library.ts, WP 10.3, the chair WP 13.16's) and the house's fittings, the pane,\\n * the switch, the lamp and the garage door (fittings.ts, WP 13.16); a game adds its own with `defineProp`\\n * (`x new prop`). WP 13.16's fields: a `kinematic` body the sim drives, `health` and what breaking leaves (`breaks`),\\n10→ * a `prompt` for its own `use`, and parts `lit` only while the prop is on; a hook's touch also names the world, the\\n * entity and its user.\\n *\\n * A prop's frame: its base, where it stands, is the origin, +Y up, and its parts stand on it as the geometry kit's\\n * shapes stand on the ground. Its body's shape stands on the base too, so the body's origin, the prop's centre, is\\n * `propCentre(prop)` above it: what a body's pose (`readBody`) and `propPose` give, and what the meshes are drawn\\n * at. A part with `flame.tongues` above 0 is drawn as that many flame tongues dancing round its origin (its geometry\\n * a cone one metre high, stretched each frame), the 2D hall's flames. The hooks: `hit` (a swing, a blast) knocks a\\n * dynamic prop away and leaves the others; `use` does nothing; shared code calls them and never compares ids.\\n *\\n20→ * Carried: the idea of my-3d2dge's 2D prop catalog (`src/starter/*`, `src/emberdeep/51-themes.js`): kinds of props\\n * as data with their light metadata (a colour, a reach and a flicker beside the drawing).\\n *\\n * Invariants: an entry is plain data plus its two hooks, every field filled with its default; a part's name is\\n * unique in its prop; colours are hex; vectors have three numbers; a body's shape has a size above 0; spawn names\\n * and light tags are words. Geometry and material ids are gfx's to resolve (a missing one draws its kind's fallback,\\n * and `node x qa geo tex --only prop:` reports it). Problems raise `CORE_BAD_SPEC` naming each; a missing id gets\\n * `prop:crate` after a warning (`CORE_UNKNOWN_ID`).\\n *\\n * @example\\n30→ * import { createRegistry } from '../../core/registry';\\n * const reg = createRegistry();\\n * defineProp('prop:stool', { parts: [{ geometry: 'geometry:frustum', params: { radiusBottom: 0.2, radiusTop: 0.2, height: 0.45 }, material: 'material:planks' }], body: { type: 'dynamic', shape: 'cylinder', radius: 0.2, height: 0.45 } }, reg);\\n * propCentre(getProp('prop:stool', reg)); // 0.225: half its height\\n * getProp('prop:crate', reg).body.type; // 'dynamic': the engine's props come with the kind\\n * @see engine/world/props/prop.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { galleryField } from '../../core/gallery';\\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Entry, type Registry } from '../../core/registry';\\nimport type { EntryOf, Schema } from '../../core/schema';\\n40→import type { Point3 } from '../level/types';\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The prop registry (PLAN.md WP 4.5, §6.6): the registry kind `prop`, one entry per kind of thing that stands\\n * in a level, as data: the meshes it is drawn with (geometry and material by id, §6.1: `world` names them, `gfx`\\n * builds them, engine/gfx/props.ts), its body (a shape and a material for the physics world), an optional light\\n * spot, where a level places it, and its interaction hooks. The engine's props are the crate, the barrel, the\\n * brazier's fire and the pillar (engine/world/props/catalog.ts), the library's sconce, banner, chest, door, table,\\n * bench, statue, lantern and chair (library.ts, WP 10.3, the chair WP 13.16's) and the house's fittings, the pane,\\n * the switch, the lamp and the garage door (fittings.ts, WP 13.16); a game adds its own with `defineProp`\\n * (`x new prop`). WP 13.16's fields: a `kinematic` body the sim drives, `health` and what breaking leaves (`breaks`),\\n10→ * a `prompt` for its own `use`, and parts `lit` only while the prop is on; a hook's touch also names the world, the\\n * entity and its user.\\n *\\n * A prop's frame: its base, where it stands, is the origin, +Y up, and its parts stand on it as the geometry kit's\\n * shapes stand on the ground. Its body's shape stands on the base too, so the body's origin, the prop's centre, is\\n * `propCentre(prop)` above it: what a body's pose (`readBody`) and `propPose` give, and what the meshes are drawn\\n * at. A part with `flame.tongues` above 0 is drawn as that many flame tongues dancing round its origin (its geometry\\n * a cone one metre high, stretched each frame), the 2D hall's flames. The hooks: `hit` (a swing, a blast) knocks a\\n * dynamic prop away and leaves the others; `use` does nothing; shared code calls them and never compares ids.\\n *\\n20→ * Carried: the idea of my-3d2dge's 2D prop catalog (`src/starter/*`, `src/emberdeep/51-themes.js`): kinds of props\\n * as data with their light metadata (a colour, a reach and a flicker beside the drawing).\\n *\\n * Invariants: an entry is plain data plus its two hooks, every field filled with its default; a part's name is\\n * unique in its prop; colours are hex; vectors have three numbers; a body's shape has a size above 0; spawn names\\n * and light tags are words. Geometry and material ids are gfx's to resolve (a missing one draws its kind's fallback,\\n * and `node x qa geo tex --only prop:` reports it). Problems raise `CORE_BAD_SPEC` naming each; a missing id gets\\n * `prop:crate` after a warning (`CORE_UNKNOWN_ID`).\\n *\\n * @example\\n30→ * import { createRegistry } from '../../core/registry';\\n * const reg = createRegistry();\\n * defineProp('prop:stool', { parts: [{ geometry: 'geometry:frustum', params: { radiusBottom: 0.2, radiusTop: 0.2, height: 0.45 }, material: 'material:planks' }], body: { type: 'dynamic', shape: 'cylinder', radius: 0.2, height: 0.45 } }, reg);\\n * propCentre(getProp('prop:stool', reg)); // 0.225: half its height\\n * getProp('prop:crate', reg).body.type; // 'dynamic': the engine's props come with the kind\\n * @see engine/world/props/prop.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { galleryField } from '../../core/gallery';\\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Entry, type Registry } from '../../core/registry';\\nimport type { EntryOf, Schema } from '../../core/schema';\\n40→import type { Point3 } from '../level/types';\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/world/props/prop.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file The prop registry (PLAN.md WP 4.5, §6.6): the registry kind `prop`, one entry per kind of thing that stands\\n * in a level, as data: the meshes it is drawn with (geometry and material by id, §6.1: `world` names them, `gfx`\\n * builds them, engine/gfx/props.ts), its body (a shape and a material for the physics world), an optional light\\n * spot, where a level places it, and its interaction hooks. The engine's props are the crate, the barrel, the\\n * brazier's fire and the pillar (engine/world/props/catalog.ts), the library's sconce, banner, chest, door, table,\\n * bench, statue, lantern and chair (library.ts, WP 10.3, the chair WP 13.16's) and the house's fittings, the pane,\\n * the switch, the lamp and the garage door (fittings.ts, WP 13.16); a game adds its own with `defineProp`\\n * (`x new prop`). WP 13.16's fields: a `kinematic` body the sim drives, `health` and what breaking leaves (`breaks`),\\n * a `prompt` for its own `use`, and parts `lit` only while the prop is on; a hook's touch also names the world, the\\n * entity and its user.\\n *\\n * A prop's frame: its base, where it stands, is the origin, +Y up, and its parts stand on it as the geometry kit's\\n * shapes stand on the ground. Its body's shape stands on the base too, so the body's origin, the prop's centre, is\\n * `propCentre(prop)` above it: what a body's pose (`readBody`) and `propPose` give, and what the meshes are drawn\\n * at. A part with `flame.tongues` above 0 is drawn as that many flame tongues dancing round its origin (its geometry\\n * a cone one metre high, stretched each frame), the 2D hall's flames. The hooks: `hit` (a swing, a blast) knocks a\\n * dynamic prop away and leaves the others; `use` does nothing; shared code calls them and never compares ids.\\n *\\n * Carried: the idea of my-3d2dge's 2D prop catalog (`src/starter/*`, `src/emberdeep/51-themes.js`): kinds of props\\n * as data with their light metadata (a colour, a reach and a flicker beside the drawing).\\n *\\n * Invariants: an entry is plain data plus its two hooks, every field filled with its default; a part's name is\\n * unique in its prop; colours are hex; vectors have three numbers; a body's shape has a size above 0; spawn names\\n * and light tags are words. Geometry and material ids are gfx's to resolve (a missing one draws its kind's fallback,\\n * and `node x qa geo tex --only prop:` reports it). Problems raise `CORE_BAD_SPEC` naming each; a missing id gets\\n * `prop:crate` after a warning (`CORE_UNKNOWN_ID`).\\n *\\n * @example\\n * import { createRegistry } from '../../core/registry';\\n * const reg = createRegistry();\\n * defineProp('prop:stool', { parts: [{ geometry: 'geometry:frustum', params: { radiusBottom: 0.2, radiusTop: 0.2, height: 0.45 }, material: 'material:planks' }], body: { type: 'dynamic', shape: 'cylinder', radius: 0.2, height: 0.45 } }, reg);\\n * propCentre(getProp('prop:stool', reg)); // 0.225: half its height\\n * getProp('prop:crate', reg).body.type; // 'dynamic': the engine's props come with the kind\\n * @see engine/world/props/prop.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { galleryField } from '../../core/gallery';\\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Entry, type Registry } from '../../core/registry';\\nimport type { EntryOf, Schema } from '../../core/schema';\\nimport type { Point3 } from '../level/types';\\n\",\"total_lines\":373}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"ef0c2fdb-43a3-49d5-9110-ab0453c0bfca"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_97","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Props can be defined from the page using defineProp from engine/index.\n\nProps must be registered before createEngine so the scene can spawn them. Live meshes use defineGeometry at module load and rewrite geometry in onFrame. The prop:sheet spawns at the table. The sheet variable may be null before the first draw.\n\nQA geo may flag the custom geometry. The baseline must be accepted if flagged. The defineGeometry budget needs to cover the vertex count. Vertex colors require a BufferAttribute with itemSize 3.\n\nBufferGeometry.computeVertexNormals will be used for normal generation. defineMaterial from engine/index handles vertex colors. look:field and look:harbor are also defined. The field camera uses cam3=fixed looking down, set via inspector.camera.set with blend enabled. The player spawns at [0, -8, 0] so the light follows while the character stays hidden under the floor.\n\nThe player will sit in a hidden side room behind a wall, not under the floor. The level is a 20 by 16 room with the spawn in a corner and the camera fixed above the center table. compileLevel and addLevelBodies need physics enabled for the character controller.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-36b8dc27-ca1b-4905-b676-4eb47c663ede-77","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"when","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/core/settings.ts","head_limit":30}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-36b8dc27-ca1b-4905-b676-4eb47c663ede-78","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/cases.ts","offset":1,"limit":60}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1205,"output_tokens":876,"cache_read_input_tokens":113280,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"546ca674-2ecb-4266-8393-77e4ec31c468"}
