{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_107","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Reading verifyGame and template check.","signature":"hkijerGMD+Ykxpj+nXnmP62WkmHbMtDL/lKvN5wO+5XSJhF9xku8MmiOMW6rtAn1eBoaFFKLlPPaL0c3J/l/"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-93ac416c-7515-46a3-98b2-a13de5967da0-92","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/tools/game/files.mjs","offset":260,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-93ac416c-7515-46a3-98b2-a13de5967da0-93","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md","limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":676,"output_tokens":194,"cache_read_input_tokens":126976,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"1961fdf9-762e-4528-8097-cc071e7e9130"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-93ac416c-7515-46a3-98b2-a13de5967da0-92","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"260→function engineDirFiles(target) {\\n  const files = [];\\n  const walk = (dir) => {\\n    if (!existsSync(join(target, dir))) return;\\n    for (const entry of readdirSync(join(target, dir), { withFileTypes: true })) {\\n      const path = `${dir}${entry.name}`;\\n      if (entry.isDirectory()) walk(`${path}/`);\\n      else if (entry.isFile() && entry.name !== '.DS_Store') files.push(path);\\n    }\\n  };\\n270→  ENGINE_DIRS.forEach(walk);\\n  return files;\\n}\\n\\n/** The engine files ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md lists under \\\"Local engine patches\\\", outside comments. */\\nexport function declaredPatches(target) {\\n  const file = join(target, FEEDBACK_FILE);\\n  if (!existsSync(file)) return [];\\n  const text = readFileSync(file, 'utf8').replace(/<!--[\\\\s\\\\S]*?-->/g, '');\\n  const section = /^## Local engine patches\\\\s*$([\\\\s\\\\S]*?)(?=^## |(?![\\\\s\\\\S]))/m.exec(text)?.[1] ?? '';\\n280→  return [...section.matchAll(/^\\\\s*[-*]\\\\s+`([^`]+)`/gm)].map((match) => match[1]);\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Compares a game's engine files with its lock: those changed, those missing, files the game added in the engine's\\n * folders, and the patches it declares; `undeclared` is every one of the first three that the game does not declare.\\n */\\nexport function verifyGame(target) {\\n  const lockFile = join(target, LOCK_FILE);\\n  if (!existsSync(lockFile)) {\\n290→    throw new Error(`${resolve(target)} has no ${LOCK_FILE}: it is no game made by tools/game/new-game.mjs`);\\n  }\\n  const restore = `restore it from git (git checkout -- ${LOCK_FILE}; in a merge, take one side whole): only new-game.mjs writes it`; // prettier-ignore\\n  let lock;\\n  try {\\n    lock = JSON.parse(readFileSync(lockFile, 'utf8'));\\n  } catch (error) {\\n    throw new Error(`${LOCK_FILE} is not JSON (${error.message}): ${restore}`);\\n  }\\n  if (typeof lock?.format !== 'string') throw new Error(`${LOCK_FILE} has no \\\"format\\\": ${restore}`);\\n300→  if (lock.format !== LOCK_FORMAT) {\\n    throw new Error(`${LOCK_FILE} says \\\"${lock.format}\\\", not ${LOCK_FORMAT}: move the game to a newer engine`);\\n  }\\n  if (\\n    typeof lock.files !== 'object' ||\\n    lock.files === null ||\\n    Array.isArray(lock.files) ||\\n    typeof lock.engine?.commit !== 'string'\\n  ) {\\n    throw new Error(`${LOCK_FILE} lacks its engine or its files: ${restore}`);\\n310→  }\\n  const [changed, missing] = [[], []];\\n  for (const [path, hash] of Object.entries(lock.files)) {\\n    const file = join(target, path);\\n    if (!existsSync(file)) missing.push(path);\\n    else if (hashFile(file) !== hash) changed.push(path);\\n  }\\n  const added = engineDirFiles(target).filter((path) => !(path in lock.files));\\n  const declared = declaredPatches(target);\\n  const undeclared = [...changed, ...missing, ...added].filter((path) => !declared.includes(path));\\n320→  return { lock, changed, missing, added, declared, undeclared };\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"260→function engineDirFiles(target) {\\n  const files = [];\\n  const walk = (dir) => {\\n    if (!existsSync(join(target, dir))) return;\\n    for (const entry of readdirSync(join(target, dir), { withFileTypes: true })) {\\n      const path = `${dir}${entry.name}`;\\n      if (entry.isDirectory()) walk(`${path}/`);\\n      else if (entry.isFile() && entry.name !== '.DS_Store') files.push(path);\\n    }\\n  };\\n270→  ENGINE_DIRS.forEach(walk);\\n  return files;\\n}\\n\\n/** The engine files ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md lists under \\\"Local engine patches\\\", outside comments. */\\nexport function declaredPatches(target) {\\n  const file = join(target, FEEDBACK_FILE);\\n  if (!existsSync(file)) return [];\\n  const text = readFileSync(file, 'utf8').replace(/<!--[\\\\s\\\\S]*?-->/g, '');\\n  const section = /^## Local engine patches\\\\s*$([\\\\s\\\\S]*?)(?=^## |(?![\\\\s\\\\S]))/m.exec(text)?.[1] ?? '';\\n280→  return [...section.matchAll(/^\\\\s*[-*]\\\\s+`([^`]+)`/gm)].map((match) => match[1]);\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Compares a game's engine files with its lock: those changed, those missing, files the game added in the engine's\\n * folders, and the patches it declares; `undeclared` is every one of the first three that the game does not declare.\\n */\\nexport function verifyGame(target) {\\n  const lockFile = join(target, LOCK_FILE);\\n  if (!existsSync(lockFile)) {\\n290→    throw new Error(`${resolve(target)} has no ${LOCK_FILE}: it is no game made by tools/game/new-game.mjs`);\\n  }\\n  const restore = `restore it from git (git checkout -- ${LOCK_FILE}; in a merge, take one side whole): only new-game.mjs writes it`; // prettier-ignore\\n  let lock;\\n  try {\\n    lock = JSON.parse(readFileSync(lockFile, 'utf8'));\\n  } catch (error) {\\n    throw new Error(`${LOCK_FILE} is not JSON (${error.message}): ${restore}`);\\n  }\\n  if (typeof lock?.format !== 'string') throw new Error(`${LOCK_FILE} has no \\\"format\\\": ${restore}`);\\n300→  if (lock.format !== LOCK_FORMAT) {\\n    throw new Error(`${LOCK_FILE} says \\\"${lock.format}\\\", not ${LOCK_FORMAT}: move the game to a newer engine`);\\n  }\\n  if (\\n    typeof lock.files !== 'object' ||\\n    lock.files === null ||\\n    Array.isArray(lock.files) ||\\n    typeof lock.engine?.commit !== 'string'\\n  ) {\\n    throw new Error(`${LOCK_FILE} lacks its engine or its files: ${restore}`);\\n310→  }\\n  const [changed, missing] = [[], []];\\n  for (const [path, hash] of Object.entries(lock.files)) {\\n    const file = join(target, path);\\n    if (!existsSync(file)) missing.push(path);\\n    else if (hashFile(file) !== hash) changed.push(path);\\n  }\\n  const added = engineDirFiles(target).filter((path) => !(path in lock.files));\\n  const declared = declaredPatches(target);\\n  const undeclared = [...changed, ...missing, ...added].filter((path) => !declared.includes(path));\\n320→  return { lock, changed, missing, added, declared, undeclared };\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/tools/game/files.mjs\",\"offset\":260,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"function engineDirFiles(target) {\\n  const files = [];\\n  const walk = (dir) => {\\n    if (!existsSync(join(target, dir))) return;\\n    for (const entry of readdirSync(join(target, dir), { withFileTypes: true })) {\\n      const path = `${dir}${entry.name}`;\\n      if (entry.isDirectory()) walk(`${path}/`);\\n      else if (entry.isFile() && entry.name !== '.DS_Store') files.push(path);\\n    }\\n  };\\n  ENGINE_DIRS.forEach(walk);\\n  return files;\\n}\\n\\n/** The engine files ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md lists under \\\"Local engine patches\\\", outside comments. */\\nexport function declaredPatches(target) {\\n  const file = join(target, FEEDBACK_FILE);\\n  if (!existsSync(file)) return [];\\n  const text = readFileSync(file, 'utf8').replace(/<!--[\\\\s\\\\S]*?-->/g, '');\\n  const section = /^## Local engine patches\\\\s*$([\\\\s\\\\S]*?)(?=^## |(?![\\\\s\\\\S]))/m.exec(text)?.[1] ?? '';\\n  return [...section.matchAll(/^\\\\s*[-*]\\\\s+`([^`]+)`/gm)].map((match) => match[1]);\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Compares a game's engine files with its lock: those changed, those missing, files the game added in the engine's\\n * folders, and the patches it declares; `undeclared` is every one of the first three that the game does not declare.\\n */\\nexport function verifyGame(target) {\\n  const lockFile = join(target, LOCK_FILE);\\n  if (!existsSync(lockFile)) {\\n    throw new Error(`${resolve(target)} has no ${LOCK_FILE}: it is no game made by tools/game/new-game.mjs`);\\n  }\\n  const restore = `restore it from git (git checkout -- ${LOCK_FILE}; in a merge, take one side whole): only new-game.mjs writes it`; // prettier-ignore\\n  let lock;\\n  try {\\n    lock = JSON.parse(readFileSync(lockFile, 'utf8'));\\n  } catch (error) {\\n    throw new Error(`${LOCK_FILE} is not JSON (${error.message}): ${restore}`);\\n  }\\n  if (typeof lock?.format !== 'string') throw new Error(`${LOCK_FILE} has no \\\"format\\\": ${restore}`);\\n  if (lock.format !== LOCK_FORMAT) {\\n    throw new Error(`${LOCK_FILE} says \\\"${lock.format}\\\", not ${LOCK_FORMAT}: move the game to a newer engine`);\\n  }\\n  if (\\n    typeof lock.files !== 'object' ||\\n    lock.files === null ||\\n    Array.isArray(lock.files) ||\\n    typeof lock.engine?.commit !== 'string'\\n  ) {\\n    throw new Error(`${LOCK_FILE} lacks its engine or its files: ${restore}`);\\n  }\\n  const [changed, missing] = [[], []];\\n  for (const [path, hash] of Object.entries(lock.files)) {\\n    const file = join(target, path);\\n    if (!existsSync(file)) missing.push(path);\\n    else if (hashFile(file) !== hash) changed.push(path);\\n  }\\n  const added = engineDirFiles(target).filter((path) => !(path in lock.files));\\n  const declared = declaredPatches(target);\\n  const undeclared = [...changed, ...missing, ...added].filter((path) => !declared.includes(path));\\n  return { lock, changed, missing, added, declared, undeclared };\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":321}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-93ac416c-7515-46a3-98b2-a13de5967da0-93","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→# Engine feedback: trauma-compass\\n\\nWhat this game needed from the my-3dge engine (at 2dbd829) and did not get. The owner collects this file\\nfrom every game to improve the engine, so write each item for an engine agent who has never seen this repository:\\nwhat you tried, what happened (the command, the error code), what you expected, and what you did instead.\\n\\n## Requests\\n\\n<!-- What the engine should add or fix, most costly first. -->\\n10→\\n## Friction\\n\\n<!-- Docs, errors, templates or APIs that slowed you down or misled you, most costly first. -->\\n\\n## Local engine patches\\n\\n<!--\\n`npm run check` accepts an edited engine file only when it is listed here, one line each, its path in backticks:\\n- `engine/path/to/file.ts`: why no workaround in the game would do, and what the engine should change instead.\\n20→-->\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→# Engine feedback: trauma-compass\\n\\nWhat this game needed from the my-3dge engine (at 2dbd829) and did not get. The owner collects this file\\nfrom every game to improve the engine, so write each item for an engine agent who has never seen this repository:\\nwhat you tried, what happened (the command, the error code), what you expected, and what you did instead.\\n\\n## Requests\\n\\n<!-- What the engine should add or fix, most costly first. -->\\n10→\\n## Friction\\n\\n<!-- Docs, errors, templates or APIs that slowed you down or misled you, most costly first. -->\\n\\n## Local engine patches\\n\\n<!--\\n`npm run check` accepts an edited engine file only when it is listed here, one line each, its path in backticks:\\n- `engine/path/to/file.ts`: why no workaround in the game would do, and what the engine should change instead.\\n20→-->\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"# Engine feedback: trauma-compass\\n\\nWhat this game needed from the my-3dge engine (at 2dbd829) and did not get. The owner collects this file\\nfrom every game to improve the engine, so write each item for an engine agent who has never seen this repository:\\nwhat you tried, what happened (the command, the error code), what you expected, and what you did instead.\\n\\n## Requests\\n\\n<!-- What the engine should add or fix, most costly first. -->\\n\\n## Friction\\n\\n<!-- Docs, errors, templates or APIs that slowed you down or misled you, most costly first. -->\\n\\n## Local engine patches\\n\\n<!--\\n`npm run check` accepts an edited engine file only when it is listed here, one line each, its path in backticks:\\n- `engine/path/to/file.ts`: why no workaround in the game would do, and what the engine should change instead.\\n-->\\n\",\"total_lines\":20}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"57f4354f-c321-4249-9662-bd86a5a22615"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_108","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md is not in lock.\n\nEngine files can be edited without breaking the lock, since verifyGame does not check template hashes. The root index.html is the engine's game page and should not be modified. A verify script can be added to package.json.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-118be616-c73a-4c8f-8011-d7d74363b632-94","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"jsdoc|max-lines|@file","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/eslint.config.js","head_limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1250,"output_tokens":434,"cache_read_input_tokens":127616,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"bebe678d-47d9-4ad6-8ed0-8ae77576fd31"}
