{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_115","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I have enough information to write the code.\n\nPlanning data-game attributes for all UI elements to support end-to-end testing. Outlining the screen flow for the stub pad.\n\nThe e2e test will use a navigator.getGamepads stub. Menus will support both engine input and direct pad polling so multiple pads work for scrub-in. Keyboard controls will handle menu navigation for simplicity, while a separate test will stub the pads.\n\nThe pad stub must drive all menus, including the title screen. The six title options are Continue, New Shift, The Board, Scrub In, Settings, and About. New Shift starts with a pre-story briefing, then a case 1 briefing, then the operation.\n\nAutoplay will be triggered by a `game.autoplay` boolean setting. The e2e test can enable it via the URL query string. This flag will be kept out of the hash so it does not alter the address bar. The engine still processes simulation steps at 60Hz per call even when the frame clock speed changes.\n\nThe e2e test can speed up the frame clock by adding `?time.scale=8` to the URL. Story boxes will auto-advance every N frames when autoplay is enabled so the playthrough finishes automatically.\n\nCross advances one story box at a time. The full eight-case e2e run should finish in about fifteen seconds at time scale twenty, though engine warm-up adds roughly twenty seconds. Total verification time could exceed ten minutes, which is acceptable if the test passes. The complete playthrough remains fragile.\n\nAutoplay will be fully deterministic: story auto-advances, ops are played by the bot, and debriefs continue automatically. The attract screen will only appear during idle title waits; it must not activate while the test presses buttons. I will download session.js to build a host/client hub harness, reading the protocol README first. I am ready to start writing files in batches.\n\nI will fix the sequencer, write the content test, start it running, and continue writing the remaining files in parallel. The `addAnchor` helper will use `locked: true` for the hidden target, since `kindDefaults` already sets `hidden` when `locked` is true.\n\nThe empty clear phase wins on the first step unless a locked target keeps the operation alive. A locked mass target prevents timeout during 3600 steps because the clock runs for 600 seconds. Vitals should not drain since the hidden mass is locked. Hashes will match across peers because hands are identical. Dropped packets will be greater than zero due to the five percent loss rate. The leaver retains their last seat after leaving, and only arrived packets apply to them.\n\nThe test cannot inspect applied hands directly. It must verify the leaver's seat.use is false after leftAt, since only that flag survives in the final state. Late packets might still arrive on the last tick and flip it back to true.\n\nThe leaver's seat.use will be false at the end because their last packets arrive by tick 1806, before the 3600-step simulation ends. The test will verify equal peer hashes, dropped packets above zero, and that the final seat.use is false for the leaving peer. The playThrough helper will be included since every case is known to win. validateCase will check case ids, phases, patients, postcards, story ids, positive par values, and banned words.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-da4bdd9e-9100-420b-9a8c-4999f3872a7a-103","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"guilt|caduceus|delphi|stiles|kyriaki|bliss|adam|healing touch|z-cell|placeholder|TODO|lorem","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game","glob":"*.ts","-i":true}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":417,"output_tokens":1879,"cache_read_input_tokens":137216,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"d37f9a88-a6b1-4d9a-83ab-dd5d70ba0e16"}
