,121,46,104,116,109,108,39,44,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":22,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/tools/cmd/replay.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":16,\"content\":\" * compares the runs (\\\"golden: other platform\\\"). Its scene module is found from its `scene` id, as `x sim` finds it,\"},{\"line_number\":18,\"content\":\" * `--browser page` plays each replay in its scene's own page instead (`labs/<name>/?scene=<scene>` for a module under\"},{\"line_number\":19,\"content\":\" * `labs/<name>/scenes/`, through `__engine.replay`, engine/app/playback.ts), drawing a frame after every step: the\"},{\"line_number\":20,\"content\":\" * CPU-only gameplay contract's proof that rendering never changes play (§6.7). Fixture scenes have no page.\"},{\"line_number\":36,\"content\":\"import { existsSync, readFileSync, statSync } from 'node:fs';\"},{\"line_number\":37,\"content\":\"import { basename, join, relative, resolve } from 'node:path';\"},{\"line_number\":38,\"content\":\"import { SIM_MATH_NAMES, type SimMathName } from '../../engine/core/simMath';\"},{\"line_number\":39,\"content\":\"import { checkReplay, firstDifference, judgeRuns, partingOf, type Parting, type Replay } from '../../engine/sim/replay';\"},{\"line_number\":40,\"content\":\"import { componentTable, hashState } from '../../engine/sim/state';\"},{\"line_number\":41,\"content\":\"import { describePageError } from '../lib/pageErrors';\"},{\"line_number\":42,\"content\":\"import { replayBrowser, type BrowserMode } from '../lib/page';\"},{\"line_number\":43,\"content\":\"import { stateFile, writeState } from '../lib/replayState';\"},{\"line_number\":44,\"content\":\"import { walk } from '../lib/docs';\"},{\"line_number\":45,\"content\":\"import type { Finding } from '../lib/report';\"},{\"line_number\":46,\"content\":\"import { UsageError, wholeFlag, type Command, type CommandResult } from '../x';\"},{\"line_number\":47,\"content\":\"import { nodeRuntime, writeReplay, type Runtime } from './sim';\"},{\"line_number\":48,\"content\":\"import { resolveSceneModule } from '../lib/scenes';\"},{\"line_number\":167,\"content\":\"    const module = resolveSceneModule(root, replay.scene);\"},{\"line_number\":325,\"content\":\"        `--browser takes sim (the sim-only page) or page (the scene's own page), not ${browserMode}`,\"},{\"line_number\":348,\"content\":\"          message: `${browserMode === 'page' ? \\\"the scene's page\\\" : 'tests/pages/replay.html'} threw: ${describePageError(error)}`,\"},{\"line_number\":354,\"content\":\"        const { describeUnlisted, findUnlisted, loadAllowList } = await import('../../tests/setup/adviceTrap');\"},{\"line_number\":360,\"content\":\"              browserMode === 'page' ? \\\" in the scene's page\\\" : ' in tests/pages/replay.html',\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"b84502e7-9b74-4e86-81f9-22883740b904"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_118","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"resolveSceneModule locates a scene by its ID.\n\nThe verify script loads scenes directly, so play.ts stays available. For browser page mode, game:play must be registered explicitly. I'll pass both compass and play scenes and default to compass unless a scene is specified.\n\nI need to check whether createEngine defaults to the first scene in its array. If so, game:main should come first so it is the default without a scene query. I will replace main.ts entirely for Trauma Compass while still importing play.ts so it registers. However, createEngine might only allow the explicitly listed scenes.\n\nThe replay page mode opens `?scene=game:play`, which the engine reads to start that scene directly. A running page cannot switch scenes, so both IDs must be registered. I will list them as `scenes: [compass.id, play.id]` and place compass first so it is the default.\n\nI will branch the page-mode replay HUD. If no chart component exists, it will fall back to the old gem HUD so the page still looks correct when the play scene is active.\n\nThe index.html title will be set to \"Trauma Compass\".\n\nI will build the 10-foot HUD manually instead of using createMenu, so I can control glyphs and data attributes directly. The engine modal will only appear when the screen is not the operator or title-3d, preventing intents from leaking. When a menu opens, the simulation pauses via inspector.pause() except during the hub screen. In the title screen, the world still steps while the camera and rain run, but stepOp is skipped.\n\nAfter ten seconds on the title screen, the game will automatically switch to the operator cut and restart the scene. Any input during that attract phase returns the game to the title screen and restarts it. A black fade overlay will cover run changes. Free surgery will be unlocked after credits by selecting a case from the board.\n\nThe board will list all cases, with locked ones showing a lock until the previous case is cleared. A Free Surgery item will open the board in practice mode for any case without rank save. The Gala-shift case will appear as a bonus after case 7 or remain available in free mode. I will begin writing fixes and core files before the page. Hand packing and scene step need testing. Settings sliders must apply each step to op.balance so developer adjustments take effect.\n\nScene settings defaults must match the slider constants so bot-through-scene behaves identically. A mapping array will link scene keys to slider names. To keep the scene file lean, these definitions will live in a new scenes/settings.ts module under the scenes folder. The scene can safely import sibling game code like op.\n\nI will define the scene settings explicitly in `scenes/settings.ts` rather than importing the slider constants directly, since appendix keys differ from slider keys. The clock range setting will use the simulation slider’s 0.4–2 bounds to match `setSlider` limits. The cursor default will remain at 8 instead of the appendix value of 13, because applying that value every step would alter bot behavior during scene playback.\n\nApplying every slider setting each step would overwrite the difficulty-based slip limit, making attending easier and changing scores. I will only apply a setting when it differs from the value stored at op creation, or restrict updates to specific keys like vitalsDrain.\n\nThe implementation will compare each slider setting against the current balance value before applying it. This prevents difficulty-based defaults from being overwritten during scene playback. Resetting a slider must update both the stored setting and the balance value to keep them aligned.\n\nThe slip limit will only be applied when the slider setting differs from its default of 5. This preserves the difficulty-based values for intern and attending while still allowing manual adjustments.\n\nA Map will track the last applied slider value per key. The scene step will only call setSlider when a setting has changed since the previous frame, ensuring manual adjustments are preserved without overwriting difficulty defaults.\n\nThe first step will record slider settings without applying them, preserving difficulty-based defaults. A WeakMap keyed by the op object will track each op’s last seen values. Resetting a slider to its default will update both the stored setting and the balance value so the next step applies the correct difficulty slip limit.\n\nThe reset flow needs an extra step to prevent the next scene step from overwriting difficulty-based defaults. After `resetSliders` restores the balance values, the page will sync each setting back to its matching balance key and then update the snapshot so the next frame sees no change.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-691a1851-e4e8-4b2c-859a-686803b421bb-107","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/audio/runtime/audio.ts","offset":90,"limit":50}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":863,"output_tokens":2409,"cache_read_input_tokens":140928,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"a9775d6d-495d-4b63-960a-533fd824d628"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-691a1851-e4e8-4b2c-859a-686803b421bb-107","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"90→  voices: string[];\\n  mixer: MixerInfo | null;\\n  music: MusicPosition | null;\\n  listener: ListenerPose | null;\\n  /** Event type → the stinger it plays. */\\n  bindings: Record<string, string>;\\n}\\n\\n/** A page's sound (see the file comment). */\\nexport interface Audio {\\n100→  readonly state: AudioState;\\n  /** The context, once there is one. */\\n  readonly context: BaseAudioContext | null;\\n  play(id: string, options?: PlayOptions): Sound | null;\\n  footstep(surface: string, position?: Vec3, options?: PlayOptions): Sound | null;\\n  event(type: string, payload?: unknown): Sound | null;\\n  bind(type: string, id: string | null): void;\\n  /** Plays a song (null stops), on the next bar line of the one playing (music.ts). */\\n  music(id: string | null, options?: MusicChange & { intensity?: number }): void;\\n  /** Sets the music's intensity, 0 to 1, on the next beat (music.ts). */\\n110→  intensity(value: number, options?: MusicChange): void;\\n  /** Plays an effect or a song once on the music bus, on the next beat (music.ts). */\\n  stinger(id: string, options?: MusicChange & { vol?: number }): void;\\n  /** Once per rendered frame: the listener follows `pose`, and placed sounds are occluded through `queries`. */\\n  update(pose?: ListenerPose, queries?: QueryView): void;\\n  volume(bus: AudioBus | 'master', value?: number): number;\\n  mute(on?: boolean): boolean;\\n  /** `true` holds a duck of the music and ambience, `false` lets it go, a number ducks for that many seconds. */\\n  duck(on: boolean | number): void;\\n  room(room: RoomName | RoomSpec): void;\\n120→  info(): AudioInfo;\\n  /** Stops listening and closes the context it made. */\\n  close(): Promise<void>;\\n}\\n\\n/** Makes a page's sound (see the file comment). */\\nexport function createAudio(options: AudioOptions = {}): Audio {\\n  const registry = options.registry ?? sharedRegistry;\\n  const out = options.log ?? sharedLog;\\n  sfxKind(registry);\\n130→  songKind(registry);\\n  /** `id` once it names a song or an effect; else throws `CORE_NO_ENTRY` naming the closest effects. */\\n  const checkSound = (id: string) => (registry.has('song', id) ? id : getSfx(id, registry).id);\\n  const footsteps = options.footsteps ?? {};\\n  const pool = createVoicePool<RuntimeSound>(options.limits);\\n  const buffers = new Map<string, AudioBuffer>();\\n  const turns = new Map<string, number>();\\n  const bindings = new Map<string, string>();\\n  const volumes = { ...BUS_VOLUMES };\\n  let muted = false;\",\"content_concise\":\"90→  voices: string[];\\n  mixer: MixerInfo | null;\\n  music: MusicPosition | null;\\n  listener: ListenerPose | null;\\n  /** Event type → the stinger it plays. */\\n  bindings: Record<string, string>;\\n}\\n\\n/** A page's sound (see the file comment). */\\nexport interface Audio {\\n100→  readonly state: AudioState;\\n  /** The context, once there is one. */\\n  readonly context: BaseAudioContext | null;\\n  play(id: string, options?: PlayOptions): Sound | null;\\n  footstep(surface: string, position?: Vec3, options?: PlayOptions): Sound | null;\\n  event(type: string, payload?: unknown): Sound | null;\\n  bind(type: string, id: string | null): void;\\n  /** Plays a song (null stops), on the next bar line of the one playing (music.ts). */\\n  music(id: string | null, options?: MusicChange & { intensity?: number }): void;\\n  /** Sets the music's intensity, 0 to 1, on the next beat (music.ts). */\\n110→  intensity(value: number, options?: MusicChange): void;\\n  /** Plays an effect or a song once on the music bus, on the next beat (music.ts). */\\n  stinger(id: string, options?: MusicChange & { vol?: number }): void;\\n  /** Once per rendered frame: the listener follows `pose`, and placed sounds are occluded through `queries`. */\\n  update(pose?: ListenerPose, queries?: QueryView): void;\\n  volume(bus: AudioBus | 'master', value?: number): number;\\n  mute(on?: boolean): boolean;\\n  /** `true` holds a duck of the music and ambience, `false` lets it go, a number ducks for that many seconds. */\\n  duck(on: boolean | number): void;\\n  room(room: RoomName | RoomSpec): void;\\n120→  info(): AudioInfo;\\n  /** Stops listening and closes the context it made. */\\n  close(): Promise<void>;\\n}\\n\\n/** Makes a page's sound (see the file comment). */\\nexport function createAudio(options: AudioOptions = {}): Audio {\\n  const registry = options.registry ?? sharedRegistry;\\n  const out = options.log ?? sharedLog;\\n  sfxKind(registry);\\n130→  songKind(registry);\\n  /** `id` once it names a song or an effect; else throws `CORE_NO_ENTRY` naming the closest effects. */\\n  const checkSound = (id: string) => (registry.has('song', id) ? id : getSfx(id, registry).id);\\n  const footsteps = options.footsteps ?? {};\\n  const pool = createVoicePool<RuntimeSound>(options.limits);\\n  const buffers = new Map<string, AudioBuffer>();\\n  const turns = new Map<string, number>();\\n  const bindings = new Map<string, string>();\\n  const volumes = { ...BUS_VOLUMES };\\n  let muted = false;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/audio/runtime/audio.ts\",\"offset\":90,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"  voices: string[];\\n  mixer: MixerInfo | null;\\n  music: MusicPosition | null;\\n  listener: ListenerPose | null;\\n  /** Event type → the stinger it plays. */\\n  bindings: Record<string, string>;\\n}\\n\\n/** A page's sound (see the file comment). */\\nexport interface Audio {\\n  readonly state: AudioState;\\n  /** The context, once there is one. */\\n  readonly context: BaseAudioContext | null;\\n  play(id: string, options?: PlayOptions): Sound | null;\\n  footstep(surface: string, position?: Vec3, options?: PlayOptions): Sound | null;\\n  event(type: string, payload?: unknown): Sound | null;\\n  bind(type: string, id: string | null): void;\\n  /** Plays a song (null stops), on the next bar line of the one playing (music.ts). */\\n  music(id: string | null, options?: MusicChange & { intensity?: number }): void;\\n  /** Sets the music's intensity, 0 to 1, on the next beat (music.ts). */\\n  intensity(value: number, options?: MusicChange): void;\\n  /** Plays an effect or a song once on the music bus, on the next beat (music.ts). */\\n  stinger(id: string, options?: MusicChange & { vol?: number }): void;\\n  /** Once per rendered frame: the listener follows `pose`, and placed sounds are occluded through `queries`. */\\n  update(pose?: ListenerPose, queries?: QueryView): void;\\n  volume(bus: AudioBus | 'master', value?: number): number;\\n  mute(on?: boolean): boolean;\\n  /** `true` holds a duck of the music and ambience, `false` lets it go, a number ducks for that many seconds. */\\n  duck(on: boolean | number): void;\\n  room(room: RoomName | RoomSpec): void;\\n  info(): AudioInfo;\\n  /** Stops listening and closes the context it made. */\\n  close(): Promise<void>;\\n}\\n\\n/** Makes a page's sound (see the file comment). */\\nexport function createAudio(options: AudioOptions = {}): Audio {\\n  const registry = options.registry ?? sharedRegistry;\\n  const out = options.log ?? sharedLog;\\n  sfxKind(registry);\\n  songKind(registry);\\n  /** `id` once it names a song or an effect; else throws `CORE_NO_ENTRY` naming the closest effects. */\\n  const checkSound = (id: string) => (registry.has('song', id) ? id : getSfx(id, registry).id);\\n  const footsteps = options.footsteps ?? {};\\n  const pool = createVoicePool<RuntimeSound>(options.limits);\\n  const buffers = new Map<string, AudioBuffer>();\\n  const turns = new Map<string, number>();\\n  const bindings = new Map<string, string>();\\n  const volumes = { ...BUS_VOLUMES };\\n  let muted = false;\\n\",\"total_lines\":321}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"9a248ceb-48df-4e03-850b-4db91325a40e"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_119","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1b0364dc-4db3-429e-a107-8ae55d0ee7e5-108","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/audio/data/effects.ts","limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1b0364dc-4db3-429e-a107-8ae55d0ee7e5-109","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/audio/dsp/voice.ts","limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3162,"output_tokens":247,"cache_read_input_tokens":141696,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"39d482cb-c160-4906-ac57-a88191159fc6"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-1b0364dc-4db3-429e-a107-8ae55d0ee7e5-108","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The engine's 33 sound effects as data (PLAN.md WP 9.2, I-23): jumps, landings, steps, pickups, hits, shots,\\n * explosions, doors, jingles and the menu and text blips, each an `sfx` entry (engine/audio/data/sfx.ts) under the id\\n * `sfx:<name>`. Every one renders in Node and hashes the same everywhere (engine/audio/data/sounds.test.ts).\\n *\\n * Invariants: the voices are the source's numbers, copied as they are; the DSP takes the source chip synth's fields\\n * (engine/audio/dsp/voice.ts). The source detuned every play by up to ±3%, so each effect has four variants, `vary`\\n * 0.03 (the kind's default), which the runtime picks between. The menu and text sounds play on the `ui` bus, the rest\\n * on `effects`.\\n10→ *\\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:3663-3697` (`SFX`).\\n *\\n * @example\\n * EFFECTS['sfx:jump'].voices; // { wave: 'pulse', freq: 280, to: 640, dur: 0.14, vol: 0.3 }\\n * Object.keys(EFFECTS).length; // 33\\n * @see engine/audio/data/sounds.test.ts\\n */\\nimport type { SfxSpec } from './sfx';\\n\\n20→/** Variants of each engine effect: the source detuned every play by up to ±3%. */\\nconst VARIANTS = 4;\\n\\n/** A gameplay effect: four variants, on the effects bus. */\\nconst effect = (voices: SfxSpec['voices']): SfxSpec => ({ voices, variants: VARIANTS });\\n\\n/** A menu or text sound: four variants, on the ui bus. */\\nconst ui = (voices: SfxSpec['voices']): SfxSpec => ({ voices, variants: VARIANTS, bus: 'ui' });\\n\\n/** The engine's effects by id. */\\n30→export const EFFECTS: Readonly<Record<string, SfxSpec>> = {\\n  'sfx:jump': effect({ wave: 'pulse', freq: 280, to: 640, dur: 0.14, vol: 0.3 }),\\n  'sfx:jump2': effect({ wave: 'pulse', freq: 420, to: 900, dur: 0.12, vol: 0.26 }),\\n  'sfx:land': effect({ wave: 'noise', freq: 500, to: 150, dur: 0.07, vol: 0.25, filter: 'lowpass' }),\\n  'sfx:step': effect({ wave: 'noise', freq: 3000, dur: 0.03, vol: 0.07, filter: 'highpass' }),\\n  'sfx:coin': effect({ wave: 'square', freq: 988, arp: [0, 5], step: 0.07, dur: 0.32, vol: 0.26 }),\\n  'sfx:pickup': effect({ wave: 'triangle', freq: 880, to: 1760, dur: 0.09, vol: 0.4 }),\\n  'sfx:key': effect({ wave: 'square', freq: 1047, arp: [0, 4, 7, 12], step: 0.045, dur: 0.22, vol: 0.24 }),\\n  'sfx:powerup': effect({ wave: 'square', freq: 523, arp: [0, 4, 7, 12, 16, 19, 24], step: 0.05, dur: 0.4, vol: 0.26 }),\\n  'sfx:oneup': effect({ wave: 'square', freq: 659, arp: [0, 3, 12, 8, 10, 15], step: 0.08, dur: 0.5, vol: 0.26 }),\\n40→  'sfx:heal': effect({ wave: 'triangle', freq: 523, arp: [0, 7, 12, 19], step: 0.06, dur: 0.3, vol: 0.4 }),\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The engine's 33 sound effects as data (PLAN.md WP 9.2, I-23): jumps, landings, steps, pickups, hits, shots,\\n * explosions, doors, jingles and the menu and text blips, each an `sfx` entry (engine/audio/data/sfx.ts) under the id\\n * `sfx:<name>`. Every one renders in Node and hashes the same everywhere (engine/audio/data/sounds.test.ts).\\n *\\n * Invariants: the voices are the source's numbers, copied as they are; the DSP takes the source chip synth's fields\\n * (engine/audio/dsp/voice.ts). The source detuned every play by up to ±3%, so each effect has four variants, `vary`\\n * 0.03 (the kind's default), which the runtime picks between. The menu and text sounds play on the `ui` bus, the rest\\n * on `effects`.\\n10→ *\\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:3663-3697` (`SFX`).\\n *\\n * @example\\n * EFFECTS['sfx:jump'].voices; // { wave: 'pulse', freq: 280, to: 640, dur: 0.14, vol: 0.3 }\\n * Object.keys(EFFECTS).length; // 33\\n * @see engine/audio/data/sounds.test.ts\\n */\\nimport type { SfxSpec } from './sfx';\\n\\n20→/** Variants of each engine effect: the source detuned every play by up to ±3%. */\\nconst VARIANTS = 4;\\n\\n/** A gameplay effect: four variants, on the effects bus. */\\nconst effect = (voices: SfxSpec['voices']): SfxSpec => ({ voices, variants: VARIANTS });\\n\\n/** A menu or text sound: four variants, on the ui bus. */\\nconst ui = (voices: SfxSpec['voices']): SfxSpec => ({ voices, variants: VARIANTS, bus: 'ui' });\\n\\n/** The engine's effects by id. */\\n30→export const EFFECTS: Readonly<Record<string, SfxSpec>> = {\\n  'sfx:jump': effect({ wave: 'pulse', freq: 280, to: 640, dur: 0.14, vol: 0.3 }),\\n  'sfx:jump2': effect({ wave: 'pulse', freq: 420, to: 900, dur: 0.12, vol: 0.26 }),\\n  'sfx:land': effect({ wave: 'noise', freq: 500, to: 150, dur: 0.07, vol: 0.25, filter: 'lowpass' }),\\n  'sfx:step': effect({ wave: 'noise', freq: 3000, dur: 0.03, vol: 0.07, filter: 'highpass' }),\\n  'sfx:coin': effect({ wave: 'square', freq: 988, arp: [0, 5], step: 0.07, dur: 0.32, vol: 0.26 }),\\n  'sfx:pickup': effect({ wave: 'triangle', freq: 880, to: 1760, dur: 0.09, vol: 0.4 }),\\n  'sfx:key': effect({ wave: 'square', freq: 1047, arp: [0, 4, 7, 12], step: 0.045, dur: 0.22, vol: 0.24 }),\\n  'sfx:powerup': effect({ wave: 'square', freq: 523, arp: [0, 4, 7, 12, 16, 19, 24], step: 0.05, dur: 0.4, vol: 0.26 }),\\n  'sfx:oneup': effect({ wave: 'square', freq: 659, arp: [0, 3, 12, 8, 10, 15], step: 0.08, dur: 0.5, vol: 0.26 }),\\n40→  'sfx:heal': effect({ wave: 'triangle', freq: 523, arp: [0, 7, 12, 19], step: 0.06, dur: 0.3, vol: 0.4 }),\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/audio/data/effects.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file The engine's 33 sound effects as data (PLAN.md WP 9.2, I-23): jumps, landings, steps, pickups, hits, shots,\\n * explosions, doors, jingles and the menu and text blips, each an `sfx` entry (engine/audio/data/sfx.ts) under the id\\n * `sfx:<name>`. Every one renders in Node and hashes the same everywhere (engine/audio/data/sounds.test.ts).\\n *\\n * Invariants: the voices are the source's numbers, copied as they are; the DSP takes the source chip synth's fields\\n * (engine/audio/dsp/voice.ts). The source detuned every play by up to ±3%, so each effect has four variants, `vary`\\n * 0.03 (the kind's default), which the runtime picks between. The menu and text sounds play on the `ui` bus, the rest\\n * on `effects`.\\n *\\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:3663-3697` (`SFX`).\\n *\\n * @example\\n * EFFECTS['sfx:jump'].voices; // { wave: 'pulse', freq: 280, to: 640, dur: 0.14, vol: 0.3 }\\n * Object.keys(EFFECTS).length; // 33\\n * @see engine/audio/data/sounds.test.ts\\n */\\nimport type { SfxSpec } from './sfx';\\n\\n/** Variants of each engine effect: the source detuned every play by up to ±3%. */\\nconst VARIANTS = 4;\\n\\n/** A gameplay effect: four variants, on the effects bus. */\\nconst effect = (voices: SfxSpec['voices']): SfxSpec => ({ voices, variants: VARIANTS });\\n\\n/** A menu or text sound: four variants, on the ui bus. */\\nconst ui = (voices: SfxSpec['voices']): SfxSpec => ({ voices, variants: VARIANTS, bus: 'ui' });\\n\\n/** The engine's effects by id. */\\nexport const EFFECTS: Readonly<Record<string, SfxSpec>> = {\\n  'sfx:jump': effect({ wave: 'pulse', freq: 280, to: 640, dur: 0.14, vol: 0.3 }),\\n  'sfx:jump2': effect({ wave: 'pulse', freq: 420, to: 900, dur: 0.12, vol: 0.26 }),\\n  'sfx:land': effect({ wave: 'noise', freq: 500, to: 150, dur: 0.07, vol: 0.25, filter: 'lowpass' }),\\n  'sfx:step': effect({ wave: 'noise', freq: 3000, dur: 0.03, vol: 0.07, filter: 'highpass' }),\\n  'sfx:coin': effect({ wave: 'square', freq: 988, arp: [0, 5], step: 0.07, dur: 0.32, vol: 0.26 }),\\n  'sfx:pickup': effect({ wave: 'triangle', freq: 880, to: 1760, dur: 0.09, vol: 0.4 }),\\n  'sfx:key': effect({ wave: 'square', freq: 1047, arp: [0, 4, 7, 12], step: 0.045, dur: 0.22, vol: 0.24 }),\\n  'sfx:powerup': effect({ wave: 'square', freq: 523, arp: [0, 4, 7, 12, 16, 19, 24], step: 0.05, dur: 0.4, vol: 0.26 }),\\n  'sfx:oneup': effect({ wave: 'square', freq: 659, arp: [0, 3, 12, 8, 10, 15], step: 0.08, dur: 0.5, vol: 0.26 }),\\n  'sfx:heal': effect({ wave: 'triangle', freq: 523, arp: [0, 7, 12, 19], step: 0.06, dur: 0.3, vol: 0.4 }),\\n\",\"total_lines\":86}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-1b0364dc-4db3-429e-a107-8ae55d0ee7e5-109","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file A sound definition and its checks (PLAN.md WP 9.1; doctrines: Assets, Agent-operable): a sound is plain data,\\n * one voice or a list of voices played together, in the source chip synth's words (`wave`, `freq`, `to`, `dur`,\\n * `vol`, `attack`, `hold`, `arp`, `step`, `loop`, `vib`, `filter`, `q`), so its effects, drums and songs copy over as\\n * they are (WP 9.2), plus ADSR (`decay`, `sustain`, `release`), a start time `at`, an explicit filter, `fm`, `pluck`\\n * and a `delay` echo. `normalizeSound` checks a definition and fills its defaults, throwing a coded error that names\\n * the voice and the field.\\n *\\n * Defaults (the source's): wave `square`, freq 440 Hz, dur 0.15 s (at least 0.012 s), vol 0.3, attack 0.004 s, step\\n10→ * 0.06 s, q 1.1. The envelope falls away unless `hold` or an ADSR field is given; a pluck holds by default (`hold:\\n * false` makes it fall), because a string fades by itself. A noise voice without `filter` goes through a bandpass that\\n * follows its pitch, as in the source. A frequency is a number in Hz or a note name (`noteFreq`), and pitches below\\n * 20 Hz are raised to 20 Hz, as in the source. A filter given by its type alone (`filter: 'lowpass'`) follows the\\n * voice's pitch; an object gives it its own `freq` (and `to`, a sweep). `pluck` voices keep one pitch: `to`, `arp`,\\n * `vib` and `fm` are refused on them, and `fm` on noise. The source's `delay` (a start offset) is `at` here, because\\n * `delay` is the echo. Unknown fields and waves are refused with the closest name, never ignored.\\n *\\n * @example\\n * const [voice] = normalizeSound({ wave: 'pulse', freq: 'A4', to: 880, dur: 0.14 }, 44100);\\n20→ * voice.f0; // 440\\n * @see engine/audio/dsp/render.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { codeError, defineCodes, didYouMean } from '../../core/log';\\nimport { withSimMath } from '../../core/simMath';\\nimport { FILTER_TYPES, type FilterType } from './biquad';\\nimport type { EchoSpec } from './delay';\\nimport { holdEnvelope, type Envelope } from './envelope';\\nimport { TONAL_WAVES } from './osc';\\n\\n30→/** The codes a definition's checks raise, with their fixes (collected into docs/ERRORS.md by `x docs`). */\\nexport const VOICE_CODES = defineCodes('audio', {\\n  AUDIO_UNKNOWN_WAVE: {\\n    template: '{where}: there is no wave \\\"{wave}\\\"{suggestion}',\\n    fix: 'use one of {waves}',\\n    doc: 'Raised by `render` (engine/audio/dsp/render.ts) when a voice names a wave the DSP does not make.',\\n  },\\n  AUDIO_UNKNOWN_FIELD: {\\n    template: '{where} has no field \\\"{field}\\\"{suggestion}',\\n    fix: 'use only the fields {fields}',\\n40→    doc: 'Raised by `render` (engine/audio/dsp/render.ts) for a field a voice, filter, fm, pluck or delay does not have: usually a typo, which would otherwise be silently ignored.',\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file A sound definition and its checks (PLAN.md WP 9.1; doctrines: Assets, Agent-operable): a sound is plain data,\\n * one voice or a list of voices played together, in the source chip synth's words (`wave`, `freq`, `to`, `dur`,\\n * `vol`, `attack`, `hold`, `arp`, `step`, `loop`, `vib`, `filter`, `q`), so its effects, drums and songs copy over as\\n * they are (WP 9.2), plus ADSR (`decay`, `sustain`, `release`), a start time `at`, an explicit filter, `fm`, `pluck`\\n * and a `delay` echo. `normalizeSound` checks a definition and fills its defaults, throwing a coded error that names\\n * the voice and the field.\\n *\\n * Defaults (the source's): wave `square`, freq 440 Hz, dur 0.15 s (at least 0.012 s), vol 0.3, attack 0.004 s, step\\n10→ * 0.06 s, q 1.1. The envelope falls away unless `hold` or an ADSR field is given; a pluck holds by default (`hold:\\n * false` makes it fall), because a string fades by itself. A noise voice without `filter` goes through a bandpass that\\n * follows its pitch, as in the source. A frequency is a number in Hz or a note name (`noteFreq`), and pitches below\\n * 20 Hz are raised to 20 Hz, as in the source. A filter given by its type alone (`filter: 'lowpass'`) follows the\\n * voice's pitch; an object gives it its own `freq` (and `to`, a sweep). `pluck` voices keep one pitch: `to`, `arp`,\\n * `vib` and `fm` are refused on them, and `fm` on noise. The source's `delay` (a start offset) is `at` here, because\\n * `delay` is the echo. Unknown fields and waves are refused with the closest name, never ignored.\\n *\\n * @example\\n * const [voice] = normalizeSound({ wave: 'pulse', freq: 'A4', to: 880, dur: 0.14 }, 44100);\\n20→ * voice.f0; // 440\\n * @see engine/audio/dsp/render.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { codeError, defineCodes, didYouMean } from '../../core/log';\\nimport { withSimMath } from '../../core/simMath';\\nimport { FILTER_TYPES, type FilterType } from './biquad';\\nimport type { EchoSpec } from './delay';\\nimport { holdEnvelope, type Envelope } from './envelope';\\nimport { TONAL_WAVES } from './osc';\\n\\n30→/** The codes a definition's checks raise, with their fixes (collected into docs/ERRORS.md by `x docs`). */\\nexport const VOICE_CODES = defineCodes('audio', {\\n  AUDIO_UNKNOWN_WAVE: {\\n    template: '{where}: there is no wave \\\"{wave}\\\"{suggestion}',\\n    fix: 'use one of {waves}',\\n    doc: 'Raised by `render` (engine/audio/dsp/render.ts) when a voice names a wave the DSP does not make.',\\n  },\\n  AUDIO_UNKNOWN_FIELD: {\\n    template: '{where} has no field \\\"{field}\\\"{suggestion}',\\n    fix: 'use only the fields {fields}',\\n40→    doc: 'Raised by `render` (engine/audio/dsp/render.ts) for a field a voice, filter, fm, pluck or delay does not have: usually a typo, which would otherwise be silently ignored.',\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/audio/dsp/voice.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file A sound definition and its checks (PLAN.md WP 9.1; doctrines: Assets, Agent-operable): a sound is plain data,\\n * one voice or a list of voices played together, in the source chip synth's words (`wave`, `freq`, `to`, `dur`,\\n * `vol`, `attack`, `hold`, `arp`, `step`, `loop`, `vib`, `filter`, `q`), so its effects, drums and songs copy over as\\n * they are (WP 9.2), plus ADSR (`decay`, `sustain`, `release`), a start time `at`, an explicit filter, `fm`, `pluck`\\n * and a `delay` echo. `normalizeSound` checks a definition and fills its defaults, throwing a coded error that names\\n * the voice and the field.\\n *\\n * Defaults (the source's): wave `square`, freq 440 Hz, dur 0.15 s (at least 0.012 s), vol 0.3, attack 0.004 s, step\\n * 0.06 s, q 1.1. The envelope falls away unless `hold` or an ADSR field is given; a pluck holds by default (`hold:\\n * false` makes it fall), because a string fades by itself. A noise voice without `filter` goes through a bandpass that\\n * follows its pitch, as in the source. A frequency is a number in Hz or a note name (`noteFreq`), and pitches below\\n * 20 Hz are raised to 20 Hz, as in the source. A filter given by its type alone (`filter: 'lowpass'`) follows the\\n * voice's pitch; an object gives it its own `freq` (and `to`, a sweep). `pluck` voices keep one pitch: `to`, `arp`,\\n * `vib` and `fm` are refused on them, and `fm` on noise. The source's `delay` (a start offset) is `at` here, because\\n * `delay` is the echo. Unknown fields and waves are refused with the closest name, never ignored.\\n *\\n * @example\\n * const [voice] = normalizeSound({ wave: 'pulse', freq: 'A4', to: 880, dur: 0.14 }, 44100);\\n * voice.f0; // 440\\n * @see engine/audio/dsp/render.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { codeError, defineCodes, didYouMean } from '../../core/log';\\nimport { withSimMath } from '../../core/simMath';\\nimport { FILTER_TYPES, type FilterType } from './biquad';\\nimport type { EchoSpec } from './delay';\\nimport { holdEnvelope, type Envelope } from './envelope';\\nimport { TONAL_WAVES } from './osc';\\n\\n/** The codes a definition's checks raise, with their fixes (collected into docs/ERRORS.md by `x docs`). */\\nexport const VOICE_CODES = defineCodes('audio', {\\n  AUDIO_UNKNOWN_WAVE: {\\n    template: '{where}: there is no wave \\\"{wave}\\\"{suggestion}',\\n    fix: 'use one of {waves}',\\n    doc: 'Raised by `render` (engine/audio/dsp/render.ts) when a voice names a wave the DSP does not make.',\\n  },\\n  AUDIO_UNKNOWN_FIELD: {\\n    template: '{where} has no field \\\"{field}\\\"{suggestion}',\\n    fix: 'use only the fields {fields}',\\n    doc: 'Raised by `render` (engine/audio/dsp/render.ts) for a field a voice, filter, fm, pluck or delay does not have: usually a typo, which would otherwise be silently ignored.',\\n\",\"total_lines\":378}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"4a6a9e41-b5b1-4735-857d-0bc989fbd6c5"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_120","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The voice format is clear. Songs use note strings.\n\nI'll write simple 4-bar loops. I'll update the sequencer and fetch session.js and the hub README API documentation in parallel.\n\nThe sheet mesh uses engine/index geometry and defineMaterial. It is 16 by 10 meters with a 96 by 60 grid. Height comes from breathing, heartbeat, organ ellipses, and wound lips. liveOp() updates each frame. Hands will be a thin prop.\n\nThe hand will be a small box-glove inside the live mesh. Instruments appear as colored markers at the cursor. Table, lamp, and drapes are spawned from geometry:box props using defineProp.\n\nmain.ts imports props.ts before createEngine so defineProp runs first. The scene spawns drape, table, lamp, sheet, and monitor props. Sheet geometry is captured during creation.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bf349ca5-f5e5-4f80-bb2a-e280aaf9c83b-110","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"vertexColors","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/gfx/materials","head_limit":15}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2115,"output_tokens":786,"cache_read_input_tokens":144768,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"4cb2dda4-7e9e-48ea-8b48-4ba6355635e6"}
