{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-6c1dd84e-2ab0-4823-9e4b-6494778b34ca-120","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"70→    default: '#000000',\\n    description:\\n      \\\"The colour it glows with, hex, unaffected by light; it multiplies the map's emissive, as three.js's emissiveMap does (write '#ffffff' to show a glowing texture as baked).\\\",\\n  },\\n  emissiveIntensity: { type: 'number', default: 1, minimum: 0, description: 'A multiplier on emissive.' },\\n  normalScale: {\\n    type: 'number',\\n    default: 1,\\n    minimum: 0,\\n    maximum: 8,\\n80→    description: \\\"How deep the map's relief looks: scales the normal map from its height (0 turns it off).\\\",\\n  },\\n  unlit: {\\n    type: 'boolean',\\n    default: false,\\n    description:\\n      'Drawn without lights (glTF unlit, three.js MeshBasicMaterial): color × map as it is; for glows, skies and markers.',\\n  },\\n  transparent: { type: 'boolean', default: false, description: 'Blended with what is behind it, by opacity.' },\\n  opacity: { type: 'number', default: 1, minimum: 0, maximum: 1, description: 'Its opacity when transparent.' },\\n90→  alphaTest: {\\n    type: 'number',\\n    default: 0,\\n    minimum: 0,\\n    maximum: 1,\\n    description: 'Texels with alpha below this are not drawn (cut-outs).',\\n  },\\n  side: {\\n    type: 'string',\\n    enum: ['front', 'back', 'double'],\\n100→    default: 'front',\\n    description: 'Which faces are drawn.',\\n  },\\n  flatShading: { type: 'boolean', default: false, description: 'Faceted: one normal per triangle.' },\\n  vertexColors: { type: 'boolean', default: false, description: \\\"Multiplies by the geometry's color attribute.\\\" },\\n  fog: { type: 'boolean', default: true, description: \\\"Whether the scene's fog applies.\\\" },\\n  depthWrite: {\\n    type: 'boolean',\\n    default: true,\\n    description: 'Whether it writes depth (off for some transparent layers).',\\n110→  },\\n  gallery: galleryField(),\\n} as const satisfies Schema;\\n\\n/** A `material` entry. */\\nexport type MaterialEntry = Entry<typeof MATERIAL_FIELDS>;\\n\\n/** What `defineMaterial` takes: any of the fields, each with its default. */\\nexport type MaterialSpec = SpecOf<typeof MATERIAL_FIELDS>;\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"70→    default: '#000000',\\n    description:\\n      \\\"The colour it glows with, hex, unaffected by light; it multiplies the map's emissive, as three.js's emissiveMap does (write '#ffffff' to show a glowing texture as baked).\\\",\\n  },\\n  emissiveIntensity: { type: 'number', default: 1, minimum: 0, description: 'A multiplier on emissive.' },\\n  normalScale: {\\n    type: 'number',\\n    default: 1,\\n    minimum: 0,\\n    maximum: 8,\\n80→    description: \\\"How deep the map's relief looks: scales the normal map from its height (0 turns it off).\\\",\\n  },\\n  unlit: {\\n    type: 'boolean',\\n    default: false,\\n    description:\\n      'Drawn without lights (glTF unlit, three.js MeshBasicMaterial): color × map as it is; for glows, skies and markers.',\\n  },\\n  transparent: { type: 'boolean', default: false, description: 'Blended with what is behind it, by opacity.' },\\n  opacity: { type: 'number', default: 1, minimum: 0, maximum: 1, description: 'Its opacity when transparent.' },\\n90→  alphaTest: {\\n    type: 'number',\\n    default: 0,\\n    minimum: 0,\\n    maximum: 1,\\n    description: 'Texels with alpha below this are not drawn (cut-outs).',\\n  },\\n  side: {\\n    type: 'string',\\n    enum: ['front', 'back', 'double'],\\n100→    default: 'front',\\n    description: 'Which faces are drawn.',\\n  },\\n  flatShading: { type: 'boolean', default: false, description: 'Faceted: one normal per triangle.' },\\n  vertexColors: { type: 'boolean', default: false, description: \\\"Multiplies by the geometry's color attribute.\\\" },\\n  fog: { type: 'boolean', default: true, description: \\\"Whether the scene's fog applies.\\\" },\\n  depthWrite: {\\n    type: 'boolean',\\n    default: true,\\n    description: 'Whether it writes depth (off for some transparent layers).',\\n110→  },\\n  gallery: galleryField(),\\n} as const satisfies Schema;\\n\\n/** A `material` entry. */\\nexport type MaterialEntry = Entry<typeof MATERIAL_FIELDS>;\\n\\n/** What `defineMaterial` takes: any of the fields, each with its default. */\\nexport type MaterialSpec = SpecOf<typeof MATERIAL_FIELDS>;\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/gfx/materials/material.ts\",\"offset\":70,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"    default: '#000000',\\n    description:\\n      \\\"The colour it glows with, hex, unaffected by light; it multiplies the map's emissive, as three.js's emissiveMap does (write '#ffffff' to show a glowing texture as baked).\\\",\\n  },\\n  emissiveIntensity: { type: 'number', default: 1, minimum: 0, description: 'A multiplier on emissive.' },\\n  normalScale: {\\n    type: 'number',\\n    default: 1,\\n    minimum: 0,\\n    maximum: 8,\\n    description: \\\"How deep the map's relief looks: scales the normal map from its height (0 turns it off).\\\",\\n  },\\n  unlit: {\\n    type: 'boolean',\\n    default: false,\\n    description:\\n      'Drawn without lights (glTF unlit, three.js MeshBasicMaterial): color × map as it is; for glows, skies and markers.',\\n  },\\n  transparent: { type: 'boolean', default: false, description: 'Blended with what is behind it, by opacity.' },\\n  opacity: { type: 'number', default: 1, minimum: 0, maximum: 1, description: 'Its opacity when transparent.' },\\n  alphaTest: {\\n    type: 'number',\\n    default: 0,\\n    minimum: 0,\\n    maximum: 1,\\n    description: 'Texels with alpha below this are not drawn (cut-outs).',\\n  },\\n  side: {\\n    type: 'string',\\n    enum: ['front', 'back', 'double'],\\n    default: 'front',\\n    description: 'Which faces are drawn.',\\n  },\\n  flatShading: { type: 'boolean', default: false, description: 'Faceted: one normal per triangle.' },\\n  vertexColors: { type: 'boolean', default: false, description: \\\"Multiplies by the geometry's color attribute.\\\" },\\n  fog: { type: 'boolean', default: true, description: \\\"Whether the scene's fog applies.\\\" },\\n  depthWrite: {\\n    type: 'boolean',\\n    default: true,\\n    description: 'Whether it writes depth (off for some transparent layers).',\\n  },\\n  gallery: galleryField(),\\n} as const satisfies Schema;\\n\\n/** A `material` entry. */\\nexport type MaterialEntry = Entry<typeof MATERIAL_FIELDS>;\\n\\n/** What `defineMaterial` takes: any of the fields, each with its default. */\\nexport type MaterialSpec = SpecOf<typeof MATERIAL_FIELDS>;\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":239}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"d40276fa-86cc-4b67-a219-8582d63d07fc"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_129","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A color field exists. I'll use hex values like '#8fd0c8'.\n\nI'm writing the main.ts page and a scene test. The page owns the screen state, while the scene owns the run. When the screen becomes 'op', the page calls beginRun to set the game run, seats, and difficulty in the inspector.\n\nThe page also seeds the inspector and sets the attract flag. Story mode displays 3D sets and scene dialogue without needing the simulation. The setup logic will spawn different props based on the run prefix, using one OR set with a corkboard and window for the board scene.\n\nAll OR props will be spawned on every screen so each has a 3D room. The page will control the camera per screen. Props are placed at fixed coordinates: table and sheet at origin, corkboard at x=6, window at z=-6. Parallax camera effects are optional.\n\nParallax will nudge the camera slightly each frame based on cursor position. Input hands for the OP screen will be computed from pads, mouse, keys, or bot logic and packed into a game:hands axis. Mouse-to-field raycasting will use screenRay and onFloor.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-18756683-518a-4ccc-a071-d599755b9e84-121","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/body.ts","offset":1,"limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":738,"output_tokens":868,"cache_read_input_tokens":159872,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"120a97f3-92d6-4bf3-a9c4-4665433682bd"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-18756683-518a-4ccc-a071-d599755b9e84-121","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file Vitals, the clock, the Code, the Gift, phase changes, and the colleague. Field time is the only clock\\n * the patient knows. Cursors already moved before this runs.\\n */\\nimport { award, failOp, heal, POINTS, winOp } from './ratings';\\nimport type { Hand, Op, Seat, Spawn } from './types';\\nimport { addTarget, enterPhase, FIELD_SECOND } from './world';\\n\\n/** Field ticks this step. Stillpoint is a quarter. The pulse-lock minigame is 30 percent. */\\n10→export function fieldDelta(op: Op): number {\\n  if (op.seats.some((seat) => seat.giftKind === 'still' && seat.giftLeft > 0)) return 25;\\n  if (op.seats.some((seat) => seat.lock >= 0)) return 30;\\n  return 100;\\n}\\n\\n/** Read hands into seats. Null means the menu is up: cursors stay, buttons do not stick. */\\nexport function applyHands(op: Op, hands: readonly Hand[] | null): void {\\n  if (!hands) {\\n    for (const seat of op.seats) seat.use = false;\\n20→    return;\\n  }\\n  for (let i = 0; i < op.seats.length; i++) {\\n    const hand = hands[i];\\n    const seat = op.seats[i];\\n    if (!hand) continue;\\n    seat.x = Math.max(-8, Math.min(8, hand.x));\\n    seat.z = Math.max(-5, Math.min(5, hand.z));\\n    if (op.roll) {\\n      const wave = Math.sin(op.tick / 40);\\n30→      if (op.tick % 420 < 36) {\\n        seat.x += wave * 0.1;\\n        seat.z += wave * 0.04;\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (hand.tool >= 0 && hand.tool <= 7 && hand.tool !== seat.tool) {\\n      seat.tool = hand.tool;\\n      op.events.push({ type: 'tool', text: 'clack', seat: seat.id });\\n    }\\n    seat.use = hand.use;\\n40→    seat.drop = hand.drop;\\n    if (hand.site >= 0 && hand.site < op.sites.length) seat.site = hand.site;\\n    if (hand.hint) op.events.push({ type: 'hint', text: op.hint || 'Steady, Doctor.', seat: seat.id });\\n    if (hand.swap && op.swapOk) swapPersona(op, seat);\\n    if (hand.gift) pressGift(op, seat);\\n    if (hand.paddle) pressPaddle(op, seat);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** Swap the lead between Stillpoint and Second Pulse. */\\n50→function swapPersona(op: Op, seat: Seat): void {\\n  if (seat.id !== 0) return;\\n  if (seat.gift === 'stillpoint') {\\n    seat.gift = 'second';\\n    op.persona = 'sabine';\\n  } else if (seat.gift === 'second') {\\n    seat.gift = 'stillpoint';\\n    op.persona = 'wren';\\n  }\\n  op.events.push({ type: 'swap', text: op.persona, seat: seat.id });\\n60→}\\n\\n/** Triangle: start a lock, or hit the next beat. Simple Gift skips the lock. */\\nfunction pressGift(op: Op, seat: Seat): void {\\n  if (seat.gift === 'none' && seat.charges <= 0 && !op.attract) return;\\n  if (seat.lock >= 0) {\\n    const window = Math.max(4, Math.round((op.balance.giftWindow / 1000) * 60));\\n    const error = Math.abs(op.tick - seat.lockBeat);\\n    if (error <= Math.max(2, Math.round(window / 2))) seat.lockPerfect += 1;\\n    else if (error <= window) seat.lockGood += 1;\\n70→    seat.lock += 1;\\n    seat.lockBeat = op.tick + 40;\\n    if (seat.lock >= 3) finishLock(op, seat);\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  if (seat.giftLeft > 0) return;\\n  if (seat.charges <= 0 && !op.attract) return;\\n  if (!op.attract) seat.charges -= 1;\\n  op.giftUsed = true;\\n  if (op.simple) {\\n80→    seat.giftKind = seat.gift === 'second' ? 'pulse' : 'still';\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file Vitals, the clock, the Code, the Gift, phase changes, and the colleague. Field time is the only clock\\n * the patient knows. Cursors already moved before this runs.\\n */\\nimport { award, failOp, heal, POINTS, winOp } from './ratings';\\nimport type { Hand, Op, Seat, Spawn } from './types';\\nimport { addTarget, enterPhase, FIELD_SECOND } from './world';\\n\\n/** Field ticks this step. Stillpoint is a quarter. The pulse-lock minigame is 30 percent. */\\n10→export function fieldDelta(op: Op): number {\\n  if (op.seats.some((seat) => seat.giftKind === 'still' && seat.giftLeft > 0)) return 25;\\n  if (op.seats.some((seat) => seat.lock >= 0)) return 30;\\n  return 100;\\n}\\n\\n/** Read hands into seats. Null means the menu is up: cursors stay, buttons do not stick. */\\nexport function applyHands(op: Op, hands: readonly Hand[] | null): void {\\n  if (!hands) {\\n    for (const seat of op.seats) seat.use = false;\\n20→    return;\\n  }\\n  for (let i = 0; i < op.seats.length; i++) {\\n    const hand = hands[i];\\n    const seat = op.seats[i];\\n    if (!hand) continue;\\n    seat.x = Math.max(-8, Math.min(8, hand.x));\\n    seat.z = Math.max(-5, Math.min(5, hand.z));\\n    if (op.roll) {\\n      const wave = Math.sin(op.tick / 40);\\n30→      if (op.tick % 420 < 36) {\\n        seat.x += wave * 0.1;\\n        seat.z += wave * 0.04;\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (hand.tool >= 0 && hand.tool <= 7 && hand.tool !== seat.tool) {\\n      seat.tool = hand.tool;\\n      op.events.push({ type: 'tool', text: 'clack', seat: seat.id });\\n    }\\n    seat.use = hand.use;\\n40→    seat.drop = hand.drop;\\n    if (hand.site >= 0 && hand.site < op.sites.length) seat.site = hand.site;\\n    if (hand.hint) op.events.push({ type: 'hint', text: op.hint || 'Steady, Doctor.', seat: seat.id });\\n    if (hand.swap && op.swapOk) swapPersona(op, seat);\\n    if (hand.gift) pressGift(op, seat);\\n    if (hand.paddle) pressPaddle(op, seat);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** Swap the lead between Stillpoint and Second Pulse. */\\n50→function swapPersona(op: Op, seat: Seat): void {\\n  if (seat.id !== 0) return;\\n  if (seat.gift === 'stillpoint') {\\n    seat.gift = 'second';\\n    op.persona = 'sabine';\\n  } else if (seat.gift === 'second') {\\n    seat.gift = 'stillpoint';\\n    op.persona = 'wren';\\n  }\\n  op.events.push({ type: 'swap', text: op.persona, seat: seat.id });\\n60→}\\n\\n/** Triangle: start a lock, or hit the next beat. Simple Gift skips the lock. */\\nfunction pressGift(op: Op, seat: Seat): void {\\n  if (seat.gift === 'none' && seat.charges <= 0 && !op.attract) return;\\n  if (seat.lock >= 0) {\\n    const window = Math.max(4, Math.round((op.balance.giftWindow / 1000) * 60));\\n    const error = Math.abs(op.tick - seat.lockBeat);\\n    if (error <= Math.max(2, Math.round(window / 2))) seat.lockPerfect += 1;\\n    else if (error <= window) seat.lockGood += 1;\\n70→    seat.lock += 1;\\n    seat.lockBeat = op.tick + 40;\\n    if (seat.lock >= 3) finishLock(op, seat);\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  if (seat.giftLeft > 0) return;\\n  if (seat.charges <= 0 && !op.attract) return;\\n  if (!op.attract) seat.charges -= 1;\\n  op.giftUsed = true;\\n  if (op.simple) {\\n80→    seat.giftKind = seat.gift === 'second' ? 'pulse' : 'still';\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/body.ts\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file Vitals, the clock, the Code, the Gift, phase changes, and the colleague. Field time is the only clock\\n * the patient knows. Cursors already moved before this runs.\\n */\\nimport { award, failOp, heal, POINTS, winOp } from './ratings';\\nimport type { Hand, Op, Seat, Spawn } from './types';\\nimport { addTarget, enterPhase, FIELD_SECOND } from './world';\\n\\n/** Field ticks this step. Stillpoint is a quarter. The pulse-lock minigame is 30 percent. */\\nexport function fieldDelta(op: Op): number {\\n  if (op.seats.some((seat) => seat.giftKind === 'still' && seat.giftLeft > 0)) return 25;\\n  if (op.seats.some((seat) => seat.lock >= 0)) return 30;\\n  return 100;\\n}\\n\\n/** Read hands into seats. Null means the menu is up: cursors stay, buttons do not stick. */\\nexport function applyHands(op: Op, hands: readonly Hand[] | null): void {\\n  if (!hands) {\\n    for (const seat of op.seats) seat.use = false;\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  for (let i = 0; i < op.seats.length; i++) {\\n    const hand = hands[i];\\n    const seat = op.seats[i];\\n    if (!hand) continue;\\n    seat.x = Math.max(-8, Math.min(8, hand.x));\\n    seat.z = Math.max(-5, Math.min(5, hand.z));\\n    if (op.roll) {\\n      const wave = Math.sin(op.tick / 40);\\n      if (op.tick % 420 < 36) {\\n        seat.x += wave * 0.1;\\n        seat.z += wave * 0.04;\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (hand.tool >= 0 && hand.tool <= 7 && hand.tool !== seat.tool) {\\n      seat.tool = hand.tool;\\n      op.events.push({ type: 'tool', text: 'clack', seat: seat.id });\\n    }\\n    seat.use = hand.use;\\n    seat.drop = hand.drop;\\n    if (hand.site >= 0 && hand.site < op.sites.length) seat.site = hand.site;\\n    if (hand.hint) op.events.push({ type: 'hint', text: op.hint || 'Steady, Doctor.', seat: seat.id });\\n    if (hand.swap && op.swapOk) swapPersona(op, seat);\\n    if (hand.gift) pressGift(op, seat);\\n    if (hand.paddle) pressPaddle(op, seat);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** Swap the lead between Stillpoint and Second Pulse. */\\nfunction swapPersona(op: Op, seat: Seat): void {\\n  if (seat.id !== 0) return;\\n  if (seat.gift === 'stillpoint') {\\n    seat.gift = 'second';\\n    op.persona = 'sabine';\\n  } else if (seat.gift === 'second') {\\n    seat.gift = 'stillpoint';\\n    op.persona = 'wren';\\n  }\\n  op.events.push({ type: 'swap', text: op.persona, seat: seat.id });\\n}\\n\\n/** Triangle: start a lock, or hit the next beat. Simple Gift skips the lock. */\\nfunction pressGift(op: Op, seat: Seat): void {\\n  if (seat.gift === 'none' && seat.charges <= 0 && !op.attract) return;\\n  if (seat.lock >= 0) {\\n    const window = Math.max(4, Math.round((op.balance.giftWindow / 1000) * 60));\\n    const error = Math.abs(op.tick - seat.lockBeat);\\n    if (error <= Math.max(2, Math.round(window / 2))) seat.lockPerfect += 1;\\n    else if (error <= window) seat.lockGood += 1;\\n    seat.lock += 1;\\n    seat.lockBeat = op.tick + 40;\\n    if (seat.lock >= 3) finishLock(op, seat);\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  if (seat.giftLeft > 0) return;\\n  if (seat.charges <= 0 && !op.attract) return;\\n  if (!op.attract) seat.charges -= 1;\\n  op.giftUsed = true;\\n  if (op.simple) {\\n    seat.giftKind = seat.gift === 'second' ? 'pulse' : 'still';\\n\",\"total_lines\":292}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"2d00459d-165d-44e8-9cd6-1491a354e5a1"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_130","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Radial slow is missing from fieldDelta.\n\nAdding `op.radial` to the Hand type would require a simulation change. The hash must exclude this field to avoid breaking bot test scores.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7a95ceb0-6bed-4589-bdbd-b47d0a3b783a-122","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/world.ts","offset":450,"limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1998,"output_tokens":338,"cache_read_input_tokens":160512,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"faf88915-fbdf-47a4-a3fc-f9106d9789cd"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-7a95ceb0-6bed-4589-bdbd-b47d0a3b783a-122","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"450→  return (x - Math.floor(x) - 0.5) * 0.16;\\n}\\n\\n/** Start the current phase: hint, teach, spawns, entrance. */\\nexport function enterPhase(op: Op): void {\\n  const phase = op.phases[op.phase];\\n  if (!phase) {\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  op.hint = phase.hint;\\n460→  op.teach = phase.teach;\\n  op.codeCleared = false;\\n  spawnPhase(op, phase, op.phase);\\n  if (phase.onEnter === 'dip') {\\n    for (const patient of op.patients) patient.vitals = Math.min(patient.vitals, 40);\\n  }\\n  if (phase.onEnter === 'flatline') {\\n    const patient = op.patients[0];\\n    patient.vitals = 0;\\n    op.events.push({ type: 'flatline', text: 'Flatline.' });\\n470→  }\\n  if (phase.onEnter === 'mercy-expose') op.mercyExposed = 1;\\n  op.events.push({ type: 'phase', text: phase.hint });\\n}\\n\\n/** Hash the gameplay state. Bot memos and event text stay out, so a replay of hands reproduces it. */\\nexport function hashOp(op: Op): string {\\n  const parts: string[] = [\\n    String(op.tick),\\n    String(op.phase),\\n480→    op.status,\\n    String(q(op.field)),\\n    String(q(op.clock)),\\n    String(op.slips),\\n    String(op.score),\\n  ];\\n  for (const patient of op.patients) parts.push(String(q(patient.vitals)), patient.alive ? '1' : '0');\\n  for (const seat of op.seats) {\\n    parts.push(String(q(seat.x)), String(q(seat.z)), String(seat.tool), String(seat.score), String(q(seat.chain)));\\n  }\\n490→  for (const target of op.targets) {\\n    parts.push(\\n      String(target.id),\\n      target.kind,\\n      target.done ? '1' : '0',\\n      String(q(target.x)),\\n      String(q(target.z)),\\n      String(q(target.volume)),\\n      String(q(target.burn)),\\n      String(target.stitches),\\n500→      String(target.cut),\\n      String(q(target.hp)),\\n      String(target.gen),\\n      target.hidden ? '1' : '0',\\n      String(target.dose),\\n      String(q(target.lift)),\\n    );\\n  }\\n  if (op.code) parts.push('code', String(op.code.tries), String(q(op.code.left)));\\n  let h = 2166136261;\\n510→  const text = parts.join(',');\\n  for (let i = 0; i < text.length; i++) {\\n    h ^= text.charCodeAt(i);\\n    h = Math.imul(h, 16777619);\\n  }\\n  return (h >>> 0).toString(16);\\n}\\n\\n/** A short picture of an operation for a failing test. */\\nexport function debugOp(op: Op): string {\\n520→  const left = op.targets.filter((target) => !target.done && target.phase === op.phase);\\n  const vitals = op.patients.map((patient) => Math.round(patient.vitals)).join('/');\\n  return `${op.id} ${op.status} ${op.fail} phase ${op.phase}/${op.phases.length} tick ${op.tick} vitals ${vitals} slips ${op.slips} left ${left.map((target) => target.kind + target.id).join(',')}`;\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"450→  return (x - Math.floor(x) - 0.5) * 0.16;\\n}\\n\\n/** Start the current phase: hint, teach, spawns, entrance. */\\nexport function enterPhase(op: Op): void {\\n  const phase = op.phases[op.phase];\\n  if (!phase) {\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  op.hint = phase.hint;\\n460→  op.teach = phase.teach;\\n  op.codeCleared = false;\\n  spawnPhase(op, phase, op.phase);\\n  if (phase.onEnter === 'dip') {\\n    for (const patient of op.patients) patient.vitals = Math.min(patient.vitals, 40);\\n  }\\n  if (phase.onEnter === 'flatline') {\\n    const patient = op.patients[0];\\n    patient.vitals = 0;\\n    op.events.push({ type: 'flatline', text: 'Flatline.' });\\n470→  }\\n  if (phase.onEnter === 'mercy-expose') op.mercyExposed = 1;\\n  op.events.push({ type: 'phase', text: phase.hint });\\n}\\n\\n/** Hash the gameplay state. Bot memos and event text stay out, so a replay of hands reproduces it. */\\nexport function hashOp(op: Op): string {\\n  const parts: string[] = [\\n    String(op.tick),\\n    String(op.phase),\\n480→    op.status,\\n    String(q(op.field)),\\n    String(q(op.clock)),\\n    String(op.slips),\\n    String(op.score),\\n  ];\\n  for (const patient of op.patients) parts.push(String(q(patient.vitals)), patient.alive ? '1' : '0');\\n  for (const seat of op.seats) {\\n    parts.push(String(q(seat.x)), String(q(seat.z)), String(seat.tool), String(seat.score), String(q(seat.chain)));\\n  }\\n490→  for (const target of op.targets) {\\n    parts.push(\\n      String(target.id),\\n      target.kind,\\n      target.done ? '1' : '0',\\n      String(q(target.x)),\\n      String(q(target.z)),\\n      String(q(target.volume)),\\n      String(q(target.burn)),\\n      String(target.stitches),\\n500→      String(target.cut),\\n      String(q(target.hp)),\\n      String(target.gen),\\n      target.hidden ? '1' : '0',\\n      String(target.dose),\\n      String(q(target.lift)),\\n    );\\n  }\\n  if (op.code) parts.push('code', String(op.code.tries), String(q(op.code.left)));\\n  let h = 2166136261;\\n510→  const text = parts.join(',');\\n  for (let i = 0; i < text.length; i++) {\\n    h ^= text.charCodeAt(i);\\n    h = Math.imul(h, 16777619);\\n  }\\n  return (h >>> 0).toString(16);\\n}\\n\\n/** A short picture of an operation for a failing test. */\\nexport function debugOp(op: Op): string {\\n520→  const left = op.targets.filter((target) => !target.done && target.phase === op.phase);\\n  const vitals = op.patients.map((patient) => Math.round(patient.vitals)).join('/');\\n  return `${op.id} ${op.status} ${op.fail} phase ${op.phase}/${op.phases.length} tick ${op.tick} vitals ${vitals} slips ${op.slips} left ${left.map((target) => target.kind + target.id).join(',')}`;\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/world.ts\",\"offset\":450,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"  return (x - Math.floor(x) - 0.5) * 0.16;\\n}\\n\\n/** Start the current phase: hint, teach, spawns, entrance. */\\nexport function enterPhase(op: Op): void {\\n  const phase = op.phases[op.phase];\\n  if (!phase) {\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  op.hint = phase.hint;\\n  op.teach = phase.teach;\\n  op.codeCleared = false;\\n  spawnPhase(op, phase, op.phase);\\n  if (phase.onEnter === 'dip') {\\n    for (const patient of op.patients) patient.vitals = Math.min(patient.vitals, 40);\\n  }\\n  if (phase.onEnter === 'flatline') {\\n    const patient = op.patients[0];\\n    patient.vitals = 0;\\n    op.events.push({ type: 'flatline', text: 'Flatline.' });\\n  }\\n  if (phase.onEnter === 'mercy-expose') op.mercyExposed = 1;\\n  op.events.push({ type: 'phase', text: phase.hint });\\n}\\n\\n/** Hash the gameplay state. Bot memos and event text stay out, so a replay of hands reproduces it. */\\nexport function hashOp(op: Op): string {\\n  const parts: string[] = [\\n    String(op.tick),\\n    String(op.phase),\\n    op.status,\\n    String(q(op.field)),\\n    String(q(op.clock)),\\n    String(op.slips),\\n    String(op.score),\\n  ];\\n  for (const patient of op.patients) parts.push(String(q(patient.vitals)), patient.alive ? '1' : '0');\\n  for (const seat of op.seats) {\\n    parts.push(String(q(seat.x)), String(q(seat.z)), String(seat.tool), String(seat.score), String(q(seat.chain)));\\n  }\\n  for (const target of op.targets) {\\n    parts.push(\\n      String(target.id),\\n      target.kind,\\n      target.done ? '1' : '0',\\n      String(q(target.x)),\\n      String(q(target.z)),\\n      String(q(target.volume)),\\n      String(q(target.burn)),\\n      String(target.stitches),\\n      String(target.cut),\\n      String(q(target.hp)),\\n      String(target.gen),\\n      target.hidden ? '1' : '0',\\n      String(target.dose),\\n      String(q(target.lift)),\\n    );\\n  }\\n  if (op.code) parts.push('code', String(op.code.tries), String(q(op.code.left)));\\n  let h = 2166136261;\\n  const text = parts.join(',');\\n  for (let i = 0; i < text.length; i++) {\\n    h ^= text.charCodeAt(i);\\n    h = Math.imul(h, 16777619);\\n  }\\n  return (h >>> 0).toString(16);\\n}\\n\\n/** A short picture of an operation for a failing test. */\\nexport function debugOp(op: Op): string {\\n  const left = op.targets.filter((target) => !target.done && target.phase === op.phase);\\n  const vitals = op.patients.map((patient) => Math.round(patient.vitals)).join('/');\\n  return `${op.id} ${op.status} ${op.fail} phase ${op.phase}/${op.phases.length} tick ${op.tick} vitals ${vitals} slips ${op.slips} left ${left.map((target) => target.kind + target.id).join(',')}`;\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":523}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"b5d231ee-15d9-4ee0-91be-5878bd2a9fa9"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_131","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A module-level flag could add radial slow without changing the hash.\n\nAdding `op.radialOpen` to the hash as one bit keeps peers in lockstep. A module-level flag would let states diverge.\n\n`radial` will be a boolean on `Op` and `Hand`, defaulting to false. It will be the 11th number in the hand stride. `applyHands` will set it from any hand's radial flag. `fieldDelta` will return 60 for radial ops before the default 100. `emptyOp` will initialize it as false.\n\nAll Op constructors and pack/unpack paths are verified. The gift button needs edge-detection so holding it does not retrigger.\n\nGift, swap, hint, paddle, drop, and site will all be edge-detected in hands.ts. Use remains a hold action. Story gala scenes will be added. The vitest timeout will be raised to 30 seconds. playThrough of eight cases should finish under two seconds. The sequencer test will run 14400 steps on a locked hidden mass.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9acdf1ce-d5c6-428a-9bb5-924091d2c113-123","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"act\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/app/engine.ts","head_limit":20}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1269,"output_tokens":808,"cache_read_input_tokens":162432,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"2602e038-63e9-468c-a5d6-7e9119470257"}
