{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-80452105-5c7a-4c3b-8b3a-80c4c3949a11-130","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"150→\\n/** The charge ring is green for a generous slice of each beat-and-a-half. */\\nexport function codeBand(op: Op): boolean {\\n  const at = op.tick % 90;\\n  return at >= 28 && at < 62;\\n}\\n\\n/** Bleeds, parasite auras, numb patches, then the flatline check. */\\nexport function stepVitals(op: Op, ft: number): void {\\n  const seconds = ft / FIELD_SECOND;\\n160→  const scale = op.balance.vitalsDrain;\\n  const diff = op.difficulty === 'intern' ? 0.6 : op.difficulty === 'attending' ? 1.3 : 1;\\n  for (const patient of op.patients) {\\n    if (!patient.alive) continue;\\n    const shielded = op.seats.some((seat) => seat.giftKind === 'pulse' && seat.giftLeft > 0);\\n    let drain = 0;\\n    for (const target of op.targets) {\\n      if (target.done || target.patient !== patient.id) continue;\\n      if (target.kind === 'pool' && target.volume > 0) drain += target.bleed * op.balance.bleed;\\n      if (target.kind === 'wound' && target.bleeding) drain += (target.deep ? 1.2 : target.bleed) * op.balance.bleed;\\n170→      if (target.kind === 'lull' || target.kind === 'matron') drain += 0.6;\\n      if (target.kind === 'numb') drain += 0.2;\\n      if (target.kind === 'balmCell') drain += 0.01;\\n      if (target.kind === 'bleeder') drain += target.bleed;\\n    }\\n    if (!shielded) patient.vitals -= drain * seconds * scale * diff;\\n    if (op.attract) patient.vitals = Math.max(30, patient.vitals);\\n    patient.vitals = Math.min(100, patient.vitals);\\n    if (patient.vitals <= 0) flatline(op, patient.id);\\n  }\\n180→}\\n\\n/** Vitals hit zero. */\\nfunction flatline(op: Op, patientId: number): void {\\n  const patient = op.patients[patientId];\\n  patient.vitals = 0;\\n  if (op.code) return;\\n  if (!op.codeAllowed || (patient.coded && op.id !== 'case:mercy')) {\\n    patient.alive = false;\\n    failOp(op, `${patient.name} is gone.`);\\n190→    return;\\n  }\\n  patient.coded = op.id !== 'case:mercy';\\n  op.code = { left: 8 * FIELD_SECOND, tries: 2, patient: patientId, free: op.id === 'case:mercy', shocks: 0 };\\n  op.events.push({ type: 'code', text: 'Paddles.' });\\n}\\n\\n/** Gifts, the Code timer, the clock, and the phase. */\\nexport function stepBody(op: Op, ft: number): void {\\n  tickLocks(op);\\n200→  for (const seat of op.seats) if (seat.giftLeft > 0 && seat.lock < 0) seat.giftLeft -= 1;\\n  if (op.code) {\\n    op.code.left -= ft;\\n    if (op.code.left <= 0) {\\n      op.code = null;\\n      failOp(op, 'The line stays flat.');\\n    }\\n  }\\n  if (!op.attract) op.clock -= ft / Math.max(0.4, op.balance.clock);\\n  if (op.clock <= 0 && op.status === 'playing') {\\n210→    op.clock = 0;\\n    failOp(op, 'Time.');\\n  }\\n  stepColleague(op);\\n  advance(op);\\n}\\n\\n/** The AI colleague drains and holds flaps. It never takes the lead's hands. */\\nfunction stepColleague(op: Op): void {\\n  op.helper = '';\",\"content_concise\":\"150→\\n/** The charge ring is green for a generous slice of each beat-and-a-half. */\\nexport function codeBand(op: Op): boolean {\\n  const at = op.tick % 90;\\n  return at >= 28 && at < 62;\\n}\\n\\n/** Bleeds, parasite auras, numb patches, then the flatline check. */\\nexport function stepVitals(op: Op, ft: number): void {\\n  const seconds = ft / FIELD_SECOND;\\n160→  const scale = op.balance.vitalsDrain;\\n  const diff = op.difficulty === 'intern' ? 0.6 : op.difficulty === 'attending' ? 1.3 : 1;\\n  for (const patient of op.patients) {\\n    if (!patient.alive) continue;\\n    const shielded = op.seats.some((seat) => seat.giftKind === 'pulse' && seat.giftLeft > 0);\\n    let drain = 0;\\n    for (const target of op.targets) {\\n      if (target.done || target.patient !== patient.id) continue;\\n      if (target.kind === 'pool' && target.volume > 0) drain += target.bleed * op.balance.bleed;\\n      if (target.kind === 'wound' && target.bleeding) drain += (target.deep ? 1.2 : target.bleed) * op.balance.bleed;\\n170→      if (target.kind === 'lull' || target.kind === 'matron') drain += 0.6;\\n      if (target.kind === 'numb') drain += 0.2;\\n      if (target.kind === 'balmCell') drain += 0.01;\\n      if (target.kind === 'bleeder') drain += target.bleed;\\n    }\\n    if (!shielded) patient.vitals -= drain * seconds * scale * diff;\\n    if (op.attract) patient.vitals = Math.max(30, patient.vitals);\\n    patient.vitals = Math.min(100, patient.vitals);\\n    if (patient.vitals <= 0) flatline(op, patient.id);\\n  }\\n180→}\\n\\n/** Vitals hit zero. */\\nfunction flatline(op: Op, patientId: number): void {\\n  const patient = op.patients[patientId];\\n  patient.vitals = 0;\\n  if (op.code) return;\\n  if (!op.codeAllowed || (patient.coded && op.id !== 'case:mercy')) {\\n    patient.alive = false;\\n    failOp(op, `${patient.name} is gone.`);\\n190→    return;\\n  }\\n  patient.coded = op.id !== 'case:mercy';\\n  op.code = { left: 8 * FIELD_SECOND, tries: 2, patient: patientId, free: op.id === 'case:mercy', shocks: 0 };\\n  op.events.push({ type: 'code', text: 'Paddles.' });\\n}\\n\\n/** Gifts, the Code timer, the clock, and the phase. */\\nexport function stepBody(op: Op, ft: number): void {\\n  tickLocks(op);\\n200→  for (const seat of op.seats) if (seat.giftLeft > 0 && seat.lock < 0) seat.giftLeft -= 1;\\n  if (op.code) {\\n    op.code.left -= ft;\\n    if (op.code.left <= 0) {\\n      op.code = null;\\n      failOp(op, 'The line stays flat.');\\n    }\\n  }\\n  if (!op.attract) op.clock -= ft / Math.max(0.4, op.balance.clock);\\n  if (op.clock <= 0 && op.status === 'playing') {\\n210→    op.clock = 0;\\n    failOp(op, 'Time.');\\n  }\\n  stepColleague(op);\\n  advance(op);\\n}\\n\\n/** The AI colleague drains and holds flaps. It never takes the lead's hands. */\\nfunction stepColleague(op: Op): void {\\n  op.helper = '';\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/body.ts\",\"offset\":150,\"limit\":70,\"raw_output\":\"\\n/** The charge ring is green for a generous slice of each beat-and-a-half. */\\nexport function codeBand(op: Op): boolean {\\n  const at = op.tick % 90;\\n  return at >= 28 && at < 62;\\n}\\n\\n/** Bleeds, parasite auras, numb patches, then the flatline check. */\\nexport function stepVitals(op: Op, ft: number): void {\\n  const seconds = ft / FIELD_SECOND;\\n  const scale = op.balance.vitalsDrain;\\n  const diff = op.difficulty === 'intern' ? 0.6 : op.difficulty === 'attending' ? 1.3 : 1;\\n  for (const patient of op.patients) {\\n    if (!patient.alive) continue;\\n    const shielded = op.seats.some((seat) => seat.giftKind === 'pulse' && seat.giftLeft > 0);\\n    let drain = 0;\\n    for (const target of op.targets) {\\n      if (target.done || target.patient !== patient.id) continue;\\n      if (target.kind === 'pool' && target.volume > 0) drain += target.bleed * op.balance.bleed;\\n      if (target.kind === 'wound' && target.bleeding) drain += (target.deep ? 1.2 : target.bleed) * op.balance.bleed;\\n      if (target.kind === 'lull' || target.kind === 'matron') drain += 0.6;\\n      if (target.kind === 'numb') drain += 0.2;\\n      if (target.kind === 'balmCell') drain += 0.01;\\n      if (target.kind === 'bleeder') drain += target.bleed;\\n    }\\n    if (!shielded) patient.vitals -= drain * seconds * scale * diff;\\n    if (op.attract) patient.vitals = Math.max(30, patient.vitals);\\n    patient.vitals = Math.min(100, patient.vitals);\\n    if (patient.vitals <= 0) flatline(op, patient.id);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** Vitals hit zero. */\\nfunction flatline(op: Op, patientId: number): void {\\n  const patient = op.patients[patientId];\\n  patient.vitals = 0;\\n  if (op.code) return;\\n  if (!op.codeAllowed || (patient.coded && op.id !== 'case:mercy')) {\\n    patient.alive = false;\\n    failOp(op, `${patient.name} is gone.`);\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  patient.coded = op.id !== 'case:mercy';\\n  op.code = { left: 8 * FIELD_SECOND, tries: 2, patient: patientId, free: op.id === 'case:mercy', shocks: 0 };\\n  op.events.push({ type: 'code', text: 'Paddles.' });\\n}\\n\\n/** Gifts, the Code timer, the clock, and the phase. */\\nexport function stepBody(op: Op, ft: number): void {\\n  tickLocks(op);\\n  for (const seat of op.seats) if (seat.giftLeft > 0 && seat.lock < 0) seat.giftLeft -= 1;\\n  if (op.code) {\\n    op.code.left -= ft;\\n    if (op.code.left <= 0) {\\n      op.code = null;\\n      failOp(op, 'The line stays flat.');\\n    }\\n  }\\n  if (!op.attract) op.clock -= ft / Math.max(0.4, op.balance.clock);\\n  if (op.clock <= 0 && op.status === 'playing') {\\n    op.clock = 0;\\n    failOp(op, 'Time.');\\n  }\\n  stepColleague(op);\\n  advance(op);\\n}\\n\\n/** The AI colleague drains and holds flaps. It never takes the lead's hands. */\\nfunction stepColleague(op: Op): void {\\n  op.helper = '';\\n\",\"total_lines\":292}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"9df5bc43-c410-45de-b95f-4da454de63e7"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_139","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I will add holdVitals and holdClock.\n\nholdVitals preserves vitals and skips drain and flatline. holdClock and attract skip clock decrease. oneHit will be a dev action that sets all target HP to 0.01 and burnNeed to tiny. Autoplay feeds botHands. Spawn target calls addTarget at the seat position. These go in scenes/dev.ts.\n\nRadial will be added to the operation types. The hash will include radial, holdVitals, and holdClock so lockstep detects them. I am now writing the complete implementation. For end-to-end verification, I will boot the engine, wait for ready, confirm the title is visible, and run the full eight-case playthrough.\n\nAutoplay will be triggered by a `?game.autoplay=1` URL parameter. The end-to-end test will set this flag and wait for the credits screen, with a 180-second timeout. A separate attract-mode test will wait 11 seconds on the title screen and verify an attract or DEMO banner appears before exiting. Menu navigation via pad and touch interactions like the phone profile and settings button will also be tested.\n\nA Python script will print JSON for Firefox and WebKit. Browsers block audio until a user gesture, so the end-to-end test will click the canvas first. It will check the music volume via the audio object and expose window.__compass.audio for testing. After the click, it will play a beep and read the analyser to confirm sound is heard.\n\nI will implement and run the hub. It will spawn a Python HTTP server and Playwright Chromium. I will download session.js to labs/game/net/session.js and embed it in index.html. I will create tools/one-file.mts. I will copy verify.mjs into labs and add the npm script. The exit interview will be written after test results are known.\n\nI will keep a testing log and update PROGRESS.md as I go so compaction can resume. I am starting the batch file writes now.\n\nFor the story gala, I will insert the new entry before the array closes. In the types, Hand.radial will be optional so existing hands remain compatible, while Op.radial, holdVitals, and holdClock will be required booleans so emptyOp initializes them. I noted that tests using partial Op literals with `as Op` would break.\n\nI will grep for `as Op` and `radial` to confirm no partial Op literals exist. The required fields will be set in emptyOp only. stepVitals will subtract drain only when not holding vitals, but still clamp and floor for attract mode. Clock decrease is skipped during attract or holdClock. fieldDelta returns 60 when radial is active. The hash string uses 'r' for radial, 'v' for holdVitals, and 'c' for holdClock.\n\napplyHands will set op.radial to true if any hand is radial. The page CSS will live in labs/game/ui/shell.css and import from main. I will download session.js first and verify its first line before embedding it. The webgpu inline script must not contain `<!--`. I will also check eslint import type and prettier settings. main.ts will be split so boot logic stays under 200 lines.\n\nI am splitting the main entry point into focused modules: ui/shell.ts for DOM, app/play.ts for the frame loop, input/hands.ts for input, and net/hub.ts for networking. The shell will be further broken into ui/dom.ts, ui/screens.ts, ui/menus.ts, and ui/hud.ts to keep each file small. I am also designing the campaign flow logic in app/campaign.ts with a Campaign interface that tracks screen state, story ID, box, case ID, difficulty, and seats.\n\nThe Campaign interface now includes fields for simple mode, glyph set, auto, attract, dev, page, focus, items, message, touch, hub, cardLeft, ready, asked, and demo. I am also defining the campaign API: createCampaign, move, accept, cancel, and tick to handle attract timers and autoplay.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-08ad79b9-cd14-4286-8f3f-5e594180352b-131","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/best.ts","limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1028,"output_tokens":1850,"cache_read_input_tokens":167808,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"ddd56e21-984d-436a-ad5e-7672df13bc72"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-08ad79b9-cd14-4286-8f3f-5e594180352b-131","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The starter game's best round (PLAN.md WP 10.9): the fastest round won, kept across sessions in the engine's\\n * store (engine/app/store.ts) under the game's own prefix. `bestOf(store)` reads it (null before a first win) and\\n * `recordBest(store, seconds)` keeps a time that beats it, returning the best after. The page (labs/game/main.ts)\\n * records each won round's time and shows the best in the HUD; a replay's page opens the store in its `demo` mode, so\\n * a replay never sets a best.\\n *\\n * Game code, a page's: it imports only the engine's public API (engine/index.ts).\\n *\\n10→ * @example\\n * import { createStore } from '../../engine';\\n * const store = createStore({ mode: 'demo' }); // in memory: nothing kept past the page\\n * [recordBest(store, 14.2), recordBest(store, 16), recordBest(store, 9.5), bestOf(store)]; // [14.2, 14.2, 9.5, 9.5]\\n * @see labs/game/best.test.ts\\n */\\nimport type { Store } from '../../engine';\\n\\n/** The key the best round is kept under. */\\nexport const BEST_KEY = 'best';\\n20→\\n/** The fastest won round kept (s), or null: none yet, or a value that is no time. */\\nexport function bestOf(store: Store): number | null {\\n  const best = store.get<unknown>(BEST_KEY, null);\\n  return typeof best === 'number' && best > 0 ? best : null;\\n}\\n\\n/** Keeps `seconds` when it beats the best kept; returns the best after. */\\nexport function recordBest(store: Store, seconds: number): number {\\n  const best = bestOf(store);\\n30→  if (best !== null && best <= seconds) return best;\\n  store.set(BEST_KEY, seconds);\\n  return seconds;\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The starter game's best round (PLAN.md WP 10.9): the fastest round won, kept across sessions in the engine's\\n * store (engine/app/store.ts) under the game's own prefix. `bestOf(store)` reads it (null before a first win) and\\n * `recordBest(store, seconds)` keeps a time that beats it, returning the best after. The page (labs/game/main.ts)\\n * records each won round's time and shows the best in the HUD; a replay's page opens the store in its `demo` mode, so\\n * a replay never sets a best.\\n *\\n * Game code, a page's: it imports only the engine's public API (engine/index.ts).\\n *\\n10→ * @example\\n * import { createStore } from '../../engine';\\n * const store = createStore({ mode: 'demo' }); // in memory: nothing kept past the page\\n * [recordBest(store, 14.2), recordBest(store, 16), recordBest(store, 9.5), bestOf(store)]; // [14.2, 14.2, 9.5, 9.5]\\n * @see labs/game/best.test.ts\\n */\\nimport type { Store } from '../../engine';\\n\\n/** The key the best round is kept under. */\\nexport const BEST_KEY = 'best';\\n20→\\n/** The fastest won round kept (s), or null: none yet, or a value that is no time. */\\nexport function bestOf(store: Store): number | null {\\n  const best = store.get<unknown>(BEST_KEY, null);\\n  return typeof best === 'number' && best > 0 ? best : null;\\n}\\n\\n/** Keeps `seconds` when it beats the best kept; returns the best after. */\\nexport function recordBest(store: Store, seconds: number): number {\\n  const best = bestOf(store);\\n30→  if (best !== null && best <= seconds) return best;\\n  store.set(BEST_KEY, seconds);\\n  return seconds;\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/best.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file The starter game's best round (PLAN.md WP 10.9): the fastest round won, kept across sessions in the engine's\\n * store (engine/app/store.ts) under the game's own prefix. `bestOf(store)` reads it (null before a first win) and\\n * `recordBest(store, seconds)` keeps a time that beats it, returning the best after. The page (labs/game/main.ts)\\n * records each won round's time and shows the best in the HUD; a replay's page opens the store in its `demo` mode, so\\n * a replay never sets a best.\\n *\\n * Game code, a page's: it imports only the engine's public API (engine/index.ts).\\n *\\n * @example\\n * import { createStore } from '../../engine';\\n * const store = createStore({ mode: 'demo' }); // in memory: nothing kept past the page\\n * [recordBest(store, 14.2), recordBest(store, 16), recordBest(store, 9.5), bestOf(store)]; // [14.2, 14.2, 9.5, 9.5]\\n * @see labs/game/best.test.ts\\n */\\nimport type { Store } from '../../engine';\\n\\n/** The key the best round is kept under. */\\nexport const BEST_KEY = 'best';\\n\\n/** The fastest won round kept (s), or null: none yet, or a value that is no time. */\\nexport function bestOf(store: Store): number | null {\\n  const best = store.get<unknown>(BEST_KEY, null);\\n  return typeof best === 'number' && best > 0 ? best : null;\\n}\\n\\n/** Keeps `seconds` when it beats the best kept; returns the best after. */\\nexport function recordBest(store: Store, seconds: number): number {\\n  const best = bestOf(store);\\n  if (best !== null && best <= seconds) return best;\\n  store.set(BEST_KEY, seconds);\\n  return seconds;\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":33}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"af68c209-3bd1-4edf-8466-981b8b45e4f3"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_140","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The store.get/set API exists. I'll use the 'trauma-compass:' prefix.\n\nStore writes will be skipped during attract and hub modes. I'll batch update existing types and world files, then create new files. The Op interface needs radial, holdVitals, and holdClock flags, plus a radial option on Hand.\n\nOptional flags avoid updating every idleHand. applyHands will cast hand.radial to boolean. emptyOp gets three falses. fieldDelta returns 60 for radial. One-hit dev mode sets target.hp and burnNeed to 0.05. Win phase marks all non-optional targets done and advances the phase runner.\n\nFail phase calls failOp with 'Called off.'. Player spawn happens only when physics is enabled. The room will be 16 by 12 tiles, centered on the sheet.\n\nTile size is 1 meter. The room will be 20 by 16 tiles. The player spawns near the center. The sheet prop sits at the player position so the operation field appears in front of the camera.\n\nThe camera sits at the table's top edge, looking down at the sheet. The player stands three meters to the side so the top-down view shows only the sheet. A lamp prop will light the sheet directly.\n\nCursor coordinates map to a 10 by 6 meter field centered on the sheet. The sheet sits at y=0.9, so mouse rays hit that plane and subtract the sheet origin. I'll start writing files now and run tests after the simulation edits. I won't add anything to cases.ts; instead I'll validate that every case has storyBefore and storyAfter, then add twelve gala scenes.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6f622722-ec4c-4a23-9c0f-b8ee2e78e65b-132","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"export function rankFor","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/ratings.ts","-A":12}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2312,"output_tokens":1270,"cache_read_input_tokens":168832,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"1f2761f3-94a5-4bc8-8fc4-17664ba7fb15"}
