{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-fc767806-9e60-4ad1-b6c2-0e93c1ede245-156","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"8→\\n/** Field ticks this step. Stillpoint is a quarter. The pulse-lock minigame is 30 percent. */\\n10→export function fieldDelta(op: Op): number {\\n  if (op.seats.some((seat) => seat.giftKind === 'still' && seat.giftLeft > 0)) return 25;\\n  if (op.seats.some((seat) => seat.lock >= 0)) return 30;\\n  if (op.radial) return 60;\\n  return 100;\\n}\\n\\n/** Read hands into seats. Null means the menu is up: cursors stay, buttons do not stick. */\\nexport function applyHands(op: Op, hands: readonly Hand[] | null): void {\\n  if (!hands) {\",\"content_concise\":\"8→\\n/** Field ticks this step. Stillpoint is a quarter. The pulse-lock minigame is 30 percent. */\\n10→export function fieldDelta(op: Op): number {\\n  if (op.seats.some((seat) => seat.giftKind === 'still' && seat.giftLeft > 0)) return 25;\\n  if (op.seats.some((seat) => seat.lock >= 0)) return 30;\\n  if (op.radial) return 60;\\n  return 100;\\n}\\n\\n/** Read hands into seats. Null means the menu is up: cursors stay, buttons do not stick. */\\nexport function applyHands(op: Op, hands: readonly Hand[] | null): void {\\n  if (!hands) {\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/body.ts\",\"offset\":8,\"limit\":12,\"raw_output\":\"\\n/** Field ticks this step. Stillpoint is a quarter. The pulse-lock minigame is 30 percent. */\\nexport function fieldDelta(op: Op): number {\\n  if (op.seats.some((seat) => seat.giftKind === 'still' && seat.giftLeft > 0)) return 25;\\n  if (op.seats.some((seat) => seat.lock >= 0)) return 30;\\n  if (op.radial) return 60;\\n  return 100;\\n}\\n\\n/** Read hands into seats. Null means the menu is up: cursors stay, buttons do not stick. */\\nexport function applyHands(op: Op, hands: readonly Hand[] | null): void {\\n  if (!hands) {\\n\",\"total_lines\":295}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"45620cd1-7e00-456f-a64b-a4585896af93"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_151","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Writing the bulk of new files.\n\nDrafting scene/main.ts and other core files in parallel. Tests will run while the remaining page files are written.\n\nReorganizing scene/main.ts imports and moving defineSettings to module level. Settings will be defined explicitly in tune.ts with TUNE entries mapping keys to balance properties. The skipUntilChanged flag prevents default values from overriding difficulty during snapshot capture.\n\nDrafting the `applyTune` function in scene/main.ts. It uses a WeakMap to track each operation's previously applied settings and only updates sliders when values change. Starting to define the `TUNE` array in tune.ts.\n\nFilling out the `TUNE` array with slider definitions for `vitalsDrain` and other balance properties. Also defining `GAME_SETTINGS` with scene-level settings for `run`, `phase`, and `seats`.\n\nAdding `difficulty`, `attract`, `simple`, `colleague`, and `autoplay` to the scene settings. Noting that `view: true` settings might not be included in the simulation hash.\n\nAutoplay will be read from the URL search parameters by the page and stored on the campaign. Dev sliders use `when: 'now'`, so they do not restart the scene. The `game.run` setting uses `when: 'scene'`, which means inspector changes to it will restart the scene.\n\nDesigning a `jumpPhase` helper for scene/main.ts. It will advance the operation phase from its current value up to the target index, marking all prior targets as done before each step.\n\nPlacing the `jumpPhase` helper in `scenes/devact.ts` so it can import `enterPhase` from world. Drafting `openRun` in `bridge.ts`: it strips the `op:` prefix, prepends `case:` to the ID if needed, creates the operation via `createFromCase`, applies any requested phase offset with `jumpPhase`, and stores the result as `live`.\n\n`openRun` returns the created operation. `createFromCase` throws on unknown cases, but title runs skip it entirely.\n\nThe chart writes a snapshot every step. When no operation is active it records idle status. The blob stores JSON of the operation including events.\n\nA restore bug was found: the first step blob is empty. After the first step the blob is set. On restore the engine restores the component blob before the next step. The live operation stays ahead of that restored state.\n\n`writeSnapshot` stringifies the operation into `chart.blob`. The next step compares `JSON.stringify(op)` against that blob. The operation has not been mutated yet so the comparison works.\n\nRestored objects are plain data without methods, but stepOp handles them fine. Balance, radial, and target stitchAt arrays all survive restoration correctly. JSON.stringify drops undefined fields, yet every object sets all its properties so parsing is safe. The per-step snapshot stringification allocates memory, which is acceptable for this game.\n\nAdding an `adoptOp` helper to assign a live operation directly. Scene steps will avoid `**` and `Math.random` and rely on JSON for state. Setup spawns the player at the hero origin with zero speed so they remain idle, plus a table and sheet prop nearby.\n\nCharacter speed is set to 1 so the player stands idle without sending movement commands. Spawn failures for missing props in headless mode will only log warnings. The chart component carries run status, title, and operation state. Scene typing uses defineScene<Components>. A winPhase dev action is being drafted.\n\nDrafting the remaining dev actions in scene/main.ts. `winPhase` marks all non-optional targets of the current phase as done. `failPhase` calls `failOp` with a \"Called off.\" message. `heal` restores every patient's vitals to 100. `freezeVitals` and `freezeClock` toggle their respective hold flags on the live operation. `oneHit` begins by iterating over all targets.\n\n`oneHit` caps each target's HP and burnNeed at 0.05. `unlock` is a placeholder for page save handling. `failOp` must be imported so it sets the operation status to lost. An infinite-gift action will set high charges. A `spawnStrain` helper adds a target at the first seat using the specified kind or defaulting to lull. SceneAction args is typed as unknown.\n\nAutoplay is handled by the page, not a dev action. The dev button sets `campaign.autoplay`, which the page reads to feed bot hands; the page also checks the `game.autoplay` URL flag. During autoplay, real `stepOp` still runs via hands so the bot wins. A time-scale action will call `actions.run('timeScale', { scale: 4 })`, and the inspector can pause and step one frame.\n\nDefining HAND_STRIDE as 11 in codec.ts with radial placed last. Content tests will cover voice line and key matching, scene box counts, case validation, banned scans, table completion, resident seed playthroughs, lockstep hashing, and slider clamping. The op.test slip suite needs re-running together. A quick test for radial slowing the field is optional. The sequencer leaver stops at tick 1800 after 3600 ticks.\n\nConfirmed the sequencer produces exactly 3600 hashes and that seat.use remains false after tick 1806. Peer count is fixed at four regardless of seat parameters. Verified no import cycle exists between sequencer, world, cases, and types. Bridge serialization will stringify a copy of the operation including events for exactness.\n\nThe WeakMap that tracks applied tune settings is module state and does not survive restore. After restoring an operation, the map still references the old object, so the first step after restore initializes it from current engine settings without reapplying balance. The restored balance remains correct because it lives in the snapshot blob.\n\nEngine settings restore correctly. A new `room.ts` will export the level text and a `FIELD_AT` constant at `{ x: 8, y: 0.82, z: 6 }` for page mouse mapping. This file lives under `scenes` so the page can import it directly.\n\n`room.ts` will compile the level text with `compileLevel` to derive the hero spawn position, then export `FIELD_AT` from that result. The scene spawns the player at `FIELD_AT.x + 3` and places props nearby. The map layout is being drafted.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d598fc2b-a2ac-465f-a886-0f7041921dd5-157","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"export function failOp","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/ratings.ts","-A":6}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":476,"output_tokens":3516,"cache_read_input_tokens":183680,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"226cf1eb-9cc5-4312-898b-4e491b3c1a4f"}
