{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_164","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The engine hash covers the entire chart.\n\nI will write a diagnostic to verify deterministic hand generation. It snapshots the chart at tick 30, steps forward, restores, and checks blob equality. I will also clone the op via JSON and step both copies with the same hand function to compare hashOp. Matching seat positions should yield identical hands.\n\nChecking whether JSON.stringify preserves exact float precision. The round-trip safety of JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(x)) for IEEE doubles needs confirmation.\n\nJSON.parse(JSON.stringify(n)) preserves exact finite numbers, though -0 becomes +0. The debug script will go in the scratch directory. I also need to check whether engine.restore copies the blob correctly.\n\nThe operation JSON is small enough to avoid size issues. The restore logic preserves field order, so the blob string should return identical after parsing.\n\nThe WeakMap seen issue is unlikely to cause hash divergence if sliders are not applied on either path. Player physics and settings reads appear deterministic. The mismatch must be in the chart entity component data.\n\nI am now examining the `publish` function. It sets `chart.hash` from `lastHash(op)` when the status is `'playing'`, so a mismatched hash there would directly affect the engine hash.\n\nI also suspect the restore path may skip the chart blob restoration entirely. The reconcile logic only parses the saved snapshot if `entity.chart.blob === snapshot(op)` fails. If that condition passes, the scene module state is used instead, which could leave the chart in an inconsistent state before the next step.\n\nThe restore logic only falls back to the saved snapshot when the tick or status differs. If the chart blob was already updated to the ahead state, the module stays at tick 50 and steps forward from there, diverging from the ahead path that captured the hash at tick 50.\n\nIf the chart blob is not restored, the world reverts to tick 30 while the chart advances to tick 70. That mixed state produces a different hash. The adopt step fails when the blob already matches the snapshot after restore, or when ticks are identical.\n\nA JSON key-order or float-formatting difference between the saved blob and the live snapshot could also prevent adoption. The chart would then advance to tick 70 while physics remain at tick 50, producing a hash that diverges from the ahead path.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-625a8917-8512-4fce-99a7-27fd5b38f0c1-17","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"type: 'string'","glob":"**/engine/core/schema.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-625a8917-8512-4fce-99a7-27fd5b38f0c1-18","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"string:","glob":"**/engine/sim/components.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-625a8917-8512-4fce-99a7-27fd5b38f0c1-19","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/sim/session.ts","offset":170,"limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3315,"output_tokens":1591,"cache_read_input_tokens":51072,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"b24acc1f-4e34-404c-bf24-6344d1b21091"}
