{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_165","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I found the bug in the JavaScript code.\n\nThe restore method reloads captured inputs and step counts. I need to check whether step() replays old inputs or uses new ones.\n\nThe starter test passes because botIntents are deterministic from world state. After restore, viewOf returns the captured state, so the restored inputs match the original continuation.\n\nThe test calls hand() before step(), so it reads the stale liveOp() from tick 50. Reconcile only happens inside step(). The restored world is at tick 30, but live state still reflects tick 50.\n\nThe root cause is now clear. Because hand() runs before step(), it reads tick-50 seat positions from the live singleton. After restore, reconcile adopts the tick-30 operation and applies those stale hands, causing divergence. The original path correctly used tick-30 seats for step 31.\n\nA synchronous hook could restore the live operation before hand() runs. Fixed hands would bypass the issue but violate the plan. The real product problem is that the page reads liveOp() between steps to draw and build hands.\n\nThe fix requires liveOp() to match the chart immediately after restore, not on the next step. Two approaches are being weighed: moving all state into the chart blob so it can be parsed at every read, or finding a scene callback that fires during engine restore.\n\nThe module singleton is invisible to engine capture because play.ts keeps all state inside components. The correct architecture is to make the chart blob the source of truth and hold the operation in component fields.\n\nI am searching for scene lifecycle hooks such as onRestore or restore. If none exist, I will add a `syncOp(engine)` helper that reads the chart from `engine.state()` and updates the live operation. The page and test would call this after every restore.\n\nI am now considering a concrete fix: store operation fields directly in components rather than a single JSON blob. The module would cache these values at the start of each step and expose a `liveOp()` function for the page to call. This would make the operation part of the world state, so restore could update it immediately without waiting for the next step.\n\nI am now checking whether the engine emits any event during restore so the scene can update its live state immediately. If no hook exists, I will change hand() to use a fixed offset from a stored copy instead of reading liveOp() before the step reconciles.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b722da56-f17a-4f59-92ff-0aa79b35cc19-20","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"defineScene\\(","glob":"**/engine/sim/scene.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b722da56-f17a-4f59-92ff-0aa79b35cc19-21","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"interface Scene|setup\\(|restore|capture","glob":"**/engine/sim/scene*.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b722da56-f17a-4f59-92ff-0aa79b35cc19-22","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/scenes/play.ts","limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":50453,"output_tokens":1492,"cache_read_input_tokens":6656,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"29ee0b7a-47e4-4d30-913b-3672dbcc7239"}
