{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_170","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The diagnostic output is being examined.\n\nThe JSON roundtrip is exact. After restore, the live tick is 50 but the chart blob is tick 30 and matches midSnap. The script adopts tick 30 before the loop, which explains why the module still appears ahead.\n\nThe engine hash matches only when the snapshot is adopted before generating hands. The test fails because hand() reads the stale tick-50 op before reconcile adopts tick 30. The first post-restore hand is computed from tick 50 positions, then reconcile applies tick 30 and diverges.\n\nThe fix requires syncing from the chart before building hands. The test should call followChart after restore so liveOp updates, matching the page's real frame path.\n\nThe test is slightly unfair because it builds hands outside the step while the page builds them inside after reconcile. The page reads the restored chart, follows it to update liveOp, then builds hands from input devices. The bot and page cursor are independent.\n\nThe test uses seat positions as a stand-in for input devices. The starter equivalent reads the restored world state via viewOf(engine), while the local equivalent reads the chart blob. A corrected hands() function should adopt the snapshot from the blob before calling liveOp, matching the page's frame path. This would make the test pass. Whether reconcile should remain is still undecided.\n\nReconcile must remain. If the page syncs first, reconcile sees matching ticks and returns early, so stepOp can safely mutate the adopted op and publish a new blob. If the page skips syncing, reconcile inside step still adopts the snapshot and applies the hands computed from the stale op.\n\nThe page's input comes from pads and mouse, not seat position. A stale liveOp therefore only causes a one-frame visual glitch after restore, not an input error. The cursor position updates from hands and the page draws from liveOp. Between restore and the next step, the draw would be stale.\n\nThe plan is to export `followChart(blob)` so the test can sync from the chart before packing hands. A fixed hand trajectory recorded up front is also an option. Both fixes will be applied.\n\nA test will verify the tick reaches 30 after restore and followChart, then confirm the hash matches after 20 steps while the chart status is playing.\n\nProps need to be defined so warnings disappear. The scene can import defineProp from sim-api. The test imports main which imports props. Warnings should go away.\n\nExisting material IDs must be checked so props do not warn about unknown materials.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-fc3ed7da-bd33-4c00-b1eb-24aa7327f46d-31","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"'prop:(table|lamp|sheet|drape|monitor|board)'","glob":"**/engine/world/props/**/*.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-fc3ed7da-bd33-4c00-b1eb-24aa7327f46d-32","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/world/props/fittings.ts","limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1617,"output_tokens":1477,"cache_read_input_tokens":73728,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"4d4014a0-6c3c-47ee-a267-3e1d384b8f35"}
