ells.ts), drawn in front of the sky.',\\n    properties: {\\n      width: {\\n110→        type: 'number',\\n        default: 0,\\n        minimum: 0,\\n        maximum: 4,\\n        description: 'Their width in pixels at 270 lines, scaled to the picture in whole pixels; 0 draws none.',\\n      },\\n      color: { type: 'string', default: '#141018', description: \\\"The shells' colour, hex.\\\" },\\n    },\\n  },\\n  skyGradient: {\\n120→    type: 'number',\\n    default: 0,\\n    minimum: 0,\\n    maximum: 1,\\n    description: \\\"How much of the sky's dome is a clean gradient, horizon haze to zenith, instead of daylight's model.\\\",\\n  },\\n  perspective: {\\n    type: 'string',\\n    default: '',\\n    description:\\n130→      \\\"The look drawn instead while the camera is a perspective one (its variant: same style, sky, resolution and textures); '' keeps this.\\\",\\n  },\\n  resolution: {\\n    type: 'string',\\n    enum: ['', ...RESOLUTION_MODES],\\n    default: '',\\n    description:\\n      \\\"The resolution mode it is drawn at while gfx.resolution is 'auto' (pixels, balanced or full); '' keeps the engine's pixels.\\\",\\n  },\\n  textures: {\\n140→    type: 'string',\\n    enum: ['', ...TEXTURE_LOOKS],\\n    default: '',\\n    description:\\n      \\\"How every material's textures are filtered: 'smooth' blends their texels, 'pixel' keeps them crisp; '' keeps each texture's own.\\\",\\n  },\\n  filters: {\\n    type: 'object',\\n    default: OFF,\\n    description: 'The filter chain: each filter it names, with its scope and numbers; the rest are off.',\\n150→    properties: FILTER_FIELDS,\\n  },\\n  combine: COMBINE_FIELD,\\n  strength: STRENGTH_FIELD,\\n  gallery: galleryField({ camera: 'cam=iso' }),\\n} as const satisfies Schema;\\n\\n/** A `look` entry. */\\nexport type LookEntry = Entry<typeof LOOK_FIELDS>;\\n\\n160→/** What `defineLook` takes: any of the fields, the filters as part of a chain. */\\nexport type LookSpec = Partial<Omit<EntryOf<typeof LOOK_FIELDS>, 'filters' | 'toon' | 'shells' | 'combine'>> & {\\n  toon?: Partial<LookEntry['toon']>;\\n  shells?: Partial<LookEntry['shells']>;\\n  filters?: FilterSpec;\\n  combine?: readonly CombineLayer[];\\n};\\n\\n/** The whole looks, from shardfall's `[[look]]` tables (see the file comment), and the clean picture. */\\nexport const LOOKS: Record<string, LookSpec> = {\\n170→  'look:clean': { description: 'No filter: the picture as the scene draws it, in its own style.' },\\n  'look:pixel-heroes': {\\n    description: 'A clean, sharp world; the characters and objects are outlined pixel art.',\\n    filters: { pixel: { scope: 'characters+objects', size: 5, outline: true } },\\n  },\\n  'look:hd-2d': {\\n    description: 'Pixel-art characters and objects in a soft, glowing 3D world with dark corners.',\\n    filters: {\\n      pixel: { scope: 'characters+objects', size: 4, outline: true },\\n      bloom: { scope: 'all', strength: 1, threshold: 0.7 },\",\"content_concise\":\"100→          \\\"The share of each band's step mixed by an ordered dither fixed to the world, edges hard; 0 smooths.\\\",\\n      },\\n    },\\n  },\\n  shells: {\\n    type: 'object',\\n    default: { width: 0, color: '#141018' },\\n    description: 'Outline shells round the props and bodies (engine/gfx/stageShells.ts), drawn in front of the sky.',\\n    properties: {\\n      width: {\\n110→        type: 'number',\\n        default: 0,\\n        minimum: 0,\\n        maximum: 4,\\n        description: 'Their width in pixels at 270 lines, scaled to the picture in whole pixels; 0 draws none.',\\n      },\\n      color: { type: 'string', default: '#141018', description: \\\"The shells' colour, hex.\\\" },\\n    },\\n  },\\n  skyGradient: {\\n120→    type: 'number',\\n    default: 0,\\n    minimum: 0,\\n    maximum: 1,\\n    description: \\\"How much of the sky's dome is a clean gradient, horizon haze to zenith, instead of daylight's model.\\\",\\n  },\\n  perspective: {\\n    type: 'string',\\n    default: '',\\n    description:\\n130→      \\\"The look drawn instead while the camera is a perspective one (its variant: same style, sky, resolution and textures); '' keeps this.\\\",\\n  },\\n  resolution: {\\n    type: 'string',\\n    enum: ['', ...RESOLUTION_MODES],\\n    default: '',\\n    description:\\n      \\\"The resolution mode it is drawn at while gfx.resolution is 'auto' (pixels, balanced or full); '' keeps the engine's pixels.\\\",\\n  },\\n  textures: {\\n140→    type: 'string',\\n    enum: ['', ...TEXTURE_LOOKS],\\n    default: '',\\n    description:\\n      \\\"How every material's textures are filtered: 'smooth' blends their texels, 'pixel' keeps them crisp; '' keeps each texture's own.\\\",\\n  },\\n  filters: {\\n    type: 'object',\\n    default: OFF,\\n    description: 'The filter chain: each filter it names, with its scope and numbers; the rest are off.',\\n150→    properties: FILTER_FIELDS,\\n  },\\n  combine: COMBINE_FIELD,\\n  strength: STRENGTH_FIELD,\\n  gallery: galleryField({ camera: 'cam=iso' }),\\n} as const satisfies Schema;\\n\\n/** A `look` entry. */\\nexport type LookEntry = Entry<typeof LOOK_FIELDS>;\\n\\n160→/** What `defineLook` takes: any of the fields, the filters as part of a chain. */\\nexport type LookSpec = Partial<Omit<EntryOf<typeof LOOK_FIELDS>, 'filters' | 'toon' | 'shells' | 'combine'>> & {\\n  toon?: Partial<LookEntry['toon']>;\\n  shells?: Partial<LookEntry['shells']>;\\n  filters?: FilterSpec;\\n  combine?: readonly CombineLayer[];\\n};\\n\\n/** The whole looks, from shardfall's `[[look]]` tables (see the file comment), and the clean picture. */\\nexport const LOOKS: Record<string, LookSpec> = {\\n170→  'look:clean': { description: 'No filter: the picture as the scene draws it, in its own style.' },\\n  'look:pixel-heroes': {\\n    description: 'A clean, sharp world; the characters and objects are outlined pixel art.',\\n    filters: { pixel: { scope: 'characters+objects', size: 5, outline: true } },\\n  },\\n  'look:hd-2d': {\\n    description: 'Pixel-art characters and objects in a soft, glowing 3D world with dark corners.',\\n    filters: {\\n      pixel: { scope: 'characters+objects', size: 4, outline: true },\\n      bloom: { scope: 'all', strength: 1, threshold: 0.7 },\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/gfx/post/looks.ts\",\"offset\":100,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"          \\\"The share of each band's step mixed by an ordered dither fixed to the world, edges hard; 0 smooths.\\\",\\n      },\\n    },\\n  },\\n  shells: {\\n    type: 'object',\\n    default: { width: 0, color: '#141018' },\\n    description: 'Outline shells round the props and bodies (engine/gfx/stageShells.ts), drawn in front of the sky.',\\n    properties: {\\n      width: {\\n        type: 'number',\\n        default: 0,\\n        minimum: 0,\\n        maximum: 4,\\n        description: 'Their width in pixels at 270 lines, scaled to the picture in whole pixels; 0 draws none.',\\n      },\\n      color: { type: 'string', default: '#141018', description: \\\"The shells' colour, hex.\\\" },\\n    },\\n  },\\n  skyGradient: {\\n    type: 'number',\\n    default: 0,\\n    minimum: 0,\\n    maximum: 1,\\n    description: \\\"How much of the sky's dome is a clean gradient, horizon haze to zenith, instead of daylight's model.\\\",\\n  },\\n  perspective: {\\n    type: 'string',\\n    default: '',\\n    description:\\n      \\\"The look drawn instead while the camera is a perspective one (its variant: same style, sky, resolution and textures); '' keeps this.\\\",\\n  },\\n  resolution: {\\n    type: 'string',\\n    enum: ['', ...RESOLUTION_MODES],\\n    default: '',\\n    description:\\n      \\\"The resolution mode it is drawn at while gfx.resolution is 'auto' (pixels, balanced or full); '' keeps the engine's pixels.\\\",\\n  },\\n  textures: {\\n    type: 'string',\\n    enum: ['', ...TEXTURE_LOOKS],\\n    default: '',\\n    description:\\n      \\\"How every material's textures are filtered: 'smooth' blends their texels, 'pixel' keeps them crisp; '' keeps each texture's own.\\\",\\n  },\\n  filters: {\\n    type: 'object',\\n    default: OFF,\\n    description: 'The filter chain: each filter it names, with its scope and numbers; the rest are off.',\\n    properties: FILTER_FIELDS,\\n  },\\n  combine: COMBINE_FIELD,\\n  strength: STRENGTH_FIELD,\\n  gallery: galleryField({ camera: 'cam=iso' }),\\n} as const satisfies Schema;\\n\\n/** A `look` entry. */\\nexport type LookEntry = Entry<typeof LOOK_FIELDS>;\\n\\n/** What `defineLook` takes: any of the fields, the filters as part of a chain. */\\nexport type LookSpec = Partial<Omit<EntryOf<typeof LOOK_FIELDS>, 'filters' | 'toon' | 'shells' | 'combine'>> & {\\n  toon?: Partial<LookEntry['toon']>;\\n  shells?: Partial<LookEntry['shells']>;\\n  filters?: FilterSpec;\\n  combine?: readonly CombineLayer[];\\n};\\n\\n/** The whole looks, from shardfall's `[[look]]` tables (see the file comment), and the clean picture. */\\nexport const LOOKS: Record<string, LookSpec> = {\\n  'look:clean': { description: 'No filter: the picture as the scene draws it, in its own style.' },\\n  'look:pixel-heroes': {\\n    description: 'A clean, sharp world; the characters and objects are outlined pixel art.',\\n    filters: { pixel: { scope: 'characters+objects', size: 5, outline: true } },\\n  },\\n  'look:hd-2d': {\\n    description: 'Pixel-art characters and objects in a soft, glowing 3D world with dark corners.',\\n    filters: {\\n      pixel: { scope: 'characters+objects', size: 4, outline: true },\\n      bloom: { scope: 'all', strength: 1, threshold: 0.7 },\\n\",\"total_lines\":363}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-5a8277e3-d79b-4555-84dd-eba70848d325-75","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file Hands as a flat list of numbers, the only shape `game:hands` carries. Ten fields, then the radial flag.\\n * Positions are quantised to 1/256 m so a replay of the same gesture is the same list.\\n */\\nimport type { Hand } from './types';\\n\\n/** Numbers per seat in a packed hand list. */\\nexport const HAND_STRIDE = 11;\\n\\n10→/** One seat's hands as eleven numbers. */\\nexport function packHand(hand: Hand): number[] {\\n  return [\\n    Math.round(hand.x * 256) / 256,\\n    Math.round(hand.z * 256) / 256,\\n    hand.tool,\\n    hand.use ? 1 : 0,\\n    hand.drop ? 1 : 0,\\n    hand.gift ? 1 : 0,\\n    hand.paddle ? 1 : 0,\\n20→    hand.site,\\n    hand.swap ? 1 : 0,\\n    hand.hint ? 1 : 0,\\n    hand.radial ? 1 : 0,\\n  ];\\n}\\n\\n/** Every seat, concatenated. */\\nexport function packHands(hands: readonly Hand[]): number[] {\\n  return hands.flatMap(packHand);\\n30→}\\n\\n/** The list back into hands. A short list returns null so the sim holds still. */\\nexport function unpackHands(raw: unknown, seats: number): Hand[] | null {\\n  if (!Array.isArray(raw) || raw.length < HAND_STRIDE) return null;\\n  const hands: Hand[] = [];\\n  const count = Math.min(seats, Math.floor(raw.length / HAND_STRIDE));\\n  for (let i = 0; i < count; i++) {\\n    const at = i * HAND_STRIDE;\\n    const n = (offset: number): number => {\\n40→      const value = raw[at + offset];\\n      return typeof value === 'number' && Number.isFinite(value) ? value : 0;\\n    };\\n    hands.push({\\n      x: n(0),\\n      z: n(1),\\n      tool: Math.round(n(2)),\\n      use: n(3) > 0,\\n      drop: n(4) > 0,\\n      gift: n(5) > 0,\\n50→      paddle: n(6) > 0,\\n      site: Math.round(n(7)),\\n      swap: n(8) > 0,\\n      hint: n(9) > 0,\\n      radial: n(10) > 0,\\n    });\\n  }\\n  return hands;\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file Hands as a flat list of numbers, the only shape `game:hands` carries. Ten fields, then the radial flag.\\n * Positions are quantised to 1/256 m so a replay of the same gesture is the same list.\\n */\\nimport type { Hand } from './types';\\n\\n/** Numbers per seat in a packed hand list. */\\nexport const HAND_STRIDE = 11;\\n\\n10→/** One seat's hands as eleven numbers. */\\nexport function packHand(hand: Hand): number[] {\\n  return [\\n    Math.round(hand.x * 256) / 256,\\n    Math.round(hand.z * 256) / 256,\\n    hand.tool,\\n    hand.use ? 1 : 0,\\n    hand.drop ? 1 : 0,\\n    hand.gift ? 1 : 0,\\n    hand.paddle ? 1 : 0,\\n20→    hand.site,\\n    hand.swap ? 1 : 0,\\n    hand.hint ? 1 : 0,\\n    hand.radial ? 1 : 0,\\n  ];\\n}\\n\\n/** Every seat, concatenated. */\\nexport function packHands(hands: readonly Hand[]): number[] {\\n  return hands.flatMap(packHand);\\n30→}\\n\\n/** The list back into hands. A short list returns null so the sim holds still. */\\nexport function unpackHands(raw: unknown, seats: number): Hand[] | null {\\n  if (!Array.isArray(raw) || raw.length < HAND_STRIDE) return null;\\n  const hands: Hand[] = [];\\n  const count = Math.min(seats, Math.floor(raw.length / HAND_STRIDE));\\n  for (let i = 0; i < count; i++) {\\n    const at = i * HAND_STRIDE;\\n    const n = (offset: number): number => {\\n40→      const value = raw[at + offset];\\n      return typeof value === 'number' && Number.isFinite(value) ? value : 0;\\n    };\\n    hands.push({\\n      x: n(0),\\n      z: n(1),\\n      tool: Math.round(n(2)),\\n      use: n(3) > 0,\\n      drop: n(4) > 0,\\n      gift: n(5) > 0,\\n50→      paddle: n(6) > 0,\\n      site: Math.round(n(7)),\\n      swap: n(8) > 0,\\n      hint: n(9) > 0,\\n      radial: n(10) > 0,\\n    });\\n  }\\n  return hands;\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/codec.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file Hands as a flat list of numbers, the only shape `game:hands` carries. Ten fields, then the radial flag.\\n * Positions are quantised to 1/256 m so a replay of the same gesture is the same list.\\n */\\nimport type { Hand } from './types';\\n\\n/** Numbers per seat in a packed hand list. */\\nexport const HAND_STRIDE = 11;\\n\\n/** One seat's hands as eleven numbers. */\\nexport function packHand(hand: Hand): number[] {\\n  return [\\n    Math.round(hand.x * 256) / 256,\\n    Math.round(hand.z * 256) / 256,\\n    hand.tool,\\n    hand.use ? 1 : 0,\\n    hand.drop ? 1 : 0,\\n    hand.gift ? 1 : 0,\\n    hand.paddle ? 1 : 0,\\n    hand.site,\\n    hand.swap ? 1 : 0,\\n    hand.hint ? 1 : 0,\\n    hand.radial ? 1 : 0,\\n  ];\\n}\\n\\n/** Every seat, concatenated. */\\nexport function packHands(hands: readonly Hand[]): number[] {\\n  return hands.flatMap(packHand);\\n}\\n\\n/** The list back into hands. A short list returns null so the sim holds still. */\\nexport function unpackHands(raw: unknown, seats: number): Hand[] | null {\\n  if (!Array.isArray(raw) || raw.length < HAND_STRIDE) return null;\\n  const hands: Hand[] = [];\\n  const count = Math.min(seats, Math.floor(raw.length / HAND_STRIDE));\\n  for (let i = 0; i < count; i++) {\\n    const at = i * HAND_STRIDE;\\n    const n = (offset: number): number => {\\n      const value = raw[at + offset];\\n      return typeof value === 'number' && Number.isFinite(value) ? value : 0;\\n    };\\n    hands.push({\\n      x: n(0),\\n      z: n(1),\\n      tool: Math.round(n(2)),\\n      use: n(3) > 0,\\n      drop: n(4) > 0,\\n      gift: n(5) > 0,\\n      paddle: n(6) > 0,\\n      site: Math.round(n(7)),\\n      swap: n(8) > 0,\\n      hint: n(9) > 0,\\n      radial: n(10) > 0,\\n    });\\n  }\\n  return hands;\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":58}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-5a8277e3-d79b-4555-84dd-eba70848d325-76","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"80→export function tableComplete(): boolean {\\n  for (const tool of TOOLS) {\\n    for (const kind of KINDS) {\\n      const row = pairOf(tool, kind);\\n      if (row.effect !== 'refuse' && row.effect !== EFFECT[`${tool}:${kind}`]) return false;\\n      if (row.effect === 'refuse' && row.line.length < 8) return false;\\n    }\\n  }\\n  return true;\\n}\\n90→\\n/** Handbook cards built from the table, one per instrument, plus the gifts and the strains once named. */\\nexport function handbookCards(): { title: string; body: string }[] {\\n  const cards: { title: string; body: string }[] = [];\\n  for (const tool of TOOLS) {\\n    const can: string[] = [];\\n    const cannot: string[] = [];\\n    for (const kind of KINDS) {\\n      const row = pairOf(tool, kind);\\n      if (row.effect === 'refuse') cannot.push(kind);\\n100→      else can.push(`${kind} (${row.effect})`);\\n    }\\n    cards.push({\\n      title: tool,\\n      body: `Can: ${can.join(', ') || 'nothing'}. Cannot: ${cannot.slice(0, 6).join(', ')}. ${refusalLine(tool, cannot[0] as Kind)}`,\\n    });\\n  }\\n  cards.push({\\n    title: 'Stillpoint',\\n    body: 'Three beats on the ECG. Field time slows to a quarter. Your hands do not. One charge, unless the case gives another.',\\n110→  });\\n  cards.push({\\n    title: 'Second Pulse',\\n    body: 'Three beats, then a frenzy. Vitals cannot fall. Clean work heals, and the chain counts double.',\\n  });\\n  cards.push({\\n    title: 'The Code',\\n    body: 'When the line goes flat, both paddles in the green band. Two tries. Land it and the vitals climb back to twenty-five.',\\n  });\\n  cards.push({\\n120→    title: 'Sites and flaps',\\n    body: 'Other sites keep bleeding while you are away. A flap lifts with the forceps and clips for eight seconds. Look under it.',\\n  });\\n  return cards;\\n}\\n\\n/** Whether `tool` is a real instrument id. */\\nexport function isTool(tool: string): tool is Tool {\\n  return (TOOLS as readonly string[]).includes(tool);\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"80→export function tableComplete(): boolean {\\n  for (const tool of TOOLS) {\\n    for (const kind of KINDS) {\\n      const row = pairOf(tool, kind);\\n      if (row.effect !== 'refuse' && row.effect !== EFFECT[`${tool}:${kind}`]) return false;\\n      if (row.effect === 'refuse' && row.line.length < 8) return false;\\n    }\\n  }\\n  return true;\\n}\\n90→\\n/** Handbook cards built from the table, one per instrument, plus the gifts and the strains once named. */\\nexport function handbookCards(): { title: string; body: string }[] {\\n  const cards: { title: string; body: string }[] = [];\\n  for (const tool of TOOLS) {\\n    const can: string[] = [];\\n    const cannot: string[] = [];\\n    for (const kind of KINDS) {\\n      const row = pairOf(tool, kind);\\n      if (row.effect === 'refuse') cannot.push(kind);\\n100→      else can.push(`${kind} (${row.effect})`);\\n    }\\n    cards.push({\\n      title: tool,\\n      body: `Can: ${can.join(', ') || 'nothing'}. Cannot: ${cannot.slice(0, 6).join(', ')}. ${refusalLine(tool, cannot[0] as Kind)}`,\\n    });\\n  }\\n  cards.push({\\n    title: 'Stillpoint',\\n    body: 'Three beats on the ECG. Field time slows to a quarter. Your hands do not. One charge, unless the case gives another.',\\n110→  });\\n  cards.push({\\n    title: 'Second Pulse',\\n    body: 'Three beats, then a frenzy. Vitals cannot fall. Clean work heals, and the chain counts double.',\\n  });\\n  cards.push({\\n    title: 'The Code',\\n    body: 'When the line goes flat, both paddles in the green band. Two tries. Land it and the vitals climb back to twenty-five.',\\n  });\\n  cards.push({\\n120→    title: 'Sites and flaps',\\n    body: 'Other sites keep bleeding while you are away. A flap lifts with the forceps and clips for eight seconds. Look under it.',\\n  });\\n  return cards;\\n}\\n\\n/** Whether `tool` is a real instrument id. */\\nexport function isTool(tool: string): tool is Tool {\\n  return (TOOLS as readonly string[]).includes(tool);\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/table.ts\",\"offset\":80,\"limit\":60,\"raw_output\":\"export function tableComplete(): boolean {\\n  for (const tool of TOOLS) {\\n    for (const kind of KINDS) {\\n      const row = pairOf(tool, kind);\\n      if (row.effect !== 'refuse' && row.effect !== EFFECT[`${tool}:${kind}`]) return false;\\n      if (row.effect === 'refuse' && row.line.length < 8) return false;\\n    }\\n  }\\n  return true;\\n}\\n\\n/** Handbook cards built from the table, one per instrument, plus the gifts and the strains once named. */\\nexport function handbookCards(): { title: string; body: string }[] {\\n  const cards: { title: string; body: string }[] = [];\\n  for (const tool of TOOLS) {\\n    const can: string[] = [];\\n    const cannot: string[] = [];\\n    for (const kind of KINDS) {\\n      const row = pairOf(tool, kind);\\n      if (row.effect === 'refuse') cannot.push(kind);\\n      else can.push(`${kind} (${row.effect})`);\\n    }\\n    cards.push({\\n      title: tool,\\n      body: `Can: ${can.join(', ') || 'nothing'}. Cannot: ${cannot.slice(0, 6).join(', ')}. ${refusalLine(tool, cannot[0] as Kind)}`,\\n    });\\n  }\\n  cards.push({\\n    title: 'Stillpoint',\\n    body: 'Three beats on the ECG. Field time slows to a quarter. Your hands do not. One charge, unless the case gives another.',\\n  });\\n  cards.push({\\n    title: 'Second Pulse',\\n    body: 'Three beats, then a frenzy. Vitals cannot fall. Clean work heals, and the chain counts double.',\\n  });\\n  cards.push({\\n    title: 'The Code',\\n    body: 'When the line goes flat, both paddles in the green band. Two tries. Land it and the vitals climb back to twenty-five.',\\n  });\\n  cards.push({\\n    title: 'Sites and flaps',\\n    body: 'Other sites keep bleeding while you are away. A flap lifts with the forceps and clips for eight seconds. Look under it.',\\n  });\\n  return cards;\\n}\\n\\n/** Whether `tool` is a real instrument id. */\\nexport function isTool(tool: string): tool is Tool {\\n  return (TOOLS as readonly string[]).includes(tool);\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":129}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"83185185-34c7-4997-a00d-405ac6d24613"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_185","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I have a clear picture. I need to write a lot of typechecking code.\n\nChecking createAudio methods, Input axis, Engine inspector types, song track examples, and geometry signatures.\n\nSheet density will be 96 by 60. That yields 5760 vertices. The grid spans 16 meters wide and 10 meters deep. Positions are built at maximum extents for culling bounds. The prop:sheet geometry switches from box to sheet.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-cd8db67b-4af9-45a6-a45c-8a6b29ca02b9-77","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/sequencer.ts","limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-cd8db67b-4af9-45a6-a45c-8a6b29ca02b9-78","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/audio/runtime/audio.ts","offset":1,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-cd8db67b-4af9-45a6-a45c-8a6b29ca02b9-79","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"axis\\(|lastDevice|bindingsFor","glob":"**/engine/app/engine.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-cd8db67b-4af9-45a6-a45c-8a6b29ca02b9-80","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/cases.ts","offset":540,"limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-cd8db67b-4af9-45a6-a45c-8a6b29ca02b9-81","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/gfx/geometry/geometry.ts","offset":90,"limit":50}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4849,"output_tokens":1192,"cache_read_input_tokens":130944,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"b9202be1-78d5-43fb-a550-6fbdc35caf12"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-cd8db67b-4af9-45a6-a45c-8a6b29ca02b9-77","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file Host lockstep without a socket. Four copies, delayed intents, loss on the way to the host, one leaver.\\n * The host's applied hands are what every copy steps. After the run, the hashes for each applied tick agree.\\n */\\nimport { stepOp, lastHash } from './step';\\nimport type { Hand, Op } from './types';\\nimport { addTarget, createBare, idleHand } from './world';\\n\\n/** A roll in 0..1 from the tick and the seat, with no Math.random. */\\n10→function roll(tick: number, seat: number): number {\\n  const x = Math.sin(tick * 12.9898 + seat * 78.233) * 43758.5453;\\n  return x - Math.floor(x);\\n}\\n\\n/** What one surgeon meant to do on one tick. Pure, so every copy would have sent the same intent. */\\nexport function intentAt(tick: number, seat: number, hand: Hand): Hand {\\n  const angle = tick / 18 + seat;\\n  return {\\n    ...hand,\\n20→    x: Math.sin(angle) * (1.4 + seat * 0.15),\\n    z: Math.cos(angle * 0.8) * 0.9,\\n    tool: Math.floor(tick / 90 + seat) % 8,\\n    use: tick % 37 < 8,\\n    gift: false,\\n    paddle: false,\\n    drop: false,\\n    site: -1,\\n    swap: false,\\n    hint: false,\\n30→  };\\n}\\n\\n/** One peer's view of the operation. */\\ninterface Peer {\\n  op: Op;\\n  /** Last intent that actually reached the host, per seat. */\\n  last: Hand[];\\n  /** Hash after each applied tick. */\\n  hashes: string[];\\n40→}\\n\\n/** Run the lockstep. Returns the peers so a test can read the hashes. */\\nexport function runLockstep(ticks = 3600, seats = 4): { peers: Peer[]; dropped: number; leftAt: number } {\\n  const peers: Peer[] = [];\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) {\\n    const op = createBare({ seats, code: false });\\n    addAnchor(op);\\n    peers.push({ op, last: op.seats.map((seat) => idleHand(seat)), hashes: [] });\\n  }\\n50→  const host = peers[0];\\n  let dropped = 0;\\n  const leftAt = Math.floor(ticks / 2);\\n  const delay = 4;\\n  /** Intents in flight: tick they were sent, seat, hand, and whether the wire kept them. */\\n  const wire: { arrive: number; seat: number; hand: Hand }[] = [];\\n  for (let tick = 0; tick < ticks; tick++) {\\n    for (let seat = 0; seat < seats; seat++) {\\n      if (seat === seats - 1 && tick >= leftAt) continue;\\n      const hand = intentAt(tick, seat, host.last[seat]);\\n60→      const lost = roll(tick, seat) < 0.05;\\n      if (lost) {\\n        dropped += 1;\\n        continue;\\n      }\\n      const jitter = Math.floor(roll(tick, seat + 3) * 3);\\n      wire.push({ arrive: tick + delay + jitter, seat, hand });\\n    }\\n    const applied = host.last.map((hand) => ({ ...hand, use: false }));\\n    for (let i = wire.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {\\n70→      const packet = wire[i];\\n      if (packet.arrive > tick) continue;\\n      applied[packet.seat] = packet.hand;\\n      host.last[packet.seat] = packet.hand;\\n      wire.splice(i, 1);\\n    }\\n    for (const peer of peers) {\\n      stepOp(peer.op, applied);\\n      peer.hashes.push(lastHash(peer.op));\\n    }\\n80→  }\\n  return { peers, dropped, leftAt };\\n}\\n\\n/** A locked mass that keeps the bare operation from ending the moment it starts. */\\nfunction addAnchor(op: Op): void {\\n  addTarget(op, { kind: 'mass', x: 6, z: 4, locked: true }, 0);\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file Host lockstep without a socket. Four copies, delayed intents, loss on the way to the host, one leaver.\\n * The host's applied hands are what every copy steps. After the run, the hashes for each applied tick agree.\\n */\\nimport { stepOp, lastHash } from './step';\\nimport type { Hand, Op } from './types';\\nimport { addTarget, createBare, idleHand } from './world';\\n\\n/** A roll in 0..1 from the tick and the seat, with no Math.random. */\\n10→function roll(tick: number, seat: number): number {\\n  const x = Math.sin(tick * 12.9898 + seat * 78.233) * 43758.5453;\\n  return x - Math.floor(x);\\n}\\n\\n/** What one surgeon meant to do on one tick. Pure, so every copy would have sent the same intent. */\\nexport function intentAt(tick: number, seat: number, hand: Hand): Hand {\\n  const angle = tick / 18 + seat;\\n  return {\\n    ...hand,\\n20→    x: Math.sin(angle) * (1.4 + seat * 0.15),\\n    z: Math.cos(angle * 0.8) * 0.9,\\n    tool: Math.floor(tick / 90 + seat) % 8,\\n    use: tick % 37 < 8,\\n    gift: false,\\n    paddle: false,\\n    drop: false,\\n    site: -1,\\n    swap: false,\\n    hint: false,\\n30→  };\\n}\\n\\n/** One peer's view of the operation. */\\ninterface Peer {\\n  op: Op;\\n  /** Last intent that actually reached the host, per seat. */\\n  last: Hand[];\\n  /** Hash after each applied tick. */\\n  hashes: string[];\\n40→}\\n\\n/** Run the lockstep. Returns the peers so a test can read the hashes. */\\nexport function runLockstep(ticks = 3600, seats = 4): { peers: Peer[]; dropped: number; leftAt: number } {\\n  const peers: Peer[] = [];\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) {\\n    const op = createBare({ seats, code: false });\\n    addAnchor(op);\\n    peers.push({ op, last: op.seats.map((seat) => idleHand(seat)), hashes: [] });\\n  }\\n50→  const host = peers[0];\\n  let dropped = 0;\\n  const leftAt = Math.floor(ticks / 2);\\n  const delay = 4;\\n  /** Intents in flight: tick they were sent, seat, hand, and whether the wire kept them. */\\n  const wire: { arrive: number; seat: number; hand: Hand }[] = [];\\n  for (let tick = 0; tick < ticks; tick++) {\\n    for (let seat = 0; seat < seats; seat++) {\\n      if (seat === seats - 1 && tick >= leftAt) continue;\\n      const hand = intentAt(tick, seat, host.last[seat]);\\n60→      const lost = roll(tick, seat) < 0.05;\\n      if (lost) {\\n        dropped += 1;\\n        continue;\\n      }\\n      const jitter = Math.floor(roll(tick, seat + 3) * 3);\\n      wire.push({ arrive: tick + delay + jitter, seat, hand });\\n    }\\n    const applied = host.last.map((hand) => ({ ...hand, use: false }));\\n    for (let i = wire.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {\\n70→      const packet = wire[i];\\n      if (packet.arrive > tick) continue;\\n      applied[packet.seat] = packet.hand;\\n      host.last[packet.seat] = packet.hand;\\n      wire.splice(i, 1);\\n    }\\n    for (const peer of peers) {\\n      stepOp(peer.op, applied);\\n      peer.hashes.push(lastHash(peer.op));\\n    }\\n80→  }\\n  return { peers, dropped, leftAt };\\n}\\n\\n/** A locked mass that keeps the bare operation from ending the moment it starts. */\\nfunction addAnchor(op: Op): void {\\n  addTarget(op, { kind: 'mass', x: 6, z: 4, locked: true }, 0);\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/sequencer.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":120,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file Host lockstep without a socket. Four copies, delayed intents, loss on the way to the host, one leaver.\\n * The host's applied hands are what every copy steps. After the run, the hashes for each applied tick agree.\\n */\\nimport { stepOp, lastHash } from './step';\\nimport type { Hand, Op } from './types';\\nimport { addTarget, createBare, idleHand } from './world';\\n\\n/** A roll in 0..1 from the tick and the seat, with no Math.random. */\\nfunction roll(tick: number, seat: number): number {\\n  const x = Math.sin(tick * 12.9898 + seat * 78.233) * 43758.5453;\\n  return x - Math.floor(x);\\n}\\n\\n/** What one surgeon meant to do on one tick. Pure, so every copy would have sent the same intent. */\\nexport function intentAt(tick: number, seat: number, hand: Hand): Hand {\\n  const angle = tick / 18 + seat;\\n  return {\\n    ...hand,\\n    x: Math.sin(angle) * (1.4 + seat * 0.15),\\n    z: Math.cos(angle * 0.8) * 0.9,\\n    tool: Math.floor(tick / 90 + seat) % 8,\\n    use: tick % 37 < 8,\\n    gift: false,\\n    paddle: false,\\n    drop: false,\\n    site: -1,\\n    swap: false,\\n    hint: false,\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n/** One peer's view of the operation. */\\ninterface Peer {\\n  op: Op;\\n  /** Last intent that actually reached the host, per seat. */\\n  last: Hand[];\\n  /** Hash after each applied tick. */\\n  hashes: string[];\\n}\\n\\n/** Run the lockstep. Returns the peers so a test can read the hashes. */\\nexport function runLockstep(ticks = 3600, seats = 4): { peers: Peer[]; dropped: number; leftAt: number } {\\n  const peers: Peer[] = [];\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) {\\n    const op = createBare({ seats, code: false });\\n    addAnchor(op);\\n    peers.push({ op, last: op.seats.map((seat) => idleHand(seat)), hashes: [] });\\n  }\\n  const host = peers[0];\\n  let dropped = 0;\\n  const leftAt = Math.floor(ticks / 2);\\n  const delay = 4;\\n  /** Intents in flight: tick they were sent, seat, hand, and whether the wire kept them. */\\n  const wire: { arrive: number; seat: number; hand: Hand }[] = [];\\n  for (let tick = 0; tick < ticks; tick++) {\\n    for (let seat = 0; seat < seats; seat++) {\\n      if (seat === seats - 1 && tick >= leftAt) continue;\\n      const hand = intentAt(tick, seat, host.last[seat]);\\n      const lost = roll(tick, seat) < 0.05;\\n      if (lost) {\\n        dropped += 1;\\n        continue;\\n      }\\n      const jitter = Math.floor(roll(tick, seat + 3) * 3);\\n      wire.push({ arrive: tick + delay + jitter, seat, hand });\\n    }\\n    const applied = host.last.map((hand) => ({ ...hand, use: false }));\\n    for (let i = wire.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {\\n      const packet = wire[i];\\n      if (packet.arrive > tick) continue;\\n      applied[packet.seat] = packet.hand;\\n      host.last[packet.seat] = packet.hand;\\n      wire.splice(i, 1);\\n    }\\n    for (const peer of peers) {\\n      stepOp(peer.op, applied);\\n      peer.hashes.push(lastHash(peer.op));\\n    }\\n  }\\n  return { peers, dropped, leftAt };\\n}\\n\\n/** A locked mass that keeps the bare operation from ending the moment it starts. */\\nfunction addAnchor(op: Op): void {\\n  addTarget(op, { kind: 'mass', x: 6, z: 4, locked: true }, 0);\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":87}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-cd8db67b-4af9-45a6-a45c-8a6b29ca02b9-78","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The audio runtime (PLAN.md WP 9.3, §6.4, I-23; doctrines: Assets, Common ground): a page's sound. It plays\\n * the effects and songs the DSP renders (engine/audio/data) through Web Audio: mixed on buses with ducking and voice\\n * limits (mixer.ts, voices.ts), placed in 3D and muffled behind walls (spatial.ts), in a room's reverb (reverb.ts),\\n * with music in layers that change on the beat (music.ts). `createAudio()` makes it; the frame loop calls\\n * `update(cameraPose, queries)` once per rendered frame, after the render.\\n *\\n * The context: a page's runtime starts `locked`, with no `AudioContext`, and makes one inside the first user gesture\\n * (gesture.ts: a key, a click, the end of a touch), so the browser lets it run and prints no warning; a later gesture\\n10→ * resumes it when the browser suspended it. Its `state` is then the context's (`running`, `suspended`, `closed`).\\n * Without Web Audio it is `off` and says so once (`AUDIO_OFF`); the game plays on in silence. A test passes its own\\n * context (`OfflineAudioContext`), which needs no gesture.\\n *\\n * Playing: `play(id, { vol, pitch, variant, bus, position, when, loop, duck })` plays an `sfx` entry on its bus (the\\n * entry's `bus` by default), its variants in turn unless one is named, placed at `position` when given; it returns\\n * the `Sound` (move it, stop it), or null when the voice limits drop it or there is no running context yet (sounds\\n * asked for while locked are dropped, music is remembered). `duck` ducks the music and ambience for the sound's\\n * length. `footstep(surface, position)` plays the effect `footsteps` maps the level's surface tag to (WP 4.2's\\n * `surfaceAt`), `'*'` for any other, `sfx:step` without one. `event(type, payload)` plays a sim event: a sound event\\n20→ * (`{ sfx, vol?, variant?, position? }`, as `x audio --replay` reads them) plays its effect, and a type bound with\\n * `bind(type, id)` plays its stinger on the beat.\\n *\\n * Invariants: presentation only: nothing here changes the sim, and the QueryView only answers occlusion rays. An\\n * unknown id throws `CORE_NO_ENTRY` naming the closest, when it is asked for, locked or not. Renders are cached per\\n * effect and variant at the context's rate (played looped, an effect with a `loop` pass is its render folded onto it:\\n * buffers.ts `foldLoop`, so it has no seam); a voice disconnects its nodes when it ends.\\n *\\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:3708-3786` (`ChipAudio`: the lazy context, resume on a gesture, the\\n * buses and their levels, `sfx` with its per-sound rule, `music`), on pre-rendered buffers.\\n30→ *\\n * @example\\n * // browser: Web Audio plays only in a page (tests/e2e/examples.spec.ts runs it; tests/e2e/audio.spec.ts the rest)\\n * const audio = createAudio({ footsteps: { iron: 'sfx:stomp', '*': 'sfx:step' } });\\n * audio.music('song:dungeon', { intensity: 0 }); // starts on the first gesture\\n * audio.bind('bossSeen', 'sfx:secret');\\n * // each frame, after the render: audio.update(camera.pose, queryViewOf(world));\\n * audio.event('hit', { sfx: 'sfx:hit', position: [2, 1, 5] });\\n * @see tests/e2e/audio.spec.ts\\n */\\n40→import { defineCodes, log as sharedLog, type Log } from '../../core/log';\\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Registry } from '../../core/registry';\\nimport type { QueryView } from '../../sim/queryView';\\nimport { getSfx, renderSfx, sfxKind, type Sfx } from '../data/sfx';\\nimport { getSong, songKind } from '../data/song';\\nimport { onGesture, type GestureTarget } from './gesture';\\nimport { BUS_VOLUMES, createMixer, type AudioBus, type Mixer, type MixerInfo } from './mixer';\\nimport { createMusic, type Music, type MusicChange, type MusicPosition } from './music';\\nimport { roomSpec, type RoomName, type RoomSpec } from './reverb';\\nimport { foldLoop, toBuffer } from './buffers';\\n50→import { checkPlay, createVoice, type PlayOptions, type Sound, type RuntimeSound } from './sound';\\nimport { placeListener, wallsBetween, type ListenerPose, type Vec3 } from './spatial';\\nimport { createVoicePool, type VoiceLimits } from './voices';\\n\\n/** The runtime's codes, with their fixes. */\\nexport const AUDIO_CODES = defineCodes('audio', {\\n  AUDIO_OFF: {\\n    template: 'sound is off: {reason}',\\n    fix: 'open the page in a browser with Web Audio (every current one has it); the game runs on in silence',\\n    doc: 'Advice from `createAudio` (engine/audio/runtime/audio.ts) when there is no Web Audio, or the context could not be made.',\\n60→  },\\n});\\n\\n/** The runtime's state: `locked` until a gesture, then the context's; `off` without Web Audio. */\\nexport type AudioState = 'locked' | 'off' | AudioContextState;\\n\\n/** How `createAudio` is set up; in a page every field has its default. */\\nexport interface AudioOptions {\\n  /** The context to play into (an `OfflineAudioContext` in a test); one is made on the first gesture by default. */\\n  context?: BaseAudioContext;\\n70→  /** Where gestures arrive (`window`). */\\n  window?: GestureTarget;\\n  /** Where the effects and songs come from (the shared registry). */\\n  registry?: Registry;\\n  /** The voice limits over the defaults (voices.ts). */\\n  limits?: Partial<VoiceLimits>;\\n  /** Surface tag → `sfx` id for footsteps; `'*'` for any other tag. */\\n  footsteps?: Readonly<Record<string, string>>;\\n  /** The seed the effects render from (0). */\\n  seed?: number;\\n80→  /** Where advice goes (the shared log). */\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The audio runtime (PLAN.md WP 9.3, §6.4, I-23; doctrines: Assets, Common ground): a page's sound. It plays\\n * the effects and songs the DSP renders (engine/audio/data) through Web Audio: mixed on buses with ducking and voice\\n * limits (mixer.ts, voices.ts), placed in 3D and muffled behind walls (spatial.ts), in a room's reverb (reverb.ts),\\n * with music in layers that change on the beat (music.ts). `createAudio()` makes it; the frame loop calls\\n * `update(cameraPose, queries)` once per rendered frame, after the render.\\n *\\n * The context: a page's runtime starts `locked`, with no `AudioContext`, and makes one inside the first user gesture\\n * (gesture.ts: a key, a click, the end of a touch), so the browser lets it run and prints no warning; a later gesture\\n10→ * resumes it when the browser suspended it. Its `state` is then the context's (`running`, `suspended`, `closed`).\\n * Without Web Audio it is `off` and says so once (`AUDIO_OFF`); the game plays on in silence. A test passes its own\\n * context (`OfflineAudioContext`), which needs no gesture.\\n *\\n * Playing: `play(id, { vol, pitch, variant, bus, position, when, loop, duck })` plays an `sfx` entry on its bus (the\\n * entry's `bus` by default), its variants in turn unless one is named, placed at `position` when given; it returns\\n * the `Sound` (move it, stop it), or null when the voice limits drop it or there is no running context yet (sounds\\n * asked for while locked are dropped, music is remembered). `duck` ducks the music and ambience for the sound's\\n * length. `footstep(surface, position)` plays the effect `footsteps` maps the level's surface tag to (WP 4.2's\\n * `surfaceAt`), `'*'` for any other, `sfx:step` without one. `event(type, payload)` plays a sim event: a sound event\\n20→ * (`{ sfx, vol?, variant?, position? }`, as `x audio --replay` reads them) plays its effect, and a type bound with\\n * `bind(type, id)` plays its stinger on the beat.\\n *\\n * Invariants: presentation only: nothing here changes the sim, and the QueryView only answers occlusion rays. An\\n * unknown id throws `CORE_NO_ENTRY` naming the closest, when it is asked for, locked or not. Renders are cached per\\n * effect and variant at the context's rate (played looped, an effect with a `loop` pass is its render folded onto it:\\n * buffers.ts `foldLoop`, so it has no seam); a voice disconnects its nodes when it ends.\\n *\\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:3708-3786` (`ChipAudio`: the lazy context, resume on a gesture, the\\n * buses and their levels, `sfx` with its per-sound rule, `music`), on pre-rendered buffers.\\n30→ *\\n * @example\\n * // browser: Web Audio plays only in a page (tests/e2e/examples.spec.ts runs it; tests/e2e/audio.spec.ts the rest)\\n * const audio = createAudio({ footsteps: { iron: 'sfx:stomp', '*': 'sfx:step' } });\\n * audio.music('song:dungeon', { intensity: 0 }); // starts on the first gesture\\n * audio.bind('bossSeen', 'sfx:secret');\\n * // each frame, after the render: audio.update(camera.pose, queryViewOf(world));\\n * audio.event('hit', { sfx: 'sfx:hit', position: [2, 1, 5] });\\n * @see tests/e2e/audio.spec.ts\\n */\\n40→import { defineCodes, log as sharedLog, type Log } from '../../core/log';\\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Registry } from '../../core/registry';\\nimport type { QueryView } from '../../sim/queryView';\\nimport { getSfx, renderSfx, sfxKind, type Sfx } from '../data/sfx';\\nimport { getSong, songKind } from '../data/song';\\nimport { onGesture, type GestureTarget } from './gesture';\\nimport { BUS_VOLUMES, createMixer, type AudioBus, type Mixer, type MixerInfo } from './mixer';\\nimport { createMusic, type Music, type MusicChange, type MusicPosition } from './music';\\nimport { roomSpec, type RoomName, type RoomSpec } from './reverb';\\nimport { foldLoop, toBuffer } from './buffers';\\n50→import { checkPlay, createVoice, type PlayOptions, type Sound, type RuntimeSound } from './sound';\\nimport { placeListener, wallsBetween, type ListenerPose, type Vec3 } from './spatial';\\nimport { createVoicePool, type VoiceLimits } from './voices';\\n\\n/** The runtime's codes, with their fixes. */\\nexport const AUDIO_CODES = defineCodes('audio', {\\n  AUDIO_OFF: {\\n    template: 'sound is off: {reason}',\\n    fix: 'open the page in a browser with Web Audio (every current one has it); the game runs on in silence',\\n    doc: 'Advice from `createAudio` (engine/audio/runtime/audio.ts) when there is no Web Audio, or the context could not be made.',\\n60→  },\\n});\\n\\n/** The runtime's state: `locked` until a gesture, then the context's; `off` without Web Audio. */\\nexport type AudioState = 'locked' | 'off' | AudioContextState;\\n\\n/** How `createAudio` is set up; in a page every field has its default. */\\nexport interface AudioOptions {\\n  /** The context to play into (an `OfflineAudioContext` in a test); one is made on the first gesture by default. */\\n  context?: BaseAudioContext;\\n70→  /** Where gestures arrive (`window`). */\\n  window?: GestureTarget;\\n  /** Where the effects and songs come from (the shared registry). */\\n  registry?: Registry;\\n  /** The voice limits over the defaults (voices.ts). */\\n  limits?: Partial<VoiceLimits>;\\n  /** Surface tag → `sfx` id for footsteps; `'*'` for any other tag. */\\n  footsteps?: Readonly<Record<string, string>>;\\n  /** The seed the effects render from (0). */\\n  seed?: number;\\n80→  /** Where advice goes (the shared log). */\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/audio/runtime/audio.ts\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file The audio runtime (PLAN.md WP 9.3, §6.4, I-23; doctrines: Assets, Common ground): a page's sound. It plays\\n * the effects and songs the DSP renders (engine/audio/data) through Web Audio: mixed on buses with ducking and voice\\n * limits (mixer.ts, voices.ts), placed in 3D and muffled behind walls (spatial.ts), in a room's reverb (reverb.ts),\\n * with music in layers that change on the beat (music.ts). `createAudio()` makes it; the frame loop calls\\n * `update(cameraPose, queries)` once per rendered frame, after the render.\\n *\\n * The context: a page's runtime starts `locked`, with no `AudioContext`, and makes one inside the first user gesture\\n * (gesture.ts: a key, a click, the end of a touch), so the browser lets it run and prints no warning; a later gesture\\n * resumes it when the browser suspended it. Its `state` is then the context's (`running`, `suspended`, `closed`).\\n * Without Web Audio it is `off` and says so once (`AUDIO_OFF`); the game plays on in silence. A test passes its own\\n * context (`OfflineAudioContext`), which needs no gesture.\\n *\\n * Playing: `play(id, { vol, pitch, variant, bus, position, when, loop, duck })` plays an `sfx` entry on its bus (the\\n * entry's `bus` by default), its variants in turn unless one is named, placed at `position` when given; it returns\\n * the `Sound` (move it, stop it), or null when the voice limits drop it or there is no running context yet (sounds\\n * asked for while locked are dropped, music is remembered). `duck` ducks the music and ambience for the sound's\\n * length. `footstep(surface, position)` plays the effect `footsteps` maps the level's surface tag to (WP 4.2's\\n * `surfaceAt`), `'*'` for any other, `sfx:step` without one. `event(type, payload)` plays a sim event: a sound event\\n * (`{ sfx, vol?, variant?, position? }`, as `x audio --replay` reads them) plays its effect, and a type bound with\\n * `bind(type, id)` plays its stinger on the beat.\\n *\\n * Invariants: presentation only: nothing here changes the sim, and the QueryView only answers occlusion rays. An\\n * unknown id throws `CORE_NO_ENTRY` naming the closest, when it is asked for, locked or not. Renders are cached per\\n * effect and variant at the context's rate (played looped, an effect with a `loop` pass is its render folded onto it:\\n * buffers.ts `foldLoop`, so it has no seam); a voice disconnects its nodes when it ends.\\n *\\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:3708-3786` (`ChipAudio`: the lazy context, resume on a gesture, the\\n * buses and their levels, `sfx` with its per-sound rule, `music`), on pre-rendered buffers.\\n *\\n * @example\\n * // browser: Web Audio plays only in a page (tests/e2e/examples.spec.ts runs it; tests/e2e/audio.spec.ts the rest)\\n * const audio = createAudio({ footsteps: { iron: 'sfx:stomp', '*': 'sfx:step' } });\\n * audio.music('song:dungeon', { intensity: 0 }); // starts on the first gesture\\n * audio.bind('bossSeen', 'sfx:secret');\\n * // each frame, after the render: audio.update(camera.pose, queryViewOf(world));\\n * audio.event('hit', { sfx: 'sfx:hit', position: [2, 1, 5] });\\n * @see tests/e2e/audio.spec.ts\\n */\\nimport { defineCodes, log as sharedLog, type Log } from '../../core/log';\\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Registry } from '../../core/registry';\\nimport type { QueryView } from '../../sim/queryView';\\nimport { getSfx, renderSfx, sfxKind, type Sfx } from '../data/sfx';\\nimport { getSong, songKind } from '../data/song';\\nimport { onGesture, type GestureTarget } from './gesture';\\nimport { BUS_VOLUMES, createMixer, type AudioBus, type Mixer, type MixerInfo } from './mixer';\\nimport { createMusic, type Music, type MusicChange, type MusicPosition } from './music';\\nimport { roomSpec, type RoomName, type RoomSpec } from './reverb';\\nimport { foldLoop, toBuffer } from './buffers';\\nimport { checkPlay, createVoice, type PlayOptions, type Sound, type RuntimeSound } from './sound';\\nimport { placeListener, wallsBetween, type ListenerPose, type Vec3 } from './spatial';\\nimport { createVoicePool, type VoiceLimits } from './voices';\\n\\n/** The runtime's codes, with their fixes. */\\nexport const AUDIO_CODES = defineCodes('audio', {\\n  AUDIO_OFF: {\\n    template: 'sound is off: {reason}',\\n    fix: 'open the page in a browser with Web Audio (every current one has it); the game runs on in silence',\\n    doc: 'Advice from `createAudio` (engine/audio/runtime/audio.ts) when there is no Web Audio, or the context could not be made.',\\n  },\\n});\\n\\n/** The runtime's state: `locked` until a gesture, then the context's; `off` without Web Audio. */\\nexport type AudioState = 'locked' | 'off' | AudioContextState;\\n\\n/** How `createAudio` is set up; in a page every field has its default. */\\nexport interface AudioOptions {\\n  /** The context to play into (an `OfflineAudioContext` in a test); one is made on the first gesture by default. */\\n  context?: BaseAudioContext;\\n  /** Where gestures arrive (`window`). */\\n  window?: GestureTarget;\\n  /** Where the effects and songs come from (the shared registry). */\\n  registry?: Registry;\\n  /** The voice limits over the defaults (voices.ts). */\\n  limits?: Partial<VoiceLimits>;\\n  /** Surface tag → `sfx` id for footsteps; `'*'` for any other tag. */\\n  footsteps?: Readonly<Record<string, string>>;\\n  /** The seed the effects render from (0). */\\n  seed?: number;\\n  /** Where advice goes (the shared log). */\\n\",\"total_lines\":321}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-cd8db67b-4af9-45a6-a45c-8a6b29ca02b9-79","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,55,51,49,95,95,120,53,57,99,49,100,51,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,78,111,32,109,97,116,99,104,101,115,32,102,111,117,110,100,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\