ne_number\":117,\"content\":\" * and so do `__engine.set`, URL parameters and with them `node x shot <page> --set post.look=…`, on a page whose\"},{\"line_number\":119,\"content\":\" * post.look=look:game-boy`), and tests/pages/post.html.\"},{\"line_number\":123,\"content\":\"  if (!has('post.look')) defineSettings(POST_SETTINGS, registry);\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"18927cfb-fb22-4363-a0af-47c689fe9de8"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_195","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"post.look is a view setting. inspector.set might still set view settings.\n\ngame.cursorSpeed is a simulation setting with fallback 8, not a view setting. The page can keep its own feel settings from FEEL defaults and update them when the slider moves.\n\nThe page cannot read view settings directly. createEngine exposes no settings getter, and w.settings.get throws a CORE_VIEW_SETTING error from the simulation side.\n\nA `sliders` record on the campaign will store feel and tune defaults. The page reads these values only for display. Cursor speed is set to 8 by default; the simulation uses `balance.cursor`, but the page handles player movement via absolute hand coordinates. The page sets `hand.radial` to true while the radial menu is open.\n\nSim fieldDelta is confirmed at 60. The prop:sheet reference will be updated to geometry:sheet. GeometrySpec create ignores its params argument. BufferGeometry types will be loosely defined to avoid importing Three.js.\n\nThe `LiveGeom` interface now includes `setAttribute`, `setIndex`, `computeVertexNormals`, and attribute constructors. Color attributes use itemSize 3. Material examples will use `vertexColors: true` with standard fields like roughness and color.\n\ndefineMaterial will be tested for unknown field errors. Song tracks will stay short and whole-bar lengths at 120 BPM with four steps per beat. The example pattern `{ beats: 2, tracks: [{ notes: 'C4 - E4 - G4 - E4 -', wave: 'pluck' }] }` will be used. Six songs are planned: title, or, strain, mercy, story, jingle, win, and lose.\n\nTwelve sound effects are planned: cut, stitch, drain, laser, syringe, gel, scan, forceps, beep, alarm, rank, and menu.\n\nVoice lines will be spoken by playing oscillator syllables mapped from voiceOf indexes. The speak function checks that the audio context is running before generating sound.\n\nThe hub page will declare global `AIHub` and `__compass` interfaces for the harness. Session.js, harness, bridge, and round.js will be fetched during packaging.\n\nBoot order follows the plan exactly. The host tick uses AIHub.time(). The game runs with null info when standalone. Card HTML renders before the engine is ready. Hash mismatches appear in window.__compass.mismatches. Server copies hide the canvas and skip input while still stepping. Colleague mode activates when only one player exists. The gala-shift case seeds both the game seed setting and the engine seed.\n\nThe engine's own frame loop steps the simulation, which would double-step if the host also calls step. The plan pauses the engine and defers stepping to the hub.\n\nThe host tick interval will call `e.step(1)` directly. Because `pause()` stops the engine clock but still allows `step(n)` to run, this cleanly separates simulation advancement from the host loop. Clients will also pause and only step buffered ticks.\n\nThe local cursor will be drawn from the device's immediate aim, while the sheet hand follows the simulation seat. Client messages will be sent unreliably with fields for input state, tool, use, drop, gift, paddle, site, swap, hint, radial, and seq.\n\nThe host will send packed hand states as `{t:'t', ticks: number[][]}` and occasional hashes as `{t:'h', tick, hash}`. Boolean edge flags for gift, drop, swap, hint, paddle, and site would lose presses if packets are lost. The plan instead uses monotonic press counters so the host can convert deltas to edges.\n\nThe local device will pulse each input edge for exactly one frame when its monotonic counter increases. The host will detect that increase and pulse the matching simulation edge for that tick. This logic will live in net/hub.ts. I also need to check whether the hub info exposes `players` or `seats` before writing the seat count code.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-827858d4-b612-4696-8c2b-5736b37e0e68-107","name":"grep","i