{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a4ce3673-d011-4bea-a009-3561f92514f2-109","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,55,51,49,95,95,120,53,57,99,49,100,51,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,50,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,55,51,49,95,95,120,53,57,99,49,100,51,47,119,111,114,107,47,84,114,97,117,109,97,45,67,111,109,112,97,115,115,45,84,114,97,117,109,97,45,67,101,110,116,101,114,45,83,101,99,111,110,100,45,79,112,105,110,105,111,110,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,55,51,49,47,101,110,103,105,110,101,47,103,102,120,47,112,111,115,116,47,112,114,101,115,101,116,115,46,116,115,10,49,55,50,58,32,32,32,32,102,105,108,116,101,114,115,58,32,123,32,97,111,58,32,123,32,115,99,111,112,101,58,32,39,97,108,108,39,32,125,32,125,44,10,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,55,51,49,95,95,120,53,57,99,49,100,51,47,119,111,114,107,47,84,114,97,117,109,97,45,67,111,109,112,97,115,115,45,84,114,97,117,109,97,45,67,101,110,116,101,114,45,83,101,99,111,110,100,45,79,112,105,110,105,111,110,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,55,51,49,47,101,110,103,105,110,101,47,103,102,120,47,112,111,115,116,47,102,105,108,116,101,114,115,46,116,115,10,49,54,53,58,32,32,32,32,97,111,58,32,123,32,46,46,46,97,111,44,32,115,116,114,101,110,103,116,104,58,32,97,111,46,115,116,114,101,110,103,116,104,32,42,32,97,111,46,97,109,111,117,110,116,32,125,44,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":2,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/gfx/post/presets.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":172,\"content\":\"    filters: { ao: { scope: 'all' } },\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/gfx/post/filters.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":165,\"content\":\"    ao: { ...ao, strength: ao.strength * ao.amount },\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a4ce3673-d011-4bea-a009-3561f92514f2-110","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The material registry (PLAN.md WP 2.3, §6.6, §6.7, I-49): the registry kind `material`, one entry per\\n * material, as data with the parameters agents know from three.js's classic materials: `color`, `map`, `roughness`,\\n * `metalness`, `emissive`, `emissiveIntensity`, `normalScale`, `opacity`, `transparent`, `alphaTest`, `side`,\\n * `flatShading`, `vertexColors`, `fog`, `depthWrite`, plus `unlit` (glTF's word: drawn without lights). How a\\n * material is drawn is the engine's business (engine/gfx/materials/compile.ts): v1 compiles the same data to\\n * `MeshLambertMaterial` or `MeshBasicMaterial`, later WPs to better node materials and styles (WP 7.2), without the\\n * data changing (doctrine: Common ground outside, Quality under the hood inside).\\n *\\n10→ * `map` names a texture generator (engine/gfx/textures/texture.ts): an id (`'texture:brick'`) or\\n * `{ texture, seed, params, size, look, repeat }`. One generator fills every slot: its colour is the `map`, its\\n * height the normal map (scaled by `normalScale`), its roughness the roughness map (used by styles that shade with\\n * roughness) and its emissive the emissive map.\\n *\\n * `defineMaterial(id, spec)` adds one (a game's own materials live with the game); `materialKind(registry)` declares\\n * the kind with the engine's built-in materials (engine/gfx/materials/builtins.ts), and `material:default` stands in,\\n * with a warning, for a missing id.\\n *\\n * Invariants: colours are hex strings; a map's texture exists when the material is defined (define textures\\n20→ * first), and its parameters, size, look and repeat are checked then, so a bad map fails at `defineMaterial`, never\\n * at the first frame. Problems raise `CORE_BAD_SPEC` naming each, as every registry kind does.\\n *\\n * @example\\n * import { createRegistry } from '../../core/registry';\\n * const reg = createRegistry();\\n * defineMaterial('material:mossyBrick', { color: '#c8d8b0', map: { texture: 'texture:brick', seed: 4 } }, reg);\\n * reg.get('material', 'material:mossyBrick').roughness; // 1, the default\\n * textureRefOf(reg.get('material', 'material:mossyBrick').map); // { texture: 'texture:brick', seed: 4, … }\\n * @see engine/gfx/materials/material.test.ts\\n30→ */\\nimport { hex } from '../../core/color';\\nimport { galleryField } from '../../core/gallery';\\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Entry, type Registry } from '../../core/registry';\\nimport { isPlainObject, type Schema, type SpecOf } from '../../core/schema';\\nimport { textureSampler, type TextureRef } from '../textures/bake';\\nimport { textureKind } from '../textures/texture';\\nimport type { TextureLook } from '../textures/types';\\nimport { BUILT_IN_MATERIALS } from './builtins';\\n\\n40→/** The fields of a `material` entry: three.js's classic material parameters, as data. */\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The material registry (PLAN.md WP 2.3, §6.6, §6.7, I-49): the registry kind `material`, one entry per\\n * material, as data with the parameters agents know from three.js's classic materials: `color`, `map`, `roughness`,\\n * `metalness`, `emissive`, `emissiveIntensity`, `normalScale`, `opacity`, `transparent`, `alphaTest`, `side`,\\n * `flatShading`, `vertexColors`, `fog`, `depthWrite`, plus `unlit` (glTF's word: drawn without lights). How a\\n * material is drawn is the engine's business (engine/gfx/materials/compile.ts): v1 compiles the same data to\\n * `MeshLambertMaterial` or `MeshBasicMaterial`, later WPs to better node materials and styles (WP 7.2), without the\\n * data changing (doctrine: Common ground outside, Quality under the hood inside).\\n *\\n10→ * `map` names a texture generator (engine/gfx/textures/texture.ts): an id (`'texture:brick'`) or\\n * `{ texture, seed, params, size, look, repeat }`. One generator fills every slot: its colour is the `map`, its\\n * height the normal map (scaled by `normalScale`), its roughness the roughness map (used by styles that shade with\\n * roughness) and its emissive the emissive map.\\n *\\n * `defineMaterial(id, spec)` adds one (a game's own materials live with the game); `materialKind(registry)` declares\\n * the kind with the engine's built-in materials (engine/gfx/materials/builtins.ts), and `material:default` stands in,\\n * with a warning, for a missing id.\\n *\\n * Invariants: colours are hex strings; a map's texture exists when the material is defined (define textures\\n20→ * first), and its parameters, size, look and repeat are checked then, so a bad map fails at `defineMaterial`, never\\n * at the first frame. Problems raise `CORE_BAD_SPEC` naming each, as every registry kind does.\\n *\\n * @example\\n * import { createRegistry } from '../../core/registry';\\n * const reg = createRegistry();\\n * defineMaterial('material:mossyBrick', { color: '#c8d8b0', map: { texture: 'texture:brick', seed: 4 } }, reg);\\n * reg.get('material', 'material:mossyBrick').roughness; // 1, the default\\n * textureRefOf(reg.get('material', 'material:mossyBrick').map); // { texture: 'texture:brick', seed: 4, … }\\n * @see engine/gfx/materials/material.test.ts\\n30→ */\\nimport { hex } from '../../core/color';\\nimport { galleryField } from '../../core/gallery';\\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Entry, type Registry } from '../../core/registry';\\nimport { isPlainObject, type Schema, type SpecOf } from '../../core/schema';\\nimport { textureSampler, type TextureRef } from '../textures/bake';\\nimport { textureKind } from '../textures/texture';\\nimport type { TextureLook } from '../textures/types';\\nimport { BUILT_IN_MATERIALS } from './builtins';\\n\\n40→/** The fields of a `material` entry: three.js's classic material parameters, as data. */\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/gfx/materials/material.ts\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file The material registry (PLAN.md WP 2.3, §6.6, §6.7, I-49): the registry kind `material`, one entry per\\n * material, as data with the parameters agents know from three.js's classic materials: `color`, `map`, `roughness`,\\n * `metalness`, `emissive`, `emissiveIntensity`, `normalScale`, `opacity`, `transparent`, `alphaTest`, `side`,\\n * `flatShading`, `vertexColors`, `fog`, `depthWrite`, plus `unlit` (glTF's word: drawn without lights). How a\\n * material is drawn is the engine's business (engine/gfx/materials/compile.ts): v1 compiles the same data to\\n * `MeshLambertMaterial` or `MeshBasicMaterial`, later WPs to better node materials and styles (WP 7.2), without the\\n * data changing (doctrine: Common ground outside, Quality under the hood inside).\\n *\\n * `map` names a texture generator (engine/gfx/textures/texture.ts): an id (`'texture:brick'`) or\\n * `{ texture, seed, params, size, look, repeat }`. One generator fills every slot: its colour is the `map`, its\\n * height the normal map (scaled by `normalScale`), its roughness the roughness map (used by styles that shade with\\n * roughness) and its emissive the emissive map.\\n *\\n * `defineMaterial(id, spec)` adds one (a game's own materials live with the game); `materialKind(registry)` declares\\n * the kind with the engine's built-in materials (engine/gfx/materials/builtins.ts), and `material:default` stands in,\\n * with a warning, for a missing id.\\n *\\n * Invariants: colours are hex strings; a map's texture exists when the material is defined (define textures\\n * first), and its parameters, size, look and repeat are checked then, so a bad map fails at `defineMaterial`, never\\n * at the first frame. Problems raise `CORE_BAD_SPEC` naming each, as every registry kind does.\\n *\\n * @example\\n * import { createRegistry } from '../../core/registry';\\n * const reg = createRegistry();\\n * defineMaterial('material:mossyBrick', { color: '#c8d8b0', map: { texture: 'texture:brick', seed: 4 } }, reg);\\n * reg.get('material', 'material:mossyBrick').roughness; // 1, the default\\n * textureRefOf(reg.get('material', 'material:mossyBrick').map); // { texture: 'texture:brick', seed: 4, … }\\n * @see engine/gfx/materials/material.test.ts\\n */\\nimport { hex } from '../../core/color';\\nimport { galleryField } from '../../core/gallery';\\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Entry, type Registry } from '../../core/registry';\\nimport { isPlainObject, type Schema, type SpecOf } from '../../core/schema';\\nimport { textureSampler, type TextureRef } from '../textures/bake';\\nimport { textureKind } from '../textures/texture';\\nimport type { TextureLook } from '../textures/types';\\nimport { BUILT_IN_MATERIALS } from './builtins';\\n\\n/** The fields of a `material` entry: three.js's classic material parameters, as data. */\\n\",\"total_lines\":239}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"d00d7eea-ddca-4332-8737-f23bf71ec365"}
