9,111,98,106,101,99,116,39,44,10,54,51,45,32,32,32,32,112,114,111,112,101,114,116,105,101,115,58,32,123,10,54,52,45,32,32,32,32,32,32,108,111,111,107,58,32,123,32,116,121,112,101,58,32,39,115,116,114,105,110,103,39,44,32,114,101,113,117,105,114,101,100,58,32,116,114,117,101,44,32,100,101,115,99,114,105,112,116,105,111,110,58,32,34,84,104,101,32,108,111,111,107,32,108,97,105,100,32,111,110,58,32,97,32,39,108,111,111,107,39,32,105,100,46,34,32,125,44,10,54,53,45,32,32,32,32,32,32,97,109,111,117,110,116,58,32,110,117,109,40,39,72,111,119,32,109,117,99,104,32,111,102,32,105,116,32,115,104,111,119,115,44,32,48,32,116,111,32,49,58,32,105,116,115,32,110,117,109,98,101,114,115,32,109,111,118,101,32,116,104,105,115,32,102,97,114,44,32,105,116,115,32,102,105,108,116,101,114,115,32,102,97,100,101,32,105,110,32,116,104,105,115,32,109,117,99,104,46,39,44,32,49,44,32,48,44,32,49,41,44,10,54,54,45,32,32,32,32,32,32,111,110,108,121,58,32,123,10,54,55,45,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,116,121,112,101,58,32,39,97,114,114,97,121,39,44,10,54,56,45,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,100,101,102,97,117,108,116,58,32,91,93,44,10,54,57,45,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,105,116,101,109,115,58,32,123,32,116,121,112,101,58,32,39,115,116,114,105,110,103,39,44,32,101,110,117,109,58,32,70,73,76,84,69,82,95,78,65,77,69,83,32,125,44,10,55,48,45,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,100,101,115,99,114,105,112,116,105,111,110,58,32,39,79,110,108,121,32,116,104,101,115,101,32,111,102,32,105,116,115,32,102,105,108,116,101,114,115,59,32,97,108,108,32,111,102,32,116,104,101,109,32,119,104,101,110,32,101,109,112,116,121,46,39,44,10,55,49,45,32,32,32,32,32,32,125,44,10,55,50,45,32,32,32,32,32,32,102,105,108,116,101,114,115,58,32,123,10,55,51,45,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,116,121,112,101,58,32,39,111,98,106,101,99,116,39,44,10,55,52,45,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,100,101,102,97,117,108,116,58,32,123,125,44,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":2,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/gfx/post/combine.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":44,\"content\":\"export interface CombineLayer {\"},{\"line_number\":56,\"content\":\"export const COMBINE_FIELD = {\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"7d5e9635-45cb-45d2-a809-22e3e153fb0e"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_209","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"post.combine can be set at runtime if it is a setting.\n\npost.combine is an array-of-objects setting. I'll define overlay looks and set it from the page when needed, catching any failure once. Now I'm writing sheet.ts: a live mesh with 96×60 cells, 16×10 spans, and cursor geometry for a glove and tool stick.\n\nThe cursor mesh will have about 24 vertices. Local positions are set relative to the prop origin at FIELD_AT, so cursor coordinates map directly to local space.\n\nFour hands will share one mesh, with unused seats hidden at y=-10. The sheet will use a cherry base with darker ellipse organs and veins. Target-driven vertex coloring will darken pools, raise lips near wounds, and animate breath and heartbeat. Performance is estimated at roughly 100k operations per frame. A `paintField` function will accept an op state, time, and a blood color option—red, teal, or off—and export the resulting geometry.\n\nA hands state module will handle integration math without DOM dependencies. It exports `integrateStick` for headless testing. The `SeatAim` interface defines seat coordinates, tool state, and radial mode. The page fills these from devices. Standard gamepad button indices are mapped: 0–3 for face buttons, 4–7 for bumpers, and 12–15 for the D-pad.\n\nGamepad axes 0 and 1 control the left stick, while 2 and 3 control the right. Edge detection will be stored per seat and button.\n\nhands.ts will export `sampleHands`, which reads navigator.getGamepads and input.held to produce a Hand array. It returns empty when navigator is absent, such as in tests.\n\nshell.ts will render into a root element with `render(root, campaign, op)` and `bind(root, handlers)`. It re-renders every frame. Dynamic strings will use textContent instead of innerHTML to avoid XSS.\n\nRebuilding innerHTML every frame would destroy focus and click handlers. The shell will instead update text and classes while keeping the DOM structure static. It will export `mount(root, handlers)` and `paint(campaign, view)`. The view object is a plain data payload for vitals, clock, score, line, tools, and story box. A ViewModel type will be defined in shell.ts.\n\nThe shell DOM will be built once in mount() with all screens present but hidden by default. paint() will then toggle visibility and update textContent on stable nodes.\n\nThe shell DOM will also include an `about` container. About cards will remain in the document permanently, with only the active one visible; the usage card is always present so the importer can locate it.\n\nThe credits screen will show a short completion card first, then hand off to the About pager. The first About card will display the ending line. This satisfies both the Credits and About requirements in one flow.\n\nAbout cards will live in a TypeScript module `ui/about.ts` that imports a matching JSON file. The page can then import the JSON directly so the build embeds it. I need to verify that `resolveJsonModule` is enabled in the engine's tsconfig.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a672c834-281d-43f8-a4cf-7d9826296d68-135","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"resolveJsonModule","glob":"**/tsconfig*.json"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1009,"output_tokens":1776,"cache_read_input_tokens":189312,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"a939ee4c-ed5e-4ec8-8e2e-9f555a16c3b1"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a672c834-281d-43f8-a4cf-7d9826296d68-135","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,55,51,49,95,95,120,53,57,99,49,100,51,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,78,111,32,109,97,116,99,104,101,115,32,102,111,117,110,100,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":1,\"match_count\":0,\"file_matches\":[]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"d037e04c-c93d-4f9b-8876-b35a1d712c24"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_210","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"resolveJsonModule is unavailable. I will use an alternative approach.\n\nI'll create `interview.ts` exporting the object and a test comparing it to `exit-interview.json`. Both files must exist.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-55eb6fd7-7d39-4792-b72d-e62c40ed63fa-136","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/view/looks.ts","content":"/**\n * @file The two looks. Harbor is the night hospital. Field is the wet sheet, full resolution, so a stitch reads at ten feet.\n */\nimport { defineLook } from '../../../engine';\n\ndefineLook('look:harbor', {\n  description: 'Harbor Light at night. Soft contact shadows, a warm teal grade, a thin outline on the people, and a little bloom on the lamp.',\n  style: 'pbr',\n  resolution: 'full',\n  textures: 'smooth',\n  filters: {\n    ao: { scope: 'all', strength: 0.6 },\n    aa: { scope: 'all' },\n    outline: { scope: 'characters+objects', width: 1.5, darken: 0.2 },\n    grade: { scope: 'all', temperature: 0.12, tint: 0.18, saturation: 0.95 },\n    bloom: { scope: 'all', strength: 0.4, threshold: 0.82 },\n  },\n});\n\ndefineLook('look:field', {\n  description: 'The operation. Wet highlights, contact, a little screen-space reflection, and full-frame smoothing.',\n  style: 'pbr',\n  resolution: 'full',\n  textures: 'smooth',\n  filters: {\n    ao: { scope: 'all', strength: 0.7 },\n    ssr: { scope: 'all', strength: 0.35 },\n    aa: { scope: 'all' },\n    bloom: { scope: 'all', strength: 0.28, threshold: 0.9 },\n    grade: { scope: 'all', saturation: 1.05, contrast: 1.04 },\n  },\n});\n\ndefineLook('look:still', {\n  description: 'Stillpoint laid over the field: teal, the colour pulled back, a vignette.',\n  filters: {\n    grade: { scope: 'all', saturation: 0.35, tint: 0.45, temperature: -0.2 },\n    vignette: { scope: 'all', strength: 0.65 },\n  },\n});\n\ndefineLook('look:pulse', {\n  description: 'Second Pulse laid over the field: amber and a streak of speed.',\n  filters: {\n    grade: { scope: 'all', temperature: 0.45, saturation: 1.2 },\n    speedlines: { scope: 'all', strength: 0.45 },\n  },\n});\n\ndefineLook('look:low', {\n  description: 'Vitals failing: a red vignette and a colder grade.',\n  filters: {\n    vignette: { scope: 'all', strength: 0.8 },\n    grade: { scope: 'all', temperature: 0.2, saturation: 0.8 },\n  },\n});\n"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-55eb6fd7-7d39-4792-b72d-e62c40ed63fa-137","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/view/field/sheet.ts","content":"/**\n * @file The living sheet and the glove. A kit box lends its geometry class. The page keeps the buffers and rewrites\n * them every frame. Ninety-six by sixty, not the plan's three hundred and twenty by one hundred and ninety-two:\n * four software-rendered copies of the denser grid were killed for memory on this machine.\n */\nimport { boxGeometry, defineGeometry, defineMaterial } from '../../../engine';\nimport type { Op } from '../../op/types';\n\n/** Columns of quads across the sheet. */\nexport const COLS = 96;\n/** Rows of quads down the sheet. */\nexport const ROWS = 60;\n/** Half-width of the sheet, metres. Cursors clamp to this. */\nexport const HALF_X = 8;\n/** Half-depth of the sheet, metres. */\nexport const HALF_Z = 5;\n\n/** Vertices across, including the last edge. */\nconst VX = COLS + 1;\n/** Vertices down. */\nconst VZ = ROWS + 1;\n/** Sheet vertices. The glove is a second geometry. */\nconst SHEET = VX * VZ;\n\n/** A buffer geometry, as much of it as this file uses. three.js stays inside the engine. */\ninterface Mesh {\n  setAttribute(name: string, attribute: unknown): void;\n  setIndex(index: number[]): void;\n  getAttribute(name: string): { array: Float32Array; needsUpdate: boolean };\n  computeVertexNormals(): void;\n}\n\n/** The attribute class taken from a kit box. */\ninterface AttributeCtor {\n  new (array: Float32Array, size: number): unknown;\n}\n\nconst sample = boxGeometry({ width: 1, height: 1, depth: 1 });\nconst Geometry = sample.constructor as new () => Mesh;\nconst Attribute = sample.getAttribute('position').constructor as AttributeCtor;\n\n/** The sheet, once the builder has run. */\nlet sheet: Mesh | null = null;\n/** The glove, once the builder has run. */\nlet glove: Mesh | null = null;\n\n/** Grid index. */\nfunction at(x: number, z: number): number {\n  return z * VX + x;\n}\n\n/** Build the sheet once, at its full extent, so the cull box covers every later height. */\nfunction buildSheet(): Mesh {\n  const position = new Float32Array(SHEET * 3);\n  const color = new Float32Array(SHEET * 3);\n  const uv = new Float32Array(SHEET * 2);\n  for (let z = 0; z < VZ; z++) {\n    for (let x = 0; x < VX; x++) {\n      const i = at(x, z);\n      position[i * 3] = -HALF_X + (x / COLS) * HALF_X * 2;\n      position[i * 3 + 1] = 0.4;\n      position[i * 3 + 2] = -HALF_Z + (z / ROWS) * HALF_Z * 2;\n      uv[i * 2] = x / COLS;\n      uv[i * 2 + 1] = z / ROWS;\n      color[i * 3] = 0.72;\n      color[i * 3 + 1] = 0.28;\n      color[i * 3 + 2] = 0.3;\n    }\n  }\n  const index: number[] = [];\n  for (let z = 0; z < ROWS; z++) {\n    for (let x = 0; x < COLS; x++) {\n      const a = at(x, z);\n      index.push(a, a + VX, a + 1, a + 1, a + VX, a + VX + 1);\n    }\n  }\n  const mesh = new Geometry();\n  mesh.setAttribute('position', new Attribute(position, 3));\n  mesh.setAttribute('normal', new Attribute(new Float32Array(SHEET * 3), 3));\n  mesh.setAttribute('color', new Attribute(color, 3));\n  mesh.setAttribute('uv', new Attribute(uv, 2));\n  mesh.setIndex(index);\n  mesh.computeVertexNormals();\n  sheet = mesh;\n  return mesh;\n}\n\n/** A small glove: a palm, a thumb, and a tool, twelve triangles, four seats packed end to end. */\nfunction buildGlove(): Mesh {\n  const count = 4 * 16;\n  const mesh = new Geometry();\n  mesh.setAttribute('position', new Attribute(new Float32Array(count * 3), 3));\n  mesh.setAttribute('normal', new Attribute(new Float32Array(count * 3), 3));\n  mesh.setAttribute('color', new Attribute(new Float32Array(count * 3), 3));\n  mesh.setAttribute('uv', new Attribute(new Float32Array(count * 2), 2));\n  const index: number[] = [];\n  for (let s = 0; s < 4; s++) {\n    const b = s * 16;\n    index.push(b, b + 1, b + 2, b, b + 2, b + 3);\n    index.push(b + 4, b + 5, b + 6, b + 4, b + 6, b + 7);\n    index.push(b + 8, b + 9, b + 10, b + 8, b + 10, b + 11);\n  }\n  mesh.setIndex(index);\n  glove = mesh;\n  return mesh;\n}\n\ndefineGeometry('geometry:sheet', {\n  description: 'The operation sheet, a grid the page rewrites every frame.',\n  budget: 200000,\n  create: () => buildSheet() as never,\n});\n\ndefineGeometry('geometry:cursor', {\n  description: 'Four gloved hands. The page moves the vertices onto the cursors.',\n  budget: 4000,\n  create: () => buildGlove() as never,\n});\n\ndefineMaterial('material:tissue', {\n  color: '#ffffff',\n  roughness: 0.32,\n  metalness: 0.04,\n  vertexColors: true,\n});\n\ndefineMaterial('material:glove', {\n  color: '#ffffff',\n  roughness: 0.55,\n  vertexColors: true,\n});\n\n/** Blood colour from the display setting. */\nfunction bloodOf(mode: string): [number, number, number] {\n  if (mode === 'teal') return [0.15, 0.45, 0.48];\n  if (mode === 'off') return [0.35, 0.32, 0.3];\n  return [0.45, 0.05, 0.08];\n}\n\n/** Tissue colour at a sheet point, before blood and burns. */\nfunction tissue(x: number, z: number): [number, number, number] {\n  const organ = Math.hypot(x * 0.55, z) < 2.2;\n  const vein = Math.abs(z - Math.sin(x * 1.3) * 0.35) < 0.08;\n  if (vein) return [0.55, 0.16, 0.22];\n  if (organ) return [0.78, 0.36, 0.34];\n  return [0.86, 0.62, 0.52];\n}\n\n/** Write one glove quad in local sheet space. */\nfunction quad(\n  array: Float32Array,\n  base: number,\n  x: number,\n  z: number,\n  w: number,\n  d: number,\n  y: number,\n  rgb: [number, number, number],\n  colors: Float32Array,\n): void {\n  const corners = [\n    [x - w, z - d],\n    [x + w, z - d],\n    [x + w, z + d],\n    [x - w, z + d],\n  ];\n  for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) {\n    const v = base + i;\n    array[v * 3] = corners[i][0];\n    array[v * 3 + 1] = y;\n    array[v * 3 + 2] = corners[i][1];\n    colors[v * 3] = rgb[0];\n    colors[v * 3 + 1] = rgb[1];\n    colors[v * 3 + 2] = rgb[2];\n  }\n}\n\n/** Rewrite the sheet and the gloves from the operation. Missing meshes wait until the builder runs. */\nexport function paintField(op: Op | null, time: number, bloodMode: string): void {\n  if (sheet) paintSheet(sheet, op, time, bloodOf(bloodMode));\n  if (glove) paintGlove(glove, op);\n}\n\n/** Heights and colours of the sheet. */\nfunction paintSheet(mesh: Mesh, op: Op | null, time: number, blood: [number, number, number]): void {\n  const position = mesh.getAttribute('position');\n  const color = mesh.getAttribute('color');\n  const pos = position.array;\n  const col = color.array;\n  const breath = Math.sin(time * 1.4) * 0.012;\n  const beat = Math.pow(Math.max(0, Math.sin(time * 6.2)), 18) * 0.03;\n  const targets = op?.targets.filter((target) => !target.done && target.site === (op.seats[0]?.site ?? 0)) ?? [];\n  for (let i = 0; i < SHEET; i++) {\n    const x = pos[i * 3];\n    const z = pos[i * 3 + 2];\n    let y = breath + beat * Math.exp(-Math.hypot(x, z) * 0.8);\n    let rgb = tissue(x, z);\n    for (const target of targets) {\n      const dx = x - target.x;\n      const dz = z - target.z;\n      const dist = Math.hypot(dx, dz);\n      if (target.kind === 'pool' && dist < 0.35 + target.volume * 0.15) {\n        y -= 0.02;\n        rgb = blood;\n      } else if ((target.kind === 'wound' || target.kind === 'guide') && dist < 0.18) {\n        y += 0.03;\n        rgb = [rgb[0] * 0.7, rgb[1] * 0.55, rgb[2] * 0.55];\n      } else if (target.kind === 'reverie' && dist < target.radius + 0.2) {\n        y += Math.sin(time * 3 + dist * 6) * 0.015;\n        rgb = [0.55, 0.62, 0.78];\n      } else if (target.burn > 0 && dist < 0.3) {\n        rgb = [0.25, 0.18, 0.14];\n      }\n    }\n    pos[i * 3 + 1] = y;\n    col[i * 3] = rgb[0];\n    col[i * 3 + 1] = rgb[1];\n    col[i * 3 + 2] = rgb[2];\n  }\n  position.needsUpdate = true;\n  color.needsUpdate = true;\n  mesh.computeVertexNormals();\n}\n\n/** Gloves follow the seats. An empty seat is parked under the floor. */\nfunction paintGlove(mesh: Mesh, op: Op | null): void {\n  const position = mesh.getAttribute('position');\n  const color = mesh.getAttribute('color');\n  const pos = position.array;\n  const col = color.array;\n  const tints: [number, number, number][] = [\n    [0.92, 0.93, 0.9],\n    [0.95, 0.78, 0.55],\n    [0.7, 0.82, 0.95],\n    [0.82, 0.7, 0.9],\n  ];\n  for (let s = 0; s < 4; s++) {\n    const seat = op?.seats[s];\n    const base = s * 16;\n    if (!seat) {\n      quad(pos, base, 0, 0, 0.01, 0.01, -4, tints[s], col);\n      quad(pos, base + 4, 0, 0, 0.01, 0.01, -4, tints[s], col);\n      quad(pos, base + 8, 0, 0, 0.01, 0.01, -4, [0.7, 0.75, 0.78], col);\n      continue;\n    }\n    quad(pos, base, seat.x, seat.z, 0.16, 0.12, 0.08, tints[s], col);\n    quad(pos, base + 4, seat.x - 0.14, seat.z + 0.08, 0.05, 0.07, 0.09, tints[s], col);\n    quad(pos, base + 8, seat.x + 0.05, seat.z - 0.16, 0.03, 0.16, 0.1, [0.75, 0.78, 0.8], col);\n  }\n  position.needsUpdate = true;\n  color.needsUpdate = true;\n  mesh.computeVertexNormals();\n}\n"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-55eb6fd7-7d39-4792-b72d-e62c40ed63fa-138","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/audio/library.ts","content":"/**\n * @file The theatre's music and effects, written as chip voices. No samples, no audio files.\n */\nimport { defineSfx, defineSong } from '../../../engine';\n\nconst effect = (freq: number, to: number, dur: number, wave: 'sine' | 'square' | 'triangle' | 'saw' | 'noise' | 'pulse' = 'sine') =>\n  defineSfx(`sfx:${wave}-${freq}`, {\n    voices: { wave, freq, to, dur, vol: 0.25 },\n  });\n\ndefineSfx('sfx:cut', { voices: { wave: 'noise', freq: 1800, to: 400, dur: 0.12, vol: 0.22, filter: 'bandpass' } });\ndefineSfx('sfx:stitch', { voices: { wave: 'triangle', freq: 520, to: 180, dur: 0.08, vol: 0.2 } });\ndefineSfx('sfx:drain', { voices: { wave: 'noise', freq: 240, to: 90, dur: 0.28, vol: 0.2, filter: 'lowpass' } });\ndefineSfx('sfx:laser', { voices: { wave: 'saw', freq: 660, to: 740, dur: 0.16, vol: 0.12 } });\ndefineSfx('sfx:syringe', { voices: { wave: 'square', freq: 1400, to: 900, dur: 0.05, vol: 0.16 } });\ndefineSfx('sfx:gel', { voices: { wave: 'sine', freq: 220, to: 140, dur: 0.18, vol: 0.2 } });\ndefineSfx('sfx:scan', { voices: { wave: 'sine', freq: 880, to: 1320, dur: 0.14, vol: 0.16 } });\ndefineSfx('sfx:forceps', { voices: { wave: 'square', freq: 340, to: 220, dur: 0.06, vol: 0.18 } });\ndefineSfx('sfx:beep', { voices: { wave: 'square', freq: 880, dur: 0.06, vol: 0.12 } });\ndefineSfx('sfx:alarm', { voices: { wave: 'saw', freq: 440, to: 660, dur: 0.3, vol: 0.2 } });\ndefineSfx('sfx:rank', { voices: { wave: 'triangle', freq: 523, arp: [0, 4, 7, 12], step: 0.07, dur: 0.4, vol: 0.22 } });\ndefineSfx('sfx:menu', { voices: { wave: 'square', freq: 660, to: 880, dur: 0.04, vol: 0.12 }, bus: 'ui' });\n\nvoid effect;\n\nconst bar = 'C4 - E4 - | G4 - E4 -';\n\ndefineSong('song:title', {\n  description: 'The harbour at night, under the title.',\n  bpm: 92,\n  tracks: [\n    { wave: 'triangle', vol: 0.16, notes: 'A3 - C4 - | E4 - C4 - | A3 - D4 - | E4 - C4 -' },\n    { wave: 'sine', vol: 0.08, notes: 'A2 - - - | A2 - - - | F2 - - - | A2 - - -' },\n  ],\n});\n\ndefineSong('song:or', {\n  description: 'Calm under the lamp, while the work is ordinary.',\n  bpm: 100,\n  tracks: [\n    { wave: 'triangle', vol: 0.14, notes: bar + ' | D4 - F4 - | E4 - C4 -' },\n    { wave: 'sine', vol: 0.07, notes: 'C3 - G3 - | A3 - G3 - | F3 - A3 - | G3 - E3 -' },\n  ],\n});\n\ndefineSong('song:strain', {\n  description: 'Something on the sheet is no longer tissue.',\n  bpm: 128,\n  tracks: [\n    { wave: 'saw', vol: 0.1, notes: 'E4 - G4 - | Bb4 - G4 - | E4 - A4 - | Bb4 - G4 -' },\n    { wave: 'triangle', vol: 0.12, notes: 'E3 - - - | E3 - - - | F3 - - - | E3 - - -' },\n  ],\n});\n\ndefineSong('song:mercy', {\n  description: 'The last case, slow and wide.',\n  bpm: 72,\n  tracks: [\n    { wave: 'sine', vol: 0.14, notes: 'G4 - - - | B4 - - - | D5 - - - | B4 - - -' },\n    { wave: 'triangle', vol: 0.1, notes: 'G3 - D4 - | G3 - D4 - | A3 - E4 - | G3 - D4 -' },\n  ],\n});\n\ndefineSong('song:story', {\n  description: 'Between operations, in the corridor.',\n  bpm: 84,\n  tracks: [{ wave: 'triangle', vol: 0.12, notes: 'F4 - A4 - | C5 - A4 - | G4 - Bb4 - | A4 - F4 -' }],\n});\n\ndefineSong('song:jingle', {\n  description: 'The sponsor spot on the gala television. Short, bright, and a little too pleased.',\n  bpm: 150,\n  tracks: [{ wave: 'square', vol: 0.1, notes: 'C5 E5 G5 C6 | E5 - G5 -' }],\n});\n\ndefineSong('song:win', {\n  description: 'The operation holds.',\n  bpm: 120,\n  tracks: [{ wave: 'triangle', vol: 0.16, notes: 'C4 E4 G4 C5 | E5 - - -' }],\n});\n\ndefineSong('song:lose', {\n  description: 'Called off.',\n  bpm: 70,\n  tracks: [{ wave: 'saw', vol: 0.08, notes: 'E4 - C4 - | A3 - - -' }],\n});\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1954,"output_tokens":5762,"cache_read_input_tokens":190208,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"80fe337e-f7df-4750-b236-e8532b969f87"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-55eb6fd7-7d39-4792-b72d-e62c40ed63fa-136","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"/**\\n * @file The two looks. Harbor is the night hospital. Field is the wet sheet, full resolution, so a stitch reads at ten feet.\\n */\\nimport { defineLook } from '../../../engine';\\n\\ndefineLook('look:harbor', {\\n  description: 'Harbor Light at night. Soft contact shadows, a warm teal grade, a thin outline on the people, and a little bloom on the lamp.',\\n  style: 'pbr',\\n  resolution: 'full',\\n  textures: 'smooth',\\n  filters: {\\n    ao: { scope: 'all', strength: 0.6 },\\n    aa: { scope: 'all' },\\n    outline: { scope: 'characters+objects', width: 1.5, darken: 0.2 },\\n    grade: { scope: 'all', temperature: 0.12, tint: 0.18, saturation: 0.95 },\\n    bloom: { scope: 'all', strength: 0.4, threshold: 0.82 },\\n  },\\n});\\n\\ndefineLook('look:field', {\\n  description: 'The operation. Wet highlights, contact, a little screen-space reflection, and full-frame smoothing.',\\n  style: 'pbr',\\n  resolution: 'full',\\n  textures: 'smooth',\\n  filters: {\\n    ao: { scope: 'all', strength: 0.7 },\\n    ssr: { scope: 'all', strength: 0.35 },\\n    aa: { scope: 'all' },\\n    bloom: { scope: 'all', strength: 0.28, threshold: 0.9 },\\n    grade: { scope: 'all', saturation: 1.05, contrast: 1.04 },\\n  },\\n});\\n\\ndefineLook('look:still', {\\n  description: 'Stillpoint laid over the field: teal, the colour pulled back, a vignette.',\\n  filters: {\\n    grade: { scope: 'all', saturation: 0.35, tint: 0.45, temperature: -0.2 },\\n    vignette: { scope: 'all', strength: 0.65 },\\n  },\\n});\\n\\ndefineLook('look:pulse', {\\n  description: 'Second Pulse laid over the field: amber and a streak of speed.',\\n  filters: {\\n    grade: { scope: 'all', temperature: 0.45, saturation: 1.2 },\\n    speedlines: { scope: 'all', strength: 0.45 },\\n  },\\n});\\n\\ndefineLook('look:low', {\\n  description: 'Vitals failing: a red vignette and a colder grade.',\\n  filters: {\\n    vignette: { scope: 'all', strength: 0.8 },\\n    grade: { scope: 'all', temperature: 0.2, saturation: 0.8 },\\n  },\\n});\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/view/looks.ts has been created.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/view/looks.ts has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/view/looks.ts\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"/**\\n * @file The two looks. Harbor is the night hospital. Field is the wet sheet, full resolution, so a stitch reads at ten feet.\\n */\\nimport { defineLook } from '../../../engine';\\n\\ndefineLook('look:harbor', {\\n  description: 'Harbor Light at night. Soft contact shadows, a warm teal grade, a thin outline on the people, and a little bloom on the lamp.',\\n  style: 'pbr',\\n  resolution: 'full',\\n  textures: 'smooth',\\n  filters: {\\n    ao: { scope: 'all', strength: 0.6 },\\n    aa: { scope: 'all' },\\n    outline: { scope: 'characters+objects', width: 1.5, darken: 0.2 },\\n    grade: { scope: 'all', temperature: 0.12, tint: 0.18, saturation: 0.95 },\\n    bloom: { scope: 'all', strength: 0.4, threshold: 0.82 },\\n  },\\n});\\n\\ndefineLook('look:field', {\\n  description: 'The operation. Wet highlights, contact, a little screen-space reflection, and full-frame smoothing.',\\n  style: 'pbr',\\n  resolution: 'full',\\n  textures: 'smooth',\\n  filters: {\\n    ao: { scope: 'all', strength: 0.7 },\\n    ssr: { scope: 'all', strength: 0.35 },\\n    aa: { scope: 'all' },\\n    bloom: { scope: 'all', strength: 0.28, threshold: 0.9 },\\n    grade: { scope: 'all', saturation: 1.05, contrast: 1.04 },\\n  },\\n});\\n\\ndefineLook('look:still', {\\n  description: 'Stillpoint laid over the field: teal, the colour pulled back, a vignette.',\\n  filters: {\\n    grade: { scope: 'all', saturation: 0.35, tint: 0.45, temperature: -0.2 },\\n    vignette: { scope: 'all', strength: 0.65 },\\n  },\\n});\\n\\ndefineLook('look:pulse', {\\n  description: 'Second Pulse laid over the field: amber and a streak of speed.',\\n  filters: {\\n    grade: { scope: 'all', temperature: 0.45, saturation: 1.2 },\\n    speedlines: { scope: 'all', strength: 0.45 },\\n  },\\n});\\n\\ndefineLook('look:low', {\\n  description: 'Vitals failing: a red vignette and a colder grade.',\\n  filters: {\\n    vignette: { scope: 'all', strength: 0.8 },\\n    grade: { scope: 'all', temperature: 0.2, saturation: 0.8 },\\n  },\\n});\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-55eb6fd7-7d39-4792-b72d-e62c40ed63fa-137","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"/**\\n * @file The living sheet and the glove. A kit box lends its geometry class. The page keeps the buffers and rewrites\\n * them every frame. Ninety-six by sixty, not the plan's three hundred and twenty by one hundred and ninety-two:\\n * four software-rendered copies of the denser grid were killed for memory on this machine.\\n */\\nimport { boxGeometry, defineGeometry, defineMaterial } from '../../../engine';\\nimport type { Op } from '../../op/types';\\n\\n/** Columns of quads across the sheet. */\\nexport const COLS = 96;\\n/** Rows of quads down the sheet. */\\nexport const ROWS = 60;\\n/** Half-width of the sheet, metres. Cursors clamp to this. */\\nexport const HALF_X = 8;\\n/** Half-depth of the sheet, metres. */\\nexport const HALF_Z = 5;\\n\\n/** Vertices across, including the last edge. */\\nconst VX = COLS + 1;\\n/** Vertices down. */\\nconst VZ = ROWS + 1;\\n/** Sheet vertices. The glove is a second geometry. */\\nconst SHEET = VX * VZ;\\n\\n/** A buffer geometry, as much of it as this file uses. three.js stays inside the engine. */\\ninterface Mesh {\\n  setAttribute(name: string, attribute: unknown): void;\\n  setIndex(index: number[]): void;\\n  getAttribute(name: string): { array: Float32Array; needsUpdate: boolean };\\n  computeVertexNormals(): void;\\n}\\n\\n/** The attribute class taken from a kit box. */\\ninterface AttributeCtor {\\n  new (array: Float32Array, size: number): unknown;\\n}\\n\\nconst sample = boxGeometry({ width: 1, height: 1, depth: 1 });\\nconst Geometry = sample.constructor as new () => Mesh;\\nconst Attribute = sample.getAttribute('position').constructor as AttributeCtor;\\n\\n/** The sheet, once the builder has run. */\\nlet sheet: Mesh | null = null;\\n/** The glove, once the builder has run. */\\nlet glove: Mesh | null = null;\\n\\n/** Grid index. */\\nfunction at(x: number, z: number): number {\\n  return z * VX + x;\\n}\\n\\n/** Build the sheet once, at its full extent, so the cull box covers every later height. */\\nfunction buildSheet(): Mesh {\\n  const position = new Float32Array(SHEET * 3);\\n  const color = new Float32Array(SHEET * 3);\\n  const uv = new Float32Array(SHEET * 2);\\n  for (let z = 0; z < VZ; z++) {\\n    for (let x = 0; x < VX; x++) {\\n      const i = at(x, z);\\n      position[i * 3] = -HALF_X + (x / COLS) * HALF_X * 2;\\n      position[i * 3 + 1] = 0.4;\\n      position[i * 3 + 2] = -HALF_Z + (z / ROWS) * HALF_Z * 2;\\n      uv[i * 2] = x / COLS;\\n      uv[i * 2 + 1] = z / ROWS;\\n      color[i * 3] = 0.72;\\n      color[i * 3 + 1] = 0.28;\\n      color[i * 3 + 2] = 0.3;\\n    }\\n  }\\n  const index: number[] = [];\\n  for (let z = 0; z < ROWS; z++) {\\n    for (let x = 0; x < COLS; x++) {\\n      const a = at(x, z);\\n      index.push(a, a + VX, a + 1, a + 1, a + VX, a + VX + 1);\\n    }\\n  }\\n  const mesh = new Geometry();\\n  mesh.setAttribute('position', new Attribute(position, 3));\\n  mesh.setAttribute('normal', new Attribute(new Float32Array(SHEET * 3), 3));\\n  mesh.setAttribute('color', new Attribute(color, 3));\\n  mesh.setAttribute('uv', new Attribute(uv, 2));\\n  mesh.setIndex(index);\\n  mesh.computeVertexNormals();\\n  sheet = mesh;\\n  return mesh;\\n}\\n\\n/** A small glove: a palm, a thumb, and a tool, twelve triangles, four seats packed end to end. */\\nfunction buildGlove(): Mesh {\\n  const count = 4 * 16;\\n  const mesh = new Geometry();\\n  mesh.setAttribute('position', new Attribute(new Float32Array(count * 3), 3));\\n  mesh.setAttribute('normal', new Attribute(new Float32Array(count * 3), 3));\\n  mesh.setAttribute('color', new Attribute(new Float32Array(count * 3), 3));\\n  mesh.setAttribute('uv', new Attribute(new Float32Array(count * 2), 2));\\n  const index: number[] = [];\\n  for (let s = 0; s < 4; s++) {\\n    const b = s * 16;\\n    index.push(b, b + 1, b + 2, b, b + 2, b + 3);\\n    index.push(b + 4, b + 5, b + 6, b + 4, b + 6, b + 7);\\n    index.push(b + 8, b + 9, b + 10, b + 8, b + 10, b + 11);\\n  }\\n  mesh.setIndex(index);\\n  glove = mesh;\\n  return mesh;\\n}\\n\\ndefineGeometry('geometry:sheet', {\\n  description: 'The operation sheet, a grid the page rewrites every frame.',\\n  budget: 200000,\\n  create: () => buildSheet() as never,\\n});\\n\\ndefineGeometry('geometry:cursor', {\\n  description: 'Four gloved hands. The page moves the vertices onto the cursors.',\\n  budget: 4000,\\n  create: () => buildGlove() as never,\\n});\\n\\ndefineMaterial('material:tissue', {\\n  color: '#ffffff',\\n  roughness: 0.32,\\n  metalness: 0.04,\\n  vertexColors: true,\\n});\\n\\ndefineMaterial('material:glove', {\\n  color: '#ffffff',\\n  roughness: 0.55,\\n  vertexColors: true,\\n});\\n\\n/** Blood colour from the display setting. */\\nfunction bloodOf(mode: string): [number, number, number] {\\n  if (mode === 'teal') return [0.15, 0.45, 0.48];\\n  if (mode === 'off') return [0.35, 0.32, 0.3];\\n  return [0.45, 0.05, 0.08];\\n}\\n\\n/** Tissue colour at a sheet point, before blood and burns. */\\nfunction tissue(x: number, z: number): [number, number, number] {\\n  const organ = Math.hypot(x * 0.55, z) < 2.2;\\n  const vein = Math.abs(z - Math.sin(x * 1.3) * 0.35) < 0.08;\\n  if (vein) return [0.55, 0.16, 0.22];\\n  if (organ) return [0.78, 0.36, 0.34];\\n  return [0.86, 0.62, 0.52];\\n}\\n\\n/** Write one glove quad in local sheet space. */\\nfunction quad(\\n  array: Float32Array,\\n  base: number,\\n  x: number,\\n  z: number,\\n  w: number,\\n  d: number,\\n  y: number,\\n  rgb: [number, number, number],\\n  colors: Float32Array,\\n): void {\\n  const corners = [\\n    [x - w, z - d],\\n    [x + w, z - d],\\n    [x + w, z + d],\\n    [x - w, z + d],\\n  ];\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) {\\n    const v = base + i;\\n    array[v * 3] = corners[i][0];\\n    array[v * 3 + 1] = y;\\n    array[v * 3 + 2] = corners[i][1];\\n    colors[v * 3] = rgb[0];\\n    colors[v * 3 + 1] = rgb[1];\\n    colors[v * 3 + 2] = rgb[2];\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** Rewrite the sheet and the gloves from the operation. Missing meshes wait until the builder runs. */\\nexport function paintField(op: Op | null, time: number, bloodMode: string): void {\\n  if (sheet) paintSheet(sheet, op, time, bloodOf(bloodMode));\\n  if (glove) paintGlove(glove, op);\\n}\\n\\n/** Heights and colours of the sheet. */\\nfunction paintSheet(mesh: Mesh, op: Op | null, time: number, blood: [number, number, number]): void {\\n  const position = mesh.getAttribute('position');\\n  const color = mesh.getAttribute('color');\\n  const pos = position.array;\\n  const col = color.array;\\n  const breath = Math.sin(time * 1.4) * 0.012;\\n  const beat = Math.pow(Math.max(0, Math.sin(time * 6.2)), 18) * 0.03;\\n  const targets = op?.targets.filter((target) => !target.done && target.site === (op.seats[0]?.site ?? 0)) ?? [];\\n  for (let i = 0; i < SHEET; i++) {\\n    const x = pos[i * 3];\\n    const z = pos[i * 3 + 2];\\n    let y = breath + beat * Math.exp(-Math.hypot(x, z) * 0.8);\\n    let rgb = tissue(x, z);\\n    for (const target of targets) {\\n      const dx = x - target.x;\\n      const dz = z - target.z;\\n      const dist = Math.hypot(dx, dz);\\n      if (target.kind === 'pool' && dist < 0.35 + target.volume * 0.15) {\\n        y -= 0.02;\\n        rgb = blood;\\n      } else if ((target.kind === 'wound' || target.kind === 'guide') && dist < 0.18) {\\n        y += 0.03;\\n        rgb = [rgb[0] * 0.7, rgb[1] * 0.55, rgb[2] * 0.55];\\n      } else if (target.kind === 'reverie' && dist < target.radius + 0.2) {\\n        y += Math.sin(time * 3 + dist * 6) * 0.015;\\n        rgb = [0.55, 0.62, 0.78];\\n      } else if (target.burn > 0 && dist < 0.3) {\\n        rgb = [0.25, 0.18, 0.14];\\n      }\\n    }\\n    pos[i * 3 + 1] = y;\\n    col[i * 3] = rgb[0];\\n    col[i * 3 + 1] = rgb[1];\\n    col[i * 3 + 2] = rgb[2];\\n  }\\n  position.needsUpdate = true;\\n  color.needsUpdate = true;\\n  mesh.computeVertexNormals();\\n}\\n\\n/** Gloves follow the seats. An empty seat is parked under the floor. */\\nfunction paintGlove(mesh: Mesh, op: Op | null): void {\\n  const position = mesh.getAttribute('position');\\n  const color = mesh.getAttribute('color');\\n  const pos = position.array;\\n  const col = color.array;\\n  const tints: [number, number, number][] = [\\n    [0.92, 0.93, 0.9],\\n    [0.95, 0.78, 0.55],\\n    [0.7, 0.82, 0.95],\\n    [0.82, 0.7, 0.9],\\n  ];\\n  for (let s = 0; s < 4; s++) {\\n    const seat = op?.seats[s];\\n    const base = s * 16;\\n    if (!seat) {\\n      quad(pos, base, 0, 0, 0.01, 0.01, -4, tints[s], col);\\n      quad(pos, base + 4, 0, 0, 0.01, 0.01, -4, tints[s], col);\\n      quad(pos, base + 8, 0, 0, 0.01, 0.01, -4, [0.7, 0.75, 0.78], col);\\n      continue;\\n    }\\n    quad(pos, base, seat.x, seat.z, 0.16, 0.12, 0.08, tints[s], col);\\n    quad(pos, base + 4, seat.x - 0.14, seat.z + 0.08, 0.05, 0.07, 0.09, tints[s], col);\\n    quad(pos, base + 8, seat.x + 0.05, seat.z - 0.16, 0.03, 0.16, 0.1, [0.75, 0.78, 0.8], col);\\n  }\\n  position.needsUpdate = true;\\n  color.needsUpdate = true;\\n  mesh.computeVertexNormals();\\n}\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/view/field/sheet.ts has been created.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/view/field/sheet.ts has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/view/field/sheet.ts\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"/**\\n * @file The living sheet and the glove. A kit box lends its geometry class. The page keeps the buffers and rewrites\\n * them every frame. Ninety-six by sixty, not the plan's three hundred and twenty by one hundred and ninety-two:\\n * four software-rendered copies of the denser grid were killed for memory on this machine.\\n */\\nimport { boxGeometry, defineGeometry, defineMaterial } from '../../../engine';\\nimport type { Op } from '../../op/types';\\n\\n/** Columns of quads across the sheet. */\\nexport const COLS = 96;\\n/** Rows of quads down the sheet. */\\nexport const ROWS = 60;\\n/** Half-width of the sheet, metres. Cursors clamp to this. */\\nexport const HALF_X = 8;\\n/** Half-depth of the sheet, metres. */\\nexport const HALF_Z = 5;\\n\\n/** Vertices across, including the last edge. */\\nconst VX = COLS + 1;\\n/** Vertices down. */\\nconst VZ = ROWS + 1;\\n/** Sheet vertices. The glove is a second geometry. */\\nconst SHEET = VX * VZ;\\n\\n/** A buffer geometry, as much of it as this file uses. three.js stays inside the engine. */\\ninterface Mesh {\\n  setAttribute(name: string, attribute: unknown): void;\\n  setIndex(index: number[]): void;\\n  getAttribute(name: string): { array: Float32Array; needsUpdate: boolean };\\n  computeVertexNormals(): void;\\n}\\n\\n/** The attribute class taken from a kit box. */\\ninterface AttributeCtor {\\n  new (array: Float32Array, size: number): unknown;\\n}\\n\\nconst sample = boxGeometry({ width: 1, height: 1, depth: 1 });\\nconst Geometry = sample.constructor as new () => Mesh;\\nconst Attribute = sample.getAttribute('position').constructor as AttributeCtor;\\n\\n/** The sheet, once the builder has run. */\\nlet sheet: Mesh | null = null;\\n/** The glove, once the builder has run. */\\nlet glove: Mesh | null = null;\\n\\n/** Grid index. */\\nfunction at(x: number, z: number): number {\\n  return z * VX + x;\\n}\\n\\n/** Build the sheet once, at its full extent, so the cull box covers every later height. */\\nfunction buildSheet(): Mesh {\\n  const position = new Float32Array(SHEET * 3);\\n  const color = new Float32Array(SHEET * 3);\\n  const uv = new Float32Array(SHEET * 2);\\n  for (let z = 0; z < VZ; z++) {\\n    for (let x = 0; x < VX; x++) {\\n      const i = at(x, z);\\n      position[i * 3] = -HALF_X + (x / COLS) * HALF_X * 2;\\n      position[i * 3 + 1] = 0.4;\\n      position[i * 3 + 2] = -HALF_Z + (z / ROWS) * HALF_Z * 2;\\n      uv[i * 2] = x / COLS;\\n      uv[i * 2 + 1] = z / ROWS;\\n      color[i * 3] = 0.72;\\n      color[i * 3 + 1] = 0.28;\\n      color[i * 3 + 2] = 0.3;\\n    }\\n  }\\n  const index: number[] = [];\\n  for (let z = 0; z < ROWS; z++) {\\n    for (let x = 0; x < COLS; x++) {\\n      const a = at(x, z);\\n      index.push(a, a + VX, a + 1, a + 1, a + VX, a + VX + 1);\\n    }\\n  }\\n  const mesh = new Geometry();\\n  mesh.setAttribute('position', new Attribute(position, 3));\\n  mesh.setAttribute('normal', new Attribute(new Float32Array(SHEET * 3), 3));\\n  mesh.setAttribute('color', new Attribute(color, 3));\\n  mesh.setAttribute('uv', new Attribute(uv, 2));\\n  mesh.setIndex(index);\\n  mesh.computeVertexNormals();\\n  sheet = mesh;\\n  return mesh;\\n}\\n\\n/** A small glove: a palm, a thumb, and a tool, twelve triangles, four seats packed end to end. */\\nfunction buildGlove(): Mesh {\\n  const count = 4 * 16;\\n  const mesh = new Geometry();\\n  mesh.setAttribute('position', new Attribute(new Float32Array(count * 3), 3));\\n  mesh.setAttribute('normal', new Attribute(new Float32Array(count * 3), 3));\\n  mesh.setAttribute('color', new Attribute(new Float32Array(count * 3), 3));\\n  mesh.setAttribute('uv', new Attribute(new Float32Array(count * 2), 2));\\n  const index: number[] = [];\\n  for (let s = 0; s < 4; s++) {\\n    const b = s * 16;\\n    index.push(b, b + 1, b + 2, b, b + 2, b + 3);\\n    index.push(b + 4, b + 5, b + 6, b + 4, b + 6, b + 7);\\n    index.push(b + 8, b + 9, b + 10, b + 8, b + 10, b + 11);\\n  }\\n  mesh.setIndex(index);\\n  glove = mesh;\\n  return mesh;\\n}\\n\\ndefineGeometry('geometry:sheet', {\\n  description: 'The operation sheet, a grid the page rewrites every frame.',\\n  budget: 200000,\\n  create: () => buildSheet() as never,\\n});\\n\\ndefineGeometry('geometry:cursor', {\\n  description: 'Four gloved hands. The page moves the vertices onto the cursors.',\\n  budget: 4000,\\n  create: () => buildGlove() as never,\\n});\\n\\ndefineMaterial('material:tissue', {\\n  color: '#ffffff',\\n  roughness: 0.32,\\n  metalness: 0.04,\\n  vertexColors: true,\\n});\\n\\ndefineMaterial('material:glove', {\\n  color: '#ffffff',\\n  roughness: 0.55,\\n  vertexColors: true,\\n});\\n\\n/** Blood colour from the display setting. */\\nfunction bloodOf(mode: string): [number, number, number] {\\n  if (mode === 'teal') return [0.15, 0.45, 0.48];\\n  if (mode === 'off') return [0.35, 0.32, 0.3];\\n  return [0.45, 0.05, 0.08];\\n}\\n\\n/** Tissue colour at a sheet point, before blood and burns. */\\nfunction tissue(x: number, z: number): [number, number, number] {\\n  const organ = Math.hypot(x * 0.55, z) < 2.2;\\n  const vein = Math.abs(z - Math.sin(x * 1.3) * 0.35) < 0.08;\\n  if (vein) return [0.55, 0.16, 0.22];\\n  if (organ) return [0.78, 0.36, 0.34];\\n  return [0.86, 0.62, 0.52];\\n}\\n\\n/** Write one glove quad in local sheet space. */\\nfunction quad(\\n  array: Float32Array,\\n  base: number,\\n  x: number,\\n  z: number,\\n  w: number,\\n  d: number,\\n  y: number,\\n  rgb: [number, number, number],\\n  colors: Float32Array,\\n): void {\\n  const corners = [\\n    [x - w, z - d],\\n    [x + w, z - d],\\n    [x + w, z + d],\\n    [x - w, z + d],\\n  ];\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) {\\n    const v = base + i;\\n    array[v * 3] = corners[i][0];\\n    array[v * 3 + 1] = y;\\n    array[v * 3 + 2] = corners[i][1];\\n    colors[v * 3] = rgb[0];\\n    colors[v * 3 + 1] = rgb[1];\\n    colors[v * 3 + 2] = rgb[2];\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** Rewrite the sheet and the gloves from the operation. Missing meshes wait until the builder runs. */\\nexport function paintField(op: Op | null, time: number, bloodMode: string): void {\\n  if (sheet) paintSheet(sheet, op, time, bloodOf(bloodMode));\\n  if (glove) paintGlove(glove, op);\\n}\\n\\n/** Heights and colours of the sheet. */\\nfunction paintSheet(mesh: Mesh, op: Op | null, time: number, blood: [number, number, number]): void {\\n  const position = mesh.getAttribute('position');\\n  const color = mesh.getAttribute('color');\\n  const pos = position.array;\\n  const col = color.array;\\n  const breath = Math.sin(time * 1.4) * 0.012;\\n  const beat = Math.pow(Math.max(0, Math.sin(time * 6.2)), 18) * 0.03;\\n  const targets = op?.targets.filter((target) => !target.done && target.site === (op.seats[0]?.site ?? 0)) ?? [];\\n  for (let i = 0; i < SHEET; i++) {\\n    const x = pos[i * 3];\\n    const z = pos[i * 3 + 2];\\n    let y = breath + beat * Math.exp(-Math.hypot(x, z) * 0.8);\\n    let rgb = tissue(x, z);\\n    for (const target of targets) {\\n      const dx = x - target.x;\\n      const dz = z - target.z;\\n      const dist = Math.hypot(dx, dz);\\n      if (target.kind === 'pool' && dist < 0.35 + target.volume * 0.15) {\\n        y -= 0.02;\\n        rgb = blood;\\n      } else if ((target.kind === 'wound' || target.kind === 'guide') && dist < 0.18) {\\n        y += 0.03;\\n        rgb = [rgb[0] * 0.7, rgb[1] * 0.55, rgb[2] * 0.55];\\n      } else if (target.kind === 'reverie' && dist < target.radius + 0.2) {\\n        y += Math.sin(time * 3 + dist * 6) * 0.015;\\n        rgb = [0.55, 0.62, 0.78];\\n      } else if (target.burn > 0 && dist < 0.3) {\\n        rgb = [0.25, 0.18, 0.14];\\n      }\\n    }\\n    pos[i * 3 + 1] = y;\\n    col[i * 3] = rgb[0];\\n    col[i * 3 + 1] = rgb[1];\\n    col[i * 3 + 2] = rgb[2];\\n  }\\n  position.needsUpdate = true;\\n  color.needsUpdate = true;\\n  mesh.computeVertexNormals();\\n}\\n\\n/** Gloves follow the seats. An empty seat is parked under the floor. */\\nfunction paintGlove(mesh: Mesh, op: Op | null): void {\\n  const position = mesh.getAttribute('position');\\n  const color = mesh.getAttribute('color');\\n  const pos = position.array;\\n  const col = color.array;\\n  const tints: [number, number, number][] = [\\n    [0.92, 0.93, 0.9],\\n    [0.95, 0.78, 0.55],\\n    [0.7, 0.82, 0.95],\\n    [0.82, 0.7, 0.9],\\n  ];\\n  for (let s = 0; s < 4; s++) {\\n    const seat = op?.seats[s];\\n    const base = s * 16;\\n    if (!seat) {\\n      quad(pos, base, 0, 0, 0.01, 0.01, -4, tints[s], col);\\n      quad(pos, base + 4, 0, 0, 0.01, 0.01, -4, tints[s], col);\\n      quad(pos, base + 8, 0, 0, 0.01, 0.01, -4, [0.7, 0.75, 0.78], col);\\n      continue;\\n    }\\n    quad(pos, base, seat.x, seat.z, 0.16, 0.12, 0.08, tints[s], col);\\n    quad(pos, base + 4, seat.x - 0.14, seat.z + 0.08, 0.05, 0.07, 0.09, tints[s], col);\\n    quad(pos, base + 8, seat.x + 0.05, seat.z - 0.16, 0.03, 0.16, 0.1, [0.75, 0.78, 0.8], col);\\n  }\\n  position.needsUpdate = true;\\n  color.needsUpdate = true;\\n  mesh.computeVertexNormals();\\n}\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-55eb6fd7-7d39-4792-b72d-e62c40ed63fa-138","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"/**\\n * @file The theatre's music and effects, written as chip voices. No samples, no audio files.\\n */\\nimport { defineSfx, defineSong } from '../../../engine';\\n\\nconst effect = (freq: number, to: number, dur: number, wave: 'sine' | 'square' | 'triangle' | 'saw' | 'noise' | 'pulse' = 'sine') =>\\n  defineSfx(`sfx:${wave}-${freq}`, {\\n    voices: { wave, freq, to, dur, vol: 0.25 },\\n  });\\n\\ndefineSfx('sfx:cut', { voices: { wave: 'noise', freq: 1800, to: 400, dur: 0.12, vol: 0.22, filter: 'bandpass' } });\\ndefineSfx('sfx:stitch', { voices: { wave: 'triangle', freq: 520, to: 180, dur: 0.08, vol: 0.2 } });\\ndefineSfx('sfx:drain', { voices: { wave: 'noise', freq: 240, to: 90, dur: 0.28, vol: 0.2, filter: 'lowpass' } });\\ndefineSfx('sfx:laser', { voices: { wave: 'saw', freq: 660, to: 740, dur: 0.16, vol: 0.12 } });\\ndefineSfx('sfx:syringe', { voices: { wave: 'square', freq: 1400, to: 900, dur: 0.05, vol: 0.16 } });\\ndefineSfx('sfx:gel', { voices: { wave: 'sine', freq: 220, to: 140, dur: 0.18, vol: 0.2 } });\\ndefineSfx('sfx:scan', { voices: { wave: 'sine', freq: 880, to: 1320, dur: 0.14, vol: 0.16 } });\\ndefineSfx('sfx:forceps', { voices: { wave: 'square', freq: 340, to: 220, dur: 0.06, vol: 0.18 } });\\ndefineSfx('sfx:beep', { voices: { wave: 'square', freq: 880, dur: 0.06, vol: 0.12 } });\\ndefineSfx('sfx:alarm', { voices: { wave: 'saw', freq: 440, to: 660, dur: 0.3, vol: 0.2 } });\\ndefineSfx('sfx:rank', { voices: { wave: 'triangle', freq: 523, arp: [0, 4, 7, 12], step: 0.07, dur: 0.4, vol: 0.22 } });\\ndefineSfx('sfx:menu', { voices: { wave: 'square', freq: 660, to: 880, dur: 0.04, vol: 0.12 }, bus: 'ui' });\\n\\nvoid effect;\\n\\nconst bar = 'C4 - E4 - | G4 - E4 -';\\n\\ndefineSong('song:title', {\\n  description: 'The harbour at night, under the title.',\\n  bpm: 92,\\n  tracks: [\\n    { wave: 'triangle', vol: 0.16, notes: 'A3 - C4 - | E4 - C4 - | A3 - D4 - | E4 - C4 -' },\\n    { wave: 'sine', vol: 0.08, notes: 'A2 - - - | A2 - - - | F2 - - - | A2 - - -' },\\n  ],\\n});\\n\\ndefineSong('song:or', {\\n  description: 'Calm under the lamp, while the work is ordinary.',\\n  bpm: 100,\\n  tracks: [\\n    { wave: 'triangle', vol: 0.14, notes: bar + ' | D4 - F4 - | E4 - C4 -' },\\n    { wave: 'sine', vol: 0.07, notes: 'C3 - G3 - | A3 - G3 - | F3 - A3 - | G3 - E3 -' },\\n  ],\\n});\\n\\ndefineSong('song:strain', {\\n  description: 'Something on the sheet is no longer tissue.',\\n  bpm: 128,\\n  tracks: [\\n    { wave: 'saw', vol: 0.1, notes: 'E4 - G4 - | Bb4 - G4 - | E4 - A4 - | Bb4 - G4 -' },\\n    { wave: 'triangle', vol: 0.12, notes: 'E3 - - - | E3 - - - | F3 - - - | E3 - - -' },\\n  ],\\n});\\n\\ndefineSong('song:mercy', {\\n  description: 'The last case, slow and wide.',\\n  bpm: 72,\\n  tracks: [\\n    { wave: 'sine', vol: 0.14, notes: 'G4 - - - | B4 - - - | D5 - - - | B4 - - -' },\\n    { wave: 'triangle', vol: 0.1, notes: 'G3 - D4 - | G3 - D4 - | A3 - E4 - | G3 - D4 -' },\\n  ],\\n});\\n\\ndefineSong('song:story', {\\n  description: 'Between operations, in the corridor.',\\n  bpm: 84,\\n  tracks: [{ wave: 'triangle', vol: 0.12, notes: 'F4 - A4 - | C5 - A4 - | G4 - Bb4 - | A4 - F4 -' }],\\n});\\n\\ndefineSong('song:jingle', {\\n  description: 'The sponsor spot on the gala television. Short, bright, and a little too pleased.',\\n  bpm: 150,\\n  tracks: [{ wave: 'square', vol: 0.1, notes: 'C5 E5 G5 C6 | E5 - G5 -' }],\\n});\\n\\ndefineSong('song:win', {\\n  description: 'The operation holds.',\\n  bpm: 120,\\n  tracks: [{ wave: 'triangle', vol: 0.16, notes: 'C4 E4 G4 C5 | E5 - - -' }],\\n});\\n\\ndefineSong('song:lose', {\\n  description: 'Called off.',\\n  bpm: 70,\\n  tracks: [{ wave: 'saw', vol: 0.08, notes: 'E4 - C4 - | A3 - - -' }],\\n});\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/audio/library.ts has been created.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/audio/library.ts has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/audio/library.ts\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"/**\\n * @file The theatre's music and effects, written as chip voices. No samples, no audio files.\\n */\\nimport { defineSfx, defineSong } from '../../../engine';\\n\\nconst effect = (freq: number, to: number, dur: number, wave: 'sine' | 'square' | 'triangle' | 'saw' | 'noise' | 'pulse' = 'sine') =>\\n  defineSfx(`sfx:${wave}-${freq}`, {\\n    voices: { wave, freq, to, dur, vol: 0.25 },\\n  });\\n\\ndefineSfx('sfx:cut', { voices: { wave: 'noise', freq: 1800, to: 400, dur: 0.12, vol: 0.22, filter: 'bandpass' } });\\ndefineSfx('sfx:stitch', { voices: { wave: 'triangle', freq: 520, to: 180, dur: 0.08, vol: 0.2 } });\\ndefineSfx('sfx:drain', { voices: { wave: 'noise', freq: 240, to: 90, dur: 0.28, vol: 0.2, filter: 'lowpass' } });\\ndefineSfx('sfx:laser', { voices: { wave: 'saw', freq: 660, to: 740, dur: 0.16, vol: 0.12 } });\\ndefineSfx('sfx:syringe', { voices: { wave: 'square', freq: 1400, to: 900, dur: 0.05, v