ontroller or keyboard required\\\" and the settings button. Let the attract mode run.\\n\\n## Done\\nNo TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features. The demo is complete.\\n\\n## Source Information\\nCRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen. Write \\\"unknown\\\" for anything you can't confirm.\\n- Date: 2026-11-04 22:47:31\\n- Source: the work it's based on\\n- Plan: the file name of the plan you were given to build from, or none\\n- Genre and Perspective: genre and camera perspective used\\n- Tech: stack, libraries/engines, with versions if applicable\\n- Art Direction: style used\\n- Animation: system used\\n- Audio: music, sound effects and voice used\\n- Online: network features used, or none\\n- Testing: testing parameters allowed\\n- Research: research done, or none\\n- Environment: Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\n- Model: xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\n- Usage: write \\\"added on import\\\". You can't see your own cost, so don't estimate it: the runner records the real cost, tokens and time, and the agent that imports the game into AI Hub puts them on your About/Credits screen.\\n\\nExit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\\\"unknown\\\" for anything you can't confirm). Tools read it (the game's run record and the AI Hub catalogue), so write plain text, and check that the file parses as JSON.\\n{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\\"date\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"plan\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"genre\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"tech\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"animation\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"audio\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"online\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"testing\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"research\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"environment\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"model\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"},\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\\"your answer to each Testing Feedback question, in order\\\"],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\\"your answer to each Engine Feedback question, in order\\\"],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\\"your answer to each Prompt Feedback question, in order\\\"],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"the game's title, as on its title screen\\\",\\n    \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"a few words to go under the title\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"one or two sentences for the catalogue\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game, Tech demo or Tool\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"one of Action, Adventure, Fighting, Flight, Horror, Kids & Learning, Life Sim, Platformer, Puzzle, Racing, RPG, Shooter, Simulation, Sports, Stealth, Strategy\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"the work it's based on, e.g. Moby-Dick\\\",\\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"its franchise, e.g. Star Fox, or empty\\\",\\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"how many can play: 1, 1–2 or 1–4\\\",\\n    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"the controls, in one line\\\",\\n    \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"3 to 6 lowercase tags, e.g. 2d, 3d, arcade, story, co-op, versus, first-person, third-person, top-down, side-scrolling, pixel art, low-poly, retro, sci-fi, fantasy, comedy, vehicles, boss fights, exploration\\\"]\\n  }\\n}\\nThe catalogue's model, effort, CLI, date and usage come from the run's record after you finish, so they aren't asked here.\\n\\nTesting Feedback\\n\\n- How many issues did testing catch?\\n- How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?\\n- What was the most helpful test you ran?\\n- What was the least helpful test you ran?\\n\\nEngine Feedback\\n\\n- What did you like most about the engine?\\n- Did you get stuck or guess wrong?\\n- What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?\\n- What was the hardest part about using the engine?\\n- What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)\\n- If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?\\n\\nPrompt Feedback\\n\\n- What did you like most about this prompt?\\n- What was confusing?\\n- What was the hardest thing to do?\\n- What would you change in this prompt?\\n\",\"total_lines\":151}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f7183990-c508-4d93-8845-14890ee832c5-4","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The starter game's page (labs/game/index.html): it starts the engine (`createEngine`, engine/app/engine.ts) on\\n * the scene `game:play` (labs/game/scenes/play.ts) with the arena's text registered for the view, offers the bot's\\n * replay to `?replay=bot`, and shows the round each drawn frame in the HTML/CSS overlay's HUD: the gems, the clock,\\n * the controls, the best round kept across sessions (labs/game/best.ts, through the engine's store) and, when the\\n * round ends, how it ended. Enter then starts a new round on the next seed. Escape (or the pad's Start) pauses the\\n * round under a menu (`createMenu`: Resume, New round), which keeps its keys out of play while it is open\\n * (`createEngine({ modal })`); the store keeps the best round and any keys rebound (`createEngine({ store })`). The\\n * camera is the chase camera unless the URL names one (`?cam=iso`, `?cam3=orbit`).\\n10→ *\\n * Everything else a page does (routes, the renderer, the frame loop, the devices, `window.__engine`, the error\\n * overlay, the touch controls) is the engine's, so this file is the game's own presentation only. It reads the run\\n * and never changes it: the HUD cannot change the hash.\\n *\\n * Game code: it imports only the engine's public API (engine/index.ts) and the game's own files.\\n *\\n * Open it at http://127.0.0.1:5173/labs/game/ (`npm run dev`): `?seed=7&game.gems=20` plays another round,\\n * `?replay=bot` the bot's, `?cam=iso` another camera. Headless, `node x shot labs/game` reports what it draws.\\n */\\n20→/// <reference types=\\\"vite/client\\\" />\\nimport { createEngine, createMenu, createStore, type Engine, type EngineFrame, type Menu } from '../../engine';\\nimport { bestOf, recordBest } from './best';\\nimport { ARENA_TEXT, play, type Round } from './scenes/play';\\n\\n/** The page's query, with the chase camera when it names none: it follows the player round the arena. */\\nconst search = new URLSearchParams(location.search);\\nif (!search.has('cam') && !search.has('cam3')) search.set('cam3', 'chase');\\n\\n/** The game's replays, by name (`?replay=bot`), as text loaded on demand. */\\n30→const replays = { bot: () => import('./replays/bot.replay.json?raw').then((module) => module.default) };\\n\\n/** The started engine; null until `createEngine` resolves (its first frames are drawn before that). */\\nlet engine: Engine | null = null;\\n\\n/** Whether the round on screen has ended, so Enter starts the next. */\\nlet ended = false;\\n\\n/** The game's store: its best round across sessions; a replay's page plays in its demo mode, so it sets none. */\\nconst store = createStore({ prefix: 'my3dge-game:', mode: search.has('replay') ? 'demo' : 'play' });\\n40→\\n/** The fastest won round kept (s), and the run whose clock the page saw running, with the steps it started with. */\\nlet best = bestOf(store);\\nlet seen: { world: object; steps: number } | null = null;\\n\\n/** The pause menu while it is open; null while the round plays. */\\nlet paused: Menu | null = null;\\n\\n/** Opens the pause menu over the paused round, or reads it a frame: Resume (or Escape again), New round. */\\nfunction pauseMenu(dt: number): void {\\n50→  const [inspector, ui, input] = [engine?.inspector, engine?.ui, engine?.input];\\n  if (!inspector || !ui || !input) return;\\n  const close = () => {\\n    paused?.remove();\\n    paused = null;\\n    inspector.resume();\\n  };\\n  if (paused) return void paused.update(dt);\\n  if (!input.pressed('pause')) return;\\n  inspector.pause();\\n60→  const items = [\\n    { label: 'Resume', id: 'resume' },\\n    { label: 'New round', id: 'new' },\\n  ];\\n  paused = createMenu(ui.root, items, { input, id: 'pause', title: 'Paused', onCancel: close, onPick: (_i, item) => {\\n    if (typeof item === 'object' && item.id === 'new') inspector.seed(inspector.seed() + 1);\\n    close();\\n  } }); // prettier-ignore\\n}\\n\\n70→/** Shows the round in the HUD: the gems, the clock, the controls, and how the round ended. */\\nfunction showRound({ world }: EngineFrame): void {\\n  const ui = engine?.ui;\\n  const entity = world.query('round')[0] as unknown as { round: Round } | undefined;\\n  if (!ui || !entity) return;\\n  const { gems, collected, left, state } = entity.round;\\n  if (seen?.world !== world) seen = state === 'playing' ? { world, steps: left + world.tick } : null;\\n  const was = ended;\\n  ui.hud('gems', `Gems ${collected} / ${gems}`, { at: 'top-left' });\\n  ui.hud('clock', `${Math.ceil(left / world.hz)} s`, { at: 'top-right', color: left < 10 * world.hz ? '#ff8f6b' : '' });\\n80→  ui.hud('keys', 'WASD: run · Space: jump · Shift: dash · Esc: pause', { at: 'bottom', keys: true });\\n  ended = state !== 'playing';\\n  if (ended && !was && state === 'won' && seen) best = recordBest(store, (seen.steps - left) / world.hz);\\n  ui.hud('best', best === null ? null : `Best ${best.toFixed(1)} s`, { at: 'top-left' });\\n  const end = state === 'won' ? 'Every gem! Enter: play again' : 'Time! Enter: play again';\\n  ui.hud('end', ended ? end : null, { at: 'top' });\\n}\\n\\nengine = await createEngine({\\n  canvas: document.querySelector<HTMLCanvasElement>('#view')!,\\n90→  scenes: [play.id],\\n  levels: { 'level:arena': { text: ARENA_TEXT, file: 'labs/game/scenes/play.ts' } },\\n  replays,\\n  search: `?${search}`,\\n  store,\\n  modal: () => paused !== null,\\n  onFrame: (frame) => {\\n    pauseMenu(frame.dt);\\n    showRound(frame);\\n  },\\n100→});\\n\\naddEventListener('keydown', (event) => {\\n  const inspector = engine?.inspector;\\n  if (event.code === 'Enter' && ended && inspector) inspector.seed(inspector.seed() + 1);\\n});\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The starter game's page (labs/game/index.html): it starts the engine (`createEngine`, engine/app/engine.ts) on\\n * the scene `game:play` (labs/game/scenes/play.ts) with the arena's text registered for the view, offers the bot's\\n * replay to `?replay=bot`, and shows the round each drawn frame in the HTML/CSS overlay's HUD: the gems, the clock,\\n * the controls, the best round kept across sessions (labs/game/best.ts, through the engine's store) and, when the\\n * round ends, how it ended. Enter then starts a new round on the next seed. Escape (or the pad's Start) pauses the\\n * round under a menu (`createMenu`: Resume, New round), which keeps its keys out of play while it is open\\n * (`createEngine({ modal })`); the store keeps the best round and any keys rebound (`createEngine({ store })`). The\\n * camera is the chase camera unless the URL names one (`?cam=iso`, `?cam3=orbit`).\\n10→ *\\n * Everything else a page does (routes, the renderer, the frame loop, the devices, `window.__engine`, the error\\n * overlay, the touch controls) is the engine's, so this file is the game's own presentation only. It reads the run\\n * and never changes it: the HUD cannot change the hash.\\n *\\n * Game code: it imports only the engine's public API (engine/index.ts) and the game's own files.\\n *\\n * Open it at http://127.0.0.1:5173/labs/game/ (`npm run dev`): `?seed=7&game.gems=20` plays another round,\\n * `?replay=bot` the bot's, `?cam=iso` another camera. Headless, `node x shot labs/game` reports what it draws.\\n */\\n20→/// <reference types=\\\"vite/client\\\" />\\nimport { createEngine, createMenu, createStore, type Engine, type EngineFrame, type Menu } from '../../engine';\\nimport { bestOf, recordBest } from './best';\\nimport { ARENA_TEXT, play, type Round } from './scenes/play';\\n\\n/** The page's query, with the chase camera when it names none: it follows the player round the arena. */\\nconst search = new URLSearchParams(location.search);\\nif (!search.has('cam') && !search.has('cam3')) search.set('cam3', 'chase');\\n\\n/** The game's replays, by name (`?replay=bot`), as text loaded on demand. */\\n30→const replays = { bot: () => import('./replays/bot.replay.json?raw').then((module) => module.default) };\\n\\n/** The started engine; null until `createEngine` resolves (its first frames are drawn before that). */\\nlet engine: Engine | null = null;\\n\\n/** Whether the round on screen has ended, so Enter starts the next. */\\nlet ended = false;\\n\\n/** The game's store: its best round across sessions; a replay's page plays in its demo mode, so it sets none. */\\nconst store = createStore({ prefix: 'my3dge-game:', mode: search.has('replay') ? 'demo' : 'play' });\\n40→\\n/** The fastest won round kept (s), and the run whose clock the page saw running, with the steps it started with. */\\nlet best = bestOf(store);\\nlet seen: { world: object; steps: number } | null = null;\\n\\n/** The pause menu while it is open; null while the round plays. */\\nlet paused: Menu | null = null;\\n\\n/** Opens the pause menu over the paused round, or reads it a frame: Resume (or Escape again), New round. */\\nfunction pauseMenu(dt: number): void {\\n50→  const [inspector, ui, input] = [engine?.inspector, engine?.ui, engine?.input];\\n  if (!inspector || !ui || !input) return;\\n  const close = () => {\\n    paused?.remove();\\n    paused = null;\\n    inspector.resume();\\n  };\\n  if (paused) return void paused.update(dt);\\n  if (!input.pressed('pause')) return;\\n  inspector.pause();\\n60→  const items = [\\n    { label: 'Resume', id: 'resume' },\\n    { label: 'New round', id: 'new' },\\n  ];\\n  paused = createMenu(ui.root, items, { input, id: 'pause', title: 'Paused', onCancel: close, onPick: (_i, item) => {\\n    if (typeof item === 'object' && item.id === 'new') inspector.seed(inspector.seed() + 1);\\n    close();\\n  } }); // prettier-ignore\\n}\\n\\n70→/** Shows the round in the HUD: the gems, the clock, the controls, and how the round ended. */\\nfunction showRound({ world }: EngineFrame): void {\\n  const ui = engine?.ui;\\n  const entity = world.query('round')[0] as unknown as { round: Round } | undefined;\\n  if (!ui || !entity) return;\\n  const { gems, collected, left, state } = entity.round;\\n  if (seen?.world !== world) seen = state === 'playing' ? { world, steps: left + world.tick } : null;\\n  const was = ended;\\n  ui.hud('gems', `Gems ${collected} / ${gems}`, { at: 'top-left' });\\n  ui.hud('clock', `${Math.ceil(left / world.hz)} s`, { at: 'top-right', color: left < 10 * world.hz ? '#ff8f6b' : '' });\\n80→  ui.hud('keys', 'WASD: run · Space: jump · Shift: dash · Esc: pause', { at: 'bottom', keys: true });\\n  ended = state !== 'playing';\\n  if (ended && !was && state === 'won' && seen) best = recordBest(store, (seen.steps - left) / world.hz);\\n  ui.hud('best', best === null ? null : `Best ${best.toFixed(1)} s`, { at: 'top-left' });\\n  const end = state === 'won' ? 'Every gem! Enter: play again' : 'Time! Enter: play again';\\n  ui.hud('end', ended ? end : null, { at: 'top' });\\n}\\n\\nengine = await createEngine({\\n  canvas: document.querySelector<HTMLCanvasElement>('#view')!,\\n90→  scenes: [play.id],\\n  levels: { 'level:arena': { text: ARENA_TEXT, file: 'labs/game/scenes/play.ts' } },\\n  replays,\\n  search: `?${search}`,\\n  store,\\n  modal: () => paused !== null,\\n  onFrame: (frame) => {\\n    pauseMenu(frame.dt);\\n    showRound(frame);\\n  },\\n100→});\\n\\naddEventListener('keydown', (event) => {\\n  const inspector = engine?.inspector;\\n  if (event.code === 'Enter' && ended && inspector) inspector.seed(inspector.seed() + 1);\\n});\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/main.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file The starter game's page (labs/game/index.html): it starts the engine (`createEngine`, engine/app/engine.ts) on\\n * the scene `game:play` (labs/game/scenes/play.ts) with the arena's text registered for the view, offers the bot's\\n * replay to `?replay=bot`, and shows the round each drawn frame in the HTML/CSS overlay's HUD: the gems, the clock,\\n * the controls, the best round kept across sessions (labs/game/best.ts, through the engine's store) and, when the\\n * round ends, how it ended. Enter then starts a new round on the next seed. Escape (or the pad's Start) pauses the\\n * round under a menu (`createMenu`: Resume, New round), which keeps its keys out of play while it is open\\n * (`createEngine({ modal })`); the store keeps the best round and any keys rebound (`createEngine({ store })`). The\\n * camera is the chase camera unless the URL names one (`?cam=iso`, `?cam3=orbit`).\\n *\\n * Everything else a page does (routes, the renderer, the frame loop, the devices, `window.__engine`, the error\\n * overlay, the touch controls) is the engine's, so this file is the game's own presentation only. It reads the run\\n * and never changes it: the HUD cannot change the hash.\\n *\\n * Game code: it imports only the engine's public API (engine/index.ts) and the game's own files.\\n *\\n * Open it at http://127.0.0.1:5173/labs/game/ (`npm run dev`): `?seed=7&game.gems=20` plays another round,\\n * `?replay=bot` the bot's, `?cam=iso` another camera. Headless, `node x shot labs/game` reports what it draws.\\n */\\n/// <reference types=\\\"vite/client\\\" />\\nimport { createEngine, createMenu, createStore, type Engine, type EngineFrame, type Menu } from '../../engine';\\nimport { bestOf, recordBest } from './best';\\nimport { ARENA_TEXT, play, type Round } from './scenes/play';\\n\\n/** The page's query, with the chase camera when it names none: it follows the player round the arena. */\\nconst search = new URLSearchParams(location.search);\\nif (!search.has('cam') && !search.has('cam3')) search.set('cam3', 'chase');\\n\\n/** The game's replays, by name (`?replay=bot`), as text loaded on demand. */\\nconst replays = { bot: () => import('./replays/bot.replay.json?raw').then((module) => module.default) };\\n\\n/** The started engine; null until `createEngine` resolves (its first frames are drawn before that). */\\nlet engine: Engine | null = null;\\n\\n/** Whether the round on screen has ended, so Enter starts the next. */\\nlet ended = false;\\n\\n/** The game's store: its best round across sessions; a replay's page plays in its demo mode, so it sets none. */\\nconst store = createStore({ prefix: 'my3dge-game:', mode: search.has('replay') ? 'demo' : 'play' });\\n\\n/** The fastest won round kept (s), and the run whose clock the page saw running, with the steps it started with. */\\nlet best = bestOf(store);\\nlet seen: { world: object; steps: number } | null = null;\\n\\n/** The pause menu while it is open; null while the round plays. */\\nlet paused: Menu | null = null;\\n\\n/** Opens the pause menu over the paused round, or reads it a frame: Resume (or Escape again), New round. */\\nfunction pauseMenu(dt: number): void {\\n  const [inspector, ui, input] = [engine?.inspector, engine?.ui, engine?.input];\\n  if (!inspector || !ui || !input) return;\\n  const close = () => {\\n    paused?.remove();\\n    paused = null;\\n    inspector.resume();\\n  };\\n  if (paused) return void paused.update(dt);\\n  if (!input.pressed('pause')) return;\\n  inspector.pause();\\n  const items = [\\n    { label: 'Resume', id: 'resume' },\\n    { label: 'New round', id: 'new' },\\n  ];\\n  paused = createMenu(ui.root, items, { input, id: 'pause', title: 'Paused', onCancel: close, onPick: (_i, item) => {\\n    if (typeof item === 'object' && item.id === 'new') inspector.seed(inspector.seed() + 1);\\n    close();\\n  } }); // prettier-ignore\\n}\\n\\n/** Shows the round in the HUD: the gems, the clock, the controls, and how the round ended. */\\nfunction showRound({ world }: EngineFrame): void {\\n  const ui = engine?.ui;\\n  const entity = world.query('round')[0] as unknown as { round: Round } | undefined;\\n  if (!ui || !entity) return;\\n  const { gems, collected, left, state } = entity.round;\\n  if (seen?.world !== world) seen = state === 'playing' ? { world, steps: left + world.tick } : null;\\n  const was = ended;\\n  ui.hud('gems', `Gems ${collected} / ${gems}`, { at: 'top-left' });\\n  ui.hud('clock', `${Math.ceil(left / world.hz)} s`, { at: 'top-right', color: left < 10 * world.hz ? '#ff8f6b' : '' });\\n  ui.hud('keys', 'WASD: run · Space: jump · Shift: dash · Esc: pause', { at: 'bottom', keys: true });\\n  ended = state !== 'playing';\\n  if (ended && !was && state === 'won' && seen) best = recordBest(store, (seen.steps - left) / world.hz);\\n  ui.hud('best', best === null ? null : `Best ${best.toFixed(1)} s`, { at: 'top-left' });\\n  const end = state === 'won' ? 'Every gem! Enter: play again' : 'Time! Enter: play again';\\n  ui.hud('end', ended ? end : null, { at: 'top' });\\n}\\n\\nengine = await createEngine({\\n  canvas: document.querySelector<HTMLCanvasElement>('#view')!,\\n  scenes: [play.id],\\n  levels: { 'level:arena': { text: ARENA_TEXT, file: 'labs/game/scenes/play.ts' } },\\n  replays,\\n  search: `?${search}`,\\n  store,\\n  modal: () => paused !== null,\\n  onFrame: (frame) => {\\n    pauseMenu(frame.dt);\\n    showRound(frame);\\n  },\\n});\\n\\naddEventListener('keydown', (event) => {\\n  const inspector = engine?.inspector;\\n  if (event.code === 'Enter' && ended && inspector) inspector.seed(inspector.seed() + 1);\\n});\\n\",\"total_lines\":105}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f7183990-c508-4d93-8845-14890ee832c5-5","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→<!doctype html>\\n<html lang=\\\"en\\\">\\n  <head>\\n    <meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\" />\\n    <meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, maximum-scale=1, user-scalable=no\\\" />\\n    <meta name=\\\"theme-color\\\" content=\\\"#15171c\\\" />\\n    <link rel=\\\"stylesheet\\\" href=\\\"../../engine/ui/touch.css\\\" />\\n    <link rel=\\\"icon\\\" href=\\\"data:,\\\" />\\n    <title>The starter game: my-3dge</title>\\n10→    <!--\\n      The starter game's page (labs/game/README.md): labs/game/main.ts starts the engine on the scene game:play and\\n      shows the round in the HUD. Ready or error: until the engine publishes window.__engine, the inline script below\\n      records a script that fails to load or throws, and shows it in #msg, so a broken page is one line of text,\\n      never a blank one; `node x shot labs/game` reports the same headless.\\n    -->\\n    <style>\\n      html,\\n      body {\\n        margin: 0;\\n20→        height: 100%;\\n        overflow: hidden;\\n        background: #15171c;\\n      }\\n      canvas {\\n        display: block;\\n        width: 100vw;\\n        height: 100vh;\\n        height: 100dvh;\\n        outline: none;\\n30→        touch-action: none;\\n      }\\n      #msg {\\n        position: fixed;\\n        inset: 0;\\n        display: flex;\\n        align-items: center;\\n        justify-content: center;\\n        padding: 24px;\\n        font:\\n40→          18px system-ui,\\n          sans-serif;\\n        color: #c9ccd4;\\n        text-align: center;\\n        white-space: pre-line;\\n        pointer-events: none;\\n      }\\n      #msg[hidden] {\\n        display: none;\\n      }\\n50→    </style>\\n    <script>\\n      window.__engine = { ready: false, errors: [] };\\n      function gameFailed(message) {\\n        if (!window.__engine || typeof window.__engine.help === 'function') return; // the engine reports now\\n        var fix = 'the console names the cause; node x shot labs/game reports it headless';\\n        var record = { code: 'APP_START', message: 'the page failed to start: ' + message, fix: fix };\\n        if (window.__engine.errors.le