-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"0f546f76-9a66-4b15-a3e9-a9c430f31f91"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_224","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"screenRay, defineActionMap, defineSfx, and createAudio are exported from input/api and audio/api.\n\nChecking inspector and EngineFrame types for safe API calls. Planning the first file, labs/game/input/map.ts, with use and gift actions mapped to mouse, keyboard, and pad inputs.\n\nThe action map now includes syringe, drop, sitePrev, siteNext, hint, swap, precision, paddle, radial, toolPrev, toolNext, move, and pause. Escape and PadStart are reserved for system pause. Next is labs/game/input/hands.ts to poll and build hands.\n\nThe hands.ts file will poll up to four pads and assign keyboard or mouse to seat 0. Edge pulses trigger gift, drop, swap, hint, paddle, and site actions. Use is held, radial comes from the right stick or mouse right button, and cursor integration is included. The file stays under 400 lines.\n\nglyphs.ts will hold SVG prompt strings. shell.ts renders the campaign into a root element with data attributes. hud.ts handles the operation HUD.\n\nSession.ts will hold hub protocol types and host or client tick logic. Interview.ts will contain the interview object. A boot file will wire everything together. Voice.ts will play animalese via audio oscillators using existing syllable indexes. The page voice can stay simple. index.html needs a rewrite. Tools are also planned. A bug was spotted: boardIds currently pushes 'case:first-cut' twice during free surgery.\n\nThe duplicate 'case:first-cut' bug will be fixed by replacing it with a 'free:surgery' sentinel. openBoard will treat IDs starting with 'free' as free-play mode, allowing the player to browse cleared cases without recording progress. The board UI displays one card at a time with left and right navigation.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-467755cc-8c16-48da-b404-bd5ed4a8c547-50","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/PLAN.md","offset":243,"limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-467755cc-8c16-48da-b404-bd5ed4a8c547-51","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/dev/inspector.ts","offset":1,"limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-467755cc-8c16-48da-b404-bd5ed4a8c547-52","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"interface Inspector|set\\(|seed\\(|timeScale|camera:|actions:|pause\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/dev/inspector.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-467755cc-8c16-48da-b404-bd5ed4a8c547-53","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"camera:","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/app/drawing.ts"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1312,"output_tokens":1200,"cache_read_input_tokens":92928,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"54bd93d5-cad1-4275-846e-6e06138c3bf9"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-467755cc-8c16-48da-b404-bd5ed4a8c547-50","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"243→## 8. The cases\\n\\nEight cases, 35 to 50 minutes for a first run, then **Free Surgery**. Each adds one new rule, so the demo shows everything\\nthe game does. Phases are data (§17.5) and each phase is a checkpoint. \\\"AI\\\" means the AI colleague is present.\\n\\n| # | Title | Surgeon | Patient | Site(s) | Limit | New here |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n250→| 1 | First Cut | Wren | Tomás Reyes, 52, harbor pilot; glass from a deck hatch | Chest | 4:00 | Cursor, radial, Drain, Forceps, Suture, Syringe, Gel |\\n| 2 | The Quiet Lump | Wren | Gwen Abara, 34, trumpet player; an old graft scar | Abdomen | 4:30 | Scalpel, Scanner, Laser |\\n| 3 | Crosstalk | Wren | Hal Minsky, 58, bus driver; crash on Breakwater Road | Liver, Lung, Arm | 5:00 | Sites, Code, Stillpoint |\\n| 4 | It Moves | Wren | Gwen again, in crisis | Abdomen | 5:30 | LULL, Binder |\\n| 5 | Struck Off | Sabine, AI | \\\"Big Ana\\\" Duarte, stevedore | Abdomen, on a ship | 5:30 | Flaps, SOLACE, Second Pulse, ship roll hazard |\\n| 6 | Reverie | Both, Swap | Chief Achterberg | Chest, Abdomen | 6:00 | REVERIE, decoys, Swap, Consult |\\n| 7 | Gala Night | Both, AI | Three donors, three tables | Tables A, B, C | 6:30 | BALM, one vitals bar per patient |\\n| 8 | Mercy | Both, AI | Dr. Lucan Voss | Heart | 8:00 | MERCY, every tool |\\n\\n**Phases.**\\n260→\\n1. **First Cut** (vitals start at 70; no Gift). Clear 3 pools, with Odie teaching cursor, use and the radial → pull 4 shards → scripted dip to 40,\\n   teach the Stabilizer → stitch 3 lacerations → gel and close.\\n2. **The Quiet Lump** (85). Curved 7 m incision → laser its tiny bleeders → scan to find a buried mass and 3 nodules, laser the\\n   nodules → loop-cut the mass, lift it with forceps. **It flinches.** Drama Cut. → stitch and gel.\\n3. **Crosstalk** (60). Each site has 2 wounds and a pool; triage while the others bleed → scripted flatline when the first site\\n   closes: teach the Code → 3 arterial bleeds at once, no time left: time slows, teach the pulse-lock, Wren discovers\\n   Stillpoint → close across all sites.\\n4. **It Moves** (75). Reopen → 3 Lulls in silence, numb patches, the Chief mocking from the gallery → cocoons, tears →\\n   the Matron → close.\\n270→5. **Struck Off** (70). Lift and clip a flap; Solace beneath → split and burn generation by generation → **the storm hits**: the\\n   ship rolls every 7 s (camera tilts up to 6°, cursor drifts, instruments slide); teach Second Pulse → Mother Solace under\\n   the flap, Wren holding it → close, still rolling.\\n6. **Reverie** (65). Two incisions, one on each site, swapping surgeons → hunt with the Scanner, 3 exposures → decoy storm, listen\\n   for the beat → the Reverie under the heart flap; Consult → close.\\n7. **Gala Night** (each table 80). Three bleeding patients while Balm spreads; a Code allowed once per patient; losing any patient fails\\n   the case → Nodes on every table → a final closing race. Voss's speech keeps playing on a big screen throughout.\\n8. **Mercy** (100). Open → the three-phase boss of §7 → close. Odie's moral line before it; see §9.\\n\\n**Session case, \\\"The Gala Shift\\\"** (`case:gala-shift`; §16). Not in the story. 4:30 limit. Two patients, wounds, shards, a Lull, a Balm\\n280→Node, one flap. Ends when both are closed (won) or one dies or time runs out (lost). Playable also from Free Surgery for couch play.\\n\\n**Free Surgery.** After a case is finished, it is on the Board for score attack on any unlocked difficulty, best rank kept, with\\nSecond Pulse or Stillpoint selectable. Attending and ★ unlock after the ending.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. World, cast, story and writing\\n\\n**Port Verity**, a rain-lashed harbour city; **Harbor Light General**, its hospital, with a lighthouse for a logo. Near future.\\n290→**Halcyon Biosciences** sells \\\"Halcyon grafts\\\": a miracle patch that heals anything, adored by everyone, ads on every ward TV.\\nTagline: **\\\"Halcyon. Because you deserve to feel nothing.\\\"** The ad has a jingle. The trials were skipped, and the grafts\\nare alive.\",\"content_concise\":\"243→## 8. The cases\\n\\nEight cases, 35 to 50 minutes for a first run, then **Free Surgery**. Each adds one new rule, so the demo shows everything\\nthe game does. Phases are data (§17.5) and each phase is a checkpoint. \\\"AI\\\" means the AI colleague is present.\\n\\n| # | Title | Surgeon | Patient | Site(s) | Limit | New here |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n250→| 1 | First Cut | Wren | Tomás Reyes, 52, harbor pilot; glass from a deck hatch | Chest | 4:00 | Cursor, radial, Drain, Forceps, Suture, Syringe, Gel |\\n| 2 | The Quiet Lump | Wren | Gwen Abara, 34, trumpet player; an old graft scar | Abdomen | 4:30 | Scalpel, Scanner, Laser |\\n| 3 | Crosstalk | Wren | Hal Minsky, 58, bus driver; crash on Breakwater Road | Liver, Lung, Arm | 5:00 | Sites, Code, Stillpoint |\\n| 4 | It Moves | Wren | Gwen again, in crisis | Abdomen | 5:30 | LULL, Binder |\\n| 5 | Struck Off | Sabine, AI | \\\"Big Ana\\\" Duarte, stevedore | Abdomen, on a ship | 5:30 | Flaps, SOLACE, Second Pulse, ship roll hazard |\\n| 6 | Reverie | Both, Swap | Chief Achterberg | Chest, Abdomen | 6:00 | REVERIE, decoys, Swap, Consult |\\n| 7 | Gala Night | Both, AI | Three donors, three tables | Tables A, B, C | 6:30 | BALM, one vitals bar per patient |\\n| 8 | Mercy | Both, AI | Dr. Lucan Voss | Heart | 8:00 | MERCY, every tool |\\n\\n**Phases.**\\n260→\\n1. **First Cut** (vitals start at 70; no Gift). Clear 3 pools, with Odie teaching cursor, use and the radial → pull 4 shards → scripted dip to 40,\\n   teach the Stabilizer → stitch 3 lacerations → gel and close.\\n2. **The Quiet Lump** (85). Curved 7 m incision → laser its tiny bleeders → scan to find a buried mass and 3 nodules, laser the\\n   nodules → loop-cut the mass, lift it with forceps. **It flinches.** Drama Cut. → stitch and gel.\\n3. **Crosstalk** (60). Each site has 2 wounds and a pool; triage while the others bleed → scripted flatline when the first site\\n   closes: teach the Code → 3 arterial bleeds at once, no time left: time slows, teach the pulse-lock, Wren discovers\\n   Stillpoint → close across all sites.\\n4. **It Moves** (75). Reopen → 3 Lulls in silence, numb patches, the Chief mocking from the gallery → cocoons, tears →\\n   the Matron → close.\\n270→5. **Struck Off** (70). Lift and clip a flap; Solace beneath → split and burn generation by generation → **the storm hits**: the\\n   ship rolls every 7 s (camera tilts up to 6°, cursor drifts, instruments slide); teach Second Pulse → Mother Solace under\\n   the flap, Wren holding it → close, still rolling.\\n6. **Reverie** (65). Two incisions, one on each site, swapping surgeons → hunt with the Scanner, 3 exposures → decoy storm, listen\\n   for the beat → the Reverie under the heart flap; Consult → close.\\n7. **Gala Night** (each table 80). Three bleeding patients while Balm spreads; a Code allowed once per patient; losing any patient fails\\n   the case → Nodes on every table → a final closing race. Voss's speech keeps playing on a big screen throughout.\\n8. **Mercy** (100). Open → the three-phase boss of §7 → close. Odie's moral line before it; see §9.\\n\\n**Session case, \\\"The Gala Shift\\\"** (`case:gala-shift`; §16). Not in the story. 4:30 limit. Two patients, wounds, shards, a Lull, a Balm\\n280→Node, one flap. Ends when both are closed (won) or one dies or time runs out (lost). Playable also from Free Surgery for couch play.\\n\\n**Free Surgery.** After a case is finished, it is on the Board for score attack on any unlocked difficulty, best rank kept, with\\nSecond Pulse or Stillpoint selectable. Attending and ★ unlock after the ending.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. World, cast, story and writing\\n\\n**Port Verity**, a rain-lashed harbour city; **Harbor Light General**, its hospital, with a lighthouse for a logo. Near future.\\n290→**Halcyon Biosciences** sells \\\"Halcyon grafts\\\": a miracle patch that heals anything, adored by everyone, ads on every ward TV.\\nTagline: **\\\"Halcyon. Because you deserve to feel nothing.\\\"** The ad has a jingle. The trials were skipped, and the grafts\\nare alive.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":243,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"## 8. The cases\\n\\nEight cases, 35 to 50 minutes for a first run, then **Free Surgery**. Each adds one new rule, so the demo shows everything\\nthe game does. Phases are data (§17.5) and each phase is a checkpoint. \\\"AI\\\" means the AI colleague is present.\\n\\n| # | Title | Surgeon | Patient | Site(s) | Limit | New here |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| 1 | First Cut | Wren | Tomás Reyes, 52, harbor pilot; glass from a deck hatch | Chest | 4:00 | Cursor, radial, Drain, Forceps, Suture, Syringe, Gel |\\n| 2 | The Quiet Lump | Wren | Gwen Abara, 34, trumpet player; an old graft scar | Abdomen | 4:30 | Scalpel, Scanner, Laser |\\n| 3 | Crosstalk | Wren | Hal Minsky, 58, bus driver; crash on Breakwater Road | Liver, Lung, Arm | 5:00 | Sites, Code, Stillpoint |\\n| 4 | It Moves | Wren | Gwen again, in crisis | Abdomen | 5:30 | LULL, Binder |\\n| 5 | Struck Off | Sabine, AI | \\\"Big Ana\\\" Duarte, stevedore | Abdomen, on a ship | 5:30 | Flaps, SOLACE, Second Pulse, ship roll hazard |\\n| 6 | Reverie | Both, Swap | Chief Achterberg | Chest, Abdomen | 6:00 | REVERIE, decoys, Swap, Consult |\\n| 7 | Gala Night | Both, AI | Three donors, three tables | Tables A, B, C | 6:30 | BALM, one vitals bar per patient |\\n| 8 | Mercy | Both, AI | Dr. Lucan Voss | Heart | 8:00 | MERCY, every tool |\\n\\n**Phases.**\\n\\n1. **First Cut** (vitals start at 70; no Gift). Clear 3 pools, with Odie teaching cursor, use and the radial → pull 4 shards → scripted dip to 40,\\n   teach the Stabilizer → stitch 3 lacerations → gel and close.\\n2. **The Quiet Lump** (85). Curved 7 m incision → laser its tiny bleeders → scan to find a buried mass and 3 nodules, laser the\\n   nodules → loop-cut the mass, lift it with forceps. **It flinches.** Drama Cut. → stitch and gel.\\n3. **Crosstalk** (60). Each site has 2 wounds and a pool; triage while the others bleed → scripted flatline when the first site\\n   closes: teach the Code → 3 arterial bleeds at once, no time left: time slows, teach the pulse-lock, Wren discovers\\n   Stillpoint → close across all sites.\\n4. **It Moves** (75). Reopen → 3 Lulls in silence, numb patches, the Chief mocking from the gallery → cocoons, tears →\\n   the Matron → close.\\n5. **Struck Off** (70). Lift and clip a flap; Solace beneath → split and burn generation by generation → **the storm hits**: the\\n   ship rolls every 7 s (camera tilts up to 6°, cursor drifts, instruments slide); teach Second Pulse → Mother Solace under\\n   the flap, Wren holding it → close, still rolling.\\n6. **Reverie** (65). Two incisions, one on each site, swapping surgeons → hunt with the Scanner, 3 exposures → decoy storm, listen\\n   for the beat → the Reverie under the heart flap; Consult → close.\\n7. **Gala Night** (each table 80). Three bleeding patients while Balm spreads; a Code allowed once per patient; losing any patient fails\\n   the case → Nodes on every table → a final closing race. Voss's speech keeps playing on a big screen throughout.\\n8. **Mercy** (100). Open → the three-phase boss of §7 → close. Odie's moral line before it; see §9.\\n\\n**Session case, \\\"The Gala Shift\\\"** (`case:gala-shift`; §16). Not in the story. 4:30 limit. Two patients, wounds, shards, a Lull, a Balm\\nNode, one flap. Ends when both are closed (won) or one dies or time runs out (lost). Playable also from Free Surgery for couch play.\\n\\n**Free Surgery.** After a case is finished, it is on the Board for score attack on any unlocked difficulty, best rank kept, with\\nSecond Pulse or Stillpoint selectable. Attending and ★ unlock after the ending.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. World, cast, story and writing\\n\\n**Port Verity**, a rain-lashed harbour city; **Harbor Light General**, its hospital, with a lighthouse for a logo. Near future.\\n**Halcyon Biosciences** sells \\\"Halcyon grafts\\\": a miracle patch that heals anything, adored by everyone, ads on every ward TV.\\nTagline: **\\\"Halcyon. Because you deserve to feel nothing.\\\"** The ad has a jingle. The trials were skipped, and the grafts\\nare alive.\\n\",\"total_lines\":952}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-467755cc-8c16-48da-b404-bd5ed4a8c547-51","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The inspector (PLAN.md §8.3, WP 1.6; doctrines: Agent-operable, Verifiable): `window.__engine` in a page and\\n * the object `createHeadless` returns in Node are one API, which `createInspector` assembles from the entries of the\\n * registry kind `inspectorMember` (engine/dev/members.ts). Later WPs add members from their own files; this module\\n * registers the core ones and never names another.\\n *\\n * A member is a call (`step(n, intents)`) or, with `value: true`, a property read without one (`errors`); a dotted\\n * name (`scene.dump`) is a call on a namespace object. A call checks its arguments against the member's schema\\n * (`DEV_BAD_ARGS` naming each problem and the signature, before anything happens), then runs `impl(host, ...args)`\\n10→ * with the arguments as given (absent ones as their default). A member that `needs: 'renderer'` throws\\n * `DEV_NO_RENDERER` on a host without one, as `createHeadless` is. The core members map onto the kernel: `describe`\\n * → the registry; `set` → the settings store through the session (text typed as `x set` types it, non-view changes\\n * recorded); `errors` and `advice` → the log; `pause`, `resume`, `step` and `timeScale` → the clock (steps recorded\\n * in the session); `capture` and `restore` → the session (a restore takes the recording back with the sim, and\\n * refuses a capture this run did not take or one changed since: engine/sim/scene.ts); `state`, `hash`, `trace`,\\n * `entities` and `get` → the world, read-only (a query names an undeclared component with the closest); `seed(n)`\\n * starts the scene again. Every member that changes the sim goes through the session (engine/dev/members.ts).\\n *\\n * Invariants: the object holds its members and nothing else, so `help()` lists exactly what it has (`x docs --check`\\n20→ * compares them, tools/lib/docsHelp.ts), and the core table is typed against `Inspector`, so tsc refuses a core member\\n * missing, extra or renamed. Members are read from `host.members` when the inspector is made: register before.\\n * Results are plain data, copied (a capture is the session's own object, so it restores in place).\\n *\\n * @example\\n * import { createRegistry } from '../core/registry';\\n * import { defineMember, type InspectorHost } from './members';\\n * const members = createRegistry();\\n * const times = { type: 'integer', default: 1, minimum: 1, description: 'How often.' } as const;\\n * defineMember('ping', { help: 'Answers pong.', args: { times }, impl: (_h, n: number) => 'pong'.repeat(n) }, members);\\n30→ * const engine = createInspector({ members } as unknown as InspectorHost);\\n * (engine.ping as (n?: number) => string)(2); // 'pongpong'; ping(0) throws DEV_BAD_ARGS\\n * @see engine/dev/inspector.test.ts\\n */\\nimport pkg from '../../package.json' with { type: 'json' };\\nimport { codeError, defineCodes, type AdviceRecord, type ErrorRecord } from '../core/log';\\nimport { checkValue, copyValue, listProblems, show, type Problem } from '../core/schema';\\nimport { createSettings, type SettingChange } from '../core/settings';\\nimport type { Intents } from '../input/intents';\\nimport type { WorldCapture } from '../sim/capture';\\n40→import type { EntityData, WorldState, WorldTrace } from '../sim/state';\\nimport {\\n  defineMember,\\n  helpText,\\n  memberKind,\\n  signatureOf,\\n  type InspectorHost,\\n  type Member,\\n  type MemberSpec,\\n} from './members';\\n50→\\n/** The codes this module raises, with their fixes. */\\nexport const INSPECTOR_CODES = defineCodes('dev', {\\n  DEV_NO_RENDERER: {\\n    template: '__engine.{member} needs a renderer, and this engine has none ({runtime}, headless)',\\n    fix: 'call it in a page started with createEngine (WP 2.7); headless, read state(), entities(), get(id) and hash() instead',\\n  },\\n  DEV_BAD_ARGS: {\\n    template: '__engine.{member}: {problems}',\\n    fix: 'call it as {signature}; __engine.help({name}) lists its arguments',\\n60→    doc: 'Raised by every `__engine` member (engine/dev/inspector.ts) before it runs, when an argument does not match the schema its member declares: a wrong type, a value out of range, a missing required argument or one too many. Nothing has happened yet.',\\n  },\\n});\\n\\n/** What `info()` reports: the engine's identity and health, and the run. */\\nexport interface EngineInfo {\\n  version: string;\\n  runtime: string;\\n  headless: boolean;\\n  adapter: Readonly<Record<string, unknown>> | null;\\n70→  features: string[];\\n  downgrades: string[];\\n  /** The runtime dependencies and their pinned versions. */\\n  deps: Record<string, string>;\\n  scene: string;\\n  seed: number;\\n  tick: number;\\n  hz: number;\\n}\\n\\n80→/** One entity as `entities()` lists it: its id and the components it holds. */\\nexport interface EntitySummary {\\n  id: number;\\n  components: string[];\\n}\\n\\n/** The inspector, `window.__engine` in a page and what `createHeadless` returns: `help()` lists every member. */\\nexport interface Inspector {\\n  info(): EngineInfo;\\n  pause(): void;\\n90→  resume(): void;\\n  step(n?: number, intents?: Intents | readonly Intents[]): number;\\n  timeScale(k?: number): number;\\n  seed(n?: number): number;\\n  state(query?: string | readonly string[]): WorldState;\\n  hash(): string;\\n  trace(): WorldTrace;\\n  entities(query?: string | readonly string[]): EntitySummary[];\\n  get(id: number): EntityData | null;\\n  set(path: string, value: unknown): SettingChange;\\n100→  capture(): WorldCapture;\\n  restore(capture: WorldCapture): void;\\n  describe(kind?: string, id?: string): unknown;\\n  help(member?: string): string;\\n  readonly errors: readonly ErrorRecord[];\\n  readonly advice: readonly AdviceRecord[];\\n  /** The members later WPs register (`input`, `stats`, `scene.dump`…). */\\n  [member: string]: unknown;\\n}\\n\\n110→/** Throws `DEV_BAD_ARGS` for `member` with these problems. */\\nfunction badArgs(member: string, problems: string, signature: string): never {\\n  throw codeError('DEV_BAD_ARGS', { member, problems, signature, name: show(member) });\\n}\\n\\n/** Runs a member on `host`: the renderer check, the argument checks, then `impl` with the arguments as given. */\\nfunction call(host: InspectorHost, member: Member, args: readonly unknown[]): unknown {\\n  if (member.needs === 'renderer' && !host.renderer) {\\n    throw codeError('DEV_NO_RENDERER', { member: member.id, runtime: host.runtime });\\n  }\\n120→  const fields = Object.entries(member.args);\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The inspector (PLAN.md §8.3, WP 1.6; doctrines: Agent-operable, Verifiable): `window.__engine` in a page and\\n * the object `createHeadless` returns in Node are one API, which `createInspector` assembles from the entries of the\\n * registry kind `inspectorMember` (engine/dev/members.ts). Later WPs add members from their own files; this module\\n * registers the core ones and never names another.\\n *\\n * A member is a call (`step(n, intents)`) or, with `value: true`, a property read without one (`errors`); a dotted\\n * name (`scene.dump`) is a call on a namespace object. A call checks its arguments against the member's schema\\n * (`DEV_BAD_ARGS` naming each problem and the signature, before anything happens), then runs `impl(host, ...args)`\\n10→ * with the arguments as given (absent ones as their default). A member that `needs: 'renderer'` throws\\n * `DEV_NO_RENDERER` on a host without one, as `createHeadless` is. The core members map onto the kernel: `describe`\\n * → the registry; `set` → the settings store through the session (text typed as `x set` types it, non-view changes\\n * recorded); `errors` and `advice` → the log; `pause`, `resume`, `step` and `timeScale` → the clock (steps recorded\\n * in the session); `capture` and `restore` → the session (a restore takes the recording back with the sim, and\\n * refuses a capture this run did not take or one changed since: engine/sim/scene.ts); `state`, `hash`, `trace`,\\n * `entities` and `get` → the world, read-only (a query names an undeclared component with the closest); `seed(n)`\\n * starts the scene again. Every member that changes the sim goes through the session (engine/dev/members.ts).\\n *\\n * Invariants: the object holds its members and nothing else, so `help()` lists exactly what it has (`x docs --check`\\n20→ * compares them, tools/lib/docsHelp.ts), and the core table is typed against `Inspector`, so tsc refuses a core member\\n * missing, extra or renamed. Members are read from `host.members` when the inspector is made: register before.\\n * Results are plain data, copied (a capture is the session's own object, so it restores in place).\\n *\\n * @example\\n * import { createRegistry } from '../core/registry';\\n * import { defineMember, type InspectorHost } from './members';\\n * const members = createRegistry();\\n * const times = { type: 'integer', default: 1, minimum: 1, description: 'How often.' } as const;\\n * defineMember('ping', { help: 'Answers pong.', args: { times }, impl: (_h, n: number) => 'pong'.repeat(n) }, members);\\n30→ * const engine = createInspector({ members } as unknown as InspectorHost);\\n * (engine.ping as (n?: number) => string)(2); // 'pongpong'; ping(0) throws DEV_BAD_ARGS\\n * @see engine/dev/inspector.test.ts\\n */\\nimport pkg from '../../package.json' with { type: 'json' };\\nimport { codeError, defineCodes, type AdviceRecord, type ErrorRecord } from '../core/log';\\nimport { checkValue, copyValue, listProblems, show, type Problem } from '../core/schema';\\nimport { createSettings, type SettingChange } from '../core/settings';\\nimport type { Intents } from '../input/intents';\\nimport type { WorldCapture } from '../sim/capture';\\n40→import type { EntityData, WorldState, WorldTrace } from '../sim/state';\\nimport {\\n  defineMember,\\n  helpText,\\n  memberKind,\\n  signatureOf,\\n  type InspectorHost,\\n  type Member,\\n  type MemberSpec,\\n} from './members';\\n50→\\n/** The codes this module raises, with their fixes. */\\nexport const INSPECTOR_CODES = defineCodes('dev', {\\n  DEV_NO_RENDERER: {\\n    template: '__engine.{member} needs a renderer, and this engine has none ({runtime}, headless)',\\n    fix: 'call it in a page started with createEngine (WP 2.7); headless, read state(), entities(), get(id) and hash() instead',\\n  },\\n  DEV_BAD_ARGS: {\\n    template: '__engine.{member}: {problems}',\\n    fix: 'call it as {signature}; __engine.help({name}) lists its arguments',\\n60→    doc: 'Raised by every `__engine` member (engine/dev/inspector.ts) before it runs, when an argument does not match the schema its member declares: a wrong type, a value out of range, a missing required argument or one too many. Nothing has happened yet.',\\n  },\\n});\\n\\n/** What `info()` reports: the engine's identity and health, and the run. */\\nexport interface EngineInfo {\\n  version: string;\\n  runtime: string;\\n  headless: boolean;\\n  adapter: Readonly<Record<string, unknown>> | null;\\n70→  features: string[];\\n  downgrades: string[];\\n  /** The runtime dependencies and their pinned versions. */\\n  deps: Record<string, string>;\\n  scene: string;\\n  seed: number;\\n  tick: number;\\n  hz: number;\\n}\\n\\n80→/** One entity as `entities()` lists it: its id and the components it holds. */\\nexport interface EntitySummary {\\n  id: number;\\n  components: string[];\\n}\\n\\n/** The inspector, `window.__engine` in a page and what `createHeadless` returns: `help()` lists every member. */\\nexport interface Inspector {\\n  info(): EngineInfo;\\n  pause(): void;\\n90→  resume(): void;\\n  step(n?: number, intents?: Intents | readonly Intents[]): number;\\n  timeScale(k?: number): number;\\n  seed(n?: number): number;\\n  state(query?: string | readonly string[]): WorldState;\\n  hash(): string;\\n  trace(): WorldTrace;\\n  entities(query?: string | readonly string[]): EntitySummary[];\\n  get(id: number): EntityData | null;\\n  set(path: string, value: unknown): SettingChange;\\n100→  capture(): WorldCapture;\\n  restore(capture: WorldCapture): void;\\n  describe(kind?: string, id?: string): unknown;\\n  help(member?: string): string;\\n  readonly errors: readonly ErrorRecord[];\\n  readonly advice: readonly AdviceRecord[];\\n  /** The members later WPs register (`input`, `stats`, `scene.dump`…). */\\n  [member: string]: unknown;\\n}\\n\\n110→/** Throws `DEV_BAD_ARGS` for `member` with these problems. */\\nfunction badArgs(member: string, problems: string, signature: string): never {\\n  throw codeError('DEV_BAD_ARGS', { member, problems, signature, name: show(member) });\\n}\\n\\n/** Runs a member on `host`: the renderer check, the argument checks, then `impl` with the arguments as given. */\\nfunction call(host: InspectorHost, member: Member, args: readonly unknown[]): unknown {\\n  if (member.needs === 'renderer' && !host.renderer) {\\n    throw codeError('DEV_NO_RENDERER', { member: member.id, runtime: host.runtime });\\n  }\\n120→  const fields = Object.entries(member.args);\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xh