{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-2a933a3f-70df-43d9-ba91-35241c60888e-74","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"60→/** What the page has started so far, read at each call: each part is null until the engine starts it. */\\nexport interface PageParts {\\n  run: AppRun | null;\\n  gfx: Gfx | null;\\n  post: Post | null;\\n  look: PageLook | null;\\n  input: Input | null;\\n  layer: TouchLayer | null;\\n  ui: Overlay | null;\\n  numbers: DamageNumbers | null;\\n70→  /** The performance governor (engine/dev/governor.ts): `auto`'s tier as the frame rate asks. */\\n  governor: Governor | null;\\n  /** The page's own camera input, laid over the devices' each drawn frame (`EngineOptions.cameraInput`). */\\n  cameraInput?: () => CameraInput | undefined;\\n  /** Whether the first frame is drawn. */\\n  ready: boolean;\\n}\\n\\n/** The read side of the run's world a page gets each frame: its step, rate, entities and the trace of its events. */\\nexport type FrameWorld = Pick<World, 'tick' | 'hz' | 'get' | 'query'> & { readonly events: Pick<WorldEvents, 'trace'> };\\n80→\\n/**\\n * What `onFrame` gets once per drawn frame: the run to read, never to change (presentation only: nothing reaches the\\n * hash), the camera the frame was drawn from, and the emitters to run.\\n */\\nexport interface EngineFrame {\\n  /** The run's world: the same object until the run starts again (a new seed, a replay), so a reader compares it. */\\n  readonly world: FrameWorld;\\n  /** The running scene: its id, its level and whether it has physics. */\\n  readonly scene: Scene;\\n90→  /** The camera's pose this frame: where a listener goes. */\\n  readonly camera: CameraPose;\\n  /** The sim's physics queries, read-only, in a physics scene; null without physics. */\\n  readonly queries: QueryView | null;\\n  /** Real seconds since the last frame. */\\n  readonly dt: number;\\n  /** The value setting `key` has now, view settings among them (`x set`, `__engine.set`, the URL). */\\n  setting(key: string): unknown;\\n  /**\\n   * Runs emitter `id` at its rate times `scale` (1) at `at` (m) for the next frame, `key` naming it so its fractions\\n100→   * and light carry over: rain over the player, a fire in a hearth (engine/gfx/fx/effects.ts `emit`). An emitter that\\n   * says `gpu` has its particles on the GPU's ring where `feature:gpuParticles` is on (WP 11.3). Presentation only.\\n   */\\n  emit(id: string, at: readonly [number, number, number], key: string, scale?: number): void;\\n}\\n\\n/** What `createPageDrawing` draws with besides the parts. */\\nexport interface PageDrawingOptions {\\n  /** The page's chrome: its touch class and top panel. */\\n  chrome: Chrome;\",\"content_concise\":\"60→/** What the page has started so far, read at each call: each part is null until the engine starts it. */\\nexport interface PageParts {\\n  run: AppRun | null;\\n  gfx: Gfx | null;\\n  post: Post | null;\\n  look: PageLook | null;\\n  input: Input | null;\\n  layer: TouchLayer | null;\\n  ui: Overlay | null;\\n  numbers: DamageNumbers | null;\\n70→  /** The performance governor (engine/dev/governor.ts): `auto`'s tier as the frame rate asks. */\\n  governor: Governor | null;\\n  /** The page's own camera input, laid over the devices' each drawn frame (`EngineOptions.cameraInput`). */\\n  cameraInput?: () => CameraInput | undefined;\\n  /** Whether the first frame is drawn. */\\n  ready: boolean;\\n}\\n\\n/** The read side of the run's world a page gets each frame: its step, rate, entities and the trace of its events. */\\nexport type FrameWorld = Pick<World, 'tick' | 'hz' | 'get' | 'query'> & { readonly events: Pick<WorldEvents, 'trace'> };\\n80→\\n/**\\n * What `onFrame` gets once per drawn frame: the run to read, never to change (presentation only: nothing reaches the\\n * hash), the camera the frame was drawn from, and the emitters to run.\\n */\\nexport interface EngineFrame {\\n  /** The run's world: the same object until the run starts again (a new seed, a replay), so a reader compares it. */\\n  readonly world: FrameWorld;\\n  /** The running scene: its id, its level and whether it has physics. */\\n  readonly scene: Scene;\\n90→  /** The camera's pose this frame: where a listener goes. */\\n  readonly camera: CameraPose;\\n  /** The sim's physics queries, read-only, in a physics scene; null without physics. */\\n  readonly queries: QueryView | null;\\n  /** Real seconds since the last frame. */\\n  readonly dt: number;\\n  /** The value setting `key` has now, view settings among them (`x set`, `__engine.set`, the URL). */\\n  setting(key: string): unknown;\\n  /**\\n   * Runs emitter `id` at its rate times `scale` (1) at `at` (m) for the next frame, `key` naming it so its fractions\\n100→   * and light carry over: rain over the player, a fire in a hearth (engine/gfx/fx/effects.ts `emit`). An emitter that\\n   * says `gpu` has its particles on the GPU's ring where `feature:gpuParticles` is on (WP 11.3). Presentation only.\\n   */\\n  emit(id: string, at: readonly [number, number, number], key: string, scale?: number): void;\\n}\\n\\n/** What `createPageDrawing` draws with besides the parts. */\\nexport interface PageDrawingOptions {\\n  /** The page's chrome: its touch class and top panel. */\\n  chrome: Chrome;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/app/drawing.ts\",\"offset\":60,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"/** What the page has started so far, read at each call: each part is null until the engine starts it. */\\nexport interface PageParts {\\n  run: AppRun | null;\\n  gfx: Gfx | null;\\n  post: Post | null;\\n  look: PageLook | null;\\n  input: Input | null;\\n  layer: TouchLayer | null;\\n  ui: Overlay | null;\\n  numbers: DamageNumbers | null;\\n  /** The performance governor (engine/dev/governor.ts): `auto`'s tier as the frame rate asks. */\\n  governor: Governor | null;\\n  /** The page's own camera input, laid over the devices' each drawn frame (`EngineOptions.cameraInput`). */\\n  cameraInput?: () => CameraInput | undefined;\\n  /** Whether the first frame is drawn. */\\n  ready: boolean;\\n}\\n\\n/** The read side of the run's world a page gets each frame: its step, rate, entities and the trace of its events. */\\nexport type FrameWorld = Pick<World, 'tick' | 'hz' | 'get' | 'query'> & { readonly events: Pick<WorldEvents, 'trace'> };\\n\\n/**\\n * What `onFrame` gets once per drawn frame: the run to read, never to change (presentation only: nothing reaches the\\n * hash), the camera the frame was drawn from, and the emitters to run.\\n */\\nexport interface EngineFrame {\\n  /** The run's world: the same object until the run starts again (a new seed, a replay), so a reader compares it. */\\n  readonly world: FrameWorld;\\n  /** The running scene: its id, its level and whether it has physics. */\\n  readonly scene: Scene;\\n  /** The camera's pose this frame: where a listener goes. */\\n  readonly camera: CameraPose;\\n  /** The sim's physics queries, read-only, in a physics scene; null without physics. */\\n  readonly queries: QueryView | null;\\n  /** Real seconds since the last frame. */\\n  readonly dt: number;\\n  /** The value setting `key` has now, view settings among them (`x set`, `__engine.set`, the URL). */\\n  setting(key: string): unknown;\\n  /**\\n   * Runs emitter `id` at its rate times `scale` (1) at `at` (m) for the next frame, `key` naming it so its fractions\\n   * and light carry over: rain over the player, a fire in a hearth (engine/gfx/fx/effects.ts `emit`). An emitter that\\n   * says `gpu` has its particles on the GPU's ring where `feature:gpuParticles` is on (WP 11.3). Presentation only.\\n   */\\n  emit(id: string, at: readonly [number, number, number], key: string, scale?: number): void;\\n}\\n\\n/** What `createPageDrawing` draws with besides the parts. */\\nexport interface PageDrawingOptions {\\n  /** The page's chrome: its touch class and top panel. */\\n  chrome: Chrome;\\n\",\"total_lines\":250}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"38dfd66e-fcf7-4733-8056-60a9fa22e531"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_233","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Adding the emitter:rain event and calling frame.emit during title and story sequences.\n\nWriting all files and downloading session.js in parallel. Fixing campaign logic for board IDs, finish operations, and win handling. Removing a duplicate Back button from the settings page.\n\nThe dev page will show TUNE sliders when devTab is 1, independent of the item list. The author tab displays live cursor coordinates, and the data tab shows a hash. Play tab items will call page listeners. The campaign act() function does not handle win or fail states.\n\nThe shell click handler will call act() first, then runDev() for any dev action ID. This double-call is safe because runDev ignores unknown IDs. During scrub, the page watches pad button 0 edges to claim seats for pads that press accept.\n\nProgress will be saved to a prefixed store key and loaded on boot. The autoplay URL flag will be preserved so the page can raise timeScale during operations when the bot is active.\n\nThe e2e script will open the page with autoplay and touch disabled. It will stub pad presses to navigate through the story, start an operation, and complete eight cases while the page raises timeScale. The test can hold cancel to skip scenes.\n\nThe e2e script will press east to skip each story scene. That requires sixteen skips plus eight starts and eight continues. The bot should finish a four-minute operation in about fourteen thousand simulation ticks at timeScale twelve.\n\nChecking whether timeScale multiplies simulation steps per frame or only scales internal delta time. At timeScale twelve, a two-minute case would take roughly fifteen seconds of real time, so eight cases plus story skips should finish within the five-to-eight minute e2e window. The test will run inside one Chromium process.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8aaa8a5a-1806-44fe-aa6c-33beff23e213-75","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"timeScale","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/app/loop.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8aaa8a5a-1806-44fe-aa6c-33beff23e213-76","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"timeScale","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/core/time.ts"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":913,"output_tokens":1342,"cache_read_input_tokens":119168,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"53a143a1-aa8f-411c-b8c9-e3583a5e2714"}
