07,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":9,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/app/loop.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":118,\"content\":\"        for (let k = 0; k < frame.steps; k++) options.step(k === 0 ? first : later);\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/app/playback.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":78,\"content\":\"      session.step(intents);\"},{\"line_number\":175,\"content\":\"    playback.step(session);\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/app/animMember.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":33,\"content\":\" * engine.step(30, { move: [1, 0] });\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/app/headless.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":35,\"content\":\" * h.step(60); // 60: the tick after the steps\"},{\"line_number\":245,\"content\":\"    meter.time('sim', () => run.session.step(intents));\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/app/view.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":235,\"content\":\"    if (fresh) rig.step(null);\"},{\"line_number\":249,\"content\":\"    rig.step(doing);\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/app/engine.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":354,\"content\":\"      playback.step(started.session);\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"2a4732fc-436f-48d3-968a-4dc027ccf28f"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_235","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Reviewing the frame loop in loop.ts.\n\nAutoplay keeps bot hands fresh by calling botHands inside each simulation step. In non-autoplay mode, page hands update once per frame and remain static across multiple steps. The scene ignores page intents during autoplay. A timeScale of 8 is acceptable for operations.\n\nEach case takes roughly 17 seconds at 60fps with timeScale 10. Eight cases total about 2.5 minutes, which fits within the six-minute end-to-end timeout.\n\nThe inspector pauses during menus so operations do not run underneath them. It resumes when leaving a menu. The attract mode runs at timescale 1 for watchability.\n\nAt timescale 1, the 24-second attract clip spans roughly 1440 ticks, giving the bot enough time to perform visible actions while the clock remains frozen. When entering an operation from a brief, the seed restarts and the page syncs game state by comparing a composite key of run, attract, seats, difficulty, simple mode, seed, and phase.\n\nThe inspector also sets difficulty, simple mode, colleague, phase, and autoplay flags. Autoplay applies immediately without a seed, but attract requires a seed to activate. During retries, the scene reads the current phase at setup and jumps directly to it rather than restarting from tick zero.\n\nThe page must read the live operation phase before seeding, because the seed restarts the simulation. A generation counter on the campaign will distinguish retry-phase from resume: it increments on both retry and start, letting the system know whether to reseed at phase zero or at the current phase.\n\nThe campaign now tracks a `boot` counter that increments on start, retry, and phase changes. Resume leaves it unchanged.\n\nThe page compares this boot value to a local `seenBoot`. When it changes, the page reads the live operation phase if `keepPhase` is set, clears that flag, and seeds the inspector.\n\nA change in the desired run string also triggers a seed.\n\nA composite signature of run, attract, seats, difficulty, simple mode, boot counter, and colleague will trigger a full state reset and seed whenever it changes. The scene reads game.seed for its operation RNG, while inspector.seed restarts the scene; both will use the same number. Retries will keep the same seed for deterministic behavior. Colleague is set to the lone hub player when local couch seats exceed one.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6ce72efb-0bc9-4179-a711-ebaffd5d097f-79","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/scenes/bridge.ts","limit":120}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1272,"output_tokens":1252,"cache_read_input_tokens":121600,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"ca16ea30-6d69-49bd-9e41-411403638968"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-6ce72efb-0bc9-4179-a711-ebaffd5d097f-79","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The live operation for the one running scene. The page reads it; the scene writes it. A JSON snapshot on the\\n * chart component is what capture and restore put back, so the object here is replaced when the snapshot disagrees.\\n */\\nimport { enterPhase } from '../op/world';\\nimport { createFromCase } from '../op/world';\\nimport type { Difficulty, Op } from '../op/types';\\n\\n/** The operation the scene is stepping, or null on a title or a story run. */\\n10→let live: Op | null = null;\\n\\n/** The operation, if this run has one. */\\nexport function liveOp(): Op | null {\\n  return live;\\n}\\n\\n/** Replace the live operation. Capture and restore call this with the parsed snapshot. */\\nexport function adoptOp(op: Op | null): void {\\n  live = op;\\n20→}\\n\\n/**\\n * Make the live operation the chart's snapshot. Call this after a restore and before reading cursors: the module\\n * copy is not part of the world capture, and the chart is.\\n */\\nexport function followChart(blob: string): void {\\n  if (!blob) {\\n    live = null;\\n    return;\\n30→  }\\n  if (live && snapshot(live) === blob) return;\\n  live = parseSnapshot(blob);\\n}\\n\\n/** Advance to phase `index` by clearing the phases before it. Phase 0 is already open. */\\nexport function jumpPhase(op: Op, index: number): void {\\n  const goal = Math.max(0, Math.min(index, Math.max(0, op.phases.length - 1)));\\n  while (op.phase < goal) {\\n    for (const target of op.targets) if (target.phase === op.phase) target.done = true;\\n40→    op.phase += 1;\\n    enterPhase(op);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** Options a run starts with. */\\nexport interface RunOpts {\\n  difficulty: Difficulty;\\n  seed: number;\\n  seats: number;\\n50→  attract: boolean;\\n  simple: boolean;\\n  colleague: boolean;\\n  phase: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** Start `op:…`, or clear the live operation for any other run. */\\nexport function openRun(run: string, opts: RunOpts): Op | null {\\n  if (!run.startsWith('op:')) {\\n    live = null;\\n60→    return null;\\n  }\\n  const raw = run.slice(3);\\n  const id = raw.startsWith('case:') ? raw : `case:${raw}`;\\n  const op = createFromCase(id, {\\n    difficulty: opts.difficulty,\\n    seed: opts.seed,\\n    seats: opts.seats,\\n    attract: opts.attract,\\n    simple: opts.simple,\\n70→    colleague: opts.colleague ? true : undefined,\\n  });\\n  if (opts.phase > 0) jumpPhase(op, opts.phase);\\n  live = op;\\n  return op;\\n}\\n\\n/** The snapshot the chart stores. */\\nexport function snapshot(op: Op): string {\\n  return JSON.stringify(op);\\n80→}\\n\\n/** An operation from a chart snapshot. */\\nexport function parseSnapshot(text: string): Op {\\n  return JSON.parse(text) as Op;\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The live operation for the one running scene. The page reads it; the scene writes it. A JSON snapshot on the\\n * chart component is what capture and restore put back, so the object here is replaced when the snapshot disagrees.\\n */\\nimport { enterPhase } from '../op/world';\\nimport { createFromCase } from '../op/world';\\nimport type { Difficulty, Op } from '../op/types';\\n\\n/** The operation the scene is stepping, or null on a title or a story run. */\\n10→let live: Op | null = null;\\n\\n/** The operation, if this run has one. */\\nexport function liveOp(): Op | null {\\n  return live;\\n}\\n\\n/** Replace the live operation. Capture and restore call this with the parsed snapshot. */\\nexport function adoptOp(op: Op | null): void {\\n  live = op;\\n20→}\\n\\n/**\\n * Make the live operation the chart's snapshot. Call this after a restore and before reading cursors: the module\\n * copy is not part of the world capture, and the chart is.\\n */\\nexport function followChart(blob: string): void {\\n  if (!blob) {\\n    live = null;\\n    return;\\n30→  }\\n  if (live && snapshot(live) === blob) return;\\n  live = parseSnapshot(blob);\\n}\\n\\n/** Advance to phase `index` by clearing the phases before it. Phase 0 is already open. */\\nexport function jumpPhase(op: Op, index: number): void {\\n  const goal = Math.max(0, Math.min(index, Math.max(0, op.phases.length - 1)));\\n  while (op.phase < goal) {\\n    for (const target of op.targets) if (target.phase === op.phase) target.done = true;\\n40→    op.phase += 1;\\n    enterPhase(op);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** Options a run starts with. */\\nexport interface RunOpts {\\n  difficulty: Difficulty;\\n  seed: number;\\n  seats: number;\\n50→  attract: boolean;\\n  simple: boolean;\\n  colleague: boolean;\\n  phase: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** Start `op:…`, or clear the live operation for any other run. */\\nexport function openRun(run: string, opts: RunOpts): Op | null {\\n  if (!run.startsWith('op:')) {\\n    live = null;\\n60→    return null;\\n  }\\n  const raw = run.slice(3);\\n  const id = raw.startsWith('case:') ? raw : `case:${raw}`;\\n  const op = createFromCase(id, {\\n    difficulty: opts.difficulty,\\n    seed: opts.seed,\\n    seats: opts.seats,\\n    attract: opts.attract,\\n    simple: opts.simple,\\n70→    colleague: opts.colleague ? true : undefined,\\n  });\\n  if (opts.phase > 0) jumpPhase(op, opts.phase);\\n  live = op;\\n  return op;\\n}\\n\\n/** The snapshot the chart stores. */\\nexport function snapshot(op: Op): string {\\n  return JSON.stringify(op);\\n80→}\\n\\n/** An operation from a chart snapshot. */\\nexport function parseSnapshot(text: string): Op {\\n  return JSON.parse(text) as Op;\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/scenes/bridge.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":120,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file The live operation for the one running scene. The page reads it; the scene writes it. A JSON snapshot on the\\n * chart component is what capture and restore put back, so the object here is replaced when the snapshot disagrees.\\n */\\nimport { enterPhase } from '../op/world';\\nimport { createFromCase } from '../op/world';\\nimport type { Difficulty, Op } from '../op/types';\\n\\n/** The operation the scene is stepping, or null on a title or a story run. */\\nlet live: Op | null = null;\\n\\n/** The operation, if this run has one. */\\nexport function liveOp(): Op | null {\\n  return live;\\n}\\n\\n/** Replace the live operation. Capture and restore call this with the parsed snapshot. */\\nexport function adoptOp(op: Op | null): void {\\n  live = op;\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Make the live operation the chart's snapshot. Call this after a restore and before reading cursors: the module\\n * copy is not part of the world capture, and the chart is.\\n */\\nexport function followChart(blob: string): void {\\n  if (!blob) {\\n    live = null;\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  if (live && snapshot(live) === blob) return;\\n  live = parseSnapshot(blob);\\n}\\n\\n/** Advance to phase `index` by clearing the phases before it. Phase 0 is already open. */\\nexport function jumpPhase(op: Op, index: number): void {\\n  const goal = Math.max(0, Math.min(index, Math.max(0, op.phases.length - 1)));\\n  while (op.phase < goal) {\\n    for (const target of op.targets) if (target.phase === op.phase) target.done = true;\\n    op.phase += 1;\\n    enterPhase(op);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** Options a run starts with. */\\nexport interface RunOpts {\\n  difficulty: Difficulty;\\n  seed: number;\\n  seats: number;\\n  attract: boolean;\\n  simple: boolean;\\n  colleague: boolean;\\n  phase: number;\\n}\\n\\n/** Start `op:…`, or clear the live operation for any other run. */\\nexport function openRun(run: string, opts: RunOpts): Op | null {\\n  if (!run.startsWith('op:')) {\\n    live = null;\\n    return null;\\n  }\\n  const raw = run.slice(3);\\n  const id = raw.startsWith('case:') ? raw : `case:${raw}`;\\n  const op = createFromCase(id, {\\n    difficulty: opts.difficulty,\\n    seed: opts.seed,\\n    seats: opts.seats,\\n    attract: opts.attract,\\n    simple: opts.simple,\\n    colleague: opts.colleague ? true : undefined,\\n  });\\n  if (opts.phase > 0) jumpPhase(op, opts.phase);\\n  live = op;\\n  return op;\\n}\\n\\n/** The snapshot the chart stores. */\\nexport function snapshot(op: Op): string {\\n  return JSON.stringify(op);\\n}\\n\\n/** An operation from a chart snapshot. */\\nexport function parseSnapshot(text: string): Op {\\n  return JSON.parse(text) as Op;\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":85}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"f8c04ee9-fbab-453e-8202-3fd4c348a914"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_236","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"game.colleague evaluates to undefined in createFromCase.\n\nHub solo sets game.colleague to true. Colleague is defined when players equals one. The hub run format is `op:case:gala-shift`. Campaign fixes and file writes will follow. An interview test will compare interview.ts output against a JSON file.\n\nThe interview test will read `exit-interview.json` from the work root via `fs.readFileSync`. The relative path from `labs/game/data/interview.test.ts` to the work folder is being verified.\n\nThe interview test will import INTERVIEW from interview.ts and compare it against a parsed JSON file. The page will import interview.ts directly. Each source field and feedback question gets its own card. A cards() helper will structure the output. SVG glyphs will use textContent for names and innerHTML only for markup. Interview strings will stay concise.\n\nShell rendering will rebuild innerHTML each frame. Buttons will use data-id for focus and clicks. To avoid resetting dev sliders, a stamp comparison will skip rebuilds when the state is unchanged and extra.force is false.\n\nThe HUD will update every frame via textContent on stable nodes, separate from the interview shell. A touch gate div appears when coarse pointers are detected without a pad, showing a settings button; attract mode still runs underneath. The classic no-webgpu script sets a message, hides engine shell elements, and adds a touch line. A module-level `if (!navigator.gpu) return` guard is being considered, though imports are hoisted.\n\nThe classic script will push a fake error record before the module loads. This prevents gameFailed from overwriting the webgpu message with APP_START.\n\nThe classic script now explicitly sets `window.__engine.errors` to `{ code: 'GFX_NO_WEBGPU', message: 'no WebGPU' }`. It also calls `AIHub.fail()` when the hub is active. This ensures `gameFailed` sees an existing error and skips overwriting the WebGPU message.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-80679b1c-ebdf-4c2d-ab26-8c55b019219d-80","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"GFX_NO_WEBGPU|error overlay|id=\\\"errors\\\"","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/ui","head_limit":20}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-80679b1c-ebdf-4c2d-ab26-8c55b019219d-81","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function showError|errors\\.ts|overlay","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/app/engine.ts","head_limit":15}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":114712,"output_tokens":1275,"cache_read_input_tokens":10112,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"c48aafbb-0fb9-4470-8699-1af8cb716a3e"}
