ond-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/input/input.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":45,\"content\":\"import { deviceOf, heldBase, HOLD_TIME, holdCode, PAD_BUTTONS, touchCode, type DeviceKind, type InputSink } from './codes'; // prettier-ignore\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/input/bindings.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":36,\"content\":\"import { codeLabel, deviceOf, isCode, type DeviceKind, type LabelOptions } from './codes';\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/input/codes.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":38,\"content\":\"export type DeviceKind = 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch' | 'virtual';\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"754a8cb3-bd15-42c0-aea1-8505f90abb6b"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_241","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Glyphs display device-specific icons. Gamepads show PS or Xbox branding. Keyboards show keycaps. Mice show mouse icons.\n\nA prompt line will appear on the HUD. I'll write the one-file replacement in tools/one-file.mts and download session.js. verify.mjs will be built from the skeleton with e2e and hub support. The e2e script will use @playwright/test from the project's node_modules.\n\nChromium will run first. Python will drive Firefox and WebKit next. The hub harness copies HTML files and serves them for four URLs. This is memory-heavy.\n\nverify runs e2e and hub sequentially. The hub harness may OOM with four players, but the plan requires it. The node sequencer already validates lockstep. A short limit= will let the harness auto-click ready and time-up before the host finishes the round. This avoids playing the full game.\n\nThe hub harness will use a 20-second limit so the round times out before the host finishes. The game will open without an active session. Hash mismatches will be tracked in window.__compass.mismatches. The server will step the world in AIHub mode while hiding the canvas, and finish still works. If the host leaves, the harness removes it and the script stops cleanly.\n\nThe hub.ts module will be compact. It defines a HubInfo interface for player state and a HubApi interface for connect, ready, answer, time, and finish.\n\nHubApi now includes send, on, and fail methods. The NetState interface tracks session state: info, started, ended, card, play, mismatches, local hands, and gone players. attach wires the hub to the engine step callback.\n\nThe host tracks received intents per seat as x, z, tool, and eight monotonic counters. Counters are unreliable messages sent about eighteen times per second. The client converts counter deltas into button pulses by comparing them to the last applied state. Lost packets never lose presses because the values only increase.\n\nThe client message format is now defined. It carries x, z, tool, a use boolean, and six counter deltas for drop, gift, paddle, site, swap, and hint. The host broadcasts packed hands every tick. Delta coding is optional; the simplest approach sends the last few ticks directly.\n\nThe host will flush all queued ticks in one message every 66 milliseconds. That yields about fifteen messages per second, plus a reliable hash every second. Clients buffer incoming hands and apply them in order, waiting for gaps to close. The host tick loop runs every 16 milliseconds, stepping the world until the round ends.\n\nThe host queues each tick's packed hands and breaks the loop if the round ends. The frame loop pauses while the world steps so they do not overlap. The client applies buffered ticks in batches of one, two, or eight depending on buffer depth, then compares hashes. An optional cursor list will be added to paintField to fix the glove lag.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ff427fcc-46ee-4242-b32b-20e492d2ce09-86","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/view/field/sheet.ts","offset":215,"limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":597,"output_tokens":1723,"cache_read_input_tokens":130176,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"57ac752f-2a5b-4833-bdd3-f4e81e970058"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-ff427fcc-46ee-4242-b32b-20e492d2ce09-86","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"215→    pos[i * 3 + 1] = y;\\n    col[i * 3] = rgb[0];\\n    col[i * 3 + 1] = rgb[1];\\n    col[i * 3 + 2] = rgb[2];\\n  }\\n220→  position.needsUpdate = true;\\n  color.needsUpdate = true;\\n  mesh.computeVertexNormals();\\n}\\n\\n/** Gloves follow the seats. An empty seat is parked under the floor. */\\nfunction paintGlove(mesh: Mesh, op: Op | null): void {\\n  const position = mesh.getAttribute('position');\\n  const color = mesh.getAttribute('color');\\n  const pos = position.array;\\n230→  const col = color.array;\\n  const tints: [number, number, number][] = [\\n    [0.92, 0.93, 0.9],\\n    [0.95, 0.78, 0.55],\\n    [0.7, 0.82, 0.95],\\n    [0.82, 0.7, 0.9],\\n  ];\\n  for (let s = 0; s < 4; s++) {\\n    const seat = op?.seats[s];\\n    const base = s * 16;\\n240→    if (!seat) {\\n      quad(pos, base, 0, 0, 0.01, 0.01, -4, tints[s], col);\\n      quad(pos, base + 4, 0, 0, 0.01, 0.01, -4, tints[s], col);\\n      quad(pos, base + 8, 0, 0, 0.01, 0.01, -4, [0.7, 0.75, 0.78], col);\\n      continue;\\n    }\\n    quad(pos, base, seat.x, seat.z, 0.16, 0.12, 0.08, tints[s], col);\\n    quad(pos, base + 4, seat.x - 0.14, seat.z + 0.08, 0.05, 0.07, 0.09, tints[s], col);\\n    quad(pos, base + 8, seat.x + 0.05, seat.z - 0.16, 0.03, 0.16, 0.1, [0.75, 0.78, 0.8], col);\\n  }\\n250→  position.needsUpdate = true;\\n  color.needsUpdate = true;\\n  mesh.computeVertexNormals();\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"215→    pos[i * 3 + 1] = y;\\n    col[i * 3] = rgb[0];\\n    col[i * 3 + 1] = rgb[1];\\n    col[i * 3 + 2] = rgb[2];\\n  }\\n220→  position.needsUpdate = true;\\n  color.needsUpdate = true;\\n  mesh.computeVertexNormals();\\n}\\n\\n/** Gloves follow the seats. An empty seat is parked under the floor. */\\nfunction paintGlove(mesh: Mesh, op: Op | null): void {\\n  const position = mesh.getAttribute('position');\\n  const color = mesh.getAttribute('color');\\n  const pos = position.array;\\n230→  const col = color.array;\\n  const tints: [number, number, number][] = [\\n    [0.92, 0.93, 0.9],\\n    [0.95, 0.78, 0.55],\\n    [0.7, 0.82, 0.95],\\n    [0.82, 0.7, 0.9],\\n  ];\\n  for (let s = 0; s < 4; s++) {\\n    const seat = op?.seats[s];\\n    const base = s * 16;\\n240→    if (!seat) {\\n      quad(pos, base, 0, 0, 0.01, 0.01, -4, tints[s], col);\\n      quad(pos, base + 4, 0, 0, 0.01, 0.01, -4, tints[s], col);\\n      quad(pos, base + 8, 0, 0, 0.01, 0.01, -4, [0.7, 0.75, 0.78], col);\\n      continue;\\n    }\\n    quad(pos, base, seat.x, seat.z, 0.16, 0.12, 0.08, tints[s], col);\\n    quad(pos, base + 4, seat.x - 0.14, seat.z + 0.08, 0.05, 0.07, 0.09, tints[s], col);\\n    quad(pos, base + 8, seat.x + 0.05, seat.z - 0.16, 0.03, 0.16, 0.1, [0.75, 0.78, 0.8], col);\\n  }\\n250→  position.needsUpdate = true;\\n  color.needsUpdate = true;\\n  mesh.computeVertexNormals();\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/view/field/sheet.ts\",\"offset\":215,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"    pos[i * 3 + 1] = y;\\n    col[i * 3] = rgb[0];\\n    col[i * 3 + 1] = rgb[1];\\n    col[i * 3 + 2] = rgb[2];\\n  }\\n  position.needsUpdate = true;\\n  color.needsUpdate = true;\\n  mesh.computeVertexNormals();\\n}\\n\\n/** Gloves follow the seats. An empty seat is parked under the floor. */\\nfunction paintGlove(mesh: Mesh, op: Op | null): void {\\n  const position = mesh.getAttribute('position');\\n  const color = mesh.getAttribute('color');\\n  const pos = position.array;\\n  const col = color.array;\\n  const tints: [number, number, number][] = [\\n    [0.92, 0.93, 0.9],\\n    [0.95, 0.78, 0.55],\\n    [0.7, 0.82, 0.95],\\n    [0.82, 0.7, 0.9],\\n  ];\\n  for (let s = 0; s < 4; s++) {\\n    const seat = op?.seats[s];\\n    const base = s * 16;\\n    if (!seat) {\\n      quad(pos, base, 0, 0, 0.01, 0.01, -4, tints[s], col);\\n      quad(pos, base + 4, 0, 0, 0.01, 0.01, -4, tints[s], col);\\n      quad(pos, base + 8, 0, 0, 0.01, 0.01, -4, [0.7, 0.75, 0.78], col);\\n      continue;\\n    }\\n    quad(pos, base, seat.x, seat.z, 0.16, 0.12, 0.08, tints[s], col);\\n    quad(pos, base + 4, seat.x - 0.14, seat.z + 0.08, 0.05, 0.07, 0.09, tints[s], col);\\n    quad(pos, base + 8, seat.x + 0.05, seat.z - 0.16, 0.03, 0.16, 0.1, [0.75, 0.78, 0.8], col);\\n  }\\n  position.needsUpdate = true;\\n  color.needsUpdate = true;\\n  mesh.computeVertexNormals();\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":253}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"bfedf4ca-2d24-4d34-94e2-91555915327d"}
