9,39,115,32,105,110,32,96,97,108,108,96,44,32,101,108,115,101,10,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,55,51,49,95,95,120,53,57,99,49,100,51,47,119,111,114,107,47,84,114,97,117,109,97,45,67,111,109,112,97,115,115,45,84,114,97,117,109,97,45,67,101,110,116,101,114,45,83,101,99,111,110,100,45,79,112,105,110,105,111,110,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,55,51,49,47,101,110,103,105,110,101,47,97,112,112,47,101,110,103,105,110,101,46,116,115,10,56,58,32,42,32,96,112,111,115,116,46,115,104,111,119,96,59,32,116,104,101,32,108,111,111,107,39,115,32,115,107,121,32,97,110,100,32,115,116,121,108,101,44,32,101,110,103,105,110,101,47,97,112,112,47,108,111,111,107,46,116,115,41,44,32,119,97,114,109,115,32,117,112,32,101,118,101,114,121,32,112,105,112,101,108,105,110,101,32,116,104,101,32,118,105,101,119,32,110,101,101,100,115,32,40,96,103,102,120,46,119,97,114,109,85,112,96,44,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":10,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/gfx/warmup.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":28,\"content\":\" * idea for a registry. What a page's warm-ups compile is the view setting `gfx.warmUp` (`WARMUP_SETTINGS`).\"},{\"line_number\":65,\"content\":\" * Its view setting `gfx.warmUp` (ADR-0008 amendment 11): what a page's warm-ups compile. r182 builds a shader for each\"},{\"line_number\":74,\"content\":\"  'gfx.warmUp': {\"},{\"line_number\":85,\"content\":\"/** Whether `settings` ask a page's warm-ups to compile only what it has drawn (`gfx.warmUp: asked`). */\"},{\"line_number\":86,\"content\":\"export const warmsAsked = (settings: { get(path: string): unknown }): boolean => settings.get('gfx.warmUp') === 'asked';\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/gfx/post/chain.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":112,\"content\":\"   * look pays that instead, once, building nothing. With `gfx.warmUp: asked` (engine/gfx/warmup.ts) it gives the scene\"},{\"line_number\":249,\"content\":\"  /** Whether a plain frame was asked for (see `plain`): `gfx.warmUp: asked` compiles its pass from then on only. */\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/app/drawing.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":7,\"content\":\" * key now: both of the view's, so switching projection later builds nothing, or, with `gfx.warmUp: asked`, those\"},{\"line_number\":53,\"content\":\" * The cameras a warm-up compiles for (`gfx.warmUp`, engine/gfx/warmup.ts): every one of the view's in `all`, else\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/app/engine.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":8,\"content\":\" * `post.show`; the look's sky and style, engine/app/look.ts), warms up every pipeline the view needs (`gfx.warmUp`,\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"93c8cc44-a952-4210-bcdb-0ff6d4e68309"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_276","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Confirmed that gfx.warmUp is a valid setting.\n\nPlanning boot.ts, session runner, main.ts, and audio helper. Defining level configs for OR and arena scenes. Setting up store prefix and modal visibility rules.\n\nSession mode will be special-cased in the frame loop. Pause opens settings without pausing the simulation. Voice synthesis will use a simple oscillator for the first 24 characters of each line. Title music maps to song:title and story music to song:story.\n\nMercy music maps to song:mercy. Strained OP uses song:strain; otherwise song:or. Win and lose stingers are planned. Volume scales with progress divided by 100. A DEV actions map is being added for quick testing toggles.\n\nThe DEV actions map now includes step, slow, fast, fly, copy, and reset. Unlock is handled by act(). Slider input events call inspector.set with the numeric value. Hovering over a [data-act] element sets focus to that index.\n\nClicks trigger act(id). Keyboard input is read inside onFrame. During attract mode, pointermove sets a flag so the frame that enters attract is not treated as input. Touch-only devices show a message; a key or pad arriving clears it via a touchCleared flag.\n\nA keydown event now clears the touch-hold flag. The touch overlay appears only when touchOnly() is true and touchHold remains active. The settings button works as a data-act element, and attract mode continues running behind the overlay. Autoplay timeScale is set to 8 during OP screens outside session mode, reverting to 1 when leaving OP. A syncRun function is being drafted to handle desired run and attract states while skipping session mode.\n\nThe syncRun function compares a signature string built from run, attract, progress, boot, and keepPhase to avoid redundant inspector updates. When the state changes, it sets game.run, game.attract, game.seats, game.difficulty, game.simple, game.phase, game.colleague, and game.autoplay.\n\nThe syncRun function now calls inspector.seed(1) and updates the signature. On first boot, seeding at the title screen is acceptable because it restarts that scene. When keepPhase is active, the phase is read before seeding so the correct state persists. Autoplay is set for attract mode bots and for URL autoplay when the screen is OP; it does nothing on the title screen.\n\nPause and menu screens will call inspector.pause() to stop the OP simulation underneath. The attract screen must stay unpaused so it continues running. The hold condition covers pause, debrief, handbook, settings, and dev screens while session mode is inactive.\n\nRetry resets boot and screen to OP, then resumes and seeds. The frame loop runs input handling first, then syncRun, then pause or resume. Seeding while paused is safe because it restarts the scene before resuming.\n\nfinishOp fires every frame after OP status changes while the screen is OP. It returns immediately if the screen has already left OP, so the first frame switches the screen to debrief. This logic is skipped during attract mode.\n\nThe camera will switch to a fixed overhead shot when an OP run starts and a wider harbor view at the title screen. These settings apply once per signature change. Post-processing look modes will toggle between field and harbor based on the run prefix. Overlay layers for stillpoint or low vitals will be set via post.combine with a try-catch fallback.\n\nStill, pulse, and low-vitality overlays are now defined with specific amounts for the post.combine array. Rain particles will be emitted at the field center during non-OP frames.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-eac38731-4a55-4220-8073-4baeb0f1ac5b-182","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"export interface ListenerPose","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/audio","-A":12}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-eac38731-4a55-4220-8073-4baeb0f1ac5b-183","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"export interface CameraPose","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/gfx/cameras/pose.ts","-A":15}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2370,"output_tokens":2159,"cache_read_input_tokens":186496,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"acdfff47-fcd3-43ad-91d4-38100d3371f7"}
