{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-d4991f7b-28f9-4154-a1ed-e12c2190814b-63","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"70→  /** The performance governor (engine/dev/governor.ts): `auto`'s tier as the frame rate asks. */\\n  governor: Governor | null;\\n  /** The page's own camera input, laid over the devices' each drawn frame (`EngineOptions.cameraInput`). */\\n  cameraInput?: () => CameraInput | undefined;\\n  /** Whether the first frame is drawn. */\\n  ready: boolean;\\n}\\n\\n/** The read side of the run's world a page gets each frame: its step, rate, entities and the trace of its events. */\\nexport type FrameWorld = Pick<World, 'tick' | 'hz' | 'get' | 'query'> & { readonly events: Pick<WorldEvents, 'trace'> };\\n80→\\n/**\\n * What `onFrame` gets once per drawn frame: the run to read, never to change (presentation only: nothing reaches the\\n * hash), the camera the frame was drawn from, and the emitters to run.\\n */\\nexport interface EngineFrame {\\n  /** The run's world: the same object until the run starts again (a new seed, a replay), so a reader compares it. */\\n  readonly world: FrameWorld;\\n  /** The running scene: its id, its level and whether it has physics. */\\n  readonly scene: Scene;\\n90→  /** The camera's pose this frame: where a listener goes. */\\n  readonly camera: CameraPose;\\n  /** The sim's physics queries, read-only, in a physics scene; null without physics. */\\n  readonly queries: QueryView | null;\\n  /** Real seconds since the last frame. */\\n  readonly dt: number;\\n  /** The value setting `key` has now, view settings among them (`x set`, `__engine.set`, the URL). */\\n  setting(key: string): unknown;\\n  /**\\n   * Runs emitter `id` at its rate times `scale` (1) at `at` (m) for the next frame, `key` naming it so its fractions\\n100→   * and light carry over: rain over the player, a fire in a hearth (engine/gfx/fx/effects.ts `emit`). An emitter that\\n   * says `gpu` has its particles on the GPU's ring where `feature:gpuParticles` is on (WP 11.3). Presentation only.\\n   */\\n  emit(id: string, at: readonly [number, number, number], key: string, scale?: number): void;\\n}\\n\\n/** What `createPageDrawing` draws with besides the parts. */\\nexport interface PageDrawingOptions {\\n  /** The page's chrome: its touch class and top panel. */\\n  chrome: Chrome;\\n110→  /** The current run's settings (`quality`). */\\n  settings: Settings;\\n  /** The page's own presentation, after each drawn frame. */\\n  onFrame?: (frame: EngineFrame) => void;\\n}\\n\\n/** The page's drawing (see the file comment). */\\nexport interface PageDrawing {\\n  /** The rendering members' drawing. */\\n  readonly drawing: Drawing;\",\"content_concise\":\"70→  /** The performance governor (engine/dev/governor.ts): `auto`'s tier as the frame rate asks. */\\n  governor: Governor | null;\\n  /** The page's own camera input, laid over the devices' each drawn frame (`EngineOptions.cameraInput`). */\\n  cameraInput?: () => CameraInput | undefined;\\n  /** Whether the first frame is drawn. */\\n  ready: boolean;\\n}\\n\\n/** The read side of the run's world a page gets each frame: its step, rate, entities and the trace of its events. */\\nexport type FrameWorld = Pick<World, 'tick' | 'hz' | 'get' | 'query'> & { readonly events: Pick<WorldEvents, 'trace'> };\\n80→\\n/**\\n * What `onFrame` gets once per drawn frame: the run to read, never to change (presentation only: nothing reaches the\\n * hash), the camera the frame was drawn from, and the emitters to run.\\n */\\nexport interface EngineFrame {\\n  /** The run's world: the same object until the run starts again (a new seed, a replay), so a reader compares it. */\\n  readonly world: FrameWorld;\\n  /** The running scene: its id, its level and whether it has physics. */\\n  readonly scene: Scene;\\n90→  /** The camera's pose this frame: where a listener goes. */\\n  readonly camera: CameraPose;\\n  /** The sim's physics queries, read-only, in a physics scene; null without physics. */\\n  readonly queries: QueryView | null;\\n  /** Real seconds since the last frame. */\\n  readonly dt: number;\\n  /** The value setting `key` has now, view settings among them (`x set`, `__engine.set`, the URL). */\\n  setting(key: string): unknown;\\n  /**\\n   * Runs emitter `id` at its rate times `scale` (1) at `at` (m) for the next frame, `key` naming it so its fractions\\n100→   * and light carry over: rain over the player, a fire in a hearth (engine/gfx/fx/effects.ts `emit`). An emitter that\\n   * says `gpu` has its particles on the GPU's ring where `feature:gpuParticles` is on (WP 11.3). Presentation only.\\n   */\\n  emit(id: string, at: readonly [number, number, number], key: string, scale?: number): void;\\n}\\n\\n/** What `createPageDrawing` draws with besides the parts. */\\nexport interface PageDrawingOptions {\\n  /** The page's chrome: its touch class and top panel. */\\n  chrome: Chrome;\\n110→  /** The current run's settings (`quality`). */\\n  settings: Settings;\\n  /** The page's own presentation, after each drawn frame. */\\n  onFrame?: (frame: EngineFrame) => void;\\n}\\n\\n/** The page's drawing (see the file comment). */\\nexport interface PageDrawing {\\n  /** The rendering members' drawing. */\\n  readonly drawing: Drawing;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/app/drawing.ts\",\"offset\":70,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"  /** The performance governor (engine/dev/governor.ts): `auto`'s tier as the frame rate asks. */\\n  governor: Governor | null;\\n  /** The page's own camera input, laid over the devices' each drawn frame (`EngineOptions.cameraInput`). */\\n  cameraInput?: () => CameraInput | undefined;\\n  /** Whether the first frame is drawn. */\\n  ready: boolean;\\n}\\n\\n/** The read side of the run's world a page gets each frame: its step, rate, entities and the trace of its events. */\\nexport type FrameWorld = Pick<World, 'tick' | 'hz' | 'get' | 'query'> & { readonly events: Pick<WorldEvents, 'trace'> };\\n\\n/**\\n * What `onFrame` gets once per drawn frame: the run to read, never to change (presentation only: nothing reaches the\\n * hash), the camera the frame was drawn from, and the emitters to run.\\n */\\nexport interface EngineFrame {\\n  /** The run's world: the same object until the run starts again (a new seed, a replay), so a reader compares it. */\\n  readonly world: FrameWorld;\\n  /** The running scene: its id, its level and whether it has physics. */\\n  readonly scene: Scene;\\n  /** The camera's pose this frame: where a listener goes. */\\n  readonly camera: CameraPose;\\n  /** The sim's physics queries, read-only, in a physics scene; null without physics. */\\n  readonly queries: QueryView | null;\\n  /** Real seconds since the last frame. */\\n  readonly dt: number;\\n  /** The value setting `key` has now, view settings among them (`x set`, `__engine.set`, the URL). */\\n  setting(key: string): unknown;\\n  /**\\n   * Runs emitter `id` at its rate times `scale` (1) at `at` (m) for the next frame, `key` naming it so its fractions\\n   * and light carry over: rain over the player, a fire in a hearth (engine/gfx/fx/effects.ts `emit`). An emitter that\\n   * says `gpu` has its particles on the GPU's ring where `feature:gpuParticles` is on (WP 11.3). Presentation only.\\n   */\\n  emit(id: string, at: readonly [number, number, number], key: string, scale?: number): void;\\n}\\n\\n/** What `createPageDrawing` draws with besides the parts. */\\nexport interface PageDrawingOptions {\\n  /** The page's chrome: its touch class and top panel. */\\n  chrome: Chrome;\\n  /** The current run's settings (`quality`). */\\n  settings: Settings;\\n  /** The page's own presentation, after each drawn frame. */\\n  onFrame?: (frame: EngineFrame) => void;\\n}\\n\\n/** The page's drawing (see the file comment). */\\nexport interface PageDrawing {\\n  /** The rendering members' drawing. */\\n  readonly drawing: Drawing;\\n\",\"total_lines\":250}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"a5a565fd-084c-4289-9016-84dcdc1d3928"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_315","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Proceeding with all edits. Checking for the emit rain key and looks to prevent errors.\n\nConfirmed look IDs are registered before engine creation. Rain emitter and song imports are correct. Now writing main.ts and the HTML generator.\n\nWriting a Node script to generate index.html. It will concatenate session.js with embedded CSS and a classic WebGPU script.\n\nThe HTML generator includes a WebGPU browser check. It shows a message if the browser lacks support.\n\nThe HTML template is complete. It includes a canvas, shell div, loading message, and a module script for main.ts. session.js must remain the first script after the charset tag.\n\nThe inlineBuild tool inserts the compatibility note immediately after the charset tag, placing session.js as the first script. The generator must preserve exact byte-for-byte fidelity with session.js to pass validation.\n\nThe generator will paste session.js verbatim without adding newlines to preserve exact byte matching. The HTML script tag contains no embedded `</script` sequences. Now drafting main.ts as the page entry point.\n\nDrafting the `HubClient` interface in main.ts. It defines the hub connection API including connect, ready, answer, send, and fail methods.\n\nmain.ts will read the hub from window, connect if active, dynamically import boot, and start the game with the hub and connection info. The HubClient interface uses an erased type-only import, so hub.ts is not pulled into the main module graph.\n\nRemoving the erased type import from main.ts. The `HubInfo` type will be duplicated as a minimal structural interface instead, avoiding any runtime import of hub.ts.\n\nmain.ts will check `navigator.gpu` before dynamically importing boot. If WebGPU is unavailable, it resolves a null promise instead of loading the engine. This prevents Firefox from throwing an error when boot is imported without GPU support.\n\nThe main.ts conditional now skips hub connection when WebGPU is absent. The HubClient interface will be checked against boot's start signature, and I am considering exporting a Hub type from boot for better type safety.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-304ccaef-57db-4e95-9279-6f1782c6b464-64","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"export interface Hand","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/types.ts","-A":18}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":876,"output_tokens":2055,"cache_read_input_tokens":97152,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"d25de05e-7f92-4c3e-a9af-ea7bfa694f02"}
