yOf<{ amount: { readonly unit?: string | undefined; readonly type: \\\"number\\\"; readonly default: number; readonly minimum: number; readonly maximum: number; readonly description: string; }; } & { ...; }>>'.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"command\":\"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731 && ./node_modules/.bin/prettier --write labs/game/app/boot.ts labs/game/app/page.test.ts labs/game/main.ts labs/game/net/hub.ts labs/game/net/live.ts labs/game/ui/shell.ts && ./node_modules/.bin/tsc --noEmit --pretty false --pretty false 2>&1 | head -c 25000\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Format page files and typecheck from package root\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3%2Fwork/01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151/terminal/call-601b0414-bb57-4912-bb47-2321d7c82e79-104.log\",\"total_bytes\":4762}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"53d78bb2-96a2-4b8b-a9fb-9dff1213c186"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_327","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"TypeScript compilation failed with errors, yet the process exited with code 0.\n\nThe exit code 0 was caused by a SIGPIPE from the head command closing the pipe. The real errors are in boot.ts: TypeScript fails to narrow canvas across nested functions, so onFrame sees it as nullable. I'll fix this by assigning canvas to a local variable after the null check.\n\nThe root cause is likely hoisted function declarations. TypeScript 5.4+ narrows captured const variables in closures, but nested function declarations are hoisted, so the narrowing may not reach onFrame.\n\nThe fix is to rewrite `onFrame` as a const arrow function placed after the null check. This prevents hoisting and lets TypeScript narrow `canvas` and `shell` inside the closure.\n\nA const arrow function would require reordering `onFrame` before `createEngine`, so that approach is too messy. The simpler fix is to add an early null guard inside `onFrame` itself, which narrows `canvas` and `shell` for the rest of the function. Shell errors are at lines 510 after prettier.\n\nThree more type fixes are needed. Remove description fields from SongSpec in library.ts. Add `export {}` to main.ts. In live.ts, the intersection of `{ t?: string }` with `Partial<IntentMsg>` creates a type conflict because IntentMsg.t is `'i'`. I'll fix this by omitting t from the intersection or using a different cast.\n\nThe live.ts fix will cast the raw message to `Record<string, unknown>` and check `raw.t === 'i'` before casting to `IntentMsg`.\n\nact.ts and body.ts have a pre-existing type error: property 'drop' does not exist on type 'Seat'. These files were not modified, but npm run check now includes strict type checking. I must fix them.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3f702a22-ec20-4f04-823f-96210bd715a9-105","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-m