{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_353","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Load is defined. Now writing the one-file.\n\nDrafting one-file.mts based on buildOneFile. Verifying verify.mjs and starting the build. Checking sheet geometry timing for Node compatibility.\n\nConfiguring the Vite build for one-file.mts. Setting the output path and aliasing three.js to three/webgpu.\n\nFinishing the Vite build configuration. Disabling writes, module preloads, and CSS code splitting. Inlining all assets and dynamic imports. The script will inline the HTML, replace the placeholder note, check for external references, and write the final file.\n\nString input should work for a single HTML page. Vite will emit assets with hashed names that inlineBuild can match. The classic session.js script will remain untouched. A short temporary directory is needed since Chromium is not involved.\n\nThe build will use a temporary directory under /tmp/g.XXXX, which will be removed afterward. verify.mjs is being written now. A focused end-to-end test is also being planned to launch the deliverable in Chromium, wait for engine readiness, check for console errors, verify data-about usage, and exercise the stub pad.\n\nReviewing gamepad stubbing and engine input to prepare the end-to-end test. The page uses both getGamepads and engine input, so stubbing affects samplePads while keyboard events drive the engine when focused. Autoplay enables bot ops but does not set autoText; story advances every 2500ms via tickFront.\n\nThe end-to-end test requires the page to auto-accept story, brief, debrief, title, and credits screens when autoplay is active. The current boot logic does not handle this, so an onFrame check will be added to skip those prompts automatically.\n\nAuto-accepting every frame would zip through the entire campaign in one pass. The title screen would launch a new shift, then each story box would advance instantly, followed by briefs, operations, debriefs, and credits. This creates a complete end-to-end playthrough for testing.\n\nRefining the autoplay auto-accept logic. Only story, brief, debrief, and title will be accepted automatically; credits will be left for manual stopping so the test can inspect it. The bot must win operations to reach debrief and after-story screens.\n\nThe autoplay auto-accept logic is finalized. It will trigger on every frame except during operations, credits, attract mode, or pause. Story boxes advance one per frame, so fourteen frames cover the full story sequence. The title screen accepts once to start a new shift, and the page reference is ready before the first accept fires.\n\nAuto-accept will run after finishOp in the onFrame sequence. This ensures debrief loads before the bot advances to the next screen.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8b647d21-7b12-4f90-a1d9-2c333665eee4-185","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/app/campaign.ts","offset":160,"limit":50}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":805,"output_tokens":1705,"cache_read_input_tokens":171008,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"610d5901-65e3-491f-b7ef-52dbe87fbec5"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-8b647d21-7b12-4f90-a1d9-2c333665eee4-185","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"160→export function items(c: Campaign): Item[] {\\n  if (c.screen === 'title') {\\n    const rows: Item[] = [];\\n    if (c.progress.cleared > 0 && c.progress.cleared < storyCases().length) rows.push({ id: 'continue', label: 'Continue' });\\n    rows.push({ id: 'new', label: 'New Shift' }, { id: 'board', label: 'The Board' }, { id: 'scrub', label: 'Scrub In' });\\n    rows.push({ id: 'settings', label: 'Settings' }, { id: 'about', label: 'About' });\\n    return rows;\\n  }\\n  if (c.screen === 'board') return [{ id: 'play', label: 'Open case' }, { id: 'postcards', label: 'Postcards' }, { id: 'back', label: 'Back' }];\\n  if (c.screen === 'brief') return [{ id: 'start', label: 'Start' }, { id: 'back', label: 'Back' }];\\n170→  if (c.screen === 'debrief') {\\n    return c.won\\n      ? [{ id: 'next', label: 'Continue' }]\\n      : [{ id: 'retry', label: 'Retry case' }, { id: 'board', label: 'The Board' }];\\n  }\\n  if (c.screen === 'pause') {\\n    return [\\n      { id: 'resume', label: 'Resume' },\\n      { id: 'phase', label: 'Retry phase' },\\n      { id: 'retry', label: 'Retry case' },\\n180→      { id: 'handbook', label: 'Handbook' },\\n      { id: 'settings', label: 'Settings' },\\n      { id: 'controls', label: 'Controls' },\\n      { id: 'dev', label: 'Dev Mode' },\\n      { id: 'board', label: 'Quit to Board' },\\n    ];\\n  }\\n  if (c.screen === 'settings') return settingsItems(c);\\n  if (c.screen === 'handbook') return [{ id: 'back', label: 'Back' }];\\n  if (c.screen === 'about' || c.screen === 'credits') return [{ id: 'back', label: c.screen === 'credits' ? 'Title' : 'Back' }];\\n190→  if (c.screen === 'scrub') return [{ id: 'start', label: 'Start' }, { id: 'back', label: 'Back' }];\\n  if (c.screen === 'dev') return devItems(c);\\n  return [];\\n}\\n\\nfunction settingsItems(c: Campaign): Item[] {\\n  const p = c.progress;\\n  const pages = [\\n    [\\n      { id: 'master', label: `Master ${p.master}` },\\n200→      { id: 'music', label: `Music ${p.music}` },\\n      { id: 'effects', label: `Effects ${p.effects}` },\\n      { id: 'voice', label: `Voice ${p.voice}` },\\n    ],\\n    [{ id: 'glyphs', label: `Glyphs ${p.glyphs === 'xbox' ? 'Xbox' : 'PlayStation'}` }],\\n    [\\n      { id: 'difficulty', label: `Difficulty ${p.difficulty}` },\\n      { id: 'simple', label: `Simple Gift ${p.simple ? 'on' : 'off'}` },\\n      { id: 'autoText', label: `Auto text ${p.autoText ? 'on' : 'off'}` },\\n    ],\",\"content_concise\":\"160→export function items(c: Campaign): Item[] {\\n  if (c.screen === 'title') {\\n    const rows: Item[] = [];\\n    if (c.progress.cleared > 0 && c.progress.cleared < storyCases().length) rows.push({ id: 'continue', label: 'Continue' });\\n    rows.push({ id: 'new', label: 'New Shift' }, { id: 'board', label: 'The Board' }, { id: 'scrub', label: 'Scrub In' });\\n    rows.push({ id: 'settings', label: 'Settings' }, { id: 'about', label: 'About' });\\n    return rows;\\n  }\\n  if (c.screen === 'board') return [{ id: 'play', label: 'Open case' }, { id: 'postcards', label: 'Postcards' }, { id: 'back', label: 'Back' }];\\n  if (c.screen === 'brief') return [{ id: 'start', label: 'Start' }, { id: 'back', label: 'Back' }];\\n170→  if (c.screen === 'debrief') {\\n    return c.won\\n      ? [{ id: 'next', label: 'Continue' }]\\n      : [{ id: 'retry', label: 'Retry case' }, { id: 'board', label: 'The Board' }];\\n  }\\n  if (c.screen === 'pause') {\\n    return [\\n      { id: 'resume', label: 'Resume' },\\n      { id: 'phase', label: 'Retry phase' },\\n      { id: 'retry', label: 'Retry case' },\\n180→      { id: 'handbook', label: 'Handbook' },\\n      { id: 'settings', label: 'Settings' },\\n      { id: 'controls', label: 'Controls' },\\n      { id: 'dev', label: 'Dev Mode' },\\n      { id: 'board', label: 'Quit to Board' },\\n    ];\\n  }\\n  if (c.screen === 'settings') return settingsItems(c);\\n  if (c.screen === 'handbook') return [{ id: 'back', label: 'Back' }];\\n  if (c.screen === 'about' || c.screen === 'credits') return [{ id: 'back', label: c.screen === 'credits' ? 'Title' : 'Back' }];\\n190→  if (c.screen === 'scrub') return [{ id: 'start', label: 'Start' }, { id: 'back', label: 'Back' }];\\n  if (c.screen === 'dev') return devItems(c);\\n  return [];\\n}\\n\\nfunction settingsItems(c: Campaign): Item[] {\\n  const p = c.progress;\\n  const pages = [\\n    [\\n      { id: 'master', label: `Master ${p.master}` },\\n200→      { id: 'music', label: `Music ${p.music}` },\\n      { id: 'effects', label: `Effects ${p.effects}` },\\n      { id: 'voice', label: `Voice ${p.voice}` },\\n    ],\\n    [{ id: 'glyphs', label: `Glyphs ${p.glyphs === 'xbox' ? 'Xbox' : 'PlayStation'}` }],\\n    [\\n      { id: 'difficulty', label: `Difficulty ${p.difficulty}` },\\n      { id: 'simple', label: `Simple Gift ${p.simple ? 'on' : 'off'}` },\\n      { id: 'autoText', label: `Auto text ${p.autoText ? 'on' : 'off'}` },\\n    ],\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/app/campaign.ts\",\"offset\":160,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"export function items(c: Campaign): Item[] {\\n  if (c.screen === 'title') {\\n    const rows: Item[] = [];\\n    if (c.progress.cleared > 0 && c.progress.cleared < storyCases().length) rows.push({ id: 'continue', label: 'Continue' });\\n    rows.push({ id: 'new', label: 'New Shift' }, { id: 'board', label: 'The Board' }, { id: 'scrub', label: 'Scrub In' });\\n    rows.push({ id: 'settings', label: 'Settings' }, { id: 'about', label: 'About' });\\n    return rows;\\n  }\\n  if (c.screen === 'board') return [{ id: 'play', label: 'Open case' }, { id: 'postcards', label: 'Postcards' }, { id: 'back', label: