{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_354","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Auto-accepting every frame on the title screen would advance the story from \"New Shift\" to \"story\".\n\nAuto-accepting should only happen after leaving the title screen. Returning to it might restart the campaign. The credits screen stops playback. Story-to-brief transitions correctly trigger the next opening. First story frames may run before the campaign draws. Autoplay sets timeScale to 8 during the opening sequence. syncRun detects the op screen and seeds autoplay before bot hands play. The bot finishes when the game is won.\n\nLeaving the opening for debrief triggers a scene reseed to the title. The 3D view shows the harbour. The desiredRun logic routes debrief and story to title. Switching from op to debrief changes the signature and reseeds. timeScale drops to 1 when the screen becomes debrief.\n\nAuto-accepting on the debrief frame is safe because syncRun already ran with the title run this frame, and the next frame syncRun stays on title. The story screen then appears normally.\n\nThe e2e test for the whole game requires this speed. Separate menu checks use a page without autoplay.\n\nAuto-accept should only trigger when the URL contains an `autoplay` query parameter. It must be skipped during the opening and credits screens.\n\nThe auto-accept logic will be inserted after the finishOp block. It excludes the attract screen and pauses during autoplay. Dev mode tests run without autoplay. The boot file is 540 lines, so four new lines are acceptable. I will write the tools next and run the campaign test. The one-file Vite build may take 30 to 60 seconds, so I will start it now while writing the e2e tests. The song library imports successfully.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9e1d5452-9549-4412-9bda-81f8f4d8298c-186","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"\"type\"","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok