{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_363","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The page boots from file:// without errors. It shows the title screen and usage text.\n\nRemaining verification tasks include end-to-end playthroughs, menus, audio, and feedback sections. I will write e2e.mjs to test the campaign at timescale 8 and run it with a timeout of eight cases.\n\nThe campaign test will run for eight minutes. I am checking that the credits screen appears after the compass. I am also reviewing autoplay edge cases like scene resets and retry loops.\n\nAutoplay is confirmed to be active from the URL parameter and re-set when entering an operation. The first frames correctly skip the title screen until the page initializes, then accept it to start the story. I am also verifying that timeScale 8 actually multiplies engine steps.\n\nHeadless WebGPU runs at roughly 10–20 fps. Eight campaign cases will take about 8–10 minutes total, so the test timeout is set to 12 minutes. The end-to-end script will poll the current screen and log progress to scratch. Other checks will run on separate pages so a campaign failure does not hide boot issues.\n\nI drafted a `report` helper to log test results as JSON. The full checklist now covers boot, autoplay credits, attract mode with key exit and storage checks, menus for pad and mouse, the dev slider, touch message, audio, couch mode, and browser-specific WebGPU warnings. I will run Firefox and WebKit separately after closing Chromium. I am also checking how keyboard input reaches the engine so menu tests can press ArrowDown and Enter.\n\nKeyboard input should reach the engine through the window if the canvas or page is focused. The attract-mode test will wait eleven seconds on the title screen, confirm the DEMO message appears, and verify that localStorage progress remains unchanged. For touch detection, I will use Playwright’s iPhone device profile to simulate a coarse-pointer viewport.\n\nI will use Playwright’s Pixel 5 device profile with `hasTouch: true` to simulate a coarse-pointer viewport. The touch overlay must display the exact message “Controller or keyboard required” and a Settings button. After ten seconds the screen should switch to attract mode while the touch overlay persists, because a tap does not trigger a keydown that would clear the hold state.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-11575ac1-0dfe-4433-8eb1-1ad8bc194e08-198","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/input/hands.ts","offset":210,"limit":60}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":593,"output_tokens":1930,"cache_read_input_tokens":181760,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"f4b3cdd0-8480-44af-9826-3646eb63cdcf"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-11575ac1-0dfe-4433-8eb1-1ad8bc194e08-198","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"210→/** Local gloves, ahead of the sim. */\\nexport function gloveSpots(seats: number): { x: number; z: number }[] {\\n  return cursors.slice(0, seats).map((cursor) => ({ x: cursor.x, z: cursor.z }));\\n}\\n\\n/** Read every pad once this frame. Menu edges and tool taps share it. */\\nexport function samplePads(): MenuEdges {\\n  const edges: MenuEdges = {\\n    accept: false,\\n    cancel: false,\\n220→    up: false,\\n    down: false,\\n    left: false,\\n    right: false,\\n    pause: false,\\n    any: false,\\n    claim: -1,\\n  };\\n  const list = pads();\\n  for (let seat = 0; seat < 4; seat++) {\\n230→    const pad = list[seat];\\n    for (let index = 0; index < 16; index++) {\\n      const now = down(pad, index);\\n      roseNow[seat][index] = now && padWas[seat][index] !== true;\\n      padWas[seat][index] = now;\\n    }\\n    if (!pad) continue;\\n    const create = down(pad, 8);\\n    if (tapped(seat, 0)) {\\n      edges.accept = true;\\n240→      edges.claim = seat;\\n    }\\n    if (tapped(seat, 1)) edges.cancel = true;\\n    if (tapped(seat, 12)) edges.up = true;\\n    if (tapped(seat, 13)) edges.down = true;\\n    if (tapped(seat, 14)) edges.left = true;\\n    if (tapped(seat, 15)) edges.right = true;\\n    if (!create && tapped(seat, 9)) edges.pause = true;\\n    const stick = Math.hypot(pad.axes[0] ?? 0, pad.axes[1] ?? 0) > 0.5;\\n    if (stick || pad.buttons.some((button) => button.pressed)) edges.any = true;\\n250→  }\\n  sampled = true;\\n  return edges;\\n}\\n\\n/** Clear the sample so the next frame reads the pads again. */\\nexport function endSample(): void {\\n  sampled = false;\\n}\\n\\n260→/** True when the device has no fine pointer and no pad yet. */\\nexport function touchOnly(): boolean {\\n  const fine = window.matchMedia?.('(any-pointer: fine)').matches ?? true;\\n  return !fine && pads().length === 0;\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"210→/** Local gloves, ahead of the sim. */\\nexport function gloveSpots(seats: number): { x: number; z: number }[] {\\n  return cursors.slice(0, seats).map((cursor) => ({ x: cursor.x, z: cursor.z }));\\n}\\n\\n/** Read every pad once this frame. Menu edges and tool taps share it. */\\nexport function samplePads(): MenuEdges {\\n  const edges: MenuEdges = {\\n    accept: false,\\n    cancel: false,\\n220→    up: false,\\n    down: false,\\n    left: false,\\n    right: false,\\n    pause: false,\\n    any: false,\\n    claim: -1,\\n  };\\n  const list = pads();\\n  for (let seat = 0; seat < 4; seat++) {\\n230→    const pad = list[seat];\\n    for (let index = 0; index < 16; index++) {\\n      const now = down(pad, index);\\n      roseNow[seat][index] = now && padWas[seat][index] !== true;\\n      padWas[seat][index] = now;\\n    }\\n    if (!pad) continue;\\n    const create = down(pad, 8);\\n    if (tapped(seat, 0)) {\\n      edges.accept = true;\\n240→      edges.claim = seat;\\n    }\\n    if (tapped(seat, 1)) edges.cancel = true;\\n    if (tapped(seat, 12)) edges.up = true;\\n    if (tapped(seat, 13)) edges.down = true;\\n    if (tapped(seat, 14)) edges.left = true;\\n    if (tapped(seat, 15)) edges.right = true;\\n    if (!create && tapped(seat, 9)) edges.pause = true;\\n    const stick = Math.hypot(pad.axes[0] ?? 0, pad.axes[1] ?? 0) > 0.5;\\n    if (stick || pad.buttons.some((button) => button.pressed)) edges.any = true;\\n250→  }\\n  sampled = true;\\n  return edges;\\n}\\n\\n/** Clear the sample so the next frame reads the pads again. */\\nexport function endSample(): void {\\n  sampled = false;\\n}\\n\\n260→/** True when the device has no fine pointer and no pad yet. */\\nexport function touchOnly(): boolean {\\n  const fine = window.matchMedia?.('(any-pointer: fine)').matches ?? true;\\n  return !fine && pads().length === 0;\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/