{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-6997022b-76f9-40e8-b9de-86acf05c4f58-199","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"40→}\\n\\nconst cursors: Cursor[] = [0, 1, 2, 3].map(() => ({ x: 0, z: 0, tool: 1, site: 0, radial: false, radialTool: 1 }));\\nconst padWas: boolean[][] = [[], [], [], []];\\nconst roseNow: boolean[][] = [[], [], [], []];\\nlet pointerX = 0;\\nlet pointerY = 0;\\nlet pointerLive = false;\\nlet sampled = false;\\n\\n50→/** Remember the pointer. Called once from the page. */\\nexport function watchPointer(canvas: HTMLCanvasElement): void {\\n  canvas.addEventListener('pointermove', (event) => {\\n    pointerX = event.clientX;\\n    pointerY = event.clientY;\\n    pointerLive = true;\\n  });\\n}\\n\\n/** Connected pads in seat order. */\\n60→function pads(): Gamepad[] {\\n  const list = navigator.getGamepads?.() ?? [];\\n  const out: Gamepad[] = [];\\n  for (const pad of list) if (pad && pad.connected) out.push(pad);\\n  return out;\\n}\\n\\n/** A pad button is down. */\\nfunction down(pad: Gamepad | undefined, index: number): boolean {\\n  return !!pad && !!pad.buttons[index]?.pressed;\",\"content_concise\":\"40→}\\n\\nconst cursors: Cursor[] = [0, 1, 2, 3].map(() => ({ x: 0, z: 0, tool: 1, site: 0, radial: false, radialTool: 1 }));\\nconst padWas: boolean[][] = [[], [], [], []];\\nconst roseNow: boolean[][] = [[], [], [], []];\\nlet pointerX = 0;\\nlet pointerY = 0;\\nlet pointerLive = false;\\nlet sampled = false;\\n\\n50→/** Remember the pointer. Called once from the page. */\\nexport function watchPointer(canvas: HTMLCanvasElement): void {\\n  canvas.addEventListener('pointermove', (event) => {\\n    pointerX = event.clientX;\\n    pointerY = event.clientY;\\n    pointerLive = true;\\n  });\\n}\\n\\n/** Connected pads in seat order. */\\n60→function pads(): Gamepad[] {\\n  const list = navigator.getGamepads?.() ?? [];\\n  const out: Gamepad[] = [];\\n  for (const pad of list) if (pad && pad.connected) out.push(pad);\\n  return out;\\n}\\n\\n/** A pad button is down. */\\nfunction down(pad: Gamepad | undefined, index: number): boolean {\\n  return !!pad && !!pad.buttons[index]?.pressed;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/input/hands.ts\",\"offset\":40,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"}\\n\\nconst cursors: Cursor[] = [0, 1, 2, 3].map(() => ({ x: 0, z: 0, tool: 1, site: 0, radial: false, radialTool: 1 }));\\nconst padWas: boolean[][] = [[], [], [], []];\\nconst roseNow: boolean[][] = [[], [], [], []];\\nlet pointerX = 0;\\nlet pointerY = 0;\\nlet pointerLive = false;\\nlet sampled = false;\\n\\n/** Remember the pointer. Called once from the page. */\\nexport function watchPointer(canvas: HTMLCanvasElement): void {\\n  canvas.addEventListener('pointermove', (event) => {\\n    pointerX = event.clientX;\\n    pointerY = event.clientY;\\n    pointerLive = true;\\n  });\\n}\\n\\n/** Connected pads in seat order. */\\nfunction pads(): Gamepad[] {\\n  const list = navigator.getGamepads?.() ?? [];\\n  const out: Gamepad[] = [];\\n  for (const pad of list) if (pad && pad.connected) out.push(pad);\\n  return out;\\n}\\n\\n/** A pad button is down. */\\nfunction down(pad: Gamepad | undefined, index: number): boolean {\\n  return !!pad && !!pad.buttons[index]?.pressed;\\n\",\"total_lines\":264}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"774ba384-36c6-47e1-9775-d1c0720bc79c"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_365","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"samplePads uses only connected pads. It indexes them by seat 0 through 3.\n\nSeat assignment follows connection order, not gamepad index. The touchOnly check correctly detects no connected pads. Playwright's Pixel 7 device sets touch and mobile flags, but headless Chromium may still report fine pointers unless coarse is forced.\n\nHeadless Chromium may still report fine pointers. The test will verify the touch message appears on Playwright devices. If the media query is not emulated, a CDP command can force touch events.\n\nStandard Playwright media emulation does not change pointer types. The CDP command `setTouchEmulationEnabled` can force `any-pointer: coarse` in recent Chrome. I will try this and record the result if the touch message still does not appear.\n\nThe test and game must agree on the touch message. If Chromium cannot flip the media query, the end-to-end test will fail. I am weighing options to resolve this.\n\nI will try the CDP touch emulation command first in the boot experiment. The end-to-end test will run as a dedicated script so I can see progress immediately and avoid waiting on a large file if autoplay fails early. I will write tools/e2e.mjs with all checks, starting with the campaign, and log JSON to console so partial results survive a kill.\n\nThe verify script must receive all JSON lines and exit with code 0. I will inspect the localStorage key prefix to ensure attract mode does not write progress. For glyph verification, I will switch the input setting to Xbox and check that the prompt text updates to gamepad face glyphs. After selecting keyboard, the prompt should display Enter or a key glyph. The test must target a screen that actually renders pad glyphs.\n\nI will focus on reliable checks. The dev slider test requires booting a case via URL, pausing, opening Dev Mode, changing the slider live, and verifying the setting. I must ensure the scene does not auto-start from the URL parameter.\n\nThe dev mode test requires an active op screen, so I will start a shift by pressing Enter or Space from the title screen. I will avoid adding a custom URL parameter for this flow.\n\nThe uiAccept binding is Enter, Space, and PadSouth. On the title screen, Enter triggers New Shift when focus is at zero. After pressing Enter through the fourteen story boxes to reach the brief, pressing Enter again starts the op. Escape pauses the scene, and the Dev Mode option can then be reached by keyboard or click.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e7064442-f626-4ee8-845a-921752baa26b-200","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/app/campaign.ts","offset":210,"limit":45}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":545,"output_tokens":1458,"cache_read_input_tokens":184832,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"ec85a83e-611e-44c5-9413-0a705a54c604"}
