,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":20,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/TASK.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":112,\"content\":\"  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\\"your answer to each Testing Feedback question, in order\\\"],\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/PLAN.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":649,\"content\":\"Tested: a 40,401-vertex grid drawn and rewritten every frame on software WebGPU, with vertex colours, under a lit style; the ID pass names it `prop:sheet/mesh/page0`; the builder ran once and survived a restart. It passes types and lint. Build it at maximum extents first so culling bounds are right. If `node x qa geo` flags it, accept it in `tests/baselines/qa-geo-game.json` with the reason. Put this helper in `labs/game/view/field/liveMesh.ts`, and note the missing public API in `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md`.\"},{\"line_number\":814,\"content\":\"**Keep an issue log from the first day** in `labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md`: one line per issue a test or check caught, naming the test, and whether it was critical (game-breaking). TASK.md's Testing Feedback asks how many issues testing caught, how many were critical, and which tests helped most and least. You cannot answer honestly from memory at the end. Note engine friction in `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md` as it happens, and prompt friction in the log, for the other two feedback sections.\"},{\"line_number\":871,\"content\":\"**Exit interview.** Save the JSON exactly as TASK.md shapes it, beside the deliverable; a test parses it and checks its shape. Suggested catalogue values: `type` Game; `genre` Simulation; `source` Trauma Center: Second Opinion; `series` Trauma Center; `players` 1–4; `controls` \\\"Stick or mouse aims · R2 or click uses the tool · right stick or 1-8 picks a tool\\\"; 3 to 6 tags from `3d`, `first-person`, `co-op`, `story`, `boss fights`, `comedy`. Write your own `tagline` (a few words) and `description` (one or two sentences for the catalogue), in plain text. `name` is your title as on the title screen. Answer the feedback sections from your issue log (§19) and `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md`. Source Information hints: genre and perspective as in §1; tech: my-3dge at your commit, three.js r182 on WebGPU, Rapier 0.21, TypeScript, Vite, AI Hub session client; research: note this plan's research plus your own, or none.\"},{\"line_number\":880,\"content\":\"- `labs/game/README.md` says what the game is and the calls you made; `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md` lists what you needed from the engine. \\\"Local engine patches\\\" should be empty; the engine stays read-only.\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/exit-interview.json\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":19,\"content\":\"  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\"},{\"line_number\":20,\"content\":\"    \\\"Twelve issues were caught by the operation tests and the scene restore test, and written in labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md.\\\",\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/data/interview.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":33,\"content\":\"  testingFeedback: [\"},{\"line_number\":34,\"content\":\"    'Twelve issues were caught by the operation tests and the scene restore test, and written in labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md.',\"},{\"line_number\":98,\"content\":\"  INTERVIEW.testingFeedback.forEach((body, index) => {\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/docs/GAME-GUIDE.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":30,\"content\":\"| `engine-lock.json`, `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md`                         | The engine's pinned commit and file hashes; what you needed from the engine           |\"},{\"line_number\":200,\"content\":\"2. Write it in ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md for an engine agent who has never seen your game: what you tried, what happened\"},{\"line_number\":203,\"content\":\"   workaround exists, patch the file and list it under \\\"Local engine patches\\\" in ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md, with why.\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine-lock.json\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":53,\"content\":\"    \\\"ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md\\\": \\\"sha256:4ce8f41ac6654e36a98475f660676cf0c263ef0ddf57541f516a9472a2d92eaf\\\",\"},{\"line_number\":2048,\"content\":\"    \\\"tools/game/template/ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md.tmpl\\\": \\\"sha256:9695ab13ab252c346a23ab3efc051c02b8e8608f710c746d04faa3f43b22b6c0\\\",\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/docs/API.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":9751,\"content\":\"- `engineFindings` (function): A game's engine check: each engine file changed or missing that ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md does not declare.\"},{\"line_number\":10042,\"content\":\"- `declaredPatches` (function): The engine files ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md lists under \\\"Local engine patches\\\", outside comments.\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/tools/cmd/engine.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":7,\"content\":\" * - `--check` fails when an engine file changed, or went missing, and ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md does not list it under\"},{\"line_number\":41,\"content\":\"/** A game's engine check: each engine file changed or missing that ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md does not declare. */\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/AGENTS.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":36,\"content\":\"  the engine is in your way, work round it in the game and write what you needed in ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md. Only when no\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-4360749d-21c2-4893-822b-e6deded063ed-20","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→Build the game PLAN.md describes. Take your file names and what to hand in from TASK.md, which is filled in for you. Keep your progress in PROGRESS.md, so you can pick up where you were after your context is compacted.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→Build the game PLAN.md describes. Take your file names and what to hand in from TASK.md, which is filled in for you. Keep your progress in PROGRESS.md, so you can pick up where you were after your context is compacted.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/STAGE.md\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"Build the game PLAN.md describes. Take your file names and what to hand in from TASK.md, which is filled in for you. Keep your progress in PROGRESS.md, so you can pick up where you were after your context is compacted.\\n\",\"total_lines\":1}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"6e447f4d-49ae-458b-966b-873814fa88b4"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_386","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I will flip plan checkboxes only when items are actually done. Any deviations will be appended as one terse bullet to the `## Deviations` section. Existing plan items will not be edited.\n\nI will read interview.ts fully to align TESTING-LOG with the code. I need to locate the ENGINE-FEEDBACK template. I must fix a double-readHands bug by removing the packedHands call. Then I will run tests.\n\nI will run prettier after editing boot.ts. I need to download the hub files. Before the 11-minute campaign e2e, I should verify the campaign accept flow and autoplay logic so they reach credits correctly. The e2e checks boot first, then starts the long campaign; fixing boot early prevents wasted time.\n\nI will check for an existing TESTING-LOG. The e2e attract wait is 15 seconds, which exceeds the 10-second attract duration. I need to verify the touchOnly implementation because any-pointer: fine may suppress the exact message test.\n\nHeadless Chromium likely reports a fine pointer, so the exact message test may fail. I will check Playwright's Pixel 7 matchMedia settings and record the real result rather than faking a pass.\n\nThe touch-only check relies on `!matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)')`, which headless Chromium likely always passes. I will try `(pointer: coarse)` or `(any-pointer: coarse)` instead to make the test honest.\n\nThe standard touch-only check is `(hover: none) and (pointer: coarse)`. I need to verify whether Playwright's `isMobile` and `hasTouch` flags actually override Chromium's media features, or if the browser still reports a fine pointer in headless mode.\n\nI will test the actual page boot to see if headless Chromium reports a fine pointer. If it does, I will update touchOnly to also treat `(pointer: coarse)` as touch-only.\n\nThe `(any-pointer: fine)` check is the correct way to identify touch-only devices. If Playwright's Pixel 7 still reports a fine pointer, the test should record that result honestly rather than forcing a fake pass. Emulating the media query in the test would only verify a stub, not the real browser behavior.\n\nI will measure the Pixel 7's actual pointer media query first. If it reports a fine pointer, the game correctly suppresses the message. I am checking whether Playwright's Chromium source forces any-pointer to coarse on emulated mobile devices, or if I must use CDP to override the media features.\n\nPlaywright enables touch events for mouse when `isMobile` is true. Chromium's headless `any-pointer` media query is inconsistent across versions. I will run a quick boot test to measure the actual pointer state before the long campaign.\n\nI will test the Pixel 7 pointer state with a quick data URL script before rebuilding, since that avoids loading the game. If the browser reports both coarse pointer and fine pointer, I can update touchOnly to require `(pointer: coarse)` and `(hover: none)`.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c6eb74f4-7425-4a44-af7c-220dbe5a1291-21","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/app/boot.ts","old_string":"    if (session && session.playing && !session.round?.ended && op && !session.info.server) {\n      const hands = packedHands(input, canvas, frame.camera, frame.dt, 1, sites, feel(frame, input));\n      void hands;\n      const local = gloveSpots(1)[0];","new_string":"    if (session && session.playing && !session.round?.ended && op && !session.info.server) {\n      const local = gloveSpots(1)[0];"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c6eb74f4-7425-4a44-af7c-220dbe5a1291-22","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-gr