he six interview answers. Note the missing public API for mutating a kept BufferGeometry and the missing post-restore scene hook.\"},{\"line_number\":272,\"content\":\"- TESTING-LOG.md (twelve issues, seven critical, matching the interview), ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md content, PROGRESS.md finished, labs/game/README.md rewrite (controls, friend play).\"},{\"line_number\":449,\"content\":\"- ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md exists but Requests/Friction/Local engine patches are empty comments. TESTING-LOG.md does NOT exist yet. Local patches must stay empty. Editing ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md, package.json scripts, labs/game files, and root README does NOT fail engine-lock: verifyGame only hashes lock.files (engine dirs), not templates. Declared patches are backtick paths under `## Local engine patches`. Do not edit engine sources. session.js NOW downloaded unmodified to labs/game/vendor/session.js (16707 bytes). Plan checkboxes untouched. No root HTML, exit-interview.json, or PROGRESS.md yet. Work root contains PLAN.md, STAGE.md, TASK.md, and the dev folder. Do not recreate work/node_modules.\"},{\"line_number\":618,\"content\":\"Planned files still NOT written: ui CSS, labs/game/main.ts rewrite (thin dynamic import), index.html rewrite, net Sample export, work-root HTML, exit-interview.json, PROGRESS.md, TESTING-LOG.md, ENGINE-FEEDBACK content, labs/game/README.md rewrite, tools/verify.mjs, tools/e2e.mjs, tools/hub.mjs, tools/one-file.mts, harness html/bridge/round.js, interview deep-equal test. main.ts and index.html are STILL the starter.\"},{\"line_number\":701,\"content\":\"- TESTING-LOG.md (~12 issues, 7 critical as already drafted in the interview) and ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md content (requests/friction; Local engine patches stays empty). PROGRESS.md finished. labs/game/README.md rewrite (controls, friend play).\"},{\"line_number\":2311,\"content\":\"**Keep an issue log from the first day** in `labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md`: one line per issue a test or check caught, naming the test, and whether it was critical (game-breaking). TASK.md's Testing Feedback asks how many issues testing caught, how many were critical, and which tests helped most and least. You cannot answer honestly from memory at the end. Note engine friction in `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md` as it happens, and prompt friction in the log, for the other two feedback sections.\"},{\"line_number\":2474,\"content\":\"- How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?\"},{\"line_number\":2635,\"content\":\"    'Twelve issues were caught by the operation tests and the scene restore test, and written in labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md.',\"},{\"line_number\":2636,\"content\":\"    'Seven were game-breaking: a restore stepped the wrong body, the gala flap never finished, Reverie left the surface early, Solace children stacked, the syringe bound the wrong target, stitches landed off the wound, and co-op copies shared one point.',\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3%2Fwork/01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151/compaction/segment_001.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":175,\"content\":\"- Everything after content: sequencer test (host + 3 clients, latency, jitter, 5% loss, leaver, 3600 ticks, equal hashes), scene game:main, live sheet, hand, OR, HUD, all screens, glyphs, saves, attract (10s, game.attract, createStore mode demo), dev sliders calling setSlider/resetSliders, audio (music bus 0.1, no &lt;audio&gt;, no data URLs), couch seats, AI Hub session.js pasted unmodified as the first script, one-file HTML at the work-root basename, verify.mjs exactly as PLAN §19 (sets its own short TMPDIR and CHROMIUM_PATH), e2e, hub harness, exit-interview.json, PROGRESS.md, TESTING-LOG.md, ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md, labs/game/README.md. Then run the whole verification plan and save logs under scratch. Stop only PIDs this work started. Remove the short TMPDIR at the end.\"},{\"line_number\":189,\"content\":\"- Hand-ins: root HTML (basename), exit-interview.json, PROGRESS.md, About screen with the four feedback sections, TESTING-LOG.md, ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md kept honest, labs/game/README.md.\"},{\"line_number\":405,\"content\":\"- Exit-interview feedback questions, in order: Testing — how many issues testing caught; how many critical/game-breaking; most helpful test; least helpful test. Engine — liked most; stuck or guessed wrong; most important thing built yourself; hardest part of using the engine; what changed in the engine and why (none if nothing); one thing you would change. Prompt — liked most; confusing; hardest; what to change.\"},{\"line_number\":433,\"content\":\"- ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md exists with empty Requests, Friction, and Local engine patches. Local engine patches must stay empty. Note missing public API for live meshes if the constructor trick is used (PLAN §17.3). Keep a TESTING-LOG.md from the first failing test. Prompt friction notes too. Suggested verify browser launch and hub flags are in PLAN §§16 and 19.\"},{\"line_number\":605,\"content\":\"- npm run verify green; exit-interview.json; About screen with data-about=\\\"usage\\\"; PROGRESS.md; TESTING-LOG.md and ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md filled from real issues; labs/game/README.md describing the game.\"},{\"line_number\":6090,\"content\":\"**Keep an issue log from the first day** in `labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md`: one line per issue a test or check caught, naming the test, and whether it was critical (game-breaking). TASK.md's Testing Feedback asks how many issues testing caught, how many were critical, and which tests helped most and least. You cannot answer honestly from memory at the end. Note engine friction in `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md` as it happens, and prompt friction in the log, for the other two feedback sections.\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3%2Fwork/01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151/compaction/segment_002.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":151,\"content\":\"Planned new files still NOT written: view/looks.ts, view/props.ts, view/field/sheet.ts, audio/songs.ts, audio/mix.ts, input/hands.ts, input/glyphs.ts, ui/copy.ts, ui/shell.css, ui screens, app/campaign.ts, app/save.ts, net/hub.ts, tools/verify.mjs, tools/e2e.mjs, tools/hub.mjs, tools/one-file.mts, work-root HTML, exit-interview.json, PROGRESS.md, TESTING-LOG.md update, ENGINE-FEEDBACK update, labs/game/README.md. Scratch scripts implementer/run-cases.ts and implementer/debug-gala.ts if still present must not ship. Do not leave them as shipped tests.\"},{\"line_number\":189,\"content\":\"- Hand-ins: root HTML (basename Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731.html), exit-interview.json, PROGRESS.md, About screen with the four feedback sections and data-about=\\\"usage\\\", TESTING-LOG.md, ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md kept honest (no local patches), labs/game/README.md.\"},{\"line_number\":505,\"content\":\"- Everything after content: sequencer test (host + 3 clients, latency, jitter, 5% loss, leaver, 3600 ticks, equal hashes), scene game:main, live sheet, hand, OR, HUD, all screens, glyphs, saves, attract (10s, game.attract, createStore mode demo), dev sliders calling setSlider/resetSliders, audio (music bus 0.1, no &lt;audio&gt;, no data URLs), couch seats, AI Hub session.js pasted unmodified as the first script, one-file HTML at the work-root basename, verify.mjs exactly as PLAN §19 (sets its own short TMPDIR and CHROMIUM_PATH), e2e, hub harness, exit-interview.json, PROGRESS.md, TESTING-LOG.md, ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md, labs/game/README.md. Then run the whole verification plan and save logs under scratch. Stop only PIDs this work started. Remove the short TMPDIR at the end.\"},{\"line_number\":519,\"content\":\"- Hand-ins: root HTML (basename), exit-interview.json, PROGRESS.md, About screen with the four feedback sections, TESTING-LOG.md, ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md kept honest, labs/game/README.md.\"},{\"line_number\":1844,\"conten