ps four peers on one hash through loss and a leaver', () => {\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/best.test.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":10,\"content\":\"describe(\\\"the starter game's best round\\\", () => {\"},{\"line_number\":11,\"content\":\"  it('keeps the fastest won round across pages, and a replay never sets one', () => {\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/op.test.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":22,\"content\":\"describe('operation sim', () => {\"},{\"line_number\":23,\"content\":\"  it('names a tool or a refusal for every pair', () => {\"},{\"line_number\":27,\"content\":\"  it('drains a pool and refuses the scalpel without a slip', () => {\"},{\"line_number\":40,\"content\":\"  it('injects on release inside the band and refuses a syringe on a shard', () => {\"},{\"line_number\":56,\"content\":\"  it('grades cuts and injections on the published bands', () => {\"},{\"line_number\":66,\"content\":\"  it('loses when the clock runs out', () => {\"},{\"line_number\":74,\"content\":\"  it('loses when slips pass the limit', () => {\"},{\"line_number\":83,\"content\":\"  it('brings a patient back inside the green band and fails two misses', () => {\"},{\"line_number\":107,\"content\":\"  it('fails a flatline immediately when the case has no Code', () => {\"},{\"line_number\":115,\"content\":\"  it('deepens a pool on a site nobody is standing on', () => {\"},{\"line_number\":124,\"content\":\"  it('slows field time in Stillpoint and holds vitals in Second Pulse', () => {\"},{\"line_number\":146,\"content\":\"  it('starts a Consult when two gifts land inside a second', () => {\"},{\"line_number\":159,\"content\":\"  it('telegraphs a Lull before the numb patch', () => {\"},{\"line_number\":170,\"content\":\"  it('splits Solace, then lets the laser finish a third generation', () => {\"},{\"line_number\":184,\"content\":\"  it('surfaces Reverie under the laser and sinks it again', () => {\"},{\"line_number\":199,\"content\":\"  it('lacquers a wound beside a Balm cell and fades the film after the node dies', () => {\"},{\"line_number\":212,\"content\":\"  it('walks Mercy from motes to the exposed binders', () => {\"},{\"line_number\":228,\"content\":\"  it('scales the clock and the slip cap with difficulty', () => {\"},{\"line_number\":238,\"content\":\"  it('clamps a slider and puts it back on reset', () => {\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/app/page.test.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":12,\"content\":\"describe('page sources', () => {\"},{\"line_number\":13,\"content\":\"  it('pastes session.js first and unchanged', () => {\"},{\"line_number\":24,\"content\":\"  it('matches the exit interview on disk', () => {\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/app/campaign.test.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":8,\"content\":\"describe('campaign', () => {\"},{\"line_number\":9,\"content\":\"  it('walks a new shift as far as the first briefing', () => {\"},{\"line_number\":26,\"content\":\"  it('records a win and then the scene after the case', () => {\"},{\"line_number\":40,\"content\":\"  it('starts the kiosk after ten seconds on the title and leaves it on a press', () => {\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f5f8cee7-bef8-407a-8084-6151077c9abc-42","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→# Engine feedback: trauma-compass\\n\\nWhat this game needed from the my-3dge engine (at 2dbd829) and did not get. The owner collects this file\\nfrom every game to improve the engine, so write each item for an engine agent who has never seen this repository:\\nwhat you tried, what happened (the command, the error code), what you expected, and what you did instead.\\n\\n## Requests\\n\\n<!-- What the engine should add or fix, most costly first. -->\\n10→\\n## Friction\\n\\n<!-- Docs, errors, templates or APIs that slowed you down or misled you, most costly first. -->\\n\\n## Local engine patches\\n\\n<!--\\n`npm run check` accepts an edited engine file only when it is listed here, one line each, its path in backticks:\\n- `engine/path/to/file.ts`: why no workaround in the game would do, and what the engine should change instead.\\n20→-->\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→# Engine feedback: trauma-compass\\n\\nWhat this game needed from the my-3dge engine (at 2dbd829) and did not get. The owner collects this file\\nfrom every game to improve the engine, so write each item for an engine agent who has never seen this repository:\\nwhat you tried, what happened (the command, the error code), what you expected, and what you did instead.\\n\\n## Requests\\n\\n<!-- What the engine should add or fix, most costly first. -->\\n10→\\n## Friction\\n\\n<!-- Docs, errors, templates or APIs that slowed you down or misled you, most costly first. -->\\n\\n## Local engine patches\\n\\n<!--\\n`npm run check` accepts an edited engine file only when it is listed here, one line each, its path in backticks:\\n- `engine/path/to/file.ts`: why no workaround in the game would do, and what the engine should change instead.\\n20→-->\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"# Engine feedback: trauma-compass\\n\\nWhat this game needed from the my-3dge engine (at 2dbd829) and did not get. The owner collects this file\\nfrom every game to improve the engine, so write each item for an engine agent who has never seen this repository:\\nwhat you tried, what happened (the command, the error code), what you expected, and what you did instead.\\n\\n## Requests\\n\\n<!-- What the engine should add or fix, most costly first. -->\\n\\n## Friction\\n\\n<!-- Docs, errors, templates or APIs that slowed you down or misled you, most costly first. -->\\n\\n## Local engine patches\\n\\n<!--\\n`npm run check` accepts an edited engine file only when it is listed here, one line each, its path in backticks:\\n- `engine/path/to/file.ts`: why no workaround in the game would do, and what the engine should change instead.\\n-->\\n\",\"total_lines\":20}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f5f8cee7-bef8-407a-8084-6151077c9abc-43","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→# The starter game\\n\\nEvery game made with my-3dge starts as this one (`node tools/game/new-game.mjs`), then becomes its own: rewrite this\\npage as the game grows. It is the game's page for the owner and the next agent: what the game is, how it plays, how to\\nsee it, and the calls made along the way.\\n\\n## The game\\n\\nRun round the arena collecting every gem before the clock runs out. WASD or the arrows run, Space jumps (over the low\\n10→walls), Shift dashes. All the gems: won. The clock at 0: lost. Enter starts a new round on the next seed.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n| File                              | What it is                                                                    |\\n| --------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\\n| labs/game/scenes/play.ts          | The rules, sim-side: the arena's text, the settings, the gems, the round, the systems |\\n| labs/game/cast/player.ts          | The player: its character (run, jump, dash) and the body it is drawn as        |\\n| labs/game/bot.ts                  | The bot: plays through intents, down the flow field to the nearest gem         |\\n| labs/game/main.ts, index.html     | The page: the engine, the HUD, Enter to play again, the chase camera           |\\n20→| labs/game/scenes/play.test.ts     | The tests: the golden replay, capture and restore, the bot wins on 10 seeds, the clock |\\n| labs/game/replays/bot.replay.json | The bot's play from seed 1, with its golden hashes                             |\\n\\n## Settings\\n\\n`game.gems` (10), `game.seconds` (30) and `game.speed` (6 m/s), read when the round starts: `?game.gems=20` in the\\npage, `--set game.gems=20` for `node x sim` and `node x shot`.\\n\\n## See it\\n\\n30→```sh\\nnpm run dev                                         # http://127.0.0.1:5173/labs/game/ (?replay=bot plays the bot's run)\\nnpm test                                            # the tests\\nnode x sim labs/game/scenes/play.ts --feel          # the rules in Node: hash, events, how the player handles\\nnode x shot labs/game                               # the page on WebGPU, as numbers\\nnode x replay labs/game/replays --browser sim       # the goldens, in Node and Chromium\\n```\\n\\n## Decisions\\n\\n40→<!-- The calls made without the owner, newest first: the date, what was decided, why. -->\",\"content_concise\":\"1→# The starter game\\n\\nEvery game made with my-3dge starts as this one (`node tools/game/new-game.mjs`), then becomes its own: rewrite this\\npage as the game grows. It is the game's page for the owner and the next agent: what the game is, how it plays, how to\\nsee it, and the calls made along the way.\\n\\n## The game\\n\\nRun round the arena collecting every gem before the clock runs out. WASD or the arrows run, Space jumps (over the low\\n10→walls), Shift dashes. All the gems: won. The clock at 0: lost. Enter starts a new round on the next seed.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n| File                              | What it is                                                                    |\\n| --------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\\n| labs/game/scenes/play.ts          | The rules, sim-side: the arena's text, the settings, the gems, the round, the systems |\\n| labs/game/cast/player.ts          | The player: its character (run, jump, dash) and the body it is drawn as        |\\n| labs/game/bot.ts                  | The bot: plays through intents, down the flow field to the nearest gem         |\\n| labs/game/main.ts, index.html     | The page: the engine, the HUD, Enter to play again, the chase camera           |\\n20→| labs/game/scenes/play.test.ts     | The tests: the golden replay, capture and restore, the bot wins on 10 seeds, the clock |\\n| labs/game/replays/bot.replay.json | The bot's play from seed 1, with its golden hashes                             |\\n\\n## Settings\\n\\n`game.gems` (10), `game.seconds` (30) and `game.speed` (6 m/s), read when the round starts: `?game.gems=20` in the\\npage, `--set game.gems=20` for `node x sim` and `node x shot`.\\n\\n## See it\\n\\n30→```sh\\nnpm run dev                                         # http://127.0.0.1:5173/labs/game/ (?replay=bot plays the bot's run)\\nnpm test                                            # the tests\\nnode x sim labs/game/scenes/play.ts --feel          # the rules in Node: hash, events, how the player handles\\nnode x shot labs/game                               # the page on WebGPU, as numbers\\nnode x replay labs/game/replays --browser sim       # the goldens, in Node and Chromium\\n```\\n\\n## Decisions\\n\\n40→<!-- The calls made without the owner, newest first: the date, what was decided, why. -->\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/README.md\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"# The starter game\\n\\nEvery game made with my-3dge starts as this one (`node tools/game/new-game.mjs`), then becomes its own: rewrite this\\npage as the game grows. It is the game's page for the owner and the next agent: what the game is, how it plays, how to\\nsee it, and the calls made along the way.\\n\\n## The game\\n\\nRun round the arena collecting every gem before the clock runs out. WASD or the arrows run, Space jumps (over the low\\nwalls), Shift dashes. All the gems: won. The clock at 0: lost. Enter starts a new round on the next seed.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n| File                              | What it is                                                                    |\\n| --------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\\n| labs/game/scenes/play.ts          | The rules, sim-side: the arena's text, the settings, the gems, the round, the systems |\\n| labs/game/cast/player.ts          | The player: its character (run, jump, dash) and the body it is drawn as        |\\n| labs/game/bot.ts                  | The bot: plays through intents, down the flow field to the nearest gem         |\\n| labs/game/main.ts, index.html     | The page: the engine, the HUD, Enter to play again, the chase camera           |\\n| labs/game/scenes/play.test.ts     | The tests: the golden replay, capture and restore, the bot wins on 10 seeds, the clock |\\n| labs/game/replays/bot.replay.json | The bot's play from seed 1, with its golden hashes                             |\\n\\n## Settings\\n\\n`game.gems` (10), `game.seconds` (30) and `game.speed` (6 m/s), read when the round starts: `?game.gems=20` in the\\npage, `--set game.gems=20` for `node x sim` and `node x shot`.\\n\\n## See it\\n\\n```sh\\nnpm run dev                                         # http://127.0.0.1:5173/labs/game/ (?replay=bot plays the bot's run)\\nnpm test                                            # the tests\\nnode x sim labs/game/scenes/play.ts --feel          # the rules in Node: hash, events, how the player handles\\nnode x shot labs/game                               # the page on WebGPU, as numbers\\nnode x replay labs/game/replays --browser sim       # the goldens, in Node and Chromium\\n```\\n\\n## Decisions\\n\\n<!-- The calls made without the owner, newest first: the date, what was decided, why. -->\\n\",\"total_lines\":40}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"54af36d9-21a0-46c0-834f-a6d558c5521c"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_397","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I will write an honest TESTING-LOG. It will cover the seven named critical bugs and other real failures caught by tests this session.\n\nInterview counts will be updated to match the actual log. The seven critical bugs will be listed as the interview already states, tied to their test names. No extra detail will be invented. One new failure was caught: importing looks.ts triggers CORE_BAD_SPEC when outline.width is 1.5.\n\nMore failures were caught this session: a duplicate sfx:laser ID blocked audio boot, campaign.test expected brief too early due to 14 boxes in before-1, SongSpec description was rejected, speedlines.strength was invalid, packedHands was not imported, and slider reset cache had a logic bug. The log will only record issues confirmed by tests.\n\nThe critical bugs are now mapped to specific tests. main.test restore fails until the chart adopts. gala flap never finishes. op.test surfaces Reverie too early and splits Solace children. op.test injects syringe into wrong target. stitches land off the wound. co-op copies shared one point. voice keys is non-critical.\n\nThe interview count will be finalized after all testing ends, so end-to-end failures are included. The log will be written once the complete issue set is known.\n\nThe interview must be rebuilt after finalizing its text because the built HTML inlines it. page.test compares interview.ts to exit-interview.json, so both files must match exactly. The plan is to run tests and end-to-end checks first without changing the interview. Then write the log and update the interview if counts change. Rebuild and rerun only the interview-checking tests and a short boot check; skip the full campaign test.\n\nThe twelve issues in the interview come from operation tests and scene restore, not from later smoke checks. The five non-critical items are missing from git history, so I will search op source and test comments to find them.\n\nI will not invent unverified non-critical issues. The log will list only the seven critical bugs with their test names, and I am still searching for the gala flap test.\n\nThe gala flap bug likely lives in bot.test or strains. I will search code comments for the remaining five non-critical issues, but if none are found, the interview text itself serves as the record of what was caught.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0394a819-2510-4ff0-a66a-c7764650158a-44","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"flap|shared one point|stitch u|wrong body|Solace children|syringe bound","path":"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3%2Fwork/01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151/compaction","head_limit":20}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0394a819-2510-4ff0-a66a-c7764650158a-45","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"cd \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731\" && mkdir -p labs/game/tools/hub && curl -fsSL -o labs/game/tools/hub/harness.html https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/harness.html && curl -fsSL -o labs/game/tools/hub/bridge.js https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/bridge.js && curl -fsSL -o labs/game/tools/hub/round.js https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/round.js && wc -c labs/game/tools/hub/*","description":"Download AI Hub harness files"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2977,"output_tokens":1536,"cache_read_input_tokens":85632,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"39b022c6-a8ad-4e92-95ef-5e93c67b9038"}
