{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_408","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Bot and content tests passed in 888 milliseconds.\n\nHTML structure is correct. I will write a short Node.js probe script to boot the page on desktop and Pixel 7, then run it and delete it. I also need to handle touch behavior for the Pixel 7, since headless Chrome always reports a mouse and sets `any-pointer` media features.\n\nChecking Playwright's Chromium source to see how `isMobile` sets touch emulation and user agent metadata. Need to verify whether Chrome's `(pointer: coarse)` media query actually reflects touch emulation, since headless Chrome always reports a mouse.\n\nThe probe will also test iPad. If neither device flips any-pointer, the PLAN still requires the message on phone profiles. I will not emulate media queries in tests. Instead, I will treat a coarse primary pointer with no hover as touch-only, matching real phones.\n\nReal iPhone Safari sets `(any-pointer: coarse)` and `(hover: none)`. Playwright WebKit likely replicates this, but Chromium Pixel 7 may report `(any-pointer: fine)` despite having a coarse pointer. The revised check will use `pointer: coarse` and `hover: none` as the coarse-only signal.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-95d859c0-f34e-4693-8c8a-576457b45ff6-66","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"cd \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731\" && export TMPDIR=$(mktemp -d /tmp/g.XXXXXX) && export CHROMIUM_PATH=\"${CHROMIUM_PATH:-$(ls -d \"$HOME\"/.cache/ms-playwright/chromium-*/chrome-linux64/chrome | head -1)}\" && echo \"TMP=$TMPDIR CHROME=$CHROMIUM_PATH\" && node --input-type=module <<'EOF'\nimport { chromium, devices } from 'playwright';\nconst file = new URL('../../../Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731.html', import.meta.url);\nconst url = file.href;\nconst args = ['--enable-unsafe-webgpu','--enable-features=Vulkan','--use-vulkan=swiftshader','--use-angle=swiftshader','--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader'];\nconst browser = await chromium.launch({ executablePath: process.env.CHROMIUM_PATH, headless: true, args });\nconst page = await browser.newPage({ viewport: { width: 1280, height: 720 } });\nconst errors = [];\npage.on('pageerror', e => errors.push(e.message));\npage.on('console', m => { if (m.type()==='error') errors.push(m.text()); });\nawait page.goto(url);\nawait page.waitForFunction(() => window.__engine && window.__engine.ready, null, { timeout: 40000 });\nconst state = await page.evaluate(() => ({\n  screen: window.__compass?.screen,\n  title: document.querySelector('[data-game=\"title\"]')?.textContent,\n  usage: document.querySelector('[data-about=\"usage\"]')?.textContent,\n  errors: (window.__engine?.errors ?? []).map(e => e.code),\n}));\nconsole.log('BOOT', JSON.stringify(state), 'console', errors);\nawait page.close();\nfor (const name of ['Pixel 7', 'iPad Pro 11', 'iPhone 13']) {\n  const ctx = await browser.newContext({ ...devices[name] });\n  const p = await ctx.newPage();\n  await p.goto('data:text/html,<title>q</title>');\n  const q = await p.evaluate(() => ({\n    fine: matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches,\n    coarse: matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches,\n    hoverNone: matchMedia('(hover: none)').matches,\n    anyCoarse: matchMedia('(any-pointer: coarse)').matches,\n    touch: navigator.maxTouchPoints,\n  }));\n  console.log(name, JSON.stringify(q));\n  await ctx.close();\n}\nawait browser.close();\nEOF\nec=$?; rm -rf \"$TMPDIR\"; echo exit=$ec","description":"Boot the page and probe phone pointer media","block_until_ms":90000}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1326,"output_tokens":1522,"cache_read_input_tokens":108672,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f