{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_410","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Playwright launches Chromium using chrome-headless-shell with blink-settings.\n\nDecoding the blink-settings pointer type enums. PointerType 4 likely corresponds to fine pointer input.\n\nAll Chromium processes appear to use these blink settings, suggesting they are Playwright's default for headless shell rather than mobile-only. Checking the Chromium mojom enum definitions to confirm the exact pointer type values.\n\nThe default headless shell settings emulate a mouse with fine pointer input. Mobile profiles use separate blink settings. Phone profiles might still report fine pointer unless the device context overrides it. I need to probe this behavior.\n\nI will write a temporary probe script in labs/game/tools/pointer-probe.mjs to test pointer detection. It will use ESM and resolve Playwright from the script location. I must avoid killing other agents' Chrome processes. The previous probe crashed and left no user-data-dir behind. The HTML test page is four directory levels above the tools folder.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-eff4eee4-c69b-4490-9be3-f44260bc66fe-68","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/tools/pointer-probe.mjs","content":"/**\n * @file Throwaway: boot the page and print pointer media queries. Deleted after the run.\n */\nimport { chromium, devices } from 'playwright';\nimport { pathToFileURL } from 'node:url';\n\nconst pageUrl = pathToFileURL(\n  new URL('../../../../Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731.html', import.meta.url),\n).href;\nconst args = [\n  '--enable-unsafe-webgpu',\n  '--enable-features=Vulkan',\n  '--use-vulkan=swiftshader',\n  '--use-angle=swiftshader',\n  '--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader',\n];\nconst browser = await chromium.launch({ executablePath: process.env.CHROMIUM_PATH, headless: true, args });\ntry {\n  const page = await browser.newPage({ viewport: { width: 1280, height: 720 } });\n  const errors = [];\n  page.on('pageerror', (e) => errors.push(e.message));\n  page.on('console', (m) => {\n    if (m.type() === 'error') errors.push(m.text());\n  });\n  await page.goto(pageUrl);\n  await page.waitForFunction(() => window.__engine && window.__engine.ready, null, { timeout: 45000 });\n  const state = await page.evaluate(() => ({\n    screen: window.__compass?.screen,\n    title: document.querySelector('[data-game=\"title\"]')?.textContent ?? '',\n    usage: document.querySelector('[data-about=\"usage\"]')?.textContent ?? '',\n    codes: (window.__engine?.errors ?? []).map((e) => e.code),\n  }));\n  console.log('BOOT', JSON.stringify({ ...state, errors }));\n  await page.close();\n  for (const name of ['Pixel 7', 'iPad (gen 7)', 'Galaxy Tab S4']) {\n    const ctx = await browser.newContext({ ...devices[name] });\n    const p = await ctx.newPage();\n    await p.goto('data:text/html,<title>q</title>');\n    const q = await p.evaluate(() => ({\n      fine: matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches,\n      coarse: matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches,\n      hoverNone: matchMedia('(hover: none)').matches,\n      anyCoarse: matchMedia('(any-pointer: coarse)').matches,\n      touch: navigator.maxTouchPoints,\n    }));\n    console.log(name, JSON.stringify(q));\n    await ctx.close();\n  }\n} finally {\n  await browser.close();\n}\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6479,"output_tokens":1333,"cache_read_input_tokens":111872,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"65bc43ec-b34a-4918-b127-4af2f2125480"}
