{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_417","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The slider test fills the input and dispatches an input event.\n\nThe slider test reads the input value immediately after resetting. The DOM may not have rebuilt yet because drawShell only runs on the next frame.\n\nThe test should wait for the input value to become 1 before reading it. This is a test timing issue, not a game bug.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-62b872fa-da59-42e7-9bba-f1b43c6bc0cf-78","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/ui/shell.ts","offset":90,"limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3416,"output_tokens":480,"cache_read_input_tokens":124544,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"385eab34-f5b7-4575-92f5-9e21ba9e0539"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-62b872fa-da59-42e7-9bba-f1b43c6bc0cf-78","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"90→      (on, index) =>\\n        `<p class=\\\"seat${on ? ' is-on' : ''}\\\" data-game=\\\"seat\\\">${on ? `Seat ${index + 1} claimed` : `Seat ${index + 1}`}</p>`,\\n    )\\n    .join('');\\n  return `<div class=\\\"seats\\\" data-game=\\\"scrub\\\">${seats}</div>`;\\n}\\n\\n/** Balance sliders. The value is the live setting. */\\nfunction sliders(extra: ShellExtra): string {\\n  return extra.sliders\\n100→    .map((row) => {\\n      const tune = TUNE.find((item) => item.setting === row.setting);\\n      if (!tune) return '';\\n      return `<label class=\\\"slider\\\">${esc(row.label)} ${row.value}<input type=\\\"range\\\" data-set=\\\"${esc(row.setting)}\\\" min=\\\"${tune.min}\\\" max=\\\"${tune.max}\\\" step=\\\"${tune.step}\\\" value=\\\"${row.value}\\\" /></label>`;\\n    })\\n    .join('');\\n}\\n\\n/** Dev panels that are not plain rows. */\\nfunction devExtra(c: Campaign, extra: ShellExtra): string {\\n110→  if (c.devTab === 1) return sliders(extra);\\n  if (c.devTab === 3) return `<p data-game=\\\"cursor\\\">${esc(extra.cursor)}</p>`;\\n  if (c.devTab === 4) return `<p data-game=\\\"hash\\\">${esc(extra.hash)}</p>`;\\n  return '';\\n}\\n\\n/** The body of the open screen. */\\nfunction cardBlock(extra: ShellExtra): string {\\n  const card = extra.card;\\n  if (!card) return '';\\n120→  const names = card.names\\n    .map((name, index) => `<li data-game=\\\"player\\\">${card.ready.includes(index) ? 'Ready · ' : ''}${esc(name)}</li>`)\\n    .join('');\\n  return `<article class=\\\"card\\\" data-game=\\\"card\\\"><h2>Trauma Compass</h2><p>Keep the patient alive and finish the op together.</p><ul>${names}</ul><p>${esc(card.left)}</p><p>Stick or mouse aims. R2 or click uses the tool.</p><button type=\\\"button\\\" class=\\\"row\\\" data-act=\\\"hub-ready\\\">Ready</button><button type=\\\"button\\\" class=\\\"row\\\" data-act=\\\"hub-more\\\">${card.asked ? 'Resume the clock' : 'More time'}</button></article>`;\\n}\\n\\nfunction body(c: Campaign, extra: ShellExtra): string {\\n  if (extra.card) return cardBlock(extra);\\n  if (c.screen === 'attract' && currentBox(c)) {\\n    return `${storyBlock(c)}<p class=\\\"demo\\\" data-game=\\\"demo\\\">DEMO</p>`;\",\"content_concise\":\"90→      (on, index) =>\\n        `<p class=\\\"seat${on ? ' is-on' : ''}\\\" data-game=\\\"seat\\\">${on ? `Seat ${index + 1} claimed` : `Seat ${index + 1}`}</p>`,\\n    )\\n    .join('');\\n  return `<div class=\\\"seats\\\" data-game=\\\"scrub\\\">${seats}</div>`;\\n}\\n\\n/** Balance sliders. The value is the live setting. */\\nfunction sliders(extra: ShellExtra): string {\\n  return extra.sliders\\n100→    .map((row) => {\\n      const tune = TUNE.find((item) => item.setting === row.setting);\\n      if (!tune) return '';\\n      return `<label class=\\\"slider\\\">${esc(row.label)} ${row.value}<input type=\\\"range\\\" data-set=\\\"${esc(row.setting)}\\\" min=\\\"${tune.min}\\\" max=\\\"${tune.max}\\\" step=\\\"${tune.step}\\\" value=\\\"${row.value}\\\" /></label>`;\\n    })\\n    .join('');\\n}\\n\\n/** Dev panels that are not plain rows. */\\nfunction devExtra(c: Campaign, extra: ShellExtra): string {\\n110→  if (c.devTab === 1) return sliders(extra);\\n  if (c.devTab === 3) return `<p data-game=\\\"cursor\\\">${esc(extra.cursor)}</p>`;\\n  if (c.devTab === 4) return `<p data-game=\\\"hash\\\">${esc(extra.hash)}</p>`;\\n  return '';\\n}\\n\\n/** The body of the open screen. */\\nfunction cardBlock(extra: ShellExtra): string {\\n  const card = extra.card;\\n  if (!card) return '';\\n120→  const names = card.names\\n    .map((name, index) => `<li data-game=\\\"player\\\">${card.ready.includes(index) ? 'Ready · ' : ''}${esc(name)}</li>`)\\n    .join('');\\n  return `<article class=\\\"card\\\" data-game=\\\"card\\\"><h2>Trauma Compass</h2><p>Keep the patient alive and finish the op together.</p><ul>${names}</ul><p>${esc(card.left)}</p><p>Stick or mouse aims. R2 or click uses the tool.</p><button type=\\\"button\\\" class=\\\"row\\\" data-act=\\\"hub-ready\\\">Ready</button><button type=\\\"button\\\" class=\\\"row\\\" data-act=\\\"hub-more\\\">${card.asked ? 'Resume the clock' : 'More time'}</button></article>`;\\n}\\n\\nfunction body(c: Campaign, extra: ShellExtra): string {\\n  if (extra.card) return cardBlock(extra);\\n  if (c.screen === 'attract' && currentBox(c)) {\\n    return `${storyBlock(c)}<p class=\\\"demo\\\" data-game=\\\"demo\\\">DEMO</p>`;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/ui/shell.ts\",\"offset\":90,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"      (on, index) =>\\n        `<p class=\\\"seat${on ? ' is-on' : ''}\\\" data-game=\\\"seat\\\">${on ? `Seat ${index + 1} claimed` : `Seat ${index + 1}`}</p>`,\\n    )\\n    .join('');\\n  return `<div class=\\\"seats\\\" data-game=\\\"scrub\\\">${seats}</div>`;\\n}\\n\\n/** Balance sliders. The value is the live setting. */\\nfunction sliders(extra: ShellExtra): string {\\n  return extra.sliders\\n    .map((row) => {\\n      const tune = TUNE.find((item) => item.setting === row.setting);\\n      if (!tune) return '';\\n      return `<label class=\\\"slider\\\">${esc(row.label)} ${row.value}<input type=\\\"range\\\" data-set=\\\"${esc(row.setting)}\\\" min=\\\"${tune.min}\\\" max=\\\"${tune.max}\\\" step=\\\"${tune.step}\\\" value=\\\"${row.value}\\\" /></label>`;\\n    })\\n    .join('');\\n}\\n\\n/** Dev panels that are not plain rows. */\\nfunction devExtra(c: Campaign, extra: ShellExtra): string {\\n  if (c.devTab === 1) return sliders(extra);\\n  if (c.devTab === 3) return `<p data-game=\\\"cursor\\\">${esc(extra.cursor)}</p>`;\\n  if (c.devTab === 4) return `<p data-game=\\\"hash\\\">${esc(extra.hash)}</p>`;\\n  return '';\\n}\\n\\n/** The body of the open screen. */\\nfunction cardBlock(extra: ShellExtra): string {\\n  const card = extra.card;\\n  if (!card) return '';\\n  const names = card.names\\n    .map((name, index) => `<li data-game=\\\"player\\\">${card.ready.includes(index) ? 'Ready · ' : ''}${esc(name)}</li>`)\\n    .join('');\\n  return `<article class=\\\"card\\\" data-game=\\\"card\\\"><h2>Trauma Compass</h2><p>Keep the patient alive and finish the op together.</p><ul>${names}</ul><p>${esc(card.left)}</p><p>Stick or mouse aims. R2 or click uses the tool.</p><button type=\\\"button\\\" class=\\\"row\\\" data-act=\\\"hub-ready\\\">Ready</button><button type=\\\"button\\\" class=\\\"row\\\" data-act=\\\"hub-more\\\">${card.asked ? 'Resume the clock' : 'More time'}</button></article>`;\\n}\\n\\nfunction body(c: Campaign, extra: ShellExtra): string {\\n  if (extra.card) return cardBlock(extra);\\n  if (c.screen === 'attract' && currentBox(c)) {\\n    return `${storyBlock(c)}<p class=\\\"demo\\\" data-game=\\\"demo\\\">DEMO</p>`;\\n\",\"total_lines\":196}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"da6e766f-51e8-4570-aff2-499a262d61f9"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_418","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Fallback 1 has a value of \"1\".","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d9fab961-0938-485f-8f8a-e8741ced1ae7-79","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/input/hands.ts","offset":215,"limit":50}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1188,"output_tokens":233,"cache_read_input_tokens":127872,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"98dadff6-71bb-4af1-be2b-a998ffd6c76f"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-d9fab961-0938-485f-8f8a-e8741ced1ae7-79","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"215→/** Read every pad once this frame. Menu edges and tool taps share it. */\\nexport function samplePads(): MenuEdges {\\n  const edges: MenuEdges = {\\n    accept: false,\\n    cancel: false,\\n220→    up: false,\\n    down: false,\\n    left: false,\\n    right: false,\\n    pause: false,\\n    any: false,\\n    claim: -1,\\n  };\\n  const list = pads();\\n  for (let seat = 0; seat < 4; seat++) {\\n230→    const pad = list[seat];\\n    for (let index = 0; index < 16; index++) {\\n      const now = down(pad, index);\\n      roseNow[seat][index] = now && padWas[seat][index] !== true;\\n      padWas[seat][index] = now;\\n    }\\n    if (!pad) continue;\\n    const create = down(pad, 8);\\n    if (tapped(seat, 0)) {\\n      edges.accept = true;\\n240→      edges.claim = seat;\\n    }\\n    if (tapped(seat, 1)) edges.cancel = true;\\n    if (tapped(seat, 12)) edges.up = true;\\n    if (tapped(seat, 13)) edges.down = true;\\n    if (tapped(seat, 14)) edges.left = true;\\n    if (tapped(seat, 15)) edges.right = true;\\n    if (!create && tapped(seat, 9)) edges.pause = true;\\n    const stick = Math.hypot(pad.axes[0] ?? 0, pad.axes[1] ?? 0) > 0.5;\\n    if (stick || pad.buttons.some((button) => button.pressed)) edges.any = true;\\n250→  }\\n  sampled = true;\\n  return edges;\\n}\\n\\n/** Clear the sample so the next frame reads the pads again. */\\nexport function endSample(): void {\\n  sampled = false;\\n}\\n\\n260→/** True when the device has no fine pointer and no pad yet. */\\nexport function touchOnly(): boolean {\\n  const fine = window.matchMedia?.('(any-pointer: fine)').matches ?? true;\\n  return !fine && pads().length === 0;\\n}\",\"content_concise\":\"215→/** Read every pad once this frame. Menu edges and tool taps share it. */\\nexport function samplePads(): MenuEdges {\\n  const edges: MenuEdges = {\\n    accept: false,\\n    cancel: false,\\n220→    up: false,\\n    down: false,\\n    left: false,\\n    right: false,\\n    pause: false,\\n    any: false,\\n    claim: -1,\\n  };\\n  const list = pads();\\n  for (let seat = 0; seat < 4; seat++) {\\n230→    const pad = list[seat];\\n    for (let index = 0; index < 16; index++) {\\n      const now = down(pad, index);\\n      roseNow[seat][index] = now && padWas[seat][index] !== true;\\n      padWas[seat][index] = now;\\n    }\\n    if (!pad) continue;\\n    const create = down(pad, 8);\\n    if (tapped(seat, 0)) {\\n      edges.accept = true;\\n240→      edges.claim = seat;\\n    }\\n    if (tapped(seat, 1)) edges.cancel = true;\\n    if (tapped(seat, 12)) edges.up = true;\\n    if (tapped(seat, 13)) edges.down = true;\\n    if (tapped(seat, 14)) edges.left = true;\\n    if (tapped(seat, 15)) edges.right = true;\\n    if (!create && tapped(seat, 9)) edges.pause = true;\\n    const stick = Math.hypot(pad.axes[0] ?? 0, pad.axes[1] ?? 0) > 0.5;\\n    if (stick || pad.buttons.some((button) => button.pressed)) edges.any = true;\\n250→  }\\n  sampled = true;\\n  return edges;\\n}\\n\\n/** Clear the sample so the next frame reads the pads again. */\\nexport function endSample(): void {\\n  sampled = false;\\n}\\n\\n260→/** True when the device has no fine pointer and no pad yet. */\\nexport function touchOnly(): boolean {\\n  const fine = window.matchMedia?.('(any-pointer: fine)').matches ?? true;\\n  return !fine && pads().length === 0;\\n}\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/input/hands.ts\",\"offset\":215,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"/** Read every pad once this frame. Menu edges and tool taps share it. */\\nexport function samplePads(): MenuEdges {\\n  const edges: MenuEdges = {\\n    accept: false,\\n    cancel: false,\\n    up: false,\\n    down: false,\\n    left: false,\\n    right: false,\\n    pause: false,\\n    any: false,\\n    claim: -1,\\n  };\\n  const list = pads();\\n  for (let seat = 0; seat < 4; seat++) {\\n    const pad = list[seat];\\n    for (let index = 0; index < 16; index++) {\\n      const now = down(pad, index);\\n      roseNow[seat][index] = now && padWas[seat][index] !== true;\\n      padWas[seat][index] = now;\\n    }\\n    if (!pad) continue;\\n    const create = down(pad, 8);\\n    if (tapped(seat, 0)) {\\n      edges.accept = true;\\n      edges.claim = seat;\\n    }\\n    if (tapped(seat, 1)) edges.cancel = true;\\n    if (tapped(seat, 12)) edges.up = true;\\n    if (tapped(seat, 13)) edges.down = true;\\n    if (tapped(seat, 14)) edges.left = true;\\n    if (tapped(seat, 15)) edges.right = true;\\n    if (!create && tapped(seat, 9)) edges.pause = true;\\n    const stick = Math.hypot(pad.axes[0] ?? 0, pad.axes[1] ?? 0) > 0.5;\\n    if (stick || pad.buttons.some((button) => button.pressed)) edges.any = true;\\n  }\\n  sampled = true;\\n  return edges;\\n}\\n\\n/** Clear the sample so the next frame reads the pads again. */\\nexport function endSample(): void {\\n  sampled = false;\\n}\\n\\n/** True when the device has no fine pointer and no pad yet. */\\nexport function touchOnly(): boolean {\\n  const fine = window.matchMedia?.('(any-pointer: fine)').matches ?? true;\\n  return !fine && pads().length === 0;\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":264}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"0eda9a15-6ab0-4657-8950-2611d1a2c31d"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_419","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The pads() function returns only connected gamepads.\n\nThe gamepad stub returns [pad, null, null, null], so pads() will find the connected device at index 0. Button 13 is a down-edge trigger; the test waits 150ms to sample it, releases it to allow re-triggering, then presses button 0 to accept. The title screen starts at \"New Shift\", moves down to \"The Board\", and accepts to open the board.\n\nThe title screen leaves correctly. A null pad frame is harmless because the down-edge still fires on the first valid sample. The board opens after accept. Two pads are used: pad 0 scrubs in, and pad 1 claims seat 1 with button 0 while pad 0 holds axes at 0.9.\n\nclaimSeat only sets a boolean flag, so pad 1 claiming seat 1 correctly marks index 1 as claimed. For the gloves test, readHands runs every frame across four seats; aimPad moves cursors using axes 0.9 and -0.9, and the hands should separate by more than 0.2 within 500ms. There is a potential issue where samplePads inside menus() sets sampled to true.\n\nreadHands reuses the existing pad state once sampled, and aimPad updates axes continuously. A potential race condition exists in the scrub screen: pressing button 0 on pad 1 triggers both accept and claim edges. If accept fires before claim, the game exits to the title screen before the test can read the seat-claimed text.\n\nThe test sequence presses pad 1 button 0, waits 400ms, releases the button, waits 500ms, then reads scrub text. Because button 0 is mapped to both accept and claim on the scrub screen, any simultaneous press triggers both edges. If accept fires first, the game exits to the title screen before the test can read the seat-claimed message.\n\nThe game code confirms that claim and accept run on the same frame. Claiming a new seat triggers accept, which exits to the title screen before the test can read the seat-claimed text. The plan may require changing the south button so it claims a seat without also starting the game.\n\nThe plan requires the scrub screen to display \"Seat N claimed\" text, so the test must observe that message. Because button 0 is the only claim input, it cannot be decoupled from accept. The proposed fix modifies menus so that claiming a seat only triggers accept if that seat was previously unclaimed.\n\nThe proposed fix requires skipping accept when a press claims a seat for the first time. Another option is to verify the claimed state through campaign.claimed instead of reading screen text, since the press still registers the claim even if it exits the scrub screen.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-dd0e4289-3486-46ee-bb73-5bf85b543a2b-80","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"Scrub|claim|couch|Seat","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/PLAN.md","head_limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":763,"output_tokens":1436,"cache_read_input_tokens":129024,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"e81c10f3-92b4-48f6-adec-28bdfd8f946c"}
