111,114,32,68,97,116,101,44,32,69,110,118,105,114,111,110,109,101,110,116,32,97,110,100,32,77,111,100,101,108,41,44,32,84,101,115,116,105,110,103,32,70,101,101,100,98,97,99,107,44,32,69,110,103,105,110,101,32,70,101,101,100,98,97,99,107,44,32,80,114,111,109,112,116,32,70,101,101,100,98,97,99,107,32,40,101,118,101,114,121,32,113,117,101,115,116,105,111,110,32,84,65,83,75,46,109,100,32,97,115,107,115,44,32,111,110,101,32,99,97,114,100,32,101,97,99,104,41,44,32,99,114,101,100,105,116,115,46,32,85,115,101,32,34,117,110,107,110,111,119,110,34,32,102,111,114,32,97,110,121,116,104,105,110,103,32,121,111,117,32,99,97,110,110,111,116,32,99,111,110,102,105,114,109,46,32,80,108,97,110,32,102,105,101,108,100,58,32,96,80,76,65,78,46,109,100,96,46,32,85,115,97,103,101,32,102,105,101,108,100,58,32,101,120,97,99,116,108,121,32,96,97,100,100,101,100,32,111,110,32,105,109,112,111,114,116,96,44,32,105,110,32,97,110,32,101,108,101,109,101,110,116,32,109,97,114,107,101,100,32,96,100,97,116,97,45,97,98,111,117,116,61,34,117,115,97,103,101,34,96,32,115,111,32,116,104,101,32,105,109,112,111,114,116,101,114,32,99,97,110,32,114,101,112,108,97,99,101,32,105,116,46,32,83,97,121,32,105,110,32,79,110,108,105,110,101,32,116,104,97,116,32,110,101,116,119,111,114,107,32,112,108,97,121,32,105,115,32,116,104,114,111,117,103,104,32,65,73,32,72,117,98,32,111,110,108,121,44,32,97,110,100,32,99,111,117,99,104,32,99,111,45,111,112,32,111,110,32,111,110,101,32,115,99,114,101,101,110,46,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":14,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/PLAN.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":39,\"content\":\"4. **Readable from the couch.** A pad in your hands, a TV at 10 feet, huge glyphs, never more than a few things to read.\"},{\"line_number\":181,\"content\":\"  stinger. Works in couch, online, and with the AI colleague.\"},{\"line_number\":187,\"content\":\"Every surgeon is a **seat** with a cursor, a tool, and its own hand and score. Vitals, clock and targets are shared. Seats\"},{\"line_number\":194,\"content\":\"- **Couch co-op, on its own (no hub):** up to four devices on one TV. On the title's **Scrub In** screen, or from the Board,\"},{\"line_number\":195,\"content\":\"  each pad presses Cross, or the keyboard and mouse press Enter, to claim a seat. Same picture, one camera; any seat\"},{\"line_number\":199,\"content\":\"- **Seat colours:** `#e8443a`, `#3b82f6`, `#22c55e`, `#f5b700`, as the hub's.\"},{\"line_number\":280,\"content\":\"Node, one flap. Ends when both are closed (won) or one dies or time runs out (lost). Playable also from Free Surgery for couch play.\"},{\"line_number\":400,\"content\":\"- **Title:** 3D lamp-lit OR with the lighthouse beam through rain on the window; the title; Continue / New Shift / The Board / Scrub In / Settings / About. Attract after 10 s idle (§14).\"},{\"line_number\":408,\"content\":\"- **Scrub In:** four big seat slots; each device claims one by pressing its accept; Start.\"},{\"line_number\":567,\"content\":\"**On its own.** With no hub, the game runs exactly as a normal game: story, Board, solo, and couch co-op for up to four devices (§6). There is no other online mode: outside a session there is no hub network and we add no servers. State this in About.\"},{\"line_number\":658,\"content\":\"- **Solo and couch:** `(inspector.input).axis('game:hands', hands)` each frame. It merges into each step and is recorded (tested). Attract and autoplay feed the bot's hands the same way.\"},{\"line_number\":839,\"content\":\"- Couch: two stub pads each claim a seat and move their own cursor.\"},{\"line_number\":858,\"content\":\"7. **Strains and flaps:** Cases 4, 5, 6, with Second Pulse, seats, AI colleague, Swap, Consult, couch co-op.\"},{\"line_number\":869,\"content\":\"**About/Credits (in game)**, paged, one card per item, big text. One screen each: Source Information (Date, Source, Plan, Genre and Perspective, Tech, Art Direction, Animation, Audio, Online, Testing, Research, Environment, Model, Usage, with your TASK.md's values for Date, Environment and Model), Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback (every question TASK.md asks, one card each), credits. Use \\\"unknown\\\" for anything you cannot confirm. Plan field: `PLAN.md`. Usage field: exactly `added on import`, in an element marked `data-about=\\\"usage\\\"` so the importer can replace it. Say in Online that network play is through AI Hub only, and couch co-op on one screen.\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"dc073322-8de6-4383-b57b-66a8f9377a78"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_420","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Plan.md specifies that pads press Cross and keyboard or mouse presses Enter to claim a seat. It also separately mentions \"Start\".\n\nClaiming a seat and activating Start are separate actions. The current code incorrectly triggers both when pressing accept. The fix is to claim the seat first, then only activate the row if the seat was previously unclaimed.\n\nThe current code always sets both accept and claim on button 0. For a fresh pad claim, accept is skipped. Keyboard Enter still claims seat 0 without starting. Pad 1 Cross claims seat 2 without starting; the test can see the text and the sticks move the gloves.\n\nThe next step is updating boot.ts menus(). The end-to-end tests need fixes: nth=1 for Board, waiting for slider reset, and tapping the settings button after waiting for messages and attract. The pointer-probe file should be deleted before verification. Pad movement logic is being reviewed to confirm the axis signs.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-fcf3b502-8dfb-45f2-9dcd-3cd8c505cffb-81","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/input/glyphs.ts","limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-fcf3b502-8dfb-45f2-9dcd-3cd8c505cffb-82","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/app/boot.ts","offset":388,"limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2295,"output_tokens":928,"cache_read_input_tokens":129664,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"32795acd-173f-41ba-ab74-59e4b6fd6405"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-fcf3b502-8dfb-45f2-9dcd-3cd8c505cffb-81","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file Prompts drawn as SVG, so a PlayStation pad, an Xbox pad, a key and a mouse each look like themselves.\\n * Unknown pads use the PlayStation shapes until Settings says otherwise.\\n */\\n\\n/** A small inline icon. The markup is ours, never a player's name. */\\nfunction svg(body: string): string {\\n  return `<svg viewBox=\\\"0 0 64 64\\\" width=\\\"48\\\" height=\\\"48\\\" aria-hidden=\\\"true\\\">${body}</svg>`;\\n}\\n10→\\n/** PlayStation face shapes, or the Xbox letters when `xbox` is set. */\\nexport function faceGlyph(which: 'south' | 'east' | 'west' | 'north', xbox: boolean): string {\\n  if (xbox) {\\n    const letter = { south: 'A', east: 'B', west: 'X', north: 'Y' }[which];\\n    return svg(`<circle cx=\\\"32\\\" cy=\\\"32\\\" r=\\\"26\\\" fill=\\\"none\\\" stroke=\\\"#f4f1ea\\\" stroke-width=\\\"4\\\"/><text x=\\\"32\\\" y=\\\"42\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" font-size=\\\"32\\\" fill=\\\"#f4f1ea\\\" font-family=\\\"sans-serif\\\">${letter}</text>`);\\n  }\\n  const shape = {\\n    south: '<path d=\\\"M32 8 56 32 32 56 8 32Z\\\" fill=\\\"none\\\" stroke=\\\"#f4f1ea\\\" stroke-width=\\\"4\\\"/>',\\n    east: '<circle cx=\\\"32\\\" cy=\\\"32\\\" r=\\\"22\\\" fill=\\\"none\\\" stroke=\\\"#f4f1ea\\\" stroke-width=\\\"4\\\"/>',\\n20→    west: '<rect x=\\\"12\\\" y=\\\"12\\\" width=\\\"40\\\" height=\\\"40\\\" fill=\\\"none\\\" stroke=\\\"#f4f1ea\\\" stroke-width=\\\"4\\\"/>',\\n    north: '<path d=\\\"M32 8 38 26 56 26 42 38 48 56 32 44 16 56 22 38 8 26 26 26Z\\\" fill=\\\"none\\\" stroke=\\\"#f4f1ea\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/>',\\n  }[which];\\n  return svg(shape);\\n}\\n\\n/** A keycap with a short label. */\\nexport function keyGlyph(label: string): string {\\n  return svg(`<rect x=\\\"6\\\" y=\\\"10\\\" width=\\\"52\\\" height=\\\"44\\\" rx=\\\"8\\\" fill=\\\"none\\\" stroke=\\\"#f4f1ea\\\" stroke-width=\\\"4\\\"/><text x=\\\"32\\\" y=\\\"40\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" font-size=\\\"22\\\" fill=\\\"#f4f1ea\\\" font-family=\\\"sans-serif\\\">${label}</text>`);\\n}\\n30→\\n/** A mouse with one button marked. */\\nexport function mouseGlyph(which: 'left' | 'right' | 'wheel'): string {\\n  const mark =\\n    which === 'left'\\n      ? '<path d=\\\"M18 16 h14 v20 h-14z\\\" fill=\\\"#f4f1ea\\\"/>'\\n      : which === 'right'\\n        ? '<path d=\\\"M32 16 h14 v20 h-14z\\\" fill=\\\"#f4f1ea\\\"/>'\\n        : '<rect x=\\\"29\\\" y=\\\"18\\\" width=\\\"6\\\" height=\\\"16\\\" fill=\\\"#f4f1ea\\\"/>';\\n  return svg(`<rect x=\\\"14\\\" y=\\\"8\\\" width=\\\"36\\\" height=\\\"48\\\" rx=\\\"16\\\" fill=\\\"none\\\" stroke=\\\"#f4f1ea\\\" stroke-width=\\\"4\\\"/>${mark}`);\\n40→}\\n\\n/** The use prompt for the device that spoke last. */\\nexport function usePrompt(device: string, xbox: boolean): string {\\n  if (device === 'mouse') return `${mouseGlyph('left')} Use`;\\n  if (device === 'keyboard') return `${keyGlyph('Enter')} Use`;\\n  return `${faceGlyph('south', xbox)} Use`;\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file Prompts drawn as SVG, so a PlayStation pad, an Xbox pad, a key and a mouse each look like themselves.\\n * Unknown pads use the PlayStation shapes until Settings says otherwise.\\n */\\n\\n/** A small inline icon. The markup is ours, never a player's name. */\\nfunction svg(body: string): string {\\n  return `<svg viewBox=\\\"0 0 64 64\\\" width=\\\"48\\\" height=\\\"48\\\" aria-hidden=\\\"true\\\">${body}</svg>`;\\n}\\n10→\\n/** PlayStation face shapes, or the Xbox letters when `xbox` is set. */\\nexport function faceGlyph(which: 'south' | 'east' | 'west' | 'north', xbox: boolean): string {\\n  if (xbox) {\\n    const letter = { south: 'A', east: 'B', west: 'X', north: 'Y' }[which];\\n    return svg(`<circle cx=\\\"32\\\" cy=\\\"32\\\" r=\\\"26\\\" fill=\\\"none\\\" stroke=\\\"#f4f1ea\\\" 