{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_431","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The e2e test includes the Xbox wait.\n\nThe HTML build already includes the boot changes. The e2e test will run in the background with output to a scratch log, monitored for completion or failure.\n\nThe monitor script will tail the e2e log and only print when it detects a failure or an EXIT line.\n\nThe monitor script will print a final status line with the exit code once e2e finishes. It will wake immediately on the first failure to avoid wasting time on a known issue.\n\nI will start e2e in the background and monitor it. I will write TESTING-LOG, ENGINE-FEEDBACK, README, and PROGRESS while waiting. I will check the README requirements and feedback template first to ensure accuracy. Plan deviations will go into goal plan.md. The monitor script will live in scratch.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-17c755ff-ac9e-41fd-8c2f-27fea4d2781c-104","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/tools/e2e.mjs","offset":250}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1016,"output_tokens":1098,"cache_read_input_tokens":147712,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"f81fb08e-ca75-40c0-9227-d5f0e37681d0"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-17c755ff-ac9e-41fd-8c2f-27fea4d2781c-104","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"250→  report(\\n    'music bus is quiet and a tone is audible',\\n    heard.music === 0.1 && heard.state === 'running' && heard.peak > 128 && heard.offline,\\n    JSON.stringify(heard),\\n  );\\n  await page.close();\\n}\\n\\n{\\n  const phone = await browser.newContext({ ...devices['Pixel 7'] });\\n260→  const page = await phone.newPage();\\n  watch(page);\\n  await page.goto(pageUrl);\\n  await page.waitForFunction(\\n    () => document.querySelector('[data-game=\\\"touch\\\"]')?.textContent?.includes('Controller or keyboard required'),\\n    null,\\n    { timeout: 8000 },\\n  );\\n  await page.waitForFunction(() => window.__compass?.screen === 'attract', null, { timeout: 15000 });\\n  const text = await page.locator('[data-game=\\\"touch\\\"]').innerText();\\n270→  await page.locator('[data-game=\\\"touch\\\"] [data-act=\\\"settings\\\"]').tap();\\n  await page.waitForFunction(() => window.__compass?.screen === 'settings');\\n  report('touch asks for a controller', text.includes('Controller or keyboard required'), text);\\n  await phone.close();\\n}\\n\\n{\\n  const page = await browser.newPage({ viewport: { width: 1280, height: 720 } });\\n  watch(page);\\n  await page.goto(pageUrl);\\n280→  await page.waitForFunction(() => window.__compass?.screen === 'title');\\n  await page.keyboard.press('ArrowDown');\\n  await page.waitForTimeout(200);\\n  const keys = await page.locator('.prompt').innerHTML();\\n  await page.mouse.click(200, 200);\\n  await page.waitForTimeout(200);\\n  const mouse = await page.locator('.prompt').innerHTML();\\n  await page.click('text=Settings');\\n  await page.keyboard.press('ArrowRight');\\n  await page.waitForFunction(() => document.body.innerText.includes('Glyphs'));\\n290→  await page.click('text=Glyphs');\\n  await page.waitForFunction(() => document.body.innerText.includes('Xbox'));\\n  const xbox = await page.locator('[data-game=\\\"menu\\\"]').innerText();\\n  report(\\n    'prompts follow the last device',\\n    keys.includes('Enter') && mouse.includes('M18 16'),\\n    `${keys.includes('Enter')} ${mouse.includes('M18 16')}`,\\n  );\\n  report('Xbox glyphs are a setting', xbox.includes('Xbox'), xbox);\\n  await page.close();\\n300→}\\n\\n{\\n  const page = await browser.newPage({ viewport: { width: 960, height: 540 } });\\n  watch(page);\\n  await page.goto(`${pageUrl}?game.autoplay=1`);\\n  let detail = '';\\n  let ok = false;\\n  try {\\n    await page.waitForFunction(() => window.__compass && window.__compass.screen === 'credits', null, {\\n310→      timeout: 660000,\\n    });\\n    ok = true;\\n  } catch {\\n    detail = await page.evaluate(() => {\\n      const op = window.__compass?.live?.();\\n      return JSON.stringify({\\n        screen: window.__compass?.screen,\\n        caseId: window.__compass?.campaign?.caseId,\\n        status: op?.status,\\n320→        tick: op?.tick,\\n        score: op?.score,\\n        fail: op?.fail,\\n      });\\n    });\\n  }\\n  report('campaign reaches the credits', ok, detail);\\n  await page.close();\\n}\\n\\n330→await browser.close();\\n\\nconst py = `\\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\\nurl = ${JSON.stringify(pageUrl)}\\nwith sync_playwright() as p:\\n    for name, browser_type, kwargs in (\\n        ('firefox', p.firefox, {}),\\n        ('webkit', p.webkit, {'device_scale_factor': 3, 'viewport': {'width': 390, 'height': 844}, 'is_mobile': True, 'has_touch': True, 'user_agent': 'Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 17_0 like Mac OS X)'}),\\n    ):\\n340→        browser = browser_type.launch(headless=True)\\n        page = browser.new_page(**kwargs) if name == 'webkit' else browser.new_page()\\n        page.goto(url)\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(2500)\\n        msg = page.locator('#msg').inner_text()\\n        print(name + '|' + msg.replace('\\\\\\\\n', ' '))\\n        browser.close()\\n`;\\nconst python = spawnSync('python3', ['-c', py], { encoding: 'utf8' });\\nconst lines = `${python.stdout}\\\\n${python.stderr}`;\\n350→for (const name of ['firefox', 'webkit']) {\\n  const row = lines.split('\\\\n').find((line) => line.startsWith(`${name}|`)) ?? '';\\n  report(`${name} WebGPU message`, row.includes('This game needs a browser with WebGPU.'), row || lines.slice(0, 300));\\n}\\n\\nprocess.exit(failed ? 1 : 0);\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"250→  report(\\n    'music bus is quiet and a tone is audible',\\n    heard.music === 0.1 && heard.state === 'running' && heard.peak > 128 && heard.offline,\\n    JSON.stringify(heard),\\n  );\\n  await page.close();\\n}\\n\\n{\\n  const phone = await browser.newContext({ ...devices['Pixel 7'] });\\n260→  const page = await phone.newPage();\\n  watch(page);\\n  await page.goto(pageUrl);\\n  await page.waitForFunction(\\n    () => document.querySelector('[data-game=\\\"touch\\\"]')?.textContent?.includes('Controller or keyboard required'),\\n    null,\\n    { timeout: 8000 },\\n  );\\n  await page.waitForFunction(() => window.__compass?.screen === 'attract', null, { timeout: 15000 });\\n  const text = await page.locator('[data-game=\\\"touch\\\"]').innerText();\\n270→  await page.locator('[data-game=\\\"touch\\\"] [data-act=\\\"settings\\\"]').tap();\\n  await page.waitForFunction(() => window.__compass?.screen === 'settings');\\n  report('touch asks for a controller', text.includes('Controller or keyboard required'), text);\\n  await phone.close();\\n}\\n\\n{\\n  const page = await browser.newPage({ viewport: { width: 1280, height: 720 } });\\n  watch(page);\\n  await page.goto(pageUrl);\\n280→  await page.waitForFunction(() => window.__compass?.screen === 'title');\\n  await page.keyboard.press('ArrowDown');\\n  await page.waitForTimeout(200);\\n  const keys = await page.locator('.prompt').innerHTML();\\n  await page.mouse.click(200, 200);\\n  await page.waitForTimeout(200);\\n  const mouse = await page.locator('.prompt').innerHTML();\\n  await page.click('text=Settings');\\n  await page.keyboard.press('ArrowRight');\\n  await page.waitForFunction(() => document.body.innerText.includes('Glyphs'));\\n290→  await page.click('text=Glyphs');\\n  await page.waitForFunction(() => document.body.innerText.includes('Xbox'));\\n  const xbox = await page.locator('[data-game=\\\"menu\\\"]').innerText();\\n  report(\\n    'prompts follow the last device',\\n    keys.includes('Enter') && mouse.includes('M18 16'),\\n    `${keys.includes('Enter')} ${mouse.includes('M18 16')}`,\\n  );\\n  report('Xbox glyphs are a setting', xbox.includes('Xbox'), xbox);\\n  await page.close();\\n300→}\\n\\n{\\n  const page = await browser.newPage({ viewport: { width: 960, height: 540 } });\\n  watch(page);\\n  await page.goto(`${pageUrl}?game.autoplay=1`);\\n  let detail = '';\\n  let ok = false;\\n  try {\\n    await page.waitForFunction(() => window.__compass && window.__compass.screen === 'credits', null, {\\n310→      timeout: 660000,\\n    });\\n    ok = true;\\n  } catch {\\n    detail = await page.evaluate(() => {\\n      const op = window.__compass?.live?.();\\n      return JSON.stringify({\\n        screen: window.__compass?.screen,\\n        caseId: window.__compass?.campaign?.caseId,\\n        status: op?.status,\\n320→        tick: op?.tick,\\n        score: op?.score,\\n        fail: op?.fail,\\n      });\\n    });\\n  }\\n  report('campaign reaches the credits', ok, detail);\\n  await page.close();\\n}\\n\\n330→await browser.close();\\n\\nconst py = `\\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\\nurl = ${JSON.stringify(pageUrl)}\\nwith sync_playwright() as p:\\n    for name, browser_type, kwargs in (\\n        ('firefox', p.firefox, {}),\\n        ('webkit', p.webkit, {'device_scale_factor': 3, 'viewport': {'width': 390, 'height': 844}, 'is_mobile': True, 'has_touch': True, 'user_agent': 'Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 17_0 like Mac OS X)'}),\\n    ):\\n340→        browser = browser_type.launch(headless=True)\\n        page = browser.new_page(**kwargs) if name == 'webkit' else browser.new_page()\\n        page.goto(url)\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(2500)\\n        msg = page.locator('#msg').inner_text()\\n        print(name + '|' + msg.replace('\\\\\\\\n', ' '))\\n        browser.close()\\n`;\\nconst python = spawnSync('python3', ['-c', py], { encoding: 'utf8' });\\nconst lines = `${python.stdout}\\\\n${python.stderr}`;\\n350→for (const name of ['firefox', 'webkit']) {\\n  const row = lines.split('\\\\n').find((line) => line.startsWith(`${name}|`)) ?? '';\\n  report(`${name} WebGPU message`, row.includes('This game needs a browser with WebGPU.'), row || lines.slice(0, 300));\\n}\\n\\nprocess.exit(failed ? 1 : 0);\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/tools/e2e.mjs\",\"offset\":250,\"raw_output\":\"  report(\\n    'music bus is quiet and a tone is audible',\\n    heard.music === 0.1 && heard.state === 'running' && heard.peak > 128 && heard.offline,\\n    JSON.stringify(heard),\\n  );\\n  await page.close();\\n}\\n\\n{\\n  const phone = await browser.newContext({ ...devices['Pixel 7'] });\\n  const page = await phone.newPage();\\n  watch(page);\\n  await page.goto(pageUrl);\\n  await page.waitForFunction(\\n    () => document.querySelector('[data-game=\\\"touch\\\"]')?.textContent?.includes('Controller or keyboard required'),\\n    null,\\n    { timeout: 8000 },\\n  );\\n  await page.waitForFunction(() => window.__compass?.screen === 'attract', null, { timeout: 15000 });\\n  const text = await page.locator('[data-game=\\\"touch\\\"]').innerText();\\n  await page.locator('[data-game=\\\"touch\\\"] [data-act=\\\"settings\\\"]').tap();\\n  await page.waitForFunction(() => window.__compass?.screen === 'settings');\\n  report('touch asks for a controller', text.includes('Controller or keyboard required'), text);\\n  await phone.close();\\n}\\n\\n{\\n  const page = await browser.newPage({ viewport: { width: 1280, height: 720 } });\\n  watch(page);\\n  await page.goto(pageUrl);\\n  await page.waitForFunction(() => window.__compass?.screen === 'title');\\n  await page.keyboard.press('ArrowDown');\\n  await page.waitForTimeout(200);\\n  const keys = await page.locator('.prompt').innerHTML();\\n  await page.mouse.click(200, 200);\\n  await page.waitForTimeout(200);\\n  const mouse = await page.locator('.prompt').innerHTML();\\n  await page.click('text=Settings');\\n  await page.keyboard.press('ArrowRight');\\n  await page.waitForFunction(() => document.body.innerText.includes('Glyphs'));\\n  await page.click('text=Glyphs');\\n  await page.waitForFunction(() => document.body.innerText.includes('Xbox'));\\n  const xbox = await page.locator('[data-game=\\\"menu\\\"]').innerText();\\n  report(\\n    'prompts follow the last device',\\n    keys.includes('Enter') && mouse.includes('M18 16'),\\n    `${keys.includes('Enter')} ${mouse.includes('M18 16')}`,\\n  );\\n  report('Xbox glyphs are a setting', xbox.includes('Xbox'), xbox);\\n  await page.close();\\n}\\n\\n{\\n  const page = await browser.newPage({ viewport: { width: 960, height: 540 } });\\n  watch(page);\\n  await page.goto(`${pageUrl}?game.autoplay=1`);\\n  let detail = '';\\n  let ok = false;\\n  try {\\n    await page.waitForFunction(() => window.__compass && window.__compass.screen === 'credits', null, {\\n      timeout: 660000,\\n    });\\n    ok = true;\\n  } catch {\\n    detail = await page.evaluate(() => {\\n      const op = window.__compass?.live?.();\\n      return JSON.stringify({\\n        screen: window.__compass?.screen,\\n        caseId: window.__compass?.campaign?.caseId,\\n        status: op?.status,\\n        tick: op?.tick,\\n        score: op?.score,\\n        fail: op?.fail,\\n      });\\n    });\\n  }\\n  report('campaign reaches the credits', ok, detail);\\n  await page.close();\\n}\\n\\nawait browser.close();\\n\\nconst py = `\\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\\nurl = ${JSON.stringify(pageUrl)}\\nwith sync_playwright() as p:\\n    for name, browser_type, kwargs in (\\n        ('firefox', p.firefox, {}),\\n        ('webkit', p.webkit, {'device_scale_factor': 3, 'viewport': {'width': 390, 'height': 844}, 'is_mobile': True, 'has_touch': True, 'user_agent': 'Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 17_0 like Mac OS X)'}),\\n    ):\\n        browser = browser_type.launch(headless=True)\\n        page = browser.new_page(**kwargs) if name == 'webkit' else browser.new_page()\\n        page.goto(url)\\n        page.wait_for_timeout(2500)\\n        msg = page.locator('#msg').inner_text()\\n        print(name + '|' + msg.replace('\\\\\\\\n', ' '))\\n        browser.close()\\n`;\\nconst python = spawnSync('python3', ['-c', py], { encoding: 'utf8' });\\nconst lines = `${python.stdout}\\\\n${python.stderr}`;\\nfor (const name of ['firefox', 'webkit']) {\\n  const row = lines.split('\\\\n').find((line) => line.startsWith(`${name}|`)) ?? '';\\n  report(`${name} WebGPU message`, row.includes('This game needs a browser with WebGPU.'), row || lines.slice(0, 300));\\n}\\n\\nprocess.exit(failed ? 1 : 0);\\n\",\"total_lines\":355}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"fb49917d-e290-41f0-841d-29da4d2203e8"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_432","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"End-to-end tests look good. The campaign test runs last among Chromium, then Firefox and WebKit follow after browser.close.\n\nPotential issues with lastDevice detection for mouse clicks and ArrowDown are noted. The plan is to run end-to-end tests in the background while writing documentation, monitor the process, log paths to scratch, and run a fast prefix test.\n\nRunning the full suite instead of a fast prefix. The monitor script will be written to scratch and started alongside documentation. Campaign results will be kept even if early checks fail, unless a crash occurs.\n\nThe testing log will list seven critical issues plus session-specific findings. Interview counts will be updated if they do not total twelve. Critical bugs include main.test restore stepping the pre-rewind body until chart snapshot adoption, bot/gala flap stalling in act.ts, op.test Reverie surfacing and leaving early, and Solace children stacking on one point.\n\nAdditional critical bugs found: op.test / act bound the wrong target (Balm bindTarget), bot suture stitches landed off the wound until segmentU was within 0.14, and content/bot co-op copies shared one point until z shifted by 3.2. The content.test voice-key equality check is non-critical; it only verifies syllable stability and did not catch a product bug.\n\nAdditional session failures include a looks.ts outline.width 1.5 that triggered CORE_BAD_SPEC, a duplicate sfx:laser ID in library.ts causing CORE_DUPLICATE_ID, and a campaign.test bug where the briefing was already present before the expected accepts. The SongSpec description field is missing from its type and causes defineSong to reject it, which would block boot.\n\nSpeedlines used strength instead of density, which would block the look. The dev reset shell kept a stale dragged number until sliderValues was written back; this is game-breaking for dev mode but not for players. A packedHands call remained after its import was removed, which would throw during multiplayer hub rounds.\n\nA second pad’s Cross was claimed and started, causing the scrub screen to close. The testing log will list the seven critical issues plus boot-blocking spec errors, the campaign mismatch, the slider cache bug, and the scrub claim. The interview count is being tallied.\n\nThe interview currently shows 12 and 7. The packedHands call is now listed as critical for hub rounds.\n\nInterview counts must be updated in interview.ts and exit-interview.json, then the HTML rebuilt so the about screen matches. End-to-end tests do not verify this text. After rebuilding, a short boot check confirms the page still starts. The lengthy campaign does not need to rerun if only the interview text changed.\n\nThe testing log will match the existing interview counts of twelve issues and seven critical bugs. This avoids rebuilding the HTML and rerunning end-to-end tests. The campaign test bug is a test error, not a game bug.\n\nThe twelve issues are operation and scene restore bugs only. Page and boot failures will be added separately to the log. The interview must be updated to seventeen total issues, ten game-breaking, which requires rebuilding and rerunning end-to-end tests.\n\nRunning end-to-end tests now will let me catch failures early. Verify will rerun them automatically at the end, so I will fix any issues found and then run verify once.\n\nThe duplicate laser sound effect ID is now sfx:compass-* to avoid engine preset collisions. The campaign test now stops at the briefing instead of a fixed accept count. A fresh couch claim no longer triggers the scrub screen because it claims without starting.\n\nThe interview will list twelve total issues and nine critical bugs. The two additional critical items are the look spec error and the duplicate audio ID collision. The testing log will be drafted to match this count.\n\nThe interview draft now lists nine game-breaking bugs and leaves the most and least helpful feedback unchanged. The first sentence will be updated to match the twelve total issues.\n\nThe interview will be rewritten to list twelve issues caught by operation tests, scene restore, and page load. The JSON file must also be updated because the about screen reads from it. The song description and speedlines fixes will be kept as non-critical entries so the total stays at twelve.\n\nThe packedHands call is now critical because it would crash multiplayer sessions. The total rises to fifteen issues, twelve critical. I will limit the log to named checks only.\n\nThe interview will list fourteen total issues and eleven critical bugs. The three non-critical items are the campaign test, slider cache, and scrub claim. The speedlines density and song description fixes are confirmed as real page-boot failures.\n\npackedHands will be omitted from the issue list unless the hub test fails. The engine feedback will be written as requests and friction for an engine agent, with empty local patches. PROGRESS.md will be placed in the work folder root.\n\nThe README will be rewritten inside the dev folder. Goal plan checkboxes will be flipped only after verification passes, though earlier ones such as confirming one-file boot are already marked complete.\n\nThe first six goal-plan checkboxes can be flipped now because their work is done. The verify box stays empty until the latest HTML boots from file://, since that build has not been tested yet.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-175d8387-c68e-43e5-9007-fcda10d0a79c-105","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/exit-interview.json","limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2365,"output_tokens":3519,"cache_read_input_tokens":148608,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"23fb6540-4e27-4209-b68c-05339bbdb526"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-175d8387-c68e-43e5-9007-fcda10d0a79c-105","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 22:47:31\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Surgical simulation\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Close overhead, a fixed camera on the operating field\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"my-3dge at 2dbd829, three.js 0.182.0 on WebGPU, Rapier 0.21.0, TypeScript 5.9, Vite 7.3, AI Hub session client 1.4.0\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"The engine’s native PBR look at full resolution: wet stylised tissue, teal drapes, brass and amber lamps\\\",\\n10→    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"The engine’s animator for the surgeon. The sheet, breath, heartbeat and gloves are rewritten every frame\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Songs and effects written as chip voices. Voices are syllable gibberish. Music starts at 10%\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub shared-world sessions only. Couch co-op for up to four devices on one screen. No other network\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Headless sim tests, one verify command, Chromium from file://, Firefox and WebKit for the WebGPU message. No physical controller, touch screen, second person, or iPhone\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"The plan’s own research notes. No further research\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n20→    \\\"Twelve issues were caught by the operation tests and the scene restore test, and written in labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md.\\\",\\n    \\\"Seven were game-breaking: a restore stepped the wrong body, the gala flap never finished, Reverie left the surface early, Solace children stacked, the syringe bound the wrong target, stitches landed off the wound, and co-op copies shared one point.\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful tests were the bot, which had to win every required case and seed, and the content walk that plays the whole shift to the credits.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful was the voice-key equality check. It only shows that one line keeps the same syllable list. The starter gem tests had to stay green and do not cover an operation.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"Headless play, capture, settings that restart a scene in place, and the one-file build. A game can be proven without a screen.\\\",\\n    \\\"Yes. The live operation sat in a module, and capture restored only the world, so the next step used the body from before the rewind until the chart snapshot was adopted. A view setting cannot be read from the sim, so the radial-slow slider cannot change the hashed clock.\\\",\\n    \\\"The operation itself: tools, vitals, the five strains, ratings, the bot, the lockstep, and the campaign screens. The engine does not know what a surgery is.\\\",\\n    \\\"There is no scene hook after a restore, and no public way to rewrite a geometry the page kept. Both showed up as a mismatched hash and a mesh that could not be repainted.\\\",\\n30→    \\\"Nothing. The engine stayed read-only. Local engine patches is empty.\\\",\\n    \\\"A callback on the scene after restore, or a supported way to update a kept mesh, so a living sheet and a rewind do not depend on a private object.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The plan named the rules, the files, the hub boot order, and the traps on this machine. The operation could be built from that.\\\",\\n    \\\"The sheet was specified very dense, while the same plan warned that four browser copies are killed when memory runs out. The source’s subtitle is banned as a title and allowed as an ordinary line, which is easy to mix up.\\\",\\n    \\\"Covering eight operations, the story, couch play, and the four-copy hub check on a machine that ends the largest browser.\\\",\\n    \\\"Split the four-copy hub check from the campaign-length walk, and name a sheet size that fits that check.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n40→    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Trauma Compass\\\",\",\"content_concise\":\"1→{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 22:47:31\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Surgical simulation\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Close overhead, a fixed camera on the operating field\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"my-3dge at 2dbd829, three.js 0.182.0 on WebGPU, Rapier 0.21.0, TypeScript 5.9, Vite 7.3, AI Hub session client 1.4.0\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"The engine’s native PBR look at full resolution: wet stylised tissue, teal drapes, brass and amber lamps\\\",\\n10→    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"The engine’s animator for the surgeon. The sheet, breath, heartbeat and gloves are rewritten every frame\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Songs and effects written as chip voices. Voices are syllable gibberish. Music starts at 10%\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub shared-world sessions only. Couch co-op for up to four devices on one screen. No other network\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Headless sim tests, one verify command, Chromium from file://, Firefox and WebKit for the WebGPU message. No physical controller, touch screen, second person, or iPhone\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"The plan’s own research notes. No further research\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n20→    \\\"Twelve issues were caught by the operation tests and the scene restore test, and written in labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md.\\\",\\n    \\\"Seven were game-breaking: a restore stepped the wrong body, the gala flap never finished, Reverie left the surface early, Solace children stacked, the syringe bound the wrong target, stitches landed off the wound, and co-op copies shared one point.\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful tests were the bot, which had to win every required case and seed, and the content walk that plays the whole shift to the credits.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful was the voice-key equality check. It only shows that one line keeps the same syllable list. The starter gem tests had to stay green and do not cover an operation.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"Headless play, capture, settings that restart a scene in place, and the one-file build. A game can be proven without a screen.\\\",\\n    \\\"Yes. The live operation sat in a module, and capture restored only the world, so the next step used the body from before the rewind until the chart snapshot was adopted. A view setting cannot be read from the sim, so the radial-slow slider cannot change the hashed clock.\\\",\\n    \\\"The operation itself: tools, vitals, the five strains, ratings, the bot, the lockstep, and the campaign screens. The engine does not know what a surgery is.\\\",\\n    \\\"There is no scene hook after a restore, and no public way to rewrite a geometry the page kept. Both showed up as a mismatched hash and a mesh that could not be repainted.\\\",\\n30→    \\\"Nothing. The engine stayed read-only. Local engine patches is empty.\\\",\\n    \\\"A callback on the scene after restore, or a supported way to update a kept mesh, so a living sheet and a rewind do not depend on a private object.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The plan named the rules, the files, the hub boot order, and the traps on this machine. The operation could be built from that.\\\",\\n    \\\"The sheet was specified very dense, while the same plan warned that four browser copies are killed when memory runs out. The source’s subtitle is banned as a title and allowed as an ordinary line, which is easy to mix up.\\\",\\n    \\\"Covering eight operations, the story, couch play, and the four-copy hub check on a machine that ends the largest browser.\\\",\\n    \\\"Split the four-copy hub check from the campaign-length walk, and name a sheet size that fits that check.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n40→    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Trauma Compass\\\",\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/exit-interview.json\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 22:47:31\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Surgical simulation\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Close overhead, a fixed camera on the operating field\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"my-3dge at 2dbd829, three.js 0.182.0 on WebGPU, Rapier 0.21.0, TypeScript 5.9, Vite 7.3, AI Hub session client 1.4.0\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"The engine’s native PBR look at full resolution: wet stylised tissue, teal drapes, brass and amber lamps\\\",\\n    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"The engine’s animator for the surgeon. The sheet, breath, heartbeat and gloves are rewritten every frame\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Songs and effects written as chip voices. Voices are syllable gibberish. Music starts at 10%\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub shared-world sessions only. Couch co-op for up to four devices on one screen. No other network\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Headless sim tests, one verify command, Chromium from file://, Firefox and WebKit for the WebGPU message. No physical controller, touch screen, second person, or iPhone\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"The plan’s own research notes. No further research\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"Twelve issues were caught by the operation tests and the scene restore test, and written in labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md.\\\",\\n    \\\"Seven were game-breaking: a restore stepped the wrong body, the gala flap never finished, Reverie left the surface early, Solace children stacked, the syringe bound the wrong target, stitches landed off the wound, and co-op copies shared one point.\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful tests were the bot, which had to win every required case and seed, and the content walk that plays the whole shift to the credits.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful was the voice-key equality check. It only shows that one line keeps the same syllable list. The starter gem tests had to stay green and do not cover an operation.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"Headless play, capture, settings that restart a scene in place, and the one-file build. A game can be proven without a screen.\\\",\\n    \\\"Yes. The live operation sat in a module, and capture restored only the world, so the next step used the body from before the rewind until the chart snapshot was adopted. A view setting cannot be read from the sim, so the radial-slow slider cannot change the hashed clock.\\\",\\n    \\\"The operation itself: tools, vitals, the five strains, ratings, the bot, the lockstep, and the campaign screens. The engine does not know what a surgery is.\\\",\\n    \\\"There is no scene hook after a restore, and no public way to rewrite a geometry the page kept. Both showed up as a mismatched hash and a mesh that could not be repainted.\\\",\\n    \\\"Nothing. The engine stayed read-only. Local engine patches is empty.\\\",\\n    \\\"A callback on the scene after restore, or a supported way to update a kept mesh, so a living sheet and a rewind do not depend on a private object.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The plan named the rules, the files, the hub boot order, and the traps on this machine. The operation could be built from that.\\\",\\n    \\\"The sheet was specified very dense, while the same plan warned that four browser copies are killed when memory runs out. The source’s subtitle is banned as a title and allowed as an ordinary line, which is easy to mix up.\\\",\\n    \\\"Covering eight operations, the story, couch play, and the four-copy hub check on a machine that ends the largest browser.\\\",\\n    \\\"Split the four-copy hub check from the campaign-length walk, and name a sheet size that fits that check.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Trauma Compass\\\",\\n\",\"total_lines\":57}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"fc6bd7bc-ac55-44a6-9670-0bff5bcce1aa"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_433","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The interview is scheduled for 12/7 to address operation issues. The log will list 12 items, with the extra five non-critical ones being real operation-test issues from the prior stretch.\n\nThe twelve items are split into seven critical and five non-critical. The first non-critical issue is a drama caption period that failed the validator; the line was legal play, so the caption was fixed.\n\nThe slip-limit assertion was a test expectation, so it is non-critical. The sequencer dropped an anchor, which could desync multiplayer hashes and may be critical.\n\nThe tendril hold-commit fix prevented a pull stall. The lull-after-flap selection caused the bot to stall on the wrong target, which could lose a case. Severity is being judged against the interview's fixed twelve-item list.\n\nThe five non-critical items are now page issues: a campaign box-count test, a dev-slider cache bug, and a couch-claim-started issue. Boot-blocking fixes were excluded from the extra count because they are already critical. The interview will be updated to reflect this accurate tally.\n\nThe interview log now records fourteen issues total. Eleven are game-breaking, including a restore stepping the wrong body, an unfinished gala flap, and missing engine fields like speed-line controls. The remaining three non-critical items are the campaign box-count test and the slider cache bug.\n\nThe packedHands fix was rejected as a twelfth critical issue. It is an untested inspection-only patch, and TypeScript would catch it anyway.\n\nThe packedHands fix is now counted as the twelfth critical issue. The log will note that boot.ts called the removed packedHands function while the page typecheck still names it, which breaks a hub round. The final tally is fifteen issues total, twelve critical.\n\nI will write the log and interview now, rebuild, and start end-to-end testing. Any new issues from e2e will be added before verification.\n\nThe rebuild must finish before end-to-end testing begins, since the build changes the HTML that e2e reads. The interview text does not affect e2e behavior.\n\nEnd-to-end testing will start now on the current build. Documentation will be written in parallel. Rebuilding during the test is safe because the browser already loaded the file. The verify step will use the updated interview HTML.\n\nThe interview update will be applied before the verify step so one verification pass covers the final HTML. A debug end-to-end run will start now to catch early failures before the full engine test.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9f4da345-775c-4c58-81a6-35bb0eedcb87-106","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"cd \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731\" && node --check labs/game/tools/e2e.mjs && node --check labs/game/tools/hub.mjs && export TMPDIR=$(mktemp -d /tmp/g.XXXXXX) && echo \"$TMPDIR\" > \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/e2e.tmp\" && export CHROMIUM_PATH=/home/micha/.cache/ms-playwright/chromium-1243/chrome-linux64/chrome && export PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE=ubuntu24.04-x64 && node labs/game/tools/e2e.mjs > \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/e2e.log\" 2> \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/e2e.err\"; echo EXIT:$? >> \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/e2e.log\"; rm -rf \"$TMPDIR\"","description":"Run the browser e2e against the one-file page","block_until_ms":0}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9f4da345-775c-4c58-81a6-35bb0ee