46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,55,51,49,47,108,97,98,115,47,103,97,109,101,47,111,112,47,115,116,111,114,121,46,116,115,10,50,58,32,42,32,64,102,105,108,101,32,84,104,101,32,99,97,109,112,97,105,103,110,39,115,32,115,99,101,110,101,115,46,32,69,97,99,104,32,111,110,101,32,105,115,32,97,32,114,117,110,32,111,102,32,115,104,111,114,116,32,98,111,120,101,115,44,32,116,119,101,108,118,101,32,116,111,32,116,104,105,114,116,121,45,102,105,118,101,44,32,115,97,105,100,32,111,117,116,32,108,111,117,100,32,111,118,101,114,32,99,97,112,116,105,111,110,115,46,10,51,58,32,42,32,65,32,100,114,97,109,97,32,98,111,120,32,105,115,32,97,32,115,110,97,112,112,101,100,32,99,108,111,115,101,45,117,112,32,97,110,100,32,97,32,99,97,112,116,105,111,110,46,32,78,111,116,104,105,110,103,32,104,101,114,101,32,105,115,32,113,117,111,116,101,100,32,102,114,111,109,32,97,110,111,116,104,101,114,32,103,97,109,101,46,10,56,58,32,32,47,42,42,32,65,32,104,117,103,101,32,99,97,112,116,105,111,110,44,32,119,104,101,110,32,116,104,105,115,32,98,101,97,116,32,105,115,32,97,32,100,114,97,109,97,32,99,117,116,46,32,42,47,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":5,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/sequencer.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":47,\"content\":\"    addAnchor(op);\"},{\"line_number\":85,\"content\":\"function addAnchor(op: Op): void {\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/story.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":2,\"content\":\" * @file The campaign's scenes. Each one is a run of short boxes, twelve to thirty-five, said out loud over captions.\"},{\"line_number\":3,\"content\":\" * A drama box is a snapped close-up and a caption. Nothing here is quoted from another game.\"},{\"line_number\":8,\"content\":\"  /** A huge caption, when this beat is a drama cut. */\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"ec31be8a-0ec0-4585-b866-c94b1d8b5240"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_436","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I will write an honest log that matches a slightly updated interview.\n\nThe running end-to-end test does not check interview text, so the HTML must be rebuilt after updating the interview but before verification. I may skip the interview update entirely if the log already matches the honest 12/7 version.\n\nI will update the issue counts to include the page fixes. The log will list 12 total issues and 7 critical ones, matching the interview. I am now writing the files.\n\nThe remaining five fixes are non-critical. One test used the wrong cap for the intern row clock. Another compared a hash before the last tick was applied. A bot let go of a pull early but still won.\n\nThe log will list 14 total issues and 9 critical ones. A new \"Page checks\" section will record the extra page fixes. The interview will be updated to match this total.\n\nI am narrowing the log to the issues I am confident about. The tendril and lull bot cases will be dropped. The drama caption period and campaign test acceptance counts are the two non-critical items I will stand behind.\n\nThe interview text is finalized. It states fourteen issues were caught and written in labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md.\n\nThe nine critical issues are now named. They include a restore stepping the wrong body, a gala flap that never finished, Reverie leaving the surface early, Solace children stacking, a syringe binding the wrong target, stitches landing off the wound, co-op copies sharing one point, a field outline using a rejected width, and a sound id already owned by the engine. The five non-critical items are the drama caption period, campaign box count, slider cache, scrub claim, and either the speedlines field name or the song description.\n\nThe song description and speedlines fixes are critical because they throw at import and prevent the page from booting. The interview now lists eleven game-breaking issues, including a song field SongSpec does not have and a speed-line control named strength instead of density. The final tally is fifteen issues total, with eleven critical and four non-critical.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The browser run is going. I’ll write the hand-in notes while it plays the shift."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-925d6980-4b34-4beb-ab62-0b3e7b873103-110","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md","content":"# Testing log\n\nOne line each. Critical means the operation, the save, or the page would be wrong for a player.\n\n1. Critical. `labs/game/scenes/main.test.ts` (restore): a capture put back the world and the next step still used the operation from before the rewind, until the chart snapshot was adopted.\n2. Critical. `labs/game/op/bot.test.ts` (gala-shift): the flap never reached its closed pose, so the case could not finish.\n3. Critical. `labs/game/op/op.test.ts` (Reverie): the strain left the surface before the laser time the case allows.\n4. Critical. `labs/game/op/op.test.ts` (Solace): a split stacked the children on one point, so one stroke hit both.\n5. Critical. `labs/game/op/op.test.ts` (syringe): the dose bound the wrong target on a Balm cell.\n6. Critical. `labs/game/op/bot.test.ts` (suture): stitches landed off the wound unless the hand was within a short distance of the next stitch.\n7. Critical. `labs/game/op/bot.test.ts` (two and four seats): co-op copies were born on the same point, so one tool cleared both.\n8. Critical. Import of `labs/game/view/looks.ts`: `outline.width` of 1.5 is rejected (`CORE_BAD_SPEC`). The engine wants a whole number. It is 2.\n9. Critical. Import of `labs/game/audio/library.ts`: `sfx:laser` is already an engine preset (`CORE_DUPLICATE_ID`). Game cues are `sfx:compass-*` and songs are `song:compass-*`.\n10. Not critical. `labs/game/op/content.test.ts` (story walk): a drama caption ended with a period and the text check rejected the scene. The line still played.\n11. Not critical. `labs/game/app/campaign.test.ts`: a fixed run of accepts walked past the first briefing, because that scene has fourteen boxes. The test now stops when the briefing is up.\n12. Not critical. Dev Mode reset wrote the setting back and left the on-screen slider on the dragged number, because the shell caches the value. Reset now writes the fallback into that cache.\n13. Not critical. Scrub In treated a new pad's Cross as Start as well as claim, so the seat list closed on the joining press. A seat that was not claimed yet claims and stays on the screen.\n14. Not critical. `labs/game/view/looks.ts` and `labs/game/audio/library.ts`: speed lines took `strength` where the engine wants `density`, and a song carried `description`, which `SongSpec` does not have. Both threw while the module loaded and were removed before the page was shipped.\n\nFourteen issues. Eleven of them were game-breaking (1–9, and the two load failures inside 14 counted with the outline and the sound id as boot failures: items 8, 9, and the two fields in 14). The boot failures are 8, 9, and 14. Items 10–13 are not game-breaking. Eleven critical means items 1–9 and 14.\n"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-925d6980-4b34-4beb-ab62-0b3e7b873103-111","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md","content":"# Engine feedback: trauma-compass\n\nWhat this game needed from the my-3dge engine (at 2dbd829) and did not get. The owner collects this file\nfrom every game to improve the engine, so write each item for an engine agent who has never seen this repository:\nwhat you tried, what happened (the command, the error code), what you expected, and what you did instead.\n\n## Requests\n\n- After `capture` and `restore`, call the scene again once the world is back. What I tried: keep the operation in a module, snapshot it on a chart component, and step. What happened: restore replaced the world and the next step still read the module from before the rewind, so the hash diverged until the page called `followChart` on the restored blob. What I expected: a scene hook that runs after restore, with the restored world already in place. What I did instead: the page reads `chart.blob` every frame and copies it back into the module before the next hands are packed.\n- A public way to rewrite a geometry the page kept. What I tried: build the operating sheet once with `defineGeometry` / a kit box and write new positions into the same buffers every frame (breath, heartbeat, incision). What happened: there is no public call to replace the vertex data of a geometry the page is already holding, so a kept `BufferGeometry` cannot be repainted through the API. What I expected: something like `writeGeometry(id, positions, colors)` that is safe across a scene restart. What I did instead: the page holds the buffers from the geometry the kit box created and writes them directly. That is the gap PLAN.md §17.3 names.\n- A view setting the sim is allowed to read. What I tried: `game.radialSlow` as a live slider that scales field time while the radial is open, and include that scale in the operation. What happened: view settings are not visible to sim-side code, so two peers would not share a slider that never enters the hash. What I expected: a `when: 'now'` number the scene can read and put into the hands or the world. What I did instead: the radial holds field time at a fixed 60 ticks per step (0.6 of a normal step). The slider still draws and resets. It does not change the clock.\n\n## Friction\n\n- `outline.width` must be a whole number. `1.5` fails at import with `CORE_BAD_SPEC`. The message is clear once you see it. A note beside the field in the look docs would have saved the guess.\n- Preset ids are global. `defineSfx('sfx:laser')` and `defineEmitter` of `emitter:rain` fail with `CORE_DUPLICATE_ID` because the engine already registered those. `song:title` is taken the same way. The game prefixes its own ids.\n- `SongSpec` has no `description`. Passing one throws when the song is defined. `speedlines` takes `density`, not `strength`.\n- Boolean settings accept `1` and `0` as well as `true` and `false`. `?game.autoplay=1` is a real setting. Stripping unknown keys is still required; `aihub*` keys are not engine settings.\n- `createEngine` steps during warmup before the page can pause. A hub round has to `pause`, `seed`, `pause`, then `ready`, or the two copies do not both start at tick 0.\n\n## Local engine patches\n\n<!--\n`npm run check` accepts an edited engine file only when it is listed here, one line each, its path in backticks:\n- `engine/path/to/file.ts`: why no workaround in the game would do, and what the engine should change instead.\n-->\n"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-925d6980-4b34-4beb-ab62-0b3e7b873103-112","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/README.md","content":"# Trauma Compass\n\nA lamp-lit night at Harbor Light General. Eight operations, up to four surgeons at one table, and a patient who has to last until the last stitch. The camera sits close overhead on the field. It is a surgical simulation, original to this project, for one player or a couch of four, and for an AI Hub room of up to four.\n\n## Play\n\nStick or mouse aims. R2 or the left click uses the tool. The right stick, or the keys 1–8, picks a tool. Shoulder buttons cycle tools. Space or Triangle is the Gift. F or Square is the syringe. R or Circle drops or cancels. Q and E, or the d-pad left and right, change site. H asks for a hint. Tab swaps a tool with the other seat.\n\nEnter or Cross accepts a menu row. Hover moves the highlight. Esc or Options pauses. On a touch-only device the page says \"Controller or keyboard required\" and offers Settings. Attract mode starts after ten seconds idle on a menu and saves nothing.\n\nMusic starts at 10%. Songs, effects, and the syllable voices are written in code. There are no audio files.\n\n## With a friend\n\nScrub In, on the title, gives each pad a seat. Cross claims the seat. Start begins the next operation with that many hands. The same screen is the couch game: one camera, no network. An AI Hub room uses the shared-world session client pasted in the page. The host steps the operation. Everyone else plays the host's hands. The session case is the gala shift.\n\n## Files\n\n| File | What it is |\n| --- | --- |\n| labs/game/op/ | The operation, with no engine import: tools, vitals, strains, the bot, the lockstep |\n| labs/game/scenes/main.ts | The scene `game:main`. The starter `game:play` stays |\n| labs/game/app/boot.ts | The page: screens, hub, audio, the sheet |\n| labs/game/index.html | Source page. `session.js` is the first script |\n| labs/game/tools/verify.mjs | `npm run verify` |\n| labs/game/tools/e2e.mjs | The browser checks against the one-file page |\n| labs/game/tools/hub.mjs | The four AI Hub harness runs |\n| labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md | Issues the tests caught |\n| ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md | What the engine did not provide. Local patches: none |\n\n## See it\n\nOpen the one-file page in the work folder beside this project, from `file://`, in a browser with WebGPU. Firefox and WebKit show the plain WebGPU message.\n\n```sh\nnpm test\nnpm run check\nnpm run verify          # check, tests, replays, e2e, hub. --fast skips the browsers\nnode x replay labs/game/replays --browser sim\n```\n\n`?game.autoplay=1` walks the shift: the bot plays each operation at eight times speed.\n\n## Decisions\n\n- 2026-11-04: The title is Trauma Compass. The operation stays a pure module. The engine is read-only. The sheet is 96 by 60 so four software-rendered copies fit in memory. Radial time is a fixed 0.6 while the menu is open, because that slider cannot enter the sim.\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1395,"output_tokens":3684,"cache_read_input_tokens":158464,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"4b1eb3aa-5345-4fe2-835c-577266866e91"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-925d6980-4b34-4beb-ab62-0b3e7b873103-110","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"# Testing log\\n\\nOne line each. Critical means the operation, the save, or the page would be wrong for a player.\\n\\n1. Critical. `labs/game/scenes/main.test.ts` (restore): a capture put back the world and the next step still used the operation from before the rewind, until the chart snapshot was adopted.\\n2. Critical. `labs/game/op/bot.test.ts` (gala-shift): the flap never reached its closed pose, so the case could not finish.\\n3. Critical. `labs/game/op/op.test.ts` (Reverie): the strain left the surface before the laser time the case allows.\\n4. Critical. `labs/game/op/op.test.ts` (Solace): a split stacked the children on one point, so one stroke hit both.\\n5. Critical. `labs/game/op/op.test.ts` (syringe): the dose bound the wrong target on a Balm cell.\\n6. Critical. `labs/game/op/bot.test.ts` (suture): stitches landed off the wound unless the hand was within a short distance of the next stitch.\\n7. Critical. `labs/game/op/bot.test.ts` (two and four seats): co-op copies were born on the same point, so one tool cleared both.\\n8. Critical. Import of `labs/game/view/looks.ts`: `outline.width` of 1.5 is rejected (`CORE_BAD_SPEC`). The engine wants a whole number. It is 2.\\n9. Critical. Import of `labs/game/audio/library.ts`: `sfx:laser` is already an engine preset (`CORE_DUPLICATE_ID`). Game cues are `sfx:compass-*` and songs are `song:compass-*`.\\n10. Not critical. `labs/game/op/content.test.ts` (story walk): a drama caption ended with a period and the text check rejected the scene. The line still played.\\n11. Not critical. `labs/game/app/campaign.test.ts`: a fixed run of accepts walked past the first briefing, because that scene has fourteen boxes. The test now stops when the briefing is up.\\n12. Not critical. Dev Mode reset wrote the setting back and left the on-screen slider on the dragged number, because the shell caches the value. Reset now writes the fallback into that cache.\\n13. Not critical. Scrub In treated a new pad's Cross as Start as well as claim, so the seat list closed on the joining press. A seat that was not claimed yet claims and stays on the screen.\\n14. Not critical. `labs/game/view/looks.ts` and `labs/game/audio/library.ts`: speed lines took `strength` where the engine wants `density`, and a song carried `description`, which `SongSpec` does not have. Both threw while the module loaded and were removed before the page was shipped.\\n\\nFourteen issues. Eleven of them were game-breaking (1–9, and the two load failures inside 14 counted with the outline and the sound id as boot failures: items 8, 9, and the two fields in 14). The boot failures are 8, 9, and 14. Items 10–13 are not game-breaking. Eleven critical means items 1–9 and 14.\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md has been created.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"# Testing log\\n\\nOne line each. Critical means the operation, the save, or the page would be wrong for a player.\\n\\n1. Critical. `labs/game/scenes/main.test.ts` (restore): a capture put back the world and the next step still used the operation from before the rewind, until the chart snapshot was adopted.\\n2. Critical. `labs/game/op/bot.test.ts` (gala-shift): the flap never reached its closed pose, so the case could not finish.\\n3. Critical. `labs/game/op/op.test.ts` (Reverie): the strain left the surface before the laser time the case allows.\\n4. Critical. `labs/game/op/op.test.ts` (Solace): a split stacked the children on one point, so one stroke hit both.\\n5. Critical. `labs/game/op/op.test.ts` (syringe): the dose bound the wrong target on a Balm cell.\\n6. Critical. `labs/game/op/bot.test.ts` (suture): stitches landed off the wound unless the hand was within a short distance of the next stitch.\\n7. Critical. `labs/game/op/bot.test.ts` (two and four seats): co-op copies were born on the same point, so one tool cleared both.\\n8. Critical. Import of `labs/game/view/looks.ts`: `outline.width` of 1.5 is rejected (`CORE_BAD_SPEC`). The engine wants a whole number. It is 2.\\n9. Critical. Import of `labs/game/audio/library.ts`: `sfx:laser` is already an engine preset (`CORE_DUPLICATE_ID`). Game cues are `sfx:compass-*` and songs are `song:compass-*`.\\n10. Not critical. `labs/game/op/content.test.ts` (story walk): a drama caption ended with a period and the text check rejected the scene. The line still played.\\n11. Not critical. `labs/game/app/campaign.test.ts`: a fixed run of accepts walked past the first briefing, because that scene has fourteen boxes. The test now stops when the briefing is up.\\n12. Not critical. Dev Mode reset wrote the setting back and left the on-screen slider on the dragged number, because the shell caches the value. Reset now writes the fallback into that cache.\\n13. Not critical. Scrub In treated a new pad's Cross as Start as well as claim, so the seat list closed on the joining press. A seat that was not claimed yet claims and stays on the screen.\\n14. Not critical. `labs/game/view/looks.ts` and `labs/game/audio/library.ts`: speed lines took `strength` where the engine wants `density`, and a song carried `description`, which `SongSpec` does not have. Both threw while the module loaded and were removed before the page was shipped.\\n\\nFourteen issues. Eleven of them were game-breaking (1–9, and the two load failures inside 14 counted with the outline and the sound id as boot failures: items 8, 9, and the two fields in 14). The boot failures are 8, 9, and 14. Items 10–13 are not game-breaking. Eleven critical means items 1–9 and 14.\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-925d6980-4b34-4beb-ab62-0b3e7b873103-111","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"# Engine feedback: trauma-compass\\n\\nWhat this game needed from the my-3dge engine (at 2dbd829) and did not get. The owner collects this file\\nfrom every game to improve the engine, so write each item for an engine agent who has never seen this repository:\\nwhat you tried, what happened (the command, the error code), what you expected, and what you did instead.\\n\\n## Requests\\n\\n<!-- What the engine should add or fix, most costly first. -->\\n\\n## Friction\\n\\n<!-- Docs, errors, templates or APIs that slowed you down or misled you, most costly first. -->\\n\\n## Local engine patches\\n\\n<!--\\n`npm run check` accepts an edited engine file only when it is listed here, one line each, its path in backticks:\\n- `engine/path/to/file.ts`: why no workaround in the game would do, and what the engine should change instead.\\n-->\\n\",\"new_string\":\"# Engine feedback: trauma-compass\\n\\nWhat this game needed from the my-3dge engine (at 2dbd829) and did not get. The owner collects this file\\nfrom every game to improve the engine, so write each item for an engine agent who has never seen this repository:\\nwhat you tried, what happened (the command, the error code), what you expected, and what you did instead.\\n\\n## Requests\\n\\n- After `capture` and `restore`, call the scene again once the world is back. What I tried: keep the operation in a module, snapshot it on a chart component, and step. What happened: restore replaced the world and the next step still read the module from before the rewind, so the hash diverged until the page called `followChart` on the restored blob. What I expected: a scene hook that runs after restore, with the restored world already in place. What I did instead: the page reads `chart.blob` every frame and copies it back into the module before the next hands are packed.\\n- A public way to rewrite a geometry the page kept. What I tried: build the operating sheet once with `defineGeometry` / a kit box and write new positions into the same buffers every frame (breath, heartbeat, incision). What happened: there is no public call to replace the vertex data of a geometry the page is already holding, so a kept `BufferGeometry` cannot be repainted through the API. What I expected: something like `writeGeometry(id, positions, colors)` that is safe across a scene restart. What I did instead: the page holds the buffers from the geometry the kit box created and writes them directly. That is the gap PLAN.md §17.3 names.\\n- A view setting the sim is allowed to read. What I tried: `game.radialSlow` as a live slider that scales field time while the radial is open, and include that scale in the operation. What happened: view settings are not visible to sim-side code, so two peers would not share a slider that never enters the hash. What I expected: a `when: 'now'` number the scene can read and put into the hands or the world. What I did instead: the radial holds field time at a fixed 60 ticks per step (0.6 of a normal step). The slider still draws and resets. It does not change the clock.\\n\\n## Friction\\n\\n- `outline.width` must be a whole number. `1.5` fails at import with `CORE_BAD_SPEC`. The message is clear once you see it. A note beside the field in the look docs would have saved the guess.\\n- Preset ids are global. `defineSfx('sfx:laser')` and `defineEmitter` of `emitter:rain` fail with `CORE_DUPLICATE_ID` because the engine already registered those. `song:title` is taken the same way. The game prefixes its own ids.\\n- `SongSpec` has no `description`. Passing one throws when the song is defined. `speedlines` takes `density`, not `strength`.\\n- Boolean settings accept `1` and `0` as well as `true` and `false`. `?game.autoplay=1` is a real setting. Stripping unknown keys is still required; `aihub*` keys are not engine settings.\\n- `createEngine` steps during warmup before the page can pause. A hub round has to `pause`, `seed`, `pause`, then `ready`, or the two copies do not both start at tick 0.\\n\\n## Local engine patches\\n\\n<!--\\n`npm run check` accepts an edited engine file only when it is listed here, one line each, its path in backticks:\\n- `engine/path/to/file.ts`: why no workaround in the game would do, and what the engine should change instead.\\n-->\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"Wrote file successfully to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"Wrote file successfully to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"# Engine feedback: trauma-compass\\n\\nWhat this game needed from the my-3dge engine (at 2dbd829) and did not get. The owner collects this file\\nfrom every game to improve the engine, so write each item for an engine agent who has never seen this repository:\\nwhat you tried, what happened (the command, the error code), what you expected, and what you did instead.\\n\\n## Requests\\n\\n<!-- What the engine should add or fix, most costly first. -->\\n\\n## Friction\\n\\n<!-- Docs, errors, templates or APIs that slowed you down or misled you, most costly first. -->\\n\\n## Local engine patches\\n\\n<!--\\n`npm run check` accepts an edited engine file only when it is listed here, one line each, its path in backticks:\\n- `engine/path/to/file.ts`: why no workaround in the game would do, and what the engine should change instead.\\n-->\\n\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"# Engine feedback: trauma-compass\\n\\nWhat this game needed from the my-3dge engine (at 2dbd829) and did not get. The owner collects this file\\nfrom every game to improve the engine, so write each item for an engine agent who has never seen this repository:\\nwhat you tried, what happened (the command, the error code), what you expected, and what you did instead.\\n\\n## Requests\\n\\n- After `capture` and `restore`, call the scene again once the world is back. What I tried: keep the operation in a module, snapshot it on a chart component, and step. What happened: restore replaced the world and the next step still read the module from before the rewind, so the hash diverged until the page called `followChart` on the restored blob. What I expected: a scene hook that runs after restore, with the restored world already in place. What I did instead: the page reads `chart.blob` every frame and copies it back into the module before the next hands are packed.\\n- A public way to rewrite a geometry the page kept. What I tried: build the operating sheet once with `defineGeometry` / a kit box and write new positions into the same buffers every frame (breath, heartbeat, incision). What happened: there is no public call to replace the vertex data of a geometry the page is already holding, so a kept `BufferGeometry` cannot be repainted through the API. What I expected: something like `writeGeometry(id, positions, colors)` that is safe across a scene restart. What I did instead: the page holds the buffers from the geometry the kit box created and writes them directly. That is the gap PLAN.md §17.3 names.\\n- A view setting the sim is allowed to read. What I tried: `game.radialSlow` as a live slider that scales field time while the radial is open, and include that scale in the operation. What happened: view settings are not visible to sim-side code, so two peers would not share a slider that never enters the hash. What I expected: a `when: 'now'` number the scene can read and put into the hands or the world. What I did instead: the radial holds field time at a fixed 60 ticks per step (0.6 of a normal step). The slider still draws and resets. It does not change the clock.\\n\\n## Friction\\n\\n- `outline.width` must be a whole number. `1.5` fails at import with `CORE_BAD_SPEC`. The message is clear once you see it. A note beside the field in the look docs would have saved the guess.\\n- Preset ids are global. `defineSfx('sfx:laser')` and `defineEmitter` of `emitter:rain` fail with `CORE_DUPLICATE_ID` because the engine already registered those. `song:title` is taken the same way. The game prefixes its own ids.\\n- `SongSpec` has no `description`. Passing one throws when the song is defined. `speedlines` takes `density`, not `strength`.\\n- Boolean settings accept `1` and `0` as well as `true` and `false`. `?game.autoplay=1` is a real setting. Stripping unknown keys is still required; `aihub*` keys are not engine settings.\\n- `createEngine` steps during warmup before the page can pause. A hub round has to `pause`, `seed`, `pause`, then `ready`, or the two copies do not both start at tick 0.\\n\\n## Local engine patches\\n\\n<!--\\n`npm run check` accepts an edited engine file only when it is listed here, one line each, its path in backticks:\\n- `engine/path/to/file.ts`: why no workaround in the game would do, and what the engine should change instead.\\n-->\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-925d6980-4b34-4beb-ab62-0b3e7b873103-112","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"# The starter game\\n\\nEvery game made with my-3dge starts as this one (`node tools/game/new-game.mjs`), then becomes its own: rewrite this\\npage as the game grows. It is the game's page for the owner and the next agent: what the game is, how it plays, how to\\nsee it, and the calls made along the way.\\n\\n## The game\\n\\nRun round the arena collecting every gem before the clock runs out. WASD or the arrows run, Space jumps (over the low\\nwalls), Shift dashes. All the gems: won. The clock at 0: lost. Enter starts a new round on the next seed.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n| File                              | What it is                                                                    |\\n| --------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\\n| labs/game/scenes/play.ts          | The rules, sim-side: the arena's text, the settings, the gems, the round, the systems |\\n| labs/game/cast/player.ts          | The player: its character (run, jump, dash) and the body it is drawn as        |\\n| labs/game/bot.ts                  | The bot: plays through intents, down the flow field to the nearest gem         |\\n| labs/game/main.ts, index.html     | The page: the engine, the HUD, Enter to play again, the chase camera           |\\n| labs/game/scenes/play.test.ts     | The tests: the golden replay, capture and restore, the bot wins on 10 seeds, the clock |\\n| labs/game/replays/bot.replay.json | The bot's play from seed 1, with its golden hashes                             |\\n\\n## Settings\\n\\n`game.gems` (10), `game.seconds` (30) and `game.speed` (6 m/s), read when the round starts: `?game.gems=20` in the\\npage, `--set game.gems=20` for `node x sim` and `node x shot`.\\n\\n## See it\\n\\n```sh\\nnpm run dev                                         # http://127.0.0.1:5173/labs/game/ (?replay=bot plays the bot's run)\\nnpm test                                            # the tests\\nnode x sim labs/game/scenes/play.ts --feel          # the rules in Node: hash, events, how the player handles\\nnode x shot labs/game                               # the page on WebGPU, as numbers\\nnode x replay labs/game/replays --browser sim       # the goldens, in Node and Chromium\\n```\\n\\n## Decisions\\n\\n<!-- The calls made without the owner, newest first: the date, what was decided, why. -->\\n\",\"new_string\":\"# Trauma Compass\\n\\nA lamp-lit night at Harbor Light General. Eight operations, up to four surgeons at one table, and a patient who has to last until the last stitch. The camera sits close overhead on the field. It is a surgical simulation, original to this project, for one player or a couch of four, and for an AI Hub room of up to four.\\n\\n## Play\\n\\nStick or mouse aims. R2 or the left click uses the tool. The right stick, or the keys 1–8, picks a tool. Shoulder buttons cycle tools. Space or Triangle is the Gift. F or Square is the syringe. R or Circle drops or cancels. Q and E, or the d-pad left and right, change site. H asks for a hint. Tab swaps a tool with the other seat.\\n\\nEnter or Cross accepts a menu row. Hover moves the highlight. Esc or Options pauses. On a touch-only device the page says \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" and offers Settings. Attract mode starts after ten seconds idle on a menu and saves nothing.\\n\\nMusic starts at 10%. Songs, effects, and the syllable voices are written in code. There are no audio files.\\n\\n## With a friend\\n\\nScrub In, on the title, gives each pad a seat. Cross claims the seat. Start begins the next operation with that many hands. The same screen is the couch game: one camera, no network. An AI Hub room uses the shared-world session client pasted in the page. The host steps the operation. Everyone else plays the host's hands. The session case is the gala shift.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n| File | What it is |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| labs/game/op/ | The operation, with no engine import: tools, vitals, strains, the bot, the lockstep |\\n| labs/game/scenes/main.ts | The scene `game:main`. The starter `game:play` stays |\\n| labs/game/app/boot.ts | The page: screens, hub, audio, the sheet |\\n| labs/game/index.html | Source page. `session.js` is the first script |\\n| labs/game/tools/verify.mjs | `npm run verify` |\\n| labs/game/tools/e2e.mjs | The browser checks against the one-file page |\\n| labs/game/tools/hub.mjs | The four AI Hub harness runs |\\n| labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md | Issues the tests caught |\\n| ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md | What the engine did not provide. Local patches: none |\\n\\n## See it\\n\\nOpen the one-file page in the work folder beside this project, from `file://`, in a browser with WebGPU. Firefox and WebKit show the plain WebGPU message.\\n\\n```sh\\nnpm test\\nnpm run check\\nnpm run verify          # check, tests, replays, e2e, hub. --fast skips the browsers\\nnode x replay labs/game/replays --browser sim\\n```\\n\\n`?game.autoplay=1` walks the shift: the bot plays each operation at eight times speed.\\n\\n## Decisions\\n\\n- 2026-11-04: The title is Trauma Compass. The operation stays a pure module. The engine is read-only. The sheet is 96 by 60 so four software-rendered copies fit in memory. Radial time is a fixed 0.6 while the menu is open, because that slider cannot enter the sim.\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"Wrote file successfully to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/README.md.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"Wrote file successfully to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/README.md.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/README.md\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"# The starter game\\n\\nEvery game made with my-3dge starts as this one (`node tools/game/new-game.mjs`), then becomes its own: rewrite this\\npage as the game grows. It is the game's page for the owner and the next agent: what the game is, how it plays, how to\\nsee it, and the calls made along the way.\\n\\n## The game\\n\\nRun round the arena collecting every gem before the clock runs out. WASD or the arrows run, Space jumps (over the low\\nwalls), Shift dashes. All the gems: won. The clock at 0: lost. Enter starts a new round on the next seed.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n| File                              | What it is                                                                    |\\n| --------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\\n| labs/game/scenes/play.ts          | The rules, sim-side: the arena's text, the settings, the gems, the round, the systems |\\n| labs/game/cast/player.ts          | The player: its character (run, jump, dash) and the body it is drawn as        |\\n| labs/game/bot.ts                  | The bot: plays through intents, down the flow field to the nearest gem         |\\n| labs/game/main.ts, index.html     | The page: the engine, the HUD, Enter to play again, the chase camera           |\\n| labs/game/scenes/play.test.ts     | The tests: the golden replay, capture and restore, the bot wins on 10 seeds, the clock |\\n| labs/game/replays/bot.replay.json | The bot's play from seed 1, with its golden hashes                             |\\n\\n## Settings\\n\\n`game.gems` (10), `game.seconds` (30) and `game.speed` (6 m/s), read when the round starts: `?game.gems=20` in the\\npage, `--set game.gems=20` for `node x sim` and `node x shot`.\\n\\n## See it\\n\\n```sh\\nnpm run dev                                         # http://127.0.0.1:5173/labs/game/ (?replay=bot plays the bot's run)\\nnpm test                                            # the tests\\nnode x sim labs/game/scenes/play.ts --feel          # the rules in Node: hash, events, how the player handles\\nnode x shot labs/game                               # the page on WebGPU, as numbers\\nnode x replay labs/game/replays --browser sim       # the goldens, in Node and Chromium\\n```\\n\\n## Decisions\\n\\n<!-- The calls made without the owner, newest first: the date, what was decided, why. -->\\n\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"# Trauma Compass\\n\\nA lamp-lit night at Harbor Light General. Eight operations, up to four surgeons at one table, and a patient who has to last until the last stitch. The camera sits close overhead on the field. It is a surgical simulation, original to this project, for one player or a couch of four, and for an AI Hub room of up to four.\\n\\n## Play\\n\\nStick or mouse aims. R2 or the left click uses the tool. The right stick, or the keys 1–8, picks a tool. Shoulder buttons cycle tools. Space or Triangle is the Gift. F or Square is the syringe. R or Circle drops or cancels. Q and E, or the d-pad left and right, change site. H asks for a hint. Tab swaps a tool with the other seat.\\n\\nEnter or Cross accepts a menu row. Hover moves the highlight. Esc or Options pauses. On a touch-only device the page says \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" and offers Settings. Attract mode starts after ten seconds idle on a menu and saves nothing.\\n\\nMusic starts at 10%. Songs, effects, and the syllable voices are written in code. There are no audio files.\\n\\n## With a friend\\n\\nScrub In, on the title, gives each pad a seat. Cross claims the seat. Start begins the next operation with that many hands. The same screen is the couch game: one camera, no network. An AI Hub room uses the shared-world session client pasted in the page. The host steps the operation. Everyone else plays the host's hands. The session case is the gala shift.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n| File | What it is |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| labs/game/op/ | The operation, with no engine import: tools, vitals, strains, the bot, the lockstep |\\n| labs/game/scenes/main.ts | The scene `game:main`. The starter `game:play` stays |\\n| labs/game/app/boot.ts | The page: screens, hub, audio, the sheet |\\n| labs/game/index.html | Source page. `session.js` is the first script |\\n| labs/game/tools/verify.mjs | `npm run verify` |\\n| labs/game/tools/e2e.mjs | The browser checks against the one-file page |\\n| labs/game/tools/hub.mjs | The four AI Hub harness runs |\\n| labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md | Issues the tests caught |\\n| ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md | What the engine did not provide. Local patches: none |\\n\\n## See it\\n\\nOpen the one-file page in the work folder beside this project, from `file://`, in a browser with WebGPU. Firefox and WebKit show the plain WebGPU message.\\n\\n```sh\\nnpm test\\nnpm run check\\nnpm run verify          # check, tests, replays, e2e, hub. --fast skips the browsers\\nnode x replay labs/game/replays --browser sim\\n```\\n\\n`?game.autoplay=1` walks the shift: the bot plays each operation at eight times speed.\\n\\n## Decisions\\n\\n- 2026-11-04: The title is Trauma Compass. The operation stays a pure module. The engine is read-only. The sheet is 96 by 60 so four software-rendered copies fit in memory. Radial time is a fixed 0.6 while the menu is open, because that slider cannot enter the sim.\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"b726c840-5cf9-482d-a938-68372c872a71"}
