{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_449","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Idle values remained at zero for roughly ten seconds before climbing to 33, then 2200, and finally 4216.\n\nIdle resets for the first ten seconds. It then accumulates at real time. The attract sequence starts about twenty seconds after the reset stops. The test timeout is fifteen seconds. So the test fails. The reset likely comes from engine warmup or input during startup.\n\nPointer events during page load are unlikely. The probe shows zero pads and no keydown. The engine may synthesize input during warmup. The inspector might also be involved.\n\nA synthetic pointerover event is unlikely to blame. It sets focus without resetting idle. The first five samples are exactly zero, so the reset is active every frame rather than a paused timer. After that, idle rises by roughly two seconds per two seconds. Either the delta time finally starts flowing or the reset stops.\n\nThe reset stops at about twelve seconds. Idle then accumulates at the correct rate. The attract sequence needs ten more seconds, so it starts roughly twenty-two seconds after the test begins. The pause key may be held during engine key binding.\n\ncreateInput might fire a fake event. aimMouse may not reset idle. A stuck Escape key could keep uiCancel pressed every frame. That would freeze the title screen and idle at zero.\n\nA stuck Escape key is unlikely. The probe does not show focus changes, so a stuck uiUp or uiDown would only cycle focus without leaving the title screen. The engine's gamepad deadzone or keyboard repeat might be the culprit. Browser pointermove events at startup do not call noteInput. Adding logging to the probe requires changing the page.\n\nI can inspect the engine input API to see which keys are actually pressed. If focus stays at zero while idle remains frozen, the reset is coming from noteInput or a stuck key rather than dt. The later growth proves delta time works; the early resets are the real problem. Since the title screen never changes, accept is not firing.\n\nPointerdown and keydown events would have to fire every frame for twelve seconds, which is unlikely unless the engine or page dispatches them. The pads.any check is also unlikely because the probe shows no active gamepads. I am now examining the menus code order and that specific condition.\n\nThe keydown and pointerdown listeners only call noteInput during the attract screen. On the title screen, the only path to noteInput is the pads.any check. Move, browse, accept, and cancel also reset idle.\n\nThe draw loop returns early while warming is true. onFrame never runs during engine warmup, so idle cannot accumulate until the warmup ends.\n\nThe compass object is initialized with campaign.screen before createEngine runs, so the title screen is already set. The probe therefore sees the title screen immediately, even though onFrame has not yet executed and idle cannot accumulate during warmup.\n\nThe test timeout is too short. Engine warmup takes roughly twelve seconds, and attract needs ten more seconds of idle time, so the total wait exceeds the current fifteen-second limit. The fix is to increase the timeout to thirty or forty seconds. This is a test timing issue rather than a game bug.\n\nThe test should wait for the attract screen rather than the title screen. A forty-second timeout covers engine warmup, idle accumulation, and the attract sequence.\n\ncreateEngine awaits warmCameras and settle before returning, so the loop is already running when start() finishes. The initial drawShell() happens after that return, meaning the attract message appears while frames are active. The first wait should use forty seconds, but the later waits can remain at fifteen.\n\nThe e2e story test waits for engine.ready before checking the title screen. The attract test only waits for screen === title, which is true before the engine is ready. This means the attract test begins its timer while the engine is still warming up.\n\nThe fix is to wait for `__engine.ready` before checking the title screen. Once the engine is ready, idle starts from zero and attract should appear within fifteen seconds. The attract and touch tests will be updated to wait for `__engine.ready` first.\n\nThe touch test waits for the touch message, which only appears after createEngine finishes. This means the message is not present before the engine is ready. The existing fifteen-second wait for attract should therefore be sufficient.\n\nThe idle probe script will be deleted. The TESTING-LOG paragraph will be cleaned up during the interview update.\n\nItem 14 is critical. The speedlines and song modules throw import errors that prevent the page from booting, so they are critical failures rather than non-critical items.\n\nThe TESTING-LOG.md tally is fourteen issues total. Ten are critical and four are not critical. The ten critical items are the seven operation faults, the outline width the engine rejects, the sound id the engine already owns, and the look plus song that use fields the engine does not have.\n\nItem 14 is one critical issue covering two fields. The interview will be updated to match the corrected tally, and the log's last paragraph will be cleaned up to remove its self-contradiction. The attract fix only changes the test file, not the HTML, so rebuilding is unnecessary unless interview.ts is modified.\n\nI will run the current e2e test before rebuilding the interview HTML. Rebuilding during the run would not affect the already-loaded page, so I will update interview.ts first, rebuild, then rerun e2e to verify the final file.\n\nPROGRESS.md is still missing. I will write it as in progress and finish it after verify.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d72f94db-43fc-4da4-83b0-68bad09e51a8-132","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/tools/e2e.mjs","old_string":"  await page.goto(pageUrl);\n  await page.waitForFunction(() => window.__compass?.screen === 'title');\n  const before = await page.evaluate(() => JSON.stringify(localStorage));\n  await page.waitForFunction(() => window.__compass?.screen === 'attract', null, { timeout: 15000 });","new_string":"  await page.goto(pageUrl);\n  await page.waitForFunction(() => window.__engine?.ready && window.__compass?.screen === 'title');\n  const before = await page.evaluate(() => JSON.stringify(localStorage));\n  await page.waitForFunction(() => window.__compass?.screen === 'attract', null, { timeout: 20000 });"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d72f94db-43fc-4da4-83b0-68bad09e51a8-133","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/data/interview.ts","old_string":"    'Twelve issues were caught by the operation tests and the scene restore test, and written in labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md.',\n    'Seven were game-breaking: a restore stepped the wrong body, the gala flap never finished, Reverie left the surface early, Solace children stacked, the syringe bound the wrong target, stitches landed off the wound, and co-op copies shared one point.',","new_string":"    'Fourteen issues were caught and written in labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md.',\n    'Ten were game-breaking: a restore stepped the wrong body, the gala flap never finished, Reverie left the surface early, Solace children stacked, the syringe bound the wrong target, stitches landed off the wound, co-op copies shared one point, an outline width the engine rejects, a sound id the engine already owns, and a look and a song that used fields the engine does not have.',"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d72f94db-43fc-4da4-83b0-68bad09e51a8-134","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/exit-interview.json","old_string":"    \"Twelve issues were caught by the operation tests and the scene restore test, and written in labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md.\",\n    \"Seven were game-breaking: a restore stepped the wrong body, the gala flap never finished, Reverie left the surface early, Solace children stacked, the syringe bound the wrong target, stitches landed off the wound, and co-op copies shared one point.\",","new_string":"    \"Fourteen issues were caught and written in labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md.\",\n    \"Ten were game-breaking: a restore stepped the wrong body, the gala flap never finished, Reverie left the surface early, Solace children stacked, the syringe bound the wrong target, stitches landed off the wound, co-op copies shared one point, an outline width the engine rejects, a sound id the engine already owns, and a look and a song that used fields the engine does not have.\","}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d72f94db-43fc-4da4-83b0-68bad09e51a8-135","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md","old_string":"14. Not critical. `labs/game/view/looks.ts` and `labs/game/audio/library.ts`: speed lines took `strength` where the engine wants `density`, and a song carried `description`, which `SongSpec` does not have. Both threw while the module loaded and were removed before the page was shipped.\n\nFourteen issues. Eleven of them were game-breaking (1–9, and the two load failures inside 14 counted with the outline and the sound id as boot failures: items 8, 9, and the two fields in 14). The boot failures are 8, 9, and 14. Items 10–13 are not game-breaking. Eleven critical means items 1–9 and 14.","new_string":"14. Critical. `labs/game/view/looks.ts` and `labs/game/audio/library.ts`: speed lines took `strength` where the engine wants `density`, and a song carried `description`, which `SongSpec` does not have. Both threw while the module loaded.\n\nFourteen issues. Ten were game-breaking: 1–9 and 14. Four were not: 10–13."}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":432,"output_tokens":4678,"cache_read_input_tokens":175872,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"084c87d0-6392-477c-b55b-5696936d7aaa"}
