{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_453","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Preparing PROGRESS.md and reviewing the hub to fix issues quickly.\n\nChecking hub protocol requirements for progress reports. The shared-world harness checks look correct: bidirectional traffic, round-end notifications, and proper finish handling. One potential issue: ready() might be called after __engine.step, though createEngine sets the engine before start().\n\nThe wait loop resolves immediately before seeding and ready(). Card mode is handled correctly: the client connects with card:true, menus answer Enter when session.card is truthy, and the harness still pokes Enter if caps.card is true.\n\nA potential race condition was found in the card menu. If session.card is null, the Enter key on the 'op' screen returns early and does not answer the card. The card handler sets session.card before the op check, so this only fails if the event never fires.\n\nHost and client traffic are synchronized: both require the round to have started before sending messages. The server copy hides its canvas, which may cause WebGPU failures. I still need to verify the exact finish body shape the harness expects.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b7cbbf84-cb83-4262-bb2f-5b71d2f8909a-140","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function finish|standings|protocol|time-up|progress","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/vendor/session.js","head_limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":655,"output_tokens":740,"cache_read_input_tokens":183680,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"45ca0b1f-a4c8-45d7-8892-61610b9294f6"}
