{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_457","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The finish payload looks correct. Waiting for end-to-end results.\n\nDrafting PROGRESS.md in the work folder. Will update the goal plan.md checkboxes rather than rewrite items. Checking e2e logs for early progress.\n\nThe testing log item 14 covers two faults, which counts as one issue toward the ten game-breaking limit. PROGRESS.md will be written now and updated when verification finishes.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d341f1eb-0c05-447b-af40-24750a0c71a1-144","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/PROGRESS.md","content":"# Trauma Compass\n\nSurgical simulation at Harbor Light General. The one-file page is `Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731.html` beside this note. The dev project is the folder of the same name.\n\n## Done\n\n- Title chosen with a real RNG: Trauma Compass.\n- Operation sim, bot, strains, campaign, and lockstep tests are green, including the bot on every required case and seed.\n- The page boots from `file://` in Chromium with WebGPU. Session client is the first script and matches the vendor file. Usage reads `added on import`.\n- Couch seats, dev sliders, attract, glyphs, and the hub metas are in the page.\n- `exit-interview.json` matches the About cards. `labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md` has fourteen issues, ten of them game-breaking. `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md` asks for a post-restore scene hook and a public way to rewrite a kept mesh. No engine files were patched.\n\n## Still running\n\n- Browser e2e against the one-file page, then the four AI Hub harness runs, then `npm run verify`.\n\n## Deviations\n\n- The sheet is 96 by 60, not 320 by 192. Four software-rendered copies of the denser grid were killed for memory.\n- Radial slow is fixed at 0.6 in the sim. The view slider cannot be read from the operation, so it does not enter the hash.\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":445,"output_tokens":649,"cache_read_input_tokens":186496,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"6c8767b4-d30d-4455-9a1d-f42e4a16c290"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-d341f1eb-0c05-447b-af40-24750a0c71a1-144","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"# Trauma Compass\\n\\nSurgical simulation at Harbor Light General. The one-file page is `Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731.html` beside this note. The dev project is the folder of the same name.\\n\\n## Done\\n\\n- Title chosen with a real RNG: Trauma Compass.\\n- Operation sim, bot, strains, campaign, and lockstep tests are green, including the bot on every required case and seed.\\n- The page boots from `file://` in Chromium with WebGPU. Session client is the first script and matches the vendor file. Usage reads `added on import`.\\n- Couch seats, dev sliders, attract, glyphs, and the hub metas are in the page.\\n- `exit-interview.json` matches the About cards. `labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md` has fourteen issues, ten of them game-breaking. `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md` asks for a post-restore scene hook and a public way to rewrite a kept mesh. No engine files were patched.\\n\\n## Still running\\n\\n- Browser e2e against the one-file page, then the four AI Hub harness runs, then `npm run verify`.\\n\\n## Deviations\\n\\n- The sheet is 96 by 60, not 320 by 192. Four software-rendered copies of the denser grid were killed for memory.\\n- Radial slow is fixed at 0.6 in the sim. The view slider cannot be read from the operation, so it does not enter the hash.\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/PROGRESS.md has been created.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/PROGRESS.md has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/PROGRESS.md\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"# Trauma Compass\\n\\nSurgical simulation at Harbor Light General. The one-file page is `Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731.html` beside this note. The dev project is the folder of the same name.\\n\\n## Done\\n\\n- Title chosen with a real RNG: Trauma Compass.\\n- Operation sim, bot, strains, campaign, and lockstep tests are green, including the bot on every required case and seed.\\n- The page boots from `file://` in Chromium with WebGPU. Session client is the first script and matches the vendor file. Usage reads `added on import`.\\n- Couch seats, dev sliders, attract, glyphs, and the hub metas are in the page.\\n- `exit-interview.json` matches the About cards. `labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md` has fourteen issues, ten of them game-breaking. `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md` asks for a post-restore scene hook and a public way to rewrite a kept mesh. No engine files were patched.\\n\\n## Still running\\n\\n- Browser e2e against the one-file page, then the four AI Hub harness runs, then `npm run verify`.\\n\\n## Deviations\\n\\n- The sheet is 96 by 60, not 320 by 192. Four software-rendered copies of the denser grid were killed for memory.\\n- Radial slow is fixed at 0.6 in the sim. The view slider cannot be read from the operation, so it does not enter the hash.\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"97dc7bdc-fcc6-4681-b079-718c9baddfb4"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_458","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I will not sit idle if useful work is available.\n\nI will review hub.mjs for cpExists and server port. I will re-read the game's hub boot to catch bugs before running the hub.\n\nThe first e2e campaign timed out. The script threw an uncaught error before browser.close() ran, so the browser may still be alive.\n\nThe first e2e's browser may be orphaned if Chrome was spawned detached. The shell removed its tmp directory, so the process might have died or lingered. The second e2e is now running; if the first browser is still alive, multiple browsers will be active.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-00c08cb2-c6a2-4349-8360-14b4262ba0c4-145","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"ps -u \"$(whoami)\" -o pid,etime,cmd | awk '/chrome-headless-shell / && /grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731/ && !/awk/ {print}'","description":"Find this run's leftover Chromium processes"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":766,"output_tokens":468,"cache_read_input_tokens":186880,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"fc14c1b8-6b8d-4b2c-8088-51fecabd0dc7"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-00c08cb2-c6a2-4349-8360-14b4262ba0c4-145","content":"{\"type\":\"Bash\",\"output\":[],\"output_for_prompt\":\"exit: 0\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"command\":\"ps -u \\\"$(whoami)\\\" -o pid,etime,cmd | awk '/chrome-headless-shell / && /grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731/ && !/awk/ {print}'\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Find this run's leftover Chromium processes\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3%2Fwork/01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151/terminal/call-00c08cb2-c6a2-4349-8360-14b4262ba0c4-145.log\",\"total_bytes\":0}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"63524c06-5709-4fc6-9169-19f468c313f6"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_459","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"No leftover chrome from the run remains.\n\nThe current e2e run is clean. I'll wait for the monitor notification rather than poll. I considered running npm run check in parallel, but that would compete with the heavy browser process and risk earlyoom.\n\nI reviewed the glyph and pad tests for failure risks. The pad test sequence looks correct. I am checking whether a pad button could be missed if it is already held down from a previous frame.\n\nThe pad test correctly detects the rising edge on the first frame. The latest build includes the joined fix, so the HTML is current. For the glyph test, ArrowDown should set lastDevice to keyboard before the mouse click.\n\nThe glyph test should see the mouse prompt after the canvas click. The 200ms wait should let the keyboard prompt update before the click. The Xbox test sequence is already covered. The dev slider is in an op after 20 enters.\n\nThe dev slider test fills the range input to 2 and dispatches the change event. The handler updates the label and the value is verified. Autoplay is disabled during the operation, so the Escape pause prevents the patient from dying or the clock from advancing while the slider is being adjusted.\n\nThe Escape pause is safe because the patient cannot die in a few hundred milliseconds. The engine stays paused while dev mode is active, so slider adjustments do not require the simulation to run.\n\nThe campaign test is the main risk. If the bot loses a case, the debrief menu retries automatically because retry is the first item and accept selects it.\n\nThe bot wins in node, so the same instance should succeed in the browser when autoplay is enabled. Eight cases at 8× speed finish in roughly three to six minutes, which is well under the 660-second timeout.\n\nAutoplay accept fires every frame. On the title screen it starts New Shift. During story it advances one box per frame; fourteen boxes take fourteen frames, then the brief and operation begin. When an operation wins, finishOp sets the debrief screen before accept moves to story. This ordering prevents a premature skip.\n\nThe bot should stay in sync with the scaled simulation because it runs inside each step. I will end this turn so the monitor can wake me when the test finishes.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The one-file page boots from `file://` with the title, the usage line, and a readable story. The first attract check timed out because the menu clock starts only after the engine is ready, so that wait now starts from ready.\n\nThe full browser pass is running again, through the shift and on to the credits. Hub harness and `npm run verify` follow when it finishes."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":607,"output_tokens":1422,"cache_read_input_tokens":187520,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"989012d9-91c0-4956-9dc9-b93291115fb3"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_460","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The e2e check failed for demo 1. The attract screen exits on click and saves nothing.\n\nThe demo element was found, so the failure is a localStorage change during the click. I am reviewing the test code to find the cause.\n\nThe test reached the title screen after the click. The localStorage change likely came from attract mode saving data, or from audio settings and engine store updates between snapshots.\n\nI am tracing the attract exit path in boot.ts. leaveAttract does not save to localStorage, but menus() might trigger a save when exiting attract mode.\n\nThe pointerdown handler exits attract without saving. The engine store is the likely culprit: running the attract scene may persist settings, best scores, or input bindings to localStorage.\n\nThe test detail only shows the demo count, not the actual localStorage difference. I need to search the code for saveProgress and any localStorage writes that occur during attract mode. The e2e script is still running in the background.\n\nI am weighing whether to let the running e2e finish or kill it before rebuilding. I am now checking if `finishOp` in the attract operation is writing to localStorage when the demo ends.\n\nfinishOp is ruled out because the attract screen is not 'op'. The engine store is the remaining suspect. I will inspect what createStore writes and what the attract scene does.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The demo starts and a click leaves it, but something is written to storage. I’ll find that write and stop it."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-61769f89-ff86-4c6d-b89c-968134c12565-146","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"saveProgress|localStorage|createStore","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game","glob":"**/*.{ts,