{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_463","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The mouse click reported the screen title instead of the hovered text \"The Board\".\n\nThe click handler updates campaign.screen immediately, but __compass.screen only refreshes at the end of onFrame. The test reads the compass value right after the click, before the frame update occurs, causing a race condition.\n\nThe story test waits for the screen to become 'story'. The mouse test should wait for 'board' instead. The timeout at line 134 is on the operation wait, not the Back click. Playwright throws if an element is missing, so Back was found. The click likely succeeded but the compass update lagged.\n\nThe 10-second timeout at line 134 is the operation wait, not the Back click. A missing Back button would trigger a 30-second default Playwright timeout instead. The Back click succeeded and Enter was pressed 21 times, but the operation never appeared.\n\nThe click likely reached the board screen. The compass object simply lagged behind. After Back returned to title, Enter accepted New Shift and 20 presses should have advanced through the story boxes to reach the operation.\n\nThe 20 Enter presses should reach the operation. The first press starts the story, 13 more advance through boxes 1 to 13, the 14th finishes the scene into the brief, and the 15th begins the operation. Accept is synchronous, so rapid presses should not be swallowed.\n\nThe 20 Enter presses may not be reaching the campaign state. The menus() function only accepts input.pressed events, not direct campaign calls. Keyboard Enter flows through the engine's input system, which might process one press per frame. If the engine is too slow to catch up, some presses could be missed.\n\nThe engine's input system is edge-triggered per frame. It only registers one accept event per keydown, so twenty rapid Enter presses in a few milliseconds collapse into one or two frames. That is too few to advance through fourteen story boxes, which explains why the operation never appeared.\n\nThe fix is to loop pressing Enter and waiting fifty milliseconds between each press, stopping once the screen reaches the operation. The board click should also wait for the board screen before asserting. I still need to check what the engine persists in localStorage during play.\n\nThe engine receives a prefixed play-mode store from the page. The attract scene may save best times or settings into it. I need to check how createEngine uses that store and whether audio writes to localStorage. The test compares the entire localStorage object.\n\nThe story test already wrote progress to localStorage in the same browser context. The attract test snapshots before and after the scene, so the delta is limited to attract-only changes. During attract, saveProgress is skipped because record is false while the screen is attract. Record only re-enables when the screen returns to title.\n\nThe pointerdown event leaves attract mode and sets the screen to title without saving progress. The subsequent click may hit a button or the canvas, and only a button with data-act triggers pick(), which saves state. The attract screen might contain buttons.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ce31a9bb-3772-4c8d-bc45-a897e908e8e0-155","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"options\\.store|store\\.set","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/app","glob":"**/*.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ce31a9bb-3772-4c8d-bc45-a897e908e8e0-156","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/best.ts","limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4565,"output_tokens":1747,"cache_read_input_tokens":195968,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"17cf72b0-5f4d-4907-8bd4-4a8f246c2308"}
