e('music', campaign.progress.music / 100);\\n    audio.volume('effects', campaign.progress.effects / 100);\\n    audio.update(frame.camera);\\n    const boxKey = campaign.screen === 'story' ? `${campaign.storyId}:${campaign.box}` : '';\\n    if (boxKey && boxKey !== spoken) {\\n      spoken = boxKey;\\n      const box = currentBox(campaign);\\n      if (box?.text) speak(audio, box.who, box.text, campaign.progress.voice / 100);\\n    }\\n    drawShell();\\n    const hashNode = shell.querySelector('[data-game=\\\"hash\\\"]');\\n    if (hashNode) hashNode.textContent = page?.hash() ?? '';\\n    const cursorNode = shell.querySelector('[data-game=\\\"cursor\\\"]');\\n    const spot = gloveSpots(1)[0];\\n    if (cursorNode && spot) cursorNode.textContent = `${spot.x.toFixed(2)}, ${spot.z.toFixed(2)}`;\\n    endSample();\\n    const found = enginePage.errors.some((error) => error.code === 'GFX_NO_WEBGPU');\\n    if (found && msg) {\\n      msg.hidden = false;\\n      msg.textContent = 'This game needs a browser with WebGPU.';\\n    }\\n    const view = (window as unknown as { __compass?: Compass }).__compass;\\n    if (view) {\\n      view.screen = campaign.screen;\\n      view.mismatches = session?.round?.mismatches ?? mismatches;\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  drawShell();\\n}\\n\\n/** What a test reads from the page. */\\nexport interface Compass {\\n  campaign: Campaign;\\n  screen: string;\\n  mismatches: string[];\\n  audio: ReturnType<typeof createAudio>;\\n  live: typeof liveOp;\\n\",\"total_lines\":563}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"61fa15e2-ef89-480c-b30e-692a22dcb151"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_470","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The governor writes once the attract scene's quality tier settles.\n\nOmitting store from createEngine prevents the governor from writing during the before snapshot. The write would otherwise occur during warmup before the attract scene's quality tier settles. This makes the before and after snapshots identical. The only remaining question is whether input rebinding persistence requires passing store.\n\nProgress persists through saveProgress, which uses localStorage independently of createEngine's store option. Action map rebinding is only needed if the game exposes it. I will omit the store argument from createEngine and add a comment explaining why.\n\nI considered logging the governor write as a friction issue in ENGINE-FEEDBACK, but that would require updating interview counts. The test already requires attract to save nothing, so this is a design choice rather than a new bug.\n\nThe governor writing to localStorage during attract is a real bug, not a test-script mistake. I will add it as issue 15 in TESTING-LOG and update the interview counts accordingly.\n\nA memory-only demo store would keep governor writes out of localStorage while still supporting session bindings. Patching the engine to prevent writes is not possible.\n\nThe e2e tests need three fixes. Attract detail should list changed keys when they differ. Mouse hover must wait for screen === 'board' after clicking before reading. Enter presses need delays until the operation completes. The mouse block also fails to wait for engine.ready, so clicks may occur during warmup when act() is not running.\n\nThe stale screen state occurs because __compass.screen updates at the end of onFrame, so the test must wait for the next frame. Shell buttons call act() directly rather than through onFrame, which is why campaign.screen becomes board immediately while __compass.screen lags behind.\n\nFor the Enter key sequence, the path from title to operation is New Shift → story → brief → op. The current test clicks Back from board to title, then presses Enter once followed by twenty more presses in a tight loop before waiting ten seconds for the operation.\n\nThe Enter key sequence requires sixteen presses to reach the operation screen: one to start the story, fourteen through its boxes, and one on the brief Start button. Twenty-one presses should suffice if they are paced per frame. However, uiAccept is edge-triggered once per frame, and Playwright's keyboard.press sends keydown and keyup immediately. If the game loop runs faster than sixty frames per second, multiple presses collapse into a single trigger.\n\nThe Enter key loop will be capped at forty presses. Each press is followed by a fifty millisecond pause until the screen reaches the operation state or story advances. The mouse page must also wait for engine ready before clicking to avoid warmup.\n\nI am checking whether the shell is visible during warmup. The summary says the screen is title before createEngine returns, but drawShell() runs after createEngine. If the shell is not yet drawn, clicks during warmup will fail.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e32fb63b-da09-48cd-8a0d-2d3f9edbf918-13","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"addEventListener\\('click'|drawShell|renderShell","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/app/boot.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e32fb63b-da09-48cd-8a0d-2d3f9edbf918-14","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md","offset":1,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e32fb63b-da09-48cd-8a0d-2d3f9edbf918-15","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"Fourteen issues|testingFeedback","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/data/interview.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e32fb63b-da09-48cd-8a0d-2d3f9edbf918-16","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/app/campaign.ts","offset":540,"limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4164,"output_tokens":1758,"cache_read_input_tokens":42624,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"7c89e261-b4f7-4cc3-a8dd-dac3e4d3f482"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-e32fb63b-da09-48cd-8a0d-2d3f9edbf918-13","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,55,51,49,95,95,120,53,57,99,49,100,51,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,54,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,55,51,49,95,95,120,53,57,99,49,100,51,47,119,111,114,107,47,84,114,97,117,109,97,45,67,111,109,112,97,115,115,45,84,114,97,117,109,97,45,67,101,110,116,101,114,45,83,101,99,111,110,100,45,79,112,105,110,105,111,110,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,55,51,49,47,108,97,98,115,47,103,97,109,101,47,97,112,112,47,98,111,111,116,46,116,115,10,50,48,58,105,109,112,111,114,116,32,123,32,114,101,110,100,101,114,83,104,101,108,108,44,32,115,104,101,108,108,83,116,97,109,112,44,32,116,121,112,101,32,83,104,101,108,108,69,120,116,114,97,32,125,32,102,114,111,109,32,39,46,46,47,117,105,47,115,104,101,108,108,39,59,10,50,52,52,58,32,32,99,111,110,115,116,32,100,114,97,119,83,104,101,108,108,32,61,32,40,41,58,32,118,111,105,100,32,61,62,32,123,10,50,52,56,58,32,32,32,32,114,101,110,100,101,114,83,104,101,108,108,40,115,104,101,108,108,44,32,99,97,109,112,97,105,103,110,44,32,101,120,116,114,97,40,41,41,59,10,50,54,55,58,32,32,115,104,101,108,108,46,97,100,100,69,118,101,110,116,76,105,115,116,101,110,101,114,40,39,99,108,105,99,107,39,44,32,40,101,118,101,110,116,41,32,61,62,32,123,10,53,51,49,58,32,32,32,32,100,114,97,119,83,104,101,108,108,40,41,59,10,53,53,48,58,32,32,100,114,97,119,83,104,101,108,108,40,41,59,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":6,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/app/boot.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":20,\"content\":\"import { renderShell, shellStamp, type ShellExtra } from '../ui/shell';\"},{\"line_number\":244,\"content\":\"  const drawShell = (): void => {\"},{\"line_number\":248,\"content\":\"    renderShell(shell, campaign, extra());\"},{\"line_number\":267,\"content\":\"  shell.addEventListener('click', (event) => {\"},{\"line_number\":531,\"content\":\"    drawShell();\"},{\"line_number\":550,\"content\":\"  drawShell();\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-e32fb63b-da09-48cd-8a0d-2d3f9edbf918-14","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→# Testing log\\n\\nOne line each. Critical means the operation, the save, or the page would be wrong for a player.\\n\\n1. Critical. `labs/game/scenes/main.test.ts` (restore): a capture put back the world and the next step still used the operation from before the rewind, until the chart snapshot was adopted.\\n2. Critical. `labs/game/op/bot.test.ts` (gala-shift): the flap never reached its closed pose, so the case could not finish.\\n3. Critical. `labs/game/op/op.test.ts` (Reverie): the strain left the surface before the laser time the case allows.\\n4. Critical. `labs/game/op/op.test.ts` (Solace): a split stacked the children on one point, so one stroke hit both.\\n5. Critical. `labs/game/op/op.test.ts` (syringe): the dose bound the wrong target on a Balm cell.\\n10→6. Critical. `labs/game/op/bot.test.ts` (suture): stitches landed off the wound unless the hand was within a short distance of the next stitch.\\n7. Critical. `labs/game/op/bot.test.ts` (two and four seats): co-op copies were born on the same point, so one tool cleared both.\\n8. Critical. Import of `labs/game/view/looks.ts`: `outline.width` of 1.5 is rejected (`CORE_BAD_SPEC`). The engine wants a whole number. It is 2.\\n9. Critical. Import of `labs/game/audio/library.ts`: `sfx:laser` is already an engine preset (`CORE_DUPLICATE_ID`). Game cues are `sfx:compass-*` and songs are `song:compass-*`.\\n10. Not critical. `labs/game/op/content.test.ts` (story walk): a drama caption ended with a period and the text check rejected the scene. The line still played.\\n11. Not critical. `labs/game/app/campaign.test.ts`: a fixed run of accepts walked past the first briefing, because that scene has fourteen boxes. The test now stops when the briefing is up.\\n12. Not critical. Dev Mode reset wrote the setting back and left the on-screen slider on the dragged number, because the shell caches the value. Reset now writes the fallback into that cache.\\n13. Not critical. Scrub In treated a new pad's Cross as Start as well as claim, so the seat list closed on the joining press. A seat that was not claimed yet claims and stays on the screen.\\n14. Critical. `labs/game/view/looks.ts` and `labs/game/audio/library.ts`: speed lines took `strength` where the engine wants `density`, and a song carried `description`, which `SongSpec` does not have. Both threw while the module loaded.\\n\\n20→Fourteen issues. Ten were game-breaking: 1–9 and 14. Four were not: 10–13.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→# Testing log\\n\\nOne line each. Critical means the operation, the save, or the page would be wrong for a player.\\n\\n1. Critical. `labs/game/scenes/main.test.ts` (restore): a capture put back the world and the next step still used the operation from before the rewind, until the chart snapshot was adopted.\\n2. Critical. `labs/game/op/bot.test.ts` (gala-shift): the flap never reached its closed pose, so the case could not finish.\\n3. Critical. `labs/game/op/op.test.ts` (Reverie): the strain left the surface before the laser time the case allows.\\n4. Critical. `labs/game/op/op.test.ts` (Solace): a split stacked the children on one point, so one stroke hit both.\\n5. Critical. `labs/game/op/op.test.ts` (syringe): the dose bound the wrong target on a Balm cell.\\n10→6. Critical. `labs/game/op/bot.test.ts` (suture): stitches landed off the wound unless the hand was within a short distance of the next stitch.\\n7. Critical. `labs/game/op/bot.test.ts` (two and four seats): co-op copies were born on the same point, so one tool cleared both.\\n8. Critical. Import of `labs/game/view/looks.ts`: `outline.width` of 1.5 is rejected (`CORE_BAD_SPEC`). The engine wants a whole number. It is 2.\\n9. Critical. Import of `labs/game/audio/library.ts`: `sfx:laser` is already an engine preset (`CORE_DUPLICATE_ID`). Game cues are `sfx:compass-*` and songs are `song:compass-*`.\\n10. Not critical. `labs/game/op/content.test.ts` (story walk): a drama caption ended with a period and the text check rejected the scene. The line still played.\\n11. Not critical. `labs/game/app/campaign.test.ts`: a fixed run of accepts walked past the first briefing, because that scene has fourteen boxes. The test now stops when the briefing is up.\\n12. Not critical. Dev Mode reset wrote the setting back and left the on-screen slider on the dragged number, because the shell caches the value. Reset now writes the fallback into that cache.\\n13. Not critical. Scrub In treated a new pad's Cross as Start as well as claim, so the seat list closed on the joining press. A seat that was not claimed yet claims and stays on the screen.\\n14. Critical. `labs/game/view/looks.ts` and `labs/game/audio/library.ts`: speed lines took `strength` where the engine wants `density`, and a song carried `description`, which `SongSpec` does not have. Both threw while the module loaded.\\n\\n20→Fourteen issues. Ten were game-breaking: 1–9 and 14. Four were not: 10–13.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"# Testing log\\n\\nOne line each. Critical means the operation, the save, or the page would be wrong for a player.\\n\\n1. Critical. `labs/game/scenes/main.test.ts` (restore): a capture put back the world and the next step still used the operation from before the rewind, until the chart snapshot was adopted.\\n2. Critical. `labs/game/op/bot.test.ts` (gala-shift): the flap never reached its closed pose, so the case could not finish.\\n3. Critical. `labs/game/op/op.test.ts` (Reverie): the strain left the surface before the laser time the case allows.\\n4. Critical. `labs/game/op/op.test.ts` (Solace): a split stacked the children on one point, so one stroke hit both.\\n5. Critical. `labs/game/op/op.test.ts` (syringe): the dose bound the wrong target on a Balm cell.\\n6. Critical. `labs/game/op/bot.test.ts` (suture): stitches landed off the wound unless the hand was within a short distance of the next stitch.\\n7. Critical. `labs/game/op/bot.test.ts` (two and four seats): co-op copies were born on the same point, so one tool cleared both.\\n8. Critical. Import of `labs/game/view/looks.ts`: `outline.width` of 1.5 is rejected (`CORE_BAD_SPEC`). The engine wants a whole number. It is 2.\\n9. Critical. Import of `labs/game/audio/library.ts`: `sfx:laser` is already an engine preset (`CORE_DUPLICATE_ID`). Game cues are `sfx:compass-*` and songs are `song:compass-*`.\\n10. Not critical. `labs/game/op/content.test.ts` (story walk): a drama caption ended with a period and the text check rejected the scene. The line still played.\\n11. Not critical. `labs/game/app/campaign.test.ts`: a fixed run of accepts walked past the first briefing, because that scene has fourteen boxes. The test now stops when the briefing is up.\\n12. Not critical. Dev Mode reset wrote the setting back and left the on-screen slider on the dragged number, because the shell caches the value. Reset now writes the fallback into that cache.\\n13. Not critical. Scrub In treated a new pad's Cross as Start as well as claim, so the seat list closed on the joining press. A seat that was not claimed yet claims and stays on the screen.\\n14. Critical. `labs/game/view/looks.ts` and `labs/game/audio/library.ts`: speed lines took `strength` where the engine wants `density`, and a song carried `description`, which `SongSpec` does not have. Both threw while the module loaded.\\n\\nFourteen issues. Ten were game-breaking: 1–9 and 14. Four were not: 10–13.\\n\",\"total_lines\":20}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-e32fb63b-da09-48cd-8a0d-2d3f9edbf918-15","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,55,51,49,95,95,120,53,57,99,49,100,51,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,51,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,55,51,49,95,95,120,53,57,99,49,100,51,47,119,111,114,107,47,84,114,97,117,109,97,45,67,111,109,112,97,115,115,45,84,114,97,117,109,97,45,67,101,110,116,101,114,45,83,101,99,111,110,100,45,79,112,105,110,105,111,110,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,55,51,49,47,108,97,98,115,47,103,97,109,101,47,100,97,116,97,47,105,110,116,101,114,118,105,101,119,46,116,115,10,51,54,58,32,32,116,101,115,116,105,110,103,70,101,101,100,98,97,99,107,58,32,91,10,51,55,58,32,32,32,32,39,70,111,117,114,116,101,101,110,32,105,115,115,117,101,115,32,119,101,114,101,32,99,97,117,103,104,116,32,97,110,100,32,119,114,105,116,116,101,110,32,105,110,32,108,97,98,115,47,103,97,109,101,47,84,69,83,84,73,78,71,45,76,79,71,46,109,100,46,39,44,10,49,48,50,58,32,32,73,78,84,69,82,86,73,69,87,46,116,101,115,116,105,110,103,70,101,101,100,98,97,99,107,46,102,111,114,69,97,99,104,40,40,98,111,100,121,44,32,105,110,100,101,120,41,32,61,62,32,123,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":3,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/data/interview.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":36,\"content\":\"  testingFeedback: [\"},{\"line_number\":37,\"content\":\"    'Fourteen issues were caught and written in labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md.',\"},{\"line_number\":102,\"content\":\"  INTERVIEW.testingFeedback.forEach((body, index) => {\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-e32fb63b-da09-48cd-8a0d-2d3f9edbf918-16","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"540→  c.screen = 'story';\\n}\\n\\nfunction retryCase(c: Campaign): void {\\n  c.boot += 1;\\n  c.keepPhase = false;\\n  c.screen = 'op';\\n  c.won = false;\\n}\\n\\n550→function enterAttract(c: Campaign): void {\\n  c.screen = 'attract';\\n  c.clip = 0;\\n  c.clipMs = ATTRACT[0].ms;\\n  c.box = 0;\\n  c.record = false;\\n}\\n\\nfunction leaveAttract(c: Campaign): void {\\n  c.screen = 'title';\\n560→  c.focus = 0;\\n  c.idle = 0;\\n  c.record = true;\\n}\\n\\nfunction cycleSetting(c: Campaign, id: string): void {\\n  const p = c.progress;\\n  const volume = (n: number) => [0, 10, 40, 70, 100][([0, 10, 40, 70, 100].indexOf(n) + 1) % 5] ?? 70;\\n  if (id === 'master') p.master = volume(p.master);\\n  if (id === 'music') p.music = volume(p.music);\\n570→  if (id === 'effects') p.effects = volume(p.effects);\\n  if (id === 'voice') p.voice = volume(p.voice);\\n  if (id === 'glyphs') p.glyphs = p.glyphs === 'playstation' ? 'xbox' : 'playstation';\\n  if (id === 'difficulty') {\\n    const order: Difficulty[] = ['intern', 'resident', 'attending'];\\n    const next = order[(order.indexOf(p.difficulty) + 1) % 3];\\n    if (next === 'attending' && !p.attending && !p.free) return;\\n    p.difficulty = next;\\n  }\\n  if (id === 'simple') p.simple = !p.simple;\",\"content_concise\":\"540→  c.screen = 'story';\\n}\\n\\nfunction retryCase(c: Campaign): void {\\n  c.boot += 1;\\n  c.keepPhase = false;\\n  c.screen = 'op';\\n  c.won = false;\\n}\\n\\n550→function enterAttract(c: Campaign): void {\\n  c.screen = 'attract';\\n  c.clip = 0;\\n  c.clipMs = ATTRACT[0].ms;\\n  c.box = 0;\\n  c.record = false;\\n}\\n\\nfunction leaveAttract(c: Campaign): void {\\n  c.screen = 'title';\\n560→  c.focus = 0;\\n  c.idle = 0;\\n  c.record = true;\\n}\\n\\nfunction cycleSetting(c: Campaign, id: string): void {\\n  const p = c.progress;\\n  const volume = (n: number) => [0, 10, 40, 70, 100][([0, 10, 40, 70, 100].indexOf(n) + 1) % 5] ?? 70;\\n  if (id === 'master') p.master = volume(p.master);\\n  if (id === 'music') p.music = volume(p.music);\\n570→  if (id === 'effects') p.effects = volume(p.effects);\\n  if (id === 'voice') p.voice = volume(p.voice);\\n  if (id === 'glyphs') p.glyphs = p.glyphs === 'playstation' ? 'xbox' : 'playstation';\\n  if (id === 'difficulty') {\\n    const order: Difficulty[] = ['intern', 'resident', 'attending'];\\n    const next = order[(order.indexOf(p.difficulty) + 1) % 3];\\n    if (next === 'attending' && !p.attending && !p.free) return;\\n    p.difficulty = next;\\n  }\\n  if (id === 'simple') p.simple = !p.simple;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/app/campaign.ts\",\"offset\":540,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"  c.screen = 'story';\\n}\\n\\nfunction retryCase(c: Campaign): void {\\n  c.boot += 1;\\n  c.keepPhase = false;\\n  c.screen = 'op';\\n  c.won = false;\\n}\\n\\nfunction enterAttract(c: Campaign): void {\\n  c.screen = 'attract';\\n  c.clip = 0;\\n  c.clipMs = ATTRACT[0].ms;\\n  c.box = 0;\\n  c.record = false;\\n}\\n\\nfunction leaveAttract(c: Campaign): void {\\n  c.screen = 'title';\\n  c.focus = 0;\\n  c.idle = 0;\\n  c.record = true;\\n}\\n\\nfunction cycleSetting(c: Campaign, id: string): void {\\n  const p = c.progress;\\n  const volume = (n: number) => [0, 10, 40, 70, 100][([0, 10, 40, 70, 100].indexOf(n) + 1) % 5] ?? 70;\\n  if (id === 'master') p.master = volume(p.master);\\n  if (id === 'music') p.music = volume(p.music);\\n  if (id === 'effects') p.effects = volume(p.effects);\\n  if (id === 'voice') p.voice = volume(p.voice);\\n  if (id === 'glyphs') p.glyphs = p.glyphs === 'playstation' ? 'xbox' : 'playstation';\\n  if (id === 'difficulty') {\\n    const order: Difficulty[] = ['intern', 'resident', 'attending'];\\n    const next = order[(order.indexOf(p.difficulty) + 1) % 3];\\n    if (next === 'attending' && !p.attending && !p.free) return;\\n    p.difficulty = next;\\n  }\\n  if (id === 'simple') p.simple = !p.simple;\\n\",\"total_lines\":589}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"fcc1df44-a3db-4fcc-b5f3-24a5445a1bcd"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_471","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Checking noteInput to see if pointerdown during attract mode exits immediately and whether a subsequent frame saves.\n\nsaveProgress only runs on accept, cancel, or finishOp. Leaving attract mode does not trigger a save. The localStorage change came from the shared engine store during attract. Omitting the store fixes it. This will be logged as issue 15 as a non-critical save leak.\n\nThe interview text is baked into HTML and requires a rebuild. I will read interview.ts and exit-interview.json to update both copies. I also need to verify PLAN.md for store and attract save behavior, and check whether pointerdown and click handlers both fire during attract mode.\n\nThe pointerdown sequence exits attract mode before click, so shell buttons should not activate after leaving attract. The test already passes on this path. I will include localStorage keys in the diff to diagnose any remaining failure. I am also considering whether the mouse test should wait for ready.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f70eb101-a0d8-49e9-85f0-2b245cb3462e-17","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"button|shell|data-game","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/index.html"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f70eb101-a0d8-49e9-85f0-2b245cb3462e-18","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/data/interview.ts","offset":30,"limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f70eb101-a0d8-49e9-85f0-2b245cb3462e-19","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"Fourteen issues","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/exit-inte