9,97,45,67,101,110,116,101,114,45,83,101,99,111,110,100,45,79,112,105,110,105,111,110,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,55,51,49,47,108,97,98,115,47,103,97,109,101,47,100,97,116,97,47,105,110,116,101,114,118,105,101,119,46,116,115,10,50,58,32,42,32,64,102,105,108,101,32,84,104,101,32,101,120,105,116,32,105,110,116,101,114,118,105,101,119,46,32,84,104,101,32,65,98,111,117,116,32,115,99,114,101,101,110,32,97,110,100,32,101,120,105,116,45,105,110,116,101,114,118,105,101,119,46,106,115,111,110,32,97,114,101,32,116,104,105,115,32,111,98,106,101,99,116,44,32,115,111,32,116,104,101,121,32,99,97,110,110,111,116,32,100,105,115,97,103,114,101,101,46,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":2,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/app/page.test.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":26,\"content\":\"      readFileSync(new URL('../../../../exit-interview.json', import.meta.url), 'utf8'),\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/data/interview.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":2,\"content\":\" * @file The exit interview. The About screen and exit-interview.json are this object, so they cannot disagree.\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-80dc7653-3b00-4698-8a68-367d01047601-44","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→# Engine feedback: trauma-compass\\n\\nWhat this game needed from the my-3dge engine (at 2dbd829) and did not get. The owner collects this file\\nfrom every game to improve the engine, so write each item for an engine agent who has never seen this repository:\\nwhat you tried, what happened (the command, the error code), what you expected, and what you did instead.\\n\\n## Requests\\n\\n- After `capture` and `restore`, call the scene again once the world is back. What I tried: keep the operation in a module, snapshot it on a chart component, and step. What happened: restore replaced the world and the next step still read the module from before the rewind, so the hash diverged until the page called `followChart` on the restored blob. What I expected: a scene hook that runs after restore, with the restored world already in place. What I did instead: the page reads `chart.blob` every frame and copies it back into the module before the next hands are packed.\\n10→- A public way to rewrite a geometry the page kept. What I tried: build the operating sheet once with `defineGeometry` / a kit box and write new positions into the same buffers every frame (breath, heartbeat, incision). What happened: there is no public call to replace the vertex data of a geometry the page is already holding, so a kept `BufferGeometry` cannot be repainted through the API. What I expected: something like `writeGeometry(id, positions, colors)` that is safe across a scene restart. What I did instead: the page holds the buffers from the geometry the kit box created and writes them directly. That is the gap PLAN.md §17.3 names.\\n- A view setting the sim is allowed to read. What I tried: `game.radialSlow` as a live slider that scales field time while the radial is open, and include that scale in the operation. What happened: view settings are not visible to sim-side code, so two peers would not share a slider that never enters the hash. What I expected: a `when: 'now'` number the scene can read and put into the hands or the world. What I did instead: the radial holds field time at a fixed 60 ticks per step (0.6 of a normal step). The slider still draws and resets. It does not change the clock.\\n\\n## Friction\\n\\n- `outline.width` must be a whole number. `1.5` fails at import with `CORE_BAD_SPEC`. The message is clear once you see it. A note beside the field in the look docs would have saved the guess.\\n- Preset ids are global. `defineSfx('sfx:laser')` and `defineEmitter` of `emitter:rain` fail with `CORE_DUPLICATE_ID` because the engine already registered those. `song:title` is taken the same way. The game prefixes its own ids.\\n- `SongSpec` has no `description`. Passing one throws when the song is defined. `speedlines` takes `density`, not `strength`.\\n- Boolean settings accept `1` and `0` as well as `true` and `false`. `?game.autoplay=1` is a real setting. Stripping unknown keys is still required; `aihub*` keys are not engine settings.\\n- `createEngine` steps during warmup before the page can pause. A hub round has to `pause`, `seed`, `pause`, then `ready`, or the two copies do not both start at tick 0.\\n20→\\n## Local engine patches\\n\\n<!--\\n`npm run check` accepts an edited engine file only when it is listed here, one line each, its path in backticks:\\n- `engine/path/to/file.ts`: why no workaround in the game would do, and what the engine should change instead.\\n-->\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→# Engine feedback: trauma-compass\\n\\nWhat this game needed from the my-3dge engine (at 2dbd829) and did not get. The owner collects this file\\nfrom every game to improve the engine, so write each item for an engine agent who has never seen this repository:\\nwhat you tried, what happened (the command, the error code), what you expected, and what you did instead.\\n\\n## Requests\\n\\n- After `capture` and `restore`, call the scene again once the world is back. What I tried: keep the operation in a module, snapshot it on a chart component, and step. What happened: restore replaced the world and the next step still read the module from before the rewind, so the hash diverged until the page called `followChart` on the restored blob. What I expected: a scene hook that runs after restore, with the restored world already in place. What I did instead: the page reads `chart.blob` every frame and copies it back into the module before the next hands are packed.\\n10→- A public way to rewrite a geometry the page kept. What I tried: build the operating sheet once with `defineGeometry` / a kit box and write new positions into the same buffers every frame (breath, heartbeat, incision). What happened: there is no public call to replace the vertex data of a geometry the page is already holding, so a kept `BufferGeometry` cannot be repainted through the API. What I expected: something like `writeGeometry(id, positions, colors)` that is safe across a scene restart. What I did instead: the page holds the buffers from the geometry the kit box created and writes them directly. That is the gap PLAN.md §17.3 names.\\n- A view setting the sim is allowed to read. What I tried: `game.radialSlow` as a live slider that scales field time while the radial is open, and include that scale in the operation. What happened: view settings are not visible to sim-side code, so two peers would not share a slider that never enters the hash. What I expected: a `when: 'now'` number the scene can read and put into the hands or the world. What I did instead: the radial holds field time at a fixed 60 ticks per step (0.6 of a normal step). The slider still draws and resets. It does not change the clock.\\n\\n## Friction\\n\\n- `outline.width` must be a whole number. `1.5` fails at import with `CORE_BAD_SPEC`. The message is clear once you see it. A note beside the field in the look docs would have saved the guess.\\n- Preset ids are global. `defineSfx('sfx:laser')` and `defineEmitter` of `emitter:rain` fail with `CORE_DUPLICATE_ID` because the engine already registered those. `song:title` is taken the same way. The game prefixes its own ids.\\n- `SongSpec` has no `description`. Passing one throws when the song is defined. `speedlines` takes `density`, not `strength`.\\n- Boolean settings accept `1` and `0` as well as `true` and `false`. `?game.autoplay=1` is a real setting. Stripping unknown keys is still required; `aihub*` keys are not engine settings.\\n- `createEngine` steps during warmup before the page can pause. A hub round has to `pause`, `seed`, `pause`, then `ready`, or the two copies do not both start at tick 0.\\n20→\\n## Local engine patches\\n\\n<!--\\n`npm run check` accepts an edited engine file only when it is listed here, one line each, its path in backticks:\\n- `engine/path/to/file.ts`: why no workaround in the game would do, and what the engine should change instead.\\n-->\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"# Engine feedback: trauma-compass\\n\\nWhat this game needed from the my-3dge engine (at 2dbd829) and did not get. The owner collects this file\\nfrom every game to improve the engine, so write each item for an engine agent who has never seen this repository:\\nwhat you tried, what happened (the command, the error code), what you expected, and what you did instead.\\n\\n## Requests\\n\\n- After `capture` and `restore`, call the scene again once the world is back. What I tried: keep the operation in a module, snapshot it on a chart component, and step. What happened: restore replaced the world and the next step still read the module from before the rewind, so the hash diverged until the page called `followChart` on the restored blob. What I expected: a scene hook that runs after restore, with the restored world already in place. What I did instead: the page reads `chart.blob` every frame and copies it back into the module before the next hands are packed.\\n- A public way to rewrite a geometry the page kept. What I tried: build the operating sheet once with `defineGeometry` / a kit box and write new positions into the same buffers every frame (breath, heartbeat, incision). What happened: there is no public call to replace the vertex data of a geometry the page is already holding, so a kept `BufferGeometry` cannot be repainted through the API. What I expected: something like `writeGeometry(id, positions, colors)` that is safe across a scene restart. What I did instead: the page holds the buffers from the geometry the kit box created and writes them directly. That is the gap PLAN.md §17.3 names.\\n- A view setting the sim is allowed to read. What I tried: `game.radialSlow` as a live slider that scales field time while the radial is open, and include that scale in the operation. What happened: view settings are not visible to sim-side code, so two peers would not share a slider that never enters the hash. What I expected: a `when: 'now'` number the scene can read and put into the hands or the world. What I did instead: the radial holds field time at a fixed 60 ticks per step (0.6 of a normal step). The slider still draws and resets. It does not change the clock.\\n\\n## Friction\\n\\n- `outline.width` must be a whole number. `1.5` fails at import with `CORE_BAD_SPEC`. The message is clear once you see it. A note beside the field in the look docs would have saved the guess.\\n- Preset ids are global. `defineSfx('sfx:laser')` and `defineEmitter` of `emitter:rain` fail with `CORE_DUPLICATE_ID` because the engine already registered those. `song:title` is taken the same way. The game prefixes its own ids.\\n- `SongSpec` has no `description`. Passing one throws when the song is defined. `speedlines` takes `density`, not `strength`.\\n- Boolean settings accept `1` and `0` as well as `true` and `false`. `?game.autoplay=1` is a real setting. Stripping unknown keys is still required; `aihub*` keys are not engine settings.\\n- `createEngine` steps during warmup before the page can pause. A hub round has to `pause`, `seed`, `pause`, then `ready`, or the two copies do not both start at tick 0.\\n\\n## Local engine patches\\n\\n<!--\\n`npm run check` accepts an edited engine file only when it is listed here, one line each, its path in backticks:\\n- `engine/path/to/file.ts`: why no workaround in the game would do, and what the engine should change instead.\\n-->\\n\",\"total_lines\":26}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"2ec790e7-1646-4916-bcfe-437124726816"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_482","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Adding a friction bullet about the governor writing localStorage when the page store is passed to createEngine.\n\nEngine feedback answers are fixed and don't need updating. The friction bullet belongs in ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md. Testing log issue 15 is a game bug from passing the store; engine behavior is expected.\n\nThe interview answers are hand-written summaries, not generated from the markdown, so adding a friction bullet is acceptable. Now applying edits and starting the e2e storage diff.\n\nThe `storageDelta` helper compares two JSON strings and returns changed keys or \"order\" if only key order differs. It will be used to report localStorage changes in the test report.\n\nThe test report will include the storage delta alongside the demo count. The mouse section is being replaced with a paced enter sequence: wait for engine readiness, hover the first row button, click the hovered element, and verify it is active.\n\nThe test sequence now waits for the board screen, clicks Back to return to title, then repeatedly presses Enter with 80ms pauses until the op screen appears. This pacing is safe because 80ms exceeds one frame.\n\nThe 40 Enter presses total roughly 3.2 seconds, which is acceptable for the 14-box story.\n\nPad, scrub, and glyphs tests need a ready wait added.\n\nFor touch testing, the message element appears immediately after createEngine returns when ready becomes true. The attract wait begins from that moment, so the test must wait up to 15 seconds for attract before the 10-second idle timeout starts.\n\nThe Pixel 7 touch test taps the settings button in the touch banner. The tap fires a window pointerdown that exits attract mode and returns to title before the button click reaches settings. The event order must be handled carefully.\n\nThe touch test tap() bubbles pointerdown to the window listener, which exits attract mode before the button click reaches settings. The settings button might be outside #shell on the touch overlay.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7f68bde0-c125-4637-922a-0aa81ce70811-45","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"touch|data-act=\\\"settings\\\"","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/ui/shell.ts"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1503,"output_tokens":1270,"cache_read_input_tokens":73472,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"e9eeed74-b5bc-4846-8877-f4cb6172cfaf"}
