ae342a3fde0e"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_483","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The touch div is a sibling.\n\nShell click listener targets data-act elements. Pointerdown during tap exits attract mode and routes to settings. Shell redraws asynchronously, but the button remains clickable. No game changes are needed.\n\nCampaign autoplay loops if the bot loses. Node tests pass and the page path should win. The 660-second campaign test is the longest e2e step. I will run it in the background. I need to check verify.mjs to avoid duplicate long runs. The plan is to apply fixes, rebuild one-file, run a quick targeted test, then run hub harness and verify until exit 0.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-79eba659-1452-4906-94fd-9f4499a09445-46","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/app/page.test.ts"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1646,"output_tokens":834,"cache_read_input_tokens":74880,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"51a134b9-c02f-45b4-893b-da3c2c9066d6"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-79eba659-1452-4906-94fd-9f4499a09445-46","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The page's session client is the unmodified file, and it is the first script. The About data matches the\\n * exit interview on disk.\\n */\\nimport { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\\nimport { INTERVIEW } from '../data/interview';\\n\\nconst html = readFileSync(new URL('../index.html', import.meta.url), 'utf8');\\n10→const session = readFileSync(new URL('../vendor/session.js', import.meta.url), 'utf8');\\n\\ndescribe('page sources', () => {\\n  it('pastes session.js first and unchanged', () => {\\n    const head = html.slice(html.indexOf('<meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\" />'));\\n    const start = head.indexOf('<script>');\\n    const end = head.indexOf('</script>');\\n    expect(start).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n    expect(head.slice(0, start)).not.toContain('<script');\\n    expect(head.slice(start + '<script>'.length, end)).toBe(session);\\n20→    expect(html).toContain('<script type=\\\"module\\\" crossorigin src=\\\"./main.ts\\\">');\\n    expect(html).not.toContain('touch.css');\\n  });\\n\\n  it('matches the exit interview on disk', () => {\\n    const disk = JSON.parse(\\n      readFileSync(new URL('../../../../exit-interview.json', import.meta.url), 'utf8'),\\n    ) as unknown;\\n    expect(disk).toEqual(INTERVIEW);\\n  });\\n30→});\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The page's session client is the unmodified file, and it is the first script. The About data matches the\\n * exit interview on disk.\\n */\\nimport { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\\nimport { INTERVIEW } from '../data/interview';\\n\\nconst html = readFileSync(new URL('../index.html', import.meta.url), 'utf8');\\n10→const session = readFileSync(new URL('../vendor/session.js', import.meta.url), 'utf8');\\n\\ndescribe('page sources', () => {\\n  it('pastes session.js first and unchanged', () => {\\n    const head = html.slice(html.indexOf('<meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\" />'));\\n    const start = head.indexOf('<script>');\\n    const end = head.indexOf('</script>');\\n    expect(start).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n    expect(head.slice(0, start)).not.toContain('<script');\\n    expect(head.slice(start + '<script>'.length, end)).toBe(session);\\n20→    expect(html).toContain('<script type=\\\"module\\\" crossorigin src=\\\"./main.ts\\\">');\\n    expect(html).not.toContain('touch.css');\\n  });\\n\\n  it('matches the exit interview on disk', () => {\\n    const disk = JSON.parse(\\n      readFileSync(new URL('../../../../exit-interview.json', import.meta.url), 'utf8'),\\n    ) as unknown;\\n    expect(disk).toEqual(INTERVIEW);\\n  });\\n30→});\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/app/page.test.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file The page's session client is the unmodified file, and it is the first script. The About data matches the\\n * exit interview on disk.\\n */\\nimport { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\\nimport { INTERVIEW } from '../data/interview';\\n\\nconst html = readFileSync(new URL('../index.html', import.meta.url), 'utf8');\\nconst session = readFileSync(new URL('../vendor/session.js', import.meta.url), 'utf8');\\n\\ndescribe('page sources', () => {\\n  it('pastes session.js first and unchanged', () => {\\n    const head = html.slice(html.indexOf('<meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\" />'));\\n    const start = head.indexOf('<script>');\\n    const end = head.indexOf('</script>');\\n    expect(start).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n    expect(head.slice(0, start)).not.toContain('<script');\\n    expect(head.slice(start + '<script>'.length, end)).toBe(session);\\n    expect(html).toContain('<script type=\\\"module\\\" crossorigin src=\\\"./main.ts\\\">');\\n    expect(html).not.toContain('touch.css');\\n  });\\n\\n  it('matches the exit interview on disk', () => {\\n    const disk = JSON.parse(\\n      readFileSync(new URL('../../../../exit-interview.json', import.meta.url), 'utf8'),\\n    ) as unknown;\\n    expect(disk).toEqual(INTERVIEW);\\n  });\\n});\\n\",\"total_lines\":30}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"86878be3-b87a-4e64-8a1b-a1e74298efc2"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_484","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"page.test compares interview.ts to exit-interview.json.\n\nThe built HTML must be rebuilt because the browser runs the bundled page, not the source files. I will apply all edits and build now. I also need to check verify.mjs for the command and TMPDIR handling.\n\nI will check for running Chrome processes and update the todos. The interview feedback will list the new attract storage issue as a non-game-breaking detail. I also verified that saveProgress is unlikely to conflict with other localStorage writers.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-530ed753-b746-4880-a734-908628b84b77-47","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"store\\.set","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1300,"output_tokens":385,"cache_read_input_tokens":76416,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"81529eeb-7832-4b0a-8412-7c50a905ec12"}
