{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_499","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"HTML rebuilt. The file is slightly smaller at 6874806 bytes after removing `store,`.\n\nThe source is correct and boot.ts is included. The HTML contains \"Fifteen issues\" and the session script loads first. End-to-end tests are starting. Worst case runtime is roughly fifteen minutes.\n\nEnd-to-end tests will run in the background. A monitor script will poll the log and print only when failures or exit occur.\n\nScratch directory and environment variables are set. The e2e script resolves Playwright from within the package directory.\n\nPlaywright resolution from the package root is confirmed. I will read verify.mjs and hub.mjs in parallel while e2e runs, and do a quick HTML verification before launching.\n\nThe monitor script will live in the scratch directory. It polls the e2e log for failures and prints the last five lines on detection, allowing diagnosis while the campaign continues.\n\nThe monitor script will exit immediately on the first failure so I can diagnose without delay. It polls every 30 seconds to respect GitHub rate limits.\n\nPolling will run every 5 seconds for faster failure detection. If a fix is needed, the running e2e process must be killed first to free the browser. earlyoom kills the largest process when memory pressure hits, so relaunching requires stopping the current run.\n\nI will not start the hub until the e2e Chromium process finishes. If an early failure occurs, I will prepare a fix but wait for the current run to complete rather than killing it, preserving the campaign result. A late failure will be caught by the monitor at the end.\n\nThe e2e script will run in a temporary directory and log to scratch/e2e2.log. The shell wrapper will record the exit code as EXIT:0 or EXIT:1 at the end of the file.\n\nI will name the new log e2e-r3.log so I can compare it with previous runs. I will check for existing Chrome processes before launching. I will read hub.mjs immediately after the tool calls return.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-05f36a50-8121-4309-87d5-07192f4caa4f-82","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"pause|uiCancel|Escape","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/input/map.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-05f36a50-8121-4309-87d5-07192f4caa4f-83","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"Escape|pause","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/input","glob":"**/*default*"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":474,"output_tokens":2127,"cache_read_input_tokens":97792,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"7876990f-541d-45dc-be0b-a96b7d2c8ed9"}
