EN: Leave the dog. I will be quick.',\\n      'ODIE: You will be careful. Quick is how people become stories.',\\n      'WREN: Drain, forceps, suture. I have had the lecture.',\\n50→      'ODIE: Then give it back to me with your hands. Vitals are seventy and rude about it.',\\n      'WREN: Sorry. I say that to them even when they cannot hear.',\\n      'ODIE: Good. Start with the water. The glass can wait its turn.',\\n    ]),\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'after-1',\\n    where: 'The corridor',\\n    boxes: boxes([\\n      'ODIE: He is breathing like a man who intends to keep the habit.',\",\"content_concise\":\"30→  });\\n}\\n\\n/** Every story scene, in the order the director plays them. */\\nexport const SCENES: readonly Scene[] = [\\n  {\\n    id: 'before-1',\\n    where: 'Harbor Light, night',\\n    boxes: boxes([\\n      'ODIE: Congratulations, Doctor. You are the only surgeon in the building.',\\n40→      'WREN: The storm took the bridge. I can hear the glass in it.',\\n      'ODIE: And the ad. Turn that down before it turns you.',\\n      'VOSS: Pain is just a feeling you have not paid to remove yet.',\\n      'WREN: Halcyon. Because you deserve to feel nothing. Who bought that line?',\\n      'ODIE: Everyone with a wallet. Tomás Reyes is on table one. Deck hatch. Glass.',\\n      'WREN: Is he awake?',\\n      'ODIE: Awake enough to ask after a dog. The dog is in the corridor, against every rule I have.',\\n      'WREN: Leave the dog. I will be quick.',\\n      'ODIE: You will be careful. Quick is how people become stories.',\\n      'WREN: Drain, forceps, suture. I have had the lecture.',\\n50→      'ODIE: Then give it back to me with your hands. Vitals are seventy and rude about it.',\\n      'WREN: Sorry. I say that to them even when they cannot hear.',\\n      'ODIE: Good. Start with the water. The glass can wait its turn.',\\n    ]),\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'after-1',\\n    where: 'The corridor',\\n    boxes: boxes([\\n      'ODIE: He is breathing like a man who intends to keep the habit.',\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/story.ts\",\"offset\":30,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"  });\\n}\\n\\n/** Every story scene, in the order the director plays them. */\\nexport const SCENES: readonly Scene[] = [\\n  {\\n    id: 'before-1',\\n    where: 'Harbor Light, night',\\n    boxes: boxes([\\n      'ODIE: Congratulations, Doctor. You are the only surgeon in the building.',\\n      'WREN: The storm took the bridge. I can hear the glass in it.',\\n      'ODIE: And the ad. Turn that down before it turns you.',\\n      'VOSS: Pain is just a feeling you have not paid to remove yet.',\\n      'WREN: Halcyon. Because you deserve to feel nothing. Who bought that line?',\\n      'ODIE: Everyone with a wallet. Tomás Reyes is on table one. Deck hatch. Glass.',\\n      'WREN: Is he awake?',\\n      'ODIE: Awake enough to ask after a dog. The dog is in the corridor, against every rule I have.',\\n      'WREN: Leave the dog. I will be quick.',\\n      'ODIE: You will be careful. Quick is how people become stories.',\\n      'WREN: Drain, forceps, suture. I have had the lecture.',\\n      'ODIE: Then give it back to me with your hands. Vitals are seventy and rude about it.',\\n      'WREN: Sorry. I say that to them even when they cannot hear.',\\n      'ODIE: Good. Start with the water. The glass can wait its turn.',\\n    ]),\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'after-1',\\n    where: 'The corridor',\\n    boxes: boxes([\\n      'ODIE: He is breathing like a man who intends to keep the habit.',\\n\",\"total_lines\":396}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-3dbd9443-81c1-4cc9-9162-5738ea565773-107","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"490→  if (!def) {\\n    c.screen = 'credits';\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  c.caseIndex = index;\\n  c.caseId = def.id;\\n  c.leg = leg;\\n  c.storyId = leg === 'before' ? def.storyBefore : def.storyAfter;\\n  c.box = 0;\\n  c.lineMs = 0;\\n500→  c.screen = 'story';\\n}\\n\\nfunction advanceStory(c: Campaign): void {\\n  const scene = sceneById(c.storyId);\\n  if (!scene) return;\\n  if (c.box < scene.boxes.length - 1) {\\n    c.box += 1;\\n    return;\\n  }\\n510→  finishScene(c);\\n}\\n\\nfunction finishScene(c: Campaign): void {\\n  if (c.leg === 'before') {\\n    c.screen = 'brief';\\n    c.focus = 0;\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  c.progress.cleared = Math.max(c.progress.cleared, c.caseIndex + 1);\\n520→  if (c.progress.cleared >= storyCases().length) {\\n    c.progress.free = true;\\n    c.progress.attending = true;\\n    c.screen = 'credits';\\n    c.page = 0;\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  openCase(c, c.progress.cleared, 'before');\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"490→  if (!def) {\\n    c.screen = 'credits';\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  c.caseIndex = index;\\n  c.caseId = def.id;\\n  c.leg = leg;\\n  c.storyId = leg === 'before' ? def.storyBefore : def.storyAfter;\\n  c.box = 0;\\n  c.lineMs = 0;\\n500→  c.screen = 'story';\\n}\\n\\nfunction advanceStory(c: Campaign): void {\\n  const scene = sceneById(c.storyId);\\n  if (!scene) return;\\n  if (c.box < scene.boxes.length - 1) {\\n    c.box += 1;\\n    return;\\n  }\\n510→  finishScene(c);\\n}\\n\\nfunction finishScene(c: Campaign): void {\\n  if (c.leg === 'before') {\\n    c.screen = 'brief';\\n    c.focus = 0;\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  c.progress.cleared = Math.max(c.progress.cleared, c.caseIndex + 1);\\n520→  if (c.progress.cleared >= storyCases().length) {\\n    c.progress.free = true;\\n    c.progress.attending = true;\\n    c.screen = 'credits';\\n    c.page = 0;\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  openCase(c, c.progress.cleared, 'before');\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/app/campaign.ts\",\"offset\":490,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"  if (!def) {\\n    c.screen = 'credits';\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  c.caseIndex = index;\\n  c.caseId = def.id;\\n  c.leg = leg;\\n  c.storyId = leg === 'before' ? def.storyBefore : def.storyAfter;\\n  c.box = 0;\\n  c.lineMs = 0;\\n  c.screen = 'story';\\n}\\n\\nfunction advanceStory(c: Campaign): void {\\n  const scene = sceneById(c.storyId);\\n  if (!scene) return;\\n  if (c.box < scene.boxes.length - 1) {\\n    c.box += 1;\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  finishScene(c);\\n}\\n\\nfunction finishScene(c: Campaign): void {\\n  if (c.leg === 'before') {\\n    c.screen = 'brief';\\n    c.focus = 0;\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  c.progress.cleared = Math.max(c.progress.cleared, c.caseIndex + 1);\\n  if (c.progress.cleared >= storyCases().length) {\\n    c.progress.free = true;\\n    c.progress.attending = true;\\n    c.screen = 'credits';\\n    c.page = 0;\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  openCase(c, c.progress.cleared, 'before');\\n}\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":589}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"0bf0787c-5802-4dd2-94ca-fd6f741a1370"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_516","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Several failures occurred while the campaign was still running.\n\nThe mouse and dev pad timed out after 40 entries. The pad stub may be invisible to the game because navigator.getGamepads is replaced after ready, though pads() calls it each frame.\n\nThe pad test nulls pad 0, presses button 13, releases, then button 0. Button 13 is d-pad down and button 0 is accept. Button 0 should work on the title screen because claim only happens when screen equals 'scrub'.\n\nThe pad stub may be invisible because the engine cached the original getGamepads function. Playwright and the game share the same window, so a window mismatch is unlikely. The PAD_SCRIPT code needs inspection.\n\nThe pad stub is correctly injected before page scripts and properly formatted for the Gamepads API. The pads() function filters connected devices, so seat 0 should receive the stub. The reason the title screen still fails to advance remains unclear.\n\nThe pad stub is likely being ignored entirely. If the d-pad down registered, the accept button would have advanced to the board screen. The suspicion now falls on the sampling state: it may be stuck true and preventing getGamepads from being read.\n\nThe sampling state is not the culprit; endSample resets it at the start of each frame. The stub gamepad object should satisfy the GamepadButton array requirements, and pointer events are unlikely to interfere.\n\nChrome headless may not allow overriding navigator.getGamepads if the property is non-configurable. The pad test reached the title screen, so the assignment likely succeeded. A silent failure is unlikely.\n\nThe pad test likely fails because navigator.getGamepads is read-only in newer Chrome. The assignment succeeds, but the game never reads window.__pads, so the title screen stays stuck. The attract stick test worked because it only injected a stub pad without replacing getGamepads.\n\nThe attract stick test passed, confirming that overriding navigator.getGamepads works and the game reads pad axes. The menu button test still fails, so the issue is isolated to button edge detection rather than pad visibility. The rose detection logic appears correct: a button pressed on the first frame registers as a rising edge.\n\nThe 150ms gap between button presses should allow the game to register both edges. Double handling from a second accept input is unlikely. The pad test code needs another careful review.\n\nThe scrub screen test also failed. Seat 1 claimed successfully, but seat 2 did not claim and the gloves remained at zero. This confirms that pads are not affecting the game after the page has loaded. The pad stub is likely being overwritten by the engine or page after addInitScript injects it.\n\nThe attract test works because it assigns navigator.getGamepads directly in the page after load. The pad and scrub tests only inject the replacement via addInitScript, which may not persist for later page evaluations. Adding an explicit assignment inside the page after load should fix the issue.\n\nThe pads() function calls navigator.getGamepads on every frame, so the replacement should be visible. The init script may fail because Chrome exposes this property as a prototype getter that cannot be overwritten by assignment. This would explain why the attract test works—assigning it directly in the page after load succeeds.\n\nThe pad test sequence may be flawed. menus() calls samplePads first, which initializes padWas. If the button is held for only 150 ms, the game might miss the rising edge because the initial state was already down.\n\nThe pad test waits for the title screen and ready state before injecting pad data. The idle attract timer starts once onFrame begins, which occurs shortly after ready. If the ready wait is delayed, attract may begin during the pad sequence and override the title screen before the test finishes.\n\nThe title screen test confirmed the pad stub was completely ignored, so attract never started. The scrub screen test also failed for the same reason: the init script replacement was not being read. The installed e2e pad section needs inspection to verify whether try/finally blocks broke the addInitScript ordering. In the scrub case, the mouse click did register and seat 1 claimed, but the pad input never advanced the game state.\n\nThe scrub click targets the shell button rather than the canvas, so pointerLive stays false and no mouse aim occurs. This confirms pads are completely ignored.\n\nThe fix is to reassign navigator.getGamepads directly inside the page after goto, matching the attract test approach. Both pad tests need this inline assignment.\n\nI also need to check whether addInitScript is accidentally placed inside a try block after goto.\n\nThe audio test timed out because the h1 element was not stable during the click. The shell re-renders every frame by replacing its innerHTML, which destroys and recreates the title element each time. If shellStamp changes on every frame, the entire shell redraws and the target element detaches before Playwright can click it. This explains both the audio timeout and the title screen failure.\n\nThe shellStamp hash may include cursor text or position. If the cursor shifts every frame, the shell rebuilds constantly and destroys the title element before Playwright can click it. The audio test needs a stable h1 to resume the audio context.\n\nThe audio test should use page.mouse.click on the canvas instead of clicking a locator, since Playwright mouse clicks do not require element stability. This would provide the user gesture needed to resume the AudioContext without relying on a title element that gets destroyed by shell re-renders.\n\nFor the glyphs test, Enter is correctly detected as a key press, but the mouse button check fails because the expected SVG path string is missing.\n\nThe mouse click at 200,200 failed to switch lastDevice to mouse. The shell title area likely blocks pointer events, so the click may have missed the engine listener on the canvas.\n\nThe mouse click at 200,200 may have hit the New Shift button instead of the canvas. If so, the shell would handle the click and the engine might not receive it. The test still reached Settings and changed glyphs, which means the mouse prompt itself failed rather than a navigation error. ArrowDown correctly switched lastDevice to keyboard.\n\nThe mouse click at 200,200 likely hit a shell button instead of the canvas, so the engine never received the pointer event. The expected SVG path string for the mouse glyph may also differ from what the prompt actually renders. If lastDevice does not update to exactly 'mouse', the game falls back to the keyboard or gamepad glyph.\n\nThe 200,200 click is inside the viewport and should reach the canvas. I will read the engine's lastDevice code to see why it did not switch. The campaign browser is still running, so I will not start another. I need to verify whether the pad init script is actually installed before goto by reading the e2e file.\n\nThe mouse-to-op test likely fails because Enter activates a focused button while also triggering the game, causing double-steps or re-clicks. I will blur the active element before the Enter loop and wait longer between state changes. I suspect software WebGPU frame timing may also prevent rapid key presses from registering, so I will read input.ts to see how keys are tracked.\n\nThe audio h1 timeout likely occurred because the attract mode started during the 30-second click retry. The touch and Xbox glyph clicks succeeded, so the shell re-rendering is not a universal bug. The audio test waits for ready before clicking, but the attract timer may have triggered while the click was still pending.\n\nThe idle timer starts roughly 10 seconds after ready. The audio test retries clicking the h1 for 30 seconds, so attract mode replaces the title with a demo overlay before the click lands. The locator finds the element but it detaches during the retry loop. The test should click immediately after ready, or use mouse.click which does not retry on stability.\n\nThe shell is not rebuilding every frame. Earlier clicks on Glyphs and Board succeeded, so the title h1 failure is likely an isolated case rather than a universal re-render bug.\n\nThe h1 element is not clickable. The shell container has pointer-events: none, so the title element beneath it receives no pointer events. Playwright retries clicking the visible element, but the canvas underneath intercepts the click and causes the timeout.\n\nThe audio test should click the canvas at (400, 300) to bypass the non-clickable title element. The engine must resume the AudioContext on that pointer event itself, because a separate evaluate call cannot satisfy Chrome's user-gesture requirement.\n\nI need to search the engine code for `context.resume` or audio unlock logic. The glyphs mouse click should register because `MouseLeft` is bound to `use`, yet the prompt never updated, so the engine may not be treating that click as a valid device action.\n\nThe 200,200 click may have hit the New Shift button instead of the canvas. That button has pointer-events auto, so the engine listener on the canvas would not receive the event. The test reads the prompt after the click, which means it cannot confirm whether the engine actually registered the device change.\n\nThe campaign browser is still running, so I will prepare fixes and restart the monitor for EXIT to know when it is free. I will patch the e2e tests and read the engine's lastDevice assignment, audio resume logic, and Enter drop behavior.\n\nI will rewrite the story test to wait for a screen or box change after each Enter, up to thirty steps. The failure will record the final state. I also want to check whether the dev mode path can be reached by clicking through the story with waitForFunction.\n\nThe story test likely fails because the engine collapses rapid key presses into a single boolean per frame. Forty Enter events in about three seconds may only register as six advances if frames are spaced far apart, leaving sixteen needed advances unmet and the game stuck in story.\n\nThe pad test likely fails because the button press lasts only one frame. A 150ms hold is too short if frames are spaced far apart, so the engine may never register the edge.\n\nPad tests should hold buttons until the screen or focus changes, rather than using a fixed 150 ms hold. Scrubbing should wait for gloves to move before releasing the button. The glyphs test will click the canvas center and wait up to two seconds for the mouse glyph to appear in the prompt; if it does not, that is a game bug. The audio test will click the canvas center and rely on the page to resume the AudioContext on pointerdown.\n\nI will read the audio code to confirm whether it resumes AudioContext on any pointerdown. The monitor has already exited, but the campaign process is still running. I will patch e2e.mjs while the campaign runs and rebuild only if the game code itself needs changes.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-645ccfd1-7c08-4571-bb23-a389def0d23c-108","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"lastDevice","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/input","glob":"**/*.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-645ccfd1-7c08-4571-bb23-a389def0d23c-109","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"resume|context\\.state|user gesture|pointerdown","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine","glob":"**/audio*.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-645ccfd1-7c08-4571-bb23-a389def0d23c-110","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20