{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_527","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I will update the shell stamp and end-to-end tests.\n\nI will restart the monitor for EXIT. After end-to-end tests finish, I will rebuild and rerun. I will check shell.ts line count after editing. I am rewriting the enter loop to poll the screen place and campaign state up to 24 times, reporting if the op screen is not reached without throwing.\n\nThe loop presses Enter and waits up to four seconds for the screen state to change. It breaks if the state does not move and the op screen is not reached.\n\nIf the op screen is not reached, the script will report the stuck state and reset. Otherwise it proceeds with the existing pause and slider logic.\n\nI will also pad section replacements, audio click replacements, and glyph clicks with waits. I will add extra.prompt to the shell stamp. The prompt not redrawing bug may cause the interview count to reach 16.\n\nI will log issue 16 as not critical. The prompt kept the previous device's glyph because the shell only redraws when the menu changes; the stamp now includes the prompt.\n\nThe interview and exit-interview need updating first, followed by TESTING-LOG. page.test comes last. Rebuild can run while end-to-end tests are active.\n\nThe running end-to-end browser already loaded the old HTML, so rebuilding in parallel could starve memory and trigger earlyoom. I will edit the source files now and defer the rebuild until the browser closes.\n\nThe monitor restart will watch only for EXIT events. It will ignore the existing failure log entry to avoid an immediate exit.\n\nThe monitor script will grep for the last EXIT line and exit with success or failure. The campaign test may take up to eleven minutes, but it started after the xbox pass at the five-hundred-seventy-five second mark. It should finish within about ten more minutes. I will wait that long.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The menu walk collapsed keypresses between slow frames, and the use prompt never redrew when only the device changed. I’ll fix both while the campaign check finishes."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d02be1b9-a6c7-4175-882d-73390064a4f5-124","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/ui/shell.ts","old_string":"    p.seats,\n    extra.touch,\n    card,\n  ].join('|');","new_string":"    p.seats,\n    extra.touch,\n    extra.prompt,\n    card,\n  ].join('|');"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d02be1b9-a6c7-4175-882d-73390064a4f5-125","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md","old_string":"15. Not critical. Attract wrote `trauma-compass:gfx.governor` because the page store was also passed to `createEngine`. The night is still saved by the page. The engine is given no store, so a demo changes nothing.\n\nFifteen issues. Ten were game-breaking: 1–9 and 14. Five were not: 10–13 and 15.","new_string":"15. Not critical. Attract wrote `trauma-compass:gfx.governor` because the page store was also passed to `createEngine`. The night is still saved by the page. The engine is given no store, so a demo changes nothing.\n16. Not critical. The use prompt kept the previous device, because the shell redrew only when the menu changed. The stamp now includes the prompt.\n\nSixteen issues. Ten were game-breaking: 1–9 and 14. Six were not: 10–13, 15, and 16."}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d02be1b9-a6c7-4175-882d-73390064a4f5-126","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-22473