{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_533","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The text \"Loading…\" appears near the end of a file at position 6735359.\n\nThe module script is in the head and very large. showNeed runs before the body is parsed, so document.getElementById('msg') returns null.\n\nFirefox showed the message. This contradicts the theory that the script runs before the body. The source HTML may be inlined as a string inside the JS bundle.\n\nThe module bundle may contain the original HTML as a string constant. The actual DOM element could be earlier in the file. Firefox might have deferred script execution, or the module's error handler could call showNeed after the body exists.\n\nThe classic script in the head runs immediately and finds no #msg element. The module script is deferred, so it only executes after the document finishes parsing. main.ts does nothing if navigator.gpu is unavailable, leaving the message stuck on Loading.\n\nThe classic script at position 20849 is the first element in the file. The #msg element is at position 6.7MB. This means the classic script runs before the body exists. It should find no element. Yet Firefox displayed the message. The actual HTML structure must differ from this assumption.\n\nThe source HTML places the classic script in the head before the body. showNeed therefore always runs before #msg exists. Firefox still displayed the message. The one-file transform may have moved elements. Another script might have called showNeed again. Or the module set the text directly.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7bea8a0e-f3ff-4372-b305-9fc2ebe79be7-143","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"node --input-type=module -e '\nimport { readFileSync } from \"node:fs\";\nconst p = \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731.html\";\nconst html = readFileSync(p, \"utf8\");\nconst re = /id=.msg.|getElementById\\(.msg.\\)|<body|<\\/head>|type=.module./g;\nlet m; let n=0;\nwhile ((m = re.exec(html)) && n < 30) { console.log(m.index, JSON.stringify(m[0])); n++; }\n'","description":"Locate msg element versus scripts in the built page"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1311,"output_tokens":1103,"cache_read_input_tokens":164224,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"cd5c5ef2-7963-4875-8828-91e69ea7109f"}
