{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_541","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"extra.prompt is a source identifier that gets minified. A false value is acceptable if the stamp includes the prompt value.\n\nThe prompt string is confirmed in the source and build. The \"store,\" flag likely appears in minified code or comments, but this is harmless. Trusting the source over minified output.\n\nLaunching e2e r4. I'll monitor for exit only to avoid being woken mid-campaign. Failures can be fixed later once the browser is free.\n\nI'll modify the monitor to print FAILED on the first new failure without exiting. It will keep running until the campaign finishes, then exit. This gives two wakeups: one for the failure and one for the final status.\n\nThe monitor script will print each new failure as it appears, then exit on the final EXIT line. I'll launch the campaign and wait for up to 12 minutes.\n\nI'll use `block_until 0` for the e2e task and a 12-minute timeout for both. The monitor will stay running until the final EXIT line so the wait returns only once the campaign fully completes. I'll avoid printing intermediate failures to prevent spurious wakeups.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8dfba2df-f50d-4a13-9c80-6f2d29af0c71-157","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731 && SCRATCH=/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer && TMP=$(mktemp -d /tmp/g.XXXXXX) && echo \"$TMP\" > \"$SCRATCH/e2e-r4.tmp\" && export CHROMIUM_PATH=/home/micha/.cache/ms-playwright/chromium-1243/chrome-linux64/chrome PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE=ubuntu24.04-x64 TMPDIR=\"$TMP\" && stdbuf -oL -eL node labs/game/tools/e2e.mjs > \"$SCRATCH/e2e-r4.log\" 2> \"$SCRATCH/e2e-r4.err\"; ec=$?; echo \"EXIT:$ec\" >> \"$SCRATCH/e2e-r4.log\"; rm -rf \"$TMP\"; exit $ec","description":"Re-run page checks against the new build","block_until_ms":0}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8dfba2df-f50d-4a13-9c80-6f2d29af0c71-158","name":"monitor","input":{"command":"LOG=/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/e2e-r4.log\nseen=0\nwhile :; do\n  if [ -f \"$LOG\" ]; then\n    bad=$(grep -c '\"ok\":false' \"$LOG\" || true)\n    if [ \"$bad\" -gt \"$seen\" ]; then\n      echo \"FAILED: $(grep '\"ok\":false' \"$LOG\" | tail -n +$((seen + 1)) | tr '\\n' ' ')\"\n      seen=$bad\n    fi\n    if grep -q '^EXIT:' \"$LOG\"; then\n      line=$(grep '^EXIT:' \"$LOG\" | tail -1)\n      if [ \"$line\" = \"EXIT:0\" ]; then echo \"DONE: $line\"; exit 0; fi\n      echo \"FAILED: $line\"\n      exit 1\n    fi\n  fi\n  sleep 5\ndone","description":"Watch the new page checks","timeout_ms":900000}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":462,"output_tokens":1475,"cache_read_input_tokens":176384,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"ab7821f6-1607-4105-b81f-033dcf07dc6a"}
