{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_543","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The dev slider failed and is stuck at \"title before-1 box 0\".\n\nThe stuck state is actually the initial campaign state. Enter never advanced past the title screen.\n\nA 4-second timeout caused the test to break. Enter works from a fresh title screen but fails after Back. Focus on New Shift should allow Enter to start the shift.\n\nFocus may not have returned to row 0 after the Back click. A lingering button could be intercepting Enter and suppressing the default action. The accept handler might also be failing silently, leaving state unchanged.\n\nThe Back click may have left the pointer in a state that swallows the Enter key. The engine should still receive it if focus is on the body.\n\nThe first test pressed Enter without clicking buttons, so a dialog or focus trap is unlikely. The state check confirms the engine never fired accept. The keydown may have been consumed between the Playwright press and the next frame.\n\nThe frame loop was running, so onFrame did not stop. The Back click reached the title screen correctly. Focus resets to row 0 after cancel.\n\nPressing Enter while the Back button is removed and focus falls on New Shift may fire a click on that button instead of the title accept handler. That click would call pick('new'), startShift, and advance to the story screen.\n\nThe browser may fire a click on the focused button during keyup. That click could call act('new') synchronously before the engine processes the Enter keydown. The engine would then see uiAccept as pressed, but the story screen might already be set by the button's own handler.\n\nThe button-click theory is unlikely because the shell's keydown listener does not intercept Enter. If Enter were reaching the engine, accept() should fire and advance the story screen. The real cause of the stuck state remains unclear.\n\nThe shell keydown listener does not block Enter. A text field is not focused. The first test passed with the same modal, so the board visit may have altered focus or state. Hover sets campaign.focus via pointerover, and clicking Back resets it to row 0.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-45895ce6-66be-46d7-94ef-a2c6b7eb5bf8-160","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/input/input.ts","offset":330,"limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-45895ce6-66be-46d7-94ef-a2c6b7eb5bf8-161","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/e2e-r4.log"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":938,"output_tokens":1784,"cache_read_input_tokens":178688,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"ea5c408e-717d-4589-ac44-cd3fa205d528"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-45895ce6-66be-46d7-94ef-a2c6b7eb5bf8-160","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"330→      told.clear();\\n      const map = bindings.map;\\n      const level = (action: string) => strengths.get(action) ?? 0;\\n      const [forward, back, left, right] = map.move;\\n      const stick = Array.isArray(own.axes.move) ? (own.axes.move as number[]) : [0, 0];\\n      const axes: [number, number] = [level(right) - level(left) + stick[0], level(forward) - level(back) + stick[1]];\\n      const thumb = touch?.stick() ?? [0, 0];\\n      if (thumb[0] !== 0 || thumb[1] !== 0) [axes[0], axes[1]] = [axes[0] + thumb[0], axes[1] + thumb[1]];\\n      const yaw = typeof own.axes.cam === 'number' ? own.axes.cam : camera?.yaw();\\n      const out: Record<string, unknown> = {};\\n340→      if (axes[0] !== 0 || axes[1] !== 0) out.move = fromCamera(yaw ?? 0, axes);\\n      if (yaw !== undefined) out.cam = yaw;\\n      if (own.axes.look) out.look = own.axes.look;\\n      else if (map.look && camera && yaw !== undefined) out.look = [yaw, camera.pose?.().pitch ?? 0];\\n      if (own.axes.aim) out.aim = own.axes.aim;\\n      else if (map.aimWith !== 'none' && camera?.aim) {\\n        const at = camera.aim(map.aimWith, aimDevices());\\n        if (at?.every(Number.isFinite)) out.aim = [...at];\\n      }\\n      const buttons = bindings\\n350→        .actions()\\n        .filter((action) => !map.move.includes(action) && !map.view.includes(action))\\n        .sort();\\n      const b = buttons.filter((action) => heldNow.has(action));\\n      const p = buttons.filter((action) => pressedNow.has(action));\\n      if (b.length) out.b = b;\\n      if (p.length) out.p = p;\\n      for (const [key, action] of Object.entries(map.values)) if (level(action) > 0) out[key] = level(action);\\n      for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(own.axes)) if (key.includes(':')) out[key] = value;\\n      return out;\\n360→    },\\n    held: (action) => heldNow.has(action),\\n    pressed: (action) => pressedNow.has(action),\\n    strength: (action) => strengths.get(action) ?? 0,\\n    camera() {\\n      const twin = bindings.map.aimWith === 'pointer'; // the right stick aims (twin sticks), not the camera\\n      const stick: [number, number] = twin ? [0, 0] : pads.rightStick();\\n      const raw = { counts: mouse?.takeLook() ?? [0, 0], stick } as const;\\n      const { look, turn } = scaleLook(raw, options.look?.() ?? DEFAULT_LOOK, heldNow.has('aim'));\\n      return { look, turn, zoom: mouse?.takeZoom() ?? 0 };\\n370→    },\\n    prompt(action) {\\n      const device = last === 'gamepad' || last === 'mouse' ? last : 'keyboard';\\n      return pickLabel(codesOf(action), device, { layout: options.layout, pad: pads.style });\\n    },\\n    listen(device) {\\n      hear(null);\\n      return new Promise((resolve) => (listening = { family: device, resolve }));\\n    },\\n    clear,\",\"content_concise\":\"330→      told.clear();\\n      const map = bindings.map;\\n      const level = (action: string) => strengths.get(action) ?? 0;\\n      const [forward, back, left, right] = map.move;\\n      const stick = Array.isArray(own.axes.move) ? (own.axes.move as number[]) : [0, 0];\\n      const axes: [number, number] = [level(right) - level(left) + stick[0], level(forward) - level(back) + stick[1]];\\n      const thumb = touch?.stick() ?? [0, 0];\\n      if (thumb[0] !== 0 || thumb[1] !== 0) [axes[0], axes[1]] = [axes[0] + thumb[0], axes[1] + thumb[1]];\\n      const yaw = typeof own.axes.cam === 'number' ? own.axes.cam : camera?.yaw();\\n      const out: Record<string, unknown> = {};\\n340→      if (axes[0] !== 0 || axes[1] !== 0) out.move = fromCamera(yaw ?? 0, axes);\\n      if (yaw !== undefined) out.cam = yaw;\\n      if (own.axes.look) out.look = own.axes.look;\\n      else if (map.look && camera && yaw !== undefined) out.look = [yaw, camera.pose?.().pitch ?? 0];\\n      if (own.axes.aim) out.aim = own.axes.aim;\\n      else if (map.aimWith !== 'none' && camera?.aim) {\\n        const at = camera.aim(map.aimWith, aimDevices());\\n        if (at?.every(Number.isFinite)) out.aim = [...at];\\n      }\\n      const buttons = bindings\\n350→        .actions()\\n        .filter((action) => !map.move.includes(action) && !map.view.includes(action))\\n        .sort();\\n      const b = buttons.filter((action) => heldNow.has(action));\\n      const p = buttons.filter((action) => pressedNow.has(action));\\n      if (b.length) out.b = b;\\n      if (p.length) out.p = p;\\n      for (const [key, action] of Object.entries(map.values)) if (level(action) > 0) out[key] = level(action);\\n      for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(own.axes)) if (key.includes(':')) out[key] = value;\\n      return out;\\n360→    },\\n    held: (action) => heldNow.has(action),\\n    pressed: (action) => pressedNow.has(action),\\n    strength: (action) => strengths.get(action) ?? 0,\\n    camera() {\\n      const twin = bindings.map.aimWith === 'pointer'; // the right stick aims (twin sticks), not the camera\\n      const stick: [number, number] = twin ? [0, 0] : pads.rightStick();\\n      const raw = { counts: mouse?.takeLook() ?? [0, 0], stick } as const;\\n      const { look, turn } = scaleLook(raw, options.look?.() ?? DEFAULT_LOOK, heldNow.has('aim'));\\n      return { look, turn, zoom: mouse?.takeZoom() ?? 0 };\\n370→    },\\n    prompt(action) {\\n      const device = last === 'gamepad' || last === 'mouse' ? last : 'keyboard';\\n      return pickLabel(codesOf(action), device, { layout: options.layout, pad: pads.style });\\n    },\\n    listen(device) {\\n      hear(null);\\n      return new Promise((resolve) => (listening = { family: device, resolve }));\\n    },\\n    clear,\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/e