{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_547","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A Playwright focused button issue appears to be interacting with the shell.\n\nThe Back button is destroyed by the shell re-render. Focus lands on a detached node. Playwright's keyboard.press sends Enter to that detached element. The window never receives the event.\n\nThe first test presses Enter without clicking a button. The glyph test presses ArrowDown without focus and succeeds. The dev path clicks a button before Enter, which is when the key disappears.\n\nThe fix is to blur the active element before pressing Enter.\n\nThe fix is to blur the active element and refocus the window before pressing Enter. Clicking a canvas corner is another way to move focus away from a destroyed button. After an initial blur, keyboard navigation stays on the body because story screens have no buttons. The Dev Mode click and ArrowRight tab are unaffected.\n\nArrowRight will reach the window because the button still exists during the keydown event. Escape works from the op screen since no button is focused. The blur will be added before the Enter loop.\n\nThe blur will run before every Enter press inside the loop. No rebuild is needed because only tests are changing. The story test does not need this fix.\n\nThe current e2e run should pass webkit because the HTML was rebuilt with DOMContentLoaded. The dev slider failure remains. Campaign may pass again. A second e2e run is needed to verify the dev slider fix. That run takes about ten minutes.\n\nI will wait for the current e2e run to finish before deciding on the next steps. I am considering skipping a separate e2e rerun and going straight to verify, since verify.mjs may run e2e internally and stop on failure. I need to check verify.mjs to confirm this behavior.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-38f26add-b233-40e4-b2fc-e4c07a4490ae-165","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/tools/verify.mjs","limit":120}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3162,"output_tokens":1091,"cache_read_input_tokens":184320,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"a7300f9f-c565-4a7f-b04a-f13471fec5ec"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-38f26add-b233-40e4-b2fc-e4c07a4490ae-165","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The one command, `npm run verify`: runs every check quietly and prints only the failures, then one line with\\n * the count. `--fast` skips what needs a browser. It sets its own short TMPDIR and CHROMIUM_PATH, so it needs no setup,\\n * and removes the temporary folder when done. Exit 0 when nothing failed.\\n */\\nimport { spawnSync } from 'node:child_process';\\nimport { existsSync, globSync, mkdtempSync, readFileSync, rmSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport { homedir } from 'node:os';\\n\\n10→const fast = process.argv.includes('--fast');\\nconst tmp = mkdtempSync('/tmp/g.');\\nconst chrome = globSync(`${homedir()}/.cache/ms-playwright/chromium-*/chrome-linux64/chrome`)[0];\\nconst env = { ...process.env, TMPDIR: tmp, CHROMIUM_PATH: process.env.CHROMIUM_PATH ?? chrome };\\nconst run = (command, ...args) => spawnSync(command, args, { env, encoding: 'utf8', maxBuffer: 2 ** 28 });\\n\\nlet passed = 0;\\nconst failed = [];\\nconst note = (name, ok, detail = '') => (ok ? (passed += 1) : failed.push(`${name}${detail ? `: ${detail}` : ''}`));\\nconst tail = (result) => `${result.stdout}${result.stderr}`.trim().split('\\\\n').slice(-6).join(' | ').slice(0, 600);\\n20→\\n/** A step whose exit status is its verdict. */\\nconst step = (name, command, ...args) => {\\n  const result = run(command, ...args);\\n  note(name, result.status === 0, tail(result));\\n};\\n\\n/** Vitest, counted test by test from the JSON report npm test writes. */\\nfunction tests() {\\n  const report = 'out/test/report.json';\\n30→  rmSync(report, { force: true });\\n  const result = run('npm', 'test', '--silent');\\n  if (!existsSync(report)) return note('npm test', false, tail(result));\\n  for (const file of JSON.parse(readFileSync(report, 'utf8')).testResults) {\\n    for (const test of file.assertionResults) {\\n      note(\\n        test.fullName,\\n        test.status === 'passed',\\n        String(test.failureMessages?.[0] ?? '')\\n          .split('\\\\n')[0]\\n40→          .slice(0, 300),\\n      );\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** A browser tool: it prints one JSON line per check, { name, ok, detail }. Add e2e and hub runs here. */\\nfunction browserTool(path) {\\n  const result = run('node', path);\\n  const lines = result.stdout.split('\\\\n').filter((line) => line.startsWith('{'));\\n50→  for (const line of lines) {\\n    const { name, ok, detail } = JSON.parse(line);\\n    note(name, ok, detail);\\n  }\\n  if (result.status !== 0 || lines.length === 0) note(path, false, tail(result));\\n}\\n\\nstep('npm run check', 'npm', 'run', '--silent', 'check');\\ntests();\\nif (!fast) {\\n60→  step('replays in Chromium', 'node', 'x', 'replay', 'labs/game/replays', '--browser', 'sim');\\n  for (const path of ['labs/game/tools/e2e.mjs', 'labs/game/tools/hub.mjs']) if (existsSync(path)) browserTool(path);\\n}\\nrmSync(tmp, { recursive: true, force: true });\\nfor (const failure of failed) console.log(`FAIL ${failure}`);\\nconsole.log(`verify: ${passed} passed, ${failed.length} failed`);\\nprocess.exit(failed.length ? 1 : 0);\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The one command, `npm run verify`: runs every check quietly and prints only the failures, then one line with\\n * the count. `--fast` skips what needs a browser. It sets its own short TMPDIR and CHROMIUM_PATH, so it needs no setup,\\n * and removes the temporary folder when done. Exit 0 when nothing failed.\\n */\\nimport { spawnSync } from 'node:child_process';\\nimport { existsSync, globSync, mkdtempSync, readFileSync, rmSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport { homedir } from 'node:os';\\n\\n10→const fast = process.argv.includes('--fast');\\nconst tmp = mkdtempSync('/tmp/g.');\\nconst chrome = globSync(`${homedir()}/.cache/ms-playwright/chromium-*/chrome-linux64/chrome`)[0];\\nconst env = { ...process.env, TMPDIR: tmp, CHROMIUM_PATH: process.env.CHROMIUM_PATH ?? chrome };\\nconst run = (command, ...args) => spawnSync(command, args, { env, encoding: 'utf8', maxBuffer: 2 ** 28 });\\n\\nlet passed = 0;\\nconst failed = [];\\nconst note = (name, ok, detail = '') => (ok ? (passed += 1) : failed.push(`${name}${detail ? `: ${detail}` : ''}`));\\nconst tail = (result) => `${result.stdout}${result.stderr}`.trim().split('\\\\n').slice(-6).join(' | ').slice(0, 600);\\n20→\\n/** A step whose exit status is its verdict. */\\nconst step = (name, command, ...args) => {\\n  const result = run(command, ...args);\\n  note(name, result.status === 0, tail(result));\\n};\\n\\n/** Vitest, counted test by test from the JSON report npm test writes. */\\nfunction tests() {\\n  const report = 'out/test/report.json';\\n30→  rmSync(report, { force: true });\\n  const result = run('npm', 'test', '--silent');\\n  if (!existsSync(report)) return note('npm test', false, tail(result));\\n  for (const file of JSON.parse(readFileSync(report, 'utf8')).testResults) {\\n    for (const test of file.assertionResults) {\\n      note(\\n        test.fullName,\\n        test.status === 'passed',\\n        String(test.failureMessages?.[0] ?? '')\\n          .split('\\\\n')[0]\\n40→          .slice(0, 300),\\n      );\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** A browser tool: it prints one JSON line per check, { name, ok, detail }. Add e2e and hub runs here. */\\nfunction browserTool(path) {\\n  const result = run('node', path);\\n  const lines = result.stdout.split('\\\\n').filter((line) => line.startsWith('{'));\\n50→  for (const line of lines) {\\n    const { name, ok, detail } = JSON.parse(line);\\n    note(name, ok, detail);\\n  }\\n  if (result.status !== 0 || lines.length === 0) note(path, false, tail(result));\\n}\\n\\nstep('npm run check', 'npm', 'run', '--silent', 'check');\\ntests();\\nif (!fast) {\\n60→  step('replays in Chromium', 'node', 'x', 'replay', 'labs/game/replays', '--browser', 'sim');\\n  for (const path of ['labs/game/tools/e2e.mjs', 'labs/game/tools/hub.mjs']) if (existsSync(path)) browserTool(path);\\n}\\nrmSync(tmp, { recursive: true, force: true });\\nfor (const failure of failed) console.log(`FAIL ${failure}`);\\nconsole.log(`verify: ${passed} passed, ${failed.length} failed`);\\nprocess.exit(failed.length ? 1 : 0);\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/tools/verify.mjs\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":120,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file The one command, `npm run verify`: runs every check quietly and prints only the failures, then one line with\\n * the count. `--fast` skips what needs a browser. It sets its own short TMPDIR and CHROMIUM_PATH, so it needs no setup,\\n * and removes the temporary folder when done. Exit 0 when nothing failed.\\n */\\nimport { spawnSync } from 'node:child_process';\\nimport { existsSync, globSync, mkdtempSync, readFileSync, rmSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport { homedir } from 'node:os';\\n\\nconst fast = process.argv.includes('--fast');\\nconst tmp = mkdtempSync('/tmp/g.');\\nconst chrome = globSync(`${homedir()}/.cache/ms-playwright/chromium-*/chrome-linux64/chrome`)[0];\\nconst env = { ...process.env, TMPDIR: tmp, CHROMIUM_PATH: process.env.CHROMIUM_PATH ?? chrome };\\nconst run = (command, ...args) => spawnSync(command, args, { env, encoding: 'utf8', maxBuffer: 2 ** 28 });\\n\\nlet passed = 0;\\nconst failed = [];\\nconst note = (name, ok, detail = '') => (ok ? (passed += 1) : failed.push(`${name}${detail ? `: ${detail}` : ''}`));\\nconst tail = (result) => `${result.stdout}${result.stderr}`.trim().split('\\\\n').slice(-6).join(' | ').slice(0, 600);\\n\\n/** A step whose exit status is its verdict. */\\nconst step = (name, command, ...args) => {\\n  const result = run(command, ...args);\\n  note(name, result.status === 0, tail(result));\\n};\\n\\n/** Vitest, counted test by test from the JSON report npm test writes. */\\nfunction tests() {\\n  const report = 'out/test/report.json';\\n  rmSync(report, { force: true });\\n  const result = run('npm', 'test', '--silent');\\n  if (!existsSync(report)) return note('npm test', false, tail(result));\\n  for (const file of JSON.parse(readFileSync(report, 'utf8')).testResults) {\\n    for (const test of file.assertionResults) {\\n      note(\\n        test.fullName,\\n        test.status === 'passed',\\n        String(test.failureMessages?.[0] ?? '')\\n          .split('\\\\n')[0]\\n          .slice(0, 300),\\n      );\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** A browser tool: it prints one JSON line per check, { name, ok, detail }. Add e2e and hub runs here. */\\nfunction browserTool(path) {\\n  const result = run('node', path);\\n  const lines = result.stdout.split('\\\\n').filter((line) => line.startsWith('{'));\\n  for (const line of lines) {\\n    const { name, ok, detail } = JSON.parse(line);\\n    note(name, ok, detail);\\n  }\\n  if (result.status !== 0 || lines.length === 0) note(path, false, tail(result));\\n}\\n\\nstep('npm run check', 'npm', 'run', '--silent', 'check');\\ntests();\\nif (!fast) {\\n  step('replays in Chromium', 'node', 'x', 'replay', 'labs/game/replays', '--browser', 'sim');\\n  for (const path of ['labs/game/tools/e2e.mjs', 'labs/game/tools/hub.mjs']) if (existsSync(path)) browserTool(path);\\n}\\nrmSync(tmp, { recursive: true, force: true });\\nfor (const failure of failed) console.log(`FAIL ${failure}`);\\nconsole.log(`verify: ${passed} passed, ${failed.length} failed`);\\nprocess.exit(failed.length ? 1 : 0);\\n\",\"total_lines\":66}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"0b549dc4-7be9-48e3-bc60-35fb17497f9d"}
