} ${row.value}<input type=\\\"range\\\" data-set=\\\"${esc(row.setting)}\\\" min=\\\"${tune.min}\\\" max=\\\"${tune.max}\\\" step=\\\"${tune.step}\\\" value=\\\"${row.value}\\\" /></label>`;\\n    })\\n    .join('');\\n}\\n\\n/** Dev panels that are not plain rows. */\\nfunction devExtra(c: Campaign, extra: ShellExtra): string {\\n110→  if (c.devTab === 1) return sliders(extra);\\n  if (c.devTab === 3) return `<p data-game=\\\"cursor\\\">${esc(extra.cursor)}</p>`;\\n  if (c.devTab === 4) return `<p data-game=\\\"hash\\\">${esc(extra.hash)}</p>`;\\n  return '';\\n}\\n\\n/** The body of the open screen. */\\nfunction cardBlock(extra: ShellExtra): string {\\n  const card = extra.card;\\n  if (!card) return '';\",\"content_concise\":\"90→      (on, index) =>\\n        `<p class=\\\"seat${on ? ' is-on' : ''}\\\" data-game=\\\"seat\\\">${on ? `Seat ${index + 1} claimed` : `Seat ${index + 1}`}</p>`,\\n    )\\n    .join('');\\n  return `<div class=\\\"seats\\\" data-game=\\\"scrub\\\">${seats}</div>`;\\n}\\n\\n/** Balance sliders. The value is the live setting. */\\nfunction sliders(extra: ShellExtra): string {\\n  return extra.sliders\\n100→    .map((row) => {\\n      const tune = TUNE.find((item) => item.setting === row.setting);\\n      if (!tune) return '';\\n      return `<label class=\\\"slider\\\">${esc(row.label)} ${row.value}<input type=\\\"range\\\" data-set=\\\"${esc(row.setting)}\\\" min=\\\"${tune.min}\\\" max=\\\"${tune.max}\\\" step=\\\"${tune.step}\\\" value=\\\"${row.value}\\\" /></label>`;\\n    })\\n    .join('');\\n}\\n\\n/** Dev panels that are not plain rows. */\\nfunction devExtra(c: Campaign, extra: ShellExtra): string {\\n110→  if (c.devTab === 1) return sliders(extra);\\n  if (c.devTab === 3) return `<p data-game=\\\"cursor\\\">${esc(extra.cursor)}</p>`;\\n  if (c.devTab === 4) return `<p data-game=\\\"hash\\\">${esc(extra.hash)}</p>`;\\n  return '';\\n}\\n\\n/** The body of the open screen. */\\nfunction cardBlock(extra: ShellExtra): string {\\n  const card = extra.card;\\n  if (!card) return '';\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/ui/shell.ts\",\"offset\":90,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"      (on, index) =>\\n        `<p class=\\\"seat${on ? ' is-on' : ''}\\\" data-game=\\\"seat\\\">${on ? `Seat ${index + 1} claimed` : `Seat ${index + 1}`}</p>`,\\n    )\\n    .join('');\\n  return `<div class=\\\"seats\\\" data-game=\\\"scrub\\\">${seats}</div>`;\\n}\\n\\n/** Balance sliders. The value is the live setting. */\\nfunction sliders(extra: ShellExtra): string {\\n  return extra.sliders\\n    .map((row) => {\\n      const tune = TUNE.find((item) => item.setting === row.setting);\\n      if (!tune) return '';\\n      return `<label class=\\\"slider\\\">${esc(row.label)} ${row.value}<input type=\\\"range\\\" data-set=\\\"${esc(row.setting)}\\\" min=\\\"${tune.min}\\\" max=\\\"${tune.max}\\\" step=\\\"${tune.step}\\\" value=\\\"${row.value}\\\" /></label>`;\\n    })\\n    .join('');\\n}\\n\\n/** Dev panels that are not plain rows. */\\nfunction devExtra(c: Campaign, extra: ShellExtra): string {\\n  if (c.devTab === 1) return sliders(extra);\\n  if (c.devTab === 3) return `<p data-game=\\\"cursor\\\">${esc(extra.cursor)}</p>`;\\n  if (c.devTab === 4) return `<p data-game=\\\"hash\\\">${esc(extra.hash)}</p>`;\\n  return '';\\n}\\n\\n/** The body of the open screen. */\\nfunction cardBlock(extra: ShellExtra): string {\\n  const card = extra.card;\\n  if (!card) return '';\\n\",\"total_lines\":197}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"13c9d412-fe58-4aca-aa5c-2fe414566955"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_556","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The layout requires roughly 1152 pixels for 18 sliders, plus space for the heading and reset button.\n\nThe reset button sits below all sliders, so it is unreachable on 720p screens. The menu is appended after the body content.\n\nThe fix is to make `.screen` scrollable with `overflow: auto`. This lets the player reach the reset button. Playwright should then be able to click it.\n\nThe body is overflow-hidden, so scrollIntoView cannot bring the reset button into view. Making `.screen` the scroll container with a bounded height fixes this. Playwright's scrollIntoView will then scroll inside `.screen`, and the button becomes visible for clicking.\n\nThe plan is controller-first. A pad user on the balance tab sees only Reset and Back as menu rows. Sliders are not menu rows, so a pad cannot change them directly. The test fills sliders with mouse input and clicks Reset. If Reset is off-screen, mouse users cannot reach it either. Pad users might still focus the Reset row and press accept even when it is visually hidden.\n\nA pad can trigger Reset by pressing accept while the row is focused, even if the button is off-screen. A mouse user cannot reach it without scrolling.\n\nPlacing the menu before the sliders for the dev balance tab would keep Reset always visible. This avoids scrolling and is cleaner for both tests and players.\n\nThe simplest CSS fix is adding `overflow: auto` and `pointer-events: auto` to `.screen`. This lets the panel scroll so the reset button becomes reachable. The screen only covers the center 6vw margins, so canvas corners still receive clicks. Empty gaps inside the panel will capture clicks, but that is acceptable.\n\nSetting `.screen` to `pointer-events: auto` would let clicks on the story text area reach the screen instead of the canvas. The op and attract screens have empty bodies, but the absolutely positioned `.screen` div still covers a large area and could block the center field.\n\nA blanket `pointer-events: auto` on `.screen` would block the center of the operation screen. The fix is a `.can-scroll` class that applies only to overflowed dev panels. This keeps the screen non-interactive outside its content area while still allowing Playwright to scroll the reset button into view.\n\nThe `can-scroll` class will be applied only to the dev screen. Settings and about pages are short enough to avoid overflow, so they do not need it.\n\nThe `.can-scroll` class will be added to the shell markup. It is derived from the screen state, so entering dev mode automatically triggers a redraw with the new class. The CSS change must be rebuilt into `index.html` before the next end-to-end test, since the test suite runs against the inlined HTML.\n\nThe test loop breaks correctly when the place is `op`. The probe loop was not the issue. The off-screen reset button is a real bug. It will be logged as issue 18. The interview update is tedious but honest.\n\nThe 720p viewport is a real size, so the off-screen reset button is a genuine bug and not merely a test artifact. The dev-probe.mjs file will be deleted once the end-to-end tests cover the dev screen.\n\nA quick probe run will test the fix before the full end-to-end suite. This avoids losing the check and test time if the reset button remains unreachable. The probe will be updated to match the new layout and rerun first.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-65f6fbec-7bed-414b-a904-feb11c36dccb-177","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/ui/shell.ts","offset":185,"limit":20}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2115,"output_tokens":2055,"cache_read_input_tokens":196480,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"19a134cc-aeb8-402f-8f62-2ed063ffd114"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-65f6fbec-7bed-414b-a904-feb11c36dccb-177","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"185→    card,\\n  ].join('|');\\n}\\n\\n/** Draw the screens into `root`. Returns the stamp it drew. */\\n190→export function renderShell(root: HTMLElement, c: Campaign, extra: ShellExtra): void {\\n  const touch = extra.touch\\n    ? `<div class=\\\"touch\\\" data-game=\\\"touch\\\"><p>Controller or keyboard required</p><button type=\\\"button\\\" class=\\\"row\\\" data-act=\\\"settings\\\">Settings</button></div>`\\n    : '';\\n  const menu = items(c).length ? `<div class=\\\"menu\\\" data-game=\\\"menu\\\">${rows(c)}</div>` : '';\\n  const prompt = c.screen === 'op' || c.screen === 'pause' ? '' : `<p class=\\\"prompt\\\">${extra.prompt}</p>`;\\n  root.innerHTML = `<div class=\\\"screen\\\" data-game=\\\"screen\\\" data-screen=\\\"${esc(c.screen)}\\\">${body(c, extra)}${menu}${prompt}</div>${touch}<p data-about=\\\"usage\\\" class=\\\"usage\\\">added on import</p>`;\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"185→    card,\\n  ].join('|');\\n}\\n\\n/** Draw the screens into `root`. Returns the stamp it drew. */\\n190→export function renderShell(root: HTMLElement, c: Campaign, extra: ShellExtra): void {\\n  const touch = extra.touch\\n    ? `<div class=\\\"touch\\\" data-game=\\\"touch\\\"><p>Controller or keyboard required</p><button type=\\\"button\\\" class=\\\"row\\\" data-act=\\\"settings\\\">Settings</button></div>`\\n    : '';\\n  const menu = items(c).length ? `<div class=\\\"menu\\\" data-game=\\\"menu\\\">${rows(c)}</div>` : '';\\n  const prompt = c.screen === 'op' || c.screen === 'pause' ? '' : `<p class=\\\"prompt\\\">${extra.prompt}</p>`;\\n  root.innerHTML = `<div class=\\\"screen\\\" data-game=\\\"screen\\\" data-screen=\\\"${esc(c.screen)}\\\">${body(c, extra)}${menu}${prompt}</div>${touch}<p data-about=\\\"usage\\\" class=\\\"usage\\\">added on import</p>`;\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/ui/shell.ts\",\"offset\":185,\"limit\":20,\"raw_output\":\"    card,\\n  ].join('|');\\n}\\n\\n/** Draw the screens into `root`. Returns the stamp it drew. */\\nexport function renderShell(root: HTMLElement, c: Campaign, extra: ShellExtra): void {\\n  const touch = extra.touch\\n    ? `<div class=\\\"touch\\\" data-game=\\\"touch\\\"><p>Controller or keyboard required</p><button type=\\\"button\\\" class=\\\"row\\\" data-act=\\\"settings\\\">Settings</button></div>`\\n    : '';\\n  const menu = items(c).length ? `<div class=\\\"menu\\\" data-game=\\\"menu\\\">${rows(c)}</div>` : '';\\n  const prompt = c.screen === 'op' || c.screen === 'pause' ? '' : `<p class=\\\"prompt\\\">${extra.prompt}</p>`;\\n  root.innerHTML = `<div class=\\\"screen\\\" data-game=\\\"screen\\\" data-screen=\\\"${esc(c.screen)}\\\">${body(c, extra)}${menu}${prompt}</div>${touch}<p data-about=\\\"usage\\\" class=\\\"usage\\\">added on import</p>`;\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":197}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"1d3d80e6-5b19-4261-b130-745982d83073"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_557","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The dev balance tab will be reorganized so the Reset menu sits above the sliders and remains visible at the top. The dev screen will also be made scrollable to ensure all sliders remain reachable.\n\nThe dev screen will be restructured so the title stays at the top, with the Reset menu placed between the heading and the sliders.\n\nCSS scroll is the primary fix. The Reset menu will be placed before the dev sliders so it appears in the first screenful. If Playwright still reports the button as outside the viewport, the menu will be moved above the title instead.\n\nThe CSS will use `bottom: 4vh` and `overflow: auto` on `.screen.can-scroll` to create a bounded scrollable area. The probe script will be kept until the fix is confirmed, then deleted. I am also checking whether `pointer-events: none` on `#shell` might interfere with `scrollIntoView`.\n\n`scrollIntoView` ignores `pointer-events`, so that is not the blocker. The real issue was the missing scroll ancestor; the bounded `.screen.can-scroll` container will fix it. I will also set `pointer-events: auto` on that element so wheel scrolling works for a real user. Next, I will implement the change, update the interview log to eighteen, rebuild, and probe.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c2bdf5ac-85cc-4b3c-b497-67912e8a36f6-178","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/index.html","old_string":"      .screen { position: absolute; left: 6vw; right: 6vw; top: 8vh; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px; max-width: 1100px; }","new_string":"      .screen { position: absolute; left: 6vw; right: 6vw; top: 8vh; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px; max-width: 1100px; }\n      .screen.can-scroll { bottom: 4vh; overflow: auto; pointer-events: auto; }"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c2bdf5ac-85cc-4b3c-b497-67912e8a36f6-179","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/ui/shell.ts","old_string":"  const menu = items(c).length ? `<div class=\"menu\" data-game=\"menu\">${rows(c)}</div>` : '';\n  const prompt = c.screen === 'op' || c.screen === 'pause' ? '' : `<p class=\"prompt\">${extra.prompt}</p>`;\n  root.innerHTML = `<div class=\"screen\" data-game=\"screen\" data-screen=\"${esc(c.screen)}\">${body(c, extra)}${menu}${prompt}</div>${touch}<p data-about=\"usage\" class=\"usage\">added on import</p>`;","new_string":"  const menu = items(c).length ? `<div class=\"menu\" data-game=\"menu\">${rows(c)}</div>` : '';\n  const prompt = c.screen === 'op' || c.screen === 'pause' ? '' : `<p class=\"prompt\">${extra.prompt}</p>`;\n  const scroll = c.screen === 'dev' ? ' can-scroll' : '';\n  const block = c.screen === 'dev' ? `${menu}${body(c, extra)}` : `${body(c, extra)}${menu}`;\n  root.innerHTML = `<div class=\"screen${scroll}\" data-game=\"screen\" data-screen=\"${esc(c.screen)}\">${block}${prompt}</div>${touch}<p data-about=\"usage\" class=\"usage\">added on import</p>`;"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c2bdf5ac-85cc-4b3c-b497-67912e8a36f6-180","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md","old_string":"17. Not critical. The WebGPU sentence ran before `#msg` existed, so a browser that did not throw stayed on \"Loading…\". It is shown again on `DOMContentLoaded`, when the line is in the page.\n\nSeventeen issues. Ten were game-breaking: 1–9 and 14. Seven were not: 10–13 and 15–17.","new_string":"17. Not critical. The WebGPU sentence ran before `#msg` existed, so a browser that did not throw stayed on \"Loading…\". It is shown again on `DOMContentLoaded`, when the line is in the page.\n18. Not critical. Balance reset sat past the bottom of a 720p screen and the page did not scroll, so a click could not reach it. The dev screen scrolls, and Reset is the first row.\n\nEighteen issues. Ten were game-breaking: 1–9 and 14. Eight were not: 10–13 and 15–18."}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c2bdf5ac-85cc-4b3c-b497-67912e8a36f6-181","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/data/interview.ts","old_string":"    'Seventeen issues were caught and written in labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md.',","new_string":"    'Eighteen issues were caught and written in labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md.',"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c2bdf5ac-85cc-4b3c-b497-67912e8a36f6-182","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/exit-interview.json","old_string":"    \"Seventeen issues were caught and written in labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md.\",","new_string":"    \"Eighteen issues were caught and written in labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md.\","}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c2bdf5ac-85cc-4b3c-b497-67912e8a36f6-183","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/tools/dev-probe.mjs","old_string":"  console.log(i, moved, place);\n  if (!moved && !place.startsWith('op')) break;\n}","new_string":"  console.log(i, moved, place);\n  if (!moved || place.startsWith('op')) break;\n}"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2366,"output_tokens":2318,"cache_read_input_tokens":198528,"cache_cre