{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_561","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The `ls` command for dev-probe and HTML returned no output, suggesting it failed early.\n\nThe shell starts in the workspace folder, not the package, so the probe path was invalid. I will check the current directory, delete the probe, verify the fix in e2e.mjs, and launch end-to-end tests carefully to avoid overlapping with other running browsers.\n\nThree other agents already run chrome-headless-shell processes. Launching another full end-to-end test risks OOM-killing. I will check memory first and retry if needed.\n\nI will check the HTML size and memory before launching. I will verify the New Shift path in e2e.mjs. The end-to-end test takes roughly 10 to 15 minutes. I will run it in the background and monitor its log for failures or completion.\n\nI will start the end-to-end test in the background and run a monitor that wakes only on `ok:false` or `EXIT:`. I am also checking whether to run verify directly instead of re-running e2e and hub.\n\nThe probe already confirmed the specific failure. Running the full end-to-end suite would duplicate work because verify also runs e2e. I will skip the redundant full run and proceed directly to verify.\n\nI am reconsidering the shortcut to verify. If e2e fails during that step, I would waste check, vitest, and replay cycles. Running e2e first first lets me prepare hub knowledge and read the verify script while it runs. If it passes, verify can proceed without duplicating the browser test.\n\nI will delete the probe and start end-to-end tests immediately. While they run, I will read hub code and interview requirements to prepare for fixes. After a green end-to-end result, I will run hub, then verify. The full verify suite repeats the browser test, so I am weighing whether to trust the probe and skip that duplicate step.\n\nThe end-to-end script now clicks Back and waits for the title screen before selecting New Shift, fixing the previous Enter-detached-button failure. I will run end-to-end tests first to avoid a long verify suite failing at the end. I can read hub code in parallel without launching another browser.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-77efaccb-fd76-4061-b9be-aac9c13594b8-3","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"PKG=\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731\"\nHTML=\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731.html\"\nls -la \"$PKG/labs/game/tools/dev-probe.mjs\" \"$HTML\"\necho \"--- mem ---\"\nfree -h\necho \"--- my chrome? ---\"\npgrep -af 'Trauma-Compass|grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731' | head -10 || true\necho \"--- e2e snippet ---\"\nrg -n \"New Shift|activeElement|Reset sliders|can-scroll\" \"$PKG/labs/game/tools/e2e.mjs\" | head -40","description":"Confirm probe, memory, and e2e walk"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":9791,"output_tokens":1581,"cache_read_input_tokens":31232,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"5da69b40-99f9-4bb5-b065-22e07f256d78"}
