{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_563","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The grep for \"Eighteen issues\" and \"added on import\" returned no matches in the first three results. The output may have been truncated by a head limit.\n\nThe three matches were lines 511, 565, and 2021. The long line at 2021 is minified JavaScript that was truncated. The target strings likely appear inside that single line.\n\nThe HTML file is 1040 bytes larger than the previous version. It was built at 02:03, but a source file was modified at 02:02, so the HTML may be stale. I will check with find -newer to confirm.\n\nI will delete the probe file before e2e to avoid leaving throwaway artifacts. I am launching the end-to-end suite in the background and monitoring its log for failures or exit codes.\n\nThe monitor will print FAILED immediately upon the first `\"ok\": false` line. The end-to-end process continues running so all failures are captured, but the monitor exits right away to avoid blocking on the final EXIT line.\n\nThe monitor will wake on the first `\"ok\": false` line so I can investigate immediately, then continue watching until the final EXIT line to report DONE or FAILED. I am writing a bash script that stays silent until either event occurs.\n\nThe monitor script polls the log every 15 seconds. It prints ACTION_REQUIRED on the first `\"ok\":false` line and exits immediately. It prints DONE or FAILED once it sees the final EXIT line. The shell wrapper will append that EXIT line itself.\n\nThe wrapper script sets a temporary directory for Chromium sockets, runs the e2e tool, appends the exit code to the log, and removes the temp folder. If the process is killed before it exits normally, the temporary directory may be left behind, so I will record its path in a file for cleanup.\n\nThe monitor script will be placed in scratch rather than ~/.grok, since this is a session-specific task. The temporary directory path will also be recorded in scratch. The e2e tool must run from the package directory so Playwright resolves correctly.\n\nThe monitor will poll every 10 seconds instead of 15 to catch early failures faster. I am checking whether any previous e2e node process is still running.\n\nNo Chrome process is running. I will verify the HTML contains the expected strings with ripgrep before launching the end-to-end suite, since the file is only 6.8 MB. I will also confirm that session.js is the first script tag in the document.\n\nI will read hub.mjs and live.ts in parallel while the end-to-end suite runs, so I can fix any failures immediately if they occur.\n\nI will read the PLAN verification section and TASK.md hand-ins in parallel with launching the end-to-end suite. The probe deletion and e2e start can be batched sequentially in one shell.\n\nThe wrapper script will use `block_until_ms=0` to run the end-to-end suite in the background. It will write its own EXIT line and avoid shell backgrounding operators. The temporary directory path will be recorded in scratch for cleanup.\n\nI am checking whether Python Playwright is available for the Firefox and WebKit tests, since e2e.mjs spawns Python. I will read the end of that file in parallel with the other tasks.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-342ded05-a5b5-4c9a-a0bf-c082ede4453d-7","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"PKG=\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731\"\nHTML=\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731.html\"\nSCRATCH=\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer\"\nrm -f \"$PKG/labs/game/tools/dev-probe.mjs\"\npython3 - <<'PY'\nhtml=open(\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.