{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_578","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The session sets game.run via search string at engine creation and campaign.\n\nThe op scene flow looks correct. The card modal may block uiAccept during op when a card is active.\n\nThe modal likely blocks gameplay actions but still allows UI actions so the card can use uiAccept. When a card is active, menus returns early after answering. The game must call ready() automatically before the card asks for a key press.\n\nready() is the loaded signal, separate from answering the card. The harness waits for all players to be ready before optionally pressing Enter for a card. The game calls hub.ready() once the engine step exists, which should fire within 20 seconds even with WebGPU warmup.\n\n__engine.step is assigned after the 10-12 second warmup. The wait loop blocks until step exists, so ready() naturally waits for warmup to finish. The 20-second timeout covers this delay.\n\nA race condition exists between the harness pressing Enter and the card handler setting session.card. If Enter arrives before the card is active, menus() ignores it because the op screen branch returns early without pause.\n\nThe harness waits for cardSent before pressing Enter. This should prevent the missed-answer race, since the game's on('card') handler fires the same event that sets cardSent.\n\nThe game registers its card handler in start() before ready() is called. Events queue until the first handler, so the card event should be captured. The wait().then block pauses and seeds the engine before ready() fires.\n\nThe hub path appears sound. I will wait for the e2e monitor before running the hub. I have finished the prep and will end this turn if no non-browser tasks remain.\n\nPreparing a launch evidence script is non-browser work. I will check the interview schema in TASK.md and PROGRESS.md to determine what the script must capture. The plan requires launching HTML from file:// twice sequentially.\n\nEach launch run must be captured as a separate folder with logs, state snapshots, and screenshots. The script will verify zero page errors, engine readiness, correct canvas pixel size, and substantial title or operating field content. It will also inject a stub pad or key and assert real visual change. The verifier will re-check these folders after e2e completes. Step 6 uses the e2e output directly for ux.log. Step 8 extracts Firefox and WebKit lines from the e2e log for nowebgpu.log.\n\nI will run the sim, bot, and content vitest suites separately to capture their logs. These tests run in Node without a browser, so they can execute after e2e completes or as part of verify.log.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-167580c5-0443-4002-ae1b-6199bdd534b9-35","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"shot\\(","glob":"**/*.{ts,md}","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/docs","head_limit":20}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-167580c5-0443-4002-ae1b-6199bdd534b9-36","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"__engine|shot|readback|pixels","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/tools/e2e.mjs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-167580c5-0443-4002-ae1b-6199bdd534b9-37","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/TASK.md","offset":90,"limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2121,"output_tokens":1823,"cache_read_input_tokens":76928,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"883b97c5-afc5-4edc-9b8b-261fc6a38ff5"}
