{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_587","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The engine sizes the canvas. The launch check requires the canvas pixel size to match the requested size.\n\nViewport will be 1280x720. Canvas dimensions will be checked against viewport times DPR. The launch script will be written to scratch and deferred until end-to-end tests finish. Thumbnail coverage will be measured by counting non-background pixels in the base64 image.\n\nThe script will call `window.__engine.shot` with `pixels`, `ids`, and `metrics` disabled to avoid heavy data transfer. It will return the canvas dimensions, engine errors, ready state, screen object, and thumbnail. A key press will be injected to verify focus changes.\n\nTwo sequential page loads will be written as launch-1 and launch-2. The script will be saved now so it is ready when end-to-end tests finish. Node stdout may be block-buffered, so the monitor might only fire at the end.\n\nThe monitor will see the EXIT marker appended by the shell after Node flushes on exit, so block-buffering is not a concern. A note about extracting ux/nowebgpu from the end-to-end log will be added. The launch script will be written now and execution paused; the monitor will wake me when tests finish.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-71bfa6a3-26d9-4afe-b5b2-177bc1d6453a-51","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/gfx/thumbnail.ts","limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-71bfa6a3-26d9-4afe-b5b2-177bc1d6453a-52","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/tools/e2e.mjs","offset":360,"limit":120}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1208,"output_tokens":797,"cache_read_input_tokens":97152,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"f8f3b584-607c-47b1-aa67-7ae310274b6c"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-71bfa6a3-26d9-4afe-b5b2-177bc1d6453a-51","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file Text thumbnails (PLAN.md §8.5): a frame as a 48 × 27 grid of hex colours, kept as JSON\\n * (tests/baselines/thumbs/<case>.json) instead of an image (doctrine: Assets), compared per cell with a tolerance,\\n * and read as a coarse map. `thumbnail(rgba, width, height, ids?)` averages the source pixels each cell covers (the\\n * nearest pixel when the source is smaller than the grid) into `rows`: 27 strings of 48 `rrggbb` colours separated\\n * by spaces. Given the ID pass's per-pixel objects (engine/gfx/idpass.ts), it also writes `map`, 27 strings of 48\\n * symbols, each cell the object covering most of it (`.` empty space, `?` a pixel no object claims), with `legend`\\n * naming each symbol: `A` is the largest visible object, then `B`…`Z`, `a`…`z`, `0`…`9`, and `+` any after those.\\n * `compareThumbnails(expected, actual, { tolerance })` counts the cells whose colour moved by more than the\\n10→ * tolerance in some channel, with the mean and largest change and the worst cells.\\n *\\n * Pure and DOM-free, so the page builds thumbnails from its shot (engine/gfx/shot.ts) and Node compares them with\\n * the baselines (`x shot --thumb <case>`, tools/cmd/shot.ts).\\n *\\n * Invariants: a thumbnail is plain JSON; the same pixels give the same thumbnail; averages are of the 8-bit sRGB\\n * values, rounded.\\n *\\n * @example\\n * const thumb = thumbnail(new Uint8Array(48 * 27 * 4).fill(255), 48, 27);\\n20→ * thumb.rows[0].slice(0, 13); // 'ffffff ffffff'\\n * compareThumbnails(thumb, thumb).cells; // 0\\n * @see engine/gfx/thumbnail.test.ts\\n */\\n\\n/** The grid's size: 48 × 27 cells (16:9). */\\nexport const THUMB_WIDTH = 48;\\n/** The grid's height. */\\nexport const THUMB_HEIGHT = 27;\\n\\n30→/** The symbols of the map, for the visible objects in order (largest first). */\\nexport const MAP_SYMBOLS = 'ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789';\\n\\n/** The per-pixel value of a pixel no object claims (an ID colour the pass did not assign). */\\nexport const STRAY = 0xffffffff;\\n\\n/** A text thumbnail. */\\nexport interface Thumbnail {\\n  /** Cells across and down: 48 × 27. */\\n  width: number;\\n40→  height: number;\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file Text thumbnails (PLAN.md §8.5): a frame as a 48 × 27 grid of hex colours, kept as JSON\\n * (tests/baselines/thumbs/<case>.json) instead of an image (doctrine: Assets), compared per cell with a tolerance,\\n * and read as a coarse map. `thumbnail(rgba, width, height, ids?)` averages the source pixels each cell covers (the\\n * nearest pixel when the source is smaller than the grid) into `rows`: 27 strings of 48 `rrggbb` colours separated\\n * by spaces. Given the ID pass's per-pixel objects (engine/gfx/idpass.ts), it also writes `map`, 27 strings of 48\\n * symbols, each cell the object covering most of it (`.` empty space, `?` a pixel no object claims), with `legend`\\n * naming each symbol: `A` is the largest visible object, then `B`…`Z`, `a`…`z`, `0`…`9`, and `+` any after those.\\n * `compareThumbnails(expected, actual, { tolerance })` counts the cells whose colour moved by more than the\\n10→ * tolerance in some channel, with the mean and largest change and the worst cells.\\n *\\n * Pure and DOM-free, so the page builds thumbnails from its shot (engine/gfx/shot.ts) and Node compares them with\\n * the baselines (`x shot --thumb <case>`, tools/cmd/shot.ts).\\n *\\n * Invariants: a thumbnail is plain JSON; the same pixels give the same thumbnail; averages are of the 8-bit sRGB\\n * values, rounded.\\n *\\n * @example\\n * const thumb = thumbnail(new Uint8Array(48 * 27 * 4).fill(255), 48, 27);\\n20→ * thumb.rows[0].slice(0, 13); // 'ffffff ffffff'\\n * compareThumbnails(thumb, thumb).cells; // 0\\n * @see engine/gfx/thumbnail.test.ts\\n */\\n\\n/** The grid's size: 48 × 27 cells (16:9). */\\nexport const THUMB_WIDTH = 48;\\n/** The grid's height. */\\nexport const THUMB_HEIGHT = 27;\\n\\n30→/** The symbols of the map, for the visible objects in order (largest first). */\\nexport const MAP_SYMBOLS = 'ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789';\\n\\n/** The per-pixel value of a pixel no object claims (an ID colour the pass did not assign). */\\nexport const STRAY = 0xffffffff;\\n\\n/** A text thumbnail. */\\nexport interface Thumbnail {\\n  /** Cells across and down: 48 × 27. */\\n  width: number;\\n40→  height: number;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/gfx/thumbnail.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file Text thumbnails (PLAN.md §8.5): a frame as a 48 × 27 grid of hex colours, kept as JSON\\n * (tests/baselines/thumbs/<case>.json) instead of an image (doctrine: Assets), compared per cell with a tolerance,\\n * and read as a coarse map. `thumbnail(rgba, width, height, ids?)` averages the source pixels each cell covers (the\\n * nearest pixel when the source is smaller than the grid) into `rows`: 27 strings of 48 `rrggbb` colours separated\\n * by spaces. Given the ID pass's per-pixel objects (engine/gfx/idpass.ts), it also writes `map`, 27 strings of 48\\n * symbols, each cell the object covering most of it (`.` empty space, `?` a pixel no object claims), with `legend`\\n * naming each symbol: `A` is the largest visible object, then `B`…`Z`, `a`…`z`, `0`…`9`, and `+` any after those.\\n * `compareThumbnails(expected, actual, { tolerance })` counts the cells whose colour moved by more than the\\n * tolerance in some channel, with the mean and largest change and the worst cells.\\n *\\n * Pure and DOM-free, so the page builds thumbnails from its shot (engine/gfx/shot.ts) and Node compares them with\\n * the baselines (`x shot --thumb <case>`, tools/cmd/shot.ts).\\n *\\n * Invariants: a thumbnail is plain JSON; the same pixels give the same thumbnail; averages are of the 8-bit sRGB\\n * values, rounded.\\n *\\n * @example\\n * const thumb = thumbnail(new Uint8Array(48 * 27 * 4).fill(255), 48, 27);\\n * thumb.rows[0].slice(0, 13); // 'ffffff ffffff'\\n * compareThumbnails(thumb, thumb).cells; // 0\\n * @see engine/gfx/thumbnail.test.ts\\n */\\n\\n/** The grid's size: 48 × 27 cells (16:9). */\\nexport const THUMB_WIDTH = 48;\\n/** The grid's height. */\\nexport const THUMB_HEIGHT = 27;\\n\\n/** The symbols of the map, for the visible objects in order (largest first). */\\nexport const MAP_SYMBOLS = 'ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789';\\n\\n/** The per-pixel value of a pixel no object claims (an ID colour the pass did not assign). */\\nexport const STRAY = 0xffffffff;\\n\\n/** A text thumbnail. */\\nexport interface Thumbnail {\\n  /** Cells across and down: 48 × 27. */\\n  width: number;\\n  height: number;\\n\",\"total_lines\":180}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-71bfa6a3-26d9-4afe-b5b2-177bc1d6453a-52","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"360→  } finally {\\n    await page.close();\\n  }\\n});\\n\\nawait block('touch', async () => {\\n  const phone = await browser.newContext({ ...devices['Pixel 7'] });\\n  const page = await phone.newPage();\\n  watch(page);\\n  await page.goto(pageUrl);\\n370→  await page.waitForFunction(\\n    () =>\\n      window.__engine?.ready &&\\n      document.querySelector('[data-game=\\\"touch\\\"]')?.textContent?.includes('Controller or keyboard required'),\\n    null,\\n    { timeout: 40000 },\\n  );\\n  await page.waitForFunction(() => window.__compass?.screen === 'attract', null, { timeout: 15000 });\\n  const text = await page.locator('[data-game=\\\"touch\\\"]').innerText();\\n  await page.locator('[data-game=\\\"touch\\\"] [data-act=\\\"settings\\\"]').tap();\\n380→  await page.waitForFunction(() => window.__compass?.screen === 'settings');\\n  report('touch asks for a controller', text.includes('Controller or keyboard required'), text);\\n  await phone.close();\\n});\\n\\nawait block('glyphs', async () => {\\n  const page = await browser.newPage({ viewport: { width: 1280, height: 720 } });\\n  try {\\n    watch(page);\\n    await page.goto(pageUrl);\\n390→    await page.waitForFunction(() => window.__engine?.ready && window.__compass?.screen === 'title', null, {\\n      timeout: 40000,\\n    });\\n    await page.keyboard.press('ArrowDown');\\n    await page.waitForFunction(() => document.querySelector('.prompt')?.innerHTML.includes('Enter'));\\n    const keys = await page.locator('.prompt').innerHTML();\\n    await page.mouse.click(30, 680);\\n    await page.waitForFunction(() => document.querySelector('.prompt')?.innerHTML.includes('M18 16'));\\n    const mouse = await page.locator('.prompt').innerHTML();\\n    await page.click('text=Settings');\\n400→    await page.keyboard.press('ArrowRight');\\n    await page.waitForFunction(() => document.body.innerText.includes('Glyphs'));\\n    await page.click('text=Glyphs');\\n    await page.waitForFunction(() => document.body.innerText.includes('Xbox'));\\n    const xbox = await page.locator('[data-game=\\\"menu\\\"]').innerText();\\n    report(\\n      'prompts follow the last device',\\n      keys.includes('Enter') && mouse.includes('M18 16'),\\n      `${keys.includes('Enter')} ${mouse.includes('M18 16')}`,\\n    );\\n410→    report('Xbox glyphs are a setting', xbox.includes('Xbox'), xbox);\\n  } finally {\\n    await page.close();\\n  }\\n});\\n\\nawait block('campaign', async () => {\\n  const page = await browser.newPage({ viewport: { width: 960, height: 540 } });\\n  try {\\n    watch(page);\\n420→    await page.goto(`${pageUrl}?game.autoplay=1`);\\n    let detail = '';\\n    let ok = false;\\n    try {\\n      await page.waitForFunction(() => window.__compass && window.__compass.screen === 'credits', null, {\\n        timeout: 660000,\\n      });\\n      ok = true;\\n    } catch {\\n      detail = await page.evaluate(() => {\\n430→        const op = window.__compass?.live?.();\\n        return JSON.stringify({\\n          screen: window.__compass?.screen,\\n          caseId: window.__compass?.campaign?.caseId,\\n          status: op?.status,\\n          tick: op?.tick,\\n          score: op?.score,\\n          fail: op?.fail,\\n        });\\n      });\\n440→    }\\n    report('campaign reaches the credits', ok, detail);\\n  } finally {\\n    await page.close();\\n  }\\n});\\n\\nawait browser.close();\\n\\nconst py = `\\n450→from playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\\nurl = ${JSON.stringify(pageUrl)}\\nwith sync_playwright() as p:\\n    for name, browser_type, kwargs in (\\n        ('firefox', p.firefox, {}),\\n        ('webkit', p.webkit, {'device_scale_factor': 3, 'viewport': {'width': 390, 'height': 844}, 'is_mobile': True, 'has_touch': True, 'user_agent': 'Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 17_0 like Mac OS X)'}),\\n    ):\\n        browser = browser_type.launch(headless=True)\\n        page = browser.new_page(**kwargs) if name == 'webkit' else browser.new_page()\\n        page.goto(url, wait_until='load', timeout=90000)\\n460→        try:\\n            page.wait_for_function(\\\"() => (document.querySelector('#msg')?.innerText || '').includes('WebGPU')\\\", timeout=20000)\\n        except Exception:\\n            pass\\n        msg = page.locator('#msg').inner_text()\\n        print(name + '|' + msg.replace('\\\\\\\\n', ' '))\\n        browser.close()\\n`;\\nconst python = spawnSync('python3', ['-c', py], { encoding: 'utf8' });\\nconst lines = `${python.stdout}\\\\n${python.stderr}`;\\n470→for (const name of ['firefox', 'webkit']) {\\n  const row = lines.split('\\\\n').find((line) => line.startsWith(`${name}|`)) ?? '';\\n  report(`${name} WebGPU message`, row.includes('This game needs a browser with WebGPU.