{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_603","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The shell exited with code 137. The campaign was interrupted because the browser was killed.\n\nThe temporary directory still exists. The wrapper's cleanup command likely failed because the shell was killed along with Chrome, or because Chrome held files open.\n\nThe log shows the shell reached the exit echo, so it should have run the cleanup command next. The temporary directory still exists, which means the rm command either failed or was never reached.\n\nThe wrapper writes the exit code to the log, then runs rm -rf, then exits. Since the temporary directory still exists after the log shows EXIT, the cleanup command likely failed or was interrupted between those two steps.\n\nThe wrapper shell was not accidentally killed, because the process pattern did not match it. The temporary directory likely still exists because the cleanup command is still running. I will check if it has been removed and clean up manually if necessary. The monitor will report failure, which is expected.\n\nThe wrapper will exit automatically once it sees the EXIT marker. I will remove the leftover temporary directory if it still exists, then run prettier and rebuild.\n\nThe campaign failure was caused by manually killing the browser, not a game bug, so I will not log it as an issue. The glyphs timeout might be a memory leak; I will only report it if the next run passes. Issue 19 already covers the root cause, and the test harness is designed to isolate failures between checks.\n\nI will rebuild using tsx with a short temporary directory. I will prettier the edited files first, then run node --check on e2e.mjs and verify boot.ts comment lengths. Finally, I will start end-to-end test run 6 with the monitor.\n\nI will remove the leftover temporary directory if it still exists. The old monitor will exit automatically when it sees the EXIT marker, so I will not kill it manually. I am starting the rebuild now and will set a 180-second timeout.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-30ca81eb-b8b8-4899-b8dc-e666b81e3cfe-79","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"PKG=\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731\"\ncd \"$PKG\"\n# leftover socket dir from the stopped run\nif [ -d /tmp/g.UrBhq7 ]; then rm -rf /tmp/g.UrBhq7 && echo 'removed old tmp'; else echo 'old tmp already gone'; fi\n./node_modules/.bin/prettier --write labs/game/app/boot.ts labs/game/tools/e2e.mjs labs/game/data/interview.ts\nnode --check labs/game/tools/e2e.mjs\nTMP=$(mktemp -d /tmp/g.XXXXXX)\nexport TMPDIR=\"$TMP\"\n./node_modules/.bin/tsx labs/game/tools/one-file.mts\ncode=$?\nrm -rf \"$TMP\"\nHTML=\"../Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731.html\"\npython3 - <<'PY'\nhtml=open(\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731.html\",encoding=\"utf-8\").read()\ni=html.find(\"<script\")\nprint(\"first\", html[i:i+70].replace(\"\\n\",\" \"))\nfor s in [\"Nineteen issues\",\"added on import\",\"A control's click is still coming\",\"can-scroll\",\"DOMContentLoaded\",\"This game needs a browser with WebGPU.\"]:\n    print(s, html.find(s)>=0)\nprint(\"bytes\", len(html.encode()))\nPY\nexit $code","description":"Format sources and rebuild the one-file page"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1173,"output_tokens":1602,"cache_read_input_tokens":122752,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"11425e03-e778-4f47-a83e-df4bd5da748d"}
