{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_621","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"End-to-end tests passed. Reviewing the full log to confirm all checks are clean.\n\nThe \"no g. chrome\" message came from stdout; the e2e output went to the log file. I will copy ux.log and nowebgpu.log from that log as evidence, then start the hub.\n\nThe hub is heavy and must not overlap with other processes. I am weighing whether to run `npm run verify` now, since it covers the full suite including e2e and hub, but it does not split sim, bot, or content logs.\n\nI will run the sim, bot, and content tests separately to capture their logs. Then I will run `npm run verify` to produce verify.log. This avoids duplicating e2e and hub work while still satisfying the plan's required files.\n\nI will run the hub test first. This catches any hub failures before the lengthy verify step.\n\nLaunch is faster than hub, so it will run first for quick feedback. Sim, bot, and content tests are CPU-only and will run before hub to avoid GPU contention. Hub follows launch, then verify.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b87c9775-c996-4b1f-b887-d3ef7ccdc3e6-102","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/e2e-r6.log"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b87c9775-c996-4b1f-b887-d3ef7ccdc3e6-103","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"it\\(|describe\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/bot.test.ts"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1710,"output_tokens":1043,"cache_read_input_tokens":138752,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"a2e727ce-a6cc-42c8-b028-bf519dd0a44a"}
