{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_622","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"End-to-end tests r6 passed completely, covering touch, glyphs, campaign, Firefox, and WebKit.\n\nThe next steps are to save logs, run sim, bot, and content tests, then launch-1, launch-2, hub, and npm run verify. PROGRESS.md will be updated with verified work and deviations. The final reply will include four feedback sections. Campaign credits confirm the operation ran via bot.\n\nChecking bot.test.ts to confirm win reporting. Content.test walks story to credits. Starting tests now, but avoiding launch-1 and launch-2 simultaneously to prevent CPU contention.\n\nTests will run first since they are not browsers. They may take one to three minutes. All three test files will execute sequentially in PKG, writing to sim.log, bot.log, and content.log with verbose vitest output. Browser launches will follow.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-24a1861d-2af4-463c-9ca8-8483ce314676-104","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/bot.test.ts","limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-24a1861d-2af4-463c-9ca8-8483ce314676-105","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/content.test.ts","limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-24a1861d-2af4-463c-9ca8-8483ce314676-106","name":"todo_write","input":{"todos":[{"id":"front","content":"front: Title, story, board, pause, settings, glyphs, attract, dev mode","status":"completed"},{"id":"field","content":"field: Living sheet, hands, HUD, campaign screens","status":"completed"},{"id":"hub","content":"hub: AI Hub session, sequencer, couch seats, one-file HTML","status":"in_progress"},{"id":"verify","content":"verify: Run verification plan and write hand-ins","status":"pending"}],"merge":true}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1869,"output_tokens":917,"cache_read_input_tokens":140416,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"5d2f4a9c-2bfb-4d40-9846-7e82c667be40"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-24a1861d-2af4-463c-9ca8-8483ce314676-104","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The shipped bot, from each case's own start. It may only steer through hands. A win is `status === 'won'`.\\n */\\nimport { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\\nimport { runBot } from './bot';\\nimport { caseById, storyCases } from './cases';\\nimport type { Difficulty } from './types';\\nimport { createFromCase, debugOp } from './world';\\n\\n10→/** One required run: case, difficulty, seed, and how many seats. */\\nfunction runs(): [string, Difficulty, number, number][] {\\n  const out: [string, Difficulty, number, number][] = [];\\n  for (const item of storyCases()) {\\n    for (const seed of [1, 2, 3]) out.push([item.id, 'resident', seed, 1]);\\n  }\\n  for (const difficulty of ['intern', 'attending'] as const) {\\n    out.push(['case:first-cut', difficulty, 1, 1], ['case:mercy', difficulty, 1, 1]);\\n  }\\n  out.push(['case:first-cut', 'resident', 1, 2], ['case:first-cut', 'resident', 1, 4]);\\n20→  out.push(['case:gala-shift', 'resident', 1, 1]);\\n  return out;\\n}\\n\\ndescribe('operation bot', () => {\\n  it.each(runs())('%s %s seed %s seats %s', (id, difficulty, seed, seats) => {\\n    const op = createFromCase(id, { seed, difficulty, seats });\\n    runBot(op);\\n    expect(op.status, debugOp(op)).toBe('won');\\n    const par = caseById(id).par;\\n30→    if (difficulty === 'resident' && seed === 1 && seats === 1) {\\n      expect(Math.abs(op.score - par) / par).toBeLessThan(0.05);\\n    }\\n  });\\n});\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The shipped bot, from each case's own start. It may only steer through hands. A win is `status === 'won'`.\\n */\\nimport { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\\nimport { runBot } from './bot';\\nimport { caseById, storyCases } from './cases';\\nimport type { Difficulty } from './types';\\nimport { createFromCase, debugOp } from './world';\\n\\n10→/** One required run: case, difficulty, seed, and how many seats. */\\nfunction runs(): [string, Difficulty, number, number][] {\\n  const out: [string, Difficulty, number, number][] = [];\\n  for (const item of storyCases()) {\\n    for (const seed of [1, 2, 3]) out.push([item.id, 'resident', seed, 1]);\\n  }\\n  for (const difficulty of ['intern', 'attending'] as const) {\\n    out.push(['case:first-cut', difficulty, 1, 1], ['case:mercy', difficulty, 1, 1]);\\n  }\\n  out.push(['case:first-cut', 'resident', 1, 2], ['case:first-cut', 'resident', 1, 4]);\\n20→  out.push(['case:gala-shift', 'resident', 1, 1]);\\n  return out;\\n}\\n\\ndescribe('operation bot', () => {\\n  it.each(runs())('%s %s seed %s seats %s', (id, difficulty, seed, seats) => {\\n    const op = createFromCase(id, { seed, difficulty, seats });\\n    runBot(op);\\n    expect(op.status, debugOp(op)).toBe('won');\\n    const par = caseById(id).par;\\n30→    if (difficulty === 'resident' && seed === 1 && seats === 1) {\\n      expect(Math.abs(op.score - par) / par).toBeLessThan(0.05);\\n    }\\n  });\\n});\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/bot.test.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":120,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file The shipped bot, from each case's own start. It may only steer through hands. A win is `status === 'won'`.\\n */\\nimport { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\\nimport { runBot } from './bot';\\nimport { caseById, storyCases } from './cases';\\nimport type { Difficulty } from './types';\\nimport { createFromCase, debugOp } from './world';\\n\\n/** One required run: case, difficulty, seed, and how many seats. */\\nfunction runs(): [string, Difficulty, number, number][] {\\n  const out: [string, Difficulty, number, number][] = [];\\n  for (const item of storyCases()) {\\n    for (const seed of [1, 2, 3]) out.push([item.id, 'resident', seed, 1]);\\n  }\\n  for (const difficulty of ['intern', 'attending'] as const) {\\n    out.push(['case:first-cut', difficulty, 1, 1], ['case:mercy', difficulty, 1, 1]);\\n  }\\n  out.push(['case:first-cut', 'resident', 1, 2], ['case:first-cut', 'resident', 1, 4]);\\n  out.push(['case:gala-shift', 'resident', 1, 1]);\\n  return out;\\n}\\n\\ndescribe('operation bot', () => {\\n  it.each(runs())('%s %s seed %s seats %s', (id, difficulty, seed, seats) => {\\n    const op = createFromCase(id, { seed, difficulty, seats });\\n    runBot(op);\\n    expect(op.status, debugOp(op)).toBe('won');\\n    const par = caseById(id).par;\\n    if (difficulty === 'resident' && seed === 1 && seats === 1) {\\n      expect(Math.abs(op.score - par) / par).toBeLessThan(0.05);\\n    }\\n  });\\n});\\n\",\"total_lines\":34}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-24a1861d-2af4-463c-9ca8-8483ce314676-105","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The operation's content, voices, the whole-story walk, and the lockstep. These drive the shipped modules.\\n */\\nimport { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\\nimport { CASES } from './cases';\\nimport { playThrough } from './director';\\nimport { runLockstep } from './sequencer';\\nimport { SCENES } from './story';\\nimport { tableComplete } from './table';\\n10→import { validateAll } from './validate';\\nimport { voiceKey } from './voice';\\n\\ndescribe('content', () => {\\n  it('accepts every case and every scene', () => {\\n    expect(validateAll()).toEqual([]);\\n    expect(CASES.length).toBe(9);\\n    expect(SCENES.length).toBe(18);\\n  });\\n\\n20→  it('gives every scene between 12 and 35 boxes', () => {\\n    for (const scene of SCENES) {\\n      expect(scene.boxes.length).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(12);\\n      expect(scene.boxes.length).toBeLessThanOrEqual(35);\\n    }\\n  });\\n\\n  it('barks the same line the same way', () => {\\n    const line = 'The storm took the bridge.';\\n    expect(voiceKey('WREN', line)).toBe(voiceKey('WREN', line));\\n30→    expect(voiceKey('WREN', line)).not.toBe(voiceKey('ODIE', line));\\n    expect(voiceKey('WREN', line)).not.toBe(voiceKey('WREN', 'Begin.'));\\n  });\\n\\n  it('covers every tool and kind', () => {\\n    expect(tableComplete()).toBe(true);\\n  });\\n\\n  it('walks the story to credits', () => {\\n    const through = playThrough('resident', 1);\\n40→    expect(through.credits).toBe(true);\\n    expect(through.free).toBe(true);\\n    expect(through.attending).toBe(true);\\n    expect(through.ranks).toHaveLength(8);\\n    expect(through.scenes.length).toBe(16);\\n    expect(through.postcards.length).toBe(8);\\n  });\\n\\n  it('keeps four peers on one hash through loss and a leaver', () => {\\n    const run = runLockstep(3600, 4);\\n50→    expect(run.dropped).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n    expect(run.leftAt).toBe(1800);\\n    const host = run.peers[0].hashes;\\n    expect(host).toHaveLength(3600);\\n    for (const peer of run.peers) expect(peer.hashes).toEqual(host);\\n    expect(run.peers[0].op.seats[3].use).toBe(false);\\n    expect(run.peers[0].op.status).toBe('playing');\\n  });\\n});\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The operation's content, voices, the whole-story walk, and the lockstep. These drive the shipped modules.\\n */\\nimport { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\\nimport { CASES } from './cases';\\nimport { playThrough } from './director';\\nimport { runLockstep } from './sequencer';\\nimport { SCENES } from './story';\\nimport { tableComplete } from './table';\\n10→import { validateAll } from './validate';\\nimport { voiceKey } from './voice';\\n\\ndescribe('content', () => {\\n  it('accepts every case and every scene', () => {\\n    expect(validateAll()).toEqual([]);\\n    expect(CASES.length).toBe(9);\\n    expect(SCENES.length).toBe(18);\\n  });\\n\\n20→  it('gives every scene between 12 and 35 boxes', () => {\\n    for (const scene of SCENES) {\\n      expect(scene.boxes.length).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(12);\\n      expect(scene.boxes.length).toBeLessThanOrEqual(35);\\n    }\\n  });\\n\\n  it('barks the same line the same way', () => {\\n    const line = 'The storm took the bridge.';\\n    expect(voiceKey('WREN', line)).toBe(voiceKey('WREN', line));\\n30→    expect(voiceKey('WREN', line)).not.toBe(voiceKey('ODIE', line));\\n    expect(voiceKey('WREN', line)).not.toBe(voiceKey('WREN', 'Begin.'));\\n  });\\n\\n  it('covers every tool and kind', () => {\\n    expect(tableComplete()).toBe(true);\\n  });\\n\\n  it('walks the story to credits', () => {\\n    const through = playThrough('resident', 1);\\n40→    expect(through.credits).toBe(true);\\n    expect(through.free).toBe(true);\\n    expect(through.attending).toBe(true);\\n    expect(through.ranks).toHaveLength(8);\\n    expect(through.scenes.length).toBe(16);\\n    expect(through.postcards.length).toBe(8);\\n  });\\n\\n  it('keeps four peers on one hash through loss and a leaver', () => {\\n    const run = runLockstep(3600, 4);\\n50→    expect(run.dropped).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n    expect(run.leftAt).toBe(1800);\\n    const host = run.peers[0].hashes;\\n    expect(host).toHaveLength(3600);\\n    for (const peer of run.peers) expect(peer.hashes).toEqual(host);\\n    expect(run.peers[0].op.seats[3].use).toBe(false);\\n    expect(run.peers[0].op.status).toBe('playing');\\n  });\\n});\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/content.test.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file The operation's content, voices, the whole-story walk, and the lockstep. These drive the shipped modules.\\n */\\nimport { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\\nimport { CASES } from './cases';\\nimport { playThrough } from './director';\\nimport { runLockstep } from './sequencer';\\nimport { SCENES } from './story';\\nimport { tableComplete } from './table';\\nimport { validateAll } from './validate';\\nimport { voiceKey } from './voice';\\n\\ndescribe('content', () => {\\n  it('accepts every case and every scene', () => {\\n    expect(validateAll()).toEqual([]);\\n    expect(CASES.length).toBe(9);\\n    expect(SCENES.length).toBe(18);\\n  });\\n\\n  it('gives every scene between 12 and 35 boxes', () => {\\n    for (const scene of SCENES) {\\n      expect(scene.boxes.length).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(12);\\n      expect(scene.boxes.length).toBeLessThanOrEqual(35);\\n    }\\n  });\\n\\n  it('barks the same line the same way', () => {\\n    const line = 'The storm took the bridge.';\\n    expect(voiceKey('WREN', line)).toBe(voiceKey('WREN', line));\\n    expect(voiceKey('WREN', line)).not.toBe(voiceKey('ODIE', line));\\n    expect(voiceKey('WREN', line)).not.toBe(voiceKey('WREN', 'Begin.'));\\n  });\\n\\n  it('covers every tool and kind', () => {\\n    expect(tableComplete()).toBe(true);\\n  });\\n\\n  it('walks the story to credits', () => {\\n    const through = playThrough('resident', 1);\\n    expect(through.credits).toBe(true);\\n    expect(through.free).toBe(true);\\n    expect(through.attending).toBe(true);\\n    expect(through.ranks).toHaveLength(8);\\n    expect(through.scenes.length).toBe(16);\\n    expect(through.postcards.length).toBe(8);\\n  });\\n\\n  it('keeps four peers on one hash through loss and a leaver', () => {\\n    const run = runLockstep(3600, 4);\\n    expect(run.dropped).toBeGreaterThan(0);\\n    expect(run.leftAt).toBe(1800);\\n    const host = run.peers[0].hashes;\\n    expect(host).toHaveLength(3600);\\n    for (const peer of run.peers) expect(peer.hashes).toEqual(host);\\n    expect(run.peers[0].op.seats[3].use).toBe(false);\\n    expect(run.peers[0].op.status).toBe('playing');\\n  });\\n});\\n\",\"total_lines\":58}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-24a1861d-2af4-463c-9ca8-8483ce314676-106","content":"{\"type\":\"Todo\",\"TodosUpdated\":{\"summary_for_prompt\":\"- [completed] title: Pick title with RNG and create the dev workspace\\n- [completed] engine: Clone my-3dge, npm ci, read API, add verify skeleton\\n- [completed] sim: sim: Finish sim tests (slip, story, voice, director, sequencer)\\n- [completed] bot: bot: Bot that wins every required case and seed\\n- [completed] field: field: Living sheet, hands, HUD, campaign screens\\n- [completed] front: front: Title, story, board, pause, settings, glyphs, attract, dev mode\\n- [in_progress] hub: hub: AI Hub session, sequencer, couch seats, one-file HTML\\n- [pending] verify: verify: Run verification plan and write hand-ins\\n\",\"todos\":[{\"content\":\"Pick title with RNG and create the dev workspace\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"Clone my-3dge, npm ci, read API, add verify skeleton\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"sim: Finish sim tests (slip, story, voice, director, sequencer)\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"bot: Bot that wins every required case and seed\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"field: Living sheet, hands, HUD, campaign screens\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"front: Title, story, board, pause, settings, glyphs, attract, dev mode\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"hub: AI Hub session, sequencer, couch seats, one-file HTML\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"in_progress\"},{\"content\":\"verify: Run verification plan and write hand-ins\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"pending\"}],\"state\":{\"todos\":{\"title\":{\"content\":\"Pick title with RNG and create the dev workspace\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"engine\":{\"content\":\"Clone my-3dge, npm ci, read API, add verify skeleton\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"sim\":{\"content\":\"sim: Finish sim tests (slip, story, voice, director, sequencer)\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"bot\":{\"content\":\"bot: Bot that wins every required case and seed\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"field\":{\"content\":\"field: Living sheet, hands, HUD, campaign screens\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"front\":{\"content\":\"front: Title, story, board, pause, settings, glyphs, attract, dev mode\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"hub\":{\"content\":\"hub: AI Hub session, sequencer, couch seats, one-file HTML\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"in_progress\"},\"verify\":{\"content\":\"verify: Run verification plan and write hand-ins\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"pending\"}}}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"dc9fcd8f-96dc-4237-b6d3-f783f4c69474"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_623","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Bot tests report each case via `it`.\n\nThe verbose reporter will list each test case and its status. The three test files will run next, likely taking one to five minutes. UX logs will be written synchronously first, then the tests will start. The hub requires a browser.\n\nTests will run in the background while UX and nowebgpu logs are extracted from the e2e output. The hub starts only after tests finish.\n\nThe verbose vitest output reports each test case name and its passed status. The assertion checks that the status equals 'won'. This satisfies the requirement to report wins rather than merely noting process exit.\n\nA scratch script importing the shipped playThrough and runBot functions could print each result directly. This would make the word \"won\" and \"free\" visible in the log. It is acceptable because it does not reimplement game rules or hard-code values.\n\nThe scratch script will be invoked with tsx from the package root. It imports the shipped game modules directly. The developer is checking whether tsx resolves those relative paths correctly.\n\nThe reporter script will be placed in scratch and deleted after use. The relative import path from the temporary directory to the package is being calculated.\n\nThe relative import path from the temporary directory to the package is confirmed. The developer is now weighing whether a separate scratch script is necessary, since vitest verbose output alone does not print assertion values like scores or ranks.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-739620b8-bf58-40f1-8cdb-9783e2409678-107","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"export function (playThrough|runBot|createFromCase)","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2261,"output_tokens":1169,"cache_read_input_tokens":142208,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"7958cda7-e71e-463d-a0a2-a13f2360c1c1"}
