{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_634","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The Python http.server failed to print its port within 8 seconds.\n\nThe Python http.server writes its port message to stderr. The hub.mjs script listens for this output via a regex on stderr. Possible causes include stderr buffering, an output format change in this Python version, or the process failing to start.\n\nThe Python version may have changed the startup message format, omitting the word \"port\". Since stderr is typically unbuffered, the 8-second timeout suggests the server hung before printing rather than buffering output.\n\nThe file copy completes before the server spawns, so the delay is not caused by copying. The process likely starts but fails immediately, producing stderr output that does not match the port regex. I will run a quick test server to verify Python's exact startup message.\n\nI will run a quick test server on port 0 to capture its stderr and verify the exact startup message format. I also need to check whether the hub-serve directory exists and if any Python server process is still running. The hub script crashed before browser launch, so the spawned server may have been orphaned or killed along with the parent process.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5671a2a1-f3bc-4763-b14a-dc94467bd870-125","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"python3 --version\n# capture the banner without leaving a server\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport http.server, inspect\nsrc = inspect.getsource(http.server)\nfor i,line in enumerate(src.splitlines(),1):\n    if \"Serving\" in line or \"port\" in line and \"print\" in line:\n        print(f\"{i}:{line}\")\nPY\necho '--- leftover servers ---'\npgrep -af 'http.server' || echo none\necho '--- hub-serve ---'\nls -la /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-