{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_635","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A leftover Python HTTP component was found.\n\nThe Python server is still running. The port regex may fail because Python 3.14 changed the print format. I will check /proc/337939 to find the bound port.\n\nThe port message likely never reached stderr because Python 3.14 buffers stderr when piped, leaving the print unflushed and the server running. I will kill only PID 337939 after confirming its bound port.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-be5df826-4628-4072-a419-35ade41648b4-126","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport http.server, inspect\nlines = inspect.getsource(http.server).splitlines()\nfor i in range(1354, 1372):\n    print(f\"{i+1}:{lines[i]}\")\nPY\necho '--- proc ---'\ntr '\\0' ' ' < /proc/337939/cmdline; echo\nls -l /proc/337939/fd 2>/dev/null | head\n# what port\nss -ltnp 2>/dev/null | grep 337939 || netstat -ltnp 2>/dev/null | grep 337939 || true\n# try reading a bit of stderr? it's a pipe to dead node\necho '--- environ PYTHON ---'\ntr '\\0' '\\n' < /proc/337939/environ | grep -E 'PYTHON|TMP' || true","description":"Read Python server banner and leftover PID"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1145,"output_tokens":567,"cache_read_input_tokens":157184,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"f860fc26-e95b-44ac-a686-f5df7234516a"}
