":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":7,\"content\":\"## Requests\"},{\"line_number\":10,\"content\":\"- A public way to rewrite a geometry the page kept. What I tried: build the operating sheet once with `defineGeometry` / a kit box and write new positions into the same buffers every frame (breath, heartbeat, incision). What happened: there is no public call to replace the vertex data of a geometry the page is already holding, so a kept `BufferGeometry` cannot be repainted through the API. What I expected: something like `writeGeometry(id, positions, colors)` that is safe across a scene restart. What I did instead: the page holds the buffers from the geometry the kit box created and writes them directly. That is the gap PLAN.md §17.3 names.\"},{\"line_number\":13,\"content\":\"## Friction\"},{\"line_number\":22,\"content\":\"## Local engine patches\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"bceb6ff4-efe2-433f-89e9-8e58232ff6a5"}
