ent\":\"    check('head metas', m && m.session === '1' && modeOf(m.mode), m ? `hub:session=${m.session} mode=${m.mode}` : 'could not fetch the page');\"},{\"line_number\":424,\"content\":\"    check('hub:session-players is a range within 1–4', seats.length >= 1 && seats.length <= 2 && least >= 1 && least <= most && most <= 4, `hub:session-players=${m?.players}`);\"},{\"line_number\":425,\"content\":\"    if (m?.minutes != null) check('hub:session-minutes, when given, is a number', Number(m.minutes) > 0, `hub:session-minutes=${m.minutes}`);\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/tools/hub/harness.html\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":102,\"content\":\"      session: meta('hub:session'),\"},{\"line_number\":103,\"content\":\"      players: meta('hub:session-players'),\"},{\"line_number\":104,\"content\":\"      mode: meta('hub:session-mode'),\"},{\"line_number\":105,\"content\":\"      minutes: meta('hub:session-minutes'),\"},{\"line_number\":170,\"content\":\"  const limitMs = params.has('limit') ? Number(params.get('limit')) * 1000 : limitFor(metas?.minutes);\"},{\"line_number\":421,\"content\":\"    check('head metas', m && m.session === '1' && modeOf(m.mode), m ? `hub:session=${m.session} mode=${m.mode}` : 'could not fetch the page');\"},{\"line_number\":424,\"content\":\"    check('hub:session-players is a range within 1–4', seats.length >= 1 && seats.length <= 2 && least >= 1 && least <= most && most <= 4, `hub:session-players=${m?.players}`);\"},{\"line_number\":425,\"content\":\"    if (m?.minutes != null) check('hub:session-minutes, when given, is a number', Number(m.minutes) > 0, `hub:session-minutes=${m.minutes}`);\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"9b5e4959-d7c8-40cc-b8ac-080c398accf9"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_645","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The hub 2 player check failed. The detail is truncated.\n\nThe harness slices the full page text to 400 characters for the failure detail. The actual failing check name is likely further down in the output and got cut off.\n\nThe truncated detail ends at \"hub:session-minutes, wh\", which is the check name \"hub:session-minutes, when given, is a number\". The actual failure reason was cut off before it could be shown.\n\nThe first two checks passed. The third check was cut off mid-word, so the failure could be there or in a later check that did not fit in the 400-character slice.\n\nThe \"welcomed\" status suggests the hello check may have passed. I need to read harness.html to clarify what \"welcomed\" means versus a hello failure. Four scenarios remain, each up to 120 seconds.\n\nThe first scenario finished in roughly 30–40 seconds. The same bug may cause the remaining scenarios to fail quickly too.\n\nI will read harness.html around status rendering and early return paths to diagnose why \"welcomed\" does not mean hello succeeded. The hello timeout is 10 seconds.\n\nThe checklist is still truncated at the minutes check, so the failure is likely just after that. The current run is already using the old script, so I cannot modify it to report the full __hubCheck JSON.\n\nThe \"↑0 ↓0\" status means no game traffic has started because the phase is still loading. The failure occurred during this loading phase, before play began.\n\nThe likely culprit is an early check such as \"every copy says hello\" timing out after 10 seconds, or \"ready without a key press\" after 20 seconds.\n\nI will read the harness code more carefully to confirm exactly which check failed. I can also modify hub.mjs to report full failed check names for the next run.\n\nThe 41-second elapsed time suggests the failure occurred at a later check such as \"ready without a key press\" or \"the round starts,\" not hello. I am counting the exact detail string length from the log to see if it fits within the 400-character limit.\n\nThe 400-character limit is intentional, so the failure detail is always truncated. I will kill the current run to avoid wasting time on three more scenarios that will likely fail identically. Then I will improve hub.mjs to log the exact failing checks from __hubCheck and re-run. I also need to read the harness player status, hello flow, and game connect/ready timing to find the root cause.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0f41755f-b805-4a1f-b0a1-bead16a002d6-139","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/tools/hub/harness.html","offset":300,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0f41755f-b805-4a1f-b0a1-bead16a002d6-140","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/tools/hub/harness.html","offset":430,"limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1848,"output_tokens":1523,"cache_read_input_tokens":165376,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"2fadc130-9bc8-4609-935c-2a1a5f485c41"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-0f41755f-b805-4a1f-b0a1-bead16a002d6-139","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"300→  log(`${cell.key} answers ${what} on the game's card`);\\n  const players = state.cells.filter((c) => !c.server && !c.gone);\\n  if (!auto && players.every((c) => ready.has(c.key))) return releaseRound(state);\\n  tickCard(state);\\n}\\n\\nfunction endCurrent() {\\n  if (!current) return;\\n  current.coordinator.abort('session-ended');\\n  for (const cell of current.cells) removeCell(cell, false);\\n310→  current.hubEnd.close();\\n  current = null;\\n}\\n\\nfunction removeCell(cell, tellRound = true) {\\n  if (cell.gone) return;\\n  cell.gone = true;\\n  cell.detach();\\n  cell.endpoint.close();\\n  cell.frame.remove();\\n320→  cell.el.classList.add('is-out');\\n  if (tellRound) {\\n    log(`${cell.key} left`);\\n    current?.coordinator.leave(cell.key, 'left');\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nfunction renderWho(state) {\\n  $('who').replaceChildren(...state.cells.map((c) => new Option(`${c.name} (${c.key})${c.server ? ' — host, no player' : c.slot === 0 && !serverMode ? ' — host' : ''}`, c.key)));\\n}\\n330→\\nfunction render(state) {\\n  const s = state.status;\\n  if (!s) return;\\n  for (const cell of state.cells) {\\n    const p = s.players.find((q) => q.key === cell.key) ?? (s.server?.key === cell.key ? s.server : null);\\n    if (!p) continue;\\n    const bits = [];\\n    if (p.out) bits.push(`out: ${p.out}`);\\n    else if (p.result) bits.push(`result ${JSON.stringify(p.result)}`);\\n340→    else if (p.ready) bits.push('ready');\\n    else if (p.hello) bits.push('welcomed');\\n    else bits.push('loading');\\n    const last = cell.progress.at(-1);\\n    if (last && !p.result) bits.push(`progress ${last.score}${last.label ? ` (${last.label})` : ''}`);\\n    bits.push(`↑${cell.bridge.stats.sent} ↓${cell.bridge.stats.received}`);\\n    cell.label.querySelector('.cell__state').textContent = bits.join(' · ');\\n    cell.el.classList.toggle('is-out', !!p.out || cell.gone);\\n  }\\n  const lines = [`Round ${s.round} · ${s.mode || 'mode unknown'} · phase ${s.phase}`, `Host: ${s.server ? 'the server, no player' : `player ${s.host}`} · seed ${state.seed}`];\\n350→  if (s.gate && !s.released) lines.push(`Card: ${state.cells.some((c) => c.bridge.showsCard) ? 'the game’s own, ' : ''}${state.splashUntil ? `${Math.max(0, Math.ceil((state.splashUntil - performance.now()) / 1000))} s left` : 'held'} (Start now ends it)`);\\n  if (state.record) {\\n    const name = (id) => s.players[id]?.name ?? `#${id}`;\\n    lines.push(`Ended ${state.record.status} (${state.record.reason})`);\\n    if (state.record.standings) state.record.standings.forEach((ids, i) => lines.push(`  ${i + 1}. ${ids.map(name).join(', ')}`));\\n  }\\n  if (s.issues.length) lines.push(...s.issues.map((i) => `✗ ${i.key}: ${i.problem}`));\\n  $('round').textContent = lines.join('\\\\n');\\n}\\n\\n360→$('restart').onclick = () => newRound();\\n$('release').onclick = () => releaseRound();\\n$('timeup').onclick = () => current?.coordinator.timeUp();\\n$('remove').onclick = () => {\\n  const cell = current?.cells.find((c) => c.key === $('who').value);\\n  if (cell) removeCell(cell);\\n};\\n$('hide').onclick = () => {\\n  if (!current) return;\\n  current.hidden = !current.hidden;\\n370→  $('hide').setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(current.hidden));\\n  (current.cells.find((c) => c.server) ?? current.cells[0])?.bridge.visibility(current.hidden);\\n  log(`host tab ${current.hidden ? 'hidden' : 'shown'}`);\\n};\\nfor (const id of ['latency', 'jitter', 'loss']) $(id).onchange = applyNet;\\n\\n/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n * ?auto=1 — the conformance run. It presses keys inside each frame with\\n * synthetic events while the round plays (the frames must be served from this\\n * page's origin). Results land in window.__hubCheck, and body[data-complete]\",\"content_concise\":\"300→  log(`${cell.key} answers ${what} on the game's card`);\\n  const players = state.cells.filter((c) => !c.server && !c.gone);\\n  if (!auto && players.every((c) => ready.has(c.key))) return releaseRound(state);\\n  tickCard(state);\\n}\\n\\nfunction endCurrent() {\\n  if (!current) return;\\n  current.coordinator.abort('session-ended');\\n  for (const cell of current.cells) removeCell(cell, false);\\n310→  current.hubEnd.close();\\n  current = null;\\n}\\n\\nfunction removeCell(cell, tellRound = true) {\\n  if (cell.gone) return;\\n  cell.gone = true;\\n  cell.detach();\\n  cell.endpoint.close();\\n  cell.frame.remove();\\n320→  cell.el.classList.add('is-out');\\n  if (tellRound) {\\n    log(`${cell.key} left`);\\n    current?.coordinator.leave(cell.key, 'left');\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nfunction renderWho(state) {\\n  $('who').replaceChildren(...state.cells.map((c) => new Option(`${c.name} (${c.key})${c.server ? ' — host, no player' : c.slot === 0 && !serverMode ? ' — host' : ''}`, c.key)));\\n}\\n330→\\nfunction render(state) {\\n  const s = state.status;\\n  if (!s) return;\\n  for (const cell of state.cells) {\\n    const p = s.players.find((q) => q.key === cell.key) ?? (s.server?.key === cell.key ? s.server : null);\\n    if (!p) continue;\\n    const bits = [];\\n    if (p.out) bits.push(`out: ${p.out}`);\\n    else if (p.result) bits.push(`result ${JSON.stringify(p.result)}`);\\n340→    else if (p.ready) bits.push('ready');\\n    else if (p.hello) bits.push('welcomed');\\n    else bits.push('loading');\\n    const last = cell.progress.at(-1);\\n    if (last && !p.result) bits.push(`progress ${last.score}${last.label ? ` (${last.label})` : ''}`);\\n    bits.push(`↑${cell.bridge.stats.sent} ↓${cell.bridge.stats.received}`);\\n    cell.label.querySelector('.cell__state').textContent = bits.join(' · ');\\n    cell.el.classList.toggle('is-out', !!p.out || cell.gone);\\n  }\\n  const lines = [`Round ${s.round} · ${s.mode || 'mode unknown'}