{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_648","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Events queue in pending state until the first handler runs, then flush.\n\nQueued ticks flush correctly once the handler registers. The 20-second ready timeout is the immediate failure. I will call hub.ready() before createEngine and answer the card from a window keydown to avoid onFrame. startRound will run after the engine is ready.\n\nThe current run must be killed first. The hub loads a compiled HTML page, so boot.ts changes require a rebuild. I will terminate the hub node and its Chrome process before rebuilding.\n\nOnly Python 340716 belongs to the hub server. Python 339844 is another agent and must be left alone.\n\nThe boot.ts edit will call hub.ready() early, register handlers early, answer the card on Enter/Space/NumpadEnter keydown without waiting for the engine, and run seed and startRound after createEngine. The non-session path needs careful handling during restructuring.\n\nI realized that calling hub.ready() before createEngine risks a race condition. The card event might arrive before the card handler is registered, so the Enter key answer must be handled separately from the hub.on('card') listener.\n\nThe harness only pokes Enter during the card phase. The keydown listener can answer('ready') on Enter whenever a session exists and the round has not started, because answer() checks that goAt is null. This removes the need to wait for the card handler to register.\n\nThe card, start, and end handlers must be registered before createEngine. This ensures queued events flush immediately rather than after warmup. The keydown listener can answer the card on Enter even while the shell is not yet drawing.\n\nThe exact boot.ts sequence is now clear: register the card, start, and end handlers first, then call hub.ready(), then await createEngine. After the engine resolves, wait() will confirm step exists before seeding the round and starting it.\n\nDouble-answering is harmless. The answer() function has no sent flag, so posting twice is safe. Once the card phase ends and goAt is set, later Enter presses are ignored.\n\nThe keydown listener is registered inside start(), which runs after connect() resolves, so ready() can safely fire because the welcome flag is already set. createEngine also receives the seed from info, but the scene setup already uses the URL seed and then we call seed() again afterward.\n\nThe host and client seeds must match. startRound catches up during warmup. Client messages queue before the message handler registers. The 16 ms interval may run before the queued flush. The first step could then have empty hands. The host processes client intents as messages.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7be5a20e-dd32-44ad-a5d7-056338a2cf82-143","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/dev/inspector.ts","offset":185,"limit":30}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7be5a20e-dd32-44ad-a5d7-056338a2cf82-144","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/app/boot.ts","offset":285,"limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1734,"output_tokens":2216,"cache_read_input_tokens":173440,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"b1c9535b-9f54-4a95-a6c2-924dfdd2cf3c"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-7be5a20e-dd32-44ad-a5d7-056338a2cf82-143","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"185→      downgrades: [...h.downgrades],\\n      deps: { ...pkg.dependencies },\\n      scene: h.session.scene.id,\\n      seed: h.session.world.seed,\\n      tick: h.session.world.tick,\\n190→      hz: h.session.world.hz,\\n    }),\\n  },\\n  pause: {\\n    help: 'Pauses sim time (the time.paused setting); step(n) still runs single steps.',\\n    impl: (h) => h.clock.pause(),\\n  },\\n  resume: { help: 'Resumes sim time.', impl: (h) => h.clock.resume() },\\n  step: {\\n    help: 'Runs n sim steps through the clock, recorded in the session (without intents, what the virtual device holds: input.hold, input.axis…); returns the tick after them.',\\n200→    args: {\\n      n: { type: 'integer', default: 1, minimum: 0, description: 'How many steps.' },\\n      intents: {\\n        type: 'any',\\n        description:\\n          'One intents object for every step (its pressed buttons, p, on the first only), or a list of one per step (none past its end); none samples the virtual device each step (__engine.input).',\\n      },\\n    },\\n    impl: (h, n: number, intents: unknown) => {\\n      h.step(n, intents);\\n210→      return h.session.world.tick;\\n    },\\n  },\\n  timeScale: {\\n    help: 'Sets sim seconds per real second (the time.scale setting) when k is given; returns it.',\",\"content_concise\":\"185→      downgrades: [...h.downgrades],\\n      deps: { ...pkg.dependencies },\\n      scene: h.session.scene.id,\\n      seed: h.session.world.seed,\\n      tick: h.session.world.tick,\\n190→      hz: h.session.world.hz,\\n    }),\\n  },\\n  pause: {\\n    help: 'Pauses sim time (the time.paused setting); step(n) still runs single steps.',\\n    impl: (h) => h.clock.pause(),\\n  },\\n  resume: { help: 'Resumes sim time.', impl: (h) => h.clock.resume() },\\n  step: {\\n   