{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_649","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Confirmed that step() works while paused.\n\nMoving hub.ready() and event handlers before createEngine. The card handler and audio.mute are safe since those objects exist earlier. The keydown listener will be extended to answer Enter.\n\nThe exact startup order is now set: register handlers, call hub.ready(), answer Enter, await createEngine, then step through warmup. Warmup events will be delivered immediately because handlers are registered before ready().\n\nEnter key presses during the startup gap are safe because answer() does not depend on the card handler. The boot.ts file is 566 lines, so adding a few more stays under the 600-line limit. I will also improve hub.mjs diagnostics to report failed check names instead of truncating page text.\n\nThe hub harness will now report failed check names instead of truncating page text. I will kill the current hub processes to stop the repeated GPU burn. I will verify the Python process working directory before terminating it. Chrome may linger after Node is killed.\n\nChrome will be killed after Node. The monitor process will be left to report FAILED; a new run will start. This bug is game-breaking for the hub path, so it should be logged as issue 20 in TESTING-LOG and the interview updated.\n\nThe bug is critical. A hub session that never starts is wrong for a player in co-op. The root cause is that ready() waits for the engine inspector, and Enter key presses are only read by the engine loop, so both miss the harness window when GPU warmup exceeds 20 seconds.\n\nReady is sent when the page has the session, and Enter on the card answers even before the first frame.\n\nThen eleven game-breaking: 1-9, 14, and 20. Nine not: 10-13, 15-19.\n\nUpdate interview first testing strings:\n\"Twenty issues were caught...\"\n\"Eleven were game-breaking: ...\" and add the hub ready clause.\n\nThe second sentence currently lists the ten. I'll add the hub one.\n\nAnd TESTING-LOG footer.\n\nThen rebuild HTML. Then re-run hub.\n\nAlso page.test will fail until interview and json match. I'll update both.\n\nCalling ready() before createEngine is safe because it only runs when a session exists. The Enter key handler will answer cards only if a session is active, leaving non-session Enter to the engine loop. If both the keydown listener and the card menu fire an answer while the engine is running, answer() will post twice but return immediately once the round starts. I will kill the running hub first to avoid CPU contention during the rebuild.\n\nThe old `wait().then()` call that invoked `hub.ready()` will be removed. The menus() card handler will remain as a fallback answer path once the engine loop starts.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The two-player hub round never left the loading card. Ready was waiting on the GPU warmup, so the harness gave up while both players were still only “welcomed.” I am sending ready when the session is connected, and answering the card key even before the first frame."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bab64b52-95b6-4a74-8502-c5d64074a4a4-145","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/app/boot.ts","old_string":"  addEventListener('keydown', (event) => {\n    touchHold = false;\n    if (campaign.screen === 'attract') noteInput(campaign);\n    if (event.key === 't' || event.key === 'T') session?.hub.answer('more');\n  });","new_string":"  addEventListener('keydown', (event) => {\n    touchHold = false;\n    if (campaign.screen === 'attract') noteInput(campaign);\n    if (!session) return;\n    if (event.key === 't' || event.key === 'T') session.hub.answer('more');\n    // The card key can arrive while the GPU is still warming, before a frame samples it.\n    if (event.key === 'Enter' || event.key === ' ' || event.code === 'NumpadEnter') session.hub.answer('ready');\n  });"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bab64b52-95b6-4a74-8502-c5d64074a4a4-146","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/app/boot.ts","old_string":"  (window as unknown as { __compass: Compass }).__compass = compass;\n\n  // The night is saved only by saveProgress. The engine's own store would write a quality tier during attract.\n  engine = await createEngine({","new_string":"  (window as unknown as { __compass: Compass }).__compass = compass;\n\n  if (session && hub) {\n    // Ready is \"the page is here\", not \"the GPU is warm\". Two software copies miss a 20s card if it waits.\n    hub.on('card', (data) => {\n      const card = data as { left?: number | null; ready?: number[]; asked?: boolean };\n      const left = card.left == null ? 'Starting' : `${Math.ceil(card.left / 1000)}s`;\n      session.card = {\n        names: (info?.players ?? []).map((player) => player.name),\n        ready: card.ready ?? [],\n        left,\n        asked: !!card.asked,\n      };\n      stamp = '';\n    });\n    hub.on('start', () => {\n      session.card = null;\n      session.playing = false;\n      stamp = '';\n    });\n    hub.on('end', () => {\n      audio.mute(true);\n      session.card = null;\n    });\n    hub.ready();\n  }\n\n  // The night is saved only by saveProgress. The engine's own store would write a quality tier during attract.\n  engine = await createEngine({"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bab64b52-95b6-4a74-8502-c5d64074a4a4-147","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/app/boot.ts","old_string":"      enginePage.pause();\n      enginePage.seed(roundInfo.seed);\n      enginePage.pause();\n      hub.ready();\n      session.round = startRound(hub, roundInfo, enginePage, Math.max(1, roundInfo.players.length));\n    });\n    hub.on('card', (data) => {\n      const card = data as { left?: number | null; ready?: number[]; asked?: boolean };\n      const left = card.left == null ? 'Starting' : `${Math.ceil(card.left / 1000)}s`;\n      session.card = {\n        names: (info?.players ?? []).map((player) => player.name),\n        ready: card.ready ?? [],\n        left,\n        asked: !!card.asked,\n      };\n      stamp = '';\n    });\n    hub.on('start', () => {\n      session.card = null;\n      session.playing = false;\n      stamp = '';\n    });\n    hub.on('end', () => {\n      audio.mute(true);\n      session.card = null;\n    });\n  }","new_string":"      enginePage.pause();\n      enginePage.seed(roundInfo.seed);\n      enginePage.pause();\n      session.round = startRound(hub, roundInfo, enginePage, Math.max(1, roundInfo.players.length));\n    });\n  }"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bab64b52-95b6-4a74-8502-c5d64074a4a4-148","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/tools/hub.mjs","old_string":"  const detail = ok ? '' : await page.evaluate(() => document.body.innerText).catch(() => errors.join(' | '));\n  report(name, ok, detail.slice(0, 400));","new_string":"  const detail = ok\n    ? ''\n    : await page\n        .evaluate(() => {\n          const bad = (window.__hubCheck?.checks ?? [])\n            .filter((item) => !item.pass)\n            .map((item) => `${item.name}: ${item.detail}`);\n          return bad.join(' | ') || document.body.innerText;\n        })\n        .catch(() => errors.join(' | '));\n  report(name, ok, detail.slice(0, 400));"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":