{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_650","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Checking the type definitions for `window.__hubCheck` in `hub.mjs`.\n\nNo type definitions are needed for the `.mjs` file. Optional chaining for `window.__hubCheck` is acceptable in JavaScript. ESLint might flag the `evaluate` function later. Next I will update the testing log and interview, then verify declaration order in `boot.ts`.\n\nConfirmed `hub.on` is inserted before `createEngine`. Verified `stamp`, `audio`, and `session` are declared in the correct order. The `info` variable is properly captured in the card handler closure. Narrowing `session` inside the conditional keeps the assignment safe. Next I will update the logs, terminate the old hub process, and rebuild.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-290cc322-1d5b-4651-bf36-c7e9b4789198-149","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md","old_string":"19. Not critical. A tap on Settings in the touch gate also counted as a pointerdown, which hid the gate and left the kiosk. The shell then replaced the button before the click arrived, so Settings never opened. A pointerdown that starts on a control is left for that control.\n\nNineteen issues. Ten were game-breaking: 1–9 and 14. Nine were not: 10–13 and 15–19.","new_string":"19. Not critical. A tap on Settings in the touch gate also counted as a pointerdown, which hid the gate and left the kiosk. The shell then replaced the button before the click arrived, so Settings never opened. A pointerdown that starts on a control is left for that control.\n20. Critical. A hub round called ready only after the engine inspector existed. Two software WebGPU copies were still warming when the card gave up, so the round stayed in loading. Ready is sent when the session is connected, and Enter on the card answers before the first frame.\n\nTwenty issues. Eleven were game-breaking: 1–9, 14, and 20. Nine were not: 10–13 and 15–19."}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-290cc322-1d5b-4651-bf36-c7e9b4789198-150","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/data/interview.ts","old_string":"    'Nineteen issues were caught and written in labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md.',\n    'Ten were game-breaking: a restore stepped the wrong body, the gala flap never finished, Reverie left the surface early, Solace children stacked, the syringe bound the wrong target, stitches landed off the wound, co-op copies shared one point, an outline width the engine rejects, a sound id the engine already owns, and a look and a song that used fields the engine does not have.',","new_string":"    'Twenty issues were caught and written in labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md.',\n    'Eleven were game-breaking: a restore stepped the wrong body, the gala flap never finished, Reverie left the surface early, Solace children stacked, the syringe bound the wrong target, stitches landed off the wound, co-op copies shared one point, an outline width the engine rejects, a sound id the engine already owns, a look and a song that used fields the engine does not have, and a hub round that never readied while the GPU was still warming up.',"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-290cc322-1d5b-4651-bf36-c7e9b4789198-151","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/exit-interview.json","old_string":"    \"Nineteen issues were caught and written in labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md.\",\n    \"Ten were game-breaking: a restore stepped the wrong body, the gala flap never finished, Reverie left the surface early, Solace children stacked, the syringe bound the wrong target, stitches landed off the wound, co-op copies shared one point, an outline width the engine rejects, a sound id the engine already owns, and a look and a song that used fields the engine does not have.\",","new_string":"    \"Twenty issues were caught and written in labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md.\",\n    \"Eleven were game-breaking: a restore stepped the wrong body, the gala flap never finished, Reverie left the surface early, Solace children stacked, the syringe bound the wrong target, stitches landed off the wound, co-op copies shared one point, an outline width the engine rejects, a sound id the engine already owns, a look and a song that used fields the engine does not have, and a hub round that never readied while the GPU was still warming up.\","}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-290cc322-1d5b-4651-bf36-c7e9b4789198-152","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"# Stop only this hub run: node, its chrome profile, and its python server.\nkill -TERM 340706 2>/dev/null || true\nif [ -d /proc/340716 ]; then\n  cwd=$(readlink /proc/340716/cwd || true)\n  echo \"python cwd=$cwd\"\n  case \"$cwd\" in\n    *hub-serve*) kill -TERM 340716 || true ;;\n    *) echo 'left other python' ;;\n  esac\nfi\nsleep 1\nmapfile -t pids < <(pgrep -f 'user-data-dir=/tmp/g.lInQ0H' || true)\nif [ ${#pids[@]} -gt 0 ]; then kill -TERM \"${pids[@]}\" 2>/dev/null || true; sleep 0.5; kill -KILL \"${pids[@]}\" 2>/dev/null || true; fi\nps -p 340706 >/dev/null 2>&1 && echo 'node still up' || echo 'node gone'\npgrep -af 'user-data-dir=/tmp/g.lInQ0H' || echo 'our chrome gone'\nPKG=\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731\"\nwc -l \"$PKG/labs/game/app/boot.ts\"\ncd \"$PKG\"\n./node_modules/.bin/prettier --write labs/game/app/boot.ts labs/game/tools/hub.mjs labs/game/data/interview.ts >/dev/null\n./node_modules/.bin/vitest run labs/game/app/page.test.ts --reporter=dot","description":"Stop the failed hub run and check the interview match"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3597,"output_tokens":1704,"cache_read_input_tokens":178560,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"1c368db9-21a7-4b77-b3a4-a57be865cfda"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-290cc322-1d5b-4651-bf36-c7e9b4789198-149","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"19. Not critical. A tap on Settings in the touch gate also counted as a pointerdown, which hid the gate and left the kiosk. The shell then replaced the button before the click arrived, so Settings never opened. A pointerdown that starts on a control is left for that control.\\n\\nNineteen issues. Ten were game-breaking: 1–9 and 14. Nine were not: 10–13 and 15–19.\",\"new_string\":\"19. Not critical. A tap on Settings in the touch gate also counted as a pointerdown, which hid the gate and left the kiosk. The shell then replaced the button before the click arrived, so Settings never opened. A pointerdown that starts on a control is left for that control.\\n20. Critical. A hub round called ready only after the engine inspector existed. Two software WebGPU copies were still warming when the card gave up, so the round stayed in loading. Ready is sent when the session is connected, and Enter on the card answers before the first frame.\\n\\nTwenty issues. Eleven were game-breaking: 1–9, 14, and 20. Nine were not: 10–13 and 15–19.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md has been updated successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md has been updated.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"19. Not critical. A tap on Settings in the touch gate also counted as a pointerdown, which hid the gate and left the kiosk. The shell then replaced the button before the click arrived, so Settings never opened. A pointerdown that starts on a control is left for that control.\\n\\nNineteen issues. Ten were game-breaking: 1–9 and 14. Nine were not: 10–13 and 15–19.\",\"old_line\":23,\"new_string\":\"19. Not critical. A tap on Settings in the touch gate also counted as a pointerdown, which hid the gate and left the kiosk. The shell then replaced the button before the click arrived, so Settings never opened. A pointerdown that starts on a control is left for that control.\\n20. Critical. A hub round called ready only after the engine inspector existed. Two software WebGPU copies were still warming when the card gave up, so the round stayed in loading. Ready is sent when the session is connected, and Enter on the card answers before the first frame.\\n\\nTwenty issues. Eleven were game-breaking: 1–9, 14, and 20. Nine were not: 10–13 and 15–19.\",\"new_line\":23,\"context_before\":\"16. Not critical. The use prompt kept the previous device, because the shell redrew only when the menu changed. The stamp now includes the prompt.\\n17. Not critical. The WebGPU sentence ran before `#msg` existed, so a browser that did not throw stayed on \\\"Loading…\\\". It is shown again on `DOMContentLoaded`, when the line is in the page.\\n18. Not critical. Balance reset sat past the bottom of a 720p screen and the page did not scroll, so a click could not reach it. The dev screen scrolls, and Reset is the first row.\\n\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-290cc322-1d5b-4651-bf36-c7e9b4789198-150","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"    'Nineteen issues were caught and written in labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md.',\\n    'Ten were game-breaking: a restore stepped the wrong body, the gala flap never finished, Reverie left the surface early, Solace children stacked, the syringe bound the wrong target, stitches landed off the wound, co-op copies shared one point, an outline width the engine rejects, a sound id the engine already owns, and a look and a song that used fields the engine does not have.',\",\"new_string\":\"    'Twenty issues were caught and written in labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md.',\\n    'Eleven were game-breaking: a restore stepped the wrong body, the gala flap never finished, Reverie left the surface early, Solace children stacked, the syringe bound the wrong target, stitches landed off the wound, co-op copies shared one point, an outline width the engine rejects, a sound id the engine already owns, a look and a song that used fields the engine does not have, and a hub round that never readied while the GPU was still warming up.',\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/data/interview.ts has been updated successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/data/interview.ts has been updated.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/data/interview.ts\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"    'Nineteen issues were caught and written in labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md.',\\n    'Ten were game-breaking: a restore stepped the wrong body, the gala flap never finished, Reverie left the surface early, Solace children stacked, the syringe bound the wrong target, stitches landed off the wound, co-op copies shared one point, an outline width the engine rejects, a sound id the engine already owns, and a look and a song that used fields the engine does not have.',\",\"old_line\":37,\"new_string\":\"    'Twenty issues were caught and written in labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md.',\\n    'Eleven were game-breaking: a restore stepped the wrong body, the gala flap never finished, Reverie left the surface early, Solace children stacked, the syringe bound the wrong target, stitches landed off the wound, co-op copies shared one point, an outline width the engine rejects, a sound id the engine already owns, a look and a song that used fields the engine does not have, and a hub round that never readied while the GPU was still warming up.',\",\"new_line\":37,\"context_before\":\"    usage: 'added on import',\\n  },\\n  testingFeedback: [\\n\",\"context_after\":\"    'The most helpful tests were the bot, which had to win every required case and seed, and the content walk that plays the whole shift to the credits.',\\n    'The least helpful was the voice-key equality check. It only shows that one line keeps the same syllable list. The starter gem tests had to stay green and do not cover an operation.',\\n  ],\\n\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-290cc322-1d5b-4651-bf36-c7e9b4789198-151","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"    \\\"Nineteen issues were caught and written in labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md.\\\",\\n    \\\"Ten were game-breaking: a restore stepped the wrong body, the gala flap never finished, Reverie left the surface early, Solace children stacked, the syringe bound the wrong target, stitches landed off the wound, co-op copies shared one point, an outline width the engine rejects, a sound id the engine already owns, and a look and a song that used fields the engine does not have.\\\",\",\"new_string\":\"    \\\"Twenty issues were caught and written in labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md.\\\",\\n    \\\"Eleven were game-breaking: a restore stepped the wrong body, the gala flap never finished, Reverie left the surface early, Solace children stacked, the syringe bound the wrong target, stitches landed off the wound, co-op copies shared one point, an outline width the engine rejects, a sound id the engine already owns, a look and a song that used fields the engine does not have, and a hub round that never readied while the GPU was still warming up.\\\",\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/exit-interview.json has been updated successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/exit-interview.json has been updated.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/exit-interview.json\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"    \\\"Nineteen issues were caught and written in labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md.\\\",\\n    \\\"Ten were game-breaking: a restore stepped the wrong body, the gala flap never finished, Reverie left the surface early, Solace children stacked, the syringe bound the wrong target, stitches landed off the wound, co-op copies shared one point, an outline width the engine rejects, a sound id the engine already owns, and a look and a song that used fields the engine does not have.\\\",\",\"old_line\":20,\"new_string\":\"    \\\"Twenty issues were caught and written in labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md.\\\",\\n    \\\"Eleven were game-breaking: a restore stepped the wrong body, the gala flap never finished, Reverie left the surface early, Solace children stacked, the syringe bound the wrong target, stitches landed off the wound, co-op copies shared one point, an outline width the engine rejects, a sound id the engine already owns, a look and a song that used fields the engine does not have, and a hub round that never readied while the GPU was still warming up.\\\",\",\"new_line\":20,\"context_before\":\"    