{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_655","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The hub failed faster at 75 seconds with a clearer error.\n\nReady and card checks likely passed. The round ended void with no traffic. Time-up probably fired before startRound registered the finish handler. Events queue until handlers exist.\n\nThe round may have been voided before time-up. No traffic means startRound never began, so the host never sent ticks. The engine warmup likely took 15 to 40 seconds with two WebGPU contexts.\n\nThe 75-second total is too fast for four scenarios to fail individually. The process likely crashed after the first failure. Engine warmup may have exceeded the harness timeout.\n\nThe 75-second total fits only one or two scenarios. The full log needs review.\n\nA void no-result means the hub ended the round without a finish message. If startRound had registered its time-up handler, it would have called finish(false) and produced a won:false result instead.\n\nThe grace period may have voided the round before the handler could run.\n\nfinish() may have been rejected because the host was already reported or standings were invalid. The server copy or host may have left. The traffic check runs before time-up.\n\nThe traffic check confirmed zero sent and received bytes during the play window. The engine was still warming up when the round ended, so startRound never began and finish() never ran within the grace period. The queued time-up event was lost before its handler could register.\n\ncreateEngine likely took longer than the ~38-second window after ready. The queued time-up flush would then happen after the harness already recorded void. The 75-second total fits one scenario plus browser launch, suggesting a crash on the second scenario. Two software WebGPU pages may be causing warmup to exceed the 25-second play window.\n\nThe plan requires running the AI Hub harness scenarios from PLAN.md §16. The current hub.mjs limit of 25 seconds is too short for engine warmup to finish before time-up. Increasing the limit to 90 seconds should allow warmup to complete and traffic to flow before the round ends.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ebf7d9b8-639b-4a83-9607-de23e1804b04-159","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/hub.log"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ebf7d9b8-639b-4a83-9607-de23e1804b04-160","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/tools/hub/round.js","offset":50,"limit":30}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ebf7d9b8-639b-4a83-9607-de23e1804b04-161","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"players=2|harness|limit","path":"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3%2Fwork/01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151/goal/plan.md"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1260,"output_tokens":1461,"cache_read_input_tokens":188288,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"9a230cbb-8707-431f-b81d-4638a54b7dc7"}
