15,32,111,110,32,115,111,102,116,119,97,114,101,32,87,101,98,71,80,85,59,32,101,97,114,108,121,111,111,109,32,119,105,108,108,32,107,105,108,108,32,116,104,101,32,108,97,114,103,101,115,116,32,98,114,111,119,115,101,114,46,32,83,101,115,115,105,111,110,32,115,104,101,101,116,32,100,101,110,115,105,116,121,32,109,97,121,32,100,114,111,112,32,111,110,108,121,32,111,110,32,83,119,105,102,116,83,104,97,100,101,114,44,32,97,110,100,32,116,104,101,32,52,45,112,108,97,121,101,114,32,104,97,114,110,101,115,115,32,109,117,115,116,32,114,117,110,32,97,108,111,110,101,46,32,83,116,101,112,32,55,226,128,153,115,32,102,97,108,108,98,97,99,107,32,97,112,112,108,105,101,115,32,111,110,108,121,32,119,105,116,104,32,97,32,99,97,112,116,117,114,101,100,32,107,105,108,108,32,108,111,103,46,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":6,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3%2Fwork/01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151/goal/plan.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":9,\"content\":\"2. **The operation is recognizably Trauma Center play, under this plan’s original rules.** Checked from each case’s own start, not one chained marathon: first-person surgery on a living field, with a clock and vitals, lost if time runs out, if slips pass the limit, or if a flatline Code fails, and won only by a closing phase. Eight tools — scalpel, forceps, suture, drain, laser, syringe, gel, scanner — each visibly change tissue on a valid target (cut along a guide, pull a shard or mass, zigzag stitches, shrink a pool, burn, inject within a band, paint gel, reveal buried targets) and otherwise refuse with no penalty and a named right tool. Finished actions rate TEXTBOOK, CLEAN, ROUGH, or SLIP and feed a chain and ranks C, B, A, S, and ★. One to three sites keep deteriorating while the surgeon is elsewhere. Stillpoint slows field time; Second Pulse blocks vitals loss and heals on clean actions; both arm from a beat-timed three-press pulse-lock, with a one-press Simple Gift option; two g [... truncated (1031 chars total)]\"},{\"line_number\":18,\"content\":\"1. gating: In the dev workspace, add or extend the engine’s existing `npm test` suite so it calls the shipped sim from a fresh start (not a copy of the rules). Assert tool-on-target effects and a refusal for every pair that has no effect, rating bands, vitals and clock failure, slip limit, flatline Code success and failure, other sites worsening while away, Stillpoint and Second Pulse, Consult, each strain’s distinguishing transition (including Mercy’s three phases), difficulty scaling, and balance sliders staying in range with reset restoring defaults. Capture the run to `{SCRATCH}/sim.log`. Pass only if those assertions pass.\"},{\"line_number\":24,\"content\":\"7. gating: Serve the deliverable with `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` (record the printed port and PID). Run the AI Hub harness scenarios from PLAN.md §16 (`players=2&auto=1`, `players=4` with latency 150, jitter 50, loss 5, `scenario=host-leave`, `scenario=server`) and require `window.__hubCheck.pass` plus zero state-hash mismatches. Also open the game with no session and confirm the title flow. Stop that server by its PID. A Node test of the shipped sequencer (host plus three clients, latency, jitter, 5% loss on unreliable input, a leaver) must keep hashes equal across 3600 ticks. Capture to `{SCRATCH}/hub.log`. Run the four-browser harness alone. If earlyoom kills it, capture that text and retry that run once; if it still dies, the 2-player harness plus the Node sequencer test are the bar only when `{SCRATCH}/hub-oom.log` shows the kill. Do not claim the 4-player run passed.\"},{\"line_number\":45,\"content\":\"- Add `npm run verify` early, as PLAN.md §19’s skeleton, and point browser checks at the single HTML file once the one-file build exists. Prefer `file://` for the game; bind `127.0.0.1` on an OS-chosen port only for the hub harness, and stop that PID only.\"},{\"line_number\":53,\"content\":\"- [ ] Add Cases 2 and 3 (scalpel, scanner, laser, sites, Code, Stillpoint) and the AI Hub session path, including the Node sequencer test and a harness run on the case that exists.\"},{\"line_number\":58,\"content\":\"- PLAN.md asks for a very dense sheet and a four-browser harness on software WebGPU; earlyoom will kill the largest browser. Session sheet density may drop only on SwiftShader, and the 4-player harness must run alone. Step 7’s fallback applies only with a captured kill log.\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"0f6819eb-4773-4657-a2b5-81053c5bba74"}
