{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-dd172732-883e-4315-ab26-1c22d3a63fcb-166","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"100→        return toHub({ type: 'hello', v: msg.v, client: String(msg.client || ''), mode: msg.mode ?? null, seats: msg.seats ?? null, card: ownsCard });\\n      case 'ready':\\n        if (!welcomed) return issue('ready before welcome');\\n        readySent = true;\\n        return toHub({ type: 'ready' });\\n      case 'answer':\\n        if (!ownsCard) return issue('answer without its own card: connect({ card: true })');\\n        if (!welcomed || started) return;\\n        if (msg.answer !== 'ready' && msg.answer !== 'more') return issue(`answer ${JSON.stringify(msg.answer)} is not ready or more`);\\n        return onAnswer(msg.answer);\\n110→      case 'result':\\n        if (!welcomed) return issue('result before welcome');\\n        return toHub({ type: 'result', time: msg.time, score: msg.score, stats: msg.stats, awards: msg.awards });\\n      case 'finish':\\n        if (!welcomed) return issue('finish before welcome');\\n        return toHub({ type: 'finish', standings: msg.standings, scores: msg.scores, won: msg.won, stats: msg.stats, awards: msg.awards });\\n      case 'error':\\n        return toHub({ type: 'error', message: String(msg.message || '').slice(0, 500), fatal: msg.fatal === true });\\n      case 'send':\\n        return sendGame(msg);\\n120→      case 'progress':\\n        return sendProgress(msg);\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  /** Progress goes to this hub's scoreboard and to every other player's, never to a game. */\\n  function sendProgress(msg) {\\n    if (!welcomed) return issue('progress before welcome');\\n    const p = cleanProgress(msg);\\n    if (!p) return issue('progress needs a finite score');\\n130→    const now = clock.now();\\n    if (now - progressAt < LIMITS.progressMs) {\\n      stats.dropped++;\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    progressAt = now;\\n    onProgress(me, p);\\n    const envelope = { k: 'p', r: round, f: me, d: p };\\n    for (const target of keys.filter((k, id) => id !== me && !gone.has(id))) net.send(target, envelope, { reliable: false });\\n  }\\n140→\\n  function sendGame(msg) {\\n    if (!welcomed) return issue('send before welcome');\\n    let text;\\n    try {\\n      text = JSON.stringify(msg.data);\\n    } catch {\\n      return issue('send: data is not JSON');\\n    }\\n    if (text === undefined) return issue('send: no data');\\n150→    if (text.length > LIMITS.maxBytes) {\\n      stats.dropped++;\\n      return issue(`send: ${text.length} bytes is over the ${LIMITS.maxBytes}-byte limit`);\\n    }\\n    const now = clock.now();\\n    tokens = Math.min(LIMITS.burst, tokens + ((now - refilled) / 1000) * LIMITS.ratePerS);\\n    refilled = now;\\n    if (tokens < 1) {\\n      stats.dropped++;\\n      return issue(`send: over ${LIMITS.ratePerS} messages a second`);\\n160→    }\\n    tokens -= 1;\\n    let targets;\\n    if (msg.to === undefined || msg.to === null) {\\n      targets = keys.filter((k, id) => id !== me && !gone.has(id));\\n    } else {\\n      if (!Number.isInteger(msg.to) || msg.to < 0 || msg.to >= keys.length || msg.to === me) {\\n        return issue(`send: no player ${JSON.stringify(msg.to)} to send to`);\\n      }\\n      if (gone.has(msg.to)) return;\\n170→      targets = [keys[msg.to]];\\n    }\\n    const reliable = msg.reliable !== false;\\n    const envelope = { k: 'g', r: round, f: me, d: JSON.parse(text) };\\n    for (const target of targets) net.send(target, envelope, { reliable });\\n    stats.sent++;\\n    stats.bytesSent += text.length;\\n  }\\n\\n  function deliverGame(fromKey, env) {\\n180→    if (ended || gone.has(env.f)) return;\\n    if (keys[env.f] !== fromKey) return issue(`traffic from ${fromKey} claims to be player ${env.f}`);\\n    stats.received++;\\n    toGame({ type: 'message', from: env.f, data: env.d });\\n  }\\n\\n  function fromNet(fromKey, env) {\\n    if (!env || env.r !== round) return;\\n    if (env.k === 'p') {\\n      const p = cleanProgress(env.d);\\n190→      if (welcomed && !ended && p && keys[env.f] === fromKey && !gone.has(env.f)) onProgress(env.f, p);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (env.k === 'g') {\\n      if (welcomed) return deliverGame(fromKey, env);\\n      const size = JSON.stringify(env.d ?? null).length;\\n      if (queue.length >= LIMITS.queueMessages || queuedBytes + size > LIMITS.queueBytes) {\\n        stats.dropped++;\\n        return;\\n      }\",\"content_concise\":\"100→        return toHub({ type: 'hello', v: msg.v, client: String(msg.client || ''), mode: msg.mode ?? null, seats: msg.seats ?? null, card: ownsCard });\\n      case 'ready':\\n        if (!welcomed) return issue('ready before welcome');\\n        readySent = true;\\n        return toHub({ type: 'ready' });\\n      case 'answer':\\n        if (!ownsCard) return issue('answer without its own card: connect({ card: true })');\\n        if (!welcomed || started) return;\\n        if (msg.answer !== 'ready' && msg.answer !== 'more') return issue(`answer ${JSON.stringify(msg.answer)} is not ready or more`);\\n        return onAnswer(msg.answer);\\n110→      case 'result':\\n        if (!welcomed) return issue('result before welcome');\\n        return toHub({ type: 'result', time: msg.time, score: msg.score, stats: msg.stats, awards: msg.awards });\\n      case 'finish':\\n        if (!welcomed) return issue('finish before welcome');\\n        return toHub({ type: 'finish', standings: msg.standings, scores: msg.scores, won: msg.won, stats: msg.stats, awards: msg.awards });\\n      case 'error':\\n        return toHub({ type: 'error', message: String(msg.message || '').slice(0, 500), fatal: msg.fatal === true });\\n      case 'send':\\n        return sendGame(msg);\\n120→      case 'progress':\\n        return sendProgress(msg);\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  /** Progress goes to this hub's scoreboard and to every other player's, never to a game. */\\n  function sendProgress(msg) {\\n    if (!welcomed) return issue('progress before welcome');\\n    const p = cleanProgress(msg);\\n    if (!p) return issue('progress needs a finite score');\\n130→    const now = clock.now();\\n    if (now - progressAt < LIMITS.progressMs) {\\n      stats.dropped++;\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    progressAt = now;\\n    onProgress(me, p);\\n    const envelope = { k: 'p', r: round, f: me, d: p };\\n    for (const target of keys.filter((k, id) => id !== me && !gone.has(id))) net.send(target, envelope, { reliable: false });\\n  }\\n140→\\n  function sendGame(msg) {\\n    if (!welcomed) return issue('send before welcome');\\n    let text;\\n    try {\\n      text = JSON.stringify(msg.data);\\n    } catch {\\n      return issue('send: data is not JSON');\\n    }\\n    if (text === undefined) return issue('send: no data');\\n150→    if (text.length > LIMITS.maxBytes) {\\n      stats.dropped++;\\n      return issue(`send: ${text.length} bytes is over the ${LIMITS.maxBytes}-byte limit`);\\n    }\\n    const now = clock.now();\\n    tokens = Math.min(LIMITS.burst, tokens + ((now - refilled) / 1000) * LIMITS.ratePerS);\\n    refilled = now;\\n    if (tokens < 1) {\\n      stats.dropped++;\\n      return issue(`send: over ${LIMITS.ratePerS} messages a second`);\\n160→    }\\n    tokens -= 1;\\n    let targets;\\n    if (msg.to === undefined || msg.to === null) {\\n      targets = keys.filter((k, id) => id !== me && !gone.has(id));\\n    } else {\\n      if (!Number.isInteger(msg.to) || msg.to < 0 || msg.to >= keys.length || msg.to === me) {\\n        return issue(`send: no player ${JSON.stringify(msg.to)} to send to`);\\n      }\\n      if (gone.has(msg.to)) return;\\n170→      targets = [keys[msg.to]];\\n    }\\n    const reliable = msg.reliable !== false;\\n    const envelope = { k: 'g', r: round, f: me, d: JSON.parse(text) };\\n    for (const target of targets) net.send(target, envelope, { reliable });\\n    stats.sent++;\\n    stats.bytesSent += text.length;\\n  }\\n\\n  function deliverGame(fromKey, env) {\\n180→    if (ended || gone.has(env.f)) return;\\n    if (keys[env.f] !== fromKey) return issue(`traffic from ${fromKey} claims to be player ${env.f}`);\\n    stats.received++;\\n    toGame({ type: 'message', from: env.f, data: env.d });\\n  }\\n\\n  function fromNet(fromKey, env) {\\n    if (!env || env.r !== round) return;\\n    if (env.k === 'p') {\\n      const p = cleanProgress(env.d);\\n190→      if (welcomed && !ended && p && keys[env.f] === fromKey && !gone.has(env.f)) onProgress(env.f, p);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (env.k === 'g') {\\n      if (welcomed) return deliverGame(fromKey, env);\\n      const size = JSON.stringify(env.d ?? null).length;\\n      if (queue.length >= LIMITS.queueMessages || queuedBytes + size > LIMITS.queueBytes) {\\n        stats.dropped++;\\n        return;\\n      }\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/tools/hub/bridge.js\",\"offset\":100,\"limit\":100,\"raw_output\":\"        return toHub({ type: 'hello', v: msg.v, client: String(msg.client || ''), mode: msg.mode ?? null, seats: msg.seats ?? null, card: ownsCard });\\n      case 'ready':\\n        if (!welcomed) return issue('ready before welcome');\\n        readySent = true;\\n        return toHub({ type: 'ready' });\\n      case 'answer':\\n        if (!ownsCard) return issue('answer without its own card: connect({ card: true })');\\n        if (!welcomed || started) return;\\n        if (msg.answer !== 'ready' && msg.answer !== 'more') return issue(`answer ${JSON.stringify(msg.answer)} is not ready or more`);\\n        return onAnswer(msg.answer);\\n      case 'result':\\n        if (!welcomed) return issue('result before welcome');\\n        return toHub({ type: 'result', time: msg.time, score: msg.score, stats: msg.stats, awards: msg.awards });\\n      case 'finish':\\n        if (!welcomed) return issue('finish before welcome');\\n        return toHub({ type: 'finish', standings: msg.standings, scores: msg.scores, won: msg.won, stats: msg.stats, awards: msg.awards });\\n      case 'error':\\n        return toHub({ type: 'error', message: String(msg.message || '').slice(0, 500), fatal: msg.fatal === true });\\n      case 'send':\\n        return sendGame(msg);\\n      case 'progress':\\n        return sendProgress(msg);\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  /** Progress goes to this hub's scoreboard and to every other player's, never to a game. */\\n  function sendProgress(msg) {\\n    if (!welcomed) return issue('progress before welcome');\\n    const p = cleanProgress(msg);\\n    if (!p) return issue('progress needs a finite score');\\n    const now = clock.now();\\n    if (now - progressAt < LIMITS.progressMs) {\\n      stats.dropped++;\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    progressAt = now;\\n    onProgress(me, p);\\n    const envelope = { k: 'p', r: round, f: me, d: p };\\n    for (const target of keys.filter((k, id) => id !== me && !gone.has(id))) net.send(target, envelope, { reliable: false });\\n  }\\n\\n  function sendGame(msg) {\\n    if (!welcomed) return issue('send before welcome');\\n    let text;\\n    try {\\n      text = JSON.stringify(msg.data);\\n    } catch {\\n      return issue('send: data is not JSON');\\n    }\\n    if (text === undefined) return issue('send: no data');\\n    if (text.length > LIMITS.maxBytes) {\\n      stats.dropped++;\\n      return issue(`send: ${text.length} bytes is over the ${LIMITS.maxBytes}-byte limit`);\\n    }\\n    const now = clock.now();\\n    tokens = Math.min(LIMITS.burst, tokens + ((now - refilled) / 1000) * LIMITS.ratePerS);\\n    refilled = now;\\n    if (tokens < 1) {\\n      stats.dropped++;\\n      return issue(`send: over ${LIMITS.ratePerS} messages a second`);\\n    }\\n    tokens -= 1;\\n    let targets;\\n    if (msg.to === undefined || msg.to === null) {\\n      targets = keys.filter((k, id) => id !== me && !gone.has(id));\\n    } else {\\n      if (!Number.isInteger(msg.to) || msg.to < 0 || msg.to >= keys.length || msg.to === me) {\\n        return issue(`send: no player ${JSON.stringify(msg.to)} to send to`);\\n      }\\n      if (gone.has(msg.to)) return;\\n      targets = [keys[msg.to]];\\n    }\\n    const reliable = msg.reliable !== false;\\n    const envelope = { k: 'g', r: round, f: me, d: JSON.parse(text) };\\n    for (const target of targets) net.send(target, envelope, { reliable });\\n    stats.sent++;\\n    stats.bytesSent += text.length;\\n  }\\n\\n  function deliverGame(fromKey, env) {\\n    if (ended || gone.has(env.f)) return;\\n    if (keys[env.f] !== fromKey) return issue(`traffic from ${fromKey} claims to be player ${env.f}`);\\n    stats.received++;\\n    toGame({ type: 'message', from: env.f, data: env.d });\\n  }\\n\\n  function fromNet(fromKey, env) {\\n    if (!env || env.r !== round) return;\\n    if (env.k === 'p') {\\n      const p = cleanProgress(env.d);\\n      if (welcomed && !ended && p && keys[env.f] === fromKey && !gone.has(env.f)) onProgress(env.f, p);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (env.k === 'g') {\\n      if (welcomed) return deliverGame(fromKey, env);\\n      const size = JSON.stringify(env.d ?? null).length;\\n      if (queue.length >= LIMITS.queueMessages || queuedBytes + size > LIMITS.queueBytes) {\\n        stats.dropped++;\\n        return;\\n      }\\n\",\"total_lines\":339}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"d493d230-2ad6-4e20-bca8-88d86bdf309b"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_660","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"hub.send() broadcasts to all other players by default when msg.to is undefined.\n\nEach hub.send() increments both sender and recipient counters. A 'start' ping before host removal ensures traffic counts are already tallied, so the round voids correctly when the host leaves. The question is whether this ping is a protocol problem.\n\nThe ping is a game message and is harmless. Its type field must not be 'i' or 't', or the host or tick handlers could misinterpret it and desync. Every peer, including the server, should send on the 'start' event so all traffic counts are tallied.\n\nThe 'start' handler resets session state and sends a reliable 'here' message. One burst token is sufficient. The event fires after the card is set, before the host-leave delay. The server copy receives it as well.\n\nfinish() must still be wired for non-host-leave cases. The time-up handler calls finish after roughly 70 seconds, which should allow engine creation to complete. If four contexts take longer, the round voids with no result. play=120 and a 180-second timeout are planned.\n\nThe host-leave check does not require finish. The ping ensures traffic counts are tallied before the host leaves, so the round voids correctly with endReason 'host-left'. In a lossy four-player run, the last player is removed after 1.5 seconds and the remaining players wait 60 seconds; their traffic counts remain valid because the start ping precedes removal. If lockstep works, hash mismatches should not occur.\n\nEngine startup delays could cause tick mismatches, so the hub check must enforce zero mismatches. Late-starting clients should receive queued ticks when they register their handler. The host sends batches of up to eight ticks every 66 milliseconds; this rate is acceptable if the limit is twenty per second, but might drop ticks at a ten-per-second limit.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4a821052-a61e-487f-8e50-9708c1e0d1b7-167","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"interface Hub |type Hub |send\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/app/boot.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4a821052-a61e-487f-8e50-9708c1e0d1b7-168","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"export interface Hub|send\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/net"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1451,"output_tokens":1217,"cache_read_input_tokens":199936,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"f5f31b17-9714-49c1-b665-050c0c67f2e9"}
