{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_670","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Another agent is running a WebGPU Chrome instance from a different run directory.\n\nI will wait for the other Chrome instance to finish before launching hub. I will fix hub.mjs and rebuild HTML with Vite without a browser. I will check node syntax and review launch.mjs and the goal plan.\n\nA stale /tmp directory from November 4 is not from the current run. I will leave it alone and remove it only if it proves unused.\n\nI will match the existing single-quote style in hub.mjs. I will not modify boot.ts, since it already satisfies the line limit. I will start the Vite rebuild with a short temporary directory; previous builds took 30 to 90 seconds.\n\nI will set a 120-second timeout for the Vite build and background it if it takes longer. I can start the build immediately while editing hub.mjs, since hub.mjs is not part of the HTML bundle.\n\nI will run the Vite rebuild in a background process while editing hub.mjs. The build script sets PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE, CHROMIUM_PATH, and a temporary directory for tsx and vite sockets. I will log output to scratch. I also verified that esbuild will minify the send call into compact code.\n\nI will wait for the Vite build to finish before launching hub. I will grep for \"here\" after rebuilding to verify the send call is present. The direct call in boot.ts will not be tree-shaken.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Another WebGPU browser is already running, so I'll rebuild the page and fix the harness report first, then start the hub run when that browser is free."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e178eb28-44ba-4fbb-a7f6-96bb18ee4d61-20","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/tools/hub.mjs","old_string":"  let ok = false;\n  try {\n    await page.waitForFunction(() => document.body.dataset.complete === 'true', null, { timeout: 180000 });\n    const read = await page.evaluate(() => {\n      const bad = (window.__hubCheck?.checks ?? [])\n        .filter((item) => !item.pass)\n        .map((item) => `${item.name}: ${item.detail}`);\n      const mismatches = [];\n      for (const frame of document.querySelectorAll('iframe')) {\n        const list = frame.contentWindow?.__compass?.mismatches;\n        if (Array.isArray(list)) mismatches.push(...list);\n      }\n      return { pass: window.__hubCheck?.pass === true, bad, mismatches };\n    });\n    ok = read.pass && read.mismatches.length === 0;\n    var detailText = ok ? '' : [...read.bad, read.mismatches.length ? `mismatches ${read.mismatches.join(';')}` : ''].filter(Boolean).join(' | ');\n  } catch {\n    ok = false;\n  }\n  const detail = ok ? '' : (detailText ?? errors.join(' | '));\n  report(name, ok, detail.slice(0, 400));","new_string":"  let ok = false;\n  let detailText = '';\n  try {\n    await page.waitForFunction(() => document.body.dataset.complete === 'true', null, { timeout: 180000 });\n    const read = await page.evaluate(() => {\n      const bad = (window.__hubCheck?.checks ?? [])\n        .filter((item) => !item.pass)\n        .map((item) => `${item.name}: ${item.detail}`);\n      const mismatches = [];\n      for (const frame of document.querySelectorAll('iframe')) {\n        const list = frame.contentWindow?.__compass?.mismatches;\n        if (Array.isArray(list)) mismatches.push(...list);\n      }\n      return { pass: window.__hubCheck?.pass === true, bad, mismatches };\n    });\n    ok = read.pass && read.mismatches.length === 0;\n    detailText = ok\n      ? ''\n      : [...read.bad, read.mismatches.length ? `mismatches ${read.mismatches.join(';')}` : ''].filter(Boolean).join(' | ');\n  } catch (error) {\n    ok = false;\n    detailText = errors.join(' | ') || String(error?.message ?? error);\n