{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-520e7b89-77bc-4fe0-a731-57ed478b6b0f-32","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"70→for (const [name, query] of runs) {\\n  const page = await browser.newPage();\\n  const errors = [];\\n  page.on('pageerror', (error) => errors.push(error.message));\\n  await page.goto(`http://127.0.0.1:${port}/harness.html?game=${gameName}&${query}`);\\n  let ok = false;\\n  let detailText = '';\\n  try {\\n    await page.waitForFunction(() => document.body.dataset.complete === 'true', null, { timeout: 180000 });\\n    const read = await page.evaluate(() => {\\n80→      const bad = (window.__hubCheck?.checks ?? [])\\n        .filter((item) => !item.pass)\\n        .map((item) => `${item.name}: ${item.detail}`);\\n      const mismatches = [];\\n      for (const frame of document.querySelectorAll('iframe')) {\\n        const list = frame.contentWindow?.__compass?.mismatches;\\n        if (Array.isArray(list)) mismatches.push(...list);\\n      }\\n      return { pass: window.__hubCheck?.pass === true, bad, mismatches };\\n    });\\n90→    ok = read.pass && read.mismatches.length === 0;\\n    detailText = ok\\n      ? ''\\n      : [...read.bad, read.mismatches.length ? `mismatches ${read.mismatches.join(';')}` : '']\\n          .filter(Boolean)\\n          .join(' | ');\\n  } catch (error) {\\n    ok = false;\\n    detailText = errors.join(' | ') || String(error?.message ?? error);\\n  }\\n100→  report(name, ok, detailText);\\n  await page.close();\\n}\\n\\nconst solo = await browser.newPage();\\nawait solo.goto(`http://127.0.0.1:${port}/${gameName}`);\\nlet soloOk = false;\\ntry {\\n  await solo.waitForFunction(\\n    () => window.__engine && window.__engine.ready && window.__compass?.screen === 'title',\",\"content_concise\":\"70→for (const [name, query] of runs) {\\n  const page = await browser.newPage();\\n  const errors = [];\\n  page.on('pageerror', (error) => errors.push(error.message));\\n  await page.goto(`http://127.0.0.1:${port}/harness.html?game=${gameName}&${query}`);\\n  let ok = false;\\n  let detailText = '';\\n  try {\\n    await page.waitForFunction(() => document.body.dataset.complete === 'true', null, { timeout: 180000 });\\n    const read = await page.evaluate(() => {\\n80→      const bad = (window.__hubCheck?.checks ?? [])\\n        .filter((item) => !item.pass)\\n        .map((item) => `${item.name}: ${item.detail}`);\\n      const mismatches = [];\\n      for (const frame of document.querySelectorAll('iframe')) {\\n        const list = frame.contentWindow?.__compass?.mismatches;\\n        if (Array.isArray(list)) mismatches.push(...list);\\n      }\\n      return { pass: window.__hubCheck?.pass === true, bad, mismatches };\\n    });\\n90→    ok = read.pass && read.mismatches.length === 0;\\n    detailText = ok\\n      ? ''\\n      : [...read.bad, read.mismatches.length ? `mismatches ${read.mismatches.join(';')}` : '']\\n          .filter(Boolean)\\n          .join(' | ');\\n  } catch (error) {\\n    ok = false;\\n    detailText = errors.join(' | ') || String(error?.message ?? error);\\n  }\\n100→  report(name, ok, detailText);\\n  await page.close();\\n}\\n\\nconst solo = await browser.newPage();\\nawait solo.goto(`http://127.0.0.1:${port}/${gameName}`);\\nlet soloOk = false;\\ntry {\\n  await solo.waitForFunction(\\n    () => window.__engine && window.__engine.ready && window.__compass?.screen === 'title',\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/tools/hub.mjs\",\"offset\":70,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"for (const [name, query] of runs) {\\n  const page = await browser.newPage();\\n  const errors = [];\\n  page.on('pageerror', (error) => errors.push(error.message));\\n  await page.goto(`http://127.0.0.1:${port}/harness.html?game=${gameName}&${query}`);\\n  let ok = false;\\n  let detailText = '';\\n  try {\\n    await page.waitForFunction(() => document.body.dataset.complete === 'true', null, { timeout: 180000 });\\n    const read = await page.evaluate(() => {\\n      const bad = (window.__hubCheck?.checks ?? [])\\n        .filter((item) => !item.pass)\\n        .map((item) => `${item.name}: ${item.detail}`);\\n      const mismatches = [];\\n      for (const frame of document.querySelectorAll('iframe')) {\\n        const list = frame.contentWindow?.__compass?.mismatches;\\n        if (Array.isArray(list)) mismatches.push(...list);\\n      }\\n      return { pass: window.__hubCheck?.pass === true, bad, mismatches };\\n    });\\n    ok = read.pass && read.mismatches.length === 0;\\n    detailText = ok\\n      ? ''\\n      : [...read.bad, read.mismatches.length ? `mismatches ${read.mismatches.join(';')}` : '']\\n          .filter(Boolean)\\n          .join(' | ');\\n  } catch (error) {\\n    ok = false;\\n    detailText = errors.join(' | ') || String(error?.message ?? error);\\n  }\\n  report(name, ok, detailText);\\n  await page.close();\\n}\\n\\nconst solo = await browser.newPage();\\nawait solo.goto(`http://127.0.0.1:${port}/${gameName}`);\\nlet soloOk = false;\\ntry {\\n  await solo.waitForFunction(\\n    () => window.__engine && window.__engine.ready && window.__compass?.screen === 'title',\\n\",\"total_lines\":120}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"e90bbc5b-0156-4725-8183-08f146cff790"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_679","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Launching the hub and monitor.\n\nWriting a scratch watcher to monitor hub output. The wrapper will avoid `set -e` traps that skip the EXIT handler. The monitor polls every 15 seconds and wakes only on failures or exit.\n\nConsidering OOM edge cases. If Chrome is killed, the hub catches the error and continues. If Node is killed, the wrapper may survive to log EXIT or the monitor will detect the dead process. The wrapper PID will be recorded in the log first.\n\nThe wrapper will echo its PID and timestamp into both the log and the function output so the monitor can locate it. The launch command sets up a temporary directory, exports the Playwright host platform override and Chromium path, runs hub.mjs from the package directory, and captures the exit status.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5ec206eb-5204-411d-acef-3a890a4ce78e-33","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/watch-hub.sh","content":"#!/bin/bash\n# Wake on the first failed hub check, then on EXIT. Silent while the run is healthy.\nLOG=$1\nPID=$2\nseen=0\nwhile true; do\n  if [[ -f \"$LOG\" ]]; then\n    if [[ \"$seen\" -eq 0 ]] && grep -q '\"ok\":false' \"$LOG\"; then\n      echo \"ACTION_REQUIRED: $(grep -m1 '\"ok\":false' \"$LOG\")\"\n      seen=1\n    fi\n    if grep -q '^EXIT:' \"$LOG\"; then\n      line=$(grep '^EXIT:' \"$LOG\" | tail -1)\n      fails=$(grep -c '\"ok\":false' \"$LOG\" || true)\n      if [[ \"$line\" == \"EXIT:0\" && \"$fails\" -eq 0 ]]; then\n        echo \"DONE: $line\"\n        exit 0\n      fi\n      echo \"FAILED: $line fails=$fails\"\n      exit 1\n    fi\n  fi\n  if [[ -n \"$PID\" ]] && ! kill -0 \"$PID\" 2>/dev/null; then\n    sleep 2\n    if [[ -f \"$LOG\" ]] && grep -q '^EXIT:' \"$LOG\"; then\n      continue\n    fi\n    echo \"FAILED: pid $PID exited without EXIT\"\n    exit 1\n  fi\n  sleep 15\ndone\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":620,"output_tokens":938,"cache_read_input_tokens":71552,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"2bef3053-01c6-4deb-890b-8d42452c608c"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-5ec206eb-5204-411d-acef-3a890a4ce78e-33","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"#!/bin/bash\\n# Wake on the first failed hub check, then on EXIT. Silent while the run is healthy.\\nLOG=$1\\nPID=$2\\nseen=0\\nwhile true; do\\n  if [[ -f \\\"$LOG\\\" ]]; then\\n    if [[ \\\"$seen\\\" -eq 0 ]] && grep -q '\\\"ok\\\":false' \\\"$LOG\\\"; then\\n      echo \\\"ACTION_REQUIRED: $(grep -m1 '\\\"ok\\\":false' \\\"$LOG\\\")\\\"\\n      seen=1\\n    fi\\n    if grep -q '^EXIT:' \\\"$LOG\\\"; then\\n      line=$(grep '^EXIT:' \\\"$LOG\\\" | tail -1)\\n      fails=$(grep -c '\\\"ok\\\":false' \\\"$LOG\\\" || true)\\n      if [[ \\\"$line\\\" == \\\"EXIT:0\\\" && \\\"$fails\\\" -eq 0 ]]; then\\n        echo \\\"DONE: $line\\\"\\n        exit 0\\n      fi\\n      echo \\\"FAILED: $line fails=$fails\\\"\\n      exit 1\\n    fi\\n  fi\\n  if [[ -n \\\"$PID\\\" ]] && ! kill -0 \\\"$PID\\\" 2>/dev/null; then\\n    sleep 2\\n    if [[ -f \\\"$LOG\\\" ]] && grep -q '^EXIT:' \\\"$LOG\\\"; then\\n      continue\\n    fi\\n    echo \\\"FAILED: pid $PID exited without EXIT\\\"\\n    exit 1\\n  fi\\n  sleep 15\\ndone\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/watch-hub.sh has been created.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/watch-hub.sh has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/watch-hub.sh\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"#!/bin/bash\\n# Wake on the first failed hub check, then on EXIT. Silent while the run is healthy.\\nLOG=$1\\nPID=$2\\nseen=0\\nwhile true; do\\n  if [[ -f \\\"$LOG\\\" ]]; then\\n    if [[ \\\"$seen\\\" -eq 0 ]] && grep -q '\\\"ok\\\":false' \\\"$LOG\\\"; then\\n      echo \\\"ACTION_REQUIRED: $(grep -m1 '\\\"ok\\\":false' \\\"$LOG\\\")\\\"\\n      seen=1\\n    fi\\n    if grep -q '^EXIT:' \\\"$LOG\\\"; then\\n      line=$(grep '^EXIT:' \\\"$LOG\\\" | tail -1)\\n      fails=$(grep -c '\\\"ok\\\":false' \\\"$LOG\\\" || true)\\n      if [[ \\\"$line\\\" == \\\"EXIT:0\\\" && \\\"$fails\\\" -eq 0 ]]; then\\n        echo \\\"DONE: $line\\\"\\n        exit 0\\n      fi\\n      echo \\\"FAILED: $line fails=$fails\\\"\\n      exit 1\\n    fi\\n  fi\\n  if [[ -n \\\"$PID\\\" ]] && ! kill -0 \\\"$PID\\\" 2>/dev/null; then\\n    sleep 2\\n    if [[ -f \\\"$LOG\\\" ]] && grep -q '^EXIT:' \\\"$LOG\\\"; then\\n      continue\\n    fi\\n    echo \\\"FAILED: pid $PID exited without EXIT\\\"\\n    exit 1\\n  fi\\n  sleep 15\\ndone\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"6a7c8e58-2d9b-4394-8646-6298cda15f8f"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_680","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Launching the hub in the background and capturing its process ID.\n\nThe command wrapper returns a task ID rather than the actual PID. I'll write the real process ID to a scratch file immediately before any slow work begins, so the monitor can read it right away.\n\nThe monitor will wait up to ten seconds for the PID file. The command will echo the process ID immediately before backgrounding.\n\nThe monitor will parse the wrapper PID from the START line in the log instead of using a separate scratch file. This avoids a race condition where the monitor starts before the PID is written.\n\nThe monitor script will poll the log file for the wrapper PID using sed. I am also considering a two-step launch: write the process ID to a scratch file immediately, then use block_until_ms so the ID appears in the command output before it backgrounds.\n\nThe command will echo its process ID immediately, then run with block_until_ms set to 5000 so the ID appears in the output before the tool backgrounds it. The monitor will start in the next turn once the PID is captured.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-cba18834-9168-4169-b398-e1e67e0e2fd1-34","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"SCRATCH=\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer\"\nPKG=\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731\"\nLOG=\"$SCRATCH/hub-r4.log\"\nTMP=\"$(mktemp -d /tmp/g.XXXXXX)\"\necho \"PID:$$ TMP:$TMP\"\n{\n  echo \"START $(date -Iseconds) tmp=$TMP wrapper=$$\"\n  export TMPDIR=\"$TMP\"\n  export PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE=ubuntu24.04-x64\n  export CHROMIUM_PATH=/home/micha/.cache/ms-playwright/chromium-1243/chrome-linux64/chrome\n  cd \"$PKG\"\n  node labs/game/tools/hub.mjs\n  status=$?\n  echo \"EXIT:$status\"\n  rm -rf \"$TMP\"\n  exit $status\n} > \"$LOG\" 2>&1","description":"Run AI Hub harness with play=90","block_until_ms":0}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1122,"output_tokens":1066,"cache_read_input_tokens":72064,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"50aaba50-7588-4e1f-818c-6e3acd8ec9cf"}
