05,116,104,32,110,111,32,115,101,115,115,105,111,110,34,44,34,111,107,34,58,116,114,117,101,44,34,100,101,116,97,105,108,34,58,34,34,125,10,69,88,73,84,58,49,10],\"output_for_prompt\":\"exit: 0\\n=== our node ===\\n=== chrome tmp g.uTdOty ===\\nnone\\n=== python hub-serve ===\\n=== log ===\\n9 /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/hub-r4.log\\nSTART 2026-11-05T02:43:58-07:00 tmp=/tmp/g.uTdOty wrapper=383182\\n(node:383189) Warning: The 'NO_COLOR' env is ignored due to the 'FORCE_COLOR' env being set.\\n(Use `node --trace-warnings ...` to show where the warning was created)\\n{\\\"name\\\":\\\"hub 2 players\\\",\\\"ok\\\":false,\\\"detail\\\":\\\"the round ends with a valid result: void (no-result)\\\"}\\n{\\\"name\\\":\\\"hub 4 players lossy\\\",\\\"ok\\\":false,\\\"detail\\\":\\\"the round ends with a valid result: void (no-result)\\\"}\\n{\\\"name\\\":\\\"hub host leaves\\\",\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"detail\\\":\\\"\\\"}\\n{\\\"name\\\":\\\"hub server copy\\\",\\\"ok\\\":false,\\\"detail\\\":\\\"a copy with no player of its own runs the world (as a server would): void (no-result), host 2, server sent 1 | the round ends with a valid result: void (no-result)\\\"}\\n{\\\"name\\\":\\\"game with no session\\\",\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"detail\\\":\\\"\\\"}\\nEXIT:1\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"command\":\"echo \\\"=== our node ===\\\"\\nps -o pid,ppid,etime,cmd -p 383182,383189 --no-headers\\necho \\\"=== chrome tmp g.uTdOty ===\\\"\\npgrep -af 'g.uTdOty' || echo none\\necho \\\"=== python hub-serve ===\\\"\\npgrep -af 'http.server' | head -20\\necho \\\"=== log ===\\\"\\nwc -l /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/hub-r4.log\\ntail -20 /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/hub-r4.log\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Find this hub run's processes and latest log\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3%2Fwork/01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151/terminal/call-48b1408b-6344-4792-9ae4-432bd8debe9c-44.log\",\"total_bytes\":975}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"13d0f3de-ae73-456d-881c-d066d53cd92b"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_685","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The hub run has finished.\n\nTraffic is fixed across all scenarios. The hub 2-player and 4-player lossy runs failed on result checks only. The hub host leaves and game-without-session tests passed. The server copy test passed presence but failed on the valid result check. The remaining issue is finish-within-grace for the two-player, four-player, and server scenarios.\n\nThe host-leave scenario needs no game finish. The four-player run passed traffic and did not OOM, so the failure is strictly a timing issue. Either creating four engine contexts exceeded the grace window, or finish is not being called when the engine is ready. The full run duration is being checked.\n\nThe harness completed all scenarios normally, so the failures are not timeouts. Each scenario ran its full play and grace window without receiving a finish signal. Engine creation should take only seconds, so the bug is likely that the time-up handler never fires once the engine is ready. This rules out warmup timing as the cause.\n\nThe finish signal is never reaching the coordinator. The protocol check passed, so the message was not rejected as invalid. The likely causes are a missing startRound call, an unregistered time-up handler, or the finish function returning early because the node is not the host.\n\nThe protocol check passed, so the host is not rejecting the finish message. Engine creation is therefore not throwing an error. The remaining suspects are a missing startRound call, a false isHost flag, or the time-up handler failing to fire. The two-player play window lasts roughly 55 to 70 seconds, which should be plenty for engine setup.\n\nTwo engine contexts might take 20 to 30 seconds to create, which should still fit inside the grace window. Playwright headless mode may throttle background iframes. The exact run duration is being checked by comparing the log start time with the file modification time.\n\nThe run lasted about three and a half minutes, confirming each scenario waited the full play window. The problem is therefore either engine creation taking over sixty seconds per page or finish failing after the engine is ready. A targeted diagnostic run of just the two-player scenario with extra logging would avoid rebuilding the large HTML harness.\n\nRebuilding the full HTML harness is too slow. A one-off script running only the two-player scenario with auto-play and a ninety-second window would dump engine state at the end without waiting for the full suite.\n\nA scratch probe will run the existing harness without rebuilding. It will check each iframe's `__engine.ready`, `__compass.screen`, performance timing, and console output. If the engine is ready but no result arrives, the finish handler is broken. If it is not ready, warmup timed out. The probe will also listen to console messages.\n\nThe harness waits for `window.__engine.step` to exist before pausing the engine and seeding the round. This confirms the engine is not ready until `createEngine` completes. The probe will check whether `__engine.ready` is set earlier than this step property.\n\nThe time-up handler is only registered inside startRound. If createEngine is still running during warmup, the timeout event is queued but never processed. The engine must finish initializing before startRound can attach the handler.\n\nThe probe will check whether `__engine.ready` is true when the harness completes. If engine creation finishes during or just after the grace window, the time-up handler may flush too late. The round would already be void by then, so `receive()` returns early and no result arrives.\n\nThe probe will check `__compass.screen` and console errors. It will also look at e2e logs to estimate engine creation time for a single context.\n\nA new hypothesis is that `hub.finish` might be blocked by rate limits, since it uses a different post type than other messages. The next step is to read `hub.finish` in `session.js`.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9cf550ba-3784-4ff6-abf0-6cdc8bd1fd61-45","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"hub\\.finish|function finish","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/vendor/session.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9cf550ba-3784-4ff6-abf0-6cdc8bd1fd61-46","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"interface HubInfo|isHost|players","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/net/hub.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9cf550ba-3784-4ff6-abf0-6cdc8bd1fd61-47","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"stat -c '%y' /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/hub-r4.log\nls -d /tmp/g.uTdOty 2>/dev/null || echo tmp-cleaned\npgrep -af 'hub.mjs|g.uTdOty' || echo 'hub processes gone'\n# kill the finished monitor if still around — it already exited\necho done","description":"Confirm hub run ended and temp dir was removed"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5863,"output_tokens":2191,"cache_read_input_tokens":84352,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"54d62e73-d90a-42bf-83b0-46a7ab23ec61"}
