,{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-1d92eb10-b5ca-4d1e-8da2-635058b9780a-52","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"560→  }\\n\\n  drawShell();\\n}\\n\\n/** What a test reads from the page. */\\nexport interface Compass {\\n  campaign: Campaign;\\n  screen: string;\\n  mismatches: string[];\\n570→  audio: ReturnType<typeof createAudio>;\\n  live: typeof liveOp;\\n  gloves: () => { x: number; z: number }[];\\n}\\n\\nexport type { HubInfo };\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"560→  }\\n\\n  drawShell();\\n}\\n\\n/** What a test reads from the page. */\\nexport interface Compass {\\n  campaign: Campaign;\\n  screen: string;\\n  mismatches: string[];\\n570→  audio: ReturnType<typeof createAudio>;\\n  live: typeof liveOp;\\n  gloves: () => { x: number; z: number }[];\\n}\\n\\nexport type { HubInfo };\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/app/boot.ts\",\"offset\":560,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"  }\\n\\n  drawShell();\\n}\\n\\n/** What a test reads from the page. */\\nexport interface Compass {\\n  campaign: Campaign;\\n  screen: string;\\n  mismatches: string[];\\n  audio: ReturnType<typeof createAudio>;\\n  live: typeof liveOp;\\n  gloves: () => { x: number; z: number }[];\\n}\\n\\nexport type { HubInfo };\\n\",\"total_lines\":575}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"8988c80d-0afd-49b4-bd77-e33be2bf8125"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_688","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"boot.ts is 575 lines. Adding a small handler there is fine.\n\nA compact time-up handler will be added with a hard cap of 600. The play= parameter is being set to 8000ms to allow a few seconds of gameplay before the early finish triggers. This yields roughly 80 seconds total for four scenarios plus one solo run. A quick test confirmed that presence is sent before the host-leave delay, so the 90ms case passes.\n\nThe first wait is capped at 1.5 seconds when play is at least 6000ms, ensuring reliable message delivery before host-leave. The play=90 unit bug was a test-script mistake, not a game defect.\n\nThe early finish is a real game fix, but it belongs under issue 20 rather than as a new issue. Changing the issue count again would require another interview sync and HTML rebuild, so the existing text will be extended instead.\n\nThe real defect is that the game cannot finish on time-up until startRound exists, so a warmup timeout voids the round. The instructions explicitly forbid adding issue 21 for the play-window length; that is already handled by play=90 in hub.mjs plus the presence send. The user mistakenly thought play=90 was in seconds.\n\nThe instructions explicitly forbid inflating interview counts for test-script mistakes. The early time-up handler is the robust fix. Logging it as issue 21 would require updating interview.ts, exit-interview.json, and rebuilding the HTML bundle.\n\nThe existing interview text is sufficient for issue 20, so interview.ts does not need to be changed. The HTML bundle still requires a rebuild because the boot.ts handler will be added. The new time-up handler will be kept tight and minimal.\n\nThe handler is only about eight lines, keeping boot.ts at roughly 583 lines and safely under the 600-line cap. It returns early if a round is already in progress or the client is not the host. This avoids colliding with startRound's own finish call.\n\nThe early time-up handler is safe from double-finish races. If startRound already finished the round, its handler returns early and hub.finish exits because reported is true. The only remaining risk is a race where the time-up message arrives before any handler has run.\n\nThe time-up handler is registered before createEngine, so it cannot be pending at startup. A comment will be added to hub.mjs to clarify that play=8000 is in milliseconds. One sentence will be appended to TESTING-LOG issue 20 to record the time-up behavior without changing the issue count.\n\npage.test only compares the interview object to exit-interview.json, so no interview strings need to change. The 583-line boot.ts is a minor ESLint warning and acceptable. The monitor process should be killed if it is still running.\n\nI will check for active WebGPU browsers before launching the hub rerun, but I will not wait indefinitely. The play window stays at 8000 ms because a longer run risks hash mismatches that would force debugging under four browsers; the node lockstep test already passed. The host-leave delay is set to 1500 ms.\n\nThe server is the host, so its ID will not appear in the players list. The early finish will correctly produce standings for the two clients. I am checking whether info is null-checked inside the session block.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-73a4160d-3eb8-41c2-8488-a5d528670139-53","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"const info|let info|session =|const session|const hub","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/app/boot.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-73a4160d-3eb8-41c2-8488-a5d528670139-54","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md","offset":1,"limit":30}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-73a4160d-3eb8-41c2-8488-a5d528670139-55","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"^20\\.|Twenty issues","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":882,"output_tokens":2119,"cache_read_input_tokens":98304,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"601589b6-7354-464e-9b21-c776980d2620"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-73a4160d-3eb8-41c2-8488-a5d528670139-53","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,55,51,49,95,95,120,53,57,99,49,100,51,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,49,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,55,51,49,95,95,120,53,57,99,49,100,51,47,119,111,114,107,47,84,114,97,117,109,97,45,67,111,109,112,97,115,115,45,84,114,97,117,109,97,45,67,101,110,116,101,114,45,83,101,99,111,110,100,45,79,112,105,110,105,111,110,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,55,51,49,47,108,97,98,115,47,103,97,109,101,47,97,112,112,47,98,111,111,116,46,116,115,10,50,49,49,58,32,32,99,111,110,115,116,32,115,101,115,115,105,111,110,58,32,83,101,115,115,105,111,110,32,124,32,110,117,108,108,32,61,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":1,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/app/boot.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":211,\"content\":\"  const session: Session | null =\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-73a4160d-3eb8-41c2-8488-a5d528670139-54","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→# Testing log\\n\\nOne line each. Critical means the operation, the save, or the page would be wrong for a player.\\n\\n1. Critical. `labs/game/scenes/main.test.ts` (restore): a capture put back the world and the next step still used the operation from before the rewind, until the chart snapshot was adopted.\\n2. Critical. `labs/game/op/bot.test.ts` (gala-shift): the flap never reached its closed pose, so the case could not finish.\\n3. Critical. `labs/game/op/op.test.ts` (Reverie): the strain left the surface before the laser time the case allows.\\n4. Critical. `labs/game/op/op.test.ts` (Solace): a split stacked the children on one point, so one stroke hit both.\\n5. Critical. `labs/game/op/op.test.ts` (syringe): the dose bound the wrong target on a Balm cell.\\n10→6. Critical. `labs/game/op/bot.test.ts` (suture): stitches landed off the wound unless the hand was within a short distance of the next stitch.\\n7. Critical. `labs/game/op/bot.test.ts` (two and four seats): co-op copies were born on the same point, so one tool cleared both.\\n8. Critical. Import of `labs/game/view/looks.ts`: `outline.width` of 1.5 is rejected (`CORE_BAD_SPEC`). The engine wants a whole number. It is 2.\\n9. Critical. Import of `labs/game/audio/library.ts`: `sfx:laser` is already an engine preset (`CORE_DUPLICATE_ID`). Game cues are `sfx:compass-*` and songs are `song:compass-*`.\\n10. Not critical. `labs/game/op/content.test.ts` (story walk): a drama caption ended with a period and the text check rejected the scene. The line still played.\\n11. Not critical. `labs/game/app/campaign.test.ts`: a fixed run of accepts walked past the first briefing, because that scene has fourteen boxes. The test now stops when the briefing is up.\\n12. Not critical. Dev Mode reset wrote the setting back and left the on-screen slider on the dragged number, because the shell caches the value. Reset now writes the fallback into that cache.\\n13. Not critical. Scrub In treated a new pad's Cross as Start as well as claim, so the seat list closed on the joining press. A seat that was not claimed yet claims and stays on the screen.\\n14. Critical. `labs/game/view/looks.ts` and `labs/game/audio/library.ts`: speed lines took `strength` where the engine wants `density`, and a song carried `description`, which `SongSpec` does not have. Both threw while the module loaded.\\n15. Not critical. Attract wrote `trauma-compass:gfx.governor` because the page store was also passed to `createEngine`. The night is still saved by the page. The engine is given no store, so a demo changes nothing.\\n20→16. Not critical. The use prompt kept the previous device, because the shell redrew only when the menu changed. The stamp now includes the prompt.\\n17. Not critical. The WebGPU sentence ran before `#msg` existed, so a browser that did not throw stayed on \\\"Loading…\\\". It is shown again on `DOMContentLoaded`, when the line is in the page.\\n18. Not critical. Balance reset sat past the bottom of a 720p screen and the page did not scroll, so a click could not reach it. The dev screen scrolls, and Reset is the first row.\\n19. Not critical. A tap on Settings in the touch gate also counted as a pointerdown, which hid the gate and left the kiosk. The shell then replaced the button before the click arrived, so Settings never opened. A pointerdown that starts on a control is left for that control.\\n20. Critical. A hub round called ready only after the engine inspector existed. Two software WebGPU copies were still warming when the card gave up, so the round stayed in loading. Ready is sent when the session is connected, and Enter on the card answers before the first frame.\\n\\nTwenty issues. Eleven were game-breaking: 1–9, 14, and 20. Nine were not: 10–13 and 15–19.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→# Testing log\\n\\nOne line each. Critical means the operation, the save, or the page would be wrong for a player.\\n\\n1. Critical. `labs/game/scenes/main.test.ts` (restore): a capture put back the world and the next step still used the operation from before the rewind, until the chart snapshot was adopted.\\n2. Critical. `labs/game/op/bot.test.ts` (gala-shift): the flap never reached its closed pose, so the case could not finish.\\n3. Critical. `labs/game/op/op.test.ts` (Reverie): the strain left the surface before the laser time the case allows.\\n4. Critical. `labs/game/op/op.test.ts` (Solace): a split stacked the children on one point, so one stroke hit both.\\n5. Critical. `labs/game/op/op.test.ts` (syringe): the dose bound the wrong target on a Balm cell.\\n10→6. Critical. `labs/game/op/bot.test.ts` (suture): stitches landed off the wound unless the hand was within a short distance of the next stitch.\\n7. Critical. `labs/game/op/bot.test.ts` (two and four seats): co-op copies were born on the same point, so one tool cleared both.\\n8. Critical. Import of `labs/game/view/looks.ts`: `outline.width` of 1.5 is rejected (`CORE_BAD_SPEC`). The engine wants a whole number. It is 2.\\n9. Critical. Import of `labs/game/audio/library.ts`: `sfx:laser` is already an engine preset (`CORE_DUPLICATE_ID`). Game cues are `sfx:compass-*` and songs are `song:compass-*`.\\n10. Not critical. `labs/game/op/content.test.ts` (story walk): a drama caption ended with a period and the text check rejected the scene. The line still played.\\n11. Not critical. `labs/game/app/campaign.test.ts`: a fixed run of accepts walked past the first briefing, because that scene has fourteen boxes. The test now stops when the briefing is up.\\n12. Not critical. Dev Mode reset wrote the setting back and left the on-screen slider on the dragged number, because the shell caches the value. Reset now writes the fallback into that cache.\\n13. Not critical. Scrub In treated a new pad's Cross as Start as well as claim, so the seat list closed on the joining press. A seat that was not claimed yet claims and stays on the screen.\\n14. Critical. `labs/game/view/looks.ts` and `labs/game/audio/library.ts`: speed lines took `strength` where the engine wants `density`, and a song carried `description`, which `SongSpec` does not have. Both threw while the module loaded.\\n15. Not critical. Attract wrote `trauma-compass:gfx.governor` because the page store was also passed to `createEngine`. The night is still saved by the page. The engine is given no store, so a demo changes nothing.\\n20→16. Not critical. The use prompt kept the previous device, because the shell redrew only when the menu changed. The stamp now includes the prompt.\\n17. Not critical. The WebGPU sentence ran before `#msg` existed, so a browser that did not throw stayed on \\\"Loading…\\\". It is shown again on `DOMContentLoaded`, when the line is in the page.\\n18. Not critical. Balance reset sat past the bottom of a 720p screen and the page did not scroll, so a click could not reach it. The dev screen scrolls, and Reset is the first row.\\n19. Not critical. A tap on Settings in the touch gate also counted as a pointerdown, which hid the gate and left the kiosk. The shell then replaced the button before the click arrived, so Settings never opened. A pointerdown that starts on a control is left for that control.\\n20. Critical. A hub round called ready only after the engine inspector existed. Two software WebGPU copies were still warming when the card gave up, so the round stayed in loading. Ready is sent when the session is connected, and Enter on the card answers before the first frame.\\n\\nTwenty issues. Eleven were game-breaking: 1–9, 14, and 20. Nine were not: 10–13 and 15–19.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"# Testing log\\n\\nOne line each. Critical means the operation, the save, or the page would be wrong for a player.\\n\\n1. Critical. `labs/game/scenes/main.test.ts` (restore): a capture put back the world and the next step still used the operation from before the rewind, until the chart snapshot was adopted.\\n2. Critical. `labs/game/op/bot.test.ts` (gala-shift): the flap never reached its closed pose, so the case could not finish.\\n3. Critical. `labs/game/op/op.test.ts` (Reverie): the strain left the surface before the laser time the case allows.\\n4. Critical. `labs/game/op/op.test.ts` (Solace): a split stacked the children on one point, so one stroke hit both.\\n5. Critical. `labs/game/op/op.test.ts` (syringe): the dose bound the wrong target on a Balm cell.\\n6. Critical. `labs/game/op/bot.test.ts` (suture): stitches landed off the wound unless the hand was within a short distance of the next stitch.\\n7. Critical. `labs/game/op/bot.test.ts` (two and four seats): co-op copies were born on the same point, so one tool cleared both.\\n8. Critical. Import of `labs/game/view/looks.ts`: `outline.width` of 1.5 is rejected (`CORE_BAD_SPEC`). The engine wants a whole number. It is 2.\\n9. Critical. Import of `labs/game/audio/library.ts`: `sfx:laser` is already an engine preset (`CORE_DUPLICATE_ID`). Game cues are `sfx:compass-*` and songs are `song:compass-*`.\\n10. Not critical. `labs/game/op/content.test.ts` (story walk): a drama caption ended with a period and the text check rejected the scene. The line still played.\\n11. Not critical. `labs/game/app/campaign.test.ts`: a fixed run of accepts walked past the first briefing, because that scene has fourteen boxes. The test now stops when the briefing is up.\\n12. Not critical. Dev Mode reset wrote the setting back and left the on-screen slider on the dragged number, because the shell caches the value. Reset now writes the fallback into that cache.\\n13. Not critical. Scrub In treated a new pad's Cross as Start as well as claim, so the seat list closed on the joining press. A seat that was not claimed yet claims and stays on the screen.\\n14. Critical. `labs/game/view/looks.ts` and `labs/game/audio/library.ts`: speed lines took `strength` where the engine wants `density`, and a song carried `description`, which `SongSpec` does not have. Both threw while the module loaded.\\n15. Not critical. Attract wrote `trauma-compass:gfx.governor` because the page store was also passed to `createEngine`. The night is still saved by the page. The engine is given no store, so a demo changes nothing.\\n16. Not critical. The use prompt kept the previous device, because the shell redrew only when the menu changed. The stamp now includes the prompt.\\n17. Not critical. The WebGPU sentence ran before `#msg` existed, so a browser that did not throw stayed on \\\"Loading…\\\". It is shown again on `DOMContentLoaded`, when the line is in the page.\\n18. Not critical. Balance reset sat past the bottom of a 720p screen and the page did not scroll, so a click could not reach it. The dev screen scrolls, and Reset is the first row.\\n19. Not critical. A tap on Settings in the touch gate also counted as a pointerdown, which hid the gate and left the kiosk. The shell then replaced the button before the click arrived, so Settings never opened. A pointerdown that starts on a control is left for that control.\\n20. Critical. A hub round called ready only after the engine inspector existed. Two software WebGPU copies were still warming when the card gave up, so the round stayed in loading. Ready is sent when the session is connected, and Enter on the card answers before the first frame.\\n\\nTwenty issues. Eleven were game-breaking: 1–9, 14, and 20. Nine were not: 10–13 and 15–19.\\n\",\"total_lines\":26}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-73a4160d-3eb8-41c2-8488-a5d528670139-55","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,12