{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_721","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The Python directory walk returned no results.\n\nThe process tree shows Chrome is a child of e2e.mjs. The Python walk likely failed because the children dictionary lacks that node, or /proc stat parsing is broken.\n\nThe e2e test has been running for 15 minutes, exceeding its 660-second campaign timeout. The total time likely includes multiple pre-campaign engine-ready checks. Chrome is showing near-zero CPU usage, which suggests the game may be stalled.\n\nThe GPU process may be nested beyond the direct child list. The browser is idle, so the campaign may not have started yet, or the game is paused waiting for a condition.\n\nThe page may have crashed and is waiting for timeout. Low browser CPU could mean the GPU process is doing the work. I will check the GPU process CPU under the user-data directory.\n\nThe campaign timeout is 11 minutes, but earlier checks may have already consumed part of that budget. The total runtime of about 15 minutes suggests the campaign could finish soon. I will check GPU CPU usage via ps to see if the game is active or idle.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6a4de1e4-1e04-43b6-9d9a-b8dcae029af1-109","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"ps -eo pid,etime,pcpu,pmem,rss,cmd | grep 'g.ynpB8N' | grep -v grep | awk '{printf \"pid=%s etime=%s cpu=%s rssMB=%.0f type=%s\\n\",$1,$2,$3,$5/1024, ($0 ~ /gpu-process/?\"gpu\":($0 ~ /renderer/?\"renderer\":\"other\"))}'","description":"Measure this e2e Chrome's CPU by process type"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1965,"output_tokens":900,"cache_read_input_tokens":135168,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"a53be7ed-194b-4330-b6df-016cd668db44"}
