tail\\\":\\\"webkit|This game needs a browser with WebGPU.\\\"} | (node:430469) Warning: The 'NO_COLOR' env is ignored due to the 'FORCE_COLOR' env being set. | (Use `node --trace-warnings ...` to show wher\"},{\"line_number\":9,\"content\":\"verify: 91 passed, 3 failed\"},{\"line_number\":10,\"content\":\"EXIT:1\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"87c7e19e-ca3a-429c-85c7-cba23bf4e7f8"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_725","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"`npm run check` failed due to an issue with `labs/game/tools/hub-serve/Trauma-Compass`.\n\nThe flagged HTML is a 1KB data URI copy created by `hub.mjs` inside `hub-serve`. The original HTML in the work folder root was outside the package and escaped the scan. Fixes include removing the copy from the package, deleting `hub-serve` after the run, or placing it outside the package.\n\nThe check runs before browser tools in verify.mjs, so the stale hub-serve HTML from a previous run caused the failure. The campaign reaches credits, and e2e.mjs fails because a non-zero status marks the entire tool as failed.\n\nThe `browserTool` helper double-counts failures. It parses JSON lines from stdout, but if the process exits with a non-zero status or returns no lines, it also marks the entire tool as failed. This causes `e2e.mjs` to be counted twice whenever any check fails.\n\nCampaign autoplay stalled at tick 594 after 660 seconds. The HTML rebuild with time-up finish likely did not break the autoplay path. The machine load probably slowed execution enough to prevent the mercy phase from finishing.\n\nThe simulation likely advanced only one frame per nine seconds. That pace is far below the expected 8× speedup, suggesting the game was paused or the machine was overloaded with other WebGPU browsers.\n\nr6 previously finished the campaign in about thirteen minutes, so the stall was likely caused by machine load. The verifier will re-run. If the campaign remains flaky under load, the sixty-six-second timeout may need to be increased.\n\nThe stall likely reflects a bug in the timeScale logic rather than simple machine load. If timeScale were active, 594 ticks would equal roughly ten seconds of simulation time; instead, the run advanced only one tick per second. The autoplay path may not be entering the high-speed mode at all.\n\nI need to inspect the timeScale logic and the onFrame autoplay handler to determine why the simulation advanced so slowly.\n\nI will delete the hub-serve directory now so the next check passes, and update hub.mjs to remove it after each run.\n\nThe flagged HTML is inside the package at `labs/game/tools/hub-serve/`. The original one-file HTML sits outside the package in the work folder root. The check scans the repository from within the package, so it catches the copy inside.\n\nA cleaner fix is to have `hub.mjs` write its serve directory to `/tmp` or scratch instead of `hub-serve` inside the package. This would avoid leaving a copy in the repository and satisfy the check entirely.\n\nMoving the serve directory to the temporary folder would let verify delete it automatically, so the check would never see the flagged HTML. The deliverable HTML in the work folder sits outside the git repository, and the scan only complained about the hub-serve copy inside the package.\n\nThe e2e.mjs double-counting only matters if the campaign fails. If the campaign passes, the process exits cleanly and the extra note never fires.\n\nA 660-second budget allows roughly 26,000 simulation ticks at 40 steps per second. The run only reached 594 ticks, so either frames were spaced about one second apart or timeScale was not active at all.\n\nThe autoplay URL parameter is present, so the stall likely stems from a bug in the timeScale logic rather than a missing flag. The campaign reached the mercy phase, which means earlier cases completed and the bot itself works; only the final case is slow.\n\nThe 594th tick likely marks the start of the mercy phase after seven previous cases. The high score suggests earlier cases accumulated points. This run stalled because machine load from other WebGPU browsers exceeded the timeout budget.\n\nThe timeout is too tight under load. I will either raise the campaign budget to 900 or 1200 seconds, raise the autoplay timeScale from 8 to 16 or 32, or both.\n\nRaising the timeout would lengthen verification. A higher timeScale is preferable if the simulation stays stable. The current 8× speedup lets the bot play, but page rendering dominates on a busy machine. Steps per frame must be checked before raising timeScale further, since too many steps could freeze the display.\n\nI need to verify whether `hub-serve` is gitignored, since the check might still scan it. I will also inspect `checkAll` to confirm the exact rule. If the engine steps before each render, raising timeScale to 32 would be a clear win; if it renders after every step, the extra work could freeze the page.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1240e927-8570-453c-9f8a-2d1433b6be83-113","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"timeScale|autoplay","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/app/boot.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1240e927-8570-453c-9f8a-2d1433b6be83-114","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/tools/hub.mjs","limit":30}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1240e927-8570-453c-9f8a-2d1433b6be83-115","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"ASSET_DATA_URI|hub-serve","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731","glob":"*.{ts,mjs,md,json}"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":753,"output_tokens":2804,"cache_read_input_tokens":139264,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"1a9dbcb8-b3f2-4109-8478-26bb2b459a1d"}
