{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_732","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Default maxSteps is 6. The maximum timeScale is 100.\n\nAt timeScale 8, frames longer than 12.5 ms are capped at 6 simulation steps per frame. Software WebGPU frames run 100–250 ms, so the effective rate is only 6 steps per frame rather than 8× realtime. Mercy needed many ticks; the 7 finished cases averaged about 90 seconds of wall time. Mercy likely started late and only reached 594 ticks, or it did not finish in the remaining time.\n\nMercy likely began only when the timeout struck. The first seven cases consumed nearly all 660 seconds. A small speedup or extra time should finish the run. Raising `time.maxSteps` from 6 to 60 during autoplay would multiply simulation throughput by ten to twenty times, because step operations are cheap and the current cap is the bottleneck. The plan is to set `engine.set('time.maxSteps', 60)` while autoplay is active and restore it to 6 otherwise.\n\n`time.maxSteps` is a view setting, so raising it will not change the simulation hash. The bot still receives fresh `botHands(op)` every step.\n\nHowever, sixty steps per frame may be too heavy if the engine step includes physics or entity publishing. I need to check what `stepRun` actually does beyond `stepOp`.\n\nThe engine runs its own systems each step. At 60 steps per frame, the draw call is the only expensive operation, and it happens once per frame. A light scene should handle this load fine.\n\nSetting maxSteps to 120 during autoplay is safe. At timeScale 8, a 200 ms frame requests about 96 steps, which fits comfortably under 120. That yields roughly 480 steps per second, or exactly 8× realtime.\n\nA 1000 ms stall still yields 120 steps, twenty times the default. The plan is to set `time.maxSteps` to 120 during autoplay on op screens and restore 6 otherwise. Story screens between ops do not need this change because menus are already accepted every frame. `engine.set` should handle this setting like any other.\n\nAttract mode will keep normal speed because it falls into the else branch with timeScale 1 and maxSteps 6. The e2e timeout does not need to increase; the faster campaign should finish within the existing 660 seconds. One risk remains: publishing or sheet updates inside the 120 engine steps per frame could still overload a single frame and stall requestAnimationFrame, though the cap would still limit the step count.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b56fb246-6ffa-4513-8b78-ae370429f917-127","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function publish|function paintField|paintField\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game","glob":"*.ts"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":600,"output_tokens":1252,"cache_read_input_tokens":154752,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"615a7588-f665-4e0c-9f85-6599bd5a9190"}
