{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_735","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A snapshot might be in codec. It is not critical.\n\n48 steps is reasonable. The hub-serve fix uses a temporary directory from tmpdir(). The server cleanup and removal must move into a finally block.\n\nThe existing hub-serve directory will be deleted before the server starts. If the copy fails, no server runs. The HTML must be rebuilt after the boot.ts change because end-to-end tests load the compiled one-file page, not the source. The hub.mjs change does not require a rebuild.\n\nCheck runs before hub.mjs, so deleting hub-serve beforehand satisfies the package scan. The HTML rebuild must precede verify's end-to-end tests. A full verify rerun is required because npm run verify must exit 0. A targeted e2e check could catch campaign failures earlier.\n\nRebuilding the HTML and running full verify once is preferable to a separate end-to-end check, since that would double the test time. The campaign should finish in two to three minutes instead of eleven, making total verification roughly eight minutes. The boot.ts change adds only two lines, which is acceptable for linting. The hub-serve directory is safely inside the package, so deleting it is safe. The watch monitor has already exited, so no further kill is needed.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8bb998b7-d87d-423b-812c-8d68e504718e-130","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/tools/hub.mjs","offset":1,"limit":30}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8bb998b7-d87d-423b-812c-8d68e504718e-131","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/to