{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_750","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Engine-lock hashes are important.\n\nI will not edit engine-tracked files like eslint.config.js or .prettierignore. The plan says to leave the HTML comment example and avoid patching the engine.\n\nI cannot edit the engine files directly. Adding a local eslint config may not override the root flat config. I cannot modify session.js or move it because the build expects it at that path.\n\nMoving the vendor file outside labs/game is impossible because the build and index.html reference it directly. I am checking whether an extra eslint config can be spread into the existing flat config.\n\nThe engine-lock check was likely already failing once these files were added, since the first verify's tail output hid earlier errors. I am now looking for a way to make the check pass without editing engine config or session.js.\n\nAdding a comment to session.js would modify it, which is forbidden. I am checking whether the project already contains an ignored directory like `out/` that could house the file without breaking the build or index.html references. I also noted that upstream session.js does not include an eslint-disable comment.\n\nI will read the root eslint config to see if a game-owned config can exclude `labs/game/vendor`.\n\nThe import in `one-file.mts` needs its `.ts` extension removed. I will verify that both `tsc` and `tsx` still work.\n\nI will run prettier on our own files, but I cannot ignore the engine-tracked vendor and hub directories because `.prettierignore` is locked.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d5aff8f3-5700-4ff2-9ab1-8ccde9dc651f-154","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"session\\.js|byte|16701|unmodified","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game","glob":"*.{ts,mjs,