{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_765","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Considering a split in cases.ts at line 554.\n\nSplitting cases.ts into two files. The first file will hold helpers and the first ~392 cases. The second file will hold the remaining ~340 cases plus imports for shared helpers. A small builders file will export helpers for both case files to use.\n\nThe split will use four files: a builders module, early cases, late cases, and a main cases file for exports. Each will stay under 600 lines. A Python script will handle the manual move to avoid errors. campaign.ts is only 29 lines over its limit, so its tail functions can move to campaignFlow.ts.\n\nMoving campaign.ts tail functions would require exporting internal helpers, so that approach is being dropped. Instead, ATTRACT and menu item builders will move to campaignMenus.ts. This should bring campaign.ts down to roughly 519 lines. Need to check what types items() depends on.\n\nCampaign.ts is only 40 lines of wrapping after prettier, so shortening long strings to fit one line should shrink it enough. A script can find wrapped continuations by checking line lengths. Cases will still be split with a script. Campaign will be handled by moving bottom helper functions out if they are exported.\n\nChecking campaign.ts from line 451 onward to map dependencies and imports. The fastest fix for the 29-line overflow is joining wrapped lines that prettier will keep on one line, possibly using tickFront as a test case. Removing comments was considered but rejected because prettier would restore blank lines.\n\nround.js can be trimmed by collapsing four getters into one line each and joining the later() call. This saves about 15 lines and should bring the file to roughly 588. Prettier will be run afterward to check if it re-expands anything. The plan is to fix round.js first, then split cases with a script, then handle campaign.","signature":