{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_772","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"round.js is 603 lines. The simplest fix that Prettier will not undo is being considered.\n\nThe header comment block is 13 lines. It can be shortened by 4 lines without changing behavior, since the @file overview remains.\n\nThe compacted header comment will drop four lines to bring round.js down to 599 lines.\n\nThe compacted header comment is 6 lines instead of 13. This saves 7 lines and brings round.js to 596. The JSDoc rule only requires the tag, not a specific length. I am checking whether hub.test.mjs exists and if it tests line-sensitive behavior.\n\nThe original engine path for hub.test.mjs is unclear. A snapshot test probably does not exist.\n\nA Node script will split cases.ts into caseBuild.ts and the case objects. This avoids hand-copying 700 lines.\n\nThe CASES array contains objects with `id: 'case:...'` fields. Phase objects use a different pattern with `id` as the first argument to `phase()`. The script will locate `export const CASES` and split the file by finding these object boundaries.\n\nThe split will use brace depth to isolate top-level CASES array elements. caseBuild.ts will hold the builder functions, and casesEarly.ts will hold the first five story operations.\n\nThe split will import only the builder functions each half actually uses to avoid ESLint no-unused-vars errors. casesLate.ts will follow the same pattern. The original cases.ts will be reduced to a thin wrapper that imports from the new modules.\n\nThe original cases.ts will be reduced to a thin wrapper that imports EARLY_CASES and LATE_CASES. The original comment about metres, seconds, and postcards should be preserved in the new file's overview. I also need to check whether tests mutate the CASES array.\n\nThe readonly CASES type is safe because spreading into a new array does not rely on literal identity. Lines 160–273 will be extracted into campaignMenus.ts for the front-end menu rows.\n\ncampaignMenus.ts will export `items`, `settingsItems`, and `devItems` as functions. campaign.ts will import them from there and re-export `items` so existing imports keep working. A potential circular type dependency between campaign.ts and campaignMenus.ts is being checked.\n\nTypeScript `import type` is fully erased at runtime, so the circular dependency between campaign.ts and campaignMenus.ts is harmless. ESLint should not flag it either.\n\nExtracting the Item and Campaign interfaces into a separate campaignTypes.ts file would eliminate the cycle entirely, but that would add more files and import churn. The current type-only cycle is the standard pattern and acceptable.\n\ncampaign.ts will keep importing storyCases because boardIds and continueShift still need it after the menu extraction.\n\ncampaignMenus.ts will import storyCases itself. campaign.ts will be 517 lines after the split, so it still exceeds the 400-line warning threshold but remains under the 600-line limit. Further reduction is optional. The round.js comment trim is the least invasive fix. I am also checking whether short comments inside createRound can be joined to save four more lines.\n\nThe parameter block in round.js is 18 lines of JSDoc. It can be compacted but is not required if the overview trim suffices.\n\nThe Node script will write the three new files. campaign.ts and round.js will then be updated manually.\n\nESLint import restrictions allow labs/game/op to import sibling files.\n\nESLint `require-file-overview` will be added to the three new files. Exported helpers such as `cards` and `phase` must be exported from `caseBuild.ts` so they are not flagged as unused. The exact split point between early and late cases will be determined by the script rather than by hand.\n\nI need to check that content.test.ts does not snapshot the source text of cases.ts. validate.ts scanning for banned words will remain unaffected by the split.\n\nAf