{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_775","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"labs/game is the game layer, so sibling imports are fine.\n\nThe sim side already has Math.hypot and Math.sin, so splitting won't add new dependencies. I'll write the splitter script and other edits now. For round.js, shrinking the comment is simpler and safer than moving checkStandings. I'll scan the file for quotes with braces before splitting the cases.\n\nI'll write the script in scratch and run prettier afterward. For campaign.ts, I'll replace the items/settings/dev functions with an import from './campaignMenus' and export the imported binding.\n\nThe `import type` in campaignMenus.ts is erased at runtime, so there's no circular dependency risk. I'll watch for an eslint import cycle warning.\n\nI'll use a Python script to extract the large functions from campaign.ts into campaignMenus.ts. This avoids transcription errors. The export statement is a value export, not a type export.\n\nThe Python script will use pathlib to read op/cases.ts. It will extract the helper section and case elements exactly, preserving the original text so behavior diffs are zero. Helper functions will be converted to exported functions in the new file.\n\nI'll verify the extracted case array ends with a newline and check line counts before running the script. After splitting, I'll patch round.js, run prettier, and execute targeted tests for campaign, content, bot, and page.\n\npage.test.ts only reads files, so it needs no browser. I'll run eslint on the new split files and round.js, then execute the full npm check. After that, I'll rebuild the one-file HTML and verify it with a monitor.\n\nI'll launch the verify monitor with block_until_ms 0 and only print on EXIT or FAIL. I need to check one-file.mts for its output path and TMPDIR requirements.\n\nThe one-file rebuild will use a temporary directory and clean it up afterward. The shipped HTML must match the source because index.html CSS changed, so the session script must remain byte-identical. I also need to verify that the new files stay under 600 lines, since max-lines counts differently with skipBlankLines disabled.\n\nThe split files are small enough to avoid new line-count warnings. campaign.ts and round.js still exceed 400 lines, but those existing warnings remain acceptable. The extracted campaignMenus code is already prettier-formatted. I confirmed that Item and Campaign types are exported from campaign.ts for the new module to import.\n\n`import type` is correct because `verbatimModuleSyntax` lets TypeScript enforce value versus type imports at compile time. Spreading the CASES array preserves the readonly tuple identity and length checks, so tests remain unaffected. Deep freezing the original array still works.\n\nI'll add one-line `@file:` comments to the new split files so the 600-line cap stays valid. The API remains unchanged, so content.test needs no review.\n\nI'll read cases.ts lines 59-61 to preserve the CASES comment. The script will verify it extracted nine cases with correct IDs, then concatenate the element sources and compare them to the original array slice to ensure a zero-diff split.\n\nThe extracted case elements will keep their original two-space indentation inside the new arrays. They will be joined with commas to preserve exact whitespace and spacing from the original source.\n\nThe Python script will extract lines 160–273 from campaign.ts into a new campaignMenus.ts file. It will prepend the correct imports and write the block there. The original file will then be patched to remove those lines and insert the import statement.\n\ncampaign.ts will import `items` from `./campaignMenus` and re-export it as a public binding. The original `export function items` will be removed from the extracted block to avoid duplicate declarations.\n\nThe re-export `export { items };` can sit immediately after the import. Deleting lines 160–273 will leave a blank line before `move()`, which is acceptable.\n\nI'll delete lines 159 through 273 from campaign.ts. This removes the blank before items and the entire extracted block, leaving a single blank line before move(). I'm now replacing the round.js header.\n\nThe round.js header will be tightened to a single `@file` comment that still explains the module. It will describe the AI Hub session coordination, message delivery and receipt, the injected clock, and player key mapping.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-22bf0600-94ce-4e2c-869e-d1e32c00c9cc-27","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/tools/eslint/simSide.ts","offset":130,"limit":50}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1907,"output_tokens":3955,"cache_read_input_tokens":61568,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"81440a66-5fe9-420b-a708-58bb9a48f371"}
