{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-ca00d965-77c1-40dc-bab6-ecaaa51e2921-29","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"43→export const SIM_SIDE = [\\n  'engine/core/**',\\n  'engine/sim/**',\\n  'engine/physics/**',\\n  'engine/anim/**',\\n  'engine/world/**',\\n  'engine/input/intents.ts',\\n50→  'engine/audio/dsp/**',\\n  'engine/audio/data/**',\\n  'engine/dev/bot.ts',\\n  'engine/dev/galleryScene.ts',\\n  'labs/*/scenes/**',\\n  'labs/*/cast/**',\\n  'labs/box/sounds/events.ts',\\n  'labs/playground/sounds/events.ts',\\n  'labs/playground/sounds/ground.ts',\\n  'fixtures/scenes/**',\\n60→];\\n\\nconst CLOCK =\\n  'sim-side code never reads the clock: time is the step count (60 Hz sim ticks; core/time). Take a wall-clock timestamp outside the sim and pass it in as an intent (PLAN.md §6.5)';\\nconst TIMER =\\n  'sim-side code never schedules by wall time: keep a tick count in sim state and act in the system that steps it (PLAN.md §6.5)';\\nconst DOM =\\n  'sim-side code never touches the DOM: what it needs from outside arrives as recorded intents, and settings come from the schema (PLAN.md §6.5)';\\nconst AUDIO = 'sim-side code never touches Web Audio: emit an event, and audio/runtime plays it (PLAN.md §6.5)';\\nconst RANDOM =\\n70→  \\\"use a named seeded stream: rng('<stream>') or rng.entity(id, '<stream>'), derived from the scene seed (PLAN.md §6.5)\\\";\\nconst NODE =\\n  'sim-side code runs in Node and in Chromium alike: no process or Node built-ins; settings come from the schema (PLAN.md §6.5)';\",\"content_concise\":\"43→export const SIM_SIDE = [\\n  'engine/core/**',\\n  'engine/sim/**',\\n  'engine/physics/**',\\n  'engine/anim/**',\\n  'engine/world/**',\\n  'engine/input/intents.ts',\\n50→  'engine/audio/dsp/**',\\n  'engine/audio/data/**',\\n  'engine/dev/bot.ts',\\n  'engine/dev/galleryScene.ts',\\n  'labs/*/scenes/**',\\n  'labs/*/cast/**',\\n  'labs/box/sounds/events.ts',\\n  'labs/playground/sounds/events.ts',\\n  'labs/playground/sounds/ground.ts',\\n  'fixtures/scenes/**',\\n60→];\\n\\nconst CLOCK =\\n  'sim-side code never reads the clock: time is the step count (60 Hz sim ticks; core/time). Take a wall-clock timestamp outside the sim and pass it in as an intent (PLAN.md §6.5)';\\nconst TIMER =\\n  'sim-side code never schedules by wall time: keep a tick count in sim state and act in the system that steps it (PLAN.md §6.5)';\\nconst DOM =\\n  'sim-side code never touches the DOM: what it needs from outside arrives as recorded intents, and settings come from the schema (PLAN.md §6.5)';\\nconst AUDIO = 'sim-side code never touches Web Audio: emit an event, and audio/runtime plays it (PLAN.md §6.5)';\\nconst RANDOM =\\n70→  \\\"use a named seeded stream: rng('<stream>') or rng.entity(id, '<stream>'), derived from the scene seed (PLAN.md §6.5)\\\";\\nconst NODE =\\n  'sim-side code runs in Node and in Chromium alike: no process or Node built-ins; settings come from the schema (PLAN.md §6.5)';\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/tools/eslint/simSide.ts\",\"offset\":43,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"export const SIM_SIDE = [\\n  'engine/core/**',\\n  'engine/sim/**',\\n  'engine/physics/**',\\n  'engine/anim/**',\\n  'engine/world/**',\\n  'engine/input/intents.ts',\\n  'engine/audio/dsp/**',\\n  'engine/audio/data/**',\\n  'engine/dev/bot.ts',\\n  'engine/dev/galleryScene.ts',\\n  'labs/*/scenes/**',\\n  'labs/*/cast/**',\\n  'labs/box/sounds/events.ts',\\n  'labs/playground/sounds/events.ts',\\n  'labs/playground/sounds/ground.ts',\\n  'fixtures/scenes/**',\\n];\\n\\nconst CLOCK =\\n  'sim-side code never reads the clock: time is the step count (60 Hz sim ticks; core/time). Take a wall-clock timestamp outside the sim and pass it in as an intent (PLAN.md §6.5)';\\nconst TIMER =\\n  'sim-side code never schedules by wall time: keep a tick count in sim state and act in the system that steps it (PLAN.md §6.5)';\\nconst DOM =\\n  'sim-side code never touches the DOM: what it needs from outside arrives as recorded intents, and settings come from the schema (PLAN.md §6.5)';\\nconst AUDIO = 'sim-side code never touches Web Audio: emit an event, and audio/runtime plays it (PLAN.md §6.5)';\\nconst RANDOM =\\n  \\\"use a named seeded stream: rng('<stream>') or rng.entity(id, '<stream>'), derived from the scene seed (PLAN.md §6.5)\\\";\\nconst NODE =\\n  'sim-side code runs in Node and in Chromium alike: no process or Node built-ins; settings come from the schema (PLAN.md §6.5)';\\n\",\"total_lines\":172}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"301cda0b-21a1-49eb-915e-437de3ec1f6b"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_778","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The labs/game/op directory is not the simulation side for ESLint.\n\nMath.sin is fine. The game avoids ** operators per project convention. I'll write the script and apply edits now. I'm checking for an ESLint import cycle between campaignMenus and campaign, and verifying that re-exporting items won't trigger consistent-type-exports issues.\n\nI'll write the Python script in scratch and run it. I'm also updating the @file comment on cases.ts to describe the public module after the helpers moved.\n\ncases.ts now exports CASES, caseById, and storyCases. It merges early and late cases into a single ordered array.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Prettier wrapped those files past the hard cap. I'll split the case list and the menu rows, and shorten the hub round header, without changing what they do."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-649166f5-542d-4a26-8ac2-5760a5f39ebc-30","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"python3 << 'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nroot = Path(\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game\")\n\n# --- cases.ts split ---\nsrc = (root / \"op/cases.ts\").read_text()\nmarker = \"export const CASES: readonly CaseDef[] = [\"\nat = src.index(marker)\nif at < 0:\n    raise SystemExit(\"CASES marker missing\")\nbracket = src.index(\"[\", at)\ni = bracket + 1\ndepth = 1\nin_str = None\nescape = False\nelements = []\nstart = i\nwhile i < len(src) and depth:\n    c = src[i]\n    if in_str:\n        if escape:\n            escape = False\n        elif c == \"\\\\\":\n            escape = True\n        elif c == in_str:\n            in_str = None\n        i += 1\n        continue\n    if c in (\"'\", '\"', \"`\"):\n        in_str = c\n    elif c in \"{[(\":\n        depth += 1\n    elif c in \"}])\":\n        depth -= 1\n        if depth == 0:\n            tail = src[start:i]\n            if tail.strip():\n                elements.append(tail)\n            break\n    elif c == \",\" and depth == 1:\n        elements.append(src[start:i])\n        start = i + 1\n    i += 1\nelse:\n    raise SystemExit(\"array did not close\")\nids = []\nfor el in elements:\n    k = el.find(\"id: '\")\n    if k < 0:\n        raise SystemExit(\"element without id: \" + el[:80])\n    ids.append(el[k + 5 : el.find(\"'\", k + 5)])\nprint(\"cases\", len(elements), ids)\nearly_ids = [\"case:first-cut\", \"case:quiet-lump\", \"case:crosstalk\", \"case:it-moves\", \"case:struck-off\"]\nlate_ids = [\"case:reverie\", \"case:gala-night\", \"case:mercy\", \"case:gala-shift\"]\nif ids != early_ids + late_ids:\n    raise SystemExit(\"unexpected ids\")\nearly, late = elements[:5], elements[5:]\n\nhelpers = src[:at]\n# drop the CASES doc comment that sits just above the export\ndoc = \"/** The eight story cases, in order, then the session case. */\\n\"\nif not helpers.endswith(doc):\n    raise SystemExit(\"helper tail is:\\n\" + helpers[-200:])\nhelpers = helpers[: -len(doc)]\nfor name in (\"cards\", \"phase\", \"pool\", \"wound\", \"shard\", \"gel\", \"curve\", \"motes\"):\n    old = f\"function {name}(\"\n    new = f\"export function {name}(\"\n    if helpers.count(old) != 1:\n        raise SystemExit(f\"{name} count {helpers.count(old)}\")\n    helpers = helpers.replace(old, new, 1)\nhelpers = helpers.replace(\n    \"\"\"/**\n * @file The eight story operations, plus the session case. Each case adds one rule from the plan: tools, sites,\n * a strain, a gift. Numbers are metres and seconds. Postcards are the patient's own words, one line per rank.\n */\n\"\"\",\n    \"\"\"/**\n * @file Builders for one operation: postcard lines, a phase row, and the things a phase spawns.\n */\n\"\"\",\n    1,\n)\n# CaseDef import is unused in the builders.\nhelpers = helpers.replace(\"import type { CaseDef, PhaseDef, Postcards, Spawn } from './types';\\n\",\n                          \"import type { PhaseDef, Postcards, Spawn } from './types';\\n\", 1)\n\ndef uses(chunks, names):\n    text = \"\\n\".join(chunks)\n    found = []\n    for name in names:\n        # call sites, not the word inside other identifiers\n        if f\"{name}(\" in text:\n            found.append(name)\n    return found\n\nnames = [\"cards\", \"phase\", \"pool\", \"wound\", \"shard\", \"gel\", \"curve\", \"motes\"]\neu, lu = uses(early, names), uses(late, names)\nprint(\"early helpers\", eu)\nprint(\"late helpers\", lu)\n\ndef case_file(file_doc, const, chunks, used):\n    body = \",\".join(chunks)\n    if not body.endswith(\"\\n\"):\n        body += \"\\n\"\n    imp = \", \".join(used)\n    return (\n        f\"/**\\n * @file {file_doc}\\n */\\n\"\n        f\"import type {{ CaseDef }} from './types';\\n\"\n        f\"import {{ {imp} }} from './caseBuild';\\n\\n\"\n        f\"export const {const}: readonly CaseDef[] = [{body}];\\n\"\n    )\n\n(root / \"op/caseBuild.ts\").write_text(helpers if helpers.endswith(\"\\n\") else helpers + \"\\n\")\n(root / \"op/casesEarly.ts\").write_text(case_file(\n    \"The first five story operations, from First Cut through Struck Off.\",\n    \"EARLY_CASES\", early, eu))\n(root / \"op/casesLate.ts\").write_text(case_file(\n    \"The last three story operations, plus the session case.\",\n    \"LATE_CASES\", late, lu))\ncases_ts = \"\"\"/**\n * @file The eight story operations, plus the session case. Each case adds one rule from the plan: tools, sites,\n * a strain, a gift. Numbers are metres and seconds. Postcards are the patient's own words, one line per rank.\n */\nimport type { CaseDef } from './types';\nimport { EARLY_CASES } from './casesEarly';\nimport { LATE_CASES } from './casesLate';\n\n/** The eight story cases, in order, then the session case. */\nexport const CASES: readonly CaseDef[] = [...EARLY_CASES, ...LATE_CASES];\n\n/** The case with this id, or a thrown error when the board names a case we do not have. */\nexport function caseById(id: string): CaseDef {\n  const found = CASES.find((item) => item.id === id);\n  if (!found) throw new Error(`Unknown case ${id}`);\n  return found;\n}\n\n/** Story cases, in campaign order. The session case is not one of them. */\nexport function storyCases(): CaseDef[] {\n  return CASES.filter((item) => item.id !== 'case:gala-shift');\n}\n\"\"\"\n(root / \"op/cases.ts\").write_text(cases_ts)\n\n# --- campaign menus ---\ncamp_path = root / \"app/campaign.ts\"\nlines = camp_path.read_text().splitlines(True)\n# 1-based 160-273 inclusive\nblock = \"\".join(lines[159:273])\nif not block.startswith(\"export function items\"):\n    raise SystemExit(\"campaign block start: \" + block[:80])\nif not block.rstrip().endswith(\"}\"):\n    raise SystemExit(\"campaign block end: \" + block[-40:])\nmenu = \"\"\"/**\n * @file Menu rows for each front-end screen: title, board, briefing, pause, settings, and dev mode.\n */\nimport type { Campaign, Item } from './campaign';\nimport { storyCases } from '../op/cases';\n\n\"\"\" + block\n(root / \"app/campaignMenus.ts\").write_text(menu if menu.endswith(\"\\n\") else menu + \"\\n\")\n# drop the blank line before items through the end of devItems (lines 159-273)\nnew_lines = lines[:158] + lines[273:]\ntext = \"\".join(new_lines)\nneedle = \"import type { Difficulty, Rank } from '../op/types';\\n\"\ninsert = needle + \"\\nimport { items } from './campaignMenus';\\n\\nexport { items };\\n\"\nif needle not in text:\n    raise SystemExit(\"import needle missing\")\ntext = text.replace(needle, insert, 1)\ncamp_path.write_text(text)\n\n# --- round.js header ---\nrnd = root / \"tools/hub/round.js\"\nrtext = rnd.read_text()\nold = \"\"\"/**\n * @file round.js — one round of an AI Hub session, run by the hub that coordinates\n * it (the harness page, or the session host's tab).\n *\n * It never touches the network or a frame itself: every message for a game\n * goes out through `deliver(key, msg)`, and everything the games report comes\n * in through `receive(key, msg)` and `leave(key, reason)`. The clock is\n * injected, so `scripts/hub.test.mjs` can walk a round through every timeout\n * without waiting for one.\n *\n * Players are known by `key` (whatever the session calls them); games see\n * contiguous ids 0..N-1 in slot order.\n */\n\"\"\"\nnew = \"\"\"/**\n * @file round.js — one round of an AI Hub session, run by the hub that coordinates\n * it (the harness page, or the session host's tab). Messages go out through\n * `deliver(key, msg)` and come in through `receive(key, msg)` and `leave(key, reason)`.\n * The clock is injected so a test can walk every timeout. Players are known by\n * `key`; games see contiguous ids 0..N-1 in slot order.\n */\n\"\"\"\nif old not in rtext:\n    raise SystemExit(\"round header missing\")\nrnd.write_text(rtext.replace(old, new, 1))\n\nfor p in [\n    root/\"op/caseBuild.ts\", root/\"op/casesEarly.ts\", root/\"op/casesLate.ts\", root/\"op/cases.ts\",\n    root/\"app/campaign.ts\", root/\"app/campaignMenus.ts\", root/\"tools/hub/round.js\",\n]:\n    n = p.read_text().count(\"\\n\")\n    print(f\"{n:4} {p.name}\")\nPY","description":"Split over-cap files and shorten round.js header"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":606,"output_tokens":2888,"cache_read_input_tokens":68224,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"bdb4e253-7165-4fce-9916-e1fa52a316b5"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-649166f5-542d-4a26-8ac2-5760a5f39ebc-30","content":"{\"type\":\"Bash\",\"output\":[99,97,115,101,115,32,48,32,91,93,10,117,110,101,120,112,101,99,116,101,100,32,105,100,115,10],\"output_for_prompt\":\"exit: 1\\ncases 0 []\\nunexpected ids\\n\",\"exit_code\":1,\"command\":\"python3 << 'PY'\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nroot = Path(\\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game\\\")\\n\\n# --- cases.ts split ---\\nsrc = (root / \\\"op/cases.ts\\\").read_text()\\nmarker = \\\"export const CASES: readonly CaseDef[] = [\\\"\\nat = src.index(marker)\\nif at < 0:\\n    raise SystemExit(\\\"CASES marker missing\\\")\\nbracket = src.index(\\\"[\\\", at)\\ni = bracket + 1\\ndepth = 1\\nin_str = None\\nescape = False\\nelements = []\\nstart = i\\nwhile i < len(src) and depth:\\n    c = src[i]\\n    if in_str:\\n        if escape:\\n            escape = False\\n        elif c == \\\"\\\\\\\\\\\":\\n            escape = True\\n        elif c == in_str:\\n            in_str = None\\n        i += 1\\n        continue\\n    if c in (\\\"'\\\", '\\\"', \\\"`\\\"):\\n        in_str = c\\n    elif c in \\\"{[(\\\":\\n        depth += 1\\n    elif c in \\\"}])\\\":\\n        depth -= 1\\n        if depth == 0:\\n            tail = src[start:i]\\n            if tail.strip():\\n                elements.append(tail)\\n            break\\n    elif c == \\\",\\\" and depth == 1:\\n        elements.append(src[start:i])\\n        start = i + 1\\n    i += 1\\nelse:\\n    raise SystemExit(\\\"array did not close\\\")\\nids = []\\nfor el in elements:\\n    k = el.find(\\\"id: '\\\")\\n    if k < 0:\\n        raise SystemExit(\\\"element without id: \\\" + el[:80])\\n    ids.append(el[k + 5 : el.find(\\\"'\\\", k + 5)])\\nprint(\\\"cases\\\", len(elements), ids)\\nearly_ids = [\\\"case:first-cut\\\", \\\"case:quiet-lump\\\", \\\"case:crosstalk\\\", \\\"case:it-moves\\\", \\\"case:struck-off\\\"]\\nlate_ids = [\\\"case:reverie\\\", \\\"case:gala-night\\\", \\\"case:mercy\\\", \\\"case:gala-shift\\\"]\\nif ids != early_ids + late_ids:\\n    raise SystemExit(\\\"unexpected ids\\\")\\nearly, late = elements[:5], elements[5:]\\n\\nhelpers = src[:at]\\n# drop the CASES doc comment that sits just above the export\\ndoc = \\\"/** The eight story cases, in order, then the session case. */\\\\n\\\"\\nif not helpers.endswith(doc):\\n    raise SystemExit(\\\"helper tail is:\\\\n\\\" + helpers[-200:])\\nhelpers = helpers[: -len(doc)]\\nfor name in (\\\"cards\\\", \\\"phase\\\", \\\"pool\\\", \\\"wound\\\", \\\"shard\\\", \\\"gel\\\", \\\"curve\\\", \\\"motes\\\"):\\n    old = f\\\"function {name}(\\\"\\n    new = f\\\"export function {name}(\\\"\\n    if helpers.count(old) != 1:\\n        raise SystemExit(f\\\"{name} count {helpers.count(old)}\\\")\\n    helpers = helpers.replace(old, new, 1)\\nhelpers = helpers.replace(\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"/**\\n * @file The eight story operations, plus the session case. Each case adds one rule from the plan: tools, sites,\\n * a strain, a gift. Numbers are metres and seconds. Postcards are the patient's own words, one line per rank.\\n */\\n\\\"\\\"\\\",\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"/**\\n * @file Builders for one operation: postcard lines, a phase row, and the things a phase spawns.\\n */\\n\\\"\\\"\\\",\\n    1,\\n)\\n# CaseDef import is unused in the builders.\\nhelpers = helpers.replace(\\\"import type { CaseDef, PhaseDef, Postcards, Spawn } from './types';\\\\n\\\",\\n                          \\\"import type { PhaseDef, Postcards, Spawn } from './types';\\\\n\\\", 1)\\n\\ndef uses(chunks, names):\\n    text = \\\"\\\\n\\\".join(chunks)\\n    found = []\\n    for name in names:\\n        # call sites, not the word inside other identifiers\\n        if f\\\"{name}(\\\" in text:\\n            found.append(name)\\n    return found\\n\\nnames = [\\\"cards\\\", \\\"phase\\\", \\\"pool\\\", \\\"wound\\\", \\\"shard\\\", \\\"gel\\\", \\\"curve\\\", \\\"motes\\\"]\\neu, lu = uses(early, names), uses(late, names)\\nprint(\\\"early helpers\\\", eu)\\nprint(\\\"late helpers\\\", lu)\\n\\ndef case_file(file_doc, const, chunks, used):\\n    body = \\\",\\\".join(chunks)\\n    if not body.endswith(\\\"\\\\n\\\"):\\n        body += \\\"\\\\n\\\"\\n    imp = \\\", \\\".join(used)\\n    return (\\n        f\\\"/**\\\\n * @file {file_doc}\\\\n */\\\\n\\\"\\n        f\\\"import type {{ CaseDef }} from './types';\\\\n\\\"\\n        f\\\"import {{ {imp} }} from './caseBuild';\\\\n\\\\n\\\"\\n        f\\\"export const {const}: readonly CaseDef[] = [{body}];\\\\n\\\"\\n    )\\n\\n(root / \\\"op/caseBuild.ts\\\").write_text(helpers if helpers.endswith(\\\"\\\\n\\\") else helpers + \\\"\\\\n\\\")\\n(root / \\\"op/casesEarly.ts\\\").write_text(case_file(\\n    \\\"The first five story operations, from First Cut through Struck Off.\\\",\\n    \\\"EARLY_CASES\\\", early, eu))\\n(root / \\\"op/casesLate.ts\\\").write_text(case_file(\\n    \\\"The last three story operations, plus the session case.\\\",\\n    \\\"LATE_CASES\\\", late, lu))\\ncases_ts = \\\"\\\"\\\"/**\\n * @file The eight story operations, plus the session case. Each case adds one rule from the plan: tools, sites,\\n * a strain, a gift. Numbers are metres and seconds. Postcards are the patient's own words, one line per rank.\\n */\\nimport type { CaseDef } from './types';\\nimport { EARLY_CASES } from './casesEarly';\\nimport { LATE_CASES } from './casesLate';\\n\\n/** The eight story cases, in order, then the session case. */\\nexport const CASES: readonly CaseDef[] = [...EARLY_CASES, ...LATE_CASES];\\n\\n/** The case with this id, or a thrown error when the board names a case we do not have. */\\nexport function caseById(id: string): CaseDef {\\n  const found = CASES.find((item) => item.id === id);\\n  if (!found) throw new Error(`Unknown case ${id}`);\\n  return found;\\n}\\n\\n/** Story cases, in campaign order. The session case is not one of them. */\\nexport function storyCases(): CaseDef[] {\\n  return CASES.filter((item) => item.id !== 'case:gala-shift');\\n}\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n(root / \\\"op/cases.ts\\\").write_text(cases_ts)\\n\\n# --- campaign menus ---\\ncamp_path = root / \\\"app/campaign.ts\\\"\\nlines = camp_path.read_text().splitlines(True)\\n# 1-based 160-273 inclusive\\nblock = \\\"\\\".join(lines[159:273])\\nif not block.startswith(\\\"export function items\\\"):\\n    raise SystemExit(\\\"campaign block start: \\\" + block[:80])\\nif not block.rstrip().endswith(\\\"}\\\"):\\n    raise SystemExit(\\\"campaign block end: \\\" + block[-40:])\\nmenu = \\\"\\\"\\\"/**\\n * @file Menu rows for each front-end screen: title, board, briefing, pause, settings, and dev mode.\\n */\\nimport type { Campaign, Item } from './campaign';\\nimport { storyCases } from '../op/cases';\\n\\n\\\"\\\"\\\" + block\\n(root / \\\"app/campaignMenus.ts\\\").write_text(menu if menu.endswith(\\\"\\\\n\\\") else menu + \\\"\\\\n\\\")\\n# drop the blank line before items through the end of devItems (lines 159-273)\\nnew_lines = lines[:158] + lines[273:]\\ntext = \\\"\\\".join(new_lines)\\nneedle = \\\"import type { Difficulty, Rank } from '../op/types';\\\\n\\\"\\ninsert = needle + \\\"\\\\nimport { items } from './campaignMenus';\\\\n\\\\nexport { items };\\\\n\\\"\\nif needle not in text:\\n    raise SystemExit(\\\"import needle missing\\\")\\ntext = text.replace(needle, insert, 1)\\ncamp_path.write_text(text)\\n\\n# --- round.js header ---\\nrnd = root / \\\"tools/hub/round.js\\\"\\nrtext = rnd.read_text()\\nold = \\\"\\\"\\\"/**\\n * @file round.js — one round of an AI Hub session, run by the hub that coordinates\\n * it (the harness page, or the session host's tab).\\n *\\n * It never touches the network or a frame itself: every message for a game\\n * goes out through `deliver(key, msg)`, and everything the games report comes\\n * in through `receive(key, msg)` and `leave(key, reason)`. The clock is\\n * injected, so `scripts/hub.test.mjs` can walk a round through every timeout\\n * without waiting for one.\\n *\\n * Players are known by `key` (whatever the session calls them); games see\\n * contiguous ids 0..N-1 in slot order.\\n */\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nnew = \\\"\\\"\\\"/**\\n * @file round.js — one round of an AI Hub session, run by the hub that coordinates\\n * it (the harness page, or the session host's tab). Messages go out through\\n * `deliver(key, msg)` and come in through `receive(key, msg)` and `leave(key, reason)`.\\n * The clock is injected so a test can walk every timeout. Players are known by\\n * `key`; games see contiguous ids 0..N-1 in slot order.\\n */\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nif old not in rtext:\\n    raise SystemExit(\\\"round header missing\\\")\\nrnd.write_text(rtext.replace(old, new, 1))\\n\\nfor p in [\\n    root/\\\"op/caseBuild.ts\\\", root/\\\"op/casesEarly.ts\\\", root/\\\"op/casesLate.ts\\\", root/\\\"op/cases.ts\\\",\\n    root/\\\"app/campaign.ts\\\", root/\\\"app/campaignMenus.ts\\\", root/\\\"tools/hub/round.js\\\",\\n]:\\n    n = p.read_text().count(\\\"\\\\n\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"{n:4} {p.name}\\\")\\nPY\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Split over-cap files and shorten round.js header\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3%2Fwork/01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151/terminal/call-649166f5-542d-4a26-8ac2-5760a5f39ebc-30.log\",\"total_bytes\":26}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"47e1d1ab-b2ad-4f18-8abb-9f20dfcdb672"}
