ck that the file parses as JSON.\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"1221ad0a-75af-4bfc-a1ab-e731ac4b756d"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_785","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The check passed. Rebuilding the HTML and running verify.\n\nRebuilding the HTML is required before verify. The source index.html changed, and the hand-in must match current source.\n\nLaunch evidence must be re-run after the rebuild. The prior launch check was for the old HTML file, so it no longer matches the shipped version.\n\nRe-running launch, hub, and verify after the rebuild would waste browser time. Hub already passed on the previous HTML, and its JavaScript behavior is unchanged. The verifier might hash the HTML file and compare it to saved evidence.\n\nEvidence is stored as logs rather than hashes, so the verifier likely does not compare file hashes. The safest path is to rebuild the HTML and run verify. I should also re-run the two file:// launches if verify.mjs does not cover them.\n\nI will rebuild the HTML first. Then I will check for other running browsers. Then I will run verify, which includes e2e and hub. Launch is a separate script, so I will refresh the launch folders afterward to match the rebuilt HTML.\n\nI will check the existing launch-1 and launch-2 directories. Updating them after the rebuild is more honest than keeping stale evidence.\n\nVerify takes roughly 8 to 15 minutes. Launches take about one to two minutes each. I cannot run them in parallel.\n\nI will draft the PROGRESS.md update only after verify completes, since it needs the actual result.\n\nI also need to confirm the Firefox and WebKit no-webgpu logs exist.\n\nI am inspecting the scratch evidence and the one-file rebuild script. I will read verify.mjs to confirm its temporary directory and output paths. Before launching browsers, I will check for any running processes from this work. The Vite build may take 30 to 90 seconds, so I will set a long timeout. I also need to ensure the temporary directory is not left set in the shell for subsequent commands.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a49bafca-3584-4e76-a265-5ce2d502662b-48","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/tools/one-file.mts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a49bafca-3584-4e76-a265-5ce2d502662b-49","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/tools/verify.mjs","limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5529,"output_tokens":1521,"cache_read_input_tokens":82176,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"bd7019e4-e9b7-43c8-995f-ce622c467f43"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a49bafca-3584-4e76-a265-5ce2d502662b-48","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file Build Trauma Compass as one HTML file. Vite inlines the module. The hub client is already the first script.\\n */\\nimport { writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport { dirname, join } from 'node:path';\\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\\nimport type { Rollup } from 'vite';\\nimport { externalRefs, inlineBuild, ONE_FILE_NOTE } from '../../../tools/lib/oneFile';\\n\\n10→const root = join(dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), '../../..');\\nconst page = join(root, 'labs/game/index.html');\\nconst out = join(root, '..', 'Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731.html');\\n\\nconst { build } = await import('vite');\\nconst result = await build({\\n  root,\\n  configFile: false,\\n  logLevel: 'warn',\\n  base: './',\\n20→  resolve: { alias: [{ find: /^three$/, replacement: 'three/webgpu' }] },\\n  build: {\\n    write: false,\\n    modulePreload: false,\\n    cssCodeSplit: false,\\n    assetsInlineLimit: () => true,\\n    chunkSizeWarningLimit: Infinity,\\n    rollupOptions: { input: page, output: { inlineDynamicImports: true } },\\n  },\\n});\\n30→\\nconst outputs = (Array.isArray(result) ? result : [result]) as Rollup.RollupOutput[];\\nconst files: Record<string, string> = {};\\nlet html: string | undefined;\\nfor (const item of outputs.flatMap((output) => output.output)) {\\n  const text =\\n    item.type === 'chunk'\\n      ? item.code\\n      : typeof item.source === 'string'\\n        ? item.source\\n40→        : new TextDecoder().decode(item.source);\\n  if (item.fileName.endsWith('.html')) html = text;\\n  else files[item.fileName] = text;\\n}\\nif (!html) throw new Error('Vite wrote no page');\\nconst built = inlineBuild(html, files).replace(\\n  ONE_FILE_NOTE,\\n  '<!-- Trauma Compass, one self-contained page. Open it in a browser with WebGPU. -->',\\n);\\nconst refs = externalRefs(built);\\n50→if (refs.length) throw new Error(`external refs: ${refs.join(', ')}`);\\nwriteFileSync(out, built);\\nconsole.log(`${out} ${built.length}`);\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file Build Trauma Compass as one HTML file. Vite inlines the module. The hub client is already the first script.\\n */\\nimport { writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport { dirname, join } from 'node:path';\\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\\nimport type { Rollup } from 'vite';\\nimport { externalRefs, inlineBuild, ONE_FILE_NOTE } from '../../../tools/lib/oneFile';\\n\\n10→const root = join(dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), '../../..');\\nconst page = join(root, 'labs/game/index.html');\\nconst out = join(root, '..', 'Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731.html');\\n\\nconst { build } = await import('vite');\\nconst result = await build({\\n  root,\\n  configFile: false,\\n  logLevel: 'warn',\\n  base: './',\\n20→  resolve: { alias: [{ find: /^three$/, replacement: 'three/webgpu' }] },\\n  build: {\\n    write: false,\\n    modulePreload: false,\\n    cssCodeSplit: false,\\n    assetsInlineLimit: () => true,\\n    chunkSizeWarningLimit: Infinity,\\n    rollupOptions: { input: page, output: { inlineDynamicImports: true } },\\n  },\\n});\\n30→\\nconst outputs = (Array.isArray(result) ? result : [result]) as Rollup.RollupOutput[];\\nconst files: Record<string, string> = {};\\nlet html: string | undefined;\\nfor (const item of outputs.flatMap((output) => output.output)) {\\n  const text =\\n    item.type === 'chunk'\\n      ? item.code\\n      : typeof item.source === 'string'\\n        ? item.source\\n40→        : new TextDecoder().decode(item.source);\\n  if (item.fileName.endsWith('.html')) html = text;\\n  else files[item.fileName] = text;\\n}\\nif (!html) throw new Error('Vite wrote no page');\\nconst built = inlineBuild(html, files).replace(\\n  ONE_FILE_NOTE,\\n  '<!-- Trauma Compass, one self-contained page. Open it in a browser with WebGPU. -->',\\n);\\nconst refs = externalRefs(built);\\n50→if (refs.length) throw new Error(`external refs: ${refs.join(', ')}`);\\nwriteFileSync(out, built);\\nconsole.log(`${out} ${built.length}`);\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/tools/one-file.mts\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file Build Trauma Compass as one HTML file. Vite inlines the module. The hub client is already the first script.\\n */\\nimport { writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport { dirname, join } from 'node:path';\\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\\nimport type { Rollup } from 'vite';\\nimport { externalRefs, inlineBuild, ONE_FILE_NOTE } from '../../../tools/lib/oneFile';\\n\\nconst root = join(dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), '../../..');\\nconst page = join(root, 'labs/game/index.html');\\nconst out = join(root, '..', 'Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731.html');\\n\\nconst { build } = await import('vite');\\nconst result = await build({\\n  root,\\n  configFile: false,\\n  logLevel: 'warn',\\n  base: './',\\n  resolve: { alias: [{ find: /^three$/, replacement: 'three/webgpu' }] },\\n  build: {\\n    write: false,\\n    modulePreload: false,\\n    cssCodeSplit: false,\\n    assetsInlineLimit: () => true,\\n    chunkSizeWarningLimit: Infinity,\\n    rollupOptions: { input: page, output: { inlineDynamicImports: true } },\\n  },\\n});\\n\\nconst outputs = (Array.isArray(result) ? result : [result]) as Rollup.RollupOutput[];\\nconst files: Record<string, string> = {};\\nlet html: string | undefined;\\nfor (const item of outputs.flatMap((output) => output.output)) {\\n  const text =\\n    item.type === 'chunk'\\n      ? item.code\\n      : typeof item.source === 'string'\\n        ? item.source\\n        : new TextDecoder().decode(item.source);\\n  if (item.fileName.endsWith('.html')) html = text;\\n  else files[item.fileName] = text;\\n}\\nif (!html) throw new Error('Vite wrote no page');\\nconst built = inlineBuild(html, files).replace(\\n  ONE_FILE_NOTE,\\n  '<!-- Trauma Compass, one self-contained page. Open it in a browser with WebGPU. -->',\\n);\\nconst refs = externalRefs(built);\\nif (refs.length) throw new Error(`external refs: ${refs.join(', ')}`);\\nwriteFileSync(out, built);\\nconsole.log(`${out} ${built.length}`);\\n\",\"total_lines\":52}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a49bafca-3584-4e76-a265-5ce2d502662b-49","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The one command, `npm run verify`: runs every check quietly and prints only the failures, then one line with\\n * the count. `--fast` skips what needs a browser. It sets its own short TMPDIR and CHROMIUM_PATH, so it needs no setup,\\n * and removes the temporary folder when done. Exit 0 when nothing failed.\\n */\\nimport { spawnSync } from 'node:child_process';\\nimport { existsSync, globSync, mkdtempSync, readFileSync, rmSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport { homedir } from 'node:os';\\n\\n10→const fast = process.argv.includes('--fast');\\nconst tmp = mkdtempSync('/tmp/g.');\\nconst chrome = globSync(`${homedir()}/.cache/ms-playwright/chromium-*/chrome-linux64/chrome`)[0];\\nconst env = { ...process.env, TMPDIR: tmp, CHROMIUM_PATH: process.env.CHROMIUM_PATH ?? chrome };\\nconst run = (command, ...args) => spawnSync(command, args, { env, encoding: 'utf8', maxBuffer: 2 ** 28 });\\n\\nlet passed = 0;\\nconst failed = [];\\nconst note = (name, ok, detail = '') => (ok ? (passed += 1) : failed.push(`${name}${detail ? `: ${detail}` : ''}`));\\nconst tail = (result) => `${result.stdout}${result.stderr}`.trim().split('\\\\n').slice(-6).join(' | ').slice(0, 600);\\n20→\\n/** A step whose exit status is its verdict. */\\nconst step = (name, command, ...args) => {\\n  const result = run(command, ...args);\\n  note(name, result.status === 0, tail(result));\\n};\\n\\n/** Vitest, counted test by test from the JSON report npm test writes. */\\nfunction tests() {\\n  const report = 'out/test/report.json';\\n30→  rmSync(report, { force: true });\\n  const result = run('npm', 'test', '--silent');\\n  if (!existsSync(report)) return note('npm test', false, tail(result));\\n  for (const file of JSON.parse(readFileSync(report, 'utf8')).testResults) {\\n    for (const test of file.assertionResults) {\\n      note(\\n        test.fullName,\\n        test.status === 'passed',\\n        String(test.failureMessages?.[0] ?? '')\\n          .split('\\\\n')[0]\\n40→          .slice(0, 300),\\n      );\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** A browser tool: it prints one JSON line per check, { name, ok, detail }. Add e2e and hub runs here. */\\nfunction browserTool(path) {\\n  const result = run('node', path);\\n  const lines = result.stdout.split('\\\\n').filter((line) => line.startsWith('{'));\\n50→  for (const line of lines) {\\n    const { name, ok, detail } = JSON.parse(line);\\n    note(name, ok, detail);\\n  }\\n  if (result.status !== 0 || lines.length === 0) note(path, false, tail(result));\\n}\\n\\nstep('npm run check', 'npm', 'run', '--silent', 'check');\\ntests();\\nif (!fast) {\\n60→  step('replays in Chromium', 'node', 'x', 'replay', 'labs/game/replays', '--browser', 'sim');\\n  for (const path of ['labs/game/tools/e2e.mjs', 'labs/game/tools/hub.mjs']) if (existsSync(path)) browserTool(path);\\n}\\nrmSync(tmp, { recursive: true, force: true });\\nfor (const failure of failed) console.log(`FAIL ${failure}`);\\nconsole.log(`verify: ${passed} passed, ${failed.length} failed`);\\nprocess.exit(failed.length ? 1 : 0);\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The one command, `npm run verify`: runs every check quietly and prints only the failures, then one line with\\n * the count. `--fast` skips what needs a browser. It sets its own short TMPDIR and CHROMIUM_PATH, so it needs no setup,\\n * and removes the temporary folder when done. Exit 0 when nothing failed.\\n */\\nimport { spawnSync } from 'node:child_process';\\nimport { existsSync, globSync, mkdtempSync, readFileSync, rmSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport { homedir } from 'node:os';\\n\\n10→const fast = process.argv.includes('--fast');\\nconst tmp = mkdtempSync('/tmp/g.');\\nconst chrome = globSync(`${homedir()}/.cache/ms-playwright/chromium-*/chrome-linux64/chrome`)[0];\\nconst env = { ...process.env, TMPDIR: tmp, CHROMIUM_PATH: process.env.CHROMIUM_PATH ?? chrome };\\nconst run = (command, ...args) => spawnSync(command, args, { env, encoding: 'utf8', maxBuffer: 2 ** 28 });\\n\\nlet passed = 0;\\nconst failed = [];\\nconst note = (name, ok, detail = '') => (ok ? (passed += 1) : failed.push(`${name}${detail ? `: ${detail}` : ''}`));\\nconst tail = (result) => `${result.stdout}${result.stderr}`.trim().split('\\\\n').slice(-6).join(' | ').slice(0, 600);\\n20→\\n/** A step whose exit status is its verdict. */\\nconst step = (name, command, ...args) => {\\n  const result = run(command, ...args);\\n  note(name, result.status === 0, tail(result));\\n};\\n\\n/** Vitest, counted test by test from the JSON report npm test writes. */\\nfunction tests() {\\n  const report = 'out/test/report.json';\\n30→  rmSync(report, { force: true });\\n  const result = run('npm', 'test', '--silent');\\n  if (!existsSync(report)) return note('npm test', false, tail(result));\\n  for (const file of JSON.parse(readFileSync(report, 'utf8')).testResults) {\\n    for (const test of file.assertionResults) {\\n      note(\\n        test.fullName,\\n        test.status === 'passed',\\n        String(test.failureMessages?.[0] ?? '')\\n          .split('\\\\n')[0]\\n40→          .slice(0, 300),\\n      );\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** A browser tool: it prints one JSON line per check, { name, ok, detail }. Add e2e and hub runs here. */\\nfunction browserTool(path) {\\n  const result = run('node', path);\\n  const lines = result.stdout.split('\\\\n').filter((line) => line.startsWith('{'));\\n50→  for (const line of lines) {\\n    const { name, ok, detail } = JSON.parse(line);\\n    note(name, ok, detail);\\n  }\\n  if (result.status !== 0 || lines.length === 0) note(path, false, tail(result));\\n}\\n\\nstep('npm run check', 'npm', 'run', '--silent', 'check');\\ntests();\\nif (!fast) {\\n60→  step('replays in Chromium', 'node', 'x', 'replay', 'labs/game/replays', '--browser', 'sim');\\n  for (const path of ['labs/game/tools/e2e.mjs', 'labs/game/tools/hub.mjs']) if (existsSync(path)) browserTool(path);\\n}\\nrmSync(tmp, { recursive: true, force: true });\\nfor (const failure of failed) console.log(`FAIL ${failure}`);\\nconsole.log(`verify: ${passed} passed, ${failed.length} failed`);\\nprocess.exit(failed.length ? 1 : 0);\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/tools/verify.mjs\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file The one command, `npm run verify`: runs every check quietly and prints only the failures, then one line with\\n * the count. `--fast` skips what needs a browser. It sets its own short TMPDIR and CHROMIUM_PATH, so it needs no setup,\\n * and removes the temporary folder when done. Exit 0 when nothing failed.\\n */\\nimport { spawnSync } from 'node:child_process';\\nimport { existsSync, globSync, mkdtempSync, readFileSync, rmSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport { homedir } from 'node:os';\\n\\nconst fast = process.argv.includes('--fast');\\nconst tmp = mkdtempSync('/tmp/g.');\\nconst chrome = globSync(`${homedir()}/.cache/ms-playwright/chromium-*/chrome-linux64/chrome`)[0];\\nconst env = { ...process.env, TMPDIR: tmp, CHROMIUM_PATH: process.env.CHROMIUM_PATH ?? chrome };\\nconst run = (command, ...args) => spawnSync(command, args, { env, encoding: 'utf8', maxBuffer: 2 ** 28 });\\n\\nlet passed = 0;\\nconst failed = [];\\nconst note = (name, ok, detail = '') => (ok ? (passed += 1) : failed.push(`${name}${detail ? `: ${detail}` : ''}`));\\nconst tail = (result) => `${result.stdout}${result.stderr}`.trim().split('\\\\n').slice(-6).join(' | ').slice(0, 600);\\n\\n/** A step whose exit status is its verdict. */\\nconst step = (name, command, ...args) => {\\n  const result = run(command, ...args);\\n  note(name, result.status === 0, tail(result));\\n};\\n\\n/** Vitest, counted test by test from the JSON report npm test writes. */\\nfunction tests() {\\n  const report = 'out/test/report.json';\\n  rmSync(report, { force: true });\\n  const result = run('npm', 'test', '--silent');\\n  if (!existsSync(report)) return note('npm test', false, tail(result));\\n  for (const file of JSON.parse(readFileSync(report, 'utf8')).testResults) {\\n    for (const test of file.assertionResults) {\\n      note(\\n        test.fullName,\\n        test.status === 'passed',\\n        String(test.failureMessages?.[0] ?? '')\\n          .split('\\\\n')[0]\\n          .slice(0, 300),\\n      );\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** A browser tool: it prints one JSON line per check, { name, ok, detail }. Add e2e and hub runs here. */\\nfunction browserTool(path) {\\n  const result = run('node', path);\\n  const lines = result.stdout.split('\\\\n').filter((line) => line.startsWith('{'));\\n  for (const line of lines) {\\n    const { name, ok, detail } = JSON.parse(line);\\n    note(name, ok, detail);\\n  }\\n  if (result.status !== 0 || lines.length === 0) note(path, false, tail(result));\\n}\\n\\nstep('npm run check', 'npm', 'run', '--silent', 'check');\\ntests();\\nif (!fast) {\\n  step('replays in Chromium', 'node', 'x', 'replay', 'labs/game/replays', '--browser', 'sim');\\n  for (const path of ['labs/game/tools/e2e.mjs', 'labs/game/tools/hub.mjs']) if (existsSync(path)) browserTool(path);\\n}\\nrmSync(tmp, { recursive: true, force: true });\\nfor (const failure of failed) console.log(`FAIL ${failure}`);\\nconsole.log(`verify: ${passed} passed, ${failed.length} failed`);\\nprocess.exit(failed.length ? 1 : 0);\\n\",\"total_lines\":66}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"bcd9367e-cf22-45b8-bde6-dad8400190a6"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_786","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Rebuilding the HTML. Starting verification next.\n\nRebuilding with a short temporary directory to limit memory use. A Python check will verify markers before starting the long verify run. The verify process will run in the background with a quiet watcher that alerts only on failure or completion.\n\nThe watcher will poll the verify process and log. It will wake on JSON `ok: false`, `EXIT:` or `FAIL:` lines, or process exit.\n\nThe verify script only prints FAIL lines at the end after all steps finish. A background monitor would not catch failures early. The command completion notification is sufficient.\n\nWhile verify runs, I will read interview files and TASK.md to prepare the final hand-in. I will also check PROGRESS.md and the About screen for post-verify updates. No other browser will be started.\n\nI will prepare hand-in updates that do not depend on verify results. Starting verify with block_until_ms 0 lets me keep working in this turn. The completion notification arrives only after the turn ends.\n\nI am weighing a 15–20 minute block against backgrounding verify. The skill recommends backgrounding for long jobs, but the goal is to finish. I will update non-verify documentation while it runs.\n\nPROGRESS.md must not be written before verify finishes. I will start verify in the background and use a monitor to wake me on failure or exit. I will also wait with get_command_or_subagent_output so I can read files during the run and receive the result without interruption.\n\nVerify will run with a long block_until_ms to capture the result directly. The child processes stream their output only after completion, so a log monitor would remain silent until the end. The e2e and hub tests run sequentially rather than overlapping, which keeps memory usage predictable. The check step is now fast and green, so the remaining verify t