et.\\n(Use `node --trace-warnings ...` to show where the warning was created)\\n{\\\"launch\\\":1,\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"detail\\\":{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"errors\\\":[],\\\"ready\\\":true,\\\"screen\\\":\\\"title\\\",\\\"canvas\\\":{\\\"width\\\":1280,\\\"height\\\":720},\\\"css\\\":{\\\"width\\\":1280,\\\"height\\\":720},\\\"dpr\\\":1,\\\"requested\\\":{\\\"width\\\":1280,\\\"height\\\":720},\\\"shot\\\":{\\\"width\\\":1280,\\\"height\\\":720},\\\"ids\\\":13,\\\"paint\\\":{\\\"cells\\\":1296,\\\"colors\\\":484,\\\"largestShare\\\":0.13194444444444445},\\\"focus\\\":{\\\"before\\\":0,\\\"after\\\":1}}}\\n{\\\"launch\\\":2,\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"detail\\\":{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"errors\\\":[],\\\"ready\\\":true,\\\"screen\\\":\\\"title\\\",\\\"canvas\\\":{\\\"width\\\":1280,\\\"height\\\":720},\\\"css\\\":{\\\"width\\\":1280,\\\"height\\\":720},\\\"dpr\\\":1,\\\"requested\\\":{\\\"width\\\":1280,\\\"height\\\":720},\\\"shot\\\":{\\\"width\\\":1280,\\\"height\\\":720},\\\"ids\\\":13,\\\"paint\\\":{\\\"cells\\\":1296,\\\"colors\\\":482,\\\"largestShare\\\":0.13194444444444445},\\\"focus\\\":{\\\"before\\\":0,\\\"after\\\":1}}}\\nEXIT:0\\n\",\"total_lines\":6}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"2fd4154d-f08f-474b-bd91-3119967f96e3"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_790","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Verification is running. I will start a monitor to wake me when the turn ends, but I will wait for it.\n\nChecking README and log files for stale issue counts while verify runs. The HTML was rebuilt after launch evidence, so the prior launch may be outdated. End-to-end tests inside verify use the current HTML, but dedicated launch-1/launch-2 might be stale.\n\nLaunches will run after verify passes to avoid browser overlap. The existing ux.log and nowebgpu.log files are from the previous HTML build, but verify's end-to-end tests already cover those checks.\n\nThe HTML rebuild is purely cosmetic. The logic and bundle behavior are unchanged, so the prior launch evidence is effectively valid. Re-running the launches after verify passes is still necessary because the plan gates on them.\n\nVerify captures hub output, but it only saves failure lines and the summary. The existing hub.log remains the detailed evidence from the previous HTML build. If verify's hub test passes against the new HTML, that behavior is proven even though the log itself is stale.\n\nI will read exit-interview.json fully to prepare the four required reply blocks. I am starting the monitor and will wait on verify with a long timeout.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7bfae605-dbae-444d-988d-ef5d2d455fef-58","name":"monitor","input":{"command":"SCRATCH=/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer\nLOG=\"$SCRATCH/verify.log\"\nPIDFILE=\"$SCRATCH/verify.pid\"\nfor i in $(seq 1 60); do [ -s \"$PIDFILE\" ] && break; sleep 1; done\nPID=$(cat \"$PIDFILE\" 2>/dev/null || true)\nif [ -z \"$PID\" ]; then echo \"FAILED: no verify pid\"; exit 1; fi\nwhile kill -0 \"$PID\" 2>/dev/null; do sleep 30; done\nif grep -q 'verify: .* 0 failed' \"$LOG\" && grep -q 'EXIT:0' \"$LOG\"; then\n  echo \"DONE: $(grep -E '^verify:|^EXIT:' \"$LOG\" | tr '\\n' ' ')\"\nelse\n  echo \"FAILED: $(tail -c 1500 \"$LOG\" | tr '\\n' ' ')\"\n  exit 1\nfi","description":"Wake when npm run verify finishes","persistent":false}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7bfae605-dbae-444d-988d-ef5d2d455fef-59","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"Fourteen|fourteen|Still running|verify|96 by 60|radial","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/README.md"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7bfae605-dbae-444d-988d-ef5d2d455fef-60","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/exit-interview.json"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7bfae605-dbae-444d-988d-ef5d2d455fef-61","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/sim.log","offset":1,"limit":15}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7bfae605-dbae-444d-988d-ef5d2d455fef-62","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/bot.log","offset":1,"limit":20}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7bfae605-dbae-444d-988d-ef5d2d455fef-63","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/content.log","offset":1,"limit":20}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3710,"output_tokens":1425,"cache_read_input_tokens":96128,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"7d62714c-57e5-4bb2-9e9d-191a64d97650"}
