t\\\", \\\"ok\\\": true, \\\"detail\\\": \\\"Vitals drain 2 reset 1\\\"}\\n{\\\"name\\\": \\\"two pads claim seats and move\\\", \\\"ok\\\": true, \\\"detail\\\": \\\"{\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Seat 1 claimedSeat 2 claimedSeat 3Seat 4\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"gloves\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"x\\\\\\\":3.305169172322869,\\\\\\\"z\\\\\\\":0},{\\\\\\\"x\\\\\\\":-3.305169172322869,\\\\\\\"z\\\\\\\":0},{\\\\\\\"x\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"z\\\\\\\":0},{\\\\\\\"x\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"z\\\\\\\":0}]}\\\"}\\n{\\\"name\\\": \\\"music bus is quiet and a tone is audible\\\", \\\"ok\\\": true, \\\"detail\\\": \\\"{\\\\\\\"music\\\\\\\":0.1,\\\\\\\"state\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"running\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"peak\\\\\\\":255,\\\\\\\"offline\\\\\\\":true}\\\"}\\n{\\\"name\\\": \\\"touch asks for a controller\\\", \\\"ok\\\": true, \\\"detail\\\": \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\\n\\\\nSettings\\\"}\\n{\\\"name\\\": \\\"prompts follow the last device\\\", \\\"ok\\\": true, \\\"detail\\\": \\\"true true\\\"}\\n{\\\"name\\\": \\\"Xbox glyphs are a setting\\\", \\\"ok\\\": true, \\\"detail\\\": \\\"Glyphs Xbox\\\\nBack\\\"}\\n\",\"total_lines\":10}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-314a596e-f84b-4dac-a892-ae1abb3bbcb9-68","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→{\\\"name\\\": \\\"firefox WebGPU message\\\", \\\"ok\\\": true, \\\"detail\\\": \\\"firefox|This game needs a browser with WebGPU.\\\"}\\n{\\\"name\\\": \\\"webkit WebGPU message\\\", \\\"ok\\\": true, \\\"detail\\\": \\\"webkit|This game needs a browser with WebGPU.\\\"}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→{\\\"name\\\": \\\"firefox WebGPU message\\\", \\\"ok\\\": true, \\\"detail\\\": \\\"firefox|This game needs a browser with WebGPU.\\\"}\\n{\\\"name\\\": \\\"webkit WebGPU message\\\", \\\"ok\\\": true, \\\"detail\\\": \\\"webkit|This game needs a browser with WebGPU.\\\"}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/nowebgpu.log\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"{\\\"name\\\": \\\"firefox WebGPU message\\\", \\\"ok\\\": true, \\\"detail\\\": \\\"firefox|This game needs a browser with WebGPU.\\\"}\\n{\\\"name\\\": \\\"webkit WebGPU message\\\", \\\"ok\\\": true, \\\"detail\\\": \\\"webkit|This game needs a browser with WebGPU.\\\"}\\n\",\"total_lines\":2}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-314a596e-f84b-4dac-a892-ae1abb3bbcb9-69","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"20→16. Not critical. The use prompt kept the previous device, because the shell redrew only when the menu changed. The stamp now includes the prompt.\\n17. Not critical. The WebGPU sentence ran before `#msg` existed, so a browser that did not throw stayed on \\\"Loading…\\\". It is shown again on `DOMContentLoaded`, when the line is in the page.\\n18. Not critical. Balance reset sat past the bottom of a 720p screen and the page did not scroll, so a click could not reach it. The dev screen scrolls, and Reset is the first row.\\n19. Not critical. A tap on Settings in the touch gate also counted as a pointerdown, which hid the gate and left the kiosk. The shell then replaced the button before the click arrived, so Settings never opened. A pointerdown that starts on a control is left for that control.\\n20. Critical. A hub round called ready only after the engine inspector existed. Two software WebGPU copies were still warming when the card gave up, so the round stayed in loading. Ready is sent when the session is connected, and Enter on the card answers before the first frame. Time-up is answered the same way: if the sequencer is not up yet, the host still finishes before grace runs out.\\n\\nTwenty issues. Eleven were game-breaking: 1–9, 14, and 20. Nine were not: 10–13 and 15–19.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"20→16. Not critical. The use prompt kept the previous device, because the shell redrew only when the menu changed. The stamp now includes the prompt.\\n17. Not critical. The WebGPU sentence ran before `#msg` existed, so a browser that did not throw stayed on \\\"Loading…\\\". It is shown again on `DOMContentLoaded`, when the line is in the page.\\n18. Not critical. Balance reset sat past the bottom of a 720p screen and the page did not scroll, so a click could not reach it. The dev screen scrolls, and Reset is the first row.\\n19. Not critical. A tap on Settings in the touch gate also counted as a pointerdown, which hid the gate and left the kiosk. The shell then replaced the button before the click arrived, so Settings never opened. A pointerdown that starts on a control is left for that control.\\n20. Critical. A hub round called ready only after the engine inspector existed. Two software WebGPU copies were still warming when the card gave up, so the round stayed in loading. Ready is sent when the session is connected, and Enter on the card answers before the first frame. Time-up is answered the same way: if the sequencer is not up yet, the host still finishes before grace runs out.\\n\\nTwenty issues. Eleven were game-breaking: 1–9, 14, and 20. Nine were not: 10–13 and 15–19.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md\",\"offset\":20,\"limit\":15,\"raw_output\":\"16. Not critical. The use prompt kept the previous device, because the shell redrew only when the menu changed. The stamp now includes the prompt.\\n17. Not critical. The WebGPU sentence ran before `#msg` existed, so a browser that did not throw stayed on \\\"Loading…\\\". It is shown again on `DOMContentLoaded`, when the line is in the page.\\n18. Not critical. Balance reset sat past the bottom of a 720p screen and the page did not scroll, so a click could not reach it. The dev screen scrolls, and Reset is the first row.\\n19. Not critical. A tap on Settings in the touch gate also counted as a pointerdown, which hid the gate and left the kiosk. The shell then replaced the button before the click arrived, so Settings never opened. A pointerdown that starts on a control is left for that control.\\n20. Critical. A hub round called ready only after the engine inspector existed. Two software WebGPU copies were still warming when the card gave up, so the round stayed in loading. Ready is sent when the session is connected, and Enter on the card answers before the first frame. Time-up is answered the same way: if the sequencer is not up yet, the host still finishes before grace runs out.\\n\\nTwenty issues. Eleven were game-breaking: 1–9, 14, and 20. Nine were not: 10–13 and 15–19.\\n\",\"total_lines\":26}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"0eb8d322-785a-445f-80ec-5b22c6d8242c"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_792","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"README still references `session.js`, but the vendor file was renamed to `session.txt`.\n\nThe session client is still inlined in index.html. The README line about `session.js` is slightly stale but acceptable for now. A one-line correction can wait until after verification.\n\nLog evidence is solid. sim.log ends at SIM:0, bot.log ends at BOT:0, and content ends at CONTENT:0.\n\nThe README line about session.js will be corrected now. It is a small factual edit that does not require verification.\n\nThe README correction will be deferred until the final hand-in pass to avoid unnecessary churn. I am pausing to wait for the monitor notification.\n\nA brief status update is appropriate: the check is green and verification is running. The README session.js line and any goal plan deviations will be corrected now.\n\nI will add true deviations to the goal plan and check the first six boxes now. The last box stays open until verification, hand-ins, and cleanup are complete.\n\nI will check boxes 1 through 6 now and add deviations to the goal plan. This avoids redoing that work if verification fails.\n\nThe two deviations will be written as terse bullets. One notes the sheet density is 96×60 rather than 320×192. The other notes the radial slow was fixed at 0.6.\n\nThe deviations will be written as two terse bullets. The first notes the sheet is 96 by 60 and four 320 by 192 copies were killed for memory. The second notes radial slow stays at 0.6 because the view slider cannot be read from the sim.\n\nThe README line about the first script will be corrected to say the hub client is kept byte for byte. The deviations will be written as two short affirmative bullets. The last plan checkbox remains unchecked until verification and hand-ins are complete.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Check is green and the one-file page is rebuilt. Verify is running. I'll record the two real deviations on the plan and mark the work that is already finished."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-99451d12-6f24-4455-8d12-7124b9386832-70","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3%2Fwork/01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151/goal/plan.md","old_string":"- [ ] Choose the title by generating 50 riffs and picking with a real RNG; create the dev subfolder; clone the engine; `npm ci`; add `npm run verify`; confirm a one-file HTML boots from `file://`.\n- [ ] Build the living operating field, cursor, hand, and one scalpel guide cut that already reads at 1080p; test field state from the sim.\n- [ ] Finish Case 1 (drain, forceps, suture, syringe, gel, radial, vitals, clock, ratings, failure, debrief) and a bot win.\n- [ ] Add title, board, story scene with gibberish voices, briefing, pause, settings, glyphs, saves, attract mode, and dev-mode sliders.\n- [ ] Add Cases 2 and 3 (scalpel, scanner, laser, sites, Code, Stillpoint) and the AI Hub session path, including the Node sequencer test and a harness run on the case that exists.\n- [ ] Add strains, flaps, Cases 4–8, couch seats, Gala Shift, Free Surgery, the rest of the story, songs, and field animations.\n- [ ] Tune until the bot clears the required seeds; run `npm run verify`; write the root HTML, `exit-interview.json`, About screen, and `PROGRESS.md`; stop only processes this work started and remove the temporary `TMPDIR`.","new_string":"- [x] Choose the title by generating 50 riffs and picking with a real RNG; create the dev subfolder; clone the engine; `npm ci`; add `npm run verify`; confirm a one-file HTML boots from `file://`.\n- [x] Build the living operating field, cursor, hand, and one scalpel guide cut that already reads at 1080p; test field state from the sim.\n- [x] Finish Case 1 (drain, forceps, suture, syringe, gel, radial, vitals, clock, ratings