{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_801","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All 93 verification checks passed.\n\nUpdating PROGRESS.md to mark the game as finished. Checking the final plan checkbox and confirming hand-ins: HTML, exit-interview.json, and PROGRESS.md. Cleaning up leftover temporary files and server processes. The launch evidence predates the HTML rebuild; the plan requires launching the rebuilt HTML twice.\n\nThe evaluator requires PROGRESS.md and the plan checklist to be updated only after hand-ins match. The existing launch evidence predates the final HTML rebuild, so a strict auditor might reject it for differing byte counts. The verification suite already launches the current HTML file:// version.\n\nThe verifier audits committed evidence rather than rebuilding it. Stale launch logs would be dishonest proof against the shipped file. I will re-run the two file:// launches against the current HTML to match the shipped deliverable. I am checking if e2e.mjs covers the same checks as launch.mjs.\n\nThe two file:// launches will run sequentially to avoid browser contention. The existing ux.log and nowebgpu.log files are from earlier e2e runs; verify re-proved those checks internally, so they do not need to be regenerated.\n\nverify.log is current and green. It serves as the primary proof that the checks passed on the rebuilt HTML. The older launch, ux, hub, and nowebgpu logs are additional evidence from earlier runs.\n\nI will read launch.mjs to re-run the two file:// launches against the rebuilt HTML. I will also clean up any leftover temporary directories and browser processes from our own verification run.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-02da5fa3-75b3-4542-a0b3-b814dd37293f-83","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/launch.mjs","limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-02da5fa3-75b3-4542-a0b3-b814dd37293f-84","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/TASK.md","offset":80,"limit":50}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":462,"output_tokens":1390,"cache_read_input_tokens":122112,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"fe5635ea-1fd8-49bc-b46f-fd93a5650e00"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-02da5fa3-75b3-4542-a0b3-b814dd37293f-83","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * Two sequential file:// launches of the shipped page. Writes launch-N/log, state, and shot.\\n * Run from the game package so Playwright resolves. Not part of the game.\\n */\\nimport { mkdirSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport { chromium } from 'playwright';\\n\\nconst FILE = new URL(\\n  'file:///home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731.html',\\n10→);\\nconst scratch = new URL(\\n  'file:///home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/',\\n);\\nconst width = 1280;\\nconst height = 720;\\nconst args = [\\n  '--enable-unsafe-webgpu',\\n  '--enable-features=Vulkan',\\n  '--use-vulkan=swiftshader',\\n20→  '--use-angle=swiftshader',\\n  '--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader',\\n];\\n\\nfunction coverage(rows) {\\n  const cells = rows.flatMap((row) => row.split(' ')).filter(Boolean);\\n  const counts = new Map();\\n  for (const cell of cells) counts.set(cell, (counts.get(cell) ?? 0) + 1);\\n  let top = 0;\\n  for (const n of counts.values()) if (n > top) top = n;\\n30→  return { cells: cells.length, colors: counts.size, largestShare: cells.length ? top / cells.length : 1 };\\n}\\n\\nconst browser = await chromium.launch({\\n  executablePath: process.env.CHROMIUM_PATH,\\n  headless: true,\\n  args,\\n});\\n\\nlet failed = 0;\\n40→for (const n of [1, 2]) {\\n  const dir = new URL(`launch-${n}/`, scratch);\\n  mkdirSync(dir, { recursive: true });\\n  const log = [];\\n  const page = await browser.newPage({ viewport: { width, height } });\\n  const errors = [];\\n  page.on('pageerror', (error) => errors.push(error.message));\\n  page.on('console', (msg) => {\\n    if (msg.type() === 'error') errors.push(msg.text());\\n  });\\n50→  await page.goto(FILE.href);\\n  await page.waitForFunction(() => window.__engine?.ready && window.__compass?.screen === 'title', null, {\\n    timeout: 40000,\\n  });\\n  const before = await page.evaluate(async () => {\\n    const canvas = document.querySelector('#view');\\n    const shot = await window.__engine.shot({ pixels: false, ids: true, metrics: false, thumbnail: true });\\n    const focus = window.__compass.campaign.focus;\\n    return {\\n      ready: window.__engine.ready,\\n60→      errors: (window.__engine.errors ?? []).map((item) => item.code),\\n      screen: window.__compass.screen,\\n      canvas: { width: canvas.width, height: canvas.height },\\n      css: { width: canvas.clientWidth, height: canvas.clientHeight },\\n      dpr: window.devicePixelRatio,\\n      shot: { width: shot.width, height: shot.height, rows: shot.thumbnail?.rows ?? [] },\\n      ids: (shot.ids?.visible ?? []).length,\\n      focus,\\n    };\\n  });\\n70→  const beforeFocus = before.focus;\\n  await page.keyboard.press('ArrowDown');\\n  await page.waitForFunction((was) => window.__compass.campaign.focus !== was, beforeFocus, { timeout: 4000 });\\n  const afterFocus = await page.evaluate(() => window.__compass.campaign.focus);\\n  const paint = coverage(before.shot.rows);\\n  const sizeOk = before.canvas.width === width * before.dpr && before.canvas.height === height * before.dpr;\\n  const filled = paint.cells > 100 && paint.largestShare < 0.85 && (paint.colors > 4 || before.ids > 2);\\n  const ok = errors.length === 0 && before.ready && sizeOk && filled && afterFocus !== beforeFocus;\\n  if (!ok) failed += 1;\\n  const state = {\\n80→    ok,\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * Two sequential file:// launches of the shipped page. Writes launch-N/log, state, and shot.\\n * Run from the game package so Playwright resolves. Not part of the game.\\n */\\nimport { mkdirSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport { chromium } from