{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_825","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A potential bug was spotted in `enterPhase`: it resets vitals to zero and pushes a flatline event, but it may not actually start the code.\n\n`enterPhase` does not call `flatline()` directly. The code actually starts in `stepVitals` when vitals reach zero or below. Because `stepVitals` runs every step, the flatline triggers on the next tick unless vitals are healed before then.\n\nA bug was found in `flatline` for the mercy phase. The code incorrectly forces the patient to die and fails the operation whenever `op.codeAllowed` is false or the patient is already coded, even for mercy.\n\nThe `free` flag for mercy is likely a misnomer. It probably means a successful shock does not consume the patient's Code allowance, not that misses are free. The `pressPaddle` function always decrements tries on miss, so the \"no try cost\" rule may be implemented elsewhere.\n\n`code.free` usage is being checked. The code phase flow is confirmed: `pressPaddle` sets `codeCleared` on success, so the advance logic sees `phaseDone`.\n\nA potential issue was noted for the kindness phase. Setting vitals to zero there may not trigger an immediate code start, since `stepVitals` only runs on the next tick. If a healing effect like attract intervenes before that tick, the patient could recover.\n\n`enterPhase` does not set `patient.alive`, but the `stepVitals` loop skips dead patients, so this is harmless. The bot must hit the band on the next tick to trigger the code.\n\nThe mercy-bind gift requirement is being checked. The plan grants a free gift, but act.ts at line 430 may refuse the binder if the gift is not up.\n\nA tag mismatch was spotted for the moving guide. driftGuide only runs on guides tagged \"moving\", yet curve() might not create that tag.\n\nThe sleep ring mechanic is missing from mercy(). The plan calls for one every nine seconds during motes, so its absence needs verification.\n\nThe sleep ring is part of phase 1, so the phase structure itself is intact.\n\nA double-counting bug was found in `retie`. It increments the timer for done tendrils, but `retieDone` also increments it. The timer therefore advances twice as fast, causing reattachment at five seconds instead of ten.\n\nThe bot still wins according to tests.\n\n`revealTimeout` is dead code. The flap clip timeout is handled in the main loop, so this function is a no-op.\n\nA demonstrable wrong result is still being sought. The missing gift grant during mercy-bind may be the culprit: if binders require it and the gift is not granted, the bot could not win unless it uses a charge.\n\nThe bot won the mercy case using its three charges, so a missing free gift grant is not a failure. The sticky `codeCleared` reset in `enterPhase` is harmless because flatline overwrites it anyway.\n\nThe stepOp execution order is being checked to see if a vitals=0 set during enterPhase is processed immediately, and whether codeCleared could be set true incorrectly.\n\nA potential conflict was noted: if the kindness phase sets vitals to zero, stepVitals may drain them further on the next tick and trigger flatline. If a code is already running from the same step, this could cause problems.\n\nMultiple patients in the gala phase are being verified; losing any patient should fail the operation.\n\nShip roll is implemented as small cursor drift rather than camera movement. The criterion requires flaps and strains.\n\nShip roll is present in PLAN case 5. It may satisfy the \"ship roll hazard\" rule even as a tiny sine nudge.\n\nStrains do not crawl. The strainSpeed slider is unused because strains only drift with the guide.\n\nWhether movement is a core distinguishing feature is being questioned.\n\nCriterion 2 lists five strains with telegraphed distinguishing features. Only Mercy's burrow with a moving guide explicitly requires movement. Lull's quieting aura may be incomplete if the ECG does not dim.\n\nLull's quieting aura is likely just a visual effect. The aura drain already exists in stepVitals.\n\nA systematic audit of HTML hand-in requirements is now underway. This includes session.js, data-about usage, never-use names, audio tags, TODOs, engine git status, title screen titles, and hub meta tags.\n\nThe launch paint file shot.txt is 9071 bytes. Its format is being inspected to verify the launch image.\n\nThe verify script runs e2e and hub tests. These must load the root HTML rather than the dev server.\n\nHub-r4 failed at 02:44 and hub-r5 passed at 02:49. The later pass is valid because code likely changed between runs. This does not constitute a failure.\n\nAn eslint failure at 03:24 was fixed before verify passed at 03:47. I should verify current line counts are still under the hard cap and check file mtimes against verify.log to confirm the evidence is fresh. The verify.log only shows a summary line, not individual test names, so I need to inspect e2e.mjs directly to confirm the campaign test exists and passed.\n\nThe verify.log matches the plan's exact output format. The captured file is valid because verify suppresses stdout and only prints failures and the summary line. To confirm the tests still pass, I will compare test file mtimes against the verify timestamp.\n\nI am now auditing act.ts for suture, syringe, and closing win-condition bugs. I will verify that every case ends with a close phase so advance() cannot win without it. The time-out, slip-limit, and flatline-failure loss conditions are confirmed implemented. I will also check case phase lists and hand-in artifacts in parallel.\n\nThe `free` flag in `pressPaddle` is stored but never used. The phrase \"does not cost a try\" likely refers to the case-level code allowance rather than skipping the patient's try count.\n\nMercy allows unlimited codes because `coded` is never set, so the unused `free` flag is harmless. The next step is to inspect Solace's mother under the flap, verify gala multi-patient vitals, and hunt for a decisive bug in win conditions, syringe targeting, or stitch placement.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b802e35f-aa35-4bd0-8dcc-84a98a4f27f0-46","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"cocoon|decoy|matron|vulnerable|quiet|dim","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game","glob":"*.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b802e35f-aa35-4bd0-8dcc-84a98a4f27f0-47","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/step.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b802e35f-aa35-4bd0-8dcc-84a98a4f27f0-48","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/act.ts","offset":330,"limit":180}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2644,"output_tokens":3046,"cache_read_input_tokens":108800,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"f41a7a5f-e378-4d1f-ad77-e1ba733cde8a"}
