,120,93,63,46,112,114,101,115,115,101,100,59,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":2,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/input/hands.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":68,\"content\":\"function down(pad: Gamepad | undefined, index: number): boolean {\"},{\"line_number\":69,\"content\":\"  return !!pad && !!pad.buttons[index]?.pressed;\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"7172b207-a647-4134-a00a-88f7ad5c0dd2"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_830","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Paddle input is level-triggered. pressPaddle counts every frame outside the green band as a miss. This is a real bug.\n\nTwo tries allow only two frames outside the green band. A human pressing slightly early fails instantly. Starting in the red zone also fails within two frames before any success can register.\n\nThe intended input is holding both triggers until the green band appears. A one-frame early press or a two-frame tap that crosses into red both fail instantly.\n\nThere is also a keyboard input issue: paddles require holding both MouseLeft and MouseRight, but Enter only maps to 'use'. Keyboard-only players cannot perform paddles.\n\nThe `use` input also maps to MouseLeft, so holding both triggers during a paddle simultaneously activates the current tool. The miss-every-frame bug is the decisive failure mode: holding both triggers while the ring is outside the green band counts as a miss every single frame.\n\nA quick script will verify the exact failure sequence: tries drop from 2 to 1 to 0, ending with \"The line stays flat.\" The applyHands function confirms no edge detection exists; paddle presses are evaluated every single step.\n\nGift input is edge-triggered at the scene layer, but the simulation still counts it as a press every step while held. Paddle input lacks any edge detection entirely. The two-try limit is effectively unusable for a human because holding triggers burns both tries in roughly 33 milliseconds. This reveals a deeper defect: the core failure rule incorrectly treats normal presses that are not perfectly single-frame as failures.\n\nThe existing test \"fails two misses\" intentionally presses the paddle on every non-green step. It passes against this buggy behavior, confirming the implementation is wrong for players.\n\nThe engine runs at a fixed 60Hz, so holding triggers for even a hundred milliseconds spans six steps and still burns both tries instantly.\n\nA successful strategy of tapping only during the green band would clear the code immediately on the first green frame.\n\nThe codeBand comment describes the timing window as generous, but the lack of edge detection nullifies that generosity for any press starting one frame early. This is a valid bug. I am now checking whether pad buttons 6 and 7 map to L2 and R2.\n\nPad button mapping is confirmed: button 6 is left trigger and button 7 is right trigger, matching the plan. The `use` input also maps to button 7, so holding both pad triggers simultaneously activates the current tool. Seat 0 correctly combines pad buttons with mouse input for paddles. Gift edge-triggering at the scene layer is correct. A minor `strainSpeed` issue was considered but set aside to avoid piling nits; the paddle bug remains the primary defect.\n\nMercy sleep ring and moving guide drift are partially implemented. Heart-stop code exists. The parenthetical criterion is largely met, so this is not a refutation.\n\nSheet vertex density is 96x60 rather than 40401. PLAN.md 17.3 treats the higher count as a technique proof, not a required baseline.\n\nThe radialSlow slider is dead. Its value is hardcoded to 0.6 and never changes.\n\nThe radial slow slider is non-functional because it is marked view:true, which prevents the simulation from reading its value. Other sliders work by using defineSettings with when:'now', so the sim can access them. This is a self-inflicted limitation rather than a core miss.\n\nThe radial slow slider is a documented deviation, not a core miss. The paddle bug remains the only solid refutation.\n\nI will verify hand-in checks and run a quick script to confirm the paddle bug. I also need to check the About screen, HTML name, exit interview, TODOs, FIXMEs, and never-use names. The launch evidence looks plausible: 482 colors across 1296 cells gives a largestShare of 0.13, which matches a filled scene rather than a blank canvas. I should inspect shot.txt to confirm whether this is a real engine shot or fabricated statistics.\n\nThe hub client and engine remain unmodified. The About screen carries `data-about=\"usage\"`. I will run a quick Node script with tsx to verify the exact failure sequence for the paddle bug.\n\nThe script revealed the exact failure sequence. In `stepOp`, `applyHands` runs before `stepVitals`. Because vitals are already zero, the code starts immediately on the first step. The paddle press is evaluated during that same step and fails instantly. This confirms the bug: a single early press or hold burns both tries before the green band ever appears.\n\nThe gift, drop, swap, and hint inputs are edge-triggered in the simulation to avoid exactly this bug. Paddle was overlooked as an oversight rather than a deliberate design choice. I am now checking whether drop or hint share the same level-triggered flaw.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-022a0113-d592-4838-81b5-d832b3470758-59","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"TODO|FIXME|unimplemented|placeholder|lorem ipsum|lorem","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game","glob":"*.{ts,js,mjs,html,md}"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-022a0113-d592-4838-81b5-d832b3470758-60","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"Derek Stiles|Angie Thompson|Naomi Kimishima|Nozomi Weaver|Hope Hospital|Caduceus|Healing Touch|Kyriaki|GUILT|Z-Cells","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-022a0113-d592-4838-81b5-d832b3470758-61","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"data-about=\\\"usage\\\"|hub:session|hub:webgpu|session.js","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game","glob":"*.{html,ts}"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-022a0113-d592-4838-81b5-d832b3470758-62","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731.html","limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1674,"output_tokens":2873,"cache_read_input_tokens":130304,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"13238212-453b-48d4-8d9b-692edeb3e308"}
