 \\\"mass\\\", x: 6, z: 4, hidden: false, locked: true }, 0);\\nop.patients[0].vitals = 0;\\nconst hold = { ...idleHand(op.seats[0]), paddle: true };\\nfor (let i = 0; i < 6; i++) {\\n  stepOp(op, [hold]);\\n  console.log(JSON.stringify({ i, tick: op.tick, status: op.status, fail: op.fail, tries: op.code?.tries ?? null, shocks: op.code?.shocks ?? null, vitals: op.patients[0].vitals, band: (op.tick % 90) }));\\n}\\n'\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Hold paddles on a live flatline and print tries\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3%2Fwork/01a1ab54-ed6b-7953-b392-c23a1a1a1e69/terminal/call-7158ed3b-36a4-4110-a99a-1de6cc5f2ab5-66.log\",\"total_bytes\":1109}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"0e54d447-2c02-4bf9-81b3-22062bbac5f9"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_834","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Confirmed. Holding both paddles from flatline.\n\nHolding both paddles from the start triggers a miss at tick 3. The green band only opens at tick 28, so the player dies long before the window appears.\n\nTapping only during the green band works. The core bug is level-triggered controls: held buttons consume a try every step outside the band. This causes a 33ms early press to fail the entire operation.\n\nThe two-try rule is unreachable for held paddles. Tests only pulse paddles for a single step, so they never catch held presses.\n\nThe strainSpeed slider is stored but never read by the strain logic. This weak finding will not be included as a refute-level gap.\n\nThe radialSlow slider is also hardcoded and never read. The Mercy test skips later phases, but the code supports them.\n\nEmpty clear phase auto-wins are by design for fixtures. The end-to-end input path confirms level-triggered paddles: boot.ts packs hands with level paddle, scene pulseEdges does not strip it, and the keyboard binds use and radial to held mouse buttons.\n\nThe bug is confirmed as a high-confidence refute. The plan requires two tries per Code, but the mechanic counts one try per frame of held input rather than one press. A single-frame tap inside the green band succeeds, yet a continuous hold outside it consumes one try every step.\n\nSwap is bound to PadRightStick, which is the same input as radial. This creates a direct hardware conflict between the two actions.\n\nThe engine may map PadRightStick to stick deflection rather than the right-stick click. Opening the radial menu could then accidentally trigger swap.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3b07bde5-467f-463d-9ea3-01969829ab8a-67","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"PadRightStick","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/input","glob":"*.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3b07bde5-467f-463d-9ea3-01969829ab8a-68","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/PLAN.md","offset":350,"limit":70}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":788,"output_tokens":1471,"cache_read_input_tokens":141184,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"391a0e87-ea21-446e-b0d6-a9406d4be60d"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-3b07bde5-467f-463d-9ea3-01969829ab8a-67","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,55,51,49,95,95,120,53,57,99,49,100,51,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,53,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,55,51,49,95,95,120,53,57,99,49,100,51,47,119,111,114,107,47,84,114,97,117,109,97,45,67,111,109,112,97,115,115,45,84,114,97,117,109,97,45,67,101,110,116,101,114,45,83,101,99,111,110,100,45,79,112,105,110,105,111,110,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,55,51,49,47,101,110,103,105,110,101,47,105,110,112,117,116,47,99,111,100,101,115,46,116,115,10,55,48,58,32,32,39,80,97,100,82,105,103,104,116,83,116,105,99,107,39,44,10,56,52,58,32,32,39,80,97,100,82,105,103,104,116,83,116,105,99,107,85,112,39,44,10,56,53,58,32,32,39,80,97,100,82,105,103,104,116,83,116,105,99,107,68,111,119,110,39,44,10,56,54,58,32,32,39,80,97,100,82,105,103,104,116,83,116,105,99,107,76,101,102,116,39,44,10,56,55,58,32,32,39,80,97,100,82,105,103,104,116,83,116,105,99,107,82,105,103,104,116,39,44,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":5,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/engine/input/codes.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":70,\"content\":\"  'PadRightStick',\"},{\"line_number\":84,\"content\":\"  'PadRightStickUp',\"},{\"line_number\":85,\"content\":\"  'PadRightStickDown',\"},{\"line_number\":86,\"content\":\"  'PadRightStickLeft',\"},{\"line_number\":87,\"content\":\"  'PadRightStickRight',\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-3b07bde5-467f-463d-9ea3-01969829ab8a-68","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"350→## 10. Controls and screens\\n\\n**Pad (DualSense, or any pad in the standard mapping). This is the design target.**\\n\\n| Input | Action | Engine code |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Left stick | Cursor | read directly (§17.4) |\\n| R2 or Cross | Use tool (hold) | `PadRightTrigger`, `PadSouth` |\\n| Right stick | Radial: push to open, aim at a tool, release to equip. Field time ×0.6 while open | `PadRightStick*` |\\n| L1 / R1 | Previous / next tool | `PadLeftShoulder`, `PadRightShoulder` |\\n360→| L2 | Precision: cursor ×0.4, stronger magnet, slight dolly-in | `PadLeftTrigger` |\\n| Triangle | Gift (and the pulse-lock beats) | `PadNorth` |\\n| Square | Quick Syringe | `PadWest` |\\n| Circle | Drop what forceps hold; cancel the radial | `PadEast` |\\n| D-pad left/right | Switch site | `PadLeft`, `PadRight` |\\n| D-pad up | Hint | `PadUp` |\\n| R3 | Swap surgeon (Cases 6 to 8) | `PadRightStick` |\\n| Options | Pause | `PadStart` |\\n| L2 + R2 | Paddles, in a Code | triggers |\\n\\n370→Menus: D-pad or left stick, Cross accepts, Circle goes back. Both sticks and triggers are analog; use dead zones. In a hub session, ignore\\nOptions while Create is held (that chord belongs to the hub).\\n\\n**Mouse and keyboard. The same game and screens, but native.**\\n\\n- **Mouse** moves the cursor absolutely, 1:1, no pointer lock, with the OS cursor hidden over the field. LMB uses the tool. **Hold RMB** for the\\n  radial at the cursor, flick and release. Wheel cycles tools. Keys **1–8** pick tools directly. The tool bar, site tabs and Board cards are clickable, and hovering a valid target highlights it. Shift: precision. Space:\\n  Gift. F: quick Syringe. R: drop. Q/E: sites. H: hint. Tab: swap. Esc: pause. LMB + RMB: paddles.\\n- **Keyboard-only** still works: WASD or arrows move the cursor, Enter uses the tool.\\n- Every menu: hover moves focus, click picks (`createMenu` already does this; do the same in custom panels). Rebinding in Settings → Controls.\\n380→\\n**Cursor feel on a pad (page-side, tune these).** Speed = `cursorSpeed × lean^2.2`. Within 0.6 m of a valid target for the current tool: velocity ×0.55 and a\\ngentle pull (the magnet). On a scalpel guide while cutting: the across-line part of stick input ×0.4 (rail assist). Suturing on a wound: a soft clamp\\nto ±0.8 m of the wound (sew assist), so you just weave. Mouse gets a light version only, at 0.2 of these strengths.\\n\\n**Prompts** follow the device used last (`input.lastDevice`). Draw your own glyph set in code (SVG/CSS): PlayStation shapes by default for **any** pad; **Settings →\\nControls → Glyphs: PlayStation / Xbox** swaps to A B X Y and LB RB LT RT. Don't use `input.prompt()` text directly, as it reads Xbox for unknown pads. Keyboard\\nshows keycaps; mouse shows mouse icons.\\n\\n**10-foot rules.** Judge every screen at 1920×1080 from a screenshot. Body text at least 32 px; instruments and menu items at least 64 px tall; thick outlines on guides\\n390→and cursor; focus state huge. One idea per screen. No tables, scrolling lists of small rows, or web-style forms.\\n\\n**In-operation HUD (at most these).** Vitals and ECG, top left, big. Clock and phase name, top centre. Score and chain, top right. Tool bar, bottom centre: 8 icons\\nat 72–96 px, current raised. Odie's line, bottom left: name, big caption, no input needed (`createDialog` with `modal: false` and `auto`). Site tabs at the edges. World labels\\nfor ratings (`ui.label`), huge and brief.\\n\\n**Screens.**\\n\\n- **Boot/Loading:** dark, lighthouse beam, status text; the engine's error text stays visible if startup fails for any other reason.\\n- **No WebGPU:** the engine has no fallback, and this cannot be left to game code. Tested: in Firefox here the bundle crashes at import (`APP_START: … \\\"VERTEX\\\", Js is undefined`), before any of your module runs; WebKit shows the engine's technical `GFX_NO_WEBGPU` text. So a **classic inline script** in the head, right after the hub client, checks `navigator.gpu`. If it is missing, it shows a large plain message saying the game needs a browser with WebGPU, adds \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" on a touch-only device, calls `AIHub.fail(…)` in a session, and hides the engine's text. Do the same if `__engine.errors` later holds `GFX_NO_WEBGPU` (no adapter).\\n400→- **Title:** 3D lamp-lit OR with the lighthouse beam through rain on the window; the title; Continue / New Shift / The Board / Scrub In / Settings / About. Attract after 10 s idle (§14).\\n- **The Board:** a corkboard wall. One big case card at a time, left/right to browse: patient, one line, rank, tools as icons. Postcards tab.\\n- **Story:** full 3D scene, dialogue box along the bottom third, name plate, gibberish voice; Cross advances; hold Circle to skip the scene; auto mode in Settings.\\n- **Briefing:** patient card and one sentence, tools needed, difficulty, Start.\\n- **Pause:** Resume, Retry phase, Retry case, Handbook, Settings, Controls, **Dev Mode**, Quit to Board.\\n- **Handbook** (from Pause and the Board): big paged cards showing what you can and cannot do. One per instrument (what it does, what it cannot do, its controls in the current glyphs), the Gift, flaps, sites and the Code, and one per strain once met. Built from the data, so it cannot go stale.\\n- **Settings:** pages with few big rows. Audio (Master 70%, **Music 10%**, Effects 100%, Voice 100%). Controls (glyphs, cursor speed, aim assist, rebinding, hold vs toggle for use). Gameplay\\n  (difficulty, Simple Gift, hints, text speed, auto-advance). Display (blood colour: red / teal / off, reduce flashes, text size).\\n- **Scrub In:** four big seat slots; each device claims one by pressing its accept; Start.\\n- **About/Credits:** see §21. Paged cards, one question per card.\\n410→\\n**Touch-only devices.** Detect with `matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)')` false and no pad seen. No touch controls: put `touch=off` in the `search` you give `createEngine`, always, or the engine shows its touch layer (tested on a phone profile: `touch=off` removes it all). Show exactly **\\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\"** and a large settings button that opens Settings, which accepts taps. Attract mode runs behind it. A pad or\\nkey arriving on such a device clears the message.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Art direction\\n\\n**Base: the engine's native style.** Everything is procedural shapes from the geometry kit, materials and textures as data, puppet bodies from the body grammar. Draw it the way the engine's own clean playground look does: `resolution: 'full'`, `textures: 'smooth'`, and the `aa` filter with `scope: 'all'`, in your looks. Do **not** use the chunky default `pixels` resolution: thin surgical lines must read at 10 feet. `labs/box/looks/` has worked looks to copy from.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"350→## 10. Controls and screens\\n\\n**Pad (DualSense, or any pad in the standard mapping). This is the design target.**\\n\\n| Input | Action | Engine code |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Left stick | Cursor | read directly (§17.4) |\\n| R2 or Cross | Use tool (hold) | `PadRightTrigger`, `PadSouth` |\\n| Right stick | Radial: push to open, aim at a tool, release to equip. Field time ×0.6 while open | `PadRightStick*` |\\n| L1 / R1 | Previous / next tool | `PadLeftShoulder`, `PadRightShoulder` |\\n360→| L2 | Precision: cursor ×0.4, stronger magnet, slight dolly-in | `PadLeftTrigger` |\\n| Triangle | Gift (and the pulse-lock beats) | `PadNorth` |\\n| Square | Quick Syringe | `PadWest` |\\n| Circle | Drop what forceps hold; cancel the radial | `PadEast` |\\n| D-pad left/right | Switch site | `PadLeft`, `PadRight` |\\n| D-pad up | Hint | `PadUp` |\\n| R3 | Swap surgeon (Cases 6 to 8) | `PadRightStick` |\\n| Options | Pause | `PadStart` |\\n| L2 + R2 | Paddles, in a Code | triggers |\\n\\n370→Menus: D-pad or left stick, Cross accepts, Circle goes back. Both sticks and triggers are analog; use dead zones. In a hub session, ignore\\nOptions while Create is held (that chord belongs to the hub).\\n\\n**Mouse and keyboard. The same game and screens, but native.**\\n\\n- **Mouse** moves the cursor absolutely, 1:1, no pointer lock, with the OS cursor hidden over the field. LMB uses the tool. **Hold RMB** for the\\n  radial at the cursor, flick and release. Wheel cycles tools. Keys **1–8** pick tools directly. The tool bar, site tabs and Board cards are clickable, and hovering a valid target highlights it. Shift: precision. Space:\\n  Gift. F: quick Syringe. R: drop. Q/E: sites. H: hint. Tab: swap. Esc: pause. LMB + RMB: paddles.\\n- **Keyboard-only** still works: WASD or arrows move the cursor, Enter uses the tool.\\n- Every menu: hover moves focus, click picks (`createMenu` already does this; do the same in custom panels). Rebinding in Settings → Controls.\\n380→\\n**Cursor feel on a pad (page-side, tune these).** Speed = `cursorSpeed × lean^2.2`. Within 0.6 m of a valid target for the current tool: velocity ×0.55 and a\\ngentle pull (the magnet). On a scalpel guide while cutting: the across-line part of stick input ×0.4 (rail assist). Suturing on a wound: a soft clamp\\nto ±0.8 m of the wound (sew assist), so you just weave. Mouse gets a light version only, at 0.2 of these strengths.\\n\\n**Prompts** follow the device used last (`input.lastDevice`). Draw your own glyph set in code (SVG/CSS): PlayStation shapes by default for **any** pad; **Settings →\\nControls → Glyphs: PlayStation / Xbox** swaps to A B X Y and LB RB LT RT. Don't use `input.prompt()` text directly, as it reads Xbox for unknown pads. Keyboard\\nshows keycaps; mouse shows mouse icons.\\n\\n**10-foot rules.** Judge every screen at 1920×1080 from a screenshot. Body text at least 32 px; instruments and menu items at least 64 px tall; thick outlines on guides\\n390→and cursor; focus state huge. One idea per screen. No tables, scrolling lists of small rows, or web-style forms.\\n\\n**In-operation HUD (at most these).** Vitals and ECG, top left, big. Clock and phase name, top centre. Score and chain, top right. Tool bar, bottom centre: 8 icons\\nat 72–96 px, current raised. Odie's line, bottom left: name, big caption, no input needed (`createDialog` with `modal: false` and `auto`). Site tabs at the edges. World labels\\nfor ratings (`ui.label`), huge and brief.\\n\\n**Screens.**\\n\\n- **Boot/Loading:** dark, lighthouse beam, status text; the engine's error text stays visible if startup fails for any other reason.\\n- **No WebGPU:** the engine has no fallback, and this cannot be left to game code. Tested: in Firefox here the bundle crashes at import (`APP_START: … \\\"VERTEX\\\", Js is undefined`), before any of your module runs; WebKit shows the engine's technical `GFX_NO_WEBGPU` text. So a **classic inline script** in the head, right after the hub client, checks `navigator.gpu`. If it is missing, it shows a large plain message saying the game needs a browser with WebGPU, adds \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" on a touch-only device, calls `AIHub.fail(…)` in a session, and hides the engine's text. Do the same if `__engine.errors` later holds `GFX_NO_WEBGPU` (no adapter).\\n400→- **Title:** 3D lamp-lit OR with the lighthouse beam through rain on the window; the title; Continue / New Shift / The Board / Scrub In / Settings / About. Attract after 10 s idle (§14).\\n- **The Board:** a corkboard wall. One big case card at a time, left/right to browse: patient, one line, rank, tools as icons. Postcards tab.\\n- **Story:** full 3D scene, dialogue box along the bottom third, name plate, gibberish voice; Cross advances; hold Circle to skip the scene; auto mode in Settings.\\n- **Briefing:** patient card and one sentence, tools needed, difficulty, Start.\\n- **Pause:** Resume, Retry phase, Retry case, Handbook, Settings, Controls, **Dev Mode**, Quit to Board.\\n- **Handbook** (from Pause and the Board): big paged cards showing what you can and cannot do. One per instrument (what it does, what it cannot do, its controls in the current glyphs), the Gift, flaps, sites and the Code, and one per strain once met. Built from the data, so it cannot go stale.\\n- **Settings:** pages with few big rows. Audio (Master 70%, **Music 10%**, Effects 100%, Voice 100%). Controls (glyphs, cursor speed, aim assist, rebinding, hold vs toggle for use). Gameplay\\n  (difficulty, Simple Gift, hints, text speed, auto-advance). Display (blood colour: red / teal / off, reduce flashes, text size).\\n- **Scrub In:** four big seat slots; each device claims one by pressing its accept; Start.\\n- **About/Credits:** see §21. Paged cards, one question per card.\\n410→\\n**Touch-only devices.** Detect with `matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)')` false and no pad seen. No touch controls: put `touch=off` in the `search` you give `createEngine`, always, or the engine shows its touch layer (tested on a phone profile: `touch=off` removes it all). Show exactly **\\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\"** and a large settings button that opens Settings, which accepts taps. Attract mode runs behind it. A pad or\\nkey arriving on such a device clears the message.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Art direction\\n\\n**Base: the engine's native style.** Everything is procedural shapes from the geometry kit, materials and textures as data, puppet bodies from the body grammar. Draw it the way the engine's own clean playground look does: `resolution: 'full'`, `textures: 'smooth'`, and the `aa` filter with `scope: 'all'`, in your looks. Do **not** use the chunky default `pixels` resolution: thin surgical lines must read at 10 feet. `labs/box/looks/` has worked looks to copy from.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":350,\"limit\":70,\"raw_output\":\"## 10. Controls and screens\\n\\n**Pad (DualSense, or any pad in the standard mapping). This is the design target.**\\n\\n| Input | Action | Engine code |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Left stick | Cursor | read directly (§17.4) |\\n| R2 or Cross | Use tool (hold) | `PadRightTrigger`, `PadSouth` |\\n| Right stick | Radial: push to open, aim at a tool, release to equip. Field time ×0.6 while open | `PadRightStick*` |\\n| L1 / R1 | Previous / next tool | `PadLeftShoulder`, `PadRightShoulder` |\\n| L2 | Precision: cursor ×0.4, stronger magnet, slight dolly-in | `PadLeftTrigger` |\\n| Triangle | Gift (and the pulse-lock beats) | `PadNorth` |\\n| Square | Quick Syringe | `PadWest` |\\n| Circle | Drop what forceps hold; cancel the radial | `PadEast` |\\n| D-pad left/right | Switch site | `PadLeft`, `PadRight` |\\n| D-pad up | Hint | `PadUp` |\\n| R3 | Swap surgeon (Cases 6 to 8) | `PadRightStick` |\\n| Options | Pause | `PadStart` |\\n| L2 + R2 | Paddles, in a Code | triggers |\\n\\nMenus: D-pad or left stick, Cross accepts, Circle goes back. Both sticks and triggers are analog; use dead zones. In a hub session, ignore\\nOptions while Create is held (that chord belongs to the hub).\\n\\n**Mouse and keyboard. The same game and screens, but native.**\\n\\n- **Mouse** moves the cursor absolutely, 1:1, no pointer lock, with the OS cursor hidden over the field. LMB uses the tool. **Hold RMB** for the\\n  radial at the cursor, flick and release. Wheel cycles tools. Keys **1–8** pick tools directly. The tool bar, site tabs and Board cards are clickable, and hovering a valid target highlights it. Shift: precision. Space:\\n  Gift. F: quick Syringe. R: drop. Q/E: sites. H: hint. Tab: swap. Esc: pause. LMB + RMB: paddles.\\n- **Keyboard-only** still works: WASD or arrows move the cursor, Enter uses the tool.\\n- Every menu: hover moves focus, click picks (`createMenu` already does this; do the same in custom panels). Rebinding in Settings → Controls.\\n\\n**Cursor feel on a pad (page-side, tune these).** Speed = `cursorSpeed × lean^2.2`. Within 0.6 m of a valid target for the current tool: velocity ×0.55 and a\\ngentle pull (the magnet). On a scalpel guide while cutting: the across-line part of stick input ×0.4 (rail assist). Suturing on a wound: a soft clamp\\nto ±0.8 m of the wound (sew assist), so you just weave. Mouse gets a light version only, at 0.2 of these strengths.\\n\\n**Prompts** follow the device used last (`input.lastDevice`). Draw your own glyph set in code (SVG/CSS): PlayStation shapes by default for **any** pad; **Settings →\\nControls → Glyphs: PlayStation / Xbox** swaps to A B X Y and LB RB LT RT. Don't use `input.prompt()` text directly, as it reads Xbox for unknown pads. Keyboard\\nshows keycaps; mouse shows mouse icons.\\n\\n**10-foot rules.** Judge every screen at 1920×1080 from a screenshot. Body text at least 32 px; instruments and menu items at least 64 px tall; thick outlines on guides\\nand cursor; focus state huge. One idea per screen. No tables, scrolling lists of small rows, or web-style forms.\\n\\n**In-operation HUD (at most these).** Vitals and ECG, top left, big. Clock and phase name, top centre. Score and chain, top right. Tool bar, bottom centre: 8 icons\\nat 72–96 px, current raised. Odie's line, bottom left: name, big caption, no input needed (`createDialog` with `modal: false` and `auto`). Site tabs at the edges. World labels\\nfor ratings (`ui.label`), huge and brief.\\n\\n**Screens.**\\n\\n- **Boot/Loading:** dark, lighthouse beam, status text; the engine's error text stays visible if startup fails for any other reason.\\n- **No WebGPU:** the engine has no fallback, and this cannot be left to game code. Tested: in Firefox here the bundle crashes at import (`APP_START: … \\\"VERTEX\\\", Js is undefined`), before any of your module runs; WebKit shows the engine's technical `GFX_NO_WEBGPU` text. So a **classic inline script** in the head, right after the hub client, checks `navigator.gpu`. If it is missing, it shows a large plain message saying the game needs a browser with WebGPU, adds \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" on a touch-only device, calls `AIHub.fail(…)` in a session, and hides the engine's text. Do the same if `__engine.errors` later holds `GFX_NO_WEBGPU` (no adapter).\\n- **Title:** 3D lamp-lit OR with the lighthouse beam through rain on the window; the title; Continue / New Shift / The Board / Scrub In / Settings / About. Attract after 10 s idle (§14).\\n- **The Board:** a corkboard wall. One big case card at a time, left/right to browse: patient, one line, rank, tools as icons. Postcards tab.\\n- **Story:** full 3D scene, dialogue box along the bottom third, name plate, gibberish voice; Cross advances; hold Circle to skip the scene; auto mode in Settings.\\n- **Briefing:** patient card and one sentence, tools needed, difficulty, Start.\\n- **Pause:** Resume, Retry phase, Retry case, Handbook, Settings, Controls, **Dev Mode**, Quit to Board.\\n- **Handbook** (from Pause and the Board): big paged cards showing what you can and cannot do. One per instrument (what it does, what it cannot do, its controls in the current glyphs), the Gift, flaps, sites and the Code, and one per strain once met. Built from the data, so it cannot go stale.\\n- **Settings:** pages with few big rows. Audio (Master 70%, **Music 10%**, Effects 100%, Voice 100%). Controls (glyphs, cursor speed, aim assist, rebinding, hold vs toggle for use). Gameplay\\n  (difficulty, Simple Gift, hints, text speed, auto-advance). Display (blood colour: red / teal / off, reduce flashes, text size).\\n- **Scrub In:** four big seat slots; each device claims one by pressing its accept; Start.\\n- **About/Credits:** see §21. Paged cards, one question per card.\\n\\n**Touch-only devices.** Detect with `matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)')` false and no pad seen. No touch controls: put `touch=off` in the `search` you give `createEngine`, always, or the engine shows its touch layer (tested on a phone profile: `touch=off` removes it all). Show exactly **\\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\"** and a large settings button that opens Settings, which accepts taps. Attract mode runs behind it. A pad or\\nkey arriving on such a device clears the message.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Art direction\\n\\n**Base: the engine's native style.** Everything is procedural shapes from the geometry kit, materials and textures as data, puppet bodies from the body grammar. Draw it the way the engine's own clean playground look does: `resolution: 'full'`, `textures: 'smooth'`, and the `aa` filter with `scope: 'all'`, in your looks. Do **not** use the chunky default `pixels` resolution: thin surgical lines must read at 10 feet. `labs/box/looks/` has worked looks to copy from.\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":952}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"99be6d71-7500-434a-af92-f66aba1ae994"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_835","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"PadRightStick is distinct from the directional PadRightStickUp, Down, Left, and Right variants.\n\nThe engine code mapping is correct. PadRightStick refers to the right stick click (R3 button 11), while the directional variants are axes. The radial menu reads those directional codes directly. The paddle bug remains.\n\nKeyboard-only mode cannot press both mouse buttons for paddles, but the rules do not require keyboard-only players to complete them. The mouse-and-keyboard combination handles that input. This resolves another potential issue.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3d2d05e3-902c-45bd-927f-3f47e4fd4fb4-69","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/net/hub.ts","offset":70,"limit":110}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3447,"output_tokens":476,"cache_read_input_tokens":141952,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"62661def-c35e-434a-82f1-5bcd0f2fef8b"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-3d2d05e3-902c-45bd-927f-3f47e4fd4fb4-69","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"70→/** The host's book of what each seat has done, and the ticks waiting to be sent. */\\nexport class HostBook {\\n  readonly latest = new Map<number, Sample>();\\n  readonly applied = new Map<number, Sample>();\\n  readonly gone = new Set<number>();\\n  queue: { tick: number; hands: number[]; hash: string }[] = [];\\n  next = 0;\\n  hash = '';\\n\\n  /** Store a client's latest intent. Older counters are ignored. */\\n80→  hear(from: number, msg: IntentMsg): void {\\n    if (this.gone.has(from)) return;\\n    const prev = this.latest.get(from) ?? { ...ZERO };\\n    this.latest.set(from, {\\n      x: msg.x,\\n      z: msg.z,\\n      tool: msg.tool,\\n      use: msg.use,\\n      gift: Math.max(prev.gift, msg.gift),\\n      drop: Math.max(prev.drop, msg.drop),\\n90→      swap: Math.max(prev.swap, msg.swap),\\n      hint: Math.max(prev.hint, msg.hint),\\n      paddle: Math.max(prev.paddle, msg.paddle),\\n      site: Math.max(prev.site, msg.site),\\n    });\\n  }\\n\\n  /** Hands for the next tick. A seat that left holds still. */\\n  handsFor(seats: number): Hand[] {\\n    const hands: Hand[] = [];\\n100→    for (let seat = 0; seat < seats; seat++) {\\n      const base: Hand = {\\n        x: 0,\\n        z: 0,\\n        tool: 1,\\n        use: false,\\n        drop: false,\\n        gift: false,\\n        paddle: false,\\n        site: -1,\\n110→        swap: false,\\n        hint: false,\\n      };\\n      if (this.gone.has(seat)) {\\n        hands.push(base);\\n        continue;\\n      }\\n      const sample = this.latest.get(seat) ?? { ...ZERO };\\n      const prev = this.applied.get(seat) ?? { ...ZERO };\\n      const gift = take(sample.gift, prev.gift);\\n120→      const drop = take(sample.drop, prev.drop);\\n      const swap = take(sample.swap, prev.swap);\\n      const hint = take(sample.hint, prev.hint);\\n      const paddle = take(sample.paddle, prev.paddle);\\n      const site = take(sample.site, prev.site);\\n      this.applied.set(seat, {\\n        ...sample,\\n        gift: gift.at,\\n        drop: drop.at,\\n        swap: swap.at,\\n130→        hint: hint.at,\\n        paddle: paddle.at,\\n        site: site.at,\\n      });\\n      hands.push({\\n        ...base,\\n        x: sample.x,\\n        z: sample.z,\\n        tool: sample.tool,\\n        use: sample.use > 0,\\n140→        gift: gift.fire,\\n        drop: drop.fire,\\n        swap: swap.fire,\\n        hint: hint.fire,\\n        paddle: paddle.fire,\\n        site: site.fire ? (prev.site + 1) % 4 : -1,\\n        radial: false,\\n      });\\n    }\\n    return hands;\\n150→  }\\n}\\n\\n/** How many buffered ticks a client should play this pass. */\\nexport function drainCount(queued: number): number {\\n  if (queued > 30) return 8;\\n  if (queued > 6) return 2;\\n  return 1;\\n}\\n\\n160→/** A local press, counted so the host still sees it if a packet is lost. */\\nexport function countPress(previous: Sample, hand: Hand, siteChanged: boolean): Sample {\\n  return {\\n    x: hand.x,\\n    z: hand.z,\\n    tool: hand.tool,\\n    use: hand.use ? 1 : 0,\\n    gift: previous.gift + (hand.gift ? 1 : 0),\\n    drop: previous.drop + (hand.drop ? 1 : 0),\\n    swap: previous.swap + (hand.swap ? 1 : 0),\\n170→    hint: previous.hint + (hand.hint ? 1 : 0),\\n    paddle: previous.paddle + (hand.paddle ? 1 : 0),\\n    site: previous.site + (siteChanged ? 1 : 0),\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nexport { ZERO };\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"70→/** The host's book of what each seat has done, and the ticks waiting to be sent. */\\nexport class HostBook {\\n  readonly latest = new Map<number, Sample>();\\n  readonly applied = new Map<number, Sample>();\\n  readonly gone = new Set<number>();\\n  queue: { tick: number; hands: number[]; hash: string }[] = [];\\n  next = 0;\\n  hash = '';\\n\\n  /** Store a client's latest intent. Older counters are ignored. */\\n80→  hear(from: number, msg: IntentMsg): void {\\n    if (this.gone.has(from)) return;\\n    const prev = this.latest.get(from) ?? { ...ZERO };\\n    this.latest.set(from, {\\n      x: msg.x,\\n      z: msg.z,\\n      tool: msg.tool,\\n      use: msg.use,\\n      gift: Math.max(prev.gift, msg.gift),\\n      drop: Math.max(prev.drop, msg.drop),\\n90→      swap: Math.max(prev.swap, msg.swap),\\n      hint: Math.max(prev.hint, msg.hint),\\n      paddle: Math.max(prev.paddle, msg.paddle),\\n      site: Math.max(prev.site, msg.site),\\n    });\\n  }\\n\\n  /** Hands for the next tick. A seat that left holds still. */\\n  handsFor(seats: number): Hand[] {\\n    const hands: Hand[] = [];\\n100→    for (let seat = 0; seat < seats; seat++) {\\n      const base: Hand = {\\n        x: 0,\\n        z: 0,\\n        tool: 1,\\n        use: false,\\n        drop: false,\\n        gift: false,\\n        paddle: false,\\n        site: -1,\\n110→        swap: false,\\n        hint: false,\\n      };\\n      if (this.gone.has(seat)) {\\n        hands.push(base);\\n        continue;\\n      }\\n      const sample = this.latest.get(seat) ?? { ...ZERO };\\n      const prev = this.applied.get(seat) ?? { ...ZERO };\\n      const gift = take(sample.gift, prev.gift);\\n120→      const drop = take(sample.drop, prev.drop);\\n      const swap = take(sample.swap, prev.swap);\\n      const hint = take(sample.hint, prev.hint);\\n      const paddle = take(sample.paddle, prev.paddle);\\n      const site = take(sample.site, prev.site);\\n      this.applied.set(seat, {\\n        ...sample,\\n        gift: gift.at,\\n        drop: drop.at,\\n        swap: swap.at,\\n130→        hint: hint.at,\\n        paddle: paddle.at,\\n        site: site.at,\\n      });\\n      hands.push({\\n        ...base,\\n        x: sample.x,\\n        z: sample.z,\\n        tool: sample.tool,\\n        use: sample.use > 0,\\n140→        gift: gift.fire,\\n        drop: drop.fire,\\n        swap: swap.fire,\\n        hint: hint.fire,\\n        paddle: paddle.fire,\\n        site: site.fire ? (prev.site + 1) % 4 : -1,\\n        radial: false,\\n      });\\n    }\\n    return hands;\\n150→  }\\n}\\n\\n/** How many buffered ticks a client should play this pass. */\\nexport function drainCount(queued: number): number {\\n  if (queued > 30) return 8;\\n  if (queued > 6) return 2;\\n  return 1;\\n}\\n\\n160→/** A local press, counted so the host still sees it if a packet is lost. */\\nexport function countPress(previous: Sample, hand: Hand, siteChanged: boolean): Sample {\\n  return {\\n    x: hand.x,\\n    z: hand.z,\\n    tool: hand.tool,\\n    use: hand.use ? 1 : 0,\\n    gift: previous.gift + (hand.gift ? 1 : 0),\\n    drop: previous.drop + (hand.drop ? 1 : 0),\\n    swap: previous.swap + (hand.swap ? 1 : 0),\\n170→    hint: previous.hint + (hand.hint ? 1 : 0),\\n    paddle: previous.paddle + (hand.paddle ? 1 : 0),\\n    site: previous.site + (siteChanged ? 1 : 0),\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nexport { ZERO };\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/net/hub.ts\",\"offset\":70,\"limit\":110,\"raw_output\":\"/** The host's book of what each seat has done, and the ticks waiting to be sent. */\\nexport class HostBook {\\n  readonly latest = new Map<number, Sample>();\\n  readonly applied = new Map<number, Sample>();\\n  readonly gone = new Set<number>();\\n  queue: { tick: number; hands: number[]; hash: string }[] = [];\\n  next = 0;\\n  hash = '';\\n\\n  /** Store a client's latest intent. Older counters are ignored. */\\n  hear(from: number, msg: IntentMsg): void {\\n    if (this.gone.has(from)) return;\\n    const prev = this.latest.get(from) ?? { ...ZERO };\\n    this.latest.set(from, {\\n      x: msg.x,\\n      z: msg.z,\\n      tool: msg.tool,\\n      use: msg.use,\\n      gift: Math.max