{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_843","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Checking hashOp to see if adding a field to Seat changes the hash.\n\nprevUse is excluded from the hash. prevPaddle should be too. The network hub and simulation both edge-detect paddle presses. A single press fires once. A hold triggers both layers.\n\nThe local couch path sends a level paddle every simulation step. This causes the hub counter to increment each frame while the button is held. The fix is to add prevPaddle tracking in applyHands and only trigger pressPaddle when the state actually changes.\n\nWhen hands is null, the menu is up and buttons do not stick. prevPaddle should be cleared to false so a held paddle re-edges after the menu closes.\n\nMissing hands for a seat should treat the paddle as up, so prevPaddle is not stuck. The network hub already sends one-tick pulses, which the simulation edge correctly handles.\n\nBot paddle presses in the green band trigger once and clear. Later ticks are ignored while the code is active. Off-band presses do not count as misses. The miss counter counts off-band steps, not edges. I will trace createBare and play() to verify the initial tick behavior.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-35fd1b66-2f69-4e4a-a09d-d4f89e51f2d0-109","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/step.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-35fd1b66-2f69-4e4a-a09d-d4f89e51f2d0-110","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/world.ts","offset":500,"limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-35fd1b66-2f69-4e4a-a09d-d4f89e51f2d0-111","name":"read_file","input":{"tar