{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_845","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The existing miss test will break.\n\nTracing the first tick sequence. Vitals start at zero and drain to negative values, triggering flatline before the tick increments.\n\nThe test increments misses on every off-band tick. It stops after two misses. Only one try is spent. The status remains playing. The test fails.\n\nThe two-miss test will be fixed by adding a release between presses. This ensures it still checks that two separate misses lose, rather than accidentally relying on the bug where level equals many tries.\n\nA new test will hold the paddle across several off-band steps and assert the operation remains playing with tries left.\n\nThe two-miss test will alternate paddle presses and releases across off-band ticks. It asserts the operation loses after two spent tries. The codeBand check happens before each step, so it correctly evaluates the upcoming tick.\n\nThe success test will press the paddle on every tick that matches the code band. A release step that lands inside the band is harmless because it does not trigger a hit.\n\nThe success test holds the paddle across the entire green window. Edge detection fires only on the first true step, clearing the code. Later true steps are ignored. The paddle state resets to false during off-band ticks before the window opens, so the edge at tick 28 is clean.\n\nThe new test holds the paddle across several off-band steps. It asserts the operation remains playing and that tries are consumed.\n\nThe new test can be simplified. Because the first tick after flatline is off-band, holding the paddle for six consecutive steps is enough to consume one try and keep the operation playing.\n\nThe first tick after flatline is off-band, so holding the paddle for six steps consumes one try and leaves the operation playing. The code timer allows eight seconds of field time, so the operation should not fail within six steps.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-429a174e-8bc3-48d4-a12f-7acbfb18cc3a-115","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/world.ts","offset":400,"limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-429a174e-8bc3-48d4-a12f-7acbfb18cc3a-116","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"makeSeat|Seat = \\{|prevUse: false","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game","glob":"*.ts"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3134,"output_tokens":1686,"cache_read_input_tokens":156544,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"b14f0893-3a87-4a91-a932-da8b693c88bd"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-429a174e-8bc3-48d4-a12f-7acbfb18cc3a-115","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"400→    mercyBindSpawned: false,\\n    lastBind: 0,\\n    bestChain: 1,\\n    score: 0,\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n/** A tiny operation for a unit test or a dev spawn. One site, one patient, a long clock. */\\nexport function createBare(\\n  opts: { code?: boolean; vitals?: number; difficulty?: Difficulty; seats?: number } = {},\\n410→): Op {\\n  const def: CaseDef = {\\n    id: 'case:bare',\\n    title: 'Bare',\\n    surgeon: 'Wren',\\n    seconds: 600,\\n    gift: 'stillpoint',\\n    charges: 2,\\n    colleague: false,\\n    swap: false,\\n420→    roll: false,\\n    code: opts.code ?? true,\\n    rule: 'fixture',\\n    patients: [\\n      {\\n        name: 'Fixture',\\n        age: 40,\\n        line: 'A test patient.',\\n        vitals: opts.vitals ?? 80,\\n        postcards: { S: 'Fine.', A: 'Fine.', B: 'Fine.', C: 'Fine.' },\\n430→      },\\n    ],\\n    sites: [{ id: 'site', name: 'Field' }],\\n    phases: [{ id: 'work', hint: 'Work.', until: 'clear', spawn: [], onEnter: '', teach: '' }],\\n    storyBefore: '',\\n    storyAfter: '',\\n    par: 1000,\\n  };\\n  return createFromDef(def, { difficulty: opts.difficulty ?? 'resident', seats: opts.seats ?? 1, seed: 1 });\\n}\\n440→\\n/** Spawn a phase's targets. Exported for the phase runner. */\\nexport function spawnPhase(op: Op, phase: PhaseDef, index: number): void {\\n  const extra = Math.max(0, op.seats.length - 1);\\n  const ordinary = phase.spawn.filter((spawn) => !UNIQUE_KIND.has(spawn.kind));\\n  for (const spawn of phase.spawn) placeSpawn(op, spawn, index);\\n  const duplicates = Math.round(ordinary.length * 0.25 * extra);\\n  for (let n = 0; n < duplicates; n++) {\\n    const spawn = ordinary[n % ordinary.length];\\n    const copy = 1 + Math.floor(n / ordinary.length);\",\"content_concise\":\"400→    mercyBindSpawned: false,\\n    lastBind: 0,\\n    bestChain: 1,\\n    score: 0,\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n/** A tiny operation for a unit test or a dev spawn. One site, one patient, a long clock. */\\nexport function createBare(\\n  opts: { code?: boolean; vitals?: number; difficulty?: Difficulty; seats?: number } = {},\\n410→): Op {\\n  const def: CaseDef = {\\n    id: 'case:bare',\\n    title: 'Bare',\\n    surgeon: 'Wren',\\n    seconds: 600,\\n    gift: 'stillpoint',\\n    charges: 2,\\n    colleague: false,\\n    swap: false,\\n420→    roll: false,\\n    code: opts.code ?? true,\\n    rule: 'fixture',\\n    patients: [\\n      {\\n        name: 'Fixture',\\n        age: 40,\\n        line: 'A test patient.',\\n        vitals: opts.vitals ?? 80,\\n        postcards: { S: 'Fine.', A: 'Fine.', B: 'Fine.', C: 'Fine.' },\\n430→      },\\n    ],\\n    sites: [{ id: 'site', name: 'Field' }],\\n    phases: [{ id: 'work', hint: 'Work.', until: 'clear', spawn: [], onEnter: '', teach: '' }],\\n    storyBefore: '',\\n    storyAfter: '',\\n    par: 1000,\\n  };\\n  return createFromDef(def, { difficulty: opts.difficulty ?? 'resident', seats: opts.seats ?? 1, seed: 1 });\\n}\\n440→\\n/** Spawn a phase's targets. Exported for the phase runner. */\\nexport function spawnPhase(op: Op, phase: PhaseDef, index: number): void {\\n  const extra = Math.max(0, op.seats.length - 1);\\n  const ordinary = phase.spawn.filter((spawn) => !UNIQUE_KIND.has(spawn.kind));\\n  for (const spawn of phase.spawn) placeSpawn(op, spawn, index);\\n  const duplicates = Math.round(ordinary.length * 0.25 * extra);\\n  for (let n = 0; n < duplicates; n++) {\\n    const spawn = ordinary[n % ordinary.length];\\n    const copy = 1 + Math.floor(n / ordinary.length);\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/world.ts\",\"offset\":400,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"    mercyBindSpawned: false,\\n    lastBind: 0,\\n    bestChain: 1,\\n    score: 0,\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n/** A tiny operation for a unit test or a dev spawn. One site, one patient, a long clock. */\\nexport function createBare(\\n  opts: { code?: boolean; vitals?: number; difficulty?: Difficulty; seats?: number } = {},\\n): Op {\\n  const def: CaseDef = {\\n    id: 'case:bare',\\n    title: 'Bare',\\n    surgeon: 'Wren',\\n    seconds: 600,\\n    gift: 'stillpoint',\\n    charges: 2,\\n    colleague: false,\\n    swap: false,\\n    roll: false,\\n    code: opts.code ?? true,\\n    rule: 'fixture',\\n    patients: [\\n      {\\n        name: 'Fixture',\\n        age: 40,\\n        line: 'A test patient.',\\n        vitals: opts.vitals ?? 80,\\n        postcards: { S: 'Fine.', A: 'Fine.', B: 'Fine.', C: 'Fine.' },\\n      },\\n    ],\\n    sites: [{ id: 'site', name: 'Field' }],\\n    phases: [{ id: 'work', hint: 'Work.', until: 'clear', spawn: [], onEnter: '', teach: '' }],\\n    storyBefore: '',\\n    storyAfter: '',\\n    par: 1000,\\n  };\\n  return createFromDef(def, { difficulty: opts.difficulty ?? 'resident', seats: opts.seats ?? 1, seed: 1 });\\n}\\n\\n/** Spawn a phase's targets. Exported for the phase runner. */\\nexport function spawnPhase(op: Op, phase: PhaseDef, index: number): void {\\n  const extra = Math.max(0, op.seats.length - 1);\\n  const ordinary = phase.spawn.filter((spawn) => !UNIQUE_KIND.has(spawn.kind));\\n  for (const spawn of phase.spawn) placeSpawn(op, spawn, index);\\n  const duplicates = Math.round(ordinary.length * 0.25 * extra);\\n  for (let n = 0; n < duplicates; n++) {\\n    const spawn = ordinary[n % ordinary.length];\\n    const copy = 1 + Math.floor(n / ordinary.length);\\n\",\"total_lines\":564}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-429a174e-8bc3-48d4-a12f-7acbfb18cc3a-116","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,6