);\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-58741018-7107-4a1c-80e2-cff04e0a0e80-118","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"185→/** Vitals hit zero. */\\nfunction flatline(op: Op, patientId: number): void {\\n  const patient = op.patients[patientId];\\n  patient.vitals = 0;\\n  if (op.code) return;\\n190→  if (!op.codeAllowed || (patient.coded && op.id !== 'case:mercy')) {\\n    patient.alive = false;\\n    failOp(op, `${patient.name} is gone.`);\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  patient.coded = op.id !== 'case:mercy';\\n  op.code = { left: 8 * FIELD_SECOND, tries: 2, patient: patientId, free: op.id === 'case:mercy', shocks: 0 };\\n  op.events.push({ type: 'code', text: 'Paddles.' });\\n}\\n\\n200→/** Gifts, the Code timer, the clock, and the phase. */\\nexport function stepBody(op: Op, ft: number): void {\\n  tickLocks(op);\\n  for (const seat of op.seats) if (seat.giftLeft > 0 && seat.lock < 0) seat.giftLeft -= 1;\\n  if (op.code) {\\n    op.code.left -= ft;\\n    if (op.code.left <= 0) {\\n      op.code = null;\\n      failOp(op, 'The line stays flat.');\\n    }\\n210→  }\\n  if (!op.attract && !op.holdClock) op.clock -= ft / Math.max(0.4, op.balance.clock);\\n  if (op.clock <= 0 && op.status === 'playing') {\\n    op.clock = 0;\\n    failOp(op, 'Time.');\\n  }\\n  stepColleague(op);\\n  advance(op);\\n}\\n\\n220→/** The AI colleague drains and holds flaps. It never takes the lead's hands. */\\nfunction stepColleague(op: Op): void {\\n  op.helper = '';\\n  if (!op.colleague || op.seats.length > 1 || op.status !== 'playing') return;\\n  const pool = op.targets.find((target) => target.kind === 'pool' && !target.done && target.volume > 0);\",\"content_concise\":\"185→/** Vitals hit zero. */\\nfunction flatline(op: Op, patientId: number): void {\\n  const patient = op.patients[patientId];\\n  patient.vitals = 0;\\n  if (op.code) return;\\n190→  if (!op.codeAllowed || (patient.coded && op.id !== 'case:mercy')) {\\n    patient.alive = false;\\n    failOp(op, `${patient.name} is gone.`);\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  patient.coded = op.id !== 'case:mercy';\\n  op.code = { left: 8 * FIELD_SECOND, tries: 2, patient: patientId, free: op.id === 'case:mercy', shocks: 0 };\\n  op.events.push({ type: 'code', text: 'Paddles.' });\\n}\\n\\n200→/** Gifts, the Code timer, the clock, and the phase. */\\nexport function stepBody(op: Op, ft: number): void {\\n  tickLocks(op);\\n  for (const seat of op.seats) if (seat.giftLeft > 0 && seat.lock < 0) seat.giftLeft -= 1;\\n  if (op.code) {\\n    op.code.left -= ft;\\n    if (op.code.left <= 0) {\\n      op.code = null;\\n      failOp(op, 'The line stays flat.');\\n    }\\n210→  }\\n  if (!op.attract && !op.holdClock) op.clock -= ft / Math.max(0.4, op.balance.clock);\\n  if (op.clock <= 0 && op.status === 'playing') {\\n    op.clock = 0;\\n    failOp(op, 'Time.');\\n  }\\n  stepColleague(op);\\n  advance(op);\\n}\\n\\n220→/** The AI colleague drains and holds flaps. It never takes the lead's hands. */\\nfunction stepColleague(op: Op): void {\\n  op.helper = '';\\n  if (!op.colleague || op.seats.length > 1 || op.status !== 'playing') return;\\n  const pool = op.targets.find((target) => target.kind === 'pool' && !target.done && target.volume > 0);\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/body.ts\",\"offset\":185,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"/** Vitals hit zero. */\\nfunction flatline(op: Op, patientId: number): void {\\n  const patient = op.patients[patientId];\\n  patient.vitals = 0;\\n  if (op.code) return;\\n  if (!op.codeAllowed || (patient.coded && op.id !== 'case:mercy')) {\\n    patient.alive = false;\\n    failOp(op, `${patient.name} is gone.`);\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  patient.coded = op.id !== 'case:mercy';\\n  op.code = { left: 8 * FIELD_SECOND, tries: 2, patient: patientId, free: op.id === 'case:mercy', shocks: 0 };\\n  op.events.push({ type: 'code', text: 'Paddles.' });\\n}\\n\\n/** Gifts, the Code timer, the clock, and the phase. */\\nexport function stepBody(op: Op, ft: number): void {\\n  tickLocks(op);\\n  for (const seat of op.seats) if (seat.giftLeft > 0 && seat.lock < 0) seat.giftLeft -= 1;\\n  if (op.code) {\\n    op.code.left -= ft;\\n    if (op.code.left <= 0) {\\n      op.code = null;\\n      failOp(op, 'The line stays flat.');\\n    }\\n  }\\n  if (!op.attract && !op.holdClock) op.clock -= ft / Math.max(0.4, op.balance.clock);\\n  if (op.clock <= 0 && op.status === 'playing') {\\n    op.clock = 0;\\n    failOp(op, 'Time.');\\n  }\\n  stepColleague(op);\\n  advance(op);\\n}\\n\\n/** The AI colleague drains and holds flaps. It never takes the lead's hands. */\\nfunction stepColleague(op: Op): void {\\n  op.helper = '';\\n  if (!op.colleague || op.seats.length > 1 || op.status !== 'playing') return;\\n  const pool = op.targets.find((target) => target.kind === 'pool' && !target.done && target.volume > 0);\\n\",\"total_lines\":295}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"cdec7786-3808-4bba-8d7d-3fe1572bee63"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_847","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Mercy free might be handled elsewhere.\n\nI'll only edge-detect. I need to check body.ts length and clear prevPaddle when hands is null. Multiple seats holding paddles could double-apply tries in one step, but the skeptic meant one seat with both triggers.\n\nI'll fix the two-miss test to release the paddle between shots so it still validates two distinct misses. The test will be written carefully without relying on level step counting.\n\nThe test creates a held-paddle scenario to verify one try is spent, then starts a second scenario to validate the second miss.\n\nThe test now uses a 200-step loop to press and release the paddle twice, confirming two distinct misses. The existing success path will be preserved alongside a new hold assertion.\n\nThe success path keeps the level hold. The miss path will press and release the paddle to create two distinct edges. A second press after release off-band will spend the second try. The release step itself may fall inside the band, but the code checks codeBand before pressing.\n\nThe release step advances the tick, so the loop can press again off-band for a second miss. The test starts by flatlining vitals and stepping to satisfy the \"no starting past the thing under test\" rule.\n\nI'll use the real flatline path to start the Code rather than setting op.code directly. I need to check if any tests expect seat keys, since prevPaddle could break full seat object comparisons. The codec doesn't pack this field. I'll also verify line counts in body.ts, types.ts, and world.ts before adding lines.\n\nworld.ts is 564 lines, so adding one line is safe. I will not edge paddles in the scene; the simulation alone will handle the edge detection to avoid double-counting tries.\n\nI will not reset prevPaddle when hands is null. The latch should stay active across pauses so a hold-through-pause still counts as one shock and does not create a second try.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4dd71795-c7db-42d2-b551-8685b79de6c0-119","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"paddle:","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game","glob":"*.ts"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1532,"output_tokens":1607,"cache_read_input_tokens":162048,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"838b41f9-54c9-4ecb-bc4e-0d29fe00f869"}
