{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_872","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The launch completed successfully.\n\nVerifying launch and sim logs. Checking the paddle fix in body.ts:132 and confirming the About screen matches. Preparing exit-interview.json.\n\nThe HTML rebuild included the About change and a strengthened paddle test. The prior 94-pass run already verified the paddle fix, so this latest rejection is the same unresolved bug.\n\nThe prior 94-pass run already included the paddle fix. The skeptic now cites body.ts:132 as tickLocks, suggesting stale line numbers or an incorrect fix. Re-reading the bug report to verify.\n\nThe paddle hold bug is a timing issue. When a hold starts on the step that creates code, the edge is consumed before the code exists, so no tries are spent. The fix using prevPaddle only works if the hold begins after the code exists.\n\nThe test covers both hold scenarios: one try spent after code exists, and no tries spent from the flatline step. Both should pass. The launch and vitest results show SIM:0. I need to read the actual code and output to confirm, since the summary may be stale. I am also clarifying whether \"both paddles\" means both seats or both paddles on one controller.\n\nI am now reading the actual source files and logs to verify the fix. I will check exit-interview.json and confirm it matches requirements. If the code is correct and tests pass, I will mark the remaining todos complete.\n\nThe prevPaddle fix correctly prevents a continuous hold from spending tries when code first appears. The hold that started before the code exists does not count as a try at all. This may conflict with the skeptic's requirement that one hold must equal one try.\n\nThe test assertion is satisfied in both hold scenarios. The old bug lost on tick 3, but the new code prevents that. SIM:0 confirms the test passed.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The launch finished cleanly. I'll read the sim and launch logs, then check that the paddle edge and the About text are what the shipped page actually runs."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3052b92b-2149-49bd-81c1-b59ac2d55baf-3","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"spends one Code try|The line stays flat|prevPaddle|FAIL|passed|failed","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/sim.log"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3052b92b-2149-49bd-81c1-b59ac2d55baf-4","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"ok|EXIT|screen|error|fail","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/launch.log"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3052b92b-2149-49bd-81c1-b59ac2d55baf-5","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"prevPaddle|pressPaddle|function applyHands|codeBand","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/body.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3052b92b-2149-49bd-81c1-b59ac2d55baf-6","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"data-about=\\\"usage\\\"|added on import","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/ui/shell.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3052b92b-2149-49bd-81c1-b59ac2d55baf-7","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"\"usage\"|testingFeedback|Twenty issues","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/exit-interview.json"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4520,"output_tokens":1623,"cache_read_input_tokens":32896,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"b1b2c77f-57ee-48ef-ba83-c99725d6d6dd"}
