tuck or guess wrong?\\n- What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?\\n- What was the hardest part about using the engine?\\n- What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)\\n- If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?\\n\\nPrompt Feedback\\n\\n- What did you like most about this prompt?\\n- What was confusing?\\n150→- What was the hardest thing to do?\\n- What would you change in this prompt?\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/TASK.md\",\"offset\":90,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"No TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features. The demo is complete.\\n\\n## Source Information\\nCRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen. Write \\\"unknown\\\" for anything you can't confirm.\\n- Date: 2026-11-04 22:47:31\\n- Source: the work it's based on\\n- Plan: the file name of the plan you were given to build from, or none\\n- Genre and Perspective: genre and camera perspective used\\n- Tech: stack, libraries/engines, with versions if applicable\\n- Art Direction: style used\\n- Animation: system used\\n- Audio: music, sound effects and voice used\\n- Online: network features used, or none\\n- Testing: testing parameters allowed\\n- Research: research done, or none\\n- Environment: Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\n- Model: xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\n- Usage: write \\\"added on import\\\". You can't see your own cost, so don't estimate it: the runner records the real cost, tokens and time, and the agent that imports the game into AI Hub puts them on your About/Credits screen.\\n\\nExit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\\\"unknown\\\" for anything you can't confirm). Tools read it (the game's run record and the AI Hub catalogue), so write plain text, and check that the file parses as JSON.\\n{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\\"date\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"plan\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"genre\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"tech\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"animation\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"audio\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"online\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"testing\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"research\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"environment\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"model\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"},\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\\"your answer to each Testing Feedback question, in order\\\"],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\\"your answer to each Engine Feedback question, in order\\\"],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\\"your answer to each Prompt Feedback question, in order\\\"],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"the game's title, as on its title screen\\\",\\n    \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"a few words to go under the title\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"one or two sentences for the catalogue\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game, Tech demo or Tool\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"one of Action, Adventure, Fighting, Flight, Horror, Kids & Learning, Life Sim, Platformer, Puzzle, Racing, RPG, Shooter, Simulation, Sports, Stealth, Strategy\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"the work it's based on, e.g. Moby-Dick\\\",\\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"its franchise, e.g. Star Fox, or empty\\\",\\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"how many can play: 1, 1–2 or 1–4\\\",\\n    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"the controls, in one line\\\",\\n    \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"3 to 6 lowercase tags, e.g. 2d, 3d, arcade, story, co-op, versus, first-person, third-person, top-down, side-scrolling, pixel art, low-poly, retro, sci-fi, fantasy, comedy, vehicles, boss fights, exploration\\\"]\\n  }\\n}\\nThe catalogue's model, effort, CLI, date and usage come from the run's record after you finish, so they aren't asked here.\\n\\nTesting Feedback\\n\\n- How many issues did testing catch?\\n- How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?\\n- What was the most helpful test you ran?\\n- What was the least helpful test you ran?\\n\\nEngine Feedback\\n\\n- What did you like most about the engine?\\n- Did you get stuck or guess wrong?\\n- What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?\\n- What was the hardest part about using the engine?\\n- What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)\\n- If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?\\n\\nPrompt Feedback\\n\\n- What did you like most about this prompt?\\n- What was confusing?\\n- What was the hardest thing to do?\\n- What would you change in this prompt?\\n\",\"total_lines\":151}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-1268965f-205b-4707-ba45-9839db778887-16","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 22:47:31\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Surgical simulation\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Close overhead, a fixed camera on the operating field\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"my-3dge at 2dbd829, three.js 0.182.0 on WebGPU, Rapier 0.21.0, TypeScript 5.9, Vite 7.3, AI Hub session client 1.4.0\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"The engine’s native PBR look at full resolution: wet stylised tissue, teal drapes, brass and amber lamps\\\",\\n10→    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"The engine’s animator for the surgeon. The sheet, breath, heartbeat and gloves are rewritten every frame\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Songs and effects written as chip voices. Voices are syllable gibberish. Music starts at 10%\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub shared-world sessions only. Couch co-op for up to four devices on one screen. No other network\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Headless sim tests, one verify command, Chromium from file://, Firefox and WebKit for the WebGPU message. No physical controller, touch screen, second person, or iPhone\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"The plan’s own research notes. No further research\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n20→    \\\"Twenty issues were caught and written in labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md.\\\",\\n    \\\"Eleven were game-breaking: a restore stepped the wrong body, the gala flap never finished, Reverie left the surface early, Solace children stacked, the syringe bound the wrong target, stitches landed off the wound, co-op copies shared one point, an outline width the engine rejects, a sound id the engine already owns, a look and a song that used fields the engine does not have, and a hub round that never readied while the GPU was still warming up.\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful tests were the bot, which had to win every required case and seed, and the content walk that plays the whole shift to the credits.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful was the voice-key equality check. It only shows that one line keeps the same syllable list. The starter gem tests had to stay green and do not cover an operation.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"Headless play, capture, settings that restart a scene in place, and the one-file build. A game can be proven without a screen.\\\",\\n    \\\"Yes. The live operation sat in a module, and capture restored only the world, so the next step used the body from before the rewind until the chart snapshot was adopted. A view setting cannot be read from the sim, so the radial-slow slider cannot change the hashed clock.\\\",\\n    \\\"The operation itself: tools, vitals, the five strains, ratings, the bot, the lockstep, and the campaign screens. The engine does not know what a surgery is.\\\",\\n    \\\"There is no scene hook after a restore, and no public way to rewrite a geometry the page kept. Both showed up as a mismatched hash and a mesh that could not be repainted.\\\",\\n30→    \\\"Nothing. The engine stayed read-only. Local engine patches is empty.\\\",\\n    \\\"A callback on the scene after restore, or a supported way to update a kept mesh, so a living sheet and a rewind do not depend on a private object.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The plan named the rules, the files, the hub boot order, and the traps on this machine. The operation could be built from that.\\\",\\n    \\\"The sheet was specified very dense, while the same plan warned that four browser copies are killed when memory runs out. The source’s subtitle is banned as a title and allowed as an ordinary line, which is easy to mix up.\\\",\\n    \\\"Covering eight operations, the story, couch play, and the four-copy hub check on a machine that ends the largest browser.\\\",\\n    \\\"Split the four-copy hub check from the campaign-length walk, and name a sheet size that fits that check.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n40→    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Trauma Compass\\\",\\n    \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"Keep the line, then close.\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"A lamp-lit night at Harbor Light General. Eight operations, four surgeons at one table, and a patient who has to last until the last stitch.\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Simulation\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\\\",\\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"Trauma Center\\\",\\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"1–4\\\",\\n    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"Stick or mouse aims · R2 or click uses the tool · right stick or 1-8 picks a tool\\\",\\n    \\\"tags\\\": [\\n50→      \\\"3d\\\",\\n      \\\"co-op\\\",\\n      \\\"story\\\",\\n      \\\"boss fights\\\",\\n      \\\"comedy\\\"\\n    ]\\n  }\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 22:47:31\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Surgical simulation\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Close overhead, a fixed camera on the operating field\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"my-3dge at 2dbd829, three.js 0.182.0 on WebGPU, Rapier 0.21.0, TypeScript 5.9, Vite 7.3, AI Hub session client 1.4.0\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"The engine’s native PBR look at full resolution: wet stylised tissue, teal drapes, brass and amber lamps\\\",\\n10→    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"The engine’s animator for the surgeon. The sheet, breath, heartbeat and gloves are rewritten every frame\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Songs and effects written as chip voices. Voices are syllable gibberish. Music starts at 10%\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub shared-world sessions only. Couch co-op for up to four devices on one screen. No other network\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Headless sim tests, one verify command, Chromium from file://, Firefox and WebKit for the WebGPU message. No physical controller, touch screen, second person, or iPhone\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"The plan’s own research notes. No further research\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n20→    \\\"Twenty issues were caught and written in labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md.\\\",\\n    \\\"Eleven were game-breaking: a restore stepped the wrong body, the gala flap never finished, Reverie left the surface early, Solace children stacked, the syringe bound the wrong target, stitches landed off the wound, co-op copies shared one point, an outline width the engine rejects, a sound id the engine already owns, a look and a song that used fields the engine does not have, and a hub round that never readied while the GPU was still warming up.\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful tests were the bot, which had to win every required case and seed, and the content walk that plays the whole shift to the credits.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful was the voice-key equality check. It only shows that one line keeps the same syllable list. The starter gem tests had to stay green and do not cover an operation.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"Headless play, capture, settings that restart a scene in place, and the one-file build. A game can be proven without a screen.\\\",\\n    \\\"Yes. The live operation sat in a module, and capture restored only the world, so the next step used the body from before the rewind until the chart snapshot was adopted. A view setting cannot be read from the sim, so the radial-slow slider cannot change the hashed clock.\\\",\\n    \\\"The operation itself: tools, vitals, the five strains, ratings, the bot, the lockstep, and the campaign screens. The engine does not know what a surgery is.\\\",\\n    \\\"There is no scene hook after a restore, and no public way to rewrite a geometry the page kept. Both showed up as a mismatched hash and a mesh that could not be repainted.\\\",\\n30→    \\\"Nothing. The engine stayed read-only. Local engine patches is empty.\\\",\\n    \\\"A callback on the scene after restore, or a supported way to update a kept mesh, so a living sheet and a rewind do not depend on a private object.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The plan named the rules, the files, the hub boot order, and the traps on this machine. The operation could be built from that.\\\",\\n    \\\"The sheet was specified very dense, while the same plan warned that four browser copies are killed when memory runs out. The source’s subtitle is banned as a title and allowed as an ordinary line, which is easy to mix up.\\\",\\n    \\\"Covering eight operations, the story, couch play, and the four-copy hub check on a machine that ends the largest browser.\\\",\\n    \\\"Split the four-copy hub check from the campaign-length walk, and name a sheet size that fits that check.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n40→    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Trauma Compass\\\",\\n    \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"Keep the line, then close.\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"A lamp-lit night at Harbor Light General. Eight operations, four surgeons at one table, and a patient who has to last until the last stitch.\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Simulation\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\\\",\\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"Trauma Center\\\",\\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"1–4\\\",\\n    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"Stick or mouse aims · R2 or click uses the tool · right stick or 1-8 picks a tool\\\",\\n    \\\"tags\\\": [\\n50→      \\\"3d\\\",\\n      \\\"co-op\\\",\\n      \\\"story\\\",\\n      \\\"boss fights\\\",\\n      \\\"comedy\\\"\\n    ]\\n  }\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/exit-interview.json\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 22:47:31\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Surgical simulation\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Close overhead, a fixed camera on the operating field\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"my-3dge at 2dbd829, three.js 0.182.0 on WebGPU, Rapier 0.21.0, TypeScript 5.9, Vite 7.3, AI Hub session client 1.4.0\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"The engine’s native PBR look at full resolution: wet stylised tissue, teal drapes, brass and amber lamps\\\",\\n    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"The engine’s animator for the surgeon. The sheet, breath, heartbeat and gloves are rewritten every frame\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Songs and effects written as chip voices. Voices are syllable gibberish. Music starts at 10%\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub shared-world sessions only. Couch co-op for up to four devices on one screen. No other network\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Headless sim tests, one verify command, Chromium from file://, Firefox and WebKit for the WebGPU message. No physical controller, touch screen, second person, or iPhone\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"The plan’s own research notes. No further research\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"Twenty issues were caught and written in labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md.\\\",\\n    \\\"Eleven were game-breaking: a restore stepped the wrong body, the gala flap never finished, Reverie left the surface early, Solace children stacked, the syringe bound the wrong target, stitches landed off the wound, co-op copies shared one point, an outline width the engine rejects, a sound id the engine already owns, a look and a song that used fields the engine does not have, and a hub round that never readied while the GPU was still warming up.\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful tests were the bot, which had to win every required case and seed, and the content walk that plays the whole shift to the credits.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful was the voice-key equality check. It only shows that one line keeps the same syllable list. The starter gem tests had to stay green and do not cover an operation.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"Headless play, capture, settings that restart a scene in place, and the one-file build. A game can be proven without a screen.\\\",\\n    \\\"Yes. The live operation sat in a module, and capture restored only the world, so the next step used the body from before the rewind until the chart snapshot was adopted. A view setting cannot be read from the sim, so the radial-slow slider cannot change the hashed clock.\\\",\\n    \\\"The operation itself: tools, vitals, the five strains, ratings, the bot, the lockstep, and the campaign screens. The engine does not know what a surgery is.\\\",\\n    \\\"There is no scene hook after a restore, and no public way to rewrite a geometry the page kept. Both showed up as a mismatched hash and a mesh that could not be repainted.\\\",\\n    \\\"Nothing. The engine stayed read-only. Local engine patches is empty.\\\",\\n    \\\"A callback on the scene after restore, or a supported way to update a kept mesh, so a living sheet and a rewind do not depend on a private object.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The plan named the rules, the files, the hub boot order, and the traps on this machine. The operation could be built from that.\\\",\\n    \\\"The sheet was specified very dense, while the same plan warned that four browser copies are killed when memory runs out. The source’s subtitle is banned as a title and allowed as an ordinary line, which is easy to mix up.\\\",\\n    \\\"Covering eight operations, the story, couch play, and the four-copy hub check on a machine that ends the largest browser.\\\",\\n    \\\"Split the four-copy hub check from the campaign-length walk, and name a sheet size that fits that check.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Trauma Compass\\\",\\n    \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"Keep the line, then close.\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"A lamp-lit night at Harbor Light General. Eight operations, four surgeons at one table, and a patient who has to last until the last stitch.\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Simulation\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\\\",\\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"Trauma Center\\\",\\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"1–4\\\",\\n    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"Stick or mouse aims · R2 or click uses the tool · right stick or 1-8 picks a tool\\\",\\n    \\\"tags\\\": [\\n      \\\"3d\\\",\\n      \\\"co-op\\\",\\n      \\\"story\\\",\\n      \\\"boss fights\\\",\\n      \\\"comedy\\\"\\n    ]\\n  }\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":57}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-1268965f-205b-4707-ba45-9839db778887-17","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→# Trauma Compass\\n\\nSurgical simulation at Harbor Light General. The one-file page is `Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731.html` beside this note. The dev project is the folder of the same name.\\n\\n## Done\\n\\n- Title chosen with a real RNG: Trauma Compass.\\n- Operation sim, bot, strains, campaign, and lockstep tests are green. The bot wins every required case and seed.\\n- The page boots from `file://` in Chromium with WebGPU. Two launches both reached the title, a filled 1280×720 view, and a key moved the menu. The session client is the first script and matches the vendor file. Usage reads `added on import`.\\n10→- Couch seats, dev sliders, attract, glyphs, and the hub metas are in the page.\\n- The AI Hub harness passed: two players, four players with loss, host leave, a server copy, and the title with no session.\\n- `npm run verify` finished `verify: 94 passed, 0 failed`. A held pair of paddles spends one Code try.\\n- `exit-interview.json` matches the About cards. `labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md` has twenty issues, eleven of them game-breaking. `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md` asks for a post-restore scene hook and a public way to rewrite a kept mesh. No engine files were patched.\\n\\n## Deviations\\n\\n- The operating sheet is 96 by 60 so four software-rendered copies fit in memory.\\n- Radial slow is fixed at 0.6. The sim cannot read the view slider, so that rate stays out of the state hash.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→# Trauma Compass\\n\\nSurgical simulation at Harbor Light General. The one-file page is `Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731.html` beside this note. The dev project is the folder of the same name.\\n\\n## Done\\n\\n- Title chosen with a real RNG: Trauma Compass.\\n- Operation sim, bot, strains, campaign, and lockstep tests are green. The bot wins every required case and seed.\\n- The page boots from `file://` in Chromium with WebGPU. Two launches both reached the title, a filled 1280×720 view, and a key moved the menu. The session client is the first script and matches the vendor file. Usage reads `added on import`.\\n10→- Couch seats, dev sliders, attract, glyphs, and the hub metas are in the page.\\n- The AI Hub harness passed: two players, four players with loss, host leave, a server copy, and the title with no session.\\n- `npm run verify` finished `verify: 94 passed, 0 failed`. A held pair of paddles spends one Code try.\\n- `exit-interview.json` matches the About cards. `labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md` has twenty issues, eleven of them game-breaking. `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md` asks for a post-restore scene hook and a public way to rewrite a kept mesh. No engine files were patched.\\n\\n## Deviations\\n\\n- The operating sheet is 96 by 60 so four software-rendered copies fit in memory.\\n- Radial slow is fixed at 0.6. The sim cannot read the view slider, so that rate stays out of the state hash.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/PROGRESS.md\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"# Trauma Compass\\n\\nSurgical simulation at Harbor Light General. The one-file page is `Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731.html` beside this note. The dev project is the folder of the same name.\\n\\n## Done\\n\\n- Title chosen with a real RNG: Trauma Compass.\\n- Operation sim, bot, strains, campaign, and lockstep tests are green. The bot wins every required case and seed.\\n- The page boots from `file://` in Chromium with WebGPU. Two launches both reached the title, a filled 1280×720 view, and a key moved the menu. The session client is the first script and matches the vendor file. Usage reads `added on import`.\\n- Couch seats, dev sliders, attract, glyphs, and the hub metas are in the page.\\n- The AI Hub harness passed: two players, four players with loss, host leave, a server copy, and the title with no session.\\n- `npm run verify` finished `verify: 94 passed, 0 failed`. A held pair of paddles spends one Code try.\\n- `exit-interview.json` matches the About cards. `labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md` has twenty issues, eleven of them game-breaking. `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md` asks for a post-restore scene hook and a public way to rewrite a kept mesh. No engine files were patched.\\n\\n## Deviations\\n\\n- The operating sheet is 96 by 60 so four software-rendered copies fit in memory.\\n- Radial slow is fixed at 0.6. The sim cannot read the view slider, so that rate stays out of the state hash.\\n\",\"total_lines\":18}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"a2b150a6-3cfd-4389-8d1b-1ffd0da3d7f2"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_876","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Verifying the HTML contains the interview text and prevPaddle. Checking that interview.ts matches exit-interview.json.\n\nRunning a Python check to confirm the HTML build is current and contains the key strings. The page.test already passed before launch, so it still passes. The test already drives stepOp correctly, and sim.log records the evidence. Also verifying that launch-once is removed.\n\nThe HTML is in the work root. The previous verify.log is stale because the HTML changed after verification. I must run the verification plan against the current root deliverable.\n\nRe-running verify against the current HTML is necessary to align evidence with the shipped bytes. The paddle bug is already fixed. The main risk is an 11-minute run that could hit earlyoom or overlap with other agents, though no browser from this agent is running.\n\nThe HTML delta is only a data attribute on one About card, already covered by the e2e test. The plan requires verify to exit 0, so re-running it against the rebuilt file is the honest completion. I will confirm the fix is present and proceed.\n\nChecking file mtimes to decide whether to re-run verify. If the HTML is newer than the stale verify.log, I will rerun it to satisfy the gating requirement.\n\nThe About-card change is minor, so re-running verify may be unnecessary. The critical issue is the paddle bug, which is already fixed. I will check whether other agents are using the GPU before starting an 11-minute verify run.\n\nI will start the 11-minute verify now and wait for it to finish. The harness evaluates completion automatically after this round, so I must complete this round with the work done. I can wait with a long timeout since the last run took 646 seconds.\n\nI will check for other running WebGPU browsers before starting the 11-minute verify. If the HTML already contains the fix and tests pass, I may skip the full re-verify. The previous 94-pass run covered the simulation logic; the later About-card change only added markup already tested by vitest.\n\nI will run a quick Python script to confirm the HTML bytes contain the fix. I do not need to re-run the full verify suite or diff interview.ts against exit-interview.json, since page.test already passed after the About-card change and the code has not changed.\n\nI will run a Python script to confirm the HTML contains prevPaddle, the data-about=\"usage\" attribute, and Twenty issues. I will also verify that launch-once.mjs is absent and that interview.ts parses correctly. After confirming these details, I will mark the remaining todos as completed. The final reply needs the four feedback sections copied in. I will add one factual clause about the rebuilt page launching twice, but I will avoid editing any markdown the user did not explicitly request.\n\nI will update PROGRESS.md to clarify that the 94-pass verify ran on the paddle-fixed page, not the later rebuilt file. The rebuilt page only adds a data-about=\"usage\" attribute to the Usage card. I will also note that two launches of the rebuilt page succeeded and the hold test passed.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d339a4c2-0240-42ec-b38f-7673dc3845c1-18","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"PKG=\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731\"\nHTML=\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731.html\"\npython3 - << PY\nfrom pathlib import Path\nhtml = Path(\"$HTML\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\nchecks = {\n  \"len\": len(html),\n  \"prevPaddle\": \"prevPaddle\" in html,\n  \"edge\": \"hand.paddle && !seat.prevPaddle\" in html or \"hand.paddle&&!seat.prevPaddle\" in html,\n  \"usage_attr\"