{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_888","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The server failed to print its port within 8 seconds.\n\nPython's stdout is block-buffered when piped, so the server banner never flushes until the buffer fills or the process exits.\n\nThe earlier successful run likely had PYTHONUNBUFFERED set. This shell may lack it if the tool does not source bashrc.\n\nThe previous successful run used the same environment, so PYTHONUNBUFFERED should have been present. The fix is to spawn Python with the `-u` flag in hub.mjs to force unbuffered output.\n\nThe banner might actually be printing to stderr instead of stdout. Python 3.14 http.server could use a different format that still matches the port regex.\n\nA missing python binary would have caused an immediate exit error rather than a timeout. The 8-second window is ample for the server to print its banner, so slowness is ruled out. Block buffering remains the most likely cause.\n\nA quick test will confirm whether piping Python's stdout causes the banner to be hidden. Port 0 makes a leftover server impossible, and the timeout confirms the process never exited. If unbuffered output fixes it, the `-u` flag will be added directly to hub.mjs so verification no longer depends on PYTHONUNBUFFERED.\n\nThe test will write to scratch instead of /tmp. Both buffered and unbuffered Python output will be captured. If the banner still does not appear with -u, another bug is present. Memory pressure after the prior Chromium replay is unlikely to cause this.\n\nMemory pressure from the prior Chromium replay may have delayed Python startup past the 8-second window. The plan will first reproduce the buffering issue, then run hub.mjs alone to confirm before doing a full verify.\n\nOnly the hub check failed in the latest verify run. The other ninety tests passed. This is fewer than the ninety-four from the previous successful run, which included five separate hub checks. I will confirm hub.mjs works alone before attempting another full verify.\n\nThe hub.mjs failure is counted as a single test failure, not five separate ones. The ninety passed tests plus this one failure equals the ninety total from the previous run. The missing five hub checks were never reported because the process crashed before they could emit their JSON lines.\n\nThe game tests passed, including the paddle test. Only the hub server banner failed.\n\nI will reproduce the buffering issue before editing hub.mjs. The fix will use `python3 -u` and possibly set PYTHONUNBUFFERED in the spawn environment. I may also increase the timeout slightly.\n\nA comment in hub.mjs already noted that Python 3.14 prints the banner on stdout, but it did not mention block buffering.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-72f377e0-2538-4ac5-a3f5-fe4b801a41b8-40","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"SCRATCH=\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer\"\necho \"PYTHONUNBUFFERED=${PYTHONUNBUFFERED-<unset>}\"\npython3 -c 'import os; print(\"py\", os.environ.get(\"PYTHONUNBUFFERED\"))'\n# piped stdout, default buffering\nd=$(mktemp -d \"$SCRATCH/hubport.XXXXXX\")\npython3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1 >\"$d/out\" 2>\"$d/err\" &\npid=$!\nsleep 1\necho \"after 1s default out=$(wc -c < \"$d/out\") err=$(wc -c < \"$d/err\")\"\nkill \"$pid\" 2>/dev/null || true\nwait \"$pid\" 2>/dev/null || true\necho \"--- default out ---\"; cat \"$d/out\"; echo \"--- default err ---\"; cat \"$d/err\"\n# unbuffered\npython3 -u -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1 >\"$d/outu\" 2>\"$d/erru\" &\npid=$!\nsleep 0.4\necho \"after 0.4s -u out=$(wc -c < \"$d/outu\") err=$(wc -c < \"$d/erru\")\"\nkill \"$pid\" 2>/dev/null || true\nwait \"$pid\" 2>/dev/null || true\necho \"--- -u out ---\"; cat \"$d/outu\"; echo \"--- -u err ---\"; cat \"$d/erru\"\nrm -rf \"$d\"","description":"See if Python hides the port banner when piped"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2197,"output_tokens":2123,"cache_read_input_tokens":82688,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"0b97e2e1-3732-4318-8e94-06c3920ec478"}
