{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_889","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Python block-buffers stdout when piped without PYTHONUNBUFFERED or -u.\n\nThe fix belongs in hub.mjs: spawn `python3 -u` directly so the harness does not depend on PYTHONUNBUFFERED from the parent environment. Any leftover python servers were already killed.\n\nThe spawn call now passes `['-u', '-m', 'http.server', '0', '--bind', '127.0.0.1']`. A comment will note the unbuffered process so the pipe sees the banner immediately. I should check if any test asserts these spawn arguments and verify line length for prettier.\n\nThe spawn line is about 90 characters, which fits within the 120-character limit. The comment will note that Python 3.14 prints the banner on stdout and a pipe blocks it until the buffer fills; `-u` flushes it immediately. After editing hub.mjs, I will run it alone to confirm the port is captured and checks pass before doing the full verification.\n\nThe previous hub run passed. I will run hub.mjs alone with a short TMPDIR and CHROMIUM_PATH, logging to scratch/hub.log. If it passes, I must still run the full verify again because the evaluator requires the entire suite to exit 0.\n\nI will run hub.mjs alone first to catch logic failures before the long verify. I also need to check for eslint and prettier issues, and I should kill any leftover servers from the failed verify.\n\nThe failed verify likely left orphaned Python http.server processes. I need to find and kill them before running hub.mjs alone.\n\nI will identify orphaned Python http.server processes by their working directory under /tmp/g.* or by the command line `http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`. Only these specific processes should be killed, not other agents.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2c230aef-7cb3-4ba8-b66e-d2f16fd4b68b-41","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"for pid in $(pgrep -f 'http.server' || true); do\n  echo \"PID $pid cwd=$(readlink -f /proc/$pid/cwd 2>/dev/null) cmd=$(tr '\\0' ' ' < /proc/$pid/cmdline 2>/dev/null)\"\ndone\necho DONE","description":"List http.server processes and their cwd"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2c230aef-7cb3-4ba8-b66e-d2f16fd4b68b-42","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/tools/hub.mjs","old_string":"const server = spawn('python3', ['-m', 'http.server', '0', '--bind', '127.0.0.1'], {\n  cwd: serve,\n  stdio: ['ignore', 'pipe', 'pipe'],\n});\nconst port = await new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n  const timer = setTimeout(() => reject(new Error('the server did not say its port')), 8000);\n  // Python 3.14 prints the banner on stdout. Older copies used stderr. Either stream counts.","new_string":"const server = spawn('python3', ['-u', '-m', 'http.server', '0', '--bind', '127.0.0.1'], {\n  cwd: serve,\n  stdio: ['ignore', 'pipe', 'pipe'],\n});\nconst port = await new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n  const timer = setTimeout(() => reject(new Error('the server did not say its port')), 8000);\n  // A pipe block-buffers Python's stdout, so -u is what makes the banner arrive. 3.14 prints it on stdout.\n  // Older copies used stderr. Either stream counts."}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2247,"output_tokens":1507,"cache_read_input_tokens":84864,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"4f8b8fb5-62df-4459-b4de-56a4ec5e8a12"}
