{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_903","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"ux.log and nowebgpu.log are from 02:28. The HTML file is from 04:17.\n\nLaunches for the current HTML already exist. UX and nowebgpu logs are stale. Re-running all three missing checks will generate current evidence.\n\nThe full e2e.mjs script is 11 minutes long and includes a campaign that already passed. I am weighing whether to run the entire script or write a shorter scratch script that only covers UX and WebGPU.\n\nDuplicating e2e.mjs without the campaign block is too fragile. No environment flag skips that section, and editing the script would change the tool itself.\n\nI will run the full e2e.mjs script and extract the UX and WebGPU lines afterward. This is the simplest honest approach, though it takes about twelve minutes.\n\nThe verifier just finished, so the machine is likely stable. I am now considering a lighter three-part run: launch.mjs for the file:// launches, a focused UX script, and the Python WebGPU check. I will not edit e2e.mjs to add a skip flag.\n\nThe previous verify run took about eleven minutes total. The campaign block inside e2e.mjs is the main bottleneck.\n\nI will run launch.mjs and e2e.mjs in sequence. I rejected extracting UX checks into a scratch script because e2e.mjs does not export its functions and duplicating the logic would risk drift.\n\nI will run launch.mjs first, then e2e.mjs in a single command with a twenty-minute timeout. The output will be parsed into ux.log and nowebgpu.log.\n\nThe paddle issue still triggers the skeptic. I will make the test more explicit so the auditor sees tick 3 specifically. I will also edge the paddle in pulseEdges to fix the cited path. Edgeing in both places should still yield only one try.\n\nDouble-edging the paddle would not break anything. The bot bypasses pulseEdges entirely and uses botHands directly, so it never sees the scene-level edge. The stepOp tests already pass because the simulator edges the paddle.\n\nThe committed test already passed in verify 95, so I will not edit it unless broken. The next step is to run the missing evidence checks.\n\nlaunch-1 already contains shot.txt, state.json, and log.txt as required. I will re-run launch.mjs and a focused UX capture. Killing e2e.mjs after the UX checks is too fragile, so I am checking the script structure to find a cleaner way to isolate those checks.\n\nI will run launch.mjs first, then e2e.mjs. The full campaign must pass. I will split the combined stdout into ux.log and nowebgpu.log by filtering for WebGPU messages and UX checks.\n\nThe full e2e run should pass because verify succeeded minutes ago on the same HTML. I will run launch.mjs and e2e.mjs in a single command with no browser overlap. I need to check that launch.mjs writes shot.txt and confirm no Chrome process is running.\n\nI am simulating the exact skeptic failure condition to harden the test. If both seats hold paddles, each seat triggers a rising edge and creates code with two tries. This confirms the test catches the bug even when the simulator is forced to treat every seat as active.\n\nThe \"both paddles\" condition is a co-op edge case. If both surgeons hold their paddles on the same off-band step, two pressPaddle calls fire in one step. Tries drop from two to zero instantly, causing an instant fail. The game design actually means L2 and R2 on a single controller.\n\nThe \"both paddles\" condition is the single L2/R2 trigger pair, not a co-op double-press. I will leave that logic untouched.\n\nI am now reading the rest of launch.mjs to confirm output paths and verifying the e2e script uses the correct file:// URL for the root HTML.\n\nThe relative path `../../../../NAME.html` from `labs/game/tools` correctly resolves to the work folder root. The launch script uses an absolute file URL, and e2e.mjs imports touch profiles from playwright devices. I am now setting up the environment variables for the combined launch and e2e command.\n\nNode resolves modules from the script file location, not the current working directory. I will copy launch.mjs into labs/game/tools so Node can find the package's playwright dependency. I will delete that copy afterward. The e2e script runs directly from the package root. After both commands finish, I will split the combined stdout into ux.log and nowebgpu.log.\n\nI will set the combined timeout to 25 minutes. The campaign block alone takes 11 minutes, so I am erring on the safe side. I will not skip the campaign because the evaluator did not ask to. After the run finishes, I will clean up temporary files and inspect the output.\n\nI considered copying e2e.mjs into scratch to strip the campaign block, but Node would not resolve the package's playwright dependency from that directory. The script must remain inside the package root, so I will copy it to labs/game/tools/launch-once.mjs instead.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8eb0e1e4-dd8d-454e-93d1-4d9f6647c549-69","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/tools/e2e.mjs","offset":300,"limit":160}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8eb0e1e4-dd8d-454e-93d1-4d9f6647c549-70","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/launch.mjs","offset":70}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2884,"output_tokens":3295,"cache_read_input_tokens":110592,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"a7e52995-acef-41e8-be18-73e502fd1840"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-8eb0e1e4-dd8d-454e-93d1-4d9f6647c549-69","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"300→        return (\\n          text.includes('Seat 2 claimed') &&\\n          Math.abs(gloves[0].x) > 0.2 &&\\n          Math.abs(gloves[1].x) > 0.2 &&\\n          gloves[0].x !== gloves[1].x\\n        );\\n      },\\n      null,\\n      { timeout: 5000 },\\n    );\\n310→    const seats = await page.evaluate(() => ({\\n      text: document.querySelector('[data-game=\\\"scrub\\\"]')?.textContent ?? '',\\n      gloves: window.__compass.gloves(),\\n    }));\\n    const claimed = seats.text.includes('Seat 1 claimed') && seats.text.includes('Seat 2 claimed');\\n    const moved =\\n      Math.abs(seats.gloves[0].x) > 0.2 && Math.abs(seats.gloves[1].x) > 0.2 && seats.gloves[0].x !== seats.gloves[1].x;\\n    report('two pads claim seats and move', claimed && moved, JSON.stringify(seats));\\n  } finally {\\n    await page.close();\\n320→  }\\n});\\n\\nawait block('audio', async () => {\\n  const page = await browser.newPage({ viewport: { width: 1280, height: 720 } });\\n  try {\\n    watch(page);\\n    await page.goto(pageUrl);\\n    await page.waitForFunction(() => window.__engine?.ready);\\n    await page.mouse.click(30, 680);\\n330→    const heard = await page.evaluate(async () => {\\n      const audio = window.__compass.audio;\\n      const music = audio.volume('music');\\n      const ctx = audio.context;\\n      if (ctx?.state === 'suspended') await ctx.resume();\\n      const analyser = ctx.createAnalyser();\\n      const osc = ctx.createOscillator();\\n      osc.frequency.value = 440;\\n      osc.connect(analyser);\\n      analyser.connect(ctx.destination);\\n340→      osc.start();\\n      await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 60));\\n      const data = new Uint8Array(analyser.fftSize);\\n      analyser.getByteTimeDomainData(data);\\n      osc.stop();\\n      const offline = new OfflineAudioContext(1, 4000, 44100);\\n      const tone = offline.createOscillator();\\n      tone.connect(offline.destination);\\n      tone.start();\\n      const rendered = await offline.startRendering();\\n350→      let sum = 0;\\n      for (const sample of rendered.getChannelData(0)) sum += Math.abs(sample);\\n      audio.play('sfx:compass-beep');\\n      return { music, state: ctx.state, peak: Math.max(...data), offline: sum > 0 };\\n    });\\n    report(\\n      'music bus is quiet and a tone is audible',\\n      heard.music === 0.1 && heard.state === 'running' && heard.peak > 128 && heard.offline,\\n      JSON.stringify(heard),\\n    );\\n360→  } finally {\\n    await page.close();\\n  }\\n});\\n\\nawait block('touch', async () => {\\n  const phone = await browser.newContext({ ...devices['Pixel 7'] });\\n  const page = await phone.newPage();\\n  try {\\n    watch(page);\\n370→    await page.goto(pageUrl);\\n    await page.waitForFunction(\\n      () =>\\n        window.__engine?.ready &&\\n        document.querySelector('[data-game=\\\"touch\\\"]')?.textContent?.includes('Controller or keyboard required'),\\n      null,\\n      { timeout: 40000 },\\n    );\\n    await page.waitForFunction(() => window.__compass?.screen === 'attract', null, { timeout: 15000 });\\n    const text = await page.locator('[data-game=\\\"touch\\\"]').innerText();\\n380→    await page.locator('[data-game=\\\"touch\\\"] [data-act=\\\"settings\\\"]').tap();\\n    await page.waitForFunction(() => window.__compass?.screen === 'settings', null, { timeout: 10000 });\\n    report('touch asks for a controller', text.includes('Controller or keyboard required'), text);\\n  } finally {\\n    await phone.close();\\n  }\\n});\\n\\nawait block('glyphs', async () => {\\n  const page = await browser.newPage({ viewport: { width: 1280, height: 720 } });\\n390→  try {\\n    watch(page);\\n    await page.goto(pageUrl);\\n    await page.waitForFunction(() => window.__engine?.ready && window.__compass?.screen === 'title', null, {\\n      timeout: 40000,\\n    });\\n    await page.keyboard.press('ArrowDown');\\n    await page.waitForFunction(() => document.querySelector('.prompt')?.innerHTML.includes('Enter'));\\n    const keys = await page.locator('.prompt').innerHTML();\\n    await page.mouse.click(30, 680);\\n400→    await page.waitForFunction(() => document.querySelector('.prompt')?.innerHTML.includes('M18 16'));\\n    const mouse = await page.locator('.prompt').innerHTML();\\n    await page.click('text=Settings');\\n    await page.keyboard.press('ArrowRight');\\n    await page.waitForFunction(() => document.body.innerText.includes('Glyphs'));\\n    await page.click('text=Glyphs');\\n    await page.waitForFunction(() => document.body.innerText.includes('Xbox'));\\n    const xbox = await page.locator('[data-game=\\\"menu\\\"]').innerText();\\n    report(\\n      'prompts follow the last device',\\n410→      keys.includes('Enter') && mouse.includes('M18 16'),\\n      `${keys.includes('Enter')} ${mouse.includes('M18 16')}`,\\n    );\\n    report('Xbox glyphs are a setting', xbox.includes('Xbox'), xbox);\\n  } finally {\\n    await page.close();\\n  }\\n});\\n\\nawait block('campaign', async () => {\\n420→  const page = await browser.newPage({ viewport: { width: 960, height: 540 } });\\n  try {\\n    watch(page);\\n    await page.goto(`${pageUrl}?game.autoplay=1`);\\n    let detail = '';\\n    let ok = false;\\n    try {\\n      await page.waitForFunction(() => window.__compass && window.__compass.screen === 'credits', null, {\\n        timeout: 660000,\\n      });\\n430→      ok = true;\\n    } catch {\\n      detail = await page.evaluate(() => {\\n        const op = window.__compass?.live?.();\\n        return JSON.stringify({\\n          screen: window.__compass?.screen,\\n          caseId: window.__compass?.campaign?.caseId,\\n          status: op?.status,\\n          tick: op?.tick,\\n          score: op?.score,\\n440→          fail: op?.fa