{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_913","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The current click test moves the mouse before clicking.\n\nAdding a pointermove exit would let the mouse move trigger attract exit before the click. The test would still pass, but the report would wrongly claim it exits on a click. I should split the tests: first wait for attract, then move the mouse and expect title without saving. Then wait again and click. Since page.mouse.click moves the cursor too, the click test may also be triggered by that move.\n\nI will test pointerdown separately using page.mouse.down() at the current position without moving the cursor. The plan calls for a mouse move, so I will rename the first exit test to \"attract exits on a mouse move and saves nothing\" and drop the old click name.\n\nThe pad button test will run before the stick test. It clears pads, waits for attract, presses button 0 with axes 0, and expects title. Pads are then cleared again so attract can restart for the stick test. The last check does not need clearing because a new page is created.\n\nThe pad button test must wait for attract to start before installing the pad. Installing it earlier would reset idle state and prevent attract from restarting.\n\nI will add an iPad tablet test after the phone block. I need to check Playwright's device names for iPad models. The phone test already confirms attract is showing.\n\nThe tablet test will report that the screen asks for a controller. I will check that no engine touch layer is created, though this may be over-scoping since the existing test already covers the message and settings button. I also considered resetting touchHold in boot.ts on pointermove, but a mouse on a touch device is rare.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6366cda0-dd4a-4e76-8f12-96640c6fc007-88","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/tools/one-file.mts","limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3292,"output_tokens":1051,"cache_read_input_tokens":134656,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"8472df6f-557d-426f-b5dd-25433e142d05"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-6366cda0-dd4a-4e76-8f12-96640c6fc007-88","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file Build Trauma Compass as one HTML file. Vite inlines the module. The hub client is already the first script.\\n */\\nimport { writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport { dirname, join } from 'node:path';\\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\\nimport type { Rollup } from 'vite';\\nimport { externalRefs, inlineBuild, ONE_FILE_NOTE } from '../../../tools/lib/oneFile';\\n\\n10→const root = join(dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), '../../..');\\nconst page = join(root, 'labs/game/index.html');\\nconst out = join(root, '..', 'Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731.html');\\n\\nconst { build } = await import('vite');\\nconst result = await build({\\n  root,\\n  configFile: false,\\n  logLevel: 'warn',\\n  base: './',\\n20→  resolve: { alias: [{ find: /^three$/, replacement: 'three/webgpu' }] },\\n  build: {\\n    write: false,\\n    modulePreload: false,\\n    cssCodeSplit: false,\\n    assetsInlineLimit: () => true,\\n    chunkSizeWarningLimit: Infinity,\\n    rollupOptions: { input: page, output: { inlineDynamicImports: true } },\\n  },\\n});\\n30→\\nconst outputs = (Array.isArray(result) ? result : [result]) as Rollup.RollupOutput[];\\nconst files: Record<string, string> = {};\\nlet html: string | undefined;\\nfor (const item of outputs.flatMap((output) => output.output)) {\\n  const text =\\n    item.type === 'chunk'\\n      ? item.code\\n      : typeof item.source === 'string'\\n        ? item.source\\n40→        : new TextDecoder().decode(item.source);\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file Build Trauma Compass as one HTML file. Vite inlines the module. The hub client is already the first script.\\n */\\nimport { writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport { dirname, join } from 'node:path';\\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\\nimport type { Rollup } from 'vite';\\nimport { externalRefs, inlineBuild, ONE_FILE_NOTE } from '../../../tools/lib/oneFile';\\n\\n10→const root = join(dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), '../../..');\\nconst page = join(root, 'labs/game/index.html');\\nconst out = join(root, '..', 'Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731.html');\\n\\nconst { build } = await import('vite');\\nconst result = await build({\\n  root,\\n  configFile: false,\\n  logLevel: 'warn',\\n  base: './',\\n20→  resolve: { alias: [{ find: /^three$/, replacement: 'three/webgpu' }] },\\n  build: {\\n    write: false,\\n    modulePreload: false,\\n    cssCodeSplit: false,\\n    assetsInlineLimit: () => true,\\n    chunkSizeWarningLimit: Infinity,\\n    rollupOptions: { input: page, output: { inlineDynamicImports: true } },\\n  },\\n});\\n30→\\nconst outputs = (Array.isArray(result) ? result : [result]) as Rollup.RollupOutput[];\\nconst files: Record<string, string> = {};\\nlet html: string | undefined;\\nfor (const item of outputs.flatMap((output) => output.output)) {\\n  const text =\\n    item.type === 'chunk'\\n      ? item.code\\n      : typeof item.source === 'string'\\n        ? item.source\\n40→        : new TextDecoder().decode(item.source);\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/tools/one-file.mts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file Build Trauma Compass as one HTML file. Vite inlines the module. The hub client is already the first script.\\n */\\nimport { writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport { dirname, join } from 'node:path';\\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\\nimport type { Rollup } from 'vite';\\nimport { externalRefs, inlineBuild, ONE_FILE_NOTE } from '../../../tools/lib/oneFile';\\n\\nconst root = join(dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), '../../..');\\nconst page = join(root, 'labs/game/index.html');\\nconst out = join(root, '..', 'Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731.html');\\n\\nconst { build } = await import('vite');\\nconst result = await build({\\n  root,\\n  configFile: false,\\n  logLevel: 'warn',\\n  base: './',\\n  resolve: { alias: [{ find: /^three$/, replacement: 'three/webgpu' }] },\\n  build: {\\n    write: false,\\n    modulePreload: false,\\n    cssCodeSplit: false,\\n    assetsInlineLimit: () => true,\\n    chunkSizeWarningLimit: Infinity,\\n    rollupOptions: { input: page, output: { inlineDynamicImports: true } },\\n  },\\n});\\n\\nconst outputs = (Array.isArray(result) ? result : [result]) as Rollup.RollupOutput[];\\nconst files: Record<string, string> = {};\\nlet html: string | undefined;\\nfor (const item of outputs.flatMap((output) => output.output)) {\\n  const text =\\n    item.type === 'chunk'\\n      ? item.code\\n      : typeof item.source === 'string'\\n        ? item.source\\n        : new TextDecoder().decode(item.source);\\n\",\"total_lines\":52}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"7d51f9c4-bd74-4f8f-8d93-1063c54f4abe"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_914","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I will make the code changes, rebuild, and run evidence to verify.\n\nI'll duplicate the phone block for the iPad Pro 11 tablet. I'll verify the device exists before editing. I'll run eslint on boot.ts and prettier on both files before rebuilding. The pad button index is correct. The gamepad will register automatically on the next frame.\n\nI'll insert the button test before the stick test and clear pads between them. The first mouse check will be renamed to a move test that exits attract mode, then a separate click test will press down and up while the mouse stays still to verify pointerdown.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"A mouse move does not leave the attract loop, and the UX log has no tablet. I’ll fix that on the shipped page, then refresh the launch, UX, and WebGPU evidence."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2bb6c53e-b95d-46c4-8817-f3663077d944-89","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/app/boot.ts","old_string":"  addEventListener('pointerdown', (event) => {\n    const node = event.target instanceof Element ? event.target : null;\n    // A control's click is still coming. Hiding the gate here replaces the button before that click lands.\n    if (node?.closest('[data-act], input, label.slider')) return;\n    touchHold = false;\n    if (campaign.screen === 'attract') noteInput(campaign);\n  });","new_string":"  addEventListener('pointerdown', (event) => {\n    const node = event.target instanceof Element ? event.target : null;\n    // A control's click is still coming. Hiding the gate here replaces the button before that click lands.\n    if (node?.closest('[data-act], input, label.slider')) return;\n    touchHold = false;\n    if (campaign.s