{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_928","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The first failure was a target crash during mouse and dev testing. The pad then crashed.\n\nThe browser crash likely stems from memory pressure rather than a logic bug. Webkit failed due to a Python traceback, possibly because Firefox output broke parsing or the script failed to launch Webkit.\n\nThe Webkit failure likely stems from memory exhaustion after the Chrome crash, not a code bug. Retrying verify once is appropriate since memory may have freed. However, the full 11-minute run might still fail if the \"mouse and dev\" test reliably crashes Chrome on this HTML.\n\nThe prior ux-once run passed mouse and dev on this same HTML, confirming the crash is flaky rather than deterministic. The crash occurred during the mouse and dev wait, which suggests a GPU process bug triggered by hovering or clicking after the attract changes.\n\nThe verify run runs after a long vitest suite and replay browser, so memory fragmentation may be contributing. The mouse and dev code was unchanged since the passing ux-once run, confirming this is environmental. I will check for leftover Chrome processes and available memory before retrying.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9fb1bbfe-2663-4cb4-9828-e1f76890a4ef-105","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/verify.log"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":986,"output_tokens":676,"cache_read_input_tokens":153472,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"6782b6f3-8316-4e9a-80b4-c29ad74a955a"}
