{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_936","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The patch file appears to be an unrelated diff from the parent repository rather than game changes.\n\nThe local simulation now edges paddle presses via prevPaddle. The hub path still fires paddle every tick while held because countPress increments the counter each frame. applyHands only triggers pressPaddle when the current hand.paddle is true and seat.prevPaddle is false.\n\nThe hub path is actually correct. prevPaddle persists after the first tick, so applyHands ignores subsequent presses and only one shock fires per hold.\n\nEven if the host skips several frames between ticks, take() only consumes one counter increment per call. The remaining hold duration still collapses to a single press via prevPaddle. Releasing and pressing again resets prevPaddle, so the next attempt works normally.\n\nAn edge case remains: if the player holds the paddle before the fix is active, prevPaddle is already true when the code starts. The ongoing hold then does not shock. The player must release and press again to trigger a new try.\n\nThis behavior is correct. It enforces one press per hold instead of allowing the original bug where holding burns both tries.\n\nThe requested test drives this with stepOp. Hold the paddle for several off-band steps and assert the operation remains active with tries remaining.\n\nPressing during off-band time consumes one try and leaves the operation active with one remaining. A hold starting on the same step as code creation is consumed by applyHands before stepVitals creates the code, so it never counts as a try. This is player-friendly because it avoids an unintended miss. The test assertions still need to be checked.\n\nI need to verify the test and re-run the reproduction.\n\nprevPaddle might be missing from snapshots or restore logic. If so, rewinding could double-fire or drop a press. I will check the snapshot code.\n\nEach seat has its own prevPaddle. Bots set paddle to codeBand every step.\n\nThe bot's paddle stays true for the entire 34-frame green band. Edge detection ensures only the first green frame triggers a press, so the bot succeeds on that single attempt and prevPaddle prevents extra shocks during the rest of the hold. When the band ends and restarts, the next cycle begins with a fresh edge.\n\nThe bot's prior behavior of setting paddle true every green frame still succeeds on the first frame and leaves code null, so the outcome is unchanged. The two-miss test was updated because the bot never misses.\n\nI still need to read the test and pressPaddle fully, verify whether prevPaddle is included in snapshots, and confirm the single HTML deliverable was rebuilt with the new logic.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f833d934-9a27-4e1b-a264-811334ff1123-76","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/body.ts","offset":17,"limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f833d934-9a27-4e1b-a264-811334ff1123-77","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/body.ts","offset":120,"limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f833d934-9a27-4e1b-a264-811334ff1123-78","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/op.test.ts","offset":80,"limit":70}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f833d934-9a27-4e1b-a264-811334ff1123-79","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"prevPaddle|One hold is one shock","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731.html"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f833d934-9a27-4e1b-a264-811334ff1123-80","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"prevPaddle|snapshot","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op","glob":"*.ts"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7500,"output_tokens":1566,"cache_read_input_tokens":170624,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"eac48bbe-c1f8-433f-9cfd-808ac5fc9422"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f833d934-9a27-4e1b-a264-811334ff1123-76","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"17→/** Read hands into seats. Null means the menu is up: cursors stay, buttons do not stick. */\\nexport function applyHands(op: Op, hands: readonly Hand[] | null): void {\\n  if (!hands) {\\n20→    for (const seat of op.seats) seat.use = false;\\n    op.radial = false;\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  op.radial = hands.some((hand) => hand.radial === true);\\n  for (let i = 0; i < op.seats.length; i++) {\\n    const hand = hands[i];\\n    const seat = op.seats[i];\\n    if (!hand) continue;\\n    seat.x = Math.max(-8, Math.min(8, hand.x));\\n30→    seat.z = Math.max(-5, Math.min(5, hand.z));\\n    if (op.roll) {\\n      const wave = Math.sin(op.tick / 40);\\n      if (op.tick % 420 < 36) {\\n        seat.x += wave * 0.1;\\n        seat.z += wave * 0.04;\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (hand.tool >= 0 && hand.tool <= 7 && hand.tool !== seat.tool) {\\n      seat.tool = hand.tool;\\n40→      op.events.push({ type: 'tool', text: 'clack', seat: seat.id });\\n    }\\n    seat.use = hand.use;\\n    seat.drop = hand.drop;\\n    if (hand.site >= 0 && hand.site < op.sites.length) seat.site = hand.site;\\n    if (hand.hint) op.events.push({ type: 'hint', text: op.hint || 'Steady, Doctor.', seat: seat.id });\\n    if (hand.swap && op.swapOk) swapPersona(op, seat);\\n    if (hand.gift) pressGift(op, seat);\\n    // One hold is one shock. The next try waits until the paddles come up.\\n    if (hand.paddle && !seat.prevPaddle) pressPaddle(op, seat);\\n50→    seat.prevPaddle = hand.paddle;\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** Swap the lead between Stillpoint and Second Pulse. */\\nfunction swapPersona(op: Op, seat: Seat): void {\\n  if (seat.id !== 0) return;\\n  if (seat.gift === 'stillpoint') {\\n    seat.gift = 'second';\\n    op.persona = 'sabine';\\n60→  } else if (seat.gift === 'second') {\\n    seat.gift = 'stillpoint';\\n    op.persona = 'wren';\\n  }\\n  op.events.push({ type: 'swap', text: op.persona, seat: seat.id });\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"17→/** Read hands into seats. Null means the menu is up: cursors stay, buttons do not stick. */\\nexport function applyHands(op: Op, hands: readonly Hand[] | null): void {\\n  if (!hands) {\\n20→    for (const seat of op.seats) seat.use = false;\\n    op.radial = false;\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  op.radial = hands.some((hand) => hand.radial === true);\\n  for (let i = 0; i < op.seats.length; i++) {\\n    const hand = hands[i];\\n    const seat = op.seats[i];\\n    if (!hand) continue;\\n    seat.x = Math.max(-8, Math.min(8, hand.x));\\n30→    seat.z = Math.max(-5, Math.min(5, hand.z));\\n    if (op.roll) {\\n      const wave = Math.sin(op.tick / 40);\\n      if (op.tick % 420 < 36) {\\n        seat.x += wave * 0.1;\\n        seat.z += wave * 0.04;\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (hand.tool >= 0 && hand.tool <= 7 && hand.tool !== seat.tool) {\\n      seat.tool = hand.tool;\\n40→      op.events.push({ type: 'tool', text: 'clack', seat: seat.id });\\n    }\\n    seat.use = hand.use;\\n    seat.drop = hand.drop;\\n    if (hand.site >= 0 && hand.site < op.sites.length) seat.site = hand.site;\\n    if (hand.hint) op.events.push({ type: 'hint', text: op.hint || 'Steady, Doctor.', seat: seat.id });\\n    if (hand.swap && op.swapOk) swapPersona(op, seat);\\n    if (hand.gift) pressGift(op, seat);\\n    // One hold is one shock. The next try waits until the paddles come up.\\n    if (hand.paddle && !seat.prevPaddle) pressPaddle(op, seat);\\n50→    seat.prevPaddle = hand.paddle;\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** Swap the lead between Stillpoint and Second Pulse. */\\nfunction swapPersona(op: Op, seat: Seat): void {\\n  if (seat.id !== 0) return;\\n  if (seat.gift === 'stillpoint') {\\n    seat.gift = 'second';\\n    op.persona = 'sabine';\\n60→  } else if (seat.gift === 'second') {\\n    seat.gift = 'stillpoint';\\n    op.persona = 'wren';\\n  }\\n  op.events.push({ type: 'swap', text: op.persona, seat: seat.id });\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/body.ts\",\"offset\":17,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"/** Read hands into seats. Null means the menu is up: cursors stay, buttons do not stick. */\\nexport function applyHands(op: Op, hands: readonly Hand[] | null): void {\\n  if (!hands) {\\n    for (const seat of op.seats) seat.use = false;\\n    op.radial = false;\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  op.radial = hands.some((hand) => hand.radial === true);\\n  for (let i = 0; i < op.seats.length; i++) {\\n    const hand = hands[i];\\n    const seat = op.seats[i];\\n    if (!hand) continue;\\n    seat.x = Math.max(-8, Math.min(8, hand.x));\\n    seat.z = Math.max(-5, Math.min(5, hand.z));\\n    if (op.roll) {\\n      const wave = Math.sin(op.tick / 40);\\n      if (op.tick % 420 < 36) {\\n        seat.x += wave * 0.1;\\n        seat.z += wave * 0.04;\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (hand.tool >= 0 && hand.tool <= 7 && hand.tool !== seat.tool) {\\n      seat.tool = hand.tool;\\n      op.events.push({ type: 'tool', text: 'clack', seat: seat.id });\\n    }\\n    seat.use = hand.use;\\n    seat.drop = hand.drop;\\n    if (hand.site >= 0 && hand.site < op.sites.length) seat.site = hand.site;\\n    if (hand.hint) op.events.push({ type: 'hint', text: op.hint || 'Steady, Doctor.', seat: seat.id });\\n    if (hand.swap && op.swapOk) swapPersona(op, seat);\\n    if (hand.gift) pressGift(op, seat);\\n    // One hold is one shock. The next try waits until the paddles come up.\\n    if (hand.paddle && !seat.prevPaddle) pressPaddle(op, seat);\\n    seat.prevPaddle = hand.paddle;\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** Swap the lead between Stillpoint and Second Pulse. */\\nfunction swapPersona(op: Op, seat: Seat): void {\\n  if (seat.id !== 0) return;\\n  if (seat.gift === 'stillpoint') {\\n    seat.gift = 'second';\\n    op.persona = 'sabine';\\n  } else if (seat.gift === 'second') {\\n    seat.gift = 'stillpoint';\\n    op.persona = 'wren';\\n  }\\n  op.events.push({ type: 'swap', text: op.persona, seat: seat.id });\\n}\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":297}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f833d934-9a27-4e1b-a264-811334ff1123-77","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"120→\\n/** Count a missed beat so a lock cannot sit forever. */\\nfunction tickLocks(op: Op): void {\\n  for (const seat of op.seats) {\\n    if (seat.lock < 0) continue;\\n    if (op.tick > seat.lockBeat + 12) {\\n      seat.lock += 1;\\n      seat.lockBeat = op.tick + 40;\\n      if (seat.lock >= 3) finishLock(op, seat);\\n    }\\n130→  }\\n}\\n\\n/** Both paddles. Inside the green band, the Code lands. */\\nfunction pressPaddle(op: Op, seat: Seat): void {\\n  if (!op.code) return;\\n  if (!codeBand(op)) {\\n    op.code.tries -= 1;\\n    op.code.shocks += 1;\\n    op.events.push({ type: 'shock', text: 'Miss.', seat: seat.id });\\n140→    if (op.code.tries <= 0) {\\n      op.code = null;\\n      failOp(op, 'The line stays flat.');\\n    }\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  const patient = op.patients[op.code.patient];\\n  if (patient) {\\n    patient.vitals = Math.max(patient.vitals, 25);\\n    patient.alive = true;\\n150→  }\\n  op.code = null;\\n  op.codeCleared = true;\\n  op.events.push({ type: 'shock', text: 'Got them.', seat: seat.id });\\n}\\n\\n/** The charge ring is green for a generous slice of each beat-and-a-half. */\\nexport function codeBand(op: Op): boolean {\\n  const at = op.tick % 90;\\n  return at >= 28 && at < 62;\\n160→}\\n\\n/** Bleeds, parasite auras, numb patches, then the flatline check. */\\nexport function stepVitals(op: Op, ft: number): void {\\n  const seconds = ft / FIELD_SECOND;\\n  const scale = op.balance.vitalsDrain;\\n  const diff = op.difficulty === 'intern' ? 0.6 : op.difficulty === 'attending' ? 1.3 : 1;\\n  for (const patient of op.patients) {\\n    if (!patient.alive) continue;\\n    const shielded = op.seats.some((seat) => seat.giftKind === 'pulse' && seat.giftLeft > 0);\",\"content_concise\":\"120→\\n/** Count a missed beat so a lock cannot sit forever. */\\nfunction tickLocks(op: Op): void {\\n  for (const seat of op.seats) {\\n    if (seat.lock < 0) continue;\\n    if (op.tick > seat.lockBeat + 12) {\\n      seat.lock += 1;\\n      seat.lockBeat = op.tick + 40;\\n      if (seat.lock >= 3) finishLock(op, seat);\\n    }\\n130→  }\\n}\\n\\n/** Both paddles. Inside the green band, the Code lands. */\\nfunction pressPaddle(op: Op, seat: Seat): void {\\n  if (!op.code) return;\\n  if (!codeBand(op)) {\\n    op.code.tries -= 1;\\n    op.code.shocks += 1;\\n    op.events.push({ type: 'shock', text: 'Miss.', seat: seat.id });\\n140→    if (op.code.tries <= 0) {\\n      op.code = null;\\n      failOp(op, 'The line stays flat.');\\n    }\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  const patient = op.patients[op.code.patient];\\n  if (patient) {\\n    patient.vitals = Math.max(patient.vitals, 25);\\n    patient.alive = true;\\n150→  }\\n  op.code = null;\\n  op.codeCleared = true;\\n  op.events.push({ type: 'shock', text: 'Got them.', seat: seat.id });\\n}\\n\\n/** The charge ring is green for a generous slice of each beat-and-a-half. */\\nexport function codeBand(op: Op): boolean {\\n  const at = op.tick % 90;\\n  return at >= 28 && at < 62;\\n160→}\\n\\n/** Bleeds, parasite auras, numb patches, then the flatline check. */\\nexport function stepVitals(op: Op, ft: number): void {\\n  const seconds = ft / FIELD_SECOND;\\n  const scale = op.balance.vitalsDrain;\\n  const diff = op.difficulty === 'intern' ? 0.6 : op.difficulty === 'attending' ? 1.3 : 1;\\n  for (const patient of op.patients) {\\n    if (!patient.alive) continue;\\n    const shielded = op.seats.some((seat) => seat.giftKind === 'pulse' && seat.giftLeft > 0);\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work