plyHands via prevPaddle, which is correct because the simulation spends tries. I still need to verify that prevPaddle initializes properly, survives restore and rewind, and is excluded from the hash so peers do not diverge.\n\nprevPaddle is not in the snapshot or hash. A restore may reset it, causing the next step to diverge from the hand stream. The prior round's live operation only captured the world state, so the body reverted to","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":11205,"output_tokens":2310,"cache_read_input_tokens":35840,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"3f66bc90-752a-494d-a374-af8e4e36aaba"}
