match_count\":8,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/verify-r4.log\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":5,\"content\":\"verify: 94 passed, 0 failed\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/verify-oom.log\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":25,\"content\":\"verify: 83 passed, 11 failed\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/verify-r6.log\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":5,\"content\":\"verify: 95 passed, 0 failed\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/verify-r3.log\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":5,\"content\":\"verify: 93 passed, 0 failed\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/verify-r2.log\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":7,\"content\":\"verify: 92 passed, 1 failed\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/verify.log\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":5,\"content\":\"verify: 98 passed, 0 failed\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/verify-r5.log\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":6,\"content\":\"verify: 90 passed, 1 failed\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/verify-r1.log\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":9,\"content\":\"verify: 91 passed, 3 failed\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"32e40142-5aa8-48cb-b9b8-cf6866493d75"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_951","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"\n\nThe fix uses prevPaddle to edge paddle input. Tests confirm one hold does not drain all tries. The input still sends level every frame, but the simulation now edges it correctly. One hold equals one try, which matches the intended design.\n\nChecking pulseEdges, hands.ts, and hub.ts for double-spend bugs or missed holds. TheThe prior gap appears second test holds the fixed. I need to verify this. paddle before code exists; pressPaddle returns immediately but still updates prevPaddle. Need to verify step ordering and green-band hold behavior.\n\nHolding from flatline does not spend a try. The code starts with two tries, and the paddle stays held without triggering pressPaddle. The prior bug where the player lost on tick 3 is fixed.\n\nThe test runs in the real suite as part of verify. I am investigating whether prevPaddle should be included in the state hash. If it is omitted but still affects outcomes, identical hashes could produce different next states across clients. I need to determine when prevPaddle might diverge.\n\nA hold that begins before code starts does not consume a try. The player must release and press again to shock. This is playable.\n\nprevPaddle updates every step from hand.paddle. It may diverge during restore or rewind if the snapshot omits it. I should check whether seat snapshots include prevPaddle. Lockstep peers rewind together from identical snapshots.\n\nThe bot sets paddle level-high during the entire green window. Edge detection triggers exactly once when codeBand becomes true, so a rising edge at the band start succeeds. If \n\nI suspect a real bugthe player holds both paddles continuously if prevPaddle is omitted from before flatline from snapshots. A restore through the band, the would overwrite it  edge is consumed beforeto missing or undefined, code exists or on the even when all peers first tick of code. were previously synchronized. The code intentionally excludes it from the hash, similar to prevUse and stitchId.\n\nThe fix treats paddle input as a press, not a hold-through. If code exists when the band rises, one miss is spent and the player must release and press again inside the green window. This matches typical defibrillator timing. The test should be confirmed in the verify suite with 98 passes.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-456c4617-531b-4348-9551-afe0b2d3f9d6-12","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function hash|prevUse|snapshot|structuredClone|JSON.stringify","glob":"**/labs/game/**/*.{ts,js}","head_limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-456c4617-531b-4348-9551-afe0b2d3f9d6-13","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/verify.log","limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-456c4617-531b-4348-9551-afe0b2d3f9d6-14","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"spends one Code try|HOLD_OK|paddle","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/sim.log"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-456c4617-531b-4348-9551-afe0b2d3f9d6-15","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function down\\(|function held\\(|pulseEdges|paddle","glob":"**/labs/game/**/*.{ts,js}"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8334,"output_tokens":735,"cache_read_input_tokens":44032,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"35728fd8-45ad-473c-a282-c6f67044cd89"}
