{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_952","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"\n\nChecking that verify.log is current and the test file is what npm run verify executes. The test must honestly drive stepOp. The input path must not reintroduce per-frame presses that bypass prevPaddle. pulseEdges and scene-level held-paddle pulses are harmless because the simulation still edges them correctly.Checking whether prevPaddle is excluded from the hash in hashOp.\n\nChecking whether the network hub's paddle counter could misbehave if the host sends a held level while the simulation only edges. This would be a real defect, not an anti-ratchet objection.\n\nprevPaddle could cause divergent shock outcomes if excluded from the hash. The network path already edge-detects\n\nprevPaddle is excluded paddle state. Now examining from the state hash. All clients derive  hub.ts, pulseEdges,it deterministically and hashOp. from the same hand stream, so they stay synchronized locally. A restore or rewind that omits prevPaddle could double-fire or miss a paddle press.\n\nDouble edge detection is safe. One-frame pulses and held levels both trigger exactly one shock. Now examining hub.ts to confirm the exact paddle sampling logic.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-837d2067-5c89-4edd-a2b2-365dd085a13f-10","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/step.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-837d2067-5c89-4edd-a2b2-365dd085a13f-11","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/input/hands.ts","offset":140,"limit":70}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-837d2067-5c89-4edd-a2b2-365dd085a13f-12","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"prevPaddle|pulseEdges|hashState|function hash","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game","glob":"*.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-837d2067-5c89-4edd-a2b2-365dd085a13f-13","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/verify.log","limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4943,"output_tokens":1617,"cache_read_input_tokens":46976,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"8b8a5ec8-9255-4cc6-93f2-9e1506dd3d30"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-837d2067-5c89-4edd-a2b2-365dd085a13f-10","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file One step of an operation. Hands in, events and a new hash out. The same function serves the bot, the\\n * couch, the attract loop, and the lockstep host.\\n */\\nimport { actAll } from './act';\\nimport { applyHands, fieldDelta, growAway, stepBody, stepVitals } from './body';\\nimport { stepStrains } from './strains';\\nimport type { Hand, Op } from './types';\\nimport { hashOp } from './world';\\n10→\\n/** Advance one sixtieth of a second. `hands` null holds still with the buttons up. */\\nexport function stepOp(op: Op, hands: readonly Hand[] | null): void {\\n  if (op.status !== 'playing') return;\\n  op.events = [];\\n  applyHands(op, hands);\\n  actAll(op);\\n  const ft = fieldDelta(op);\\n  op.field += ft;\\n  stepStrains(op, ft);\\n20→  growAway(op, ft);\\n  stepVitals(op, ft);\\n  stepBody(op, ft);\\n  op.tick += 1;\\n  op.events.push({ type: 'hash', text: hashOp(op) });\\n}\\n\\n/** The latest hash, from the step that just ran. */\\nexport function lastHash(op: Op): string {\\n  const found = op.events.find((event) => event.type === 'hash');\\n30→  return found?.text ?? hashOp(op);\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file One step of an operation. Hands in, events and a new hash out. The same function serves the bot, the\\n * couch, the attract loop, and the lockstep host.\\n */\\nimport { actAll } from './act';\\nimport { applyHands, fieldDelta, growAway, stepBody, stepVitals } from './body';\\nimport { stepStrains } from './strains';\\nimport type { Hand, Op } from './types';\\nimport { hashOp } from './world';\\n10→\\n/** Advance one sixtieth of a second. `hands` null holds still with the buttons up. */\\nexport function stepOp(op: Op, hands: readonly Hand[] | null): void {\\n  if (op.status !== 'playing') return;\\n  op.events = [];\\n  applyHands(op, hands);\\n  actAll(op);\\n  const ft = fieldDelta(op);\\n  op.field += ft;\\n  stepStrains(op, ft);\\n20→  growAway(op, ft);\\n  stepVitals(op, ft);\\n  stepBody(op, ft);\\n  op.tick += 1;\\n  op.events.push({ type: 'hash', text: hashOp(op) });\\n}\\n\\n/** The latest hash, from the step that just ran. */\\nexport function lastHash(op: Op): string {\\n  const found = op.events.find((event) => event.type === 'hash');\\n30→  return found?.text ?? hashOp(op);\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/step.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file One step of an operation. Hands in, events and a new hash out. The same function serves the bot, the\\n * couch, the attract loop, and the lockstep host.\\n */\\nimport { actAll } from './act';\\nimport { applyHands, fieldDelta, growAway, stepBody, stepVitals } from './body';\\nimport { stepStrains } from './strains';\\nimport type { Hand, Op } from './types';\\nimport { hashOp } from './world';\\n\\n/** Advance one sixtieth of a second. `hands` null holds still with the buttons up. */\\nexport function stepOp(op: Op, hands: readonly Hand[] | null): void {\\n  if (op.status !== 'playing') return;\\n  op.events = [];\\n  applyHands(op, hands);\\n  actAll(op);\\n  const ft = fieldDelta(op);\\n  op.field += ft;\\n  stepStrains(op, ft);\\n  growAway(op, ft);\\n  stepVitals(op, ft);\\n  stepBody(op, ft);\\n  op.tick += 1;\\n  op.events.push({ type: 'hash', text: hashOp(op) });\\n}\\n\\n/** The latest hash, from the step that just ran. */\\nexport function lastHash(op: Op): string {\\n  const found = op.events.find((event) => event.type === 'hash');\\n  return found?.text ?? hashOp(op);\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":31}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-837d2067-5c89-4edd-a2b2-365dd085a13f-11","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"140→  if (input.pressed('toolNext')) cursor.tool = (cursor.tool + 1) % 8;\\n  if (input.pressed('toolPrev')) cursor.tool = (cursor.tool + 7) % 8;\\n  for (let tool = 0; tool < 8; tool++) if (input.pressed(`tool${tool + 1}`)) cursor.tool = tool;\\n  if (input.pressed('siteNext')) cursor.site = (cursor.site + 1) % sites;\\n  if (input.pressed('sitePrev')) cursor.site = (cursor.site + sites - 1) % sites;\\n  if (input.held('radial')) cursor.radial = true;\\n  else if (cursor.radial) {\\n    cursor.radial = false;\\n  }\\n}\\n150→\\n/** Hands for the seats in this operation. */\\nexport function readHands(\\n  input: Input,\\n  canvas: HTMLCanvasElement,\\n  camera: CameraPose,\\n  dt: number,\\n  seats: number,\\n  sites: number,\\n  feel: Feel,\\n160→): Hand[] {\\n  if (!sampled) samplePads();\\n  const list = pads();\\n  aimMouse(camera, canvas);\\n  if (!list.length) aimKeys(input, dt, feel, sites);\\n  const hands: Hand[] = [];\\n  for (let seat = 0; seat < seats; seat++) {\\n    const pad = list[seat];\\n    const cursor = cursors[seat];\\n    if (pad) aimPad(seat, pad, dt, feel);\\n170→    const use = (seat === 0 && input.held('use')) || down(pad, 7) || down(pad, 0);\\n    const gift = (seat === 0 && input.held('gift')) || down(pad, 3);\\n    const drop = (seat === 0 && input.held('drop')) || down(pad, 1);\\n    const swap = (seat === 0 && input.held('swap')) || down(pad, 11);\\n    const hint = (seat === 0 && input.held('hint')) || down(pad, 12);\\n    const paddle = down(pad, 6) && down(pad, 7);\\n    const syringe = (seat === 0 && input.pressed('syringe')) || tapped(seat, 2);\\n    if (syringe) cursor.tool = 5;\\n    if (pad && tapped(seat, 14)) cursor.site = (cursor.site + sites - 1) % sites;\\n    if (pad && tapped(seat, 15)) cursor.site = (cursor.site + 1) % sites;\\n180→    hands.push({\\n      x: cursor.x,\\n      z: cursor.z,\\n      tool: cursor.radial ? cursor.radialTool : cursor.tool,\\n      use,\\n      drop,\\n      gift,\\n      paddle: paddle || (seat === 0 && input.held('use') && input.held('radial')),\\n      site: cursor.site,\\n      swap,\\n190→      hint,\\n      radial: cursor.radial,\\n    });\\n  }\\n  return hands;\\n}\\n\\n/** The packed list the scene reads. */\\nexport function packedHands(\\n  input: Input,\\n200→  canvas: HTMLCanvasElement,\\n  camera: CameraPose,\\n  dt: number,\\n  seats: number,\\n  sites: number,\\n  feel: Feel,\\n): number[] {\\n  return packHands(readHands(input, canvas, camera, dt, seats, sites, feel));\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"140→  if (input.pressed('toolNext')) cursor.tool = (cursor.tool + 1) % 8;\\n  if (input.pressed('toolPrev')) cursor.tool = (cursor.tool + 7) % 8;\\n  for (let tool = 0; tool < 8; tool++) if (input.pressed(`tool${tool + 1}`)) cursor.tool = tool;\\n  if (input.pressed('siteNext')) cursor.site = (cursor.site + 1) % sites;\\n  if (input.pressed('sitePrev')) cursor.site = (cursor.site + sites - 1) % sites;\\n  if (input.held('radial')) cursor.radial = true;\\n  else if (cursor.radial) {\\n    cursor.radial = false;\\n  }\\n}\\n150→\\n/** Hands for the seats in this operation. */\\nexport function readHands(\\n  input: Input,\\n  canvas: HTMLCanvasElement,\\n  camera: CameraPose,\\n  dt: number,\\n  seats: number,\\n  sites: number,\\n  feel: Feel,\\n160→): Hand[] {\\n  if (!sampled) samplePads();\\n  const list = pads();\\n  aimMouse(camera, canvas);\\n  if (!list.length) aimKeys(input, dt, feel, sites);\\n  const hands: Hand[] = [];\\n  for (let seat = 0; seat < seats; seat++) {\\n    const pad = list[seat];\\n    const cursor = cursors[seat];\\n    if (pad) aimPad(seat, pad, dt, feel);\\n170→    const use = (seat === 0 && input.held('use')) || down(pad, 7) || down(pad, 0);\\n    const gift = (seat === 0 && input.held('gift')) || down(pad, 3);\\n    const drop = (seat === 0 && input.held('drop')) || down(pad, 1);\\n    const swap = (seat === 0 && input.held('swap')) || down(pad, 11);\\n    const hint = (seat === 0 && input.held('hint')) || down(pad, 12);\\n    const paddle = down(pad, 6) && down(pad, 7);\\n    const syringe = (seat === 0 && input.pressed('syringe')) || tapped(seat, 2);\\n    if (syringe) cursor.tool = 5;\\n    if (pad && tapped(seat, 14)) cursor.site = (cursor.site + sites - 1) % sites;\\n    if (pad && tapped(seat, 15)) cursor.site = (cursor.site + 1) % sites;\\n180→    hands.push({\\n      x: cursor.x,\\n      z: cursor.z,\\n      tool: cursor.radial ? cursor.radialTool : cursor.tool,\\n      use,\\n      drop,\\n      gift,\\n      paddle: paddle || (seat === 0 && input.held('use') && input.held('radial')),\\n      site: cursor.site,\\n      swap,\\n190→      hint,\\n      radial: cursor.radial,\\n    });\\n  }\\n  return hands;\\n}\\n\\n/** The packed list the scene reads. */\\nexport function packedHands(\\n  input: Input,\\n200→  canvas: HTMLCanvasElement,\\n  camera: CameraPose,\\n  dt: number,\\n  seats: number,\\n  sites: number,\\n  feel: Feel,\\n): number[] {\\n  return packHands(readHands(input, canvas, camera, dt, seats, sites, feel));\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/input/hands.ts\",\"offset\":140,\"limit\":70,\"raw_output\":\"  if (input.pressed('toolNext')) cursor.tool = (cursor.tool + 1) % 8;\\n  if (input.pressed('toolPrev')) cursor.tool = (cursor.tool + 7) % 8;\\n  for (let tool = 0; tool < 8; tool++) if (input.pressed(`tool${tool + 1}`)) cursor.tool = tool;\\n  if (input.pressed('siteNext')) cursor.site = (cursor.site + 1) % sites;\\n  if (input.pressed('sitePrev')) cursor.site = (cursor.site + sites - 1) % sites;\\n  if (input.held('radial')) cursor.radial = true;\\n  else if (cursor.radial) {\\n    cursor.radial = false;\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** Hands for the seats in this operation. */\\nexport function readHands(\\n  input: Input,\\n  canvas: HTMLCanvasElement,\\n  camera: CameraPose,\\n  dt: number,\\n  seats: number,\\n  sites: number,\\n  feel: Feel,\\n): Hand[] {\\n  if (!sampled) samplePads();\\n  const list = pads();\\n  aimMouse(camera, canvas);\\n  if (!list.length) aimKeys(input, dt, feel, sites);\\n  const hands: Hand[] = [];\\n  for (let seat = 0; seat < seats; seat++) {\\n    const pad = list[seat];\\n    const cursor = cursors[seat];\\n    if (pad) aimPad(seat, pad, dt, feel);\\n    const use = (seat === 0 && input.held('use')) || down(pad, 7) || down(pad, 0);\\n    const gift = (seat === 0 && input.held('gift')) || down(pad, 3);\\n    const drop = (seat === 0 && input.held('drop')) || down(pad, 1);\\n    const swap = (seat === 0 && input.held('swap')) || down(pad, 11);\\n    const hint = (seat === 0 && input.held('hint')) || down(pad, 12);\\n    const paddle = down(pad, 6) && down(pad, 7);\\n    const syringe = (seat === 0 && input.pressed('syringe')) || tapped(seat, 2);\\n    if (syringe) cursor.tool = 5;\\n    if (pad && tapped(seat, 14)) cursor.site = (cursor.site + sites - 1) % sites;\\n    if (pad && tapped(seat, 15)) cursor.site = (cursor.site + 1) % sites;\\n    hands.push({\\n      x: cursor.x,\\n      z: cursor.z,\\n      tool: cursor.radial ? cursor.radialTool : cursor.tool,\\n      use,\\n      drop,\\n      gift,\\n      paddle: paddle || (seat === 0 && input.held('use') && input.held('radial')),\\n      site: cursor.site,\\n      swap,\\n      hint,\\n      radial: cursor.radial,\\n    });\\n  }\\n  return hands;\\n}\\n\\n/** The packed list the scene reads. */\\nexport function packedHands(\\n  input: Input,\\n  canvas: HTMLCanvasElement,\\n  camera: CameraPose,\\n  dt: number,\\n  seats: number,\\n  sites: number,\\n  feel: Feel,\\n): number[] {\\n  return packHands(readHands(input, canvas, camera, dt, seats, sites, feel));\\n}\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":264}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-837d2067-5c89-4edd-a2b2-365dd085a13f-12","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,