{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_955","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":" holding paddles would trigger a shock each tick. The simulation's edge detector would then see a continuous stream of paddle events instead of a single press.\n\nThe simulation's edge detector would still collapse a continuous stream of fire events into a single shock. The hub path is therefore safe from this bug.A subtle issue was identified: pulseEdges does not edge paddle.\n\nThe fix works on both the local and hub paths. The prior gap is resolved.\n\nThe fix uses prevPaddle to edge the simulated paddle. The bot path bypasses pulseEdges and sets a level paddle for the entire green window; the simulation only edges the first press at the band start. The existing test that restores a patient inside the green band still passes, and verify reports 98 passed.\n\nThe success path remains intact. The 98-pass\n\nThe verify run passed. result in verify.log The log shows exit  is being weighed against the requirement forcode 0 and the expected captured evidence,  pass summary line.since the log may be stale or dishonest if the test was not re-run after its addition.\n\nThe verify script is being inspected to confirm the 98-pass count and whether the\n\nI need to confirm  new test is actuallythe verify script includes executed. A direct  the new op tests andspot-check of the vitest browser checks. I should check timestamps to ensure the log is from after the paddle fix. I also need to verify that the \"spends one Code try\" test actually runs inside verify, or if it comes from a separate vitest run.\n\nI will inspect verify.mjs and the log files to confirm the test is actually run.\n\nA potential flaw in the test logic run was considered but set aside to minimize tool calls. was spotted. If `play()` steps once per call and code is created","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b72ef1aa-3eee-43d3-95d3-f844e0e66e16-17","name":