{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_967","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"An important finding about `take` has been identified.\n\n`take()` advances the counter by only one per tick. If a player holds the paddle for multiple frames, the host misses intermediate counts and falls behind.\n\nThe simulation's `prevPaddle` edge prevents duplicate presses during a hold. The hub path also limits paddle input to one attempt per hold. The only remaining risk is that something resets `prevPaddle` between ticks.\n\n`prevPaddle` stays true while the hand stream holds paddle. Extra queued fires during catch-up are harmless because `prevPaddle` blocks them. The flag clears once the stream stops.\n\nConsecutive true values still produce a single rising edge. The counter increments per frame, while the host consumes one tick at a time. A long hold therefore leaves many counts queued. After release, those extra ticks fire continuously until the host catches up. `prevPaddle` remains true during this catch-up, so only one shock occurs.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3e23b0ef-db0b-4dcf-b939-fccde6738183-28","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/tools/verify.mjs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3e23b0ef-db0b-4dcf-b939-fccde6738183-29","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/ux.log"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3e23b0ef-db0b-4dcf-b939-fccde6738183-30","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/nowebgpu.log"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3e23b0ef-db0b-4dcf-b939-fccde6738183-31","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/hub.log","limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4498,"output_tokens":982,"cache_read_input_tokens":66560,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"914aaa5e-3c96-43c9-b116-c0c52f6507b9"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-3e23b0ef-db0b-4dcf-b939-fccde6738183-28","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The one command, `npm run verify`: runs every check quietly and prints only the failures, then one line with\\n * the count. `--fast` skips what needs a browser. It sets its own short TMPDIR and CHROMIUM_PATH, so it needs no setup,\\n * and removes the temporary folder when done. Exit 0 when nothing failed.\\n */\\nimport { spawnSync } from 'node:child_process';\\nimport { existsSync, globSync, mkdtempSync, readFileSync, rmSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport { homedir } from 'node:os';\\n\\n10→const fast = process.argv.includes('--fast');\\nconst tmp = mkdtempSync('/tmp/g.');\\nconst chrome = globSync(`${homedir()}/.cache/ms-playwright/chromium-*/chrome-linux64/chrome`)[0];\\nconst env = { ...process.env, TMPDIR: tmp, CHROMIUM_PATH: process.env.CHROMIUM_PATH ?? chrome };\\nconst run = (command, ...args) => spawnSync(command, args, { env, encoding: 'utf8', maxBuffer: 2 ** 28 });\\n\\nlet passed = 0;\\nconst failed = [];\\nconst note = (name, ok, detail = '') => (ok ? (passed += 1) : failed.push(`${name}${detail ? `: ${detail}` : ''}`));\\nconst tail = (result) => `${result.stdout}${result.stderr}`.trim().split('\\\\n').slice(-6).join(' | ').slice(0, 600);\\n20→\\n/** A step whose exit status is its verdict. */\\nconst step = (name, command, ...args) => {\\n  const result = run(command, ...args);\\n  note(name, result.status === 0, tail(result));\\n};\\n\\n/** Vitest, counted test by test from the JSON report npm test writes. */\\nfunction tests() {\\n  const report = 'out/test/report.json';\\n30→  rmSync(report, { force: true });\\n  const result = run('npm', 'test', '--silent');\\n  if (!existsSync(report)) return note('npm test', false, tail(result));\\n  for (const file of JSON.parse(readFileSync(report, 'utf8')).testResults) {\\n    for (const test of file.assertionResults) {\\n      note(\\n        test.fullName,\\n        test.status === 'passed',\\n        String(test.failureMessages?.[0] ?? '')\\n          .split('\\\\n')[0]\\n40→          .slice(0, 300),\\n      );\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** A browser tool: it prints one JSON line per check, { name, ok, detail }. Add e2e and hub runs here. */\\nfunction browserTool(path) {\\n  const result = run('node', path);\\n  const lines = result.stdout.split('\\\\n').filter((line) => line.startsWith('{'));\\n50→  for (const line of lines) {\\n    const { name, ok, detail } = JSON.parse(line);\\n    note(name, ok, detail);\\n  }\\n  if (result.status !== 0 || lines.length === 0) note(path, false, tail(result));\\n}\\n\\nstep('npm run check', 'npm', 'run', '--silent', 'check');\\ntests();\\nif (!fast) {\\n60→  step('replays in Chromium', 'node', 'x', 'replay', 'labs/game/replays', '--browser', 'sim');\\n  for (const path of ['labs/game/tools/e2e.mjs', 'labs/game/tools/hub.mjs']) if (existsSync(path)) browserTool(path);\\n}\\nrmSync(tmp, { recursive: true, force: true });\\nfor (const failure of failed) console.log(`FAIL ${failure}`);\\nconsole.log(`verify: ${passed} passed, ${failed.length} failed`);\\nprocess.exit(failed.length ? 1 : 0);\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * @file The one command, `npm run verify`: runs every check quietly and prints only the failures, then one line with\\n * the count. `--fast` skips what needs a browser. It sets its own short TMPDIR and CHROMIUM_PATH, so it needs no setup,\\n * and removes the temporary folder when done. Exit 0 when nothing failed.\\n */\\nimport { spawnSync } from 'node:child_process';\\nimport { existsSync, globSync, mkdtempSync, readFileSync, rmSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport { homedir } from 'node:os';\\n\\n10→const fast = process.argv.includes('--fast');\\nconst tmp = mkdtempSync('/tmp/g.');\\nconst chrome = globSync(`${homedir()}/.cache/ms-playwright/chromium-*/chrome-linux64/chrome`)[0];\\nconst env = { ...process.env, TMPDIR: tmp, CHROMIUM_PATH: process.env.CHROMIUM_PATH ?? chrome };\\nconst run = (command, ...args) => spawnSync(command, args, { env, encoding: 'utf8', maxBuffer: 2 ** 28 });\\n\\nlet passed = 0;\\nconst failed = [];\\nconst note = (name, ok, detail = '') => (ok ? (passed += 1) : failed.push(`${name}${detail ? `: ${detail}` : ''}`));\\nconst tail = (result) => `${result.stdout}${result.stderr}`.trim().split('\\\\n').slice(-6).join(' | ').slice(0, 600);\\n20→\\n/** A step whose exit status is its verdict. */\\nconst step = (name, command, ...args) => {\\n  const result = run(command, ...args);\\n  note(name, result.status === 0, tail(result));\\n};\\n\\n/** Vitest, counted test by test from the JSON report npm test writes. */\\nfunction tests() {\\n  const report = 'out/test/report.json';\\n30→  rmSync(report, { force: true });\\n  const result = run('npm', 'test', '--silent');\\n  if (!existsSync(report)) return note('npm test', false, tail(result));\\n  for (const file of JSON.parse(readFileSync(report, 'utf8')).testResults) {\\n    for (const test of file.assertionResults) {\\n      note(\\n        test.fullName,\\n        test.status === 'passed',\\n        String(test.failureMessages?.[0] ?? '')\\n          .split('\\\\n')[0]\\n40→          .slice(0, 300),\\n      );\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** A browser tool: it prints one JSON line per check, { name, ok, detail }. Add e2e and hub runs here. */\\nfunction browserTool(path) {\\n  const result = run('node', path);\\n  const lines = result.stdout.split('\\\\n').filter((line) => line.startsWith('{'));\\n50→  for (const line of lines) {\\n    const { name, ok, detail } = JSON.parse(line);\\n    note(name, ok, detail);\\n  }\\n  if (result.status !== 0 || lines.length === 0) note(path, false, tail(result));\\n}\\n\\nstep('npm run check', 'npm', 'run', '--silent', 'check');\\ntests();\\nif (!fast) {\\n60→  step('replays in Chromium', 'node', 'x', 'replay', 'labs/game/replays', '--browser', 'sim');\\n  for (const path of ['labs/game/tools/e2e.mjs', 'labs/game/tools/hub.mjs']) if (existsSync(path)) browserTool(path);\\n}\\nrmSync(tmp, { recursive: true, force: true });\\nfor (const failure of failed) console.log(`FAIL ${failure}`);\\nconsole.log(`verify: ${passed} passed, ${failed.length} failed`);\\nprocess.exit(failed.length ? 1 : 0);\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/tools/verify.mjs\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * @file The one command, `npm run verify`: runs every check quietly and prints only the failures, then one line with\\n * the count. `--fast` skips what needs a browser. It sets its own short TMPDIR and CHROMIUM_PATH, so it needs no setup,\\n * and removes the temporary folder when done. Exit 0 when nothing failed.\\n */\\nimport { spawnSync } from 'node:child_process';\\nimport { existsSync, globSync, mkdtempSync, readFileSync, rmSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport { homedir } from 'node:os';\\n\\nconst fast = process.argv.includes('--fast');\\nconst tmp = mkdtempSync('/tmp/g.');\\nconst chrome = globSync(`${homedir()}/.cache/ms-playwright/chromium-*/chrome-linux64/chrome`)[0];\\nconst env = { ...process.env, TMPDIR: tmp, CHROMIUM_PATH: process.env.CHROMIUM_PATH ?? chrome };\\nconst run = (command, ...args) => spawnSync(command, args, { env, encoding: 'utf8', maxBuffer: 2 ** 28 });\\n\\nlet passed = 0;\\nconst failed = [];\\nconst note = (name, ok, detail = '') => (ok ? (passed += 1) : failed.push(`${name}${detail ? `: ${detail}` : ''}`));\\nconst tail = (result) => `${result.stdout}${result.stderr}`.trim().split('\\\\n').slice(-6).join(' | ').slice(0, 600);\\n\\n/** A step whose exit status is its verdict. */\\nconst step = (name, command, ...args) => {\\n  const result = run(command, ...args);\\n  note(name, result.status === 0, tail(result));\\n};\\n\\n/** Vitest, counted test by test from the JSON report npm test writes. */\\nfunction tests() {\\n  const report = 'out/test/report.json';\\n  rmSync(report, { force: true });\\n  const result = run('npm', 'test', '--silent');\\n  if (!existsSync(report)) return note('npm test', false, tail(result));\\n  for (const file of JSON.parse(readFileSync(report, 'utf8')).testResults) {\\n    for (const test of file.assertionResults) {\\n      note(\\n        test.fullName,\\n        test.status === 'passed',\\n        String(test.failureMessages?.[0] ?? '')\\n          .split('\\\\n')[0]\\n          .slice(0, 300),\\n      );\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** A browser tool: it prints one JSON line per check, { name, ok, detail }. Add e2e and hub runs here. */\\nfunction browserTool(path) {\\n  const result = run('node', path);\\n  const lines = result.stdout.split('\\\\n').filter((line) => line.startsWith('{'));\\n  for (const line of lines) {\\n    const { name, ok, detail } = JSON.parse(line);\\n    note(name, ok, detail);\\n  }\\n  if (result.status !== 0 || lines.length === 0) note(path, false, tail(result));\\n}\\n\\nstep('npm run check', 'npm', 'run', '--silent', 'check');\\ntests();\\nif (!fast) {\\n  step('replays in Chromium', 'node', 'x', 'replay', 'labs/game/replays', '--browser', 'sim');\\n  for (const path of ['labs/game/tools/e2e.mjs', 'labs/game/tools/hub.mjs']) if (existsSync(path)) browserTool(path);\\n}\\nrmSync(tmp, { recursive: true, force: true });\\nfor (const failure of failed) console.log(`FAIL ${failure}`);\\nconsole.log(`verify: ${passed} passed, ${failed.length} failed`);\\nprocess.exit(failed.length ? 1 : 0);\\n\",\"total_lines\":66}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-3e23b0ef-db0b-4dcf-b939-fccde6738183-29","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→{\\\"name\\\":\\\"no audio element\\\",\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"detail\\\":\\\"\\\"}\\n{\\\"name\\\":\\\"session client is first\\\",\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"detail\\\":\\\"\\\"}\\n{\\\"name\\\":\\\"boots from