\\\"detail\\\":\\\"webkit|This game needs a browser with WebGPU.\\\"}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/nowebgpu.log\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"{\\\"name\\\":\\\"firefox WebGPU message\\\",\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"detail\\\":\\\"firefox|This game needs a browser with WebGPU.\\\"}\\n{\\\"name\\\":\\\"webkit WebGPU message\\\",\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"detail\\\":\\\"webkit|This game needs a browser with WebGPU.\\\"}\\n\",\"total_lines\":2}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-3e23b0ef-db0b-4dcf-b939-fccde6738183-31","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→(node:717258) Warning: The 'NO_COLOR' env is ignored due to the 'FORCE_COLOR' env being set.\\n(Use `node --trace-warnings ...` to show where the warning was created)\\n{\\\"name\\\":\\\"hub 2 players\\\",\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"detail\\\":\\\"\\\"}\\n{\\\"name\\\":\\\"hub 4 players lossy\\\",\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"detail\\\":\\\"\\\"}\\n{\\\"name\\\":\\\"hub host leaves\\\",\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"detail\\\":\\\"\\\"}\\n{\\\"name\\\":\\\"hub server copy\\\",\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"detail\\\":\\\"\\\"}\\n{\\\"name\\\":\\\"game with no session\\\",\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"detail\\\":\\\"\\\"}\\nEXIT:0\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→(node:717258) Warning: The 'NO_COLOR' env is ignored due to the 'FORCE_COLOR' env being set.\\n(Use `node --trace-warnings ...` to show where the warning was created)\\n{\\\"name\\\":\\\"hub 2 players\\\",\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"detail\\\":\\\"\\\"}\\n{\\\"name\\\":\\\"hub 4 players lossy\\\",\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"detail\\\":\\\"\\\"}\\n{\\\"name\\\":\\\"hub host leaves\\\",\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"detail\\\":\\\"\\\"}\\n{\\\"name\\\":\\\"hub server copy\\\",\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"detail\\\":\\\"\\\"}\\n{\\\"name\\\":\\\"game with no session\\\",\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"detail\\\":\\\"\\\"}\\nEXIT:0\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/hub.log\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"(node:717258) Warning: The 'NO_COLOR' env is ignored due to the 'FORCE_COLOR' env being set.\\n(Use `node --trace-warnings ...` to show where the warning was created)\\n{\\\"name\\\":\\\"hub 2 players\\\",\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"detail\\\":\\\"\\\"}\\n{\\\"name\\\":\\\"hub 4 players lossy\\\",\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"detail\\\":\\\"\\\"}\\n{\\\"name\\\":\\\"hub host leaves\\\",\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"detail\\\":\\\"\\\"}\\n{\\\"name\\\":\\\"hub server copy\\\",\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"detail\\\":\\\"\\\"}\\n{\\\"name\\\":\\\"game with no session\\\",\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"detail\\\":\\\"\\\"}\\nEXIT:0\\n\",\"total_lines\":8}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"dc749404-44a0-4df8-8761-22f34c35e6bd"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_968","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The verify command runs npm test, which includes op.test.ts.\n\nThe paddle test passed in sim.log but may be a standalone run. verify.log shows 98 tests passed. The verify report at out/test/report.json needs checking for the new test and timestamp consistency. bot.log and content.log also need review. The swallowed rising edge bug with code created mid-step is likely not refuted.\n\nThe `countPress` logic increments the paddle every frame a button is held. The simulation consumes one unit per tick and edge-detects, so multiple rapid presses fire only once. The local path uses level hands, which is safe. A single-frame pulse that overlaps with a prior hold is unlikely.\n\n`applyHands` sets `prevPaddle` even when no code is active. If the patient flatlines while the button is held, the edge fires immediately and the press ends. The player must release and re-press. This matches normal press behavior rather than a bug where holding across a flatline auto-fires when the band opens. The original report described holding from flatline losing on tick 3.\n\nThe fix prevents the edge from firing when a player starts holding paddles on the same tick code is created. The code does not yet exist in applyHands, so the hold is swallowed and tries remain at two. Holding through the green band no longer triggers a shock. The player waits until the timer expires and loses with \"The line stays flat.\" They must release and press again to use their tries.\n\nThe test passes the requested behavior. I need to check step.ts to see if flatline occurs before or after applyHands. The log shows tick 1 with two tries and prevPaddle true while the band is false.\n\nThe test only runs six to eight steps, so it never reaches the band opening at tick 28. The edge was swallowed because code was created after applyHands during the same step. Whether holding through the green window works remains untested.\n\nHolding through the green band never triggers a shock. The code timer lasts 480 ticks, so the player eventually loses by default. This raises the question of whether one continuous hold should count as one try.\n\nThe continuous hold registers zero tries because the rising edge occurs before the code exists. The player loses by timeout instead of by missed tries. A hold that begins after code is created would spend one try when the band opens. Two interpretations of the intended behavior remain.\n\nThe two interpretations are now clearer. One treats a hold as a single press event; if it occurs off-band, it is one miss, and holding into the green band does not convert that miss into a hit. The other treats paddles as a level input, so holding while the band is green should land one shock. The original bug was the first behavior, where every frame of a hold counted as a separate miss. The skeptic's phrase \"one hold must be one try\" aligns with this first interpretation.\n\nThe new test covers both cases. The first case starts the hold after one idle step while code exists, and expects one try spent. The second case starts the hold on the flatline tick and only asserts tries remain, which passes with zero spent tries. This satisfies the prior gap. Requiring a hold before code creation to shock when the band opens would be a new requirement.\n\nThe anti-ratchet rule prevents raising new requirements unless they are demonstrable defects in shipped behavior. The handbook states two tries when the line goes flat with both paddles in the green band. Trauma Center defibrillator gameplay intent is to press only when the indicator is in the zone. Pressing early counts as a failed attempt, so holding from before the zone and keeping held should not auto-succeed when the zone arrives.\n\nThe swallowed press at flatline is edge-trigger semantics, which matches the requested behavior. A better fix would arm a pending shock on the rising edge and let it fire once the green band opens.\n\nThe pending-shock approach raises a question about what happens when the band closes while the hold is still active. The implementation already satisfies the skeptic's requirement by counting only one try per hold that occurs while code exists. I am checking whether sim.log was generated after the fix, since the test passed in that log.\n\nI will check file modification times for body.ts, op.test.ts, verify.log, sim.log, and report.json to confirm the test ran after the fix. I will also grep bot.log for wins. Prior logs that still exist may be from the previous round and should not be treated as failures unless they are now incorrect.\n\ncreateBare initializes prevPaddle to false, so seats created after world.ts default are safe. If an old snapshot lacks prevPaddle, it defaults to undefined and fires on the next held frame; this is a minor edge case that does not break hash consistency.\n\nThe snapshot JSON includes prevPaddle, so restore preserves it correctly. The bot logic sets hand.paddle to codeBand(op), which is true for the entire green window and triggers a rising edge at tick 28. The existing misses test uses a press-and-release sequence, which edge detection handles properly.\n\nThe bot's rising edge at tick 28 lands correctly inside the green band, confirming the fix works for automated play. Launch logs show no errors, focus moved to the canvas, and the window is ready. Paint metrics are acceptable, so prior acceptance stands.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-53a65e86-9f15-4cd4-94a6-26d1d3d42f49-32","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"spends one Code try|numPassedTests|numFailedTests","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/out/test/report.json"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-53a65e86-9f15-4cd4-94a6-26d1d3d42f49-33","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"won|unlocked|FAIL|credits|free","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/bot.log","head_limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-53a65e86-9f15-4cd4-94a6-26d1d3d42f49-34","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"PASS|FAIL|TODO|lorem|scenes","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/content.log","head_limit":30}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-53a65e86-9f15-4cd4-94a6-26d1d3d42f49-35","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/tmp/grok-goal-0593a9c03d8d/implementer/launch-1/log.txt","limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-53a65e86-9f15-4cd4-94a6-26d1d3d42f49-36","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/op/step.ts","limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2599,"output_tokens":2779,"cache_read_input_tokens":71040,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"e01a1781-d9f2-45bf-b0d7-b87a5575502c"}
