"format\\\": \\\"prettier --write --cache .\\\",\\n    \\\"check\\\": \\\"node tools/checkAll.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"test\\\": \\\"vitest run\\\",\\n    \\\"verify\\\": \\\"node labs/game/tools/verify.mjs\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"dependencies\\\": {\\n    \\\"@dimforge/rapier3d-simd-compat\\\": \\\"0.21.0\\\",\\n    \\\"@stdlib/math-base-special-cos\\\": \\\"0.3.1\\\",\\n    \\\"@stdlib/math-base-special-pow\\\": \\\"0.3.1\\\",\\n    \\\"@stdlib/math-base-special-sin\\\": \\\"0.3.1\\\",\\n    \\\"three\\\": \\\"0.182.0\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"devDependencies\\\": {\\n    \\\"@modelcontextprotocol/sdk\\\": \\\"1.32.2\\\",\\n    \\\"@playwright/test\\\": \\\"1.64.1\\\",\\n    \\\"@stryker-mutator/core\\\": \\\"9.6.1\\\",\\n    \\\"@stryker-mutator/vitest-runner\\\": \\\"9.6.1\\\",\\n    \\\"@types/node\\\": \\\"24.19.2\\\",\\n    \\\"@types/three\\\": \\\"0.182.0\\\",\\n    \\\"eslint\\\": \\\"9.39.5\\\",\\n    \\\"eslint-plugin-jsdoc\\\": \\\"61.7.1\\\",\\n    \\\"globals\\\": \\\"16.5.0\\\",\\n    \\\"prettier\\\": \\\"3.9.10\\\",\\n    \\\"tsx\\\": \\\"4.23.15\\\",\\n    \\\"typescript\\\": \\\"5.9.3\\\",\\n    \\\"typescript-eslint\\\": \\\"8.72.1\\\",\\n    \\\"vite\\\": \\\"7.3.7\\\",\\n    \\\"vitest\\\": \\\"4.1.12\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"allowScripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"esbuild\\\": false\\n  }\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":47}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-742151bc-68d2-440a-83a9-fa6e1c77cc35-8","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→# Trauma Compass\\n\\nA lamp-lit night at Harbor Light General. Eight operations, up to four surgeons at one table, and a patient who has to last until the last stitch. The camera sits close overhead on the field. It is a surgical simulation, original to this project, for one player or a couch of four, and for an AI Hub room of up to four.\\n\\n## Play\\n\\nStick or mouse aims. R2 or the left click uses the tool. The right stick, or the keys 1–8, picks a tool. Shoulder buttons cycle tools. Space or Triangle is the Gift. F or Square is the syringe. R or Circle drops or cancels. Q and E, or the d-pad left and right, change site. H asks for a hint. Tab swaps a tool with the other seat.\\n\\nEnter or Cross accepts a menu row. Hover moves the highlight. Esc or Options pauses. On a touch-only device the page says \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" and offers Settings. Attract mode starts after ten seconds idle on a menu and saves nothing.\\n10→\\nMusic starts at 10%. Songs, effects, and the syllable voices are written in code. There are no audio files.\\n\\n## With a friend\\n\\nScrub In, on the title, gives each pad a seat. Cross claims the seat. Start begins the next operation with that many hands. The same screen is the couch game: one camera, no network. An AI Hub room uses the shared-world session client pasted in the page. The host steps the operation. Everyone else plays the host's hands. The session case is the gala shift.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n| File | What it is |\\n20→| --- | --- |\\n| labs/game/op/ | The operation, with no engine import: tools, vitals, strains, the bot, the lockstep |\\n| labs/game/scenes/main.ts | The scene `game:main`. The starter `game:play` stays |\\n| labs/game/app/boot.ts | The page: screens, hub, audio, the sheet |\\n| labs/game/index.html | Source page. The hub client is the first script, byte for byte |\\n| labs/game/tools/verify.mjs | `npm run verify` |\\n| labs/game/tools/e2e.mjs | The browser checks against the one-file page |\\n| labs/game/tools/hub.mjs | The four AI Hub harness runs |\\n| labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md | Issues the tests caught |\\n| ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md | What the engine did not provide. Local patches: none |\\n30→\\n## See it\\n\\nOpen the one-file page in the work folder beside this project, from `file://`, in a browser with WebGPU. Firefox and WebKit show the plain WebGPU message.\\n\\n```sh\\nnpm test\\nnpm run check\\nnpm run verify          # check, tests, replays, e2e, hub. --fast skips the browsers\\nnode x replay labs/game/replays --browser sim\\n40→```\\n\\n`?game.autoplay=1` walks the shift: the bot plays each operation at eight times speed.\\n\\n## Decisions\\n\\n- 2026-11-04: The title is Trauma Compass. The operation stays a pure module. The engine is read-only. The sheet is 96 by 60 so four software-rendered copies fit in memory. Radial time is a fixed 0.6 while the menu is open, because that slider cannot enter the sim.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→# Trauma Compass\\n\\nA lamp-lit night at Harbor Light General. Eight operations, up to four surgeons at one table, and a patient who has to last until the last stitch. The camera sits close overhead on the field. It is a surgical simulation, original to this project, for one player or a couch of four, and for an AI Hub room of up to four.\\n\\n## Play\\n\\nStick or mouse aims. R2 or the left click uses the tool. The right stick, or the keys 1–8, picks a tool. Shoulder buttons cycle tools. Space or Triangle is the Gift. F or Square is the syringe. R or Circle drops or cancels. Q and E, or the d-pad left and right, change site. H asks for a hint. Tab swaps a tool with the other seat.\\n\\nEnter or Cross accepts a menu row. Hover moves the highlight. Esc or Options pauses. On a touch-only device the page says \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" and offers Settings. Attract mode starts after ten seconds idle on a menu and saves nothing.\\n10→\\nMusic starts at 10%. Songs, effects, and the syllable voices are written in code. There are no audio files.\\n\\n## With a friend\\n\\nScrub In, on the title, gives each pad a seat. Cross claims the seat. Start begins the next operation with that many hands. The same screen is the couch game: one camera, no network. An AI Hub room uses the shared-world session client pasted in the page. The host steps the operation. Everyone else plays the host's hands. The session case is the gala shift.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n| File | What it is |\\n20→| --- | --- |\\n| labs/game/op/ | The operation, with no engine import: tools, vitals, strains, the bot, the lockstep |\\n| labs/game/scenes/main.ts | The scene `game:main`. The starter `game:play` stays |\\n| labs/game/app/boot.ts | The page: screens, hub, audio, the sheet |\\n| labs/game/index.html | Source page. The hub client is the first script, byte for byte |\\n| labs/game/tools/verify.mjs | `npm run verify` |\\n| labs/game/tools/e2e.mjs | The browser checks against the one-file page |\\n| labs/game/tools/hub.mjs | The four AI Hub harness runs |\\n| labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md | Issues the tests caught |\\n| ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md | What the engine did not provide. Local patches: none |\\n30→\\n## See it\\n\\nOpen the one-file page in the work folder beside this project, from `file://`, in a browser with WebGPU. Firefox and WebKit show the plain WebGPU message.\\n\\n```sh\\nnpm test\\nnpm run check\\nnpm run verify          # check, tests, replays, e2e, hub. --fast skips the browsers\\nnode x replay labs/game/replays --browser sim\\n40→```\\n\\n`?game.autoplay=1` walks the shift: the bot plays each operation at eight times speed.\\n\\n## Decisions\\n\\n- 2026-11-04: The title is Trauma Compass. The operation stays a pure module. The engine is read-only. The sheet is 96 by 60 so four software-rendered copies fit in memory. Radial time is a fixed 0.6 while the menu is open, because that slider cannot enter the sim.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731/labs/game/README.md\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":100,\"raw_output\":\"# Trauma Compass\\n\\nA lamp-lit night at Harbor Light General. Eight operations, up to four surgeons at one table, and a patient who has to last until the last stitch. The camera sits close overhead on the field. It is a surgical simulation, original to this project, for one player or a couch of four, and for an AI Hub room of up to four.\\n\\n## Play\\n\\nStick or mouse aims. R2 or the left click uses the tool. The right stick, or the keys 1–8, picks a tool. Shoulder buttons cycle tools. Space or Triangle is the Gift. F or Square is the syringe. R or Circle drops or cancels. Q and E, or the d-pad left and right, change site. H asks for a hint. Tab swaps a tool with the other seat.\\n\\nEnter or Cross accepts a menu row. Hover moves the highlight. Esc or Options pauses. On a touch-only device the page says \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" and offers Settings. Attract mode starts after ten seconds idle on a menu and saves nothing.\\n\\nMusic starts at 10%. Songs, effects, and the syllable voices are written in code. There are no audio files.\\n\\n## With a friend\\n\\nScrub In, on the title, gives each pad a seat. Cross claims the seat. Start begins the next operation with that many hands. The same screen is the couch game: one camera, no network. An AI Hub room uses the shared-world session client pasted in the page. The host steps the operation. Everyone else plays the host's hands. The session case is the gala shift.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n| File | What it is |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| labs/game/op/ | The operation, with no engine import: tools, vitals, strains, the bot, the lockstep |\\n| labs/game/scenes/main.ts | The scene `game:main`. The starter `game:play` stays |\\n| labs/game/app/boot.ts | The page: screens, hub, audio, the sheet |\\n| labs/game/index.html | Source page. The hub client is the first script, byte for byte |\\n| labs/game/tools/verify.mjs | `npm run verify` |\\n| labs/game/tools/e2e.mjs | The browser checks against the one-file page |\\n| labs/game/tools/hub.mjs | The four AI Hub harness runs |\\n| labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md | Issues the tests caught |\\n| ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md | What the engine did not provide. Local patches: none |\\n\\n## See it\\n\\nOpen the one-file page in the work folder beside this project, from `file://`, in a browser with WebGPU. Firefox and WebKit show the plain WebGPU message.\\n\\n```sh\\nnpm test\\nnpm run check\\nnpm run verify          # check, tests, replays, e2e, hub. --fast skips the browsers\\nnode x replay labs/game/replays --browser sim\\n```\\n\\n`?game.autoplay=1` walks the shift: the bot plays each operation at eight times speed.\\n\\n## Decisions\\n\\n- 2026-11-04: The title is Trauma Compass. The operation stays a pure module. The engine is read-only. The sheet is 96 by 60 so four software-rendered copies fit in memory. Radial time is a fixed 0.6 while the menu is open, because that slider cannot enter the sim.\\n\",\"total_lines\":46}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-742151bc-68d2-440a-83a9-fa6e1c77cc35-9","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→# Trauma Compass\\n\\nSurgical simulation at Harbor Light General. The one-file page is `Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731.html` beside this note. The dev project is the folder of the same name.\\n\\n## Done\\n\\n- Title chosen with a real RNG: Trauma Compass.\\n- Operation sim, bot, strains, campaign, and lockstep tests are green. The bot wins every required case and seed.\\n- The shipped page boots from `file://` in Chromium with WebGPU. Two launches both reached the title, a filled 1280×720 view, and a key moved the menu. The session client is the first script and matches the vendor file. Usage reads `added on import`, and the Usage card is marked `data-about=\\\"usage\\\"`.\\n10→- Couch seats, dev sliders, attract, glyphs, and the hub metas are in the page.\\n- The AI Hub harness passed: two players, four players with loss, host leave, a server copy, and the title with no session.\\n- `npm run verify` finished `verify: 98 passed, 0 failed` on the shipped page. Holding the paddles from flatline stays in the Code with tries left. A mouse move, a click, a key, a pad button, and a stick each leave the attract loop. Phone and tablet touch profiles ask for a controller. Firefox and WebKit show the WebGPU message.\\n- `exit-interview.json` matches the About cards. `labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md` has twenty issues, eleven of them game-breaking. `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md` asks for a post-restore scene hook and a public way to rewrite a kept mesh. No engine files were patched.\\n\\n## Deviations\\n\\n- The operating sheet is 96 by 60 so four software-rendered copies fit in memory.\\n- Radial slow is fixed at 0.6. The sim cannot read the view slider, so that rate stays out of the state hash.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→# Trauma Compass\\n\\nSurgical simulation at Harbor Light General. The one-file page is `Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731.html` beside this note. The dev project is the folder of the same name.\\n\\n## Done\\n\\n- Title chosen with a real RNG: Trauma Compass.\\n- Operation sim, bot, strains, campaign, and lockstep tests are green. The bot wins every required case and seed.\\n- The shipped page boots from `file://` in Chromium with WebGPU. Two launches both reached the title, a filled 1280×720 view, and a key moved the menu. The session client is the first script and matches the vendor file. Usage reads `added on import`, and the Usage card is marked `data-about=\\\"usage\\\"`.\\n10→- Couch seats, dev sliders, attract, glyphs, and the hub metas are in the page.\\n- The AI Hub harness passed: two players, four players with loss, host leave, a server copy, and the title with no session.\\n- `npm run verify` finished `verify: 98 passed, 0 failed` on the shipped page. Holding the paddles from flatline stays in the Code with tries left. A mouse move, a click, a key, a pad button, and a stick each leave the attract loop. Phone and tablet touch profiles ask for a controller. Firefox and WebKit show the WebGPU message.\\n- `exit-interview.json` matches the About cards. `labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md` has twenty issues, eleven of them game-breaking. `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md` asks for a post-restore scene hook and a public way to rewrite a kept mesh. No engine files were patched.\\n\\n## Deviations\\n\\n- The operating sheet is 96 by 60 so four software-rendered copies fit in memory.\\n- Radial slow is fixed at 0.6. The sim cannot read the view slider, so that rate stays out of the state hash.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224731__x59c1d3/work/PROGRESS.md\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"# Trauma Compass\\n\\nSurgical simulation at Harbor Light General. The one-file page is `Trauma-Compass-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224731.html` beside this note. The dev project is the folder of the same name.\\n\\n## Done\\n\\n- Title chosen with a real RNG: Trauma Compass.\\n- Operation sim, bot, strains, campaign, and lockstep tests are green. The bot wins every required case and seed.\\n- The shipped page boots from `file://` in Chromium with WebGPU. Two launches both reached the title, a filled 1280×720 view, and a key moved the menu. The session client is the first script and matches the vendor file. Usage reads `added on import`, and the Usage card is marked `data-about=\\\"usage\\\"`.\\n- Couch seats, dev sliders, attract, glyphs, and the hub metas are in the page.\\n- The AI Hub harness passed: two players, four players with loss, host leave, a server copy, and the title with no session.\\n- `npm run verify` finished `verify: 98 passed, 0 failed` on the shipped page. Holding the paddles from flatline stays in the Code with tries left. A mouse move, a click, a key, a pad button, and a stick each leave the attract loop. Phone and tablet touch profiles ask for a controller. Firefox and WebKit show the WebGPU message.\\n- `exit-interview.json` matches the About cards. `labs/game/TESTING-LOG.md` has twenty issues, eleven of them game-breaking. `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md` asks for a post-restore scene hook and a public way to rewrite a kept mesh. No engine files were patched.\\n\\n## Deviations\\n\\n- The operating sheet is 96 by 60 so four software-rendered copies fit in memory.\\n- Radial slow is fixed at 0.6. The sim cannot read the view slider, so that rate stays out of the state hash.\\n\",\"total_lines\":18}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa3f-84ea-7700-ba58-234d6f85e151","uuid":"d1486adb-fb10-4a99-b16c-02254ab693b1"}
